        {
          "id": "lem-cm-mass-metric-positivity",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "The mass metric is symmetric, positive semidefinite, and positive definite exactly when the configuration differential is injective",
          "statement": "Let $N\\ge1$, let $Q$ be a smooth manifold, let $X:Q\\to\\mathbb R^{3N}$ be smooth, let $m_1,\\dots,m_N>0$ and let $G_q$ be the mass metric of [[def-cm-constrained-configuration-and-mass-metric]].\n\n1. For every $q\\in Q$ the map $G_q$ is a symmetric bilinear form on $T_qQ$.\n2. $G_q(u,u)=\\sum_{i=1}^N m_i\\|dX_q(u)_i\\|_2^2\\ge 0$ for every $u\\in T_qQ$, so $G_q$ is positive semidefinite.\n3. $G_q$ is positive definite ([[def-definiteness-inertia-and-signature-data-over-the-reals]]) if and only if $dX_q$ is injective. In particular, if $X$ is an immersion ([[def-immersion-submersion-and-constant-rank-map]]) then $G_q$ is positive definite for every $q$.\n4. If $b_1,\\dots,b_n$ is an ordered basis of $T_qQ$ and $A$ is the matrix whose $j$-th column is the coordinate vector of $dX_q(b_j)$ in the standard basis of $\\mathbb R^{3N}$, then the matrix of the bilinear form $G_q$ in this basis is $A^{\\mathsf T}MA$, with $M$ the mass matrix.",
          "deps": [
            "def-cm-constrained-configuration-and-mass-metric",
            "def-inner-product-space",
