        {
          "id": "lem-cm-adapted-coordinates-exist-and-are-unique",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Existence and uniqueness of adapted coordinates, and the affine structure of simultaneous slices",
          "statement": "Let $(V,\\tau,g,A)$ and an adapted chart $(o,u,(e_1,e_2,e_3))$ be as in [[def-cm-affine-time-space]].\n\n1. Every $p\\in A$ has exactly one pair $(t,x)\\in\\mathbb R\\times\\mathbb R^3$ with\n\n$$p=o+tu+\\sum_{i=1}^3x_ie_i,$$\n\nso the adapted-coordinate map $\\iota:A\\to\\mathbb R\\times\\mathbb R^3$ of that definition is well defined, and it is a bijection.\n\n2. For every $t\\in\\mathbb R$ the simultaneous slice $A_t=\\{p:\\tau(p-o)=t\\}$ is an affine space modelled on $K=\\ker\\tau$, and for $p,q\\in A_t$ one has $p-q\\in K$ with $p-q=\\sum_i(x_i(p)-x_i(q))e_i$ and\n\n$$d_g(p,q)=\\|x(p)-x(q)\\|_2.$$\n\n3. For every set of data $(V,\\tau,g,A)$ and fixed orientation of $K$ satisfying [[def-cm-affine-time-space]], at least one adapted chart exists. No origin, time vector or spatial basis is distinguished by this existence assertion.",
          "deps": [
            "def-cm-affine-time-space",
            "def-kernel-and-image-of-a-linear-map",
            "def-orthogonal-vectors-sets-and-orthonormal-bases",
            "def-linear-map",
            "cor-finite-dimensional-inner-product-spaces-have-orthonormal-bases",
            "def-orientation-of-a-finite-dimensional-real-vector-space"
          ],
