        {
          "id": "lem-cm-so3-is-a-matrix-group",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "$SO(3)$ is a subgroup of the general linear group, with $R^{-1}=R^{\\mathsf T}$",
          "statement": "In the notation of [[def-cm-special-orthogonal-group]]:\n\n1. $I_3\\in SO(3)$, and for all $R,S\\in SO(3)$ the matrices $RS$ and $R^{\\mathsf T}$ again lie in $SO(3)$; moreover $\\det R=1$, $R$ is invertible, and its inverse is $R^{\\mathsf T}$, so also $RR^{\\mathsf T}=I_3$.\n2. Consequently $SO(3)$ is a subgroup of the general linear group $GL_3(\\mathbb R)$ ([[def-invertible-matrix-and-general-linear-group]], [[cor-general-linear-group-is-a-group]]).",
          "deps": [
