        {
          "id": "lem-cm-rigid-labeling-stabilizer",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "A labeling containing two independent vectors has trivial $SO(3)$-stabilizer",
          "statement": "For $S\\subseteq\\mathbb R^3$, its **pointwise $SO(3)$ stabilizer** is\n\n$$\\operatorname{Stab}_{SO(3)}(S):=\\{R\\in SO(3):Rs=s\\text{ for every }s\\in S\\}.$$\n\nLet $u,v\\in\\mathbb R^3$ be linearly independent and let $S\\subseteq\\mathbb R^3$ be a nonempty set with $u,v\\in S$. If $R\\in SO(3)$ satisfies $Rs=s$ for every $s\\in S$, then $R=I_3$.\n\nEquivalently, $\\operatorname{Stab}_{SO(3)}(S)=\\{I_3\\}$. The conclusion uses only the two indicated independent vectors; no assumption that $0\\in S$ is made.",
          "deps": [
            "def-cm-special-orthogonal-group",
            "def-cross-product-in-r3",
            "lem-cross-product-is-bilinear-alternating-and-orthogonal",
            "thm-cross-product-norm-is-the-two-vector-gram-determinant",
