      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "ex-cm-galilean-boost-coordinate-change",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Worked change of adapted chart with a rotation, a boost and a spatial shift",
          "statement": "Take $V=\\mathbb R^4$ with coordinates $(t,x_1,x_2,x_3)$, $\\tau(t,x_1,x_2,x_3)=t$, so that $K=\\{0\\}\\times\\mathbb R^3$ with the standard inner product $g$, and take $A=V$ as an affine space over itself. Let the first adapted chart be the standard one, $o=0$, $u=e_0$, $(e_1,e_2,e_3)$ the standard basis of $K$. Let the second adapted chart be\n\n$$o'=e_2,\\qquad u'=e_0+e_1,\\qquad e_1'=e_2,\\quad e_2'=-e_1,\\quad e_3'=e_3,$$\n\nwhich is adapted: $\\tau(u')=1$, and $(e_1',e_2',e_3')$ is a positively oriented $g$-orthonormal basis of $K$.\n\nFor a point with first coordinates $(t,x_1,x_2,x_3)$, equating the two expansions gives $t'=t$, $x_2=x_1'+1$ and $x_1=t'-x_2'$, that is\n\n$$x'_1=x_2-1,\\qquad x'_2=t-x_1,\\qquad x'_3=x_3,$$\n\nwhich is the transformation $x'=Rx+vt+a$ of [[lem-cm-adapted-charts-and-galilean-transformations]] with $b=0$,\n\n$$R=\\begin{pmatrix}0&1&0\\\\-1&0&0\\\\0&0&1\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad v=\\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\1\\\\0\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad a=\\begin{pmatrix}-1\\\\0\\\\0\\end{pmatrix}.$$\n\nThe matrix $R$ satisfies $R^{\\mathsf T}R=I_3$ and $\\det R=1$, so $R\\in SO(3)$.",
          "deps": [
            "def-cm-affine-time-space",
            "lem-cm-adapted-coordinates-exist-and-are-unique",
            "lem-cm-adapted-charts-and-galilean-transformations",
            "def-cm-special-orthogonal-group"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-cm-affine-time-space": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-cm-adapted-coordinates-exist-and-are-unique": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-cm-adapted-charts-and-galilean-transformations": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-cm-special-orthogonal-group": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "provenance": {
