          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Let $D:=\\mathbb R\\times\\mathbb R$. For $z\\in\\mathbb R$ define $G_+(z):=z^2$ and $G_-(z):=-z^2$, and define the autonomous vector fields $F_\\pm:D\\to\\mathbb R$ by $F_\\pm(t,z):=G_\\pm(z)$. Their continuity and local Lipschitz property in the state variable are verified below.\n\n**(i) Finite-time breakdown despite a pointwise-finite vector field.** The function $x_+:[0,1)\\to\\mathbb R$, $x_+(t):=\\frac{1}{1-t}$, solves $x'(t)=F_+(t,x_+(t))$ with $x(0)=1$ on $[0,1)$, and no solution of this initial value problem extends past $b=1$. For every compact $K\\subseteq D$ and every $\\eta>0$ there is $t\\in(1-\\eta,1)$ with $(t,x_+(t))\\notin K$: the graph leaves every compact subset of $D$ as $t\\uparrow1$. The compact-containment hypothesis of [[thm-cm-compact-continuation-for-locally-lipschitz-odes]] fails here, and its escape consequence [[cor-cm-finite-time-breakdown-requires-escape]] is witnessed explicitly.\n\n**(ii) Trapping forces continuation.** The function $x_-:[0,\\infty)\\to\\mathbb R$, $x_-(t):=\\frac{1}{1+t}$, solves $x'(t)=F_-(t,x_-(t))$ with $x(0)=1$, and its values lie in the compact set $K_0:=[0,1]\\subseteq\\mathbb R$. For each finite $b>0$, its restriction to $[0,b)$ is trapped in $K_0$, so clause 2 of [[cor-cm-finite-time-breakdown-requires-escape]] extends it past $b$; thus no finite right endpoint is nonextendable, and the displayed formula supplies a global extension on $[0,\\infty)$.\n\nBoth fields are the same polynomial expression up to sign, so (i) and (ii) exhibit the continuation criterion of [[thm-cm-compact-continuation-for-locally-lipschitz-odes]] as a statement about compact trapping, not about pointwise finiteness of the vector field.",
          "strategy": "Verify the closed forms by the quotient rule and local Lipschitz continuity of the fields by the mean value inequality; prove non-extendability by uniqueness plus boundedness of a continuous solution on [0,1]; verify trapping directly.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-generated",
            "proof": "ai-generated"
          },
          "generation": {
            "role": "example"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Gerald Teschl, Ordinary Differential Equations and Dynamical Systems, §2.6, printed pp. 50-53: the blow-up of $x'=x^2$ and the compact-continuation criterion",
                "url": "https://schecter.math.ncsu.edu/ma_732_sp13/teschl_ode.pdf"
              },
