        {
          "id": "def-cm-local-flow-of-an-autonomous-system",
          "kind": "definition",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "The local flow of an autonomous first-order system",
          "reference": "expansion-proofs.md#d1",
          "design_state": "completed-local-definition; recorded in the batch notes",
          "dependency_level": 0,
          "deps": [
            "def-first-order-ode-initial-value-problem-and-solution",
            "def-maximal-ode-solution",
            "thm-existence-and-uniqueness-of-a-maximal-ode-solution",
            "def-locally-lipschitz-in-the-state-variable"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-first-order-ode-initial-value-problem-and-solution": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-maximal-ode-solution": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-existence-and-uniqueness-of-a-maximal-ode-solution": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-locally-lipschitz-in-the-state-variable": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Let $n\\ge1$, let $U\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n$ be open, and let $F:U\\to\\mathbb R^n$ be continuous and locally Lipschitz in the state variable in the sense of [[def-locally-lipschitz-in-the-state-variable]]. Read the autonomous system\n\n$$x'(t)=F(x(t))$$\n\nas the first-order system of [[def-first-order-ode-initial-value-problem-and-solution]] with domain $D=\\mathbb R\\times U\\subseteq\\mathbb R\\times\\mathbb R^n$ and right-hand side $(t,x)\\mapsto F(x)$. Its initial value problems satisfy the Picard-Lindelöf hypotheses, so by [[thm-existence-and-uniqueness-of-a-maximal-ode-solution]] every $a\\in U$ has a unique maximal solution.\n\nFor $a\\in U$ denote by\n\n$$x(\\,\\cdot\\,;a):I_a\\longrightarrow U$$\n\nthe unique maximal solution with $x(0;a)=a$, where $I_a\\subseteq\\mathbb R$ is its maximal interval of existence ([[def-maximal-ode-solution]]); $I_a$ is an open interval containing $0$, and every solution of $x'=F(x)$ through $(0,a)$ is a restriction of $x(\\,\\cdot\\,;a)$.\n\nThe **flow domain** of $F$ is the set\n\n$$\\Omega:=\\{\\,(t,a)\\in\\mathbb R\\times U\\;:\\;t\\in I_a\\,\\},$$\n\nand the **local flow** (also **phase flow**) of $F$ is the map\n\n$$\\Phi:\\Omega\\longrightarrow U,\\qquad \\Phi(t,a):=x(t;a).$$\n\nFor $t\\in\\mathbb R$ the **time-$t$ map** is the partial map\n\n$$\\Phi_t:\\Omega_t\\longrightarrow U,\\qquad \\Omega_t:=\\{\\,a\\in U:(t,a)\\in\\Omega\\,\\},\\qquad \\Phi_t(a):=\\Phi(t,a).$$\n\nThus $\\Phi_0(a)=a$ whenever it is defined, and $(t,a)\\in\\Omega$ exactly when the maximal solution of $x'=F(x)$ through $a$ is defined at time $t$.",
          "strategy": "Define the flow as the solution family of the autonomous field, with all domain conditions explicit; no uniqueness or completeness statement is smuggled into the definition.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "not-applicable"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Ordinary Differential Equations and Dynamical Systems (AMS Graduate Studies in Mathematics 140, online edition), Section 2.1 (autonomous systems) and Section 6.1 (the flow of a dynamical system), printed pages 17-19 and 190-192",
                "url": "https://schecter.math.ncsu.edu/ma_732_sp13/teschl_ode.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "J. Arino, MATH 8430 Fundamental Theory of Ordinary Differential Equations (University of Manitoba), Section 1.3 (maximal solutions) and Section 1.4 (continuous dependence), printed pages 22-30",
                "url": "https://julien-arino.github.io/assets/pdf/courses/math8430_lecture_notes.pdf"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "lem-cm-local-flow-composition-law",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "The local flow is a partial one-parameter group: identity, composition and inverse-time laws",
          "reference": "expansion-proofs.md#e2",
          "design_state": "completed-local-argument; recorded in the batch notes",
          "dependency_level": 1,
          "deps": [
            "def-cm-local-flow-of-an-autonomous-system",
            "def-maximal-ode-solution",
