          "statement": "Let $n\\ge1$, let $U\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n$ be open, let $F:U\\to\\mathbb R^n$ be of class $C^1$ ([[def-ck-euclidean-maps-and-diffeomorphisms]]), and let $\\Phi:\\Omega\\to U$ be the local flow of $x'=F(x)$ with maximal solutions $x(\\,\\cdot\\,;a):I_a\\to U$ ([[def-cm-local-flow-of-an-autonomous-system]]). Then $\\Omega$ is open in $\\mathbb R\\times U$ ([[def-metric-topology]]), and $\\Phi$ is of class $C^1$ on $\\Omega$, with\n\n$$\\partial_t\\Phi(t,a)=F\\bigl(\\Phi(t,a)\\bigr)\\qquad((t,a)\\in\\Omega).$$",
