          "statement": "Let $X=\\{0,1\\}^{\\mathbb Z}$, let $d$ be the metric of [[lem-cm-bilateral-shift-metric-and-sequential-compactness]] and let $\\sigma:X\\to X$, $\\sigma(s)_k=s_{k+1}$, be the bilateral shift of [[def-cm-bilateral-shift-space-and-cylinders]]. Then:\n\n1. $\\sigma$ is continuous ([[def-metric-continuity]]);\n2. $\\sigma$ is topologically mixing;\n3. the periodic points of $\\sigma$ are dense in $X$;\n4. $\\sigma$ has sensitive dependence on initial conditions with sensitivity constant $\\delta=1$;\n\nconsequently $\\sigma$ is chaotic in the stated sense ([[def-cm-topologically-mixing-dense-periodic-and-sensitive-maps]]).",
          "strategy": "Use cylinders as a basis: continuity from the metric estimate, mixing by prescribing the two blocks at disjoint index sets for all large n, periodic points by repeating a finite block, and sensitivity by flipping a coordinate in the future tail.",
