          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Let $V$ be a real vector space of finite dimension $n\\ge1$, equipped with a symmetric positive-definite bilinear form $\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle:V\\times V\\to\\mathbb R$, and set $\\|v\\|_2:=\\sqrt{\\langle v,v\\rangle}$. Let $T:V\\to V$ be linear, let $V_{\\mathbb C}:=\\mathbb C\\otimes_{\\mathbb R}V$ with canonical embedding $\\iota v:=1\\otimes v$ and complex-linear extension $T_{\\mathbb C}:=\\operatorname{id}_{\\mathbb C}\\otimes T$ ([[def-complexification-of-a-real-vector-space]], [[def-complexification-of-a-real-linear-map]]), and use the exponential series $e^{tT}$ and $e^{tT_{\\mathbb C}}$ of these bounded operators ([[lem-exponential-series-of-a-bounded-operator]]; boundedness is justified in [F1]). Suppose that no eigenvalue of $T_{\\mathbb C}$ in the sense of [[def-eigenvalue-eigenvector-eigenspace-and-spectrum]] has real part $0$.\n\nThen there exist $T$-invariant linear subspaces $E_s,E_u\\subseteq V$ and real constants $C\\ge1$, $c>0$ such that $V=E_s\\oplus E_u$ and, for every $t\\in\\mathbb R$:\n\n1. $\\|e^{tT}v\\|_2\\le Ce^{-ct}\\|v\\|_2$ for $v\\in E_s$ and $t\\ge0$;\n2. $\\|e^{tT}v\\|_2\\le Ce^{ct}\\|v\\|_2$ for $v\\in E_u$ and $t\\le0$;\n3. $\\|e^{tT}v\\|_2\\ge C^{-1}e^{ct}\\|v\\|_2$ for $v\\in E_u$ and $t\\ge0$;\n4. $E_s=\\{v\\in V:e^{tT}v\\to0\\ (t\\to+\\infty)\\}$ and $E_u=\\{v\\in V:e^{tT}v\\to0\\ (t\\to-\\infty)\\}$.",
          "strategy": "Split the spectrum into the open left and right half-planes, build real invariant subspaces from coprime factors of the minimal polynomial via a Bezout identity, estimate each Jordan block by its exponential series with the polynomial factor, and characterise the subspaces by the exponential estimates.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Ordinary Differential Equations and Dynamical Systems (AMS Graduate Studies in Mathematics 140, online edition), Section 9.1, Theorems 9.1 and 9.2 and formulas (9.2), (9.4), (9.6), printed pages 253-254",
                "url": "https://schecter.math.ncsu.edu/ma_732_sp13/teschl_ode.pdf"
              },
