          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Let $n\\ge1$, let $\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n$ be open, let $M:\\Omega\\to M_n(\\mathbb R)$ be a $C^2$ field of symmetric positive definite matrices, let $U:\\Omega\\to\\mathbb R$ be $C^2$, and let $E(q,v)=\\tfrac12v^{\\mathsf T}M(q)v+U(q)$ be the energy of [[def-cm-mechanical-vector-field-and-energy-in-a-chart]]. If $q:I\\to\\Omega$ is a $C^2$ solution of the mechanical system $M(q)q''=\\tfrac12\\nabla_q(q'^{\\mathsf T}M(q)q')-(D_qM(q)[q'])q'-\\nabla U(q)$ on the interval $I$, then\n\n$$\\frac{d}{dt}E\\bigl(q(t),q'(t)\\bigr)=0\\qquad(t\\in I);$$\n\nthat is, the energy is constant along every solution.",
          "strategy": "Differentiate the kinetic energy using the product rule and the derivative of the matrix field along the curve, substitute the equation of motion, and cancel the two configuration-dependence terms.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
