          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Let $n\\ge1$, let $M\\in M_n(\\mathbb R)$ be symmetric positive definite and let $K\\in M_n(\\mathbb R)$ be symmetric and non-negative, that is $v^{\\mathsf T}Kv\\ge0$ for all $v\\in\\mathbb R^n$. Let $M^{1/2}$, $M^{-1/2}$ be the square roots of [[lem-cm-positive-definite-matrix-square-roots]] and let\n\n$$S:=M^{-1/2}KM^{-1/2}.$$\n\nBy the real spectral theorem choose an orthogonal matrix $O$ and a diagonal matrix $\\Lambda=\\operatorname{diag}(\\lambda_1,\\dots,\\lambda_n)$ with $S=O\\Lambda O^{\\mathsf T}$ and $\\lambda_i\\ge0$ for all $i$.\n\nLet $I\\subseteq\\mathbb R$ contain at least two points and satisfy $r,s\\in I,\\ r\\le u\\le s\\Longrightarrow u\\in I$ for all $r,s,u\\in\\mathbb R$; suppose also $0\\in I$. Let $q:I\\to\\mathbb R^n$ be twice differentiable with continuous first and second domain-relative derivatives, in the sense of [[def-vector-valued-derivative-and-integral]]. Put $z:=O^{\\mathsf T}M^{1/2}q$. Then:\n\n1. $q$ satisfies the quadratic system $Mq''+Kq=0$ on $I$ if and only if $z$ satisfies the decoupled system\n\n$$z_i''+\\lambda_iz_i=0\\qquad(1\\le i\\le n)$$\n\non $I$;\n2. for every $i$ the solutions of the scalar equation in clause 1 on an interval containing $0$, with prescribed initial data, are exactly as follows:\n\n$$z_i(t)=a_i\\cos(\\omega_it)+b_i\\sin(\\omega_it)\\quad\\text{with }\\omega_i:=\\sqrt{\\lambda_i}>0\\ \\text{when }\\lambda_i>0,$$\n\nequivalently $z_i(t)=\\operatorname{Re}(C_ie^{i\\omega_it})$ with $C_i=a_i-ib_i\\in\\mathbb C$, and\n\n$$z_i(t)=a_i+b_it\\qquad\\text{when }\\lambda_i=0;$$\n\nthe coefficients are $a_i=z_i(0)$, $b_i=z_i'(0)/\\omega_i$ for $\\lambda_i>0$ and $b_i=z_i'(0)$ for $\\lambda_i=0$, so the displayed families cover every initial datum and are the complete solution sets for the first-order system $\\bigl(z_i,z_i'\\bigr)'=(z_i',-\\lambda_iz_i)$;\n3. consequently every solution of $Mq''+Kq=0$ is $q=M^{-1/2}Oz$ for a unique choice of the modal solutions of clause 2, and the correspondence between initial data $(q(0),q'(0))\\in\\mathbb R^{2n}$ and the coefficient tuples $(a_i,b_i)$ is a bijection;\n4. for every solution the modal energies $E_i:=\\tfrac12\\bigl(z_i'^2+\\lambda_iz_i^2\\bigr)$ are constant on $I$, and so are\n\n$$\\tfrac12\\dot q^{\\mathsf T}M\\dot q+\\tfrac12q^{\\mathsf T}Kq=\\tfrac12|z'|_2^2+\\tfrac12\\sum_{i=1}^n\\lambda_iz_i^2=\\sum_{i=1}^nE_i .$$",
          "strategy": "Transform the system by M^{-1/2} and the orthogonal diagonalisation of S, solve the decoupled scalar equations with a uniqueness argument, and verify the modal-energy identities by direct differentiation.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Ordinary Differential Equations and Dynamical Systems (AMS Graduate Studies in Mathematics 140, online edition), Section 8.4, formulas (8.76)-(8.79): decoupling M q'' + W q = 0 by V M^{-1/2} W M^{-1/2} and the mode energies",
                "url": "https://schecter.math.ncsu.edu/ma_732_sp13/teschl_ode.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "D. Tong, Classical Dynamics (Cambridge lecture notes, January 2015 version), Section 2.6 (normal modes and the mode frequencies), printed pages 40-45",
                "url": "https://www.davidtong.org/pdfs/teaching/classical-dynamics/clas.pdf"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "thm-cm-energy-stability-of-a-strict-minimum",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "A strict local minimum of the potential gives a Lyapunov stable equilibrium of the mechanical system, by energy conservation",
          "reference": "mathematical-prerequisites.md#m7",
          "design_state": "completed-local-argument; recorded in the batch notes",
          "dependency_level": 2,
          "deps": [
            "def-cm-mechanical-vector-field-and-energy-in-a-chart",
            "lem-cm-energy-conservation-for-the-mechanical-system",
            "def-cm-equilibrium-and-lyapunov-stability",
            "thm-cm-compact-continuation-for-locally-lipschitz-odes",
            "def-locally-lipschitz-in-the-state-variable",
            "lem-a-c1-map-is-locally-lipschitz-on-compact-coordinate-subsets",
