            "def-locally-lipschitz-in-the-state-variable": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-a-c1-map-is-locally-lipschitz-on-compact-coordinate-subsets": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-existence-and-uniqueness-of-a-maximal-ode-solution": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-maximal-ode-solution": "mathematical-premise",
            "cor-inverse-matrix-by-adjugate": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-continuous-partial-derivatives-imply-total-differentiability": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-metric-ball": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-heine-borel-rn": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-extreme-value-metric": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-additivity-over-subintervals": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-euclidean-inner-product": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-intermediate-value": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-cauchy-schwarz-and-the-euclidean-norm": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Let $n\\ge1$, let $\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n$ be open, let $M:\\Omega\\to M_n(\\mathbb R)$ be a $C^2$ field of symmetric positive definite matrices, let $U:\\Omega\\to\\mathbb R$ be $C^2$, let $q_0\\in\\Omega$ with $\\nabla U(q_0)=0$, and suppose $q_0$ is a **strict local minimum** of $U$: there is $r_0>0$ with $\\overline B(q_0,r_0)\\subseteq\\Omega$ and\n\n$$U(q)>U(q_0)\\qquad(0<\\|q-q_0\\|_2<r_0).$$\n\nLet $G$ be the mechanical vector field of [[def-cm-mechanical-vector-field-and-energy-in-a-chart]] on $\\Omega\\times\\mathbb R^n$, with energy $E(q,v)=\\tfrac12v^{\\mathsf T}M(q)v+U(q)$. Then $(q_0,0)$ is a Lyapunov stable equilibrium of $(q',v')=G(q,v)$ in the sense of [[def-cm-equilibrium-and-lyapunov-stability]]: for every $\\varepsilon>0$ with $\\overline B((q_0,0),\\varepsilon)\\subseteq\\Omega\\times\\mathbb R^n$ there is $\\delta>0$ such that every maximal solution $(q,v)$ with $\\|(q(0),v(0))-(q_0,0)\\|_2<\\delta$ is defined for all $t\\ge0$ and satisfies\n\n$$\\|(q(t),v(t))-(q_0,0)\\|_2<\\varepsilon\\qquad(t\\ge0).$$\n\nNo asymptotic stability is asserted.",
          "strategy": "Use exact energy conservation: E-E_0 has a positive minimum on the sphere of radius epsilon, continuity of E gives a delta, and the energy barrier forbids a first exit; compact continuation then gives forward existence for all time.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Ordinary Differential Equations and Dynamical Systems (AMS Graduate Studies in Mathematics 140, online edition), Section 6.7, Theorem 6.16: a fixed point of Newton's equation is stable if the potential has a local minimum there",
                "url": "https://schecter.math.ncsu.edu/ma_732_sp13/teschl_ode.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "D. Tong, Classical Dynamics (Cambridge lecture notes, January 2015 version), Section 2.6 (stability of equilibria from the potential), printed pages 37-39",
                "url": "https://www.davidtong.org/pdfs/teaching/classical-dynamics/clas.pdf"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "prop-cm-linearization-of-the-mechanical-system-at-an-equilibrium",
          "kind": "proposition",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Linearisation of the mechanical system at an equilibrium: M(q_0) xi'' + D²U(q_0) xi = 0, and the small-oscillation quadratic model",
          "reference": "mathematical-prerequisites.md#m7",
          "design_state": "completed-local-argument; recorded in the batch notes",
          "dependency_level": 2,
          "deps": [
            "def-cm-mechanical-vector-field-and-energy-in-a-chart",
