            "def-vector-valued-derivative-and-integral": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-euclidean-inner-product": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-abs-value": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Let $\\mathcal L:J\\times U\\times\\mathbb R^n\\to\\mathbb R$ be a fibre-full $C^2$ time-dependent\nLagrangian chart that is hyperregular, with inverse Legendre branch $v(t,q,p)$ and Hamiltonian\n$H(t,q,p)=p\\cdot v(t,q,p)-\\mathcal L(t,q,v(t,q,p))$\n([[def-cm-legendre-map-in-a-time-dependent-chart]]). Then:\n\n1. **(differential)** for every $(t,q,p)\\in J\\times U\\times\\mathbb R^n$,\n\n$$H_p(t,q,p)=v(t,q,p),\\qquad H_q(t,q,p)=-\\mathcal L_q\\bigl(t,q,v(t,q,p)\\bigr),\\qquad H_t(t,q,p)=-\\mathcal L_t\\bigl(t,q,v(t,q,p)\\bigr);$$\n\n2. **(equivalence)** for a $C^1$ curve $(q,p):I\\to U\\times\\mathbb R^n$ on an open interval $I\\subseteq J$\n   ([[def-interval]], [[def-vector-valued-derivative-and-integral]]) the following are\n   equivalent:\n   (a) $q$ is $C^2$ and $E_{\\mathcal L}(q)(t)=0$ for all $t\\in I$, with\n   $p(t)=\\mathcal L_v\\bigl(t,q(t),q'(t)\\bigr)$;\n   (b) $(q,p)$ satisfies Hamilton's equations\n   $q'(t)=H_p\\bigl(t,q(t),p(t)\\bigr)$ and $p'(t)=-H_q\\bigl(t,q(t),p(t)\\bigr)$ for all $t\\in I$;\n3. **(energy)** along any curve satisfying (a) or (b), the function\n   $e(t):=\\mathcal L_v(t,q,q')\\cdot q'(t)-\\mathcal L(t,q(t),q'(t))$ equals $H(t,q(t),p(t))$ and\n   satisfies $e'(t)=-\\mathcal L_t(t,q(t),q'(t))$ on $I$; in particular, if $\\mathcal L_t$ vanishes\n   on the set $\\{(s,q(s),q'(s)):s\\in I\\}$, then $e$ is constant on $I$.",
          "strategy": "Differentiate H=p.v-L along the inverse branch and cancel the dv terms; the equivalence is the chain rule on the branch.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "D. Cline, Variational Principles in Classical Mechanics (2nd edition, University of Rochester River Campus Libraries, open textbook, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0), Section 8.2 (Legendre Transformation between Lagrangian and Hamiltonian mechanics) and Section 8.3 (Hamilton's Equations of Motion)",
                "url": "https://downloads.libretexts.org/api/v1/download/phys-9557/pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "D. Tong, Classical Dynamics (University of Cambridge Part II Mathematical Tripos), Sections 4.1.1-4.1.2 (the Legendre transform identities and Hamilton's equations), printed pages 82-84",
                "url": "https://www.davidtong.org/pdfs/teaching/classical-dynamics/clas.pdf"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
