            "def-cm-mechanical-vector-field-and-energy-in-a-chart": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-cm-quadratic-mode-decomposition": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-sine-and-cosine-derivatives": "mathematical-premise",
            "cor-trigonometric-parity-and-pythagorean-identity": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-sine-cosine-zero-sets-and-fundamental-period": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-chain-rule-for-total-derivatives": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-algebra-of-derivatives": "mathematical-premise",
            "cor-zero-derivative-implies-constant": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-euclidean-submersions-and-immersions": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-ck-euclidean-maps-and-diffeomorphisms": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-euclidean-inner-product": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-matrix-product-and-identity-matrix": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-interval": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Let $m,l,g>0$ and let $\\Omega:=(-\\pi,\\pi)\\subseteq\\mathbb R$. Consider the embedding\n\n$$X:\\Omega\\to\\mathbb R^2,\\qquad X(\\theta):=\\bigl(l\\sin\\theta,\\,-l\\cos\\theta\\bigr),$$\n\nthe ambient mass $M:=mI_2$ and the constant force $F:=(0,-mg)$. Let $\\theta:I\\to\\Omega$ be a\n$C^2$ curve and put $x(t):=X(\\theta(t))$. Then:\n\n1. $X$ is a $C^3$ immersion with $\\|X'(\\theta)\\|_2=l$ for every $\\theta$; if the ambient motion\n   satisfies $Mx''=F+R$ with $R(t)\\cdot X'(\\theta(t))\\delta=0$ for all $\\delta\\in\\mathbb R$, then\n\n$$ml^2\\theta''(t)+mgl\\sin\\theta(t)=0\\qquad(t\\in I);$$\n\n2. the **reduced energy** $E(\\theta,\\theta'):=\\tfrac12ml^2\\theta'^2-mgl\\cos\\theta$ is constant\n   along every solution of the equation;\n3. $\\theta=0$ is a strict local minimum of the reduced potential\n   $U_{\\mathrm{red}}(\\theta):=-mgl\\cos\\theta$ on $\\Omega$, and the equilibrium $(0,0)$ of the\n   pendulum system $\\theta'=v$, $v'=-(g/l)\\sin\\theta$ is Lyapunov stable;\n4. the linearisation at $\\theta=0$ is $ml^2\\xi''+mgl\\xi=0$, a quadratic mode with angular\n   frequency\n\n$$\\omega=\\sqrt{g/l}.$$",
          "strategy": "Contract the ambient equation with the tangent and identify the one-dimensional mechanical system; then invoke the energy-stability and quadratic-mode theorems.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-generated",
            "proof": "ai-generated"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "D. Cline, Variational Principles in Classical Mechanics (2nd edition, University of Rochester River Campus Libraries, open textbook, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0), Sections 3.4 (Geometrical Representations of Dynamical Motion: the plane pendulum) and 6.5 (Constrained Systems)",
                "url": "https://downloads.libretexts.org/api/v1/download/phys-9557/pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "D. Tong, Classical Dynamics (University of Cambridge Part II Mathematical Tripos), Section 2.3 'Constraints and Generalised Coordinates' (the simple pendulum: the equation theta-ddot = -(g/l) sin theta and the tension), printed pages 17-19",
                "url": "https://www.davidtong.org/pdfs/teaching/classical-dynamics/clas.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "generation": {
            "role": "example"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "ex-cm-rotating-hoop-reduced-energy",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "The rotating hoop: reduced Lagrangian, the equation $\\theta''=\\Omega^2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta-(g/a)\\sin\\theta$, and the reduced energy versus the inertial mechanical energy",
          "reference": "expansion-proofs.md#e22",
          "design_state": "completed-local-example; recorded in the batch notes",
          "dependency_level": 3,
          "deps": [
            "thm-sine-and-cosine-addition-formulas",
