            "thm-algebra-of-derivatives": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-sine-and-cosine-derivatives": "mathematical-premise",
            "cor-trigonometric-parity-and-pythagorean-identity": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-derivative": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-limit-point-r": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-interval": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-ck-euclidean-maps-and-diffeomorphisms": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Let $\\mu>0$, let $J_0\\subseteq(0,\\infty)$ be an open interval, let\n$U:J_0\\to\\mathbb R$ be of class $C^2$, let $I$ be an interval with at least two\npoints, and let $r:I\\to\\mathbb R^3$ be a central-force trajectory for $(\\mu,U)$\nwith constant nonzero angular momentum $j=Je_3$, $J>0$, and polar data\n$(\\rho,\\theta)$ as in [[thm-cm-central-force-polar-reduction]], so that\n$\\rho^2\\theta'=J/\\mu$ and $\\mu\\rho''=-\\bigl(U^{\\mathrm{eff}}_J\\bigr)'(\\rho)$ on\n$I$. Fix $r_0\\in J_0$. Then:\n\n1. **(Necessity.)** If $\\rho\\equiv r_0$ is constant on $I$, then\n   $\\bigl(U^{\\mathrm{eff}}_J\\bigr)'(r_0)=0$ and $\\theta'\\equiv J/(\\mu r_0^2)$\n   is constant; the trajectory is the uniform rotation\n   $r(t)=r_0(\\cos\\theta(t)\\,e_1+\\sin\\theta(t)\\,e_2)$.\n2. **(Existence.)** Conversely, if $\\bigl(U^{\\mathrm{eff}}_J\\bigr)'(r_0)=0$,\n   then for every $\\theta_0\\in\\mathbb R$ the curve\n   $$r^\\circ(t):=r_0\\bigl(\\cos(\\theta_0+\\omega t)\\,e_1+\\sin(\\theta_0+\\omega t)\\,e_2\\bigr), \\qquad \\omega:=\\frac{J}{\\mu r_0^2},$$\n   is a central-force trajectory for $(\\mu,U)$ defined on $\\mathbb R$, with\n   angular momentum $j=Je_3$ and constant energy\n   $E=\\frac12\\mu r_0^2\\omega^2+U(r_0)=U^{\\mathrm{eff}}_J(r_0)$.\n3. **(Linearised radial equation.)** Let $\\rho$ be a solution of the reduced\n   equation $\\mu\\rho''=-\\bigl(U^{\\mathrm{eff}}_J\\bigr)'(\\rho)$ on $I$ with\n   $\\bigl(U^{\\mathrm{eff}}_J\\bigr)'(r_0)=0$, and put\n   $\\delta:=\\rho-r_0$. Then\n   $$\\mu\\delta''=-\\bigl(U^{\\mathrm{eff}}_J\\bigr)''(r_0)\\,\\delta +g(\\delta),\\qquad g(x):=\\bigl(U^{\\mathrm{eff}}_J\\bigr)''(r_0)x-\\bigl(U^{\\mathrm{eff}}_J\\bigr)'(r_0+x),$$\n   where $g(x)/x\\to0$ as $x\\to0$; if moreover\n   $\\bigl(U^{\\mathrm{eff}}_J\\bigr)''(r_0)>0$, then the associated linearised\n   equation $\\mu\\delta''=-\\bigl(U^{\\mathrm{eff}}_J\\bigr)''(r_0)\\delta$ has\n   exactly the solutions\n   $\\delta(t)=A\\cos(\\omega_{\\rm lin}(t-t_0))+B\\sin(\\omega_{\\rm lin}(t-t_0))$\n   with $A,B\\in\\mathbb R$ and $\\omega_{\\rm lin}:=\\sqrt{\\bigl(U^{\\mathrm{eff}}_J\\bigr)''(r_0)/\\mu}>0$,\n   for any $t_0\\in I$. This is a statement about the quadratic radial\n   approximation; no nonlinear stability of the circular orbit is asserted.",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "David Tong, Classical Dynamics (University of Cambridge), §2.5.4 and Figure 15, printed pp. 31-33: circular, elliptic and hyperbolic orbits as features of the effective potential $V_{\\rm eff}$",
                "url": "https://www.davidtong.org/pdfs/teaching/classical-dynamics/clas.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "Konstantin Likharev, Essential Graduate Physics: Classical Mechanics, §3.4, Eqs. (3.52)-(3.58): the circular-orbit condition $\\mathrm dU_{\\rm eff}/\\mathrm dr=0$ and small radial oscillations about it",
                "url": "https://essentialgraduatephysics.org/Files/CM%20merged.pdf"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "thm-cm-kepler-binet-equation",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Binet's equation for the attractive inverse-square field: $\\mathrm d^2u/\\mathrm d\\varphi^2+u=\\mu\\kappa/J^2$ for $u=1/\\rho$",
          "reference": "mathematical-prerequisites.md#m9",
          "design_state": "completed-local-argument (M9 split into items; new local prerequisites recorded in the batch notes)",
          "dependency_level": 3,
          "deps": [
