          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ ([[def-countable-choice]]) for the cited scattering measures and vocabulary.\n\nTake the repulsive Coulomb data $\\kappa=1$ and $E=1$ (with any $\\mu>0$ and\n$J=\\sqrt{2\\mu}$, so that the asymptotic impact distance of\n[[thm-cm-coulomb-scattering]] is $b=1$). Then the deflection map of\n[[thm-cm-rutherford-cross-section]] has the exact values\n$$\\theta_{\\rm def}(1)=2\\arctan\\frac12\\in(0,\\pi), \\qquad \\frac{\\pi}{2}-\\Delta=\\arctan\\frac12,\\qquad \\Delta=\\frac{\\pi}{2}-\\arctan\\frac12,$$\nthe inverse branch satisfies $b(\\theta_{\\rm def}(1))=1$, and\n$$\\frac{\\mathrm d\\sigma}{\\mathrm d\\Omega}\\Bigl(\\theta_{\\rm def}(1)\\Bigr) =\\Bigl(\\frac{\\kappa}{4E}\\Bigr)^2\\csc^4\\Bigl(\\frac{\\theta_{\\rm def}(1)}{2}\\Bigr) =\\frac{25}{16},$$\nbecause $\\theta_{\\rm def}(1)/2=\\arctan\\frac12$ and $\\csc^2(\\arctan\\frac12)=1+\\cot^2(\\arctan\\frac12)=1+4=5$.",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-generated",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Richard Fitzpatrick, Newtonian Dynamics (University of Texas at Austin), §6.4, Eqs. (358)-(365): the Rutherford angle and density, checked here at exact rational data",
                "url": "https://farside.ph.utexas.edu/teaching/336k/Newtonhtml/node51.html"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
