          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "D. Tong, Classical Dynamics (University of Cambridge Part II Mathematical Tripos), Section 4.2 (Liouville's theorem: the flow of Hamilton's equations preserves phase-space volume), printed pages 88-92",
                "url": "https://www.davidtong.org/pdfs/teaching/classical-dynamics/clas.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "Ana Cannas da Silva, Lectures on Symplectic Geometry, revised January 2006, canonical symplectomorphisms preserve the symplectic volume form omega^n / n!",
                "url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20120413034139if_/http://www.math.ist.utl.pt:80/%7Eacannas/Books/symplectic.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice where the cited change-of-variables theorem requires it\n([[def-countable-choice]], [[cor-c-one-change-of-variables-for-l-one-functions]]). Let $n\\ge1$, let\n$U$ be a phase domain ([[def-cm-phase-domain-and-standard-symplectic-two-form]]), let\n$H\\in C^2(U)$, and let $\\Phi$ be the local flow of $X_H=J\\nabla H$\n([[prop-cm-hamiltonian-field-and-poisson-bracket-in-a-phase-chart]]). Let $t\\in\\mathbb R$, let\n$D_t:=\\{z\\in U:(t,z)\\text{ lies in the flow domain}\\}$ be the open domain of $\\Phi_t$\n([[cor-cm-flow-domain-open-and-flow-is-c1]]), and let $A\\subseteq D_t$ be a bounded Borel set with\n$\\overline A\\subseteq D_t$. Then $A$ and $\\Phi_t(A)$ are Lebesgue measurable with\n\n$$\\lambda_{2n}\\bigl(\\Phi_t(A)\\bigr)=\\lambda_{2n}(A).$$\n\nFor a $C^2$ time-dependent Hamiltonian $\\mathcal H:T\\times U\\to\\mathbb R$ and the evolution $E$ of [[prop-cm-flow-derivative-satisfies-the-canonical-matrix-identity]], fix $t_0,t\\in T$. Its initial-state domain $D_{t,t_0}=\\{z:E(t,t_0,z)\\text{ is defined}\\}$ is open. For every bounded Borel $A\\subseteq D_{t,t_0}$ with $\\overline A\\subseteq D_{t,t_0}$,\n$$\\lambda_{2n}(E(t,t_0,A))=\\lambda_{2n}(A).$$\nNo completeness or time independence is needed."
        },
