          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "D. Tong, Classical Dynamics (University of Cambridge Part II Mathematical Tripos), Sections 4.4-4.4.2 (canonical transformations, the condition M^T J M = J and infinitesimal canonical transformations), printed pages 100-104",
                "url": "https://www.davidtong.org/pdfs/teaching/classical-dynamics/clas.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "D. Cline, Variational Principles in Classical Mechanics (2nd edition, University of Rochester River Campus Libraries, open textbook, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0), Section 15.3 (canonical transformations in Hamiltonian mechanics)",
                "url": "https://downloads.libretexts.org/api/v1/download/phys-9557/pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Let $n\\ge1$, let $U,V\\subseteq\\mathbb R^{2n}$ be phase domains with standard two-forms $\\omega_U$,\n$\\omega_V$ and the same matrix $J$ ([[def-cm-phase-domain-and-standard-symplectic-two-form]]), and\nlet $C:U\\to V$ be of class $C^1$ ([[def-ck-euclidean-maps-and-diffeomorphisms]]). Then:\n\n1. $C^*\\omega_V=\\omega_U$ if and only if $DC(z)^{\\mathsf T}J\\,DC(z)=J$ for every $z\\in U$;\n2. if $C$ is a $C^1$ diffeomorphism onto $V$ and $C^*\\omega_V=\\omega_U$, then $C$ is a \n   $C^1$ canonical transformation in the finite-regularity sense of\n   [[def-cm-finite-regularity-canonical-calculus]] and $|\\det DC(z)|=1$ for every $z\\in U$;\n3. if in addition $H\\in C^2(V)$ and $C:U\\to V$ is a $C^2$ diffeomorphism with $C^*\\omega_V=\\omega_U$,\n   then $H\\circ C\\in C^2(U)$ and\n   $$DC(z)\\,X_{H\\circ C}(z)=X_H\\bigl(C(z)\\bigr)\\qquad(z\\in U).$$"
        },
        {
          "id": "def-cm-generating-function-of-the-first-and-second-kind",
          "kind": "definition",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Generating functions of the first and second kind for a local canonical map",
          "reference": "expansion-proofs.md#e7",
          "design_state": "completed local argument; carrier and readiness record authored in this batch",
          "dependency_level": 4,
          "deps": [
            "def-cm-phase-domain-and-standard-symplectic-two-form",
            "prop-cm-canonical-map-tests-and-hamiltonian-transport",
            "thm-euclidean-inverse-function-theorem",
            "def-ck-euclidean-maps-and-diffeomorphisms",
            "def-jacobian-matrix-and-gradient",
