            ]
          },
          "statement": "Let $n\\ge1$ and let $S$ be a generating function of the first kind or of the second kind, with data\n$O_q,O_Q$ resp. $O_q,O_P$ and the local map $C$ it generates\n([[def-cm-generating-function-of-the-first-and-second-kind]]). Then $C$ is a $C^2$ local\ndiffeomorphism and it is canonical: on its domain,\n\n$$C^*\\Bigl(\\sum_{i=1}^n dQ^i\\wedge dP_i\\Bigr)=\\sum_{i=1}^n dq^i\\wedge dp_i .$$\n\nMoreover $|\\det DC|=1$ wherever $C$ is defined\n([[prop-cm-canonical-map-tests-and-hamiltonian-transport]]).\n\nThe words canonical and the finite-regularity form operations here use [[def-cm-finite-regularity-canonical-calculus]], with the displayed $C^2$ maps; smoothness is not inferred."
        },
