          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "D. Tong, Classical Dynamics (University of Cambridge Part II Mathematical Tripos), Section 4.4.3 'Generating Functions' (existence of a generating function on a neighbourhood where the relevant projection is a diffeomorphism), printed pages 104-105",
                "url": "https://www.davidtong.org/pdfs/teaching/classical-dynamics/clas.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "D. Cline, Variational Principles in Classical Mechanics (2nd edition, University of Rochester River Campus Libraries, open textbook, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0), Section 15.3 (canonical transformations and the local existence of a generating function)",
                "url": "https://downloads.libretexts.org/api/v1/download/phys-9557/pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Let $n\\ge1$, let $U,V\\subseteq\\mathbb R^{2n}$ be phase domains with standard two-forms\n$\\omega_U,\\omega_V$, and let $C:U\\to V$ be a $C^2$ diffeomorphism with $C^*\\omega_V=\\omega_U$\n([[def-cm-phase-domain-and-standard-symplectic-two-form]],\n[[prop-cm-canonical-map-tests-and-hamiltonian-transport]]). Write $C(z)=(Q(z),P(z))$ and\n$z=(q(z),p(z))$ for the coordinate functions, and let $z_0\\in U$. If the map\n$$F:U\\to\\mathbb R^n\\times\\mathbb R^n,\\qquad F(z):=\\bigl(q(z),Q(z)\\bigr)$$\nhas invertible derivative at $z_0$, then there are an open neighbourhood $W\\subseteq U$ of $z_0$ and\nan open ball $W''\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n\\times\\mathbb R^n$ about $F(z_0)$ with $F(W)=W''$ on which\n$F$ is a $C^2$ diffeomorphism, and a $C^3$ function $S:W''\\to\\mathbb R$ with\n$\\det S_{qQ}(F(z_0))\\ne0$, such that the restriction of $S$ to a product neighbourhood $O_q\\times O_Q\\subseteq W''$ of $F(z_0)$ is a first-kind generating function and its generated local map agrees with $C$ on a neighbourhood of $z_0$.\n\nThe words canonical and the finite-regularity form operations here use [[def-cm-finite-regularity-canonical-calculus]], with the displayed $C^2$ maps; smoothness is not inferred."
        },
        {
          "id": "prop-cm-time-dependent-generating-function",
          "kind": "proposition",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "A time-dependent generating function produces canonical time slices and shifts the Hamiltonian by $S_t$",
          "reference": "expansion-proofs.md#e7",
          "design_state": "completed local argument; carrier and readiness record authored in this batch",
          "dependency_level": 6,
          "deps": [
            "def-cm-phase-domain-and-standard-symplectic-two-form",
