          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "D. Tong, Classical Dynamics (University of Cambridge Part II Mathematical Tripos), Section 4.4.3 (worked generating functions and the infinitesimal shear as a canonical transformation), printed pages 104-105",
                "url": "https://www.davidtong.org/pdfs/teaching/classical-dynamics/clas.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "D. Cline, Variational Principles in Classical Mechanics (2nd edition, University of Rochester River Campus Libraries, open textbook, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0), Section 15.3 (canonical transformations and simple generating functions)",
                "url": "https://downloads.libretexts.org/api/v1/download/phys-9557/pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Let $n=1$, let $\\lambda\\in\\mathbb R$, and let $S:\\mathbb R^2\\to\\mathbb R$,\n$S(q,P):=qP+\\lambda q^2/2$. Then:\n\n1. $S$ is a generating function of the second kind with $S_{qP}=1\\ne0$, and the local map it\n   generates is $\\Psi_\\lambda(q,p)=(Q,P)=(q,\\,p-\\lambda q)$, defined on all of $\\mathbb R^2$\n   ([[def-cm-generating-function-of-the-first-and-second-kind]]);\n2. $\\Psi_\\lambda$ is canonical, both by the generating-function theorem\n   ([[prop-cm-generating-functions-yield-canonical-maps]]) and by direct verification of the matrix\n   identity $D\\Psi_\\lambda^{\\mathsf T}J\\,D\\Psi_\\lambda=J$\n   ([[prop-cm-canonical-map-tests-and-hamiltonian-transport]])."
        },
        {
          "id": "ex-cm-cylinder-shift-obstruction-checks",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "The unit cylinder shift: explicit local generating function, loop integral and global failure",
          "reference": "expansion-proofs.md#e7",
          "design_state": "completed local argument; carrier and readiness record authored in this batch",
          "dependency_level": 7,
          "deps": [
