            "lem-of-square-monotone",
            "lem-of-inverse-positive",
            "def-interval",
            "thm-of-square-roots"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "thm-cm-forced-oscillator-sinusoidal-response": "mathematical-premise",
            "cor-mean-value-theorem": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-chain-rule": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-algebra-of-derivatives": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-derivative-of-a-power": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-of-square-monotone": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-of-inverse-positive": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-interval": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-of-square-roots": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Let $m>0$, $k>0$, $c>0$ and $f_0\\ne0$. For $\\Omega\\ge0$ let\n\n$$A(\\Omega):=\\frac{|f_0|}{\\sqrt{(k-m\\Omega^2)^2+c^2\\Omega^2}}$$\n\nbe the amplitude about zero of the steady response of [[thm-cm-forced-oscillator-sinusoidal-response]] clause 1, and put\n\n$$u_*:=\\frac{k}{m}-\\frac{c^2}{2m^2},\\qquad \\Omega_*:=\\sqrt{u_*}\\ \\ \\text{when }u_*>0 .$$\n\nThen:\n\n1. If $u_*>0$ (equivalently $c^2<2mk$), $A$ is strictly increasing on $[0,\\Omega_*]$, strictly decreasing on $[\\Omega_*,\\infty)$, and its maximum on $[0,\\infty)$ is attained at $\\Omega_*$ and at no other point, with\n$$A(\\Omega_*)=\\frac{2m|f_0|}{c\\sqrt{4mk-c^2}} .$$\n2. If $u_*\\le0$ then $A$ is strictly decreasing on $[0,\\infty)$ and its maximum on $[0,\\infty)$ is attained at $\\Omega=0$ and at no other point.",
          "strategy": "Write the denominator as an exact square m^2(u-u_*)^2+c^2(4mk-c^2)/(4m^2) in u=Omega^2, locate the vertex, and convert the monotonicity through the strictly decreasing maps x->1/x and x->sqrt(x).",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
