          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Let $n\\ge1$, let $U\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n$ be open with $0\\in U$, let $F:U\\to\\mathbb R^n$ be continuous and locally Lipschitz in the state variable, and let $r>0$, $C\\ge0$, $L\\ge0$ and $A\\in M_n(\\mathbb R)$ satisfy $\\overline B(0,r)\\subseteq U$ ([[def-metric-ball]]) and\n\n$$\\|F(z)-Az\\|_2\\le C\\|z\\|_2^2,\\qquad \\|F(z)\\|_2\\le L\\|z\\|_2\\qquad(\\|z\\|_2\\le r),$$\nwhere $Az$ and $\\|A\\|$ use the matrix-action and induced Euclidean operator-norm convention of [[cor-cm-variation-of-constants-for-linear-systems]].\n\nLet $z_0\\in\\mathbb R^n$ with $\\delta:=\\|z_0\\|_2>0$, let $T>0$ with $\\delta e^{LT}<r$, and let $y:\\mathbb R\\to\\mathbb R^n$ be the solution of the linear system $y'=Ay$, $y(0)=z_0$ ([[cor-cm-variation-of-constants-for-linear-systems]]). Then:\n\n1. The maximal solution $z$ of $z'=F(z)$, $z(0)=z_0$ is defined on $[0,T]$ and satisfies $\\|z(t)\\|_2\\le\\delta e^{Lt}$ for $t\\in[0,T]$ ([[def-maximal-ode-solution]]).\n2. For every $t\\in[0,T]$,\n$$\\|z(t)-y(t)\\|_2\\le C\\delta^2\\int_0^te^{\\|A\\|(t-s)}e^{2Ls}\\,ds\\le C\\delta^2\\,t\\,e^{(\\|A\\|+2L)t},$$\nwhere $\\|A\\|$ is the operator norm of $A$ for the Euclidean norm ([[def-operator-norm]]).",
          "strategy": "Bound the maximal solution by Gronwall while it stays in the ball, extend it to [0,T] by compact continuation, and compare it with the linear solution by the variation-of-constants formula.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Ordinary Differential Equations and Dynamical Systems (retrieved 365-page online edition), Section 2.4, Theorem 2.10, printed pp. 45-48 (smooth dependence and variational equation); Section 3.4, Theorem 3.12, printed pp. 83-84 (variation of constants). The explicit quadratic error estimate is derived locally.",
                "url": "https://schecter.math.ncsu.edu/ma_732_sp13/teschl_ode.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "I. Stewart, Advanced Classical Mechanics (MIT 8.09 Fall 2014, complete course text), Chapter 7 Section 7.1.3: the linearised version of the damped oscillator and the limits of linear reasoning, printed pages 147-148",
                "url": "https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/8-09-classical-mechanics-iii-fall-2014/d9bac33f6c60b304dc0398e99b327102_MIT8_09F14_full.pdf"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
