          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Let $n\\ge1$, $P>0$, let $O\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n$ be open, and let $f:\\mathbb R\\times O\\to\\mathbb R^n$ be continuous, continuously partially differentiable in the second variable and $P$-periodic in time, with average $\\bar f$ and deviation $g$ as in [[def-cm-averaging-data-and-averaged-field]]. Here $D_xf(t,x)$ is the total derivative in the state variable defined in [[lem-cm-averaging-data-basic-bounds]]. Let $x_0\\in O$, let $0<\\rho<R$ with $\\overline B(x_0,R)\\subseteq O$ ([[def-metric-ball]]), and let $M,L\\ge0$ satisfy\n\n$$\\|f(t,x)\\|_2\\le M,\\qquad \\|D_xf(t,x)\\|\\le L\\qquad\\bigl(t\\in\\mathbb R,\\ x\\in\\overline B(x_0,R)\\bigr),$$\n\n$\\|\\cdot\\|$ being the operator norm ([[def-operator-norm]]). Put\n\n$$B:=2MP,\\qquad B_1:=2LP,\\qquad K:=e^{LA}\\bigl[B+(LB+B_1M)A\\bigr],$$\n\nwhere $\\varepsilon>0$ and $A>0$ are parameters. Suppose $y:[0,A/\\varepsilon]\\to\\overline B(x_0,R-\\rho)$ is a solution of the averaged system\n\n$$y'(t)=\\varepsilon\\bar f(y(t)),\\qquad y(0)=x_0 .$$\n\nIf $\\varepsilon K<\\rho$, then the solution $x$ of $x'(t)=\\varepsilon f(t,x(t))$, $x(0)=x_0$ exists on all of $[0,A/\\varepsilon]$ and satisfies, for every $t\\in[0,A/\\varepsilon]$,\n\n$$\\|x(t)-y(t)\\|_2\\le\\varepsilon K=\\varepsilon\\,e^{LA}\\bigl[B+(LB+B_1M)A\\bigr].$$",
          "strategy": "Conjugate x by the deviation g to cancel the oscillatory term exactly, apply Gronwall to the resulting difference with y, and use the smallness condition to prevent exit from the trapping ball.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
