            "thm-derivative-of-exponential": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-algebra-of-derivatives": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Let $m>0$, $g\\in\\mathbb R$ and consider the two constant-forcing models with time domain $I=\\mathbb R$ (the half-line solution in (ii) is the restriction of its global solution) ([[def-cm-oscillator-model-and-phase-system]]).\n\n- (i) Uniform force: $x''=g$ with data $x(0)=x_0$, $x'(0)=v_0$. The unique solution is $x(t)=x_0+v_0t+\\tfrac12gt^2$.\n- (ii) Linear drag: $m=1$, $c=2$, $g=1$, that is $x''+2x'=1$, with data $(x_0,v_0)=(0,0)$. The unique solution on $[0,\\infty)$ is $x(t)=\\tfrac12t-\\tfrac14(1-e^{-2t})$, and its velocity $x'(t)=\\tfrac12(1-e^{-2t})$ increases to the limiting value $\\tfrac12$.",
          "strategy": "Read the solutions from the convolution representation with the explicit homogeneous kernels and differentiate.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-generated",
            "proof": "ai-generated"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "K. Likharev, Essential Graduate Physics, Classical Mechanics (complete 252-page volume), Chapter 5 Section 5.1, Eq. (5.13) and Chapter 2 Section 2.4 (linear drag and terminal velocity in one-dimensional motion), printed pages 3 and 2-4 of the respective chapters",
                "url": "https://essentialgraduatephysics.org/Files/CM%20merged.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "I. Stewart, Advanced Classical Mechanics (MIT 8.09 Fall 2014, complete course text), Chapter 7 Section 7.1: the damped oscillator equation and its damping parameter, printed pages 146-148",
                "url": "https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/8-09-classical-mechanics-iii-fall-2014/d9bac33f6c60b304dc0398e99b327102_MIT8_09F14_full.pdf"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "ex-cm-pendulum-linearization-bound-check",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Finite-time linearization bound for the planar pendulum with explicit constants",
          "reference": "expansion-proofs.md#e8",
          "design_state": "scaffolder-constructed-explicit-mathematical-example; recorded in the batch notes",
          "dependency_level": 3,
          "deps": [
