          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$, which supplies the measure properties of Lebesgue measure used below ([[def-countable-choice]]).\n\nLet $W\\subseteq\\mathbb R^3$ be open and let $H:W\\to\\mathbb R$ be continuous in the Euclidean metric: for every $y\\in W$ and $\\varepsilon>0$ there is $\\delta>0$ such that $z\\in W$, $\\|z-y\\|_2<\\delta$ imply $|H(z)-H(y)|<\\varepsilon$. Let $\\mathcal F$ be a family of nonempty open subsets of $W$ such that\n\n$$ \\text{for every }y_0\\in W\\text{ and every neighbourhood }V\\text{ of }y_0\\text{ there is }A\\in\\mathcal F\\text{ with }y_0\\in A\\subseteq V . \\tag{L} $$\n\nSuppose the signed Lebesgue integral is defined and $\\int_AH\\,dx=0$ for every $A\\in\\mathcal F$ ([[def-integral-over-a-measurable-set]], [[def-integrable-real-and-complex-functions-and-their-integrals]], [[def-lebesgue-measure-and-the-lebesgue-sigma-algebra]]). Then $H=0$ on $W$.",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
