          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ ([[def-countable-choice]]), as used by the transport theorem. Let $I\\subseteq\\mathbb R$ be a nonempty open interval, let $B\\subseteq\\mathbb R^3$ be a material region, let $\\chi:I\\times O\\to\\mathbb R^3$ be a motion of $B$ on $I$ with spatial velocity $u$ ([[def-cm-continuum-motion]]), and let $J_0\\subseteq I$ be an open interval with $\\overline{J_0}\\subseteq I$. Define the swept region\n\n$$\\Sigma:=\\bigl\\{(t,x):t\\in\\overline{J_0},\\ x\\in\\chi_t(\\overline B)\\bigr\\}.$$\n\nWrite $\\mathcal D_\\chi:=\\{(t,x):t\\in I,\\ x\\in\\chi_t(O)\\}$ for the open domain of the spatial velocity $u$ ([[def-cm-continuum-motion]]). Let $U\\subseteq\\mathcal D_\\chi$ be open and contain the swept region $\\Sigma$. Let $\\rho:U\\to(0,\\infty)$ be of class $C^1$ ([[def-ck-euclidean-maps-and-diffeomorphisms]]); call it a **density field**. A **material subregion** is a nonempty bounded open $B'\\subseteq B$ with $\\overline{B'}\\subseteq B$ ([[def-cm-material-region-and-density]]); for such $B'$ the same $\\chi$ is a motion of $B'$.\n\n**(i) Localization.** Assume for every material subregion $B'$ and every $t\\in J_0$\n\n$$\\frac{d}{dt}\\int_{\\chi_t(B')}\\rho(t,x)\\,dx=0, \\tag{CM}$$\n\nIt is sufficient to assume this identity only for those pairs $(t,B')$ for which $\\chi_t(B')$ is an open Euclidean ball with closure inside $\\chi_t(B)$. Under either version of the conservation hypothesis,\n\n$$\\partial_t\\rho(t,x)+\\operatorname{div}\\bigl(\\rho u\\bigr)(t,x)=0$$\n\nfor every $(t,x)\\in J_0\\times\\chi_t(B)$, with the material derivative and divergence of [[def-cm-euclidean-spatial-calculus]].\n\n**(ii) Converse.** Conversely, if $\\partial_t\\rho+\\operatorname{div}(\\rho u)=0$ on an open neighbourhood of $\\Sigma$ in $U$, then (CM) holds for every material subregion $B'$ and every $t\\in J_0$.",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
