          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ ([[def-countable-choice]]), as used by the transport and divergence theorems. Let $I\\subseteq\\mathbb R$ be a nonempty open interval, let $B\\subseteq\\mathbb R^3$ be a material region, let $\\chi:I\\times O\\to\\mathbb R^3$ be a motion of $B$ on $I$ with spatial velocity $u$ and material derivative $D_t$ ([[def-cm-continuum-motion]], [[def-cm-euclidean-spatial-calculus]]), and let $J_0\\subseteq I$ be an open interval with $\\overline{J_0}\\subseteq I$. Define the swept region $\\Sigma=\\{(t,x):t\\in\\overline{J_0},\\ x\\in\\chi_t(\\overline B)\\}$.\n\nWrite $\\mathcal D_\\chi:=\\{(t,x):t\\in I,\\ x\\in\\chi_t(O)\\}$ for the open domain of the spatial velocity $u$ ([[def-cm-continuum-motion]]), and take $U\\subseteq\\mathcal D_\\chi$ open and containing $\\Sigma$. Let $\\rho:U\\to(0,\\infty)$ be a $C^1$ density field, let $\\sigma:U\\to M_3(\\mathbb R)$ be a $C^1$ field (the stress field of [[def-cm-traction-and-stress]]), and let $b:U\\to\\mathbb R^3$ be continuous. Suppose:\n\n**(K)** $\\rho$ satisfies $\\partial_t\\rho+\\operatorname{div}(\\rho u)=0$ at every $(t,x)$ with $t\\in J_0$ and $x\\in\\chi_t(B)$;\n\n**(L)** for every material subregion $B'$ (nonempty bounded open with $\\overline{B'}\\subseteq B$) and every $t\\in J_0$ for which $\\chi_t(B')$ is a bounded $C^1$ domain ([[def-bounded-c-one-domain-boundary-charts-and-outward-normal]]) , the balance is\n\n$$\\frac{d}{dt}\\int_{\\chi_t(B')}\\rho(t,x)u(t,x)\\,dx=\\int_{\\chi_t(B')}\\rho(t,x)b(t,x)\\,dx+\\int_{\\partial\\chi_t(B')}\\sigma(t,y)\\,\\nu(y)\\,dS(y),$$\n\nwhere $\\nu$ is the outward unit normal and the surface integral is that of [[def-surface-integral-on-a-compact-c-one-hypersurface]].\n\nDefine the **row divergence** of $\\sigma$ componentwise by\n\n$$g(t,x):=\\Bigl(\\sum_{j}\\partial_j\\sigma_{1j},\\ \\sum_{j}\\partial_j\\sigma_{2j},\\ \\sum_{j}\\partial_j\\sigma_{3j}\\Bigr)(t,x).$$\n\nThen for every $(t,x)\\in J_0\\times\\chi_t(B)$,\n\n$$\\rho(t,x)\\,D_tu(t,x)=\\rho(t,x)\\,b(t,x)+g(t,x).$$",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "R. Abeyaratne, Continuum Mechanics, Volume II of Lecture Notes on the Mechanics of Solids (MIT, 1988, revised 2020), Sections 4.4–4.6 (balance of momentum principles and the field equations)",
                "url": "https://web.mit.edu/abeyaratne/Volumes/RCA_Vol_II.pdf"
              },
