          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ ([[def-countable-choice]]), as used by the divergence and surface-integral machinery. Let $O\\subseteq\\mathbb R^3$ be open, let $\\sigma:O\\to M_3(\\mathbb R)$ be of class $C^1$, and let $b:O\\to\\mathbb R^3$ be continuous. Suppose that for every bounded $C^1$ domain $D$ with $\\overline D\\subseteq O$ ([[def-bounded-c-one-domain-boundary-charts-and-outward-normal]]), with outward unit normal $\\nu$ and the surface integral of [[def-surface-integral-on-a-compact-c-one-hypersurface]]:\n\n$$\\int_{\\partial D}\\sigma\\nu\\,dS+\\int_Db\\,dx=0 \\tag{LB}$$\n\nand\n\n$$\\int_{\\partial D}y\\times(\\sigma\\nu)\\,dS+\\int_Dy\\times b\\,dx=0. \\tag{AB}$$\n\nThen\n\n$$\\sigma(y)^{\\mathsf T}=\\sigma(y)\\qquad\\text{for every }y\\in O .$$",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
