          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-cm-continuum-motion": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-cm-euclidean-spatial-calculus": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-cm-transport-theorem": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-cm-traction-and-stress": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-bounded-c-one-domain-boundary-charts-and-outward-normal": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-surface-integral-on-a-compact-c-one-hypersurface": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-divergence-theorem-for-bounded-c-one-euclidean-domains": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-integral-over-a-measurable-set": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-linearity-of-the-lebesgue-integral-on-l-one": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-ck-euclidean-maps-and-diffeomorphisms": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-algebra-of-derivatives": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-total-derivative-computes-directional-and-partial-derivatives": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-metric-ball": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-interval": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ ([[def-countable-choice]]), as used by the transport and divergence theorems. Let $I\\subseteq\\mathbb R$ be a nonempty open interval, let $B\\subseteq\\mathbb R^3$ be a material region, and let $\\chi:I\\times O\\to\\mathbb R^3$ be a motion of $B$ on $I$ with spatial velocity $u$. Write\n\n$$\\mathcal D_\\chi:=\\{(t,x):t\\in I,\\ x\\in\\chi_t(O)\\}$$\n\nfor the open domain on which $u$ is defined ([[def-cm-continuum-motion]]). Let $J_0\\subseteq I$ be an open interval with compact closure in $I$, and let $U\\subseteq\\mathcal D_\\chi$ be open and contain the swept region of $B$ over $\\overline{J_0}$.\n\nLet $\\rho:U\\to(0,\\infty)$ and $\\sigma:U\\to M_3(\\mathbb R)$ be $C^1$ and let $b:U\\to\\mathbb R^3$ be continuous. Define $g_i:=\\sum_j\\partial_j\\sigma_{ij}$ and suppose, on $U$:\n\n$$\\partial_t\\rho+\\operatorname{div}(\\rho u)=0\\qquad\\text{and}\\qquad\\rho\\,D_tu=\\rho b+g . \\tag{KM}$$\n\nLet $\\psi:I\\times O'\\to\\mathbb R^3$ be a second motion of a material region $B'\\subseteq B$ (with the same reference chart domain $O'=O$ used for $B$; write $w$ for its spatial velocity), and suppose that for every $t\\in J_0$ the control region $C_t:=\\psi_t(B')$ is a bounded $C^1$ domain ([[def-bounded-c-one-domain-boundary-charts-and-outward-normal]]) with outward unit normal $\\nu$ and boundary surface integral as in [[def-surface-integral-on-a-compact-c-one-hypersurface]].\n\nAssume also that the control sweep $\\Sigma_C:=\\{(t,x):t\\in\\overline{J_0},\\ x\\in\\psi_t(\\overline{B'})\\}$ is contained in $U$. Thus the fields and the local equations (KM) are defined on a neighbourhood of every closed control region. No condition that the control motion coincide with the material motion is imposed.\n\nThen for every $t\\in J_0$:\n\n$$\\frac{d}{dt}\\int_{C_t}\\rho\\,dx=-\\int_{\\partial C_t}\\rho\\,(u-w)\\cdot\\nu\\,dS, \\tag{CV1}$$\n\nand componentwise\n\n$$\\frac{d}{dt}\\int_{C_t}\\rho u_i\\,dx=\\int_{C_t}\\rho b_i\\,dx+\\Bigl(\\int_{\\partial C_t}\\sigma\\nu\\,dS\\Bigr)_i-\\int_{\\partial C_t}\\rho u_i\\,(u-w)\\cdot\\nu\\,dS\\qquad(i=1,2,3). \\tag{CV2}$$",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "R. Abeyaratne, Continuum Mechanics, Volume II of Lecture Notes on the Mechanics of Solids (MIT, 1988, revised 2020), Sections 3.7 and 4.4 (transport equations for a moving part; the balance laws in integral form)",
                "url": "https://web.mit.edu/abeyaratne/Volumes/RCA_Vol_II.pdf"
              },
