          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Let $O\\subseteq\\mathbb R^3$ be open, let $I\\subseteq\\mathbb R$ be a nonempty open interval, let $u:I\\times O\\to\\mathbb R^3$ and $\\rho:I\\times O\\to(0,\\infty)$ be $C^1$, let $p:(0,\\infty)\\to\\mathbb R$ be $C^1$ on the positive density interval $(0,\\infty)$, with enthalpy $h(r):=\\int_1^r p'(s)/s\\,ds$ for $r>0$ as in [[def-cm-fluid-constitutive-models]], and let $V:I\\times O\\to\\mathbb R$ be $C^1$, with the barotropic inviscid stress $\\sigma=-p(\\rho)I_3$; assume the local equations (M) of [[thm-cm-barotropic-momentum-and-bernoulli]] on $I\\times O$:\n\n$$\\partial_t\\rho+\\operatorname{div}(\\rho u)=0,\\qquad \\rho\\,D_tu=\\rho(-\\nabla V)+g,\\qquad g_i=\\sum_j\\partial_j\\sigma_{ij},$$\n\nso that, by part (i) of that theorem, $D_tu=-\\nabla(h(\\rho)+V)$ on $I\\times O$.\n\nLet $t_0<t_1$ with $[t_0,t_1]\\subseteq I$ and let $\\gamma:[t_0,t_1]\\times[0,1]\\to O$ be $C^1$ with\n\n$$\\gamma(t,0)=\\gamma(t,1)\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\\partial_t\\gamma(t,s)=u\\bigl(t,\\gamma(t,s)\\bigr)\\qquad\\bigl((t,s)\\in[t_0,t_1]\\times[0,1]\\bigr) .$$\n\nHere $C^1$ on the closed parameter rectangle means that $\\gamma$ is continuous and its first partial derivatives exist and are continuous there, with one-sided derivatives on the edges.\n\nThen the **circulation**\n\n$$\\Gamma(t):=\\int_0^1\\sum_{i=1}^3u_i\\bigl(t,\\gamma(t,s)\\bigr)\\,\\partial_s\\gamma_i(t,s)\\,ds$$\n\nis constant on $[t_0,t_1]$. The integral is an ordinary Riemann integral of a continuous real function; a singleton time interval has a trivially constant circulation and requires no time differentiation.",
