          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Let $N\\ge2$, $a>0$, $c>0$, let $\\kappa,\\omega\\in\\mathbb R$ satisfy $\\kappa Na\\in2\\pi\\mathbb Z$, and let $A\\in\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{0\\}$. Consider the travelling cosine ansatz for the cyclic chain of [[def-cm-cyclic-spring-chain]]:\n\n$$q_j(t):=A\\cos(\\kappa ja-\\omega t)\\qquad(j\\in\\mathbb Z/N).$$\n\n**(a)** The curve $q:\\mathbb R\\to\\mathbb R^N$ solves $q_j''=\\frac{c^2}{a^2}(q_{j+1}-2q_j+q_{j-1})$ for all $t\\in\\mathbb R$ and all $j$ if and only if\n\n$$\\omega^2=\\frac{4c^2}{a^2}\\sin^2\\!\\Bigl(\\frac{\\kappa a}{2}\\Bigr). \\tag{DR}$$\n\n**(b)** If (DR) holds and $|\\kappa a|\\le1$, then\n\n$$\\Bigl|\\omega^2-c^2\\kappa^2\\Bigr|\\le\\frac{c^2\\kappa^4a^2}{12},$$\n\nso the continuum dispersion $\\omega^2=c^2\\kappa^2$ is recovered with an explicit error bound of second order in the spacing $a$ and fourth order in the wave number $\\kappa$.",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
