        {
          "id": "lem-cm-discrete-periodic-summation-by-parts",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Discrete periodic summation by parts, the scaled Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, and the discrete energy identity",
          "reference": "expansion-proofs.md#e26",
          "design_state": "completed-local-argument; recorded in the batch notes",
          "dependency_level": 1,
          "deps": [
            "def-cm-cyclic-spring-chain",
            "prop-coordinate-cauchy-schwarz-agrees-with-the-finite-sum-theorem",
            "def-derivative",
            "thm-algebra-of-derivatives",
            "thm-linearity-of-the-integral",
            "def-euclidean-inner-product"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-cm-cyclic-spring-chain": "mathematical-premise",
            "prop-coordinate-cauchy-schwarz-agrees-with-the-finite-sum-theorem": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-derivative": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-algebra-of-derivatives": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-linearity-of-the-integral": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-euclidean-inner-product": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Use the notation $z_{j+N}=z_j$, $(D_+z)_j=(z_{j+1}-z_j)/a$, $(\\Delta_az)_j=(z_{j+1}-2z_j+z_{j-1})/a^2$, $\\langle z,w\\rangle_a=a\\sum_jz_jw_j$, $\\|z\\|_a^2=\\langle z,z\\rangle_a$ and $E_a(q,p)=\\tfrac12(\\|p\\|_a^2+c^2\\|D_+q\\|_a^2)$ of [[def-cm-cyclic-spring-chain]].\n\n**(a) Summation by parts.** For all $z,w\\in\\mathbb R^N$,\n\n$$\\langle D_+z,D_+w\\rangle_a=-\\langle \\Delta_az,w\\rangle_a .$$\n\n**(b) Scaled Cauchy-Schwarz.** For all $z,w\\in\\mathbb R^N$, $|\\langle z,w\\rangle_a|\\le\\|z\\|_a\\|w\\|_a$ ([[prop-coordinate-cauchy-schwarz-agrees-with-the-finite-sum-theorem]], [[def-euclidean-inner-product]]).\n\n**(c) Energy identity.** Let $I\\subseteq\\mathbb R$ be an open interval, let $q:I\\to\\mathbb R^N$ be $C^2$ and let $R:I\\to\\mathbb R^N$ be continuous with\n\n$$q_j''=\\frac{c^2}{a^2}\\bigl(q_{j+1}-2q_j+q_{j-1}\\bigr)+R_j=c^2(\\Delta_aq)_j+R_j\\qquad(j\\in\\mathbb Z/N).$$\n\nThen $t\\mapsto E_a(q(t),q'(t))$ is $C^1$ on $I$ with\n\n$$\\frac{d}{dt}E_a\\bigl(q(t),q'(t)\\bigr)=a\\sum_{j=1}^N R_j(t)\\,q_j'(t),$$\n\nand consequently $\\bigl|\\frac{d}{dt}E_a\\bigr|\\le\\|R(t)\\|_a\\,\\sqrt{2E_a(t)}$ whenever $E_a\\ge0$ (which always holds).",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
