            "def-continuity-real": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-continuous-implies-integrable": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-ftc-first-part": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "All integrals in this statement and proof are ordinary Riemann integrals of continuous functions on compact intervals, as in [[def-cm-sine-coefficients-of-periodic-functions]].\n\nLet $L>0$. Then:\n\n**(a)** For all integers $n,k\\ge1$,\n\n$$\\int_0^L\\sin\\Bigl(\\frac{n\\pi x}{L}\\Bigr)\\sin\\Bigl(\\frac{k\\pi x}{L}\\Bigr)dx=\\frac{L}{2}\\,\\delta_{nk}.$$\n\n**(b)** Let $W:\\mathbb R\\to\\mathbb R$ be continuous ([[def-continuity-real]]), odd and $2L$-periodic. Then\n\n$$\\int_0^{2L}W(x)\\,dx=0,\\qquad \\int_0^{2L}W(x)\\cos\\Bigl(\\frac{k\\pi x}{L}\\Bigr)dx=0\\quad\\text{for every integer }k ,$$\n\nand, for every integer $k\\ge1$,\n\n$$\\frac{1}{2L}\\int_0^{2L}W(x)\\sin\\Bigl(\\frac{k\\pi x}{L}\\Bigr)dx=\\frac{1}{L}\\int_0^{L}W(x)\\sin\\Bigl(\\frac{k\\pi x}{L}\\Bigr)dx .$$",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "R. Laugesen, Harmonic Analysis Lecture Notes (arXiv:0903.3845), Theorem 5.4(c) and its proof (orthonormality of the trigonometric system)",
                "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/0903.3845"
              },
