          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Let $T,L>0$ and $R:=[0,T]\\times[0,L]$ ([[def-interval]]). For each $k\\in\\mathbb N$ let $u_k$ be of class $C^2$ on an open neighbourhood of $R$ ([[def-ck-euclidean-maps-and-diffeomorphisms]], [[def-directional-and-partial-derivatives]]). Suppose that on $R$:\n\n$$u_k\\to u,\\quad \\partial_tu_k\\to v,\\quad \\partial_xu_k\\to w,\\quad \\partial_t^2u_k\\to v_2,\\quad \\partial_t\\partial_xu_k\\to z,\\quad \\partial_x^2u_k\\to w_2$$\n\npointwise for $u$ and uniformly for the five derivative sequences ([[def-continuity-real]]). Then $u$ is $C^2$ on the interior of $R$, all listed limits are continuous on $R$, and on the interior\n\n$$\\partial_tu=v,\\quad \\partial_xu=w,\\quad \\partial_t^2u=v_2,\\quad \\partial_t\\partial_xu=\\partial_x\\partial_tu=z,\\quad \\partial_x^2u=w_2 ,$$\n\nthe derivatives extending continuously to $R$.",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "W. Trench, Introduction to Real Analysis, Section 4.4, Theorem 4.4.11 (differentiation of a uniformly convergent sequence of functions)",
                "url": "https://ramanujan.math.trinity.edu/wtrench/texts/trench_real_analysis.pdf"
