          "statement": "Let $L>0$, $c>0$. Let $F:\\mathbb R\\to\\mathbb R$ be odd and $2L$-periodic of class $C^5$ and let $G:\\mathbb R\\to\\mathbb R$ be odd and $2L$-periodic of class $C^4$ ([[def-cm-sine-coefficients-of-periodic-functions]], [[def-ck-euclidean-maps-and-diffeomorphisms]]), with $M_5:=\\sup|F^{(5)}|<\\infty$, $M_4:=\\sup|G^{(4)}|<\\infty$. Put\n\n$$a_n:=b_n(F),\\qquad d_n:=\\frac{b_n(G)}{\\omega_n},\\qquad \\omega_n:=\\frac{cn\\pi}{L}\\qquad(n\\ge1),$$\n\nand define, for $(t,x)\\in\\mathbb R^2$,\n\n$$u(t,x):=\\sum_{n\\ge1}\\Bigl[a_n\\cos(\\omega_nt)+d_n\\sin(\\omega_nt)\\Bigr]\\sin\\Bigl(\\frac{n\\pi x}{L}\\Bigr). \\tag{S}$$\n\nThen:\n\n**(i)** the series (S) and the termwise series of $\\partial_tu,\\partial_xu,\\partial_t^2u,\\partial_t\\partial_xu,\\partial_x^2u$ converge absolutely and uniformly on every strip $[-T,T]\\times[0,L]$; the sum $u$ is $C^2$, is odd and $2L$-periodic in $x$, satisfies $u_{tt}=c^2u_{xx}$, obeys the fixed-end conditions $u(t,0)=u(t,L)=0$, and has\n\n$$u(0,x)=F(x),\\qquad u_t(0,x)=G(x)\\qquad(x\\in\\mathbb R).$$\n\n**(ii)** (Uniqueness.) If $v$ is $C^2$ on $[0,T]\\times[0,L]$ for some $T>0$, satisfies $v_{tt}=c^2v_{xx}$ there, $v(t,0)=v(t,L)=0$ for all $t$, and $v(0,\\cdot)=v_t(0,\\cdot)=0$, then $v=0$ on $[0,T]\\times[0,L]$.\n\n**(iii)** (Tail bound.) For every $N\\ge1$ and every $(t,x)\\in[-T,T]\\times[0,L]$,\n\n$$\\Bigl|u(t,x)-\\sum_{n\\le N}\\Bigl[a_n\\cos(\\omega_nt)+d_n\\sin(\\omega_nt)\\Bigr]\\sin\\Bigl(\\frac{n\\pi x}{L}\\Bigr)\\Bigr|\\le C\\,(N+1)^{-4},$$\n\nwhere $C:=2\\bigl(\\frac{2L^5M_5}{\\pi^5}+\\frac{2L^5M_4}{c\\pi^5}\\bigr)$.",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "R. Laugesen, Harmonic Analysis Lecture Notes (arXiv:0903.3845), Chapters 1–2 (Fourier coefficients, summability and the uniqueness theorem (2.14))",
                "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/0903.3845"
              },
              {
                "title": "K. Likharev, Essential Graduate Physics, Classical Mechanics (September 1, 2026 complete volume), Section 6.5 (standing waves of the fixed-end string)",
                "url": "https://essentialgraduatephysics.org/Files/CM%20merged.pdf"
              }
            ],
            "precheck": "pass"
          }
        }
      ],
