        {
          "id": "cor-cm-principal-axes-of-the-inertia-matrix",
          "kind": "corollary",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Principal axes and principal moments of the inertia matrix, and positivity in the nondegenerate case",
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ ([[def-countable-choice]]), used through [[lem-cm-inertia-matrix-properties]] to ensure finiteness of the inertia integrals. Let $\\nu$ be a mass distribution on $\\mathbb R^3$ with inertia matrix $I=I(\\nu)$ ([[def-cm-mass-distribution-and-inertia-matrix]]), and write $I\\omega$ for the matrix-vector product and $\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle$ for the Euclidean inner product on $\\mathbb R^3$ ([[def-matrix-product-and-identity-matrix]], [[def-euclidean-inner-product]]). Then:\n\n1. there is an orthonormal basis $(e_1,e_2,e_3)$ of $\\mathbb R^3$ ([[def-orthogonal-vectors-sets-and-orthonormal-bases]]) and real numbers $I_1,I_2,I_3$ with $Ie_j=I_je_j$ for $j=1,2,3$;\n2. for any such basis and any $\\omega=\\sum_j\\omega_je_j$ one has $I\\omega=\\sum_jI_j\\omega_je_j$, $I_j=e_j^{\\mathsf T}Ie_j$, and $\\omega^{\\mathsf T}I\\omega=\\sum_jI_j\\omega_j^2=\\int\\lVert\\omega\\times\\rho\\rVert_2^2\\,d\\nu(\\rho)\\ \\ge0$;\n3. each $I_j$ vanishes exactly when $\\nu(\\mathbb R^3\\setminus\\mathbb Re_j)=0$, that is, the whole mass lies on the line $\\mathbb Re_j$; if the inertia form is positive definite then every $I_j>0$ and $I$ is invertible with $I^{-1}e_j=I_j^{-1}e_j$; and if $\\nu$ is not supported on any line through the origin, meaning that $\\nu(\\mathbb R^3\\setminus\\mathbb R\\omega)>0$ for every $\\omega\\ne0$, then every $I_j>0$.",
          "deps": [
            "def-countable-choice",
            "def-cm-mass-distribution-and-inertia-matrix",
            "lem-cm-inertia-matrix-properties",
            "cor-real-spectral-theorem-for-self-adjoint-endomorphisms",
