        {
          "id": "thm-cm-instability-of-the-intermediate-axis",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Instability of spin about the intermediate principal axis of the torque-free top",
          "statement": "Let $I_1<I_2<I_3$ be positive reals, let $I:\\mathbb R^3\\to\\mathbb R^3$ be the linear map with $Ie_j=I_je_j$ on the standard orthonormal basis, and consider the torque-free Euler system $l'=F(l)$, $F(l)=l\\times(I^{-1}l)$, on $U=\\mathbb R^3$ ([[thm-cm-euler-equations-and-torque-free-invariants]], [[def-cm-equilibrium-and-lyapunov-stability]]). Let $L\\ne0$. Then $l_0:=Le_2$ is an equilibrium of $F$ and is **not Lyapunov stable**: with $$\\varepsilon_0:=\\frac{|L|}{2},\\qquad a:=\\sqrt{\\frac{1/I_1-1/I_2}{1/I_2-1/I_3}}>0,\\qquad c_0:=a\\Bigl(\\frac1{I_2}-\\frac1{I_3}\\Bigr)\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}|L|>0,$$ for every $\\delta>0$ there is a solution $l$ with $\\lVert l(0)-l_0\\rVert_2<\\delta$ and some $t\\ge0$ with $\\lVert l(t)-l_0\\rVert_2\\ge\\varepsilon_0$; Moreover, with $\\delta_0:=|L|/(2\\sqrt{1+a^2})$, the escape can be arranged at a time $t\\le c_0^{-1}\\log(\\delta_0/\\eta)$ where $\\eta=l_1(0)>0$ may be chosen as small as desired.",
          "deps": [
            "def-natural-logarithm",
            "cor-exponential-is-a-bijection-onto-positive-reals",
            "thm-exponential-is-strictly-increasing",
