        {
          "id": "lem-cm-coordinate-rotation-matrices",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "The coordinate rotation matrices $R_z(a)$ and $R_y(a)$: values in $SO(3)$, composition law, and derivatives",
          "statement": "For $a\\in\\mathbb R$ define, in the standard basis of $\\mathbb R^3$,\n$$R_z(a):=\\begin{pmatrix}\\cos a&-\\sin a&0\\\\ \\sin a&\\cos a&0\\\\ 0&0&1\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad R_y(a):=\\begin{pmatrix}\\cos a&0&\\sin a\\\\ 0&1&0\\\\ -\\sin a&0&\\cos a\\end{pmatrix}\\in M_3(\\mathbb R).$$\nThen:\n\n1. $R_z(a)\\in SO(3)$ and $R_y(a)\\in SO(3)$ for every $a$ ([[def-cm-special-orthogonal-group]]), $R_z(a)e_3=e_3$ and $R_y(a)e_2=e_2$, and $R_z(0)=R_y(0)=I_3$.\n2. $R_z(a)R_z(b)=R_z(a+b)$ and $R_y(a)R_y(b)=R_y(a+b)$ for all $a,b\\in\\mathbb R$.\n3. For every differentiable $a:I\\to\\mathbb R$ on an interval $I\\subseteq\\mathbb R$ ([[def-derivative]], [[def-interval]]), the matrix-valued curves $t\\mapsto R_z(a(t))$ and $t\\mapsto R_y(a(t))$ are differentiable with $$(R_z\\circ a)'=a'\\,R_z(a)\\,[e_3]_\\times=a'\\,[e_3]_\\times R_z(a),\\qquad (R_y\\circ a)'=a'\\,R_y(a)\\,[e_2]_\\times=a'\\,[e_2]_\\times R_y(a),$$ where $[e_3]_\\times,[e_2]_\\times$ are the cross-product matrices of [[lem-cm-skew-matrix-cross-product-correspondence]].",
          "deps": [
            "def-cm-special-orthogonal-group",
            "lem-cm-so3-is-a-matrix-group",
            "lem-cm-skew-matrix-cross-product-correspondence",
            "def-matrix-space",
