        {
          "id": "thm-cm-heavy-top-reduction",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Reduction of the heavy symmetric top system: conserved momenta, one-dimensional $\\theta$ equation and conserved reduced energy",
          "statement": "Fix the parameters $A>0$, $C>0$, $m>0$, $d>0$, $g>0$ and let $q=(\\varphi,\\theta,\\psi):I\\to\\mathbb R\\times(0,\\pi)\\times\\mathbb R$ be a heavy-top trajectory of [[def-cm-euler-angle-parametrization-and-heavy-top-system]] on an interval $I$ with at least two points; write $q'=(\\varphi',\\theta',\\psi')$ for its derivative. Then:\n\n1. the functions $t\\mapsto b(t):=C\\bigl(\\psi'(t)+\\varphi'(t)\\cos\\theta(t)\\bigr)$ and $t\\mapsto a(t):=A\\varphi'(t)\\sin^2\\theta(t)+b(t)\\cos\\theta(t)$ are constant on $I$; write $b,a$ for their values;\n2. consequently $\\varphi'=\\dfrac{a-b\\cos\\theta}{A\\sin^2\\theta}$ and $\\psi'=\\dfrac{b}{C}-\\dfrac{(a-b\\cos\\theta)\\cos\\theta}{A\\sin^2\\theta}$ on $I$;\n3. the **reduced energy**\n$$E(t):=\\tfrac12A\\theta'(t)^2+\\frac{(a-b\\cos\\theta(t))^2}{2A\\sin^2\\theta(t)}+\\frac{b^2}{2C}+mgd\\cos\\theta(t)$$\nis constant on $I$;\n4. with the **effective potential** $U(\\theta):=\\dfrac{(a-b\\cos\\theta)^2}{2A\\sin^2\\theta}+\\dfrac{b^2}{2C}+mgd\\cos\\theta$ on $(0,\\pi)$, one has\n$$A\\theta''(t)=-U'\\bigl(\\theta(t)\\bigr)\\qquad(t\\in I),$$\nso that the angle $\\theta$ alone obeys the one-dimensional second-order equation $A\\theta''=-U'(\\theta)$ with the constants $a,b$ determined by the initial data.",
          "deps": [
            "def-cm-euler-angle-parametrization-and-heavy-top-system",
            "def-sine-and-cosine-by-power-series",
            "thm-sine-and-cosine-derivatives",
            "thm-chain-rule",
