        {
          "id": "lem-cm-euler-angle-angular-velocity",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Angular velocity in Euler angles: $\\omega_3=\\psi'+\\varphi'\\cos\\theta$ and $\\omega_1^2+\\omega_2^2=\\theta'^2+\\varphi'^2\\sin^2\\theta$",
          "statement": "Let $J\\subseteq\\mathbb R$ be an interval with at least two points, let $\\varphi,\\theta,\\psi:J\\to\\mathbb R$ be differentiable with $\\theta(J)\\subseteq(0,\\pi)$, and put\n$$R(t):=\\Theta\\bigl(\\varphi(t),\\theta(t),\\psi(t)\\bigr)=R_z(\\varphi(t))\\,R_y(\\theta(t))\\,R_z(\\psi(t)),$$\nthe Euler-angle parametrization of [[def-cm-euler-angle-parametrization-and-heavy-top-system]]. Then $R$ is a differentiable $SO(3)$-valued curve, and its **body angular velocity** $\\omega:J\\to\\mathbb R^3$ in the sense of [[def-cm-rigid-placement-and-body-angular-velocity]] (the unique vector with $R(t)^{\\mathsf T}R'(t)=[\\omega(t)]_\\times$) is, in the standard basis,\n$$\\omega=\\bigl(-\\varphi'\\sin\\theta\\cos\\psi+\\theta'\\sin\\psi\\bigr)e_1+\\bigl(\\varphi'\\sin\\theta\\sin\\psi+\\theta'\\cos\\psi\\bigr)e_2+\\bigl(\\psi'+\\varphi'\\cos\\theta\\bigr)e_3,$$\nall functions evaluated at $t$. Consequently\n$$\\omega_3=\\psi'+\\varphi'\\cos\\theta,\\qquad \\omega_1^2+\\omega_2^2=\\theta'^2+\\varphi'^2\\sin^2\\theta,\\qquad \\lVert\\omega\\rVert_2^2=\\theta'^2+\\varphi'^2\\sin^2\\theta+\\bigl(\\psi'+\\varphi'\\cos\\theta\\bigr)^2.$$\nMoreover, if $A,C>0$ and $I:\\mathbb R^3\\to\\mathbb R^3$ is the linear map with $Ie_1=Ae_1$, $Ie_2=Ae_2$, $Ie_3=Ce_3$, then $\\omega^{\\mathsf T}I\\omega=A\\bigl(\\theta'^2+\\varphi'^2\\sin^2\\theta\\bigr)+C\\bigl(\\psi'+\\varphi'\\cos\\theta\\bigr)^2$.",
          "deps": [
            "def-cm-euler-angle-parametrization-and-heavy-top-system",
            "lem-cm-coordinate-rotation-matrices",
            "lem-cm-skew-matrix-cross-product-correspondence",
