      "items": [
        {
          "id": "ex-cm-inertia-tensors-of-point-masses",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Finite point-mass inertia matrices computed and checked against the positivity criterion",
          "statement": "Throughout, the ambient data are the Euclidean inner product and cross product of $\\mathbb R^3$ ([[def-euclidean-inner-product]], [[def-cross-product-in-r3]]), and $\\nu$ is a finite weighted sum of Dirac measures at distinct points $x_1,\\dots,x_n\\in\\mathbb R^3$ with weights $c_1,\\dots,c_n>0$ ([[def-dirac-measure]], [[thm-nonnegative-weighted-sums-of-measures]]), which is a mass distribution of total mass $m=\\sum_kc_k$ in the sense of [[def-cm-mass-distribution-and-inertia-matrix]]; let $I=I(\\nu)$ be its inertia matrix. Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ ([[def-countable-choice]]), used only through the Borel measurability of the polynomial integrands, which is what makes the entries of $I$ finite real numbers ([[lem-cm-mass-moments-are-finite]]). Three cases are computed and each is checked against the positivity criterion of [[lem-cm-inertia-matrix-properties]] and the principal-axis corollary [[cor-cm-principal-axes-of-the-inertia-matrix]].\n\n**(i) Two unit masses on the third axis.** $n=2$, $x_1=e_3$, $x_2=-e_3$, $c_1=c_2=1$: then $m=2$, $\\mu(\\nu)=e_3-e_3=0$, and $I=\\mathrm{diag}(2,2,0)$.\n\n**(ii) Three unit masses at an equilateral triangle in the plane $e_3=0$.** $n=3$, $c_k=1$ and $x_k=\\cos(2\\pi k/3)e_1+\\sin(2\\pi k/3)e_2$ for $k=0,1,2$: then $m=3$, $\\mu(\\nu)=0$ and $I=\\mathrm{diag}(\\tfrac32,\\tfrac32,3)$.\n\n**(iii) Two unit masses on the first axis.** $n=2$, $x_1=e_1$, $x_2=2e_1$, $c_1=c_2=1$: then $m=2$, $\\mu(\\nu)=3e_1\\ne0$, and $I=\\mathrm{diag}(0,5,5)$.",
          "deps": [
