        {
          "id": "ex-cm-torque-free-spin-checks",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Finite checks of the torque-free spin results: stability certificates, an escape-time bound, and the linearized dichotomy",
          "statement": "Fix the diagonal inertia map with principal moments $(I_1,I_2,I_3)=(1,2,3)$ ([[cor-cm-principal-axes-of-the-inertia-matrix]]) and the torque-free Euler system $l'=l\\times(I^{-1}l)$ of [[thm-cm-euler-equations-and-torque-free-invariants]] on $\\mathbb R^3$. The three computations below check the certificates of [[thm-cm-stability-of-extreme-principal-axes]], the escape bound of [[thm-cm-instability-of-the-intermediate-axis]], and the linearized formulas of [[thm-cm-linearized-torque-free-euler-equations]] at explicit data. The inertia values and component calculations are exact rationals or square roots; the escape-time upper bound is the exact expression $4\\log25$. No measurement or simulation is involved, and no claim about a physical top is made.",
          "deps": [
            "thm-cm-stability-of-extreme-principal-axes",
            "thm-cm-instability-of-the-intermediate-axis",
            "thm-cm-linearized-torque-free-euler-equations",
            "thm-cm-euler-equations-and-torque-free-invariants",
            "cor-cm-principal-axes-of-the-inertia-matrix",
            "lem-cm-inertia-matrix-properties",
            "def-euclidean-inner-product",
            "thm-cross-product-norm-is-the-two-vector-gram-determinant",
