          "reference": "expansion-proofs.md#e15",
          "design_state": "Fully authored draft; outside artifact completion cycle 1; independent native review remains pending",
          "statement": "Let $d\\ge1$, let $U$, $M$, $V$, $A$, $B$, $H=A+B$, $D_h$, $K_h$ and $V_h$ be as in [[def-cm-splitting-hamiltonian-and-verlet-map]], with $\\omega_U$ the standard two-form and $J=\\begin{pmatrix}0_d&I_d\\\\-I_d&0_d\\end{pmatrix}$ the standard symplectic matrix ([[def-cm-phase-domain-and-standard-symplectic-two-form]]). Then, on the sets where the maps are defined:\n\n1. $D_h$ is $C^\\infty$ with constant derivative\n $$DD_h(q,p)=\\begin{pmatrix}I_d&hM^{-1}\\\\0_d&I_d\\end{pmatrix},$$\n and, when the whole segment $(q+tM^{-1}p,p)$ for $t$ between $0$ and $h$ lies in $U$, $D_h(q,p)$ is the time-$h$ value of the local flow ([[def-cm-local-flow-of-an-autonomous-system]]) of the Hamiltonian field $X_A(q,p)=(M^{-1}p,0)$ of the kinetic part; moreover\n $$DD_h(q,p)^{\\mathsf T}J\\,DD_h(q,p)=J.$$\n2. $K_h$ is $C^2$ with derivative\n $$DK_h(q,p)=\\begin{pmatrix}I_d&0_d\\\\-h\\,H_V(q)&I_d\\end{pmatrix},$$\n where $H_V$ is the Hessian matrix of $V$, and, when the whole segment $(q,p-t\\nabla V(q))$ for $t$ between $0$ and $h$ lies in $U$, $K_h(q,p)$ is the time-$h$ value of the local flow of the Hamiltonian field $X_B(q,p)=(0,-\\nabla V(q))$ of the potential part; moreover\n $$DK_h(q,p)^{\\mathsf T}J\\,DK_h(q,p)=J.$$\n3. The admissible composition domain of $V_h$ is open, $V_h$ is $C^2$ there, and its derivative satisfies\n $$DV_h(q,p)^{\\mathsf T}J\\,DV_h(q,p)=J,$$\n so that $V_h^*\\omega_U=\\omega_U$: the velocity-Verlet map preserves the standard two-form and is a local $C^2$ canonical transformation in the finite-regularity sense of [[def-cm-finite-regularity-canonical-calculus]]. This matrix/form conclusion holds on the full algebraic composition domain; the separate flow interpretations in clauses 1-2 require the stated intermediate-segment containment.",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false
        },
