          "design_state": "Fully authored draft; outside artifact completion cycle 1; independent native review remains pending",
          "statement": "Use the data, finite field and derivative bounds, and constants $h_1,C_1$ of [[lem-cm-verlet-local-truncation-error-is-cubic]] on an open bounded convex tube $W$, with compact $K_1$ and positive tube margin. Let $T>0$, $0<|h|\\le h_1$, and $n\\in\\mathbb N$ satisfy $n|h|\\le T$. Suppose $z_j=V_h^j(z_0)$ and $y_j=\\Phi_{jh}(z_0)$ both lie in $K_1$ for $0\\le j\\le n$. With $L=L_1=\\sup_W\\|DX_H\\|$, the following holds:\n\n$$\\|z_n-y_n\\|\\le C_1h^2\\frac{e^{LT}-1}{L}\\quad(L>0),\\qquad \\|z_n-y_n\\|\\le C_1Th^2\\quad(L=0).$$\n\nThe constants are independent of $n,h,T$, with the displayed data fixed.",
