          "reference": "expansion-proofs.md#e15",
          "design_state": "Fully authored draft; outside artifact completion cycle 1; independent native review remains pending",
          "statement": "Let $d\\ge1$ and let $(U,U_\\rho,\\tilde A,\\tilde B,M,K,\\delta,\\Psi_h)$ be analytic splitting data as in [[def-cm-analytic-splitting-data-and-exact-splitting-map]], with $J$ the standard matrix and $\\omega_{\\mathbb C}$, $\\{\\,\\cdot\\,,\\,\\cdot\\,\\}$ the complexified form and bracket of [[def-cm-complex-phase-domains-and-holomorphic-maps]]. Let $F\\in\\{\\tilde A,\\tilde B\\}$ and let $\\varphi_F^t$ be the flow of $X_F$ as in [[lem-cm-complex-analytic-flow-existence-and-holomorphy]], on the domain where it is defined.\n\n1. For every $(t,Z)$ in the flow domain, $\\varphi_F^t$ is holomorphic near $Z$, its derivative is invertible, and\n $$D\\varphi_F^t(Z)^{\\mathsf T}J\\,D\\varphi_F^t(Z)=J.$$\n2. For every $h$ and every point $Z$ where $\\Psi_h$ is defined and holomorphic, $D\\Psi_h(Z)$ is invertible and\n $$D\\Psi_h(Z)^{\\mathsf T}J\\,D\\Psi_h(Z)=J.$$\n3. For all holomorphic $f,g$ on an open set containing $\\Psi_h(Z)$,\n $$\\{f\\circ\\Psi_h,\\;g\\circ\\Psi_h\\}(Z)=\\{f,g\\}\\bigl(\\Psi_h(Z)\\bigr).$$",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false
        },
