          "reference": "analytic-backward-error.md#e29",
          "design_state": "Fully authored draft; outside artifact completion cycle 1; independent native review remains pending",
          "statement": "Let $d\\ge1$, let $(U,U_\\rho,\\tilde A,\\tilde B,M,K,\\delta,\\Psi_h)$ be analytic splitting data ([[def-cm-analytic-splitting-data-and-exact-splitting-map]]), and use the notation of [[def-cm-modified-log-coefficients-and-truncations]] and [[lem-cm-log-coefficients-are-symplectic-fields-with-hamiltonian-primitives]]: the coefficient fields $X_j$ ($j\\ge1$, with $X_j$ acting on holomorphic functions as the coefficient operator $D_j=[h^j]L(h)$, and $X_j=D_j$ in the notation of that lemma) and the normalized primitives $H_j$ with $dH_j=\\iota_{X_j}\\omega_{\\mathbb C}$, $H_j(0)=0$, on the domains $D_j$.\n\n1. **Reversibility.** For the local flow germs at $h=0$, and their mutually reverse continuation branches wherever defined, $\\Psi_{-h}=\\Psi_h^{-1}$.\n2. **Parity.** $X_j=0$ for every even $j\\ge2$.\n3. **Modified energy.** Consequently $H_2=0$. For $N\\ge2$ define the finite complex modified Hamiltonian on $D_N$ by\n$$H_h:=\\tilde H+\\sum_{j=2}^{N}h^{j-1}H_j.$$\nThen $H_h=\\tilde H+\\sum_{j=3}^{N}h^{j-1}H_j$ on $D_N$, so the first possible correction is of order $h^2$. On the real part of $D_N$, $H_h$ restricts to the corresponding real function with baseline $H=A+B$.",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false
        },
