          "reference": "analytic-backward-error.md#e29",
          "design_state": "Fully authored draft; outside artifact completion cycle 1; independent native review remains pending",
          "statement": "For analytic splitting data of [[def-cm-analytic-splitting-data-and-exact-splitting-map]], put $m=2d$, $C_0=\\max\\{16,128d^2\\}$, $C_1=1024m^2$, $C_2=16eC_0C_1$, $a=\\rho/(C_2M)$ and $c=a\\log(2)/2>0$. Here $e=\\exp(1)$ and $\\log$ is the inverse of the real exponential on $(0,\\infty)$ ([[def-real-exponential-function-and-e]], [[def-natural-logarithm]]); positivity of $c$ follows from strict increase of $\\exp$ ([[thm-exponential-is-strictly-increasing]]). For $0<h\\le a/3$, set $N=\\lfloor a/h\\rfloor\\ge2$ and\n\n$$H_h=\\tilde H+\\sum_{j=2}^{N}h^{j-1}H_j,\\qquad X^{[N]}(h)=\\sum_{j=1}^{N}h^{j-1}X_j,$$\n\nusing the normalized primitives of [[lem-cm-log-coefficients-are-symplectic-fields-with-hamiltonian-primitives]]. The time-$h$ flow $\\varphi_{H_h}^h$ exists for initial data in $D(\\rho/8)$, for sufficiently small $h$ depending only on the displayed data. There is $C<\\infty$, independent of $h,N$, such that\n\n$$\\|\\Psi_h(Z)-\\varphi_{H_h}^h(Z)\\|\\le CMh\\,e^{-c/h}\\qquad(Z\\in D(\\rho/8)).$$\n\nThe same result holds for the splitting with $A,B$ interchanged. The series defining $H_h$ is finite.",
