          "reference": "analytic-backward-error.md#e29",
          "design_state": "Fully authored draft; outside artifact completion cycle 1; independent native review remains pending",
          "statement": "For analytic splitting data, let $0<h\\le h_0$ be sufficiently small as in [[lem-cm-optimal-truncation-gives-exponential-local-defect]], and let $z_j=\\Psi_h^j(z_0)\\in K$ for $0\\le j\\le n$. Here $e=\\exp(1)$ and $e^x$ denotes $\\exp(x)$ ([[def-real-exponential-function-and-e]]). There are constants $C,c,h_0>0$, independent of $h,n$, such that\n\n$$|H_h(z_n)-H_h(z_0)|\\le Cnh\\,e^{-c/h},\\qquad |H(z_n)-H(z_0)|\\le Ch^2\\quad\\text{if }nh\\le e^{c/(2h)}.$$\n\nHere $H_h$ is the finite optimally truncated Hamiltonian with $|H_h-H|\\le Ch^2$ on a neighbourhood of $K$. For kinetic-plus-potential data, choose the analytic labels $\\tilde A=V$, $\\tilde B=\\tfrac12p^{\\mathsf T}\\mathsf M^{-1}p$ to obtain the velocity-Verlet map $K_{h/2}\\circ D_h\\circ K_{h/2}$; the other order is the position-Verlet variant. Each variant has the stated energy estimate. Compact retention of numerical iterates is assumed; no original-trajectory accuracy on exponential times is asserted.",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false
        },
