          "reference": "analytic-backward-error.md#e29",
          "design_state": "Fully authored draft; outside artifact completion cycle 1; independent native review remains pending",
          "statement": "Use the analytic data and small step of [[thm-cm-analytic-verlet-energy-on-exponential-times]]. Suppose computed points $x_j\\in K$ satisfy $\\|x_{j+1}-\\Psi_h(x_j)\\|\\le\\eta$, for $0\\le j<n$, with $\\eta\\ge0$ small enough that all comparison segments lie in $D(\\rho/8)$. Then\n\n$$|H(x_n)-H(x_0)|\\le 2C_Eh^2+Cnh e^{-c/h}+C_Gn\\eta.$$\n\nIn particular the state-error contribution is $C_G(t/h)\\eta$ for $t=nh$. This is a deterministic additive-error hypothesis, not an analysis of floating-point arithmetic or a claim of rounded symplecticity.",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false
