        {
          "id": "ex-cm-verlet-map-of-the-harmonic-oscillator",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Oscillator Verlet: a preserved quadratic form and bounded original-energy oscillation",
          "dependency_level": 5,
          "deps": [
            "def-cm-splitting-hamiltonian-and-verlet-map",
            "prop-cm-drift-kick-and-verlet-preserve-the-canonical-form"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-cm-splitting-hamiltonian-and-verlet-map": "mathematical-premise",
            "prop-cm-drift-kick-and-verlet-preserve-the-canonical-form": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-generated",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Hairer, Geometric Numerical Integration, Lecture 3: backward error analysis, Sections 1–3 and 5; local analytic estimates supplied here",
                "url": "https://www.unige.ch/~hairer/poly_geoint/week3.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "reference": "analytic-backward-error.md#e29",
          "design_state": "Fully authored draft; outside artifact completion cycle 1; independent native review remains pending",
          "statement": "Take $d=1$, $U=\\mathbb R^2$, $\\Pi=\\mathbb R$, $M=(1)$, and $V(q)=q^2/2$ in [[def-cm-splitting-hamiltonian-and-verlet-map]]. Thus the dimensionless oscillator has $H(q,p)=(q^2+p^2)/2$. For each initial state $z_0=(q_0,p_0)\\in U$, velocity Verlet is the matrix map $z\\mapsto S_hz$, where\n\n$$S_h=\\begin{pmatrix}1-h^2/2&h\\\\-h(1-h^2/4)&1-h^2/2\\end{pmatrix}.$$\n\nFor $0<h<2$, put $\\alpha=1-h^2/4$ and $I_h(q,p)=(\\alpha q^2+p^2)/2$. This positive quadratic form is exactly preserved. Every iterate satisfies\n\n$$|H(z_n)-H(z_0)|\\le\\frac{h^2}{4\\alpha}I_h(z_0).$$\n\nThe conclusion is an explicit exact-arithmetic all-step fact for this linear example. At $h=2$ positivity fails; at $h>2$ the map has a real eigenvalue of modulus greater than one.",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "generation": {
            "role": "example"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "ex-cm-analytic-pendulum-verlet-domain-check",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Analytic pendulum: checking the complex bounds and compact-iterate hypothesis",
          "dependency_level": 18,
          "deps": [
            "def-cm-analytic-splitting-data-and-exact-splitting-map",
            "thm-cm-analytic-verlet-energy-on-exponential-times",
            "lem-cm-separate-roundoff-energy-accumulation"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
