        {
          "id": "lem-cm-finite-iid-sample-mean-bound",
          "statement": "For a finite repeated-observation model of [[def-cm-iid-sampling-model]] with $n\\ge1$, write its variables as $Y_1,\\ldots,Y_n$, where $Y_i$ here denotes the supplier's $Y_{i-1}$ for $1\\le i\\le n$. They are IID square-integrable real random variables on one probability space, with common mean $\\mu$ and variance $\\sigma^2$. Put $\\overline Y=n^{-1}\\sum_{k=1}^nY_k$. Then\n$$E[\\overline Y]=\\mu,\\qquad E|\\overline Y-\\mu|^2=\\frac{\\sigma^2}{n},\\qquad \\mathbb P(|\\overline Y-\\mu|\\ge a)\\le\\frac{\\sigma^2}{na^2}\\quad(a>0).$$\nNo extension to an infinite IID sequence is required; no convergence assertion is made for a single finite family.",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Finite IID sample-mean variance and Chebyshev bound",
          "deps": [
            "cor-chebyshev-inequality-for-random-variables",
            "cor-expectation-linearity-monotonicity-and-modulus-bound",
            "def-cm-iid-sampling-model",
            "lem-variance-and-covariance-identities-for-random-variables",
            "thm-factorization-of-expectations-for-independent-variables"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
