            "cor-integrability-of-absolute-values-products-and-lattice-operations"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-cm-second-variation-of-the-action": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-cm-time-dependent-lagrangian-and-action": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-cm-first-variation-formula": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-differentiation-under-the-integral-sign-on-a-compact-rectangle": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-chain-rule-for-total-derivatives": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-clairaut-schwarz-mixed-partials": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-continuous-partial-derivatives-imply-total-differentiability": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-total-derivative-in-euclidean-space": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-ck-euclidean-maps-and-diffeomorphisms": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-ck-and-multi-index-notation-in-several-variables": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-jacobian-matrix-and-gradient": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-directional-and-partial-derivatives": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-vector-valued-derivative-and-integral": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-interval": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-darboux-integral": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-continuous-implies-integrable": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-linearity-of-the-integral": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-derivative": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-continuity-real": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-abs-value": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-heine-borel-rn": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-heine-cantor-metric": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-monotonicity-of-the-integral": "mathematical-premise",
            "cor-integrability-of-absolute-values-products-and-lattice-operations": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "justified_by": [],
          "reference": "expansion-proofs.md#e19 (the second-order step that the prose section differentiates silently)",
          "design_state": "completed-local-argument",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Let $(O,\\mathcal L)$ be a time-dependent Lagrangian chart over $[a,b]\\times U$ in the sense of\n[[def-cm-time-dependent-lagrangian-and-action]] (so $\\mathcal L$ is $C^2$ and\n$[a,b]\\times U\\times\\mathbb R^n\\subseteq O$), let $q:[a,b]\\to U$ be a $C^2$ curve and let $\\eta$\nbe a variation of $q$ (a $C^2$ map with $\\eta(a)=\\eta(b)=0$). Write\n$\\psi(\\varepsilon,t):=\\bigl(t,q(t)+\\varepsilon\\eta(t),q'(t)+\\varepsilon\\eta'(t)\\bigr)$ and, for\n$|\\varepsilon|<\\varepsilon_0$ with $\\varepsilon_0$ as in clause 1 below,\n\n$$H(\\varepsilon,t):=\\sum_{j,k=1}^n\\Bigl[\\frac{\\partial^2\\mathcal L}{\\partial q_j\\partial q_k}\\bigl(\\psi(\\varepsilon,t)\\bigr)\\eta_j(t)\\eta_k(t)+2\\frac{\\partial^2\\mathcal L}{\\partial q_j\\partial v_k}\\bigl(\\psi(\\varepsilon,t)\\bigr)\\eta_j(t)\\eta_k'(t)+\\frac{\\partial^2\\mathcal L}{\\partial v_j\\partial v_k}\\bigl(\\psi(\\varepsilon,t)\\bigr)\\eta_j'(t)\\eta_k'(t)\\Bigr].$$\n\nThen:\n\n1. there is $\\varepsilon_0>0$ such that for every $\\varepsilon\\in(-\\varepsilon_0,\\varepsilon_0)$\n   the curve $q+\\varepsilon\\eta$ is a $C^2$ admissible curve with values in $U$, and the map\n   $\\varepsilon\\mapsto S(q+\\varepsilon\\eta)$ is of class $C^2$ on $(-\\varepsilon_0,\\varepsilon_0)$;\n2. for every $\\varepsilon\\in(-\\varepsilon_0,\\varepsilon_0)$,\n\n$$\\frac{d^2}{d\\varepsilon^2}S(q+\\varepsilon\\eta)=\\int_a^bH(\\varepsilon,t)\\,dt ;$$\n\n3. in particular the second variation of [[def-cm-second-variation-of-the-action]] is\n\n$$\\delta^2S(q)[\\eta,\\eta]=\\int_a^bH(0,t)\\,dt,$$\n\nthe formula of clause 2 with every second partial of $\\mathcal L$ evaluated at\n$\\bigl(t,q(t),q'(t)\\bigr)$.",
          "strategy": "Apply the compact-rectangle differentiation theorem twice: the first epsilon-derivative is the first-variation integrand, the second is the chain-rule derivative of that integrand along the affine family, computed with the C^1 gradients L_q and L_v; symmetrise the mixed sums by Clairaut.",
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "D. Cline, Variational Principles in Classical Mechanics (2nd edition, University of Rochester River Campus Libraries, open textbook, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0), Sections 5.1-5.2: the parametric family and the first-variation computation; the second variation is not treated there",
                "url": "https://downloads.libretexts.org/api/v1/download/phys-9557/pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "D. Tong, Classical Dynamics (University of Cambridge Part II Mathematical Tripos), Section 2.1: the first variation of the action with fixed endpoints, printed pages 11-12",
                "url": "https://www.davidtong.org/pdfs/teaching/classical-dynamics/clas.pdf"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
