      "items": [
        {
          "id": "def-bilateral-symbol-and-bounded-sequence-space",
          "kind": "definition",
          "title": "The two-sign bilateral shift space, its coding map, and the ball of bounded bilateral real sequences",
          "dependency_level": 2,
          "deps": [
            "def-cm-bilateral-shift-space-and-cylinders",
            "lem-cm-bilateral-shift-metric-and-sequential-compactness",
            "def-function-space",
            "def-metric-space",
            "def-bounded-set",
            "lem-sup-unique",
            "def-complete-ordered-field",
            "def-abs-value",
            "def-integer-power",
            "def-series",
            "thm-geometric-series"
          ],
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "not-applicable"
          },
          "reference": "mechanical-horseshoe.md#1 (the sign alphabet X={-1,+1}^Z, the shift, and the ball B_R of bounded bilateral sequences)",
          "design_state": "completed-local-definition",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Write $\\Sigma_{\\pm}:=\\{-1,+1\\}$ and\n\n$$X_{\\pm}\\ :=\\ \\Sigma_{\\pm}^{\\mathbb Z}\\ =\\ \\{\\,s\\ :\\ s \\text{ is a function } \\mathbb Z\\to\\Sigma_{\\pm}\\,\\},$$\n\nwith the function-set convention of [[def-function-space]]; for $s\\in X_{\\pm}$ write $s_k:=s(k)$. The elements of $X_{\\pm}$ are called **two-sign bilateral sequences**.\n\n**Coding correspondence with the published two-symbol space.** Let\n\n$$\\varphi:X_{\\pm}\\longrightarrow\\{0,1\\}^{\\mathbb Z},\\qquad \\varphi(s)_k:=\\frac{s_k+1}{2}\\in\\{0,1\\},$$\n\nand let $X_2:=\\{0,1\\}^{\\mathbb Z}$, $d_2$ and $\\sigma_2$ be the set, the metric expression and the shift map of [[def-cm-bilateral-shift-space-and-cylinders]]. The formulas $\\varphi(s)_k=(s_k+1)/2$ and $\\varphi^{-1}(t)_k=2t_k-1$ define maps $X_{\\pm}\\to X_2$ and $X_2\\to X_{\\pm}$ that are inverse to each other, coordinate by coordinate.\n\n**Metric expression on $X_{\\pm}$.** Define\n\n$$D_{\\pm}(s,t):=d_2\\bigl(\\varphi(s),\\varphi(t)\\bigr)\\qquad(s,t\\in X_{\\pm}).$$\n\nUnwinding the series of [[def-cm-bilateral-shift-space-and-cylinders]] and using $|\\varphi(s)_k-\\varphi(t)_k|=\\tfrac12|s_k-t_k|$ for every $k\\in\\mathbb Z$ gives the explicit expression\n\n$$D_{\\pm}(s,t)=\\sum_{k\\ge 0}2^{-(k+1)}\\,|s_k-t_k|\\;+\\;\\sum_{k\\ge 1}2^{-(k+1)}\\,|s_{-k}-t_{-k}| .$$\n\nBoth series converge by comparison with the geometric series $\\sum_{k\\ge0}2^{-k}=2$ ([[def-series]], [[thm-geometric-series]], [[def-integer-power]], [[def-abs-value]]), because $|s_k-t_k|\\in\\{0,2\\}$ for every $k$; hence $D_{\\pm}(s,t)$ is a well-defined nonnegative real number. Whether $D_{\\pm}$ is a metric is **not** asserted here; it is proved in the companion lemma on this page, together with the statement that $\\varphi$ is an isometry of $(X_{\\pm},D_{\\pm})$ onto $(X_2,d_2)$.\n\n**The shift.** The **(bilateral) shift** of $X_{\\pm}$ is\n\n$$S_{\\pm}:X_{\\pm}\\longrightarrow X_{\\pm},\\qquad S_{\\pm}(s)_k:=s_{k+1}\\qquad(k\\in\\mathbb Z,\\ s\\in X_{\\pm}).$$\n\nFor $m\\in\\mathbb Z$ its iterate satisfies $S_{\\pm}^{m}(s)_k=s_{k+m}$; in particular $S_{\\pm}$ is a bijection with inverse $S_{\\pm}^{-1}(s)_k=s_{k-1}$, and $S_{\\pm}=\\varphi^{-1}\\circ\\sigma_2\\circ\\varphi$.\n\n**Bounded bilateral sequences.** A function $x:\\mathbb Z\\to\\mathbb R$ is **bounded** when its range $\\{x_k:k\\in\\mathbb Z\\}$ is a bounded subset of $\\mathbb R$ ([[def-bounded-set]]). Write\n\n$$\\ell^{\\infty}(\\mathbb Z):=\\{\\,x:\\mathbb Z\\to\\mathbb R\\ :\\ x \\text{ is bounded}\\,\\},\\qquad \\|x\\|_{\\infty}:=\\sup\\{\\,|x_k|\\ :\\ k\\in\\mathbb Z\\,\\}.$$\n\nThe set $\\{|x_k|:k\\in\\mathbb Z\\}$ whose supremum is taken is nonempty and bounded above ([[def-bounded-set]]), so $\\|x\\|_\\infty$ is a well-defined nonnegative real number ([[lem-sup-unique]], [[def-complete-ordered-field]]). For $R>0$ put\n\n$$B_R:=\\{\\,x\\in\\ell^{\\infty}(\\mathbb Z)\\ :\\ \\|x\\|_{\\infty}\\le R\\,\\}.$$\n\nThus $B_R$ is the closed ball of radius $R$ in the supremum norm, and $\\|x\\|_\\infty\\le R$ is by definition the statement that $|x_k|\\le R$ for every $k\\in\\mathbb Z$ ([[def-bounded-set]], [[def-abs-value]]).",
          "strategy": "Define the listed objects over the published two-symbol shift space and its metric; state exactly which properties are deferred to the companion items.",
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Ordinary Differential Equations and Dynamical Systems, AMS Graduate Studies in Mathematics 140 (author's preliminary online edition, complete PDF), Section 11.5, the two-sided shift on finitely many symbols with the metric (11.35)",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-ode/ode.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "P. Cvitanović, R. Artuso, R. Mainieri, G. Tanner, G. Vattay, Chaos: Classical and Quantum (ChaosBook.org, edition 17.6.8, complete PDF), Chapter 14 Section 14.6, symbolic dynamics and the binary itinerary of a trajectory",
                "url": "https://chaosbook.org/chapters/ChaosBook.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "R. Devaney and Z. Nitecki, Shift automorphisms in the Hénon mapping, Communications in Mathematical Physics 67 (1979) 137-146, the coding of an invariant Cantor set by bi-infinite binary sequences",
                "url": "https://projecteuclid.org/journals/communications-in-mathematical-physics/volume-67/issue-2/Shift-automorphisms-in-the-H%C3%A9non-mapping/cmp/1103905161.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-cm-bilateral-shift-space-and-cylinders": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-cm-bilateral-shift-metric-and-sequential-compactness": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-function-space": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-metric-space": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-bounded-set": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-sup-unique": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-complete-ordered-field": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-abs-value": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-integer-power": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-series": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-geometric-series": "mathematical-premise"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "lem-bounded-bilateral-sequence-ball-is-complete",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "title": "The bounded functions on a set form a complete metric space in the supremum metric, and the coding map of the two-sign shift space is an isometry",
          "dependency_level": 3,
          "deps": [
            "def-bilateral-symbol-and-bounded-sequence-space",
            "lem-cm-bilateral-shift-metric-and-sequential-compactness",
            "lem-sup-metric-is-a-metric",
            "def-metric-space",
            "def-cauchy-in-metric",
