        {
          "id": "lem-coded-quadratic-recurrence-is-a-contraction",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "title": "The square-root recurrence $T_s(x)_n = s_n\\sqrt{a+x_{n-1}+x_{n+1}}$ is a contraction of $B_R$ with a unique coded solution",
          "dependency_level": 4,
          "deps": [
            "def-bilateral-symbol-and-bounded-sequence-space",
            "lem-bounded-bilateral-sequence-ball-is-complete",
            "thm-banach-fixed-point",
            "def-lipschitz-holder-contraction",
            "thm-of-square-roots",
            "lem-of-abs-value",
            "def-abs-value",
            "def-interval",
            "def-complete-ordered-field",
            "def-metric-space",
            "def-metric-convergence"
          ],
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "reference": "mechanical-horseshoe.md#1 (radicand bounds, the derivative bound 1/(2L), and the unique coded sequence)",
          "design_state": "completed-local-argument",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Fix $a\\ge100$ and put\n\n$$R:=\\sqrt a+3,\\qquad L:=\\sqrt{\\,a-2R\\,}.$$\n\nLet $X_{\\pm}$ and $B_R$ be the two-sign shift space and the closed ball of bounded bilateral sequences of [[def-bilateral-symbol-and-bounded-sequence-space]], and for $s\\in X_{\\pm}$ define\n\n$$T_s:B_R\\longrightarrow \\mathbb R^{\\mathbb Z},\\qquad (T_sx)_n:=s_n\\sqrt{\\,a+x_{n-1}+x_{n+1}\\,}\\qquad(n\\in\\mathbb Z).$$\n\nFor a nonzero real $r$, define $\\operatorname{sign}r:=+1$ when $r>0$ and\n$\\operatorname{sign}r:=-1$ when $r<0$. Once clause 2 establishes\n$T_s(B_R)\\subseteq B_R$, its iterates are defined by\n$T_s^0:=\\operatorname{id}_{B_R}$ and $T_s^{m+1}:=T_s\\circ T_s^m$ for\n$m\\in\\mathbb N$.\n\nThen:\n\n1. $a-2R=(\\sqrt a-1)^2-7\\ge74$, so $L\\ge\\sqrt{74}>1$; moreover $a+2R<R^2$, hence $\\sqrt{a+2R}<R$;\n2. for every $s\\in X_{\\pm}$ and $x\\in B_R$ the radicands $a+x_{n-1}+x_{n+1}$ lie in $[a-2R,a+2R]\\subseteq(0,\\infty)$, so $T_sx$ is a well-defined bounded sequence with $\\|T_sx\\|_\\infty\\le\\sqrt{a+2R}<R$; in particular $T_s(B_R)\\subseteq B_R$;\n3. for all $x,y\\in B_R$ and every $s\\in X_{\\pm}$,\n\n$$\\|T_sx-T_sy\\|_\\infty\\le\\frac1L\\,\\|x-y\\|_\\infty,\\qquad \\frac1L<1 ;$$\n\n4. hence $T_s$ has, for each $s\\in X_{\\pm}$, exactly one fixed point $x(s)\\in B_R$, and for every $n\\in\\mathbb Z$\n\n$$\\operatorname{sign}x_n(s)=s_n,\\qquad |x_n(s)|\\ge L,\\qquad x_{n+1}(s)+x_{n-1}(s)=x_n(s)^2-a .$$",
          "strategy": "Positivity of the radicand interval, the Lipschitz bound of the square root on [L^2,a+2R], Banach's fixed point theorem on the complete ball, and the sign/recurrence identities at the fixed point.",
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Ordinary Differential Equations and Dynamical Systems, AMS Graduate Studies in Mathematics 140 (author's preliminary online edition, complete PDF), Section 13.1, contraction and invariant-coding constructions for quadratic horseshoe maps",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-ode/ode.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "R. Devaney and Z. Nitecki, Shift automorphisms in the Hénon mapping, Communications in Mathematical Physics 67 (1979) 137-146, nested-disk coding by a contraction on a compact set",
                "url": "https://projecteuclid.org/journals/communications-in-mathematical-physics/volume-67/issue-2/Shift-automorphisms-in-the-H%C3%A9non-mapping/cmp/1103905161.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "domain": "mathematics",
