            "cor-banach-error-estimates",
            "def-metric-continuity",
            "def-metric-convergence",
            "lem-geometric-sequence-null",
            "def-series",
            "lem-of-abs-value",
            "def-abs-value",
            "lem-of-triangle-inequality",
            "def-lipschitz-holder-contraction",
            "def-metric-space",
            "def-metric-ball",
            "lem-cm-bilateral-shift-metric-and-sequential-compactness"
          ],
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "reference": "mechanical-horseshoe.md#1 (finite-locality of the iterates, error 2R L^{-m}, continuity and injectivity of the coding map)",
          "design_state": "completed-local-argument",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Fix $a\\ge100$ and let $R=\\sqrt a+3$, $L=\\sqrt{a-2R}$, $X_\\pm$, $D_\\pm$ and $B_R$ be as in [[def-bilateral-symbol-and-bounded-sequence-space]] and [[lem-coded-quadratic-recurrence-is-a-contraction]]. Define the **quadratic phase map**\n\n$$F:\\mathbb R^2\\longrightarrow\\mathbb R^2,\\qquad F(x,y):=(y,\\;y^2-a-x),$$\n\nand for each $s\\in X_\\pm$ let $x(s)$ be the unique fixed point of $T_s$ in $B_R$. Define the **coding map**\n\n$$h:X_\\pm\\longrightarrow\\mathbb R^2,\\qquad h(s):=\\bigl(x_{-1}(s),\\,x_0(s)\\bigr).$$\n\nThen:\n\n1. $F$ is a bijection with $F^{-1}(x,y)=(x^2-a-y,\\,x)$, and for every $s\\in X_\\pm$ and $n\\in\\mathbb Z$\n\n$$F\\bigl(x_{n-1}(s),x_n(s)\\bigr)=\\bigl(x_n(s),x_{n+1}(s)\\bigr);$$\n\n2. **(locality)** for all $m\\ge0$, $n\\in\\mathbb Z$ and $s,t\\in X_\\pm$: if $s_j=t_j$ for all $j$ with $|j-n|\\le m-1$, then $\\bigl(T_s^m0\\bigr)_n=\\bigl(T_t^m0\\bigr)_n$, where $T_s^m$ is the $m$-fold iterate and $0$ the zero sequence;\n3. **(uniform error)** for all $m\\ge0$ and $s\\in X_\\pm$,\n\n$$\\bigl\\|T_s^m0-x(s)\\bigr\\|_\\infty\\le 2R\\,L^{-m};$$\n\n4. **(coding continuity)** if $s,t\\in X_\\pm$ agree at every coordinate $j$ with $|j|\\le m$, then $|x_n(s)-x_n(t)|\\le4R\\,L^{-m}$ for $n\\in\\{-1,0\\}$, and consequently\n\n$$\\bigl\\|h(s)-h(t)\\bigr\\|_2\\le4\\sqrt2\\,R\\,L^{-m};$$\n\nin particular $h$ is continuous at every $s\\in X_\\pm$ ([[def-metric-continuity]]) when $X_\\pm$ carries $D_\\pm$ and $\\mathbb R^2$ the Euclidean metric;\n\n5. **(injectivity)** $h$ is injective.",
          "strategy": "Induction on m for the window dependence, the Banach a priori error estimate for the uniform tail bound, and the inverse-map sign argument for injectivity.",
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Ordinary Differential Equations and Dynamical Systems, AMS Graduate Studies in Mathematics 140 (author's preliminary online edition, complete PDF), Section 11.5, the proof that the itinerary map for the tent map is a homeomorphism, and Lemma 11.15",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-ode/ode.pdf"
              },
