            "lem-of-square-monotone",
            "thm-geometric-series",
            "lem-geometric-sequence-null"
          ],
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "reference": "mechanical-horseshoe.md#1 (constant codes, finite-word deviations and their homoclinic limits)",
          "design_state": "completed-local-argument",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Fix $a\\ge100$, let $R=\\sqrt a+3$, $L=\\sqrt{a-2R}$, let $x(s)$ and $h$ be the coded sequence and coding map of [[def-bilateral-symbol-and-bounded-sequence-space]], [[lem-coded-quadratic-recurrence-is-a-contraction]] and [[lem-symbol-locality-gives-coding-continuity]], and let $F(x,y)=(y,y^2-a-x)$. For $u\\in\\{-1,+1\\}$ write $\\bar u\\in X_\\pm$ for the constant code $\\bar u_n:=u$, and put\n\n$$r_u:=1+u\\sqrt{a+1},$$\n\nso that $r_+>0>r_-$, and write $W^s,W^u$ for the stable and unstable sets of [[def-stable-unstable-cones-and-line-slopes]]. Then:\n\n1. $x_n(\\bar u)=r_u$ for every $n$, and $r_u^2=a+2r_u$; consequently $h(\\bar u)=(r_u,r_u)$ is a fixed point of $F$;\n2. if $s\\in X_\\pm$ satisfies $s_n=u$ for all $|n|\\ge N$ for some $N\\ge0$, then\n\n$$F^n\\bigl(h(s)\\bigr)\\longrightarrow(r_u,r_u)\\quad\\text{as }n\\to+\\infty\\quad\\text{and as }n\\to-\\infty ;$$\n\n3. if moreover $s$ is not the constant code $\\bar u$, then $h(s)\\ne(r_u,r_u)$, $F^n(h(s))\\ne(r_u,r_u)$ for every $n\\in\\mathbb Z$, and $h(s)\\in W^s(r_u,r_u)\\cap W^u(r_u,r_u)$; hence $h(s)$ is a homoclinic point of the fixed point $(r_u,r_u)$;\n4. distinct codes $s\\ne t$ of the kind in clause 2 give distinct points $h(s)\\ne h(t)$; in particular the finite-word deviations from the two constant codes produce infinitely many distinct homoclinic points.",
          "strategy": "Constant codes are fixed by the sign-preserving square-root recurrence; the finite-word deviation has constant tails, and the locality estimate forces convergence of the coded orbit to the corresponding constant fixed point in both time directions.",
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-bilateral-symbol-and-bounded-sequence-space": "mathematical-premise",
