            "def-metric-compactness-variants",
            "def-metric-compactness",
            "def-countable-choice",
            "def-dependent-choice",
            "thm-geometric-series",
            "lem-geometric-sequence-null",
            "def-series",
            "def-abs-value",
            "lem-of-abs-value",
            "def-metric-space",
            "def-continuity-real",
            "thm-of-square-roots",
            "def-metric-ball",
            "def-interval",
            "def-lipschitz-holder-contraction"
          ],
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "reference": "mechanical-horseshoe.md#4 (the perturbed horseshoe, coding, chaos transfer, cones and transversality)",
          "design_state": "completed-local-argument",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Fix $a\\ge100$ and put\n\n$$R:=\\sqrt a+3,\\qquad l:=\\sqrt a-3\\ge7,\\qquad \\mathcal Q:=[-R-1,R+1]^2,\\qquad \\Sigma(x,y):=(y,x).$$\n\nLet $C=C(a,R)$ be the constant of [[lem-perturbed-scalar-recurrence-root-bounds]], let $0<\\varepsilon\\le1/6$ with $\\eta:=C\\varepsilon\\le1$, and let $U\\subseteq\\mathbb R^2$ be open with $\\mathcal Q\\subseteq U$. Let $G=(A,B):U\\to\\mathbb R^2$ be a $C^2$ diffeomorphism onto its image whose components satisfy, on $\\mathcal Q$,\n\n$$|A(x,y)-y|\\le\\varepsilon,\\quad |\\partial_xA(x,y)|\\le\\varepsilon,\\quad |\\partial_yA(x,y)-1|\\le\\varepsilon,$$\n\n$$|B(x,y)-(y^2-a-x)|\\le\\varepsilon,\\quad |\\partial_xB(x,y)+1|\\le\\varepsilon,\\quad |\\partial_yB(x,y)-2y|\\le\\varepsilon,$$\n\nand assume in addition that $H:=\\Sigma\\circ G^{-1}\\circ\\Sigma$ is defined and of class $C^2$ on a neighbourhood of $\\mathcal Q$ and satisfies the same six inequalities on $\\mathcal Q$ with the same constant $\\varepsilon$. For each sign $u$ let $M_u$ be the root map of [[lem-perturbed-scalar-recurrence-root-bounds]] applied to $G$, let $V$ be the inverse branch of [[lem-close-map-first-component-has-uniform-inverse]], and let $M^H_u,V^H$ be the corresponding objects for $H$.\n\nFor a nonzero real $x$, write $\\operatorname{sign}x:=+1$ if $x>0$ and\n$\\operatorname{sign}x:=-1$ if $x<0$; the sequence coordinates used below are\nnonzero because their absolute values are at least $l\\ge7$. Then:\n\n1. **(coding)** for every $s\\in X_\\pm$ there is exactly one $q(s)\\in B_R$ with $q_n(s)=M_{s_n}\\bigl(q_{n-1}(s),q_{n+1}(s)\\bigr)$ for all $n\\in\\mathbb Z$; it satisfies $l\\le|q_n(s)|\\le R$, $\\operatorname{sign}q_n(s)=s_n$ and $R-|q_n(s)|\\ge\\tfrac34$, $|q_n(s)|-l\\ge\\tfrac34$; setting $v_n(s):=V(q_n(s),q_{n+1}(s))$ and\n\n$$z_n(s):=\\bigl(q_n(s),v_n(s)\\bigr),\\qquad h_G(s):=z_0(s)=\\bigl(q_0(s),V(q_0(s),q_1(s))\\bigr),$$\n\none has $G(z_n(s))=z_{n+1}(s)$ for all $n$;\n2. **(conjugacy and chaos)** $h_G$ is a continuous bijection of $(X_\\pm,D_\\pm)$ onto $\\Lambda_G:=h_G(X_\\pm)$; granting the Axiom of Countable Choice (used once through the equivalence between closed and sequentially closed subsets of $\\mathbb R^2$), it is a homeomorphism, and $G\\circ h_G=h_G\\circ S_\\pm$, so $\\Lambda_G$ is $G$-invariant. The set $\\Lambda_G$ is sequentially compact and is compact under $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega+\\mathrm{DC}$. Under $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$, $G|_{\\Lambda_G}$ is continuous, topologically mixing, and has dense periodic points; it is sensitive with sensitivity constant $2l$. Hence under $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ it is chaotic in the stated sense.\n3. **(fixed points)** for each sign $u$ the constant code $\\bar u$ gives a fixed point $z_{\\bar u}:=h_G(\\bar u)=\\bigl(\\rho_u,V(\\rho_u,\\rho_u)\\bigr)$, where $\\rho_u=M_u(\\rho_u,\\rho_u)$ is the unique element of $u\\,[l,R]$ with $\\rho_u=M_u(\\rho_u,\\rho_u)$; these two fixed points are hyperbolic;\n4. **(transverse homoclinic points)** let $s\\in X_\\pm$ be nonconstant with $s_n=u$ for $|n|\\ge N$. Then $z_*:=h_G(s)\\ne z_{\\bar u}$, and there are $C^1$ curves $\\gamma_s,\\gamma_u:(-\\varepsilon_0,\\varepsilon_0)\\to\\mathbb R^2$ with $\\gamma_s(0)=\\gamma_u(0)=z_*$, $\\gamma_s\\bigl((-\\varepsilon_0,\\varepsilon_0)\\bigr)\\subseteq W^s_G(z_{\\bar u})$, $\\gamma_u\\bigl((-\\varepsilon_0,\\varepsilon_0)\\bigr)\\subseteq W^u_G(z_{\\bar u})$, tangent vectors $\\gamma_s'(0)\\in C^s_{3/4}$, $\\gamma_u'(0)\\in C^u_{3/4}$; since $C^s_{3/4}\\cap C^u_{3/4}=\\{0\\}$ the tangent lines are distinct, so $z_*$ is a transverse homoclinic point of $z_{\\bar u}$ ([[def-stable-unstable-cones-and-line-slopes]]).",
          "strategy": "Contraction of the perturbed recurrence with factor 2d<1, finite-locality of the coding map and sign separation for sensitivity, the weighted half-tail lemma for the C^1 curves, the slope bound |d_0|<=2/3 for tangents in complementary cones, and hyperbolicity from closeness of the differential to DF at the constant codes.",
          "sources": {
