        {
          "id": "thm-smooth-fixed-mass-mechanical-horseshoe",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "title": "A smooth periodic one-degree-of-freedom oscillator with polynomial pulse forcing has stroboscopic chaos and a transverse homoclinic point",
          "dependency_level": 6,
          "deps": [
            "def-smooth-periodic-oscillator-pulse-model",
            "lem-rescaled-pulse-map-is-c-one-close-to-kick",
            "thm-explicit-perturbed-horseshoe-and-transversality",
            "def-bilateral-symbol-and-bounded-sequence-space",
            "def-stable-unstable-cones-and-line-slopes",
            "def-cm-topologically-mixing-dense-periodic-and-sensitive-maps",
            "def-metric-continuity",
            "def-metric-convergence",
            "def-abs-value",
            "def-countable-choice",
            "def-dependent-choice"
          ],
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "reference": "mechanical-horseshoe.md#5 (the smooth fixed-mass realization and its chaos conclusions)",
          "design_state": "completed-local-argument",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Grant the Axioms of Countable and Dependent Choice ([[def-countable-choice]], [[def-dependent-choice]]), inherited from the compactness and homeomorphism clauses of [[thm-explicit-perturbed-horseshoe-and-transversality]]. Fix $a\\ge100$, let $w$, $\\beta_\\delta$, $P=\\pi/2+\\delta$ and the stroboscopic map $G_\\delta$ be as in [[def-smooth-periodic-oscillator-pulse-model]], and let $X_\\pm$, $S_\\pm$, $D_\\pm$ be the two-sign shift space of [[def-bilateral-symbol-and-bounded-sequence-space]]. Then there is $\\delta_0>0$, depending only on $a$ and $w$, such that for every $0<\\delta<\\delta_0$:\n\n1. there is a function $h_\\delta:X_\\pm\\to\\mathbb R^2$ that is a homeomorphism of $(X_\\pm,D_\\pm)$ onto a compact subset $\\Lambda_\\delta:=h_\\delta(X_\\pm)$ of $\\mathbb R^2$ and satisfies $G_\\delta\\circ h_\\delta=h_\\delta\\circ S_\\pm$; in particular $\\Lambda_\\delta$ is compact and $G_\\delta$-invariant, and $G_\\delta|_{\\Lambda_\\delta}$ is conjugate to the shift;\n2. $G_\\delta|_{\\Lambda_\\delta}$ is continuous, topologically mixing, has dense periodic points and is sensitive with a positive constant; hence it is chaotic in the stated sense ([[def-cm-topologically-mixing-dense-periodic-and-sensitive-maps]]);\n3. the two constant codes give two hyperbolic fixed points of $G_\\delta$, one of each sign;\n4. for every nonconstant code $s\\in X_\\pm$ that is constant outside a finite set, the point $h_\\delta(s)$ is a transverse homoclinic point of the corresponding fixed point, and distinct such codes give distinct points ([[def-stable-unstable-cones-and-line-slopes]]).\n\nAll statements are about the explicit smooth $P$-periodic ordinary differential equation $q''=-q+\\beta_\\delta(t)(q^2-a)$ and its time-$P$ map; no empirical claim, measurement or physical assumption occurs.",
          "strategy": "Choose delta below the explicit bounds of the pulse approximation lemma so that the closeness hypotheses of the perturbed horseshoe theorem are met, and apply that theorem to G_delta.",
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Ordinary Differential Equations and Dynamical Systems, AMS Graduate Studies in Mathematics 140 (author's preliminary online edition, complete PDF), Sections 13.1-13.3, the Smale horseshoe and periodically forced planar systems",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-ode/ode.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "P. Cvitanović, R. Artuso, R. Mainieri, G. Tanner, G. Vattay, Chaos: Classical and Quantum (ChaosBook.org, edition 17.6.8, complete PDF), Chapter 15 Section 15.2, the complete Hénon horseshoe and its persistence",
                "url": "https://chaosbook.org/chapters/ChaosBook.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "R. Devaney and Z. Nitecki, Shift automorphisms in the Hénon mapping, Communications in Mathematical Physics 67 (1979) 137-146, hyperbolic invariant sets of quadratic area-preserving maps",
                "url": "https://projecteuclid.org/journals/communications-in-mathematical-physics/volume-67/issue-2/Shift-automorphisms-in-the-H%C3%A9non-mapping/cmp/1103905161.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-smooth-periodic-oscillator-pulse-model": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-rescaled-pulse-map-is-c-one-close-to-kick": "mathematical-premise",
