        {
          "id": "ex-cm-chaos-perturbed-root-and-margin-checks",
          "kind": "example",
          "title": "Explicit root margins at $a=100$: endpoint signs $25$ and $43$, and $d=2/13$ for $\\eta=1$",
          "dependency_level": 5,
          "deps": [
            "lem-close-map-first-component-has-uniform-inverse",
            "lem-perturbed-scalar-recurrence-root-bounds",
            "def-bilateral-symbol-and-bounded-sequence-space",
            "thm-of-square-roots",
            "def-abs-value",
            "lem-of-abs-value",
            "def-interval"
          ],
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-generated",
            "proof": "ai-generated"
          },
          "generation": {
            "role": "example"
          },
          "reference": "mechanical-horseshoe.md#4 (worked root bounds at the explicit parameter a=100)",
          "design_state": "completed-local-example",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Take $a=100$ in [[lem-perturbed-scalar-recurrence-root-bounds]], so that $R=13$, $l=7$, and suppose the defect bound is $\\eta=1$. Then:\n\n1. for all $u,w\\in[-13,13]$ the unperturbed quadratic $v^2-100-u-w$ satisfies\n\n$$v^2-100-u-w\\Big|_{v=7}\\le49-100+26=-25,\\qquad v^2-100-u-w\\Big|_{v=13}\\ge169-100-26=43,$$\n\nso the signs at the endpoints are strictly opposite with margins $25$ and $43$;\n2. the derivative bound is $d=(1+\\eta)/(2l-\\eta)=(1+1)/(14-1)=2/13$, and\n\n$$2d=\\frac4{13}<1,\\qquad d\\Bigl(\\frac12+2\\Bigr)=\\frac5{13}<1,\\qquad \\frac d{1-d/2}=\\frac{2/13}{12/13}=\\frac16<\\frac23;$$\n\n3. the root margins are at least $24/27>3/4$ and $42/27>3/4$, since the slope of $P_{u,w}$ is bounded by $2R+\\eta=27$ on $[7,13]$.",
          "strategy": "Direct evaluation of the endpoint forms and the margin inequalities at the explicit constants.",
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "R. Devaney and Z. Nitecki, Shift automorphisms in the Hénon mapping, Communications in Mathematical Physics 67 (1979) 137-146, quadratic root location in the horseshoe region",
                "url": "https://projecteuclid.org/journals/communications-in-mathematical-physics/volume-67/issue-2/Shift-automorphisms-in-the-H%C3%A9non-mapping/cmp/1103905161.pdf"
              },
