          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Let $X$ be a real vector space ([[def-vector-space]]) with a norm $\\|\\cdot\\|$ ([[def-norm-and-normed-space]]) whose metric $d(x,y):=\\|x-y\\|$ is complete ([[def-complete-metric-space]]). Let $a<b$ be reals ([[def-interval]]) and let $g:[a,b]\\to X$ be continuous ([[def-metric-continuity]]). For endpoints $c,d\\in[a,b]$, set $\\int_c^c g:=0_X$ and, when $c>d$, set $\\int_c^d g:=-\\int_d^c g$; for $c<d$ use the Riemann-sum construction below on the restriction to $[c,d]$. Then:\n\n1. **Integral.** For every sequence of tagged partitions of $[a,b]$ whose mesh tends to $0$, the Riemann sums $\\sum_i(t_{i+1}-t_i)\\,g(s_i)$ converge in $X$; the limit, written $\\int_a^b g$, is independent of the sequence, and\n$$\\Bigl\\|\\int_a^b g\\Bigr\\|\\;\\le\\;(b-a)\\sup_{t\\in[a,b]}\\|g(t)\\| .$$\n2. **Fundamental theorem.** The curve $G:[a,b]\\to X$, $G(t):=\\int_a^t g$, is well defined, satisfies $\\|G(t)-G(s)\\|\\le(t-s)\\sup_{[s,t]}\\|g\\|$ for $a\\le s\\le t\\le b$, and is differentiable with $G'=g$ on $[a,b]$ in the one-sided sense at the endpoints.\n3. **Linearity.** For continuous $g,h:[a,b]\\to X$ and reals $\\alpha,\\beta$: $\\int_a^b(\\alpha g+\\beta h)=\\alpha\\int_a^b g+\\beta\\int_a^b h$; and for $a\\le c\\le b$, $\\int_a^b g=\\int_a^c g+\\int_c^b g$.\n4. **Bounded linear images.** If $Y$ is a normed real vector space and $T:X\\to Y$ is linear with $\\|Tx\\|\\le C\\|x\\|$ for some $C<+\\infty$ and all $x$, then $T\\circ g$ is continuous and $T\\bigl(\\int_a^b g\\bigr)=\\int_a^b (T\\circ g)$; in particular, for every real-linear functional $\\Lambda:X\\to\\mathbb R$ with $|\\Lambda x|\\le C\\|x\\|$, $\\Lambda\\bigl(\\int_a^b g\\bigr)=\\int_a^b\\Lambda\\circ g$.",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
