          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "**Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice** $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ ([[def-countable-choice]]), used through the two lattice and embedding suppliers quoted below. Use the scalar and vector spaces and weights of [[def-periodic-vector-sobolev-space-and-leray-projection]]. For scalar $a,b$ put $ab$ equal to ordinary multiplication; for scalar $a$ and vector $v$ put $av=(av_1,av_2,av_3)$; for vectors $v,z$ put $vz=(v_1z_1,v_2z_2,v_3z_3)$ (componentwise product). These products extend complex-bilinearly to coefficients and satisfy $|ab|\\le|a||b|$, with Euclidean norm for vectors and absolute value for scalars. The output is scalar only for two scalar inputs, and vector otherwise. The convolution for the same typed products is $(a*b)(k):=\\sum_l a(l)b(k-l)$ whenever the sum is absolutely convergent. In claim 3, $f,g$ are vector fields and $f\\cdot\\nabla$ denotes the explicitly displayed scalar-component action, not componentwise vector multiplication.\n\n1. **Discrete Young.** Let $a\\in\\ell^1(\\mathbb Z^3;\\mathbb C)$, $b\\in\\ell^2(\\mathbb Z^3;\\mathbb C)$ and define $(a*b)(k):=\\sum_{l\\in\\mathbb Z^3}a(k-l)b(l)$. The sum converges absolutely, and\n$$\\|a*b\\|_{\\ell^2}\\;\\le\\;\\|a\\|_{\\ell^1}\\|b\\|_{\\ell^2}.$$\n2. **Sobolev product.** Let $\\sigma>3/2$ and let $f,g$ each belong to its scalar or vector $H^\\sigma$. Then the pointwise product $fg$ of the continuous representatives ([[lem-fourier-lattice-sobolev-embedding]]) belongs to $H^\\sigma$, and with $W_\\sigma=(\\sum_kw_k^{-2\\sigma})^{1/2}$ of [[lem-cm-lattice-shell-count-and-weight-sums]],\n$$\\|fg\\|_{H^\\sigma}\\;\\le\\;C_\\sigma\\|f\\|_{H^\\sigma}\\|g\\|_{H^\\sigma},\\qquad C_\\sigma:=2^\\sigma W_\\sigma .$$\n3. **Transport product.** Let $\\sigma>3/2$, $f\\in H^\\sigma$ and $g\\in H^{\\sigma+1}$. Then $(f\\cdot\\nabla)g:=\\sum_{j=1}^{3}f_j\\,\\partial_jg$ belongs to $H^\\sigma$ and\n$$\\|(f\\cdot\\nabla)g\\|_{H^\\sigma}\\;\\le\\;3C_\\sigma\\|f\\|_{H^\\sigma}\\|g\\|_{H^{\\sigma+1}}.$$",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
