          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "**Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice** $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ ([[def-countable-choice]]). Fix $N\\ge1$, $\\nu\\ge0$, a real $s>5/2$, and $u_0\\in H^s_\\sigma$ with $Y_0=\\|u_0\\|_{H^s}$, and let $T$ and $u_N:[0,T]\\to X_N$ be as in [[lem-fluid-energy-common-lifespan]]. For every real $m\\ge s$ with $\\|u_0\\|_{H^m}<+\\infty$ define\n$$B_m:=\\|u_0\\|_{H^m}\\,e^{4C_mY_0T},\\qquad B_m':=\\nu B_m+3C_{m-2}B_{m-1}^2 ,$$\nwhere $C_m$ is the commutator constant of [[lem-tame-transport-commutator]] and $3C_{m-2}$ is the product constant of [[lem-discrete-young-and-sobolev-product]] at order $m-2$ (so that $B_m'$ is defined for $m>7/2$). For lower orders $0\\le r<s$ set $B_r:=B_s$; then $\\|u_N(t)\\|_{H^r}\\le B_r$ follows from monotonicity of the weights and the base bound. At any order where an initial norm is infinite, take $B_r=+\\infty$ and the corresponding $B_r\\prime=+\\infty$ by convention, reading the estimate as an extended upper bound. Then for $0\\le t\\le T$:\n\n1. $\\|u_N(t)\\|_{H^m}\\le B_m$ for every real $m\\ge s$; in particular all bounds hold on the single interval $[0,T]$ whose length depends only on $Y_0$ and $s$, uniformly in $N$.\n2. $\\|u_N'(t)\\|_{H^{m-2}}\\le B_m'$ for every real $m>7/2$; in particular, for the integer orders of the main theorem ($s\\ge4$, $m\\ge s$) these are the uniform-in-$N$ bounds on $L^\\infty(0,T;H^m)$ and $L^\\infty(0,T;H^{m-2})$ of the Galerkin approximations.",
