          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "**Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice** $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $\\nu\\ge0$, let $T>0$, and let $u:[0,T]\\to\\bigcap_{p\\in\\mathbb R}H^p(\\mathbb T^3;\\mathbb R^3)$ be a curve such that, in the notation of [[def-periodic-vector-sobolev-space-and-leray-projection]]:\n\n1. for every real $p$, $t\\mapsto u(t)$ is continuous into $H^p$;\n2. for every real $p$, $t\\mapsto u(t)$ is differentiable into $H^p$, with\n$$u'(t)=\\nu\\Delta u(t)-P\\bigl((u(t)\\cdot\\nabla)u(t)\\bigr)\\qquad(0\\le t\\le T),$$\nthe right-hand side being an element of $H^p$ for every $p$ (which follows from the other hypotheses as below);\n3. $u(t)$ is divergence-free and real for every $t$.\n\nThen the map $(t,x)\\mapsto u(t,x)$ belongs to $C^\\infty([0,T]\\times\\mathbb T^3;\\mathbb R^3)$ (with one-sided time derivatives at the endpoints), and for all $r\\ge0$ and every multi-index $\\alpha$ the derivative $\\partial_t^r\\partial_x^\\alpha u$ is the one obtained from the right-hand side of the equation by the formal product rule and differentiation under $P$, $\\nabla$ and $\\Delta$.",
