          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "**Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice** $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $s\\ge4$ be an integer, let $\\nu\\ge0$, and let $u_0\\in H^s_\\sigma(\\mathbb T^3;\\mathbb R^3)\\cap C^\\infty(\\mathbb T^3;\\mathbb R^3)$ be a smooth divergence-free field (so that $\\|u_0\\|_{H^m}<+\\infty$ for every $m$). Let $Y_0:=\\|u_0\\|_{H^s}$, let $C_s$ be the commutator constant of [[lem-tame-transport-commutator]], and set\n$$T:=\\begin{cases}(2C_sY_0)^{-1},&Y_0>0,\\\\ 1,&Y_0=0.\\end{cases}$$\nThen there exists a field $u\\in C^\\infty([0,T]\\times\\mathbb T^3;\\mathbb R^3)$ such that:\n\n1. $u(0,\\cdot)=u_0$; for every real $m\\ge s$ the identity\n$$\\partial_tu+P\\bigl((u\\cdot\\nabla)u\\bigr)=\\nu\\Delta u$$\nholds in $C([0,T],H^{m-2})$ (hence pointwise on the strip after the smoothness conclusion), where $P$ is the Leray projection of [[def-periodic-vector-sobolev-space-and-leray-projection]]; the identities $\\operatorname{div}u=0$ and $\\int_{\\mathbb T^3}u(t,x)\\,dx=\\int_{\\mathbb T^3}u_0(x)\\,dx$ hold for all $t$;\n2. for every real $m\\ge s$ the uniform bound $\\sup_{0\\le t\\le T}\\|u(t)\\|_{H^m}\\le B_m:=\\|u_0\\|_{H^m}e^{4C_mY_0T}$ holds, where $C_m$ is the commutator constant of order $m$;\n3. if $Y_0=0$ then $u_0=0$ and $u\\equiv0$. The existence time $T$ depends only on the single number $Y_0=\\|u_0\\|_{H^s}$ (and on $s$), not on the finer profile of $u_0$; the case $\\nu=0$ is the periodic incompressible Euler model and $\\nu>0$ the constant-viscosity Navier-Stokes model.",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
