        },
        {
          "id": "thm-fluid-uniqueness-and-continuous-dependence",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Uniqueness of smooth periodic solutions and continuous dependence in $H^{s-1}$ on the common local interval",
          "reference": "local-fluid-wellposedness.md (E30)",
          "design_state": "completed-local-argument; recorded in the batch notes",
          "dependency_level": 8,
          "deps": [
            "def-periodic-vector-sobolev-space-and-leray-projection",
            "lem-fourier-lattice-sobolev-embedding",
            "lem-discrete-young-and-sobolev-product",
            "lem-tame-transport-commutator",
            "thm-local-smooth-periodic-euler-viscous-solution",
            "def-countable-choice",
            "thm-gronwall-integral-inequality",
            "thm-holder-finite-real-exponents",
            "thm-linearity-of-the-lebesgue-integral-on-l-one",
            "def-integral-over-a-measurable-set"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-periodic-vector-sobolev-space-and-leray-projection": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-fourier-lattice-sobolev-embedding": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-discrete-young-and-sobolev-product": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-tame-transport-commutator": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-local-smooth-periodic-euler-viscous-solution": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-gronwall-integral-inequality": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-holder-finite-real-exponents": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-linearity-of-the-lebesgue-integral-on-l-one": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-integral-over-a-measurable-set": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "**Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice** $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $s\\ge4$ be an integer, $\\nu\\ge0$, and let $B>0$ with $T:=(2C_sB)^{-1}$, where $C_s$ is the commutator constant of [[lem-tame-transport-commutator]]. Let $u_0,v_0\\in H^s_\\sigma(\\mathbb T^3;\\mathbb R^3)\\cap C^\\infty(\\mathbb T^3;\\mathbb R^3)$ be smooth divergence-free data with $\\|u_0\\|_{H^s}\\le B$ and $\\|v_0\\|_{H^s}\\le B$, and let $u,v\\in C^\\infty([0,T]\\times\\mathbb T^3;\\mathbb R^3)$ be the corresponding smooth solutions of the projected equation $\\partial_tu+P((u\\cdot\\nabla)u)=\\nu\\Delta u$ given by [[thm-local-smooth-periodic-euler-viscous-solution]] (each nonzero datum has lifespan at least $T$ by its norm bound; for a zero datum use the explicit solution $z\\equiv0$ on $[0,T]$, even when $T>1$).\n\n1. **Uniqueness.** If $u(0)=v(0)$, then $u=v$ on $[0,T]$.\n2. **Stability in $L^2$.** With $w:=u-v$ and $\\Theta:=\\sup_{0\\le t\\le T}\\||\\nabla v(t)|\\|_{L^\\infty}\\le6W_{s-1}B$, where $|\\nabla v|=(\\sum_j|\\partial_jv|^2)^{1/2}$ ([[lem-fourier-lattice-sobolev-embedding]]),\n$$\\|w(t)\\|_{L^2}\\le e^{\\Theta t}\\|w(0)\\|_{L^2}\\qquad(0\\le t\\le T).$$\n3. **Continuous dependence in $H^{s-1}$.** There is a finite constant $K=K(s,B,T,\\nu)$ such that\n$$\\sup_{0\\le t\\le T}\\|u(t)-v(t)\\|_{H^{s-1}}\\;\\le\\;K\\,\\|u_0-v_0\\|_{L^2}^{1/s}.$$\nIn particular the solution map $u_0\\mapsto u$ is continuous from the bounded set $\\{\\|u_0\\|_{H^s}\\le B\\}$ with the $L^2$-topology into $C([0,T],H^{s-1})$.",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "E. Wiedemann (ed. J. Skipper), Lecture Notes: Navier-Stokes Equations (Universität Ulm, WS 2018/19), Section 4.2 and Theorem 4.11 (energy estimates for differences of solutions; uniqueness and stability of strong solutions)",
                "url": "https://www.uni-ulm.de/fileadmin/website_uni_ulm/mawi.inst.020/skipper/NSEEmilFinished.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "A. J. Majda and A. L. Bertozzi, Vorticity and Incompressible Flow (CUP 2002), Proposition 3.1, Corollary 3.1 and Lemma 3.8 (the basic energy estimate, uniqueness of solutions, and interpolation in Sobolev spaces)",
                "url": "http://inis.jinr.ru/sl/P_Physics/PC_Classical%20physics/PCfm_Fluid%20mechanics/Majda,%20Bertozzi.%20Vorticity%20and%20incompressible%20flow%20(CUP,%202002)(558s).pdf"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
