    {
      "id": "cm-math-rotation-double-cover",
      "title": "Rotation Double Cover",
      "category": "non-relativistic-classical-mechanics-mathematics",
      "library": "mathematics",
      "companion": "cm-math-rotation-double-cover-examples",
      "kind": "A",
      "requires": [
        "cm-math-dynamics",
        "lie-subgroups-actions-and-homogeneous-spaces",
        "cm-math-geometry",
        "cm-math-balances"
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "def-cm-quaternion-rotation-map-and-cover",
          "kind": "definition",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "The quaternion rotation map $\\rho$: conjugation on the imaginary quaternions, the unit sphere $S^3$, and quaternion lifts",
          "statement": "Let $\\mathbb H$ be the quaternion algebra with its product, conjugation $x\\mapsto\\bar x$, real-valued norm $N:\\mathbb H\\to\\mathbb R$, and real embedding $r\\mapsto\\hat r=(r,0,0,0)$, in the notation of [[def-quaternions]]. Thus $x=x_0+x_1i+x_2j+x_3k$ with the multiplication formula of [[def-quaternions]], and\n\n$$N(x)=x_0^2+x_1^2+x_2^2+x_3^2,\\qquad \\widehat{N(x)}=x\\bar x=\\bar x x.$$\n\nIn particular, $N(x)>0$ for $x\\ne0$, and the imported division-ring theorem gives the typed inverse formula $x^{-1}=\\widehat{N(x)^{-1}}\\,\\bar x$ ([[thm-quaternions-form-a-division-ring]]). Under the identification of $\\mathbb H$ with $\\mathbb R^4$ by the coordinates $x_0,\\dots,x_3$ one has $N(x)=\\|x\\|_2^2$ for the Euclidean norm of [[def-euclidean-inner-product]].\n\n**Imaginary quaternions and the vector identification.** Put\n\n$$\\operatorname{Im}\\mathbb H:=\\{x\\in\\mathbb H:\\bar x=-x\\}=\\mathbb Ri\\oplus\\mathbb Rj\\oplus\\mathbb Rk,\\qquad \\varphi:\\mathbb R^3\\to\\operatorname{Im}\\mathbb H,\\quad \\varphi(v_1,v_2,v_3):=v_1i+v_2j+v_3k .$$\n\nThen $\\varphi$ is a linear isomorphism with $N(\\varphi(v))=\\|v\\|_2^2$ for every $v\\in\\mathbb R^3$. Throughout the collection, $\\varphi$ translates between vectors of $\\mathbb R^3$ (their inner product $\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_2$, norm $\\|\\cdot\\|_2$ and cross product) and imaginary quaternions inside quaternion products.\n\n**The unit sphere.** Define\n\n$$S^3:=\\{q\\in\\mathbb H:N(q)=1\\},$$\n\nthe unit sphere of $\\mathbb H\\cong\\mathbb R^4$. The identification of $S^3$ with $SU(2)$ is the one of the published covering example `ex-su-two-to-so-three-as-a-covering-homomorphism`, which is also the source of the covering statement recorded in the second remark below; that example is linked from the page summary of this pair.\n\n**Conjugation and the rotation map.** For $q\\in\\mathbb H$ with $q\\ne0$ let $c_q:\\mathbb H\\to\\mathbb H$ be\n\n$$c_q(x):=qxq^{-1}=qx\\,\\widehat{N(q)^{-1}}\\,\\bar q,$$\n\nwhere the real scalar is embedded by $r\\mapsto\\hat r$, and define\n\n$$\\rho(q):=c_q|_{\\operatorname{Im}\\mathbb H}:\\operatorname{Im}\\mathbb H\\longrightarrow\\operatorname{Im}\\mathbb H .$$\n\nBoth the $\\mathbb R$-linear map $\\rho(q)$ and its matrix in the ordered basis $(i,j,k)$ of $\\operatorname{Im}\\mathbb H$ are written $\\rho(q)$; the equality $\\rho(q)\\in SO(3)$ for $q\\in S^3$ is part of the cited covering statement, and the matrix is the one meant whenever $\\rho(q)$ is composed with the identifications above. The map $\\rho$ itself is never linear in $q$ and no such structure is used.\n\n**Quaternion lifts.** Let $I\\subseteq\\mathbb R$ be an interval and let $R:I\\to SO(3)$ be a map, with $SO(3)$ as in [[def-cm-special-orthogonal-group]]. A **quaternion lift** of $R$ is a map $q:I\\to S^3$ with $\\rho(q(t))=R(t)$ for every $t\\in I$.",
          "deps": [
            "def-quaternions",
            "thm-quaternions-form-a-division-ring",
            "def-cm-special-orthogonal-group",
            "ex-su-two-to-so-three-as-a-covering-homomorphism",
            "def-euclidean-inner-product",
            "def-countable-choice"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-quaternions": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-quaternions-form-a-division-ring": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-cm-special-orthogonal-group": "mathematical-premise",
            "ex-su-two-to-so-three-as-a-covering-homomorphism": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-euclidean-inner-product": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "not-applicable"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "P. Etingof, MIT 18.745 Lie Groups and Lie Algebras I (Fall 2020), Exercise 3.9 (conjugation action of SU(2) on traceless Hermitian matrices and the covering SU(2) -> SO(3)), printed page 26, and Proposition 6.7 (unit quaternions are isomorphic to SU(2)), printed page 40",
