        {
          "id": "ex-cm-quaternion-lift-of-a-varying-rate-about-a-fixed-axis",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "A time-varying rate about a fixed axis: $q(t)=q_0\\bigl(\\cos((\\theta(t)-\\theta(0))/2)+\\varphi(\\hat n)\\sin((\\theta(t)-\\theta(0))/2)\\bigr)$ solves the lift equation with $\\omega(t)=\\theta'(t)\\hat n$",
          "statement": "Let $I\\subseteq\\mathbb R$ be a nondegenerate open interval with $0\\in I$, let $\\theta:I\\to\\mathbb R$ be of class $C^1$, let $\\hat n\\in\\mathbb R^3$ be a unit vector, let $q_0\\in S^3$, and define the normalized phase $\\alpha(t):=\\theta(t)-\\theta(0)$ and\n\n$$e(t):=\\cos\\bigl(\\alpha(t)/2\\bigr)+\\varphi(\\hat n)\\sin\\bigl(\\alpha(t)/2\\bigr),\\qquad q(t):=q_0\\,e(t),$$\n\nwith $\\varphi,S^3,\\rho$ as in [[def-cm-quaternion-rotation-map-and-cover]]. Then:\n\n1. $e$ and $q$ are of class $C^1$, they take values in $S^3$, and $q(0)=q_0$.\n2. The curve $q$ solves $q'(t)=\\tfrac12q(t)\\,\\varphi(\\omega(t))$ with $\\omega(t):=\\theta'(t)\\hat n$, on all of $I$.\n3. Consequently $R:=\\rho\\circ q$ is a $C^1$ rotation path whose body angular velocity is $\\omega(t)=\\theta'(t)\\hat n$, and $R(t)=\\rho(q_0)\\rho(e(t))$, where $\\rho(e(t))$ is the rotation about $\\hat n$ through the angle $\\alpha(t)=\\theta(t)-\\theta(0)$.",
          "deps": [
            "def-cm-quaternion-rotation-map-and-cover",
            "lem-cm-quaternion-product-rule-and-conjugation-formula",
            "lem-cm-body-angular-velocity-of-a-rotation-path",
