        {
          "id": "ex-cm-two-to-one-preimages-and-homomorphism-check",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Finite checks of the cover: the half-turn rotations $\\rho(\\pm i),\\rho(\\pm j),\\rho(\\pm k)$, the identity $\\rho(i)\\rho(j)=\\rho(ij)$, and the exact preimages of $\\rho(k)$",
          "statement": "Let $e_1,e_2,e_3$ be the standard basis of $\\mathbb R^3$ and identify $\\mathbb R^3$ with $\\operatorname{Im}\\mathbb H$ through $\\varphi$ as in [[def-cm-quaternion-rotation-map-and-cover]]; matrices of linear maps are taken in the ordered basis $(i,j,k)$. Then:\n\n1. $\\rho(1)$ is the identity matrix and $\\rho(-1)=\\rho(1)$; moreover, if $q\\in S^3$ satisfies $\\rho(q)=I_3$, then $q=\\pm1$.\n2. $\\rho(i),\\rho(j),\\rho(k)$ are the half-turns about the coordinate axes,\n\n$$\\rho(i)=\\begin{pmatrix}1&0&0\\\\0&-1&0\\\\0&0&-1\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad \\rho(j)=\\begin{pmatrix}-1&0&0\\\\0&1&0\\\\0&0&-1\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad \\rho(k)=\\begin{pmatrix}-1&0&0\\\\0&-1&0\\\\0&0&1\\end{pmatrix},$$\n\nand $\\rho(i)\\rho(j)=\\rho(k)=\\rho(ij)$: the homomorphism identity is verified on the generating pair $i,j$ by finite matrix multiplication.\n3. The exact preimages of $\\rho(k)$ in $S^3$ are $\\pm k$: $\\rho(\\pm k)=\\rho(k)$, and every $q\\in S^3$ with $\\rho(q)=\\rho(k)$ satisfies $q=\\pm k$.",
          "deps": [
            "def-cm-quaternion-rotation-map-and-cover",
