        {
          "id": "ex-cm04-harmonic-motion-check",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "A harmonic model on explicit data: the sinusoid, its least period, the conserved energy and the phase ellipse checked at $m=1$, $k=4$",
          "statement": "Declare the harmonic model of [[post-cm04-harmonic-model]] with the data\n$$m=1\\ \\mathrm{kg},\\qquad k=4\\ \\mathrm{N/m}=4\\ \\mathrm{kg/s^{2}},$$\ntime window $\\mathbb R$ and configuration domain $\\mathbb R$, and the datum\nat $t_{0}=0$\n$$x_{0}=0\\ \\mathrm{m},\\qquad v_{0}=1\\ \\mathrm{m/s}.$$\nThe claim checked below is that the curve\n$$x_{\\mathrm{phys}}(t_{\\mathrm{phys}})=\\frac12\\sin\\bigl(2t_{\\mathrm{phys}}/(1\\,\\mathrm s)\\bigr)\\,\\mathrm m\\qquad(t_{\\mathrm{phys}}\\in\\mathbb R)$$\nis the unique maximal motion of the model with this datum, that its least\npositive period is $\\pi$ seconds, that its energy is the constant\n$\\tfrac12$ joule, and that its phase curve is the ellipse\n$$4x^{2}+v^{2}=1$$\nin the numerical SI phase coordinates $x:=x_{\\mathrm{phys}}/(1\\,\\mathrm m)$ and $v:=v_{\\mathrm{phys}}/(1\\,\\mathrm{m/s})$ of [[def-cm04-phase-plane-and-energy-level-sets]]. All coefficient calculations below use these numerical coordinates and $t:=t_{\\mathrm{phys}}/(1\\,\\mathrm s)$; equivalently the physical ellipse is $4(x_{\\mathrm{phys}}/(1\\,\\mathrm m))^2+(v_{\\mathrm{phys}}/(1\\,\\mathrm{m/s}))^2=1$.",
          "strategy": "A worked check: read the harmonic-motion theorem at the declared data m=1, k=4, datum (0,0,1), producing the sinusoid, its amplitude and phase, least period, energy and phase ellipse, with a direct verification of the energy identity.",
          "deps": [
            "post-cm04-harmonic-model",
            "def-cm04-one-dimensional-models-and-equilibria",
            "def-cm04-phase-plane-and-energy-level-sets",
