        {
          "id": "cex-cm04-undamped-resonance-with-bounded-drive-is-unbounded",
          "kind": "counterexample",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "A bounded sinusoidal drive with unbounded motions: the undamped driven oscillator at $\\Omega=\\omega_0$ refutes the unqualified boundedness claim",
          "statement": "In the sinusoidally driven oscillator model of\n[[post-cm04-sinusoidal-drive-model]] with data $m>0$, $k>0$, $c\\ge0$,\n$f_{0}\\in\\mathbb R$, $\\Omega>0$: **if the drive\n$t\\mapsto f_{0}\\cos(\\Omega t)$ is bounded, then every maximal motion of the model is\nbounded on $[0,\\infty)$.**",
          "strategy": "A direct refutation: declare the undamped driven model at m=k=f_0=Omega=1, note that its drive is bounded, exhibit the unbounded motion t sin t/2 supplied by the resonance theorem, note that every motion is unbounded, and show by contrast that the strictly damped and the undamped off-resonant cases are bounded.",
          "deps": [
            "post-cm04-sinusoidal-drive-model",
            "post-cm04-linear-damping-model",
            "def-cm04-one-dimensional-models-and-equilibria",
            "pthm-cm04-resonance-and-boundedness",
