      "items": [
        {
          "id": "ex-cm05-gravitational-ellipse-and-period-check",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "An elliptic gravitational relative orbit checked on declared model data: $p=10^{6}\\,$m, $e=3/5$, $a=25\\cdot10^{6}/16\\,$m, $b=5\\cdot10^{6}/4\\,$m, $E=-3.2\\cdot10^{17}\\,$J and $T=125\\pi\\cdot10^{9}/32\\,$s, with $T^{2}=4\\pi^{2}a^{3}/(G_{\\mathrm N}M)$",
          "statement": "Declare the gravitational two-label model of [[post-cm05-gravity]] clause (i)\nwith time window $I_0=\\mathbb R$ and the following **model data** (decimal numbers declared for this\ncomputation; $G_{\\mathrm N}=2.5\\times10^{-25}\\ \\mathrm{m^{3}\\,kg^{-1}\\,s^{-2}}$\nis a declared datum of the example, **not** the measured value of clause\n(iii), and the couplings are identified with the inertial masses as in clause\n(ii)):\n$$m_1=m_2=2\\times10^{24}\\ \\mathrm{kg},\\qquad M=4\\times10^{24}\\ \\mathrm{kg},\\qquad \\mu=\\frac{m_1m_2}{M}=10^{24}\\ \\mathrm{kg},\\qquad \\kappa=G_{\\mathrm N}m_1m_2=10^{24}\\ \\mathrm{kg\\,m^{3}\\,s^{-2}}.$$\nSuppose a motion $x$ of this model has a relative orbit with angular momentum\nmagnitude $J=10^{27}\\ \\mathrm{kg\\,m^{2}\\,s^{-1}}$, conic parameter\n$$p=\\frac{J^{2}}{\\mu\\kappa}=10^{6}\\ \\mathrm{m},$$\nand eccentricity $e=\\tfrac35$ (the conic data of\n[[pthm-cm05-conic]] clause 1). Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice\n([[def-countable-choice]]), as in the cited conic and period items. Then the\ncited items predict, as exact consequences of these data:\n\n1. the energy $E=\\dfrac{\\mu\\kappa^{2}}{2J^{2}}\\bigl(e^{2}-1\\bigr)=-\\dfrac{8}{25}\\times10^{18}\\ \\mathrm J=-3.2\\times10^{17}\\ \\mathrm J$, and $E<0$ with $e<1$, consistent with the elliptic branch;\n2. the semiaxes $a=\\dfrac{p}{1-e^{2}}=\\dfrac{25}{16}\\times10^{6}\\ \\mathrm m$ and $b=a\\sqrt{1-e^{2}}=\\dfrac54\\times10^{6}\\ \\mathrm m$, with $a=-\\kappa/(2E)$;\n3. the relative period $T=2\\pi\\sqrt{\\dfrac{\\mu a^{3}}{\\kappa}}=2\\pi\\dfrac{\\mu ab}{J}=\\dfrac{125\\pi}{32}\\times10^{9}\\ \\mathrm s$, so $T^{2}=\\dfrac{4\\pi^{2}\\mu a^{3}}{\\kappa}$;\n4. the third-law form $T^{2}=\\dfrac{4\\pi^{2}a^{3}}{G_{\\mathrm N}M}$ of [[pthm-cm05-kepler-period]] clause 2 under the declared identification;\n5. the areal rate $J/(2\\mu)=500\\ \\mathrm{m^{2}\\,s^{-1}}$ and the identity $\\pi ab/T=J/(2\\mu)$;\n6. both labels trace ellipses with the centre of mass at a focus, the same eccentricity $e$, and semimajor axes $a_1=a_2=\\tfrac12a=\\dfrac{25}{32}\\times10^{6}\\ \\mathrm m$ (equal masses), each periodic about the centre of mass with period $T$.",
          "strategy": "A worked verification: declare the gravitational data, substitute the conic parameter and eccentricity into the cited formulas, and check the energy, semiaxes, two period routes, the third-law form, the areal rate and the barycentric semiaxes by exact arithmetic.",
          "deps": [
            "post-cm05-central-model",
            "post-cm05-gravity",
            "pthm-cm05-relative-reduction",
            "pthm-cm05-plane-area",
            "pthm-cm05-conic",
            "pthm-cm05-kepler-period",
            "def-cm-central-force-trajectory",
            "def-cm01-units",
            "def-interval",
            "def-countable-choice"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
