            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-generated",
            "proof": "ai-generated"
          },
          "physical_scope": "A numerical consistency check of the zero- and positive-energy branches of the gravitational relative orbit on declared model data: the eccentricity-energy correspondence $E=0\\iff e=1$ and $E>0\\iff e>1$, the periapsis distances as zeros of the effective potential, the angular domain of the hyperbolic branch and the barrier bound. Every number is declared model data or an exact consequence of the cited items; no observation, no asymptotics and no scattering cross-section is claimed.",
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Konstantin Likharev, Essential Graduate Physics: Classical Mechanics (title page last edited September 1, 2026), Section 3.4, Eq. (3.65) and the discussion of the $E\\ge0$ cases, chapter pages 14-15 (PDF pages 47-48): the parabolic orbit at $E=0$ and the open hyperbolic branch at $E>0$ with its angular sector",
                "url": "https://essentialgraduatephysics.org/Files/CM%20merged.pdf"
              },
