          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "physical_scope": "The general point Noether theorem of the force model with a declared potential presentation in one inertial frame: for a symmetry datum with time reparametrisation, the charge M x' . xi - (K+U) tau - B is constant along every motion of the global potential branch; the charge has derivative equal to the residual force paired with xi - x' tau for an arbitrary presentation; the tau=0 and xi=0, tau=1 specialisations reduce to the strict point-symmetry charge and to minus the mechanical energy; and replacing the potential representative U by U+c(t) with the boundary function B-c tau preserves the identity and leaves the charge unchanged. The theorem is conditional on the adopted force branch, the declared presentation and the symmetry identity; it asserts no symmetry of any particular force law, no converse from conservation to symmetry, and carries no empirical content.",
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "D. Tong, Classical Dynamics (Cambridge lecture notes, January 2015 printing), Sections 2.4 and 2.4.1, printed pages 23-26 (PDF pages 29-32): constants of motion, the time-translation case H = sum qdot_j p_j - L, and the Noether proof with the generator paired with the conjugate momentum",
                "url": "https://www.davidtong.org/pdfs/teaching/classical-dynamics/clas.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "G. J. Sussman and J. Wisdom, Structure and Interpretation of Classical Mechanics, second edition (MIT Press, 2014/2015), Section 1.8.5: Noether's theorem for parametric coordinate transformations and the Noether integral, with the total-time-derivative gauge of Section 5.4.5 shifting momenta and Hamiltonians",
                "url": "https://mitp-content-server.mit.edu/books/content/sectbyfn/books_pres_0/9579/sicm_edition_2.zip"
              },
              {
                "title": "K. K. Likharev, Essential Graduate Physics, Part CM: Classical Mechanics (title page last edited September 1, 2026), Section 2.3, chapter pages 7-10 (PDF pages 25-28): the Hamiltonian function as the energy-type charge and its conservation when the Lagrangian has no explicit time dependence",
                "url": "https://essentialgraduatephysics.org/Files/CM%20merged.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "dependency_level": 16
        },
        {
          "id": "pthm-cm08-time-energy",
          "kind": "physics-theorem",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "Time translation and the mechanical energy of the model: conservation in the autonomous global potential branch and the sharp failure for a time-dependent potential",
          "statement": "Adopt the force model with potential presentation $(U,d)$ and mechanical\nLagrangian $L=K-U$ of [[def-cm07-action-and-mechanical-lagrangian]], with\nmasses $m_{1},\\dots,m_{N}>0$, open configuration domain $Q\\subseteq\\mathbb R^{3N}$,\ntime window $I_{0}$, mass operator $\\mathsf M$ and $U$ of\n[[def-cm03-potential-and-mechanical-energy]], and let\n\n$$E(t,x,v):=K(v)+U(t,x)=\\frac12\\,v\\cdot\\mathsf M v+U(t,x)$$\n\nbe the model's mechanical energy function. Consider the datum\n$\\tau\\equiv1$, $\\xi\\equiv0$, $B\\equiv0$ of\n[[def-cm08-symmetry-of-the-mechanical-lagrangian]]. Then:\n\nFor this time-translation family take its parameter $s$ to be measured in\nseconds; $\\tau\\equiv1$ is dimensionless and the charge $-E$ has units of\naction per second, namely joules.\n\n1. **(the identity).** The datum satisfies the model's Noether identity on\n   $O$ if and only if $\\partial_{t}U\\equiv0$ on $I_{0}\\times Q$; its charge is\n   the function $-E$.\n2. **(conservation).** If $d\\equiv0$ and $\\partial_{t}U\\equiv0$, then for\n   every motion $x:J\\to Q$ of the model on an interval $J$ with nonempty\n   interior ([[def-cm02-newtonian-flow]]), the function\n   $t\\mapsto E\\bigl(t,x(t),x'(t)\\bigr)=K(x'(t))+U(t,x(t))$ is constant on $J$.\n3. **(sharpness).** If $d\\equiv0$ and there is a state $(t_{0},x_{0})\\in I_{0}\\times Q$\n   with $\\partial_{t}U(t_{0},x_{0})\\ne0$, then the maximal motion\n   $x_{\\max}:J_{\\max}\\to Q$ of the model through the initial datum\n   $(t_{0},x_{0},0)$ satisfies\n   $\\frac{d}{dt}\\bigl(K(x_{\\max}')+U(\\cdot,x_{\\max})\\bigr)|_{t_{0}}=\\partial_{t}U(t_{0},x_{0})\\ne0$,\n   and the mechanical energy is not constant on $J_{\\max}$.\n\nThe conservation clause is the energy case of the model's Noether identity and\nis conditional on the adopted force branch, the declared representative $U$ and\nthe absence of residual forces; the sharpness clause shows that explicit time\ndependence of the declared representative destroys conservation along an actual\nmotion. No empirical content is asserted.",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "deps": [
            "def-cm08-symmetry-of-the-mechanical-lagrangian",
            "pthm-cm08-general-noether",
            "pthm-cm03-energy-balance",
