            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "physical_scope": "Under the inherited Axiom of Countable Choice $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ of the inertia and kinetic-splitting suppliers, a counterexample inside the rigid-material model branch of [[post-cm10-rigid-material]]: two equal point masses at opposite points of a line through the reference origin give a centred mass distribution whose inertia matrix has a zero principal moment and is not invertible, and a rotation of the model about that line has zero rotational kinetic energy and zero angular momentum about the centre of mass. The item refutes only the claim that every positive-mass rigid-material model has positive definite inertia; it asserts no measured value and no failure of the model's other statements, which carry the degeneracy caveat.",
          "sources": {
