          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "physical_scope": "Conditional deductions inside the external-torque branch of [[post-cm11-torque-balance]] for the rigid-material model of [[post-cm10-rigid-material]]: the body-frame Euler equations with the declared torque datum, their principal-axis components, the power identity $\\frac{d}{dt}\\tfrac12\\omega^{\\mathsf T}I\\omega=\\omega\\cdot R^{\\mathsf T}\\tau$ (and constancy of the rotational kinetic energy in the torque-free case), the torque-free reduction $l'=l\\times(I^{-1}l)$ under nondegeneracy, and the preservation of the balance under changes of inertial frame with the declared transformation of the torque datum. No force law producing $\\tau$, no conservation of $L_c$ (which is proved on the same page), no measurement and no empirical value is asserted.",
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "D. Tong, Classical Dynamics (Cambridge lecture notes, January 2015 printing), Section 3.3, Eqs. (3.31)-(3.33), printed pages 53-55 (PDF pages 59-61): angular-momentum rate, Euler's equations with torque in the body frame and the free-top case",
                "url": "https://www.davidtong.org/pdfs/teaching/classical-dynamics/clas.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "K. K. Likharev, Essential Graduate Physics, Part CM: Classical Mechanics (title page last edited September 1, 2026), Chapter 4 Section 4.4, Eq. (4.66) and its derivation, chapter page 15 (PDF page 69): Euler equations $I_j\\dot\\omega_j+(I_{j''}-I_{j'})\\omega_{j'}\\omega_{j''}=\\tau_j$ and the free-symmetric-top specialisation",
                "url": "https://essentialgraduatephysics.org/Files/CM%20merged.pdf"
              },
              {
