          "physical_scope": "The first-order linearization of the torque-free body-angular-velocity dynamics of a nondegenerate rigid-material model of [[post-cm10-rigid-material]] at a principal-axis spin $\\Omega e_j$, for pairwise distinct principal moments: the total derivative of the spin field, the explicit transverse equations, the sign criterion $\\lambda_j<0$ for an extreme axis and $\\lambda_j>0$ for the intermediate axis, the bounded oscillatory solutions in the extreme case and the exponentially growing solutions in the intermediate case, and the corresponding linear-stability verdicts in the sense of [[def-cm-orbital-and-linear-stability]]. The statement concerns the linearized system only; no nonlinear Lyapunov conclusion is drawn here, and no measurement, damping, friction or empirical value is asserted.",
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "D. Tong, Classical Dynamics (Cambridge lecture notes, January 2015 printing), Section 3.4.3, Eqs. (3.41)-(3.45), printed pages 57-58 (PDF pages 63-64): the perturbed principal-axis spin, the linearized equations, and the sign criterion for oscillation versus exponential growth",
                "url": "https://www.davidtong.org/pdfs/teaching/classical-dynamics/clas.pdf"
              },
