            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "physical_scope": "Worked checks inside the torque-free branch of the rigid-material model of [[post-cm10-rigid-material]] on two declared inertia matrices: a symmetric model with body inertia matrix diag(1,1,2) and an asymmetric model with diag(1,2,3). The checks verify principal-axis spins and their invariants, an explicit non-uniform symmetric-top motion with conserved angular momentum and energy, and the linearized frequencies at the principal-axis spins of the asymmetric model. No measured value, no concrete body and no experiment is asserted; the numerical data are declared model parameters under the explicit numerical SI convention dimensionless t = T / (one second) in the Example.",
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "D. Tong, Classical Dynamics (Cambridge lecture notes, January 2015 printing), Section 3.4.1-3.4.3, printed pages 55-58 (PDF pages 61-64): the free symmetric top and worked stability computations for principal-axis spins",
                "url": "https://www.davidtong.org/pdfs/teaching/classical-dynamics/clas.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "K. K. Likharev, Essential Graduate Physics, Part CM: Classical Mechanics (title page last edited September 1, 2026), Chapter 4 Section 4.4, chapter pages 15-16 (PDF pages 69-70): free-rotation invariants and computed examples for symmetric and asymmetric bodies",
                "url": "https://essentialgraduatephysics.org/Files/CM%20merged.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "I. W. Stewart, Advanced Classical Mechanics (MIT 8.09 Advanced Classical Mechanics, Fall 2014 course text), Chapter 2 Section 2.4, printed pages 41-48 (PDF pages 44-51): principal-axis spins and their linear stability with worked examples",
                "url": "https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/8-09-classical-mechanics-iii-fall-2014/d9bac33f6c60b304dc0398e99b327102_MIT8_09F14_full.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
