        {
          "id": "cex-cm11-invariants-do-not-force-uniform-rotation",
          "kind": "counterexample",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "A torque-free motion of a symmetric rigid-material model with constant angular momentum and energy whose body angular velocity is not constant: the invariants do not force a uniform rotation",
          "statement": "Let a model of the rigid-material branch [[post-cm10-rigid-material]] be used\nin the **torque-free** branch of [[post-cm11-torque-balance]] clause (iv), and\nlet $x(t,\\rho)=c(t)+R(t)\\rho$ be a motion of the resulting model on a time\nwindow containing $[0,\\infty)$. Suppose that along the motion the angular\nmomentum about the centre of mass $L_c$ and the rotational kinetic energy\n$\\tfrac12\\omega^{\\mathsf T}I\\omega$ are constant in time. Then the body\nangular velocity $\\omega$ of the motion is constant in time.",
          "deps": [
            "post-cm10-rigid-material",
            "post-cm11-torque-balance",
            "pthm-cm11-torque-free-invariants",
            "ex-cm11-free-top-checks",
