            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "dependency_level": 23,
          "physical_scope": "Generating-function theory for the declared potential presentation: first- and second-kind generating functions of action dimension generate equal-dimensional canonical local diffeomorphisms with the recorded one-form identities and unit determinant; a canonical diffeomorphism with invertible $(q,Q)$-projection is locally generated in the first kind; and for a time-dependent generating function the time derivative has energy dimension and the transformed Hamiltonian is $K=H+\\partial_tS$, with the Hamilton systems of $H$ and $K$ carried into one another by the generated time-dependent map. The statement is a conditional deduction from the adopted force branch, the declared presentation and the cited mathematics; it asserts no global generating function and no empirical content.",
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "D. Tong, Classical Dynamics (Cambridge lecture notes, January 2015 printing), Section 4.4.3, printed pages 104-105 (PDF pages 110-111): first-kind relations $p=\\partial F/\\partial q$, $P=-\\partial F/\\partial Q$, and second-kind relations $p=\\partial F_2/\\partial q$, $Q=\\partial F_2/\\partial P$",
                "url": "https://www.davidtong.org/pdfs/teaching/classical-dynamics/clas.pdf"
              },
              {
