                "url": "https://mitp-content-server.mit.edu/books/content/sectbyfn/books_pres_0/9579/sicm_edition_2.zip"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "ex-cm13-free-particle-flow-generating-function",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "The free particle of the model: the flow $Q=q+(t/m)p$ generated by the first-kind function $S_t(q,Q)=-m\\lvert Q-q\\rvert^{2}/(2t)$, the projection check and the exact change of $\\lambda$",
          "statement": "Declare the one-label model of the force branch\n[[post-cm02-force-superposition]] with $N=1$, mass $m>0$, time window\n$\\mathbb R$, configuration domain $Q=\\mathbb R^{3}$, zero potential $U\\equiv0$\nand no residual forces (the **free particle instance**,\n[[def-cm01-configuration]], [[def-cm03-potential-and-mechanical-energy]],\n[[def-cm07-action-and-mechanical-lagrangian]]). By\n[[pthm-cm12-mechanical-hyperregularity]] the branch Hamiltonian is\n$H(x,p)=\\lvert p\\rvert^{2}/(2m)$ with Hamiltonian system\n$\\dot x=m^{-1}p$, $\\dot p=0$\n([[def-cm12-hamiltonian]], [[pthm-cm13-hamiltonian-field-integrates-the-model-equations]]).\nThen:\n\n1. for every initial datum the maximal solution is\n\n$$\\Phi_{t}(x,p)=\\bigl(x+(t/m)\\,p,\\ p\\bigr)\\qquad(t\\in\\mathbb R),$$\n\n   the free-particle flow of the presentation;\n2. for $t\\neq0$ the function\n   $S_{t}(q,Q):=-\\frac{m}{2t}\\lvert Q-q\\rvert^{2}$ is of class $C^{\\infty}$\n   on $\\mathbb R^{3}\\times\\mathbb R^{3}$ with\n   $[S_t]=[m][Q-q]^2/[t]=\\mu\\ell^2\\tau^{-1}$ (action),\n   $S_{t,qQ}=(m/t)I_{3}$ invertible everywhere, and the first-kind map it\n   generates is exactly $\\Phi_{t}$: indeed\n   $p=S_{t,q}=m(Q-q)/t$ gives $Q=q+(t/m)p$, and\n   $P=-S_{t,Q}=m(Q-q)/t=p$; consequently $\\Phi_{t}$ is a canonical map of\n   the presentation with $\\lvert\\det D\\Phi_{t}\\rvert=1$\n   ([[pthm-cm13-generating-functions]] clauses 1,\n   [[def-cm-generating-function-of-the-first-and-second-kind]],\n   [[prop-cm-generating-functions-yield-canonical-maps]]);\n3. projection check: the map\n   $(q,p)\\mapsto(q,Q)=(q,q+(t/m)p)$ has invertible derivative\n   $\\begin{pmatrix}I_{3}&0\\\\ I_{3}&(t/m)I_{3}\\end{pmatrix}$ for $t\\neq0$,\n   while the family degenerates at $t=0$: $S_{t}$ has no value there and the\n   projection becomes singular, so this family does not represent the\n   identity map;\n4. the canonical one-form changes by an exact form along the flow:\n   $\\Phi_{t}^{*}\\lambda=\\lambda+t\\,dK$ with $K=\\lvert p\\rvert^{2}/(2m)$,\n   because $\\Phi_{t}^{*}\\lambda=P\\cdot dQ=p\\cdot\\bigl(dq+(t/m)dp\\bigr)=\\lambda+(t/m)\\,d\\bigl(\\lvert p\\rvert^{2}/2\\bigr)$;\n   in particular $\\Phi_{t}^{*}d\\lambda=d\\lambda$, recovering canonicity\n   directly ([[def-cm13-two-form]],\n   [[prop-cm-canonical-map-tests-and-hamiltonian-transport]]).\n\nAll quantities are model values of the declared idealization; no measurement\nis reported.",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "deps": [
            "def-cm13-two-form",
            "pthm-cm13-two-form-is-symplectic",
            "def-cm13-canonical-form",
            "def-cm13-canonical-map",
