          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "dependency_level": 21,
          "physical_scope": "The characteristics theorem of the Hamilton-Jacobi method for a declared hyperregular potential presentation of the framework's force branch: from a complete integral of the presentation's Hamilton-Jacobi equation in a fixed momentum chart, the characteristic curves of the equation solve the chart's Hamilton equations; when $d\u001bquiv0$, Cartesian characteristics are motions of the model and generalized-coordinate characteristics solve the substituted Lagrange equations; the derivatives of the complete integral in the parameters are constant along them; a local converse solves the constants equation for the configuration; and the Jacobi data are local canonical coordinates of the presentation's two-form. The statement is a conditional deduction from the adopted force branch, the declared presentation and the cited mathematics; it is local in the time, configuration and parameter variables, assumes the nondegeneracy of the mixed derivative at the base point only, and asserts no global solution, no completeness and no empirical content.",
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "D. Tong, Classical Dynamics (University of Cambridge Part II Mathematical Tripos), Section 4.7, printed pages 121-126 (PDF pages 127-132): from a solution $W$ of the Hamilton-Jacobi equation the flow with $q$-dot $=H_p$ and $p=W_q$ satisfies the second Hamilton equation, and the constants carried by the family",
                "url": "https://www.davidtong.org/pdfs/teaching/classical-dynamics/clas.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "D. Cline, Variational Principles in Classical Mechanics (2nd edition, University of Rochester River Campus Libraries, open textbook, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0), Section 15.4: Jacobi's complete integral, its constants and their use in reconstructing the motion",
                "url": "https://downloads.libretexts.org/api/v1/download/phys-9557/pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "G. J. Sussman and J. Wisdom, Structure and Interpretation of Classical Mechanics, second edition (MIT Press, 2014/2015), Chapter 6, Sections 6.1-6.1.4: the complete-integral strategy and the action as the generating function of time evolution; the treatment is local in character and states no caustic condition",
                "url": "https://mitp-content-server.mit.edu/books/content/sectbyfn/books_pres_0/9579/sicm_edition_2.zip"
              },
              {
                "title": "I. Stewart, Advanced Classical Mechanics (MIT 8.09/8.309 Fall 2014 course text), Chapter 4, Sections 4.1-4.6, printed pages 60-91 (PDF pages 63-94): generating functions, Hamilton-Jacobi separation and local action conventions",
                "url": "https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/8-09-classical-mechanics-iii-fall-2014/d9bac33f6c60b304dc0398e99b327102_MIT8_09F14_full.pdf"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "pthm-cm14-regular-tori",
          "kind": "physics-theorem",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "Compact connected regular fibres of a completely integrable datum of the presentation are Lagrangian tori with a full period lattice",
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice $\\mathrm{AC}_{\\omega}$\n([[def-countable-choice]]). Adopt the force model with potential\npresentation $(U,d)$ and mechanical Lagrangian $L=K-U$ of\n[[def-cm07-action-and-mechanical-lagrangian]], with the momentum charts and\ntwo-form datum of [[def-cm13-two-form]], the Hamiltonian fields of\n[[def-cm13-hamiltonian-field]] and the branch Hamiltonian $H$ of\n[[def-cm12-hamiltonian]]; by clauses 1–2 of\n[[pthm-cm13-two-form-is-symplectic]] (clause 1 for Cartesian domains and\nclause 2 for generalized-coordinate domains), each momentum phase domain is a\nsymplectic manifold for the presentation's two-form $\\omega$\n([[def-symplectic-form-and-symplectic-manifold]]). Let $W_{0}\\subseteq W$\nbe a nonempty open phase domain of dimension $2n$ and let\n$F=(F_{1}=H|_{W_{0}},\\dots,F_{n})$ be a completely integrable datum of the\npresentation on $W_{0}$ ([[def-cm14-complete-integrability]]). Let $b_{0}$\nbe a regular value of the integral map whose regular fibre\n$N:=F^{-1}(b_{0})\\subseteq W_{0}$ is nonempty, compact and connected, and\nassume there are a saturated open neighbourhood $U\\subseteq W_{0}$ of $N$\nand a ball $B\\subseteq\\mathbb R^{n}$ of regular values with $F(U)=B$ such\nthat $\\pi:=F|_{U}:U\\to B$ is a proper submersion with connected fibres.\nThen:\n\n1. **(Lagrangian fibre)** $N$ is a compact connected embedded\n   $n$-dimensional Lagrangian submanifold of $(W_{0},\\omega)$, and for\n   every $z\\in N$\n   $$T_{z}N=\\operatorname{span}\\{X_{F_{1}}(z),\\dots,X_{F_{n}}(z)\\},$$\n   the fields being those of [[def-cm13-hamiltonian-field]].\n2. **(commuting flows and period lattice)** The fields\n   $X_{F_{1}},\\dots,X_{F_{n}}$ have pairwise commuting flows; these flows\n   combine into a local $\\mathbb R^{n}$ action on $W_{\\mathrm{reg}}$, and\n   on the compact invariant fibre $N$ their restrictions are complete and\n   generate a transitive action of $\\mathbb R^{n}$ whose stabilizer at\n   every point is one and the same full lattice $\\Gamma\\subseteq\n   \\mathbb R^{n}$, with $N\\cong\\mathbb R^{n}/\\Gamma$.\n3. **(torus)** $N$ is diffeomorphic to the torus\n   $T^{n}=\\mathbb R^{n}/\\mathbb Z^{n}$.\n\nThe statement is conditional on the adopted force branch, the declared\npresentation, the smooth completely integrable datum and the listed\nhypotheses on the fibre; it asserts no global product structure of $U$, no\naction-angle coordinates, no completeness of any flow outside the compact\nfibre and no empirical content.",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "deps": [
            "def-cm14-complete-integrability",
            "def-cm14-involution",
            "def-cm13-hamiltonian-field",
            "def-cm13-poisson",
            "def-cm13-two-form",
            "pthm-cm13-two-form-is-symplectic",
            "def-cm12-hamiltonian",
            "def-cm07-action-and-mechanical-lagrangian",
            "def-cm07-generalized-coordinates-and-forces",
            "post-cm02-force-superposition",
            "def-cm01-configuration",
            "def-cm01-units",
            "def-completely-integrable-hamiltonian-system",
            "def-first-integral-and-poisson-commuting-functions",
            "def-poisson-bracket-on-a-symplectic-manifold",
            "def-symplectic-form-and-symplectic-manifold",
            "def-isotropic-coisotropic-symplectic-and-lagrangian-submanifolds",
            "def-hamiltonian-vector-field-and-hamiltonian-function",
            "def-countable-choice",
            "prop-regular-common-level-sets-are-lagrangian-submanifolds",
            "prop-commuting-hamiltonian-vector-fields-integrate-to-a-local-r-n-action",
            "lem-stabilizer-of-the-r-n-action-on-a-compact-connected-regular-fibre-is-a-full-lattice",
