          "dependency_level": 27,
          "physical_scope": "Adiabatic invariance of the action coordinate of a declared hyperregular potential presentation of the framework's force branch when the model carries a slow real parameter: if in a one-degree-of-freedom radian action-angle chart the branch Hamiltonian is $h(I,s)+\\varepsilon k(I,\\theta,s)$ with nonvanishing frequency $|\\partial_Ih|\\ge\\omega_0$ and the parameter runs as $s(t)=s_0+\\varepsilon t$, then along every model solution that stays in the compact chart region the action changes by at most the displayed order-$\\varepsilon$ bound on $0\\le t\\le A/\\varepsilon$. The statement uses a dimensionless slow parameter, an inverse-time slow rate, energy-dimension h and action-dimension k; it is conditional on C2 open extension data, a uniform fixed canonical chart for the parameter-dependent Hamiltonian on the zero-residual-force branch, the frequency bound and the trapping of the solution; it asserts no exact invariance, no statement across a separatrix or a chart boundary, and no empirical content.",
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "D. Tong, Classical Dynamics (Cambridge lecture notes, January 2015 printing), Section 4.6, Eqs. (4.148)-(4.158), printed pages 113-115 (PDF pages 119-121): the slow-parameter action calculation and the author's explicit remark that stricter proofs are deferred to the literature",
                "url": "https://www.davidtong.org/pdfs/teaching/classical-dynamics/clas.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "K. K. Likharev, Essential Graduate Physics, Part CM: Classical Mechanics (title page last edited September 1, 2026), Section 10.2, Eqs. (10.39)-(10.42), chapter pages 5-8 (PDF pages 241-244): the averaged energy-change identity and the adiabatic invariance of the action variable, with stricter proofs of the final statement referred to the literature in the source's footnote",
                "url": "https://essentialgraduatephysics.org/Files/CM%20merged.pdf"
              },
