          "dependency_level": 27,
          "physical_scope": "A counterexample in the autonomous zero-force one-label presentation on R6: the smooth three-integral datum F=(H,p1,p2) on p3>0 has connected regular fibres diffeomorphic to R3, hence noncompact. Its commuting R3 action has trivial stabilizer, so no full period lattice exists, and the physical Hamiltonian flow has no nonzero period. This is declared model data, with no measured value or apparatus claim.",
