            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "physical_scope": "Assuming countable choice for the locally defined incident and solid-angle measures, a separately adopted fixed-wall contact model of a reduced label of mass $\\mu$ reflecting elastically from an impenetrable sphere of radius $a$: the example-specific rule reverses the normal velocity component and preserves the tangential component, so speed and angular momentum are conserved across contact. The example computes the branch contribution $b=a\\cos(\\theta/2)$, the constant density $a^2/4$ and the total $\\pi a^2$. This fixed-wall rule is outside both the $C^2$ finite-range hypothesis of the central-scattering theorem and the finite-mass two-label restitution postulate; the $e=1$ comparison concerns only the normal-velocity reversal. The finite total does not contradict the Coulomb forward divergence. The data are declared model data; the example reports no observation or measured value.",
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Richard Fitzpatrick, Newtonian Dynamics (University of Texas at Austin), §6.4, Eqs. (352)-(357): the impenetrable-sphere interaction, b = a cos(theta/2), the constant differential cross-section a^2/4 and the total cross-section pi a^2",
                "url": "https://farside.ph.utexas.edu/teaching/336k/Newtonhtml/node51.html"
              },
              {
                "title": "Jacob Moore and Contributors, Mechanics Map (Pennsylvania State University, 2nd ed.), Engineering LibreTexts, §11.4 'Surface Collisions and the Coefficient of Restitution': the normal/tangential split of a surface impact with the tangential velocity unchanged and the normal velocity ratio fixed by the coefficient of restitution",
                "url": "https://eng.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Mechanical_Engineering/Mechanics_Map_(Moore_2nd_Edition)/11%3A_Impulse_and_Momentum_in_Particles/11.04%3A_Surface_Collisions_and_the_Coefficient_of_Restitution"
              }
            ]
          },
          "dependency_level": 18
        },
        {
          "id": "ex-cm15-rutherford-cutoff-check",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "A declared-data Rutherford check: $\\alpha=1$, $\\theta=\\pi/2$, $(\\mathrm d\\sigma/\\mathrm d\\Omega)=4\\times10^{-24}\\,\\mathrm{m^2}$, the band values $\\pi b(\\theta_1)^2$ and the growth of the truncated total as $\\theta_1\\downarrow0$",
          "statement": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ ([[def-countable-choice]]) for the cited scattering measures and vocabulary.\n\n**Declared model data.** For a central scattering model of\n[[pthm-cm15-rutherford-model]] declare the repulsive Coulomb coupling and\nthe reduced data\n$$\\mu=2\\times10^{-26}\\ \\mathrm{kg},\\qquad E=10^{-18}\\ \\mathrm{J},\\qquad J=4\\times10^{-34}\\ \\mathrm{kg\\,m^2\\,s^{-1}},\\qquad \\kappa=4\\times10^{-30}\\ \\mathrm{J\\,m},$$\nall read as *model data*, not as measured values of any physical pair.\nAbbreviate $\\kappa_4:=\\kappa/(4E)=10^{-12}\\ \\mathrm{m}$ and\n$\\kappa_2:=\\kappa/(2E)=2\\times10^{-12}\\ \\mathrm{m}$.\n\n**Assertions to check.** The model quantities of\n[[pthm-cm15-rutherford-model]] take the values\n$$v_\\infty=10^4\\ \\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}},\\qquad b=2\\times10^{-12}\\ \\mathrm{m},\\qquad \\alpha:=\\frac{\\kappa}{2Eb}=1,\\qquad \\theta=\\frac{\\pi}{2},$$\nthe branch density at $\\theta=\\pi/2$ is\n$(\\mathrm d\\sigma/\\mathrm d\\Omega)(\\pi/2)=\\kappa_4^2\\csc^4(\\pi/4)=4\\times10^{-24}\\ \\mathrm{m^2}$,\nthe angular band $(\\theta_1,\\theta_2)$ carries the truncated total\n$\\sigma=\\pi\\bigl(b(\\theta_1)^2-b(\\theta_2)^2\\bigr)$ with\n$b(\\theta)=\\kappa_2\\cot(\\theta/2)$, and as $\\theta_1\\downarrow0$ the band\nvalue $\\pi b(\\theta_1)^2$ grows like\n$(16\\pi\\times10^{-24}\\ \\mathrm{m^2})/\\theta_1^2$, so no finite ideal total is\nassigned.",
          "strategy": "A declared-data numeric check in SI units: v_inf, b, alpha=1, theta=pi/2, the density 4e-24 m^2, finite band values and the small-angle growth of the truncated total.",
          "deps": [
            "pthm-cm15-rutherford-model",
            "def-cm15-asymptotic-data",
