        {
          "id": "cex-cm16-stability-does-not-imply-attraction",
          "kind": "counterexample",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "Lyapunov stability does not imply attraction: the harmonic model is stable at its equilibrium while every nonzero datum keeps its distance and never converges",
          "statement": "**False statement.** *Every Lyapunov stable equilibrium of a one-dimensional\nmechanical chart model attracts every sufficiently close initial state;\nequivalently, Lyapunov stability implies asymptotic stability.*",
          "strategy": "Counterexample on the harmonic model: the equilibrium is Lyapunov stable while every nonzero datum keeps its distance, in agreement with the no-attraction clause of the energy theorem.",
          "deps": [
