          "dependency_roles": {
            "pthm-cm17-transport-and-material-derivative": "physical-result",
            "pthm-cm17-continuity-equation": "physical-result",
            "post-cm17-continuum-kinematic-model": "physical-assumption",
            "post-cm17-mass-balance": "physical-assumption",
            "def-cm17-density-and-mass": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-cm-continuum-motion": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-cm-euclidean-spatial-calculus": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-integral-over-a-measurable-set": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-cm17-continuum-body-and-units": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-ck-euclidean-maps-and-diffeomorphisms": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "physical_scope": "A worked verification of the model's transport identity and continuity equation on the explicit uniform expansion of a cube of side L_0 (including the one-metre cube), with constant reference density rho_0 and time-dependent spatial density: the model velocity, divergence, density field and mass are computed exactly, the integral mass balance holds identically, the continuity equation holds identically, and both sides of the transport identity are evaluated for a nonconstant field. The example is an exact conditional check within the adopted model; it reports no measurement.",
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "W. Barsukow, Introduction to Conservation Laws: Theory and Numerics (lecture notes, TUM, Winter term 2021/22), Section 1.1 (the continuity equation) and Section 1.2.3 (the transport theorem)",
                "url": "https://user.math.uzh.ch/barsukow/exercises2122/conservationlaws.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "R. Abeyaratne, Continuum Mechanics, Volume II of Lecture Notes on the Mechanics of Solids (MIT, 1988, revised 2020), Sections 3.7 and 4.2 (transport equations and conservation of mass with worked examples of the local form)",
                "url": "https://web.mit.edu/abeyaratne/Volumes/RCA_Vol_II.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ ([[def-countable-choice]]) for the cited Lebesgue transport and continuity suppliers.\n\nLet $L_0>0$ have dimension length and let $B=(0,L_0)^3\\subseteq\\mathbb R^3$ be the reference cube (the unit-cube case is $L_0=1\\,\\mathrm m$). Fix an expansion rate $\\alpha>0$ with $[\\alpha]=\\tau^{-1}$ and put $I=(-1/\\alpha,\\infty)$ and define the uniform\nexpansion\n\n$$\\chi(t,X):=\\bigl((1+\\alpha t)X_1,(1+\\alpha t)X_2,(1+\\alpha t)X_3\\bigr)\\qquad\\bigl((t,X)\\in I\\times\\mathbb R^3\\bigr).$$\n\nThen $\\chi$ is a motion of $B$ on $I$ in the sense of\n[[def-cm-continuum-motion]] (with $O=\\mathbb R^3$): it is $C^\\infty$, each\n$\\chi_t$ is a diffeomorphism with $D_X\\chi_t=(1+\\alpha t)I_3$ and\n$J(t,X)=(1+\\alpha t)^3>0$ on $I\\times B$. Adopt the model of\n[[post-cm17-continuum-kinematic-model]] with these data and the\nconstant-reference-density field\n\n$$\\rho(t,x):=\\frac{\\rho_0}{(1+\\alpha t)^3}\\qquad(\\rho_0>0)$$\n\non the swept region. Then:\n\n1. the spatial velocity is $u(t,x)=\\alpha x/(1+\\alpha t)$ and\n   $\\operatorname{div}u(t,x)=3\\alpha/(1+\\alpha t)$\n   ([[def-cm-euclidean-spatial-calculus]]);\n2. the model mass of $B$ at time $t$ is\n   $\\int_{\\chi_t(B)}\\rho\\,dx=\\rho_0L_0^3$ for every $t\\in I$: the mass-balance\n   assumption of [[post-cm17-mass-balance]] holds for every material subregion, since more generally $m(t,B')=\\rho_0\\operatorname{vol}(B')$, and the continuity\n   equation $\\partial_t\\rho+\\operatorname{div}(\\rho u)=0$ of\n   [[pthm-cm17-continuity-equation]] holds identically on $I\\times\\mathbb R^3$;\n3. for the field $f(t,x):=x_1^2$ the transport identity of\n   [[pthm-cm17-transport-and-material-derivative]] is verified exactly:\n   with $F(t)=\\int_{\\chi_t(B)}f(t,x)\\,dx$ one has $F(t)=L_0^5(1+\\alpha t)^5/3$ and\n   $F'(t)=5\\alpha L_0^5(1+\\alpha t)^4/3=\\int_{\\chi_t(B)}(\\partial_tf+\\operatorname{div}(fu))\\,dx$\n   for every $t\\in I$;\n4. along each label the density satisfies\n   $\\rho(t,\\chi(t,X))(1+\\alpha t)^3=\\rho_0$, the constant-product form of density\n   times volume of part (ii) of the continuity theorem, and the material\n   derivative is\n   $D_t\\rho(t,\\chi(t,X))=-3\\alpha\\rho_0/(1+\\alpha t)^4=-\\rho\\operatorname{div}u$, as the\n   material form of that theorem requires.",
          "strategy": "direct"
        },
        {
          "id": "ex-cm17-elastic-plane-wave-and-energy-check",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "A longitudinal plane wave in the linear elastic branch: stress, equation of motion and strain energy computed",
          "reference": "batch-33 B page; constructed from the A-page statements",
          "design_state": "authored; step-1 readiness recorded in the batch notes",
          "dependency_level": 17,
          "deps": [
            "pthm-cm17-elastic-plane-wave-speeds",
            "pthm-cm17-linear-elastic-equation-of-motion",
            "post-cm17-linear-elastic-constitutive",
            "def-cm-linear-elastic-constitutive-law",
            "lem-cm-isotropic-elastic-strain-energy-positivity",
            "def-cm-euclidean-spatial-calculus",
            "thm-sine-and-cosine-derivatives",
            "cor-trigonometric-parity-and-pythagorean-identity",
            "def-ck-euclidean-maps-and-diffeomorphisms",
            "def-cm17-continuum-body-and-units"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "pthm-cm17-elastic-plane-wave-speeds": "physical-result",
            "pthm-cm17-linear-elastic-equation-of-motion": "physical-result",
            "post-cm17-linear-elastic-constitutive": "physical-assumption",
            "def-cm-linear-elastic-constitutive-law": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-cm-isotropic-elastic-strain-energy-positivity": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-cm-euclidean-spatial-calculus": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-sine-and-cosine-derivatives": "mathematical-premise",
            "cor-trigonometric-parity-and-pythagorean-identity": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-ck-euclidean-maps-and-diffeomorphisms": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-cm17-continuum-body-and-units": "formulation-prerequisite"
          },
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "physical_scope": "A worked longitudinal plane wave of the adopted linear elastic branch: explicit strain, stress, verification of the displacement equation at the longitudinal speed root((lambda+2mu_s)/rho_0) and the positive strain-energy density of the wave. The computation is exact within the branch and asserts no measurement and no completeness of plane waves.",
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "K. Likharev, Essential Graduate Physics, Classical Mechanics (September 1, 2026 complete volume), Section 7.7 (the longitudinal plane elastic wave and its speed, and the elastic energy density)",
                "url": "https://essentialgraduatephysics.org/Files/CM%20merged.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "R. Abeyaratne, Continuum Mechanics, Volume II of Lecture Notes on the Mechanics of Solids (MIT, 1988, revised 2020), Section 11.2 and Problem 11.5 (isotropic linear elasticity and the positive definite strain energy)",
                "url": "https://web.mit.edu/abeyaratne/Volumes/RCA_Vol_II.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Adopt the isotropic linear elastic branch of\n[[post-cm17-linear-elastic-constitutive]] with reference density\n$\\rho_0>0$ of dimension $\\mu\\ell^{-3}$ and moduli $\\lambda,\\mu_s$ of\ndimension $\\mu\\ell^{-1}\\tau^{-2}$, with $\\mu_s>0$ and\n$\\lambda+\\tfrac{2\\mu_s}{3}>0$ ([[def-cm17-continuum-body-and-units]]). Let\n$x_1$ be position in metres and $t$ time in seconds. The amplitude $A\\ne0$ has\ndimension $\\ell$, and the wave number $\\kappa\\ne0$ has dimension $\\ell^{-1}$.\nDefine the positive longitudinal speed and angular frequency by\n$c_L:=\\sqrt{(\\lambda+2\\mu_s)/\\rho_0}$ and $\\omega:=\\kappa c_L$; then\n$[c_L]=\\ell\\tau^{-1}$, $[\\omega]=\\tau^{-1}$ and the phase is dimensionless.\nLet\n\n$$\\xi(t,x):=A\\cos\\bigl(\\kappa x_1-\\omega t\\bigr)\\,e_1,$$\n\nwith $A\\ne0$, $\\kappa\\ne0$ and $e_1$ the first standard basis vector: a\nlongitudinal plane wave travelling along $e_1$. Then:\n\n1. the linear strain is $e_{11}(t,x)=-A\\kappa\\sin(\\kappa x_1-\\omega t)$ with\n   all other entries zero, so $\\operatorname{tr}e=e_{11}$ and\n   $e_0=e-\\tfrac13(\\operatorname{tr}e)I_3$ has Frobenius squared norm\n   $\\tfrac23e_{11}^2$;\n2. the stress matrix is\n   $$\\sigma(t,x)=(\\lambda+2\\mu_s)e_{11}(t,x)\\,e_1e_1^{\\mathsf T}+\\lambda e_{11}(t,x)\\,(e_2e_2^{\\mathsf T}+e_3e_3^{\\mathsf T});$$\n3. the displacement equation (E) of\n   [[pthm-cm17-linear-elastic-equation-of-motion]] with $b\\equiv0$ holds\n   exactly: $\\rho_0\\partial_t^2\\xi_1=(\\lambda+2\\mu_s)\\partial_1^2\\xi_1$;\n4. the strain-energy density, of dimension $\\mu\\ell^{-1}\\tau^{-2}$, is\n   $W(e)=(\\tfrac\\lambda2+\\mu_s)e_{11}^2=\\mu_s\\tfrac23e_{11}^2\n   +(\\tfrac\\lambda2+\\tfrac{\\mu_s}3)e_{11}^2\\ge0$, with equality only where\n   $e_{11}=0$; both coefficients in the decomposition are positive under the\n   branch's hypotheses, and the squared speed\n   $c_L^2=(\\lambda+2\\mu_s)/\\rho_0$ is positive with $[c_L]=\\ell\\tau^{-1}$.",
          "strategy": "direct"
        },
        {
          "id": "ex-cm17-string-modes-and-tail-check",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "Two-mode fixed-end string: exact solution, d'Alembert cross-check and the O(N^{-4}) tail bound at N=1",
          "reference": "batch-33 B page; constructed from the A-page statements",
          "design_state": "authored; step-1 readiness recorded in the batch notes",
          "dependency_level": 11,
          "deps": [
            "thm-sine-and-cosine-addition-formulas",
            "pthm-cm17-string-wave-solutions",
            "thm-cm-smooth-string-fourier-series-solution",
            "thm-cm-dalembert-formula-and-string-solutions",
            "def-cm-sine-coefficients-of-periodic-functions",
            "def-ck-euclidean-maps-and-diffeomorphisms",
            "thm-sine-and-cosine-derivatives",
            "cor-trigonometric-parity-and-pythagorean-identity",
            "def-cm17-continuum-body-and-units"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "thm-sine-and-cosine-addition-formulas": "mathematical-premise",
            "pthm-cm17-string-wave-solutions": "physical-result",
            "thm-cm-smooth-string-fourier-series-solution": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-cm-dalembert-formula-and-string-solutions": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-cm-sine-coefficients-of-periodic-functions": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-ck-euclidean-maps-and-diffeomorphisms": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-sine-and-cosine-derivatives": "mathematical-premise",
            "cor-trigonometric-parity-and-pythagorean-identity": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-cm17-continuum-body-and-units": "formulation-prerequisite"
          },
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "physical_scope": "A worked fixed-end string problem of the adopted model: an initial displacement with two sine modes and zero initial velocity, its exact two-mode solution, agreement with the d'Alembert formula, mode frequencies and a finite check of the O(N^{-4}) tail bound at N=1. The example is an exact conditional computation within the linear string model and reports no measurement.",
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "K. Likharev, Essential Graduate Physics, Classical Mechanics (September 1, 2026 complete volume), Section 6.5 (standing waves of the fixed-end string and the mode frequencies)",
                "url": "https://essentialgraduatephysics.org/Files/CM%20merged.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "R. Laugesen, Harmonic Analysis Lecture Notes (arXiv:0903.3845), Chapters 1-2 (Fourier coefficients, uniqueness and summability of the sine series)",
                "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/0903.3845"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Let $L>0$ be a length, $c>0$ a speed, $A_*>0$ a displacement scale with\n$[A_*]=\\ell$, and $\\beta\\in\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{0\\}$ dimensionless. Let\n$[x]=\\ell$ and $[t]=\\tau$, and consider the\nfixed-end string model of [[pthm-cm17-string-wave-solutions]] with initial\ndisplacement and velocity\n\n$$F(x):=A_*\\left[\\sin\\Bigl(\\frac{\\pi x}{L}\\Bigr)+\\beta\\sin\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi x}{L}\\Bigr)\\right],\\qquad G(x):=0 .$$\n\nThen $F$ is odd and $2L$-periodic of class $C^\\infty$ and $G$ is odd and\n$2L$-periodic of class $C^4$, with\n$M_4=\\sup|G^{(4)}|=0$ and\n$M_5=\\sup|F^{(5)}|\\le A_*(\\pi/L)^5(1+243|\\beta|)=:\\overline M_5$\n([[def-cm-sine-coefficients-of-periodic-functions]]). Put\n$\\omega_n:=n\\pi c/L$ and\n\n$$u(t,x):=A_*\\left[\\cos(\\omega_1t)\\sin\\Bigl(\\frac{\\pi x}{L}\\Bigr) +\\beta\\cos(\\omega_3t)\\sin\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi x}{L}\\Bigr)\\right].$$\n\nThen:\n\n1. the sine coefficients of $F$ are $b_1(F)=A_*$, $b_3(F)=\\beta A_*$ and $b_n(F)=0$\n   otherwise, and the coefficients of $G$ all vanish; hence the series\n   solution of [[thm-cm-smooth-string-fourier-series-solution]] is exactly\n   the displayed finite sum $u$;\n2. $u$ is $C^\\infty$ on $\\mathbb R^2$, satisfies $u_{tt}=c^2u_{xx}$,\n   vanishes at $x=0$ and $x=L$ for every $t$, and has\n   $u(0,\\cdot)=F$, $u_t(0,\\cdot)=0$; by the uniqueness clause of the theorem\n   it is the unique $C^2$ fixed-end solution with these data;\n3. the d'Alembert formula of [[thm-cm-dalembert-formula-and-string-solutions]]\n   with data $(F,0)$ gives the same field:\n   $\\tfrac12[F(x-ct)+F(x+ct)]=u(t,x)$ by the product-to-sum identity\n   ([[thm-sine-and-cosine-addition-formulas]],\n   [[cor-trigonometric-parity-and-pythagorean-identity]]);\n4. the tail bound at $N=1$ is verified: with\n   $S_1u=A_*\\cos(\\omega_1t)\\sin(\\pi x/L)$ one has\n   $|u-S_1u|=A_*|\\beta||\\cos(\\omega_3t)||\\sin(3\\pi x/L)|\\le A_*|\\beta|$, while the\n   theorem gives $|u-S_Nu|\\le C(N+1)^{-4}$ with\n   $C\\le\\overline C:=4A_*(1+243|\\beta|)$, so the explicit upper estimate is\n   $A_*(1+243|\\beta|)/4$ at $N=1$, which also dominates the direct bound\n   $A_*|\\beta|$ for every $\\beta$;\n5. the mode frequencies satisfy $[\\omega_n]=\\tau^{-1}$ under\n   $[c]=\\ell\\tau^{-1}$ and $[L]=\\ell$ ([[def-cm17-continuum-body-and-units]]).",
          "strategy": "direct"
        },
        {
          "id": "ex-cm17-spring-chain-limit-numbers",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "Chain versus string on the normalized standing wave: exact discrete error, the N=100 bounds, and physical circumference 2π m",
          "reference": "batch-33 B page; constructed from the A-page statements",
          "design_state": "authored; step-1 readiness recorded in the batch notes",
          "dependency_level": 10,
          "deps": [
            "thm-ftc-second-part",
