          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "physical_scope": "A scope remark on the kinematic regime of the framework and its consequences for observable models: the adopted absolute time and Euclidean slices, the Galilean frame changes, the frame-relativity of protocols and prediction maps, and the absence of any intrinsic speed scale or numerical validity cutoff inside the framework. The item asserts no measured speed, no numerical regime boundary and no limit theorem relating the framework to any other model."
        },
        {
          "id": "rem-cm18-em-bridge",
          "kind": "remark",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "The electromagnetic bridge: what a charged-particle coupling must add to the framework, what the force branch then yields, and what is not imported",
          "statement": "## What the framework already supplies\n\nThe particle side of the framework is complete on its own terms: labels with\n$C^{2}$ worldlines parametrized by frame time and fixed positive masses\n([[post-cm01-worldlines]]); a force branch in which the force map is declared\nmodel input with standing continuity and state-local-Lipschitz hypotheses\n([[post-cm02-force-superposition]]); motions, unique maximal motions and the\ncontinuation criterion ([[def-cm02-newtonian-flow]], [[pthm-cm02-ivp]],\n[[pthm-cm02-continuation]]); the mechanical quantities and their balance\ntheorems, conditional on the declared interaction structure\n([[def-cm03-centre-of-mass-and-momenta]], [[pthm-cm03-frame-transformations]],\n[[rem-cm03-conservation-scope]]); and the operational observable model\nthrough which predictions at observation times are read\n([[def-cm18-observable-model]]). The framework contains no charge, no field\nand no coupling law.\n\n## What an electromagnetic coupling must add\n\nA charged-particle coupling is a **new physical assumption**, not a\nconsequence of the framework, and it must supply at least:\n\n1. **Charge attributes.** To each label an attribute with a declared\n   dimension and unit. The dimension group of the framework is generated by\n   length, duration and mass alone ([[def-cm01-units]] clause (a)); the\n   dimension and unit of charge, and of the components of any field used,\n   must therefore be declared by the coupling and cannot be inferred from\n   this framework.\n2. **Field maps.** Electric and magnetic fields (or the corresponding\n   potentials) as maps with declared domains, regularity, sources and\n   boundary or radiation conditions, supplied by an independently developed\n   electromagnetic model; the particle framework constrains none of these.\n3. **A coupling law.** An added force map $F^{\\mathrm{EM}}$ per label, for\n   instance a declared function of the fields, the charge and the label's\n   velocity in the chosen frame, as in the Lorentz force of the cited\n   electromagnetic treatment. The coupling law is adopted: the framework\n   neither derives it nor tests it.\n4. **Field-side bookkeeping.** If statements about the energy or momentum of\n   the combined system are wanted, the field contributions and their balance\n   with the particles must be declared as separate objects; this framework\n   contains no field energy or field momentum.\n\n## What the force branch yields conditionally\n\nOnce a coupling has been declared, the mechanical theorems apply to the\ntotal force map $F+F^{\\mathrm{EM}}$ provided it satisfies the standing\nhypotheses of the force branch (continuity and state-local Lipschitz,\nlocally uniformly in time) on the declared domain: then\n[[pthm-cm02-ivp]] and [[pthm-cm02-continuation]] give the local, unique and\nmaximal motions of the coupled model, and the balance laws of the\n[[def-cm03-centre-of-mass-and-momenta|balance page]] apply with the coupling\nforce among the external contributions.\n\nNo field-momentum theorem is imported. With the electromagnetic force\ntreated as external to the declared particle labels, the particle mechanical\nmomentum alone need not be conserved; the balance laws record the exchange\nthrough the external force, and the open-system boundary of\n[[rem-cm02-open-system-warning]] applies. A conservation statement for\nmatter plus field requires the field contributions of item 4 above as\nadditional declared data, and is not a consequence of this framework.\n\n## What is not claimed\n\nNo field equation, no value or dimension of any charge or coupling constant,\nno derivation or validation of a coupling law, no prediction of any\nelectromagnetic phenomenon and no measured electromagnetic quantity is\nasserted. The observable models of [[def-cm18-observable-model]] acquire an\nelectromagnetic readout only after a coupling has been declared; until then\nthis framework is silent about electric and magnetic effects.",
          "strategy": "Scope and status remark; no proof supplied.",
          "deps": [
            "def-cm18-observable-model",
            "def-cm01-units",
            "post-cm01-worldlines",
            "post-cm02-force-superposition",
            "post-cm02-interactions",
            "def-cm02-newtonian-flow",
            "pthm-cm02-ivp",
            "pthm-cm02-continuation",
