            "def-self-adjoint-positive-unitary-and-normal-operator",
            "def-hilbert-space",
            "def-countable-choice"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-trace-class-operator": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-finite-rank-operators-are-compact": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-nuclear-series-characterizes-trace-norm": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-trace-is-absolutely-convergent-and-basis-independent": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-trace-class-is-a-two-sided-banach-operator-ideal": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-operator-norm": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-bounded-linear-operator": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-hilbert-space-adjoint": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-real-and-complex-inner-product-space": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-cauchy-schwarz-for-real-and-complex-inner-product-spaces": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-self-adjoint-positive-unitary-and-normal-operator": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-hilbert-space": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $H$ be a complex Hilbert space with the pairing linear in the first argument ([[def-hilbert-space]], [[def-real-and-complex-inner-product-space]]), and for $u,v\\in H$ let\n\n$$T_{u,v}x:=\\langle x,v\\rangle u\\qquad(x\\in H).$$\n\nThen:\n\n(a) $T_{u,v}\\in\\mathcal B(H)$ with $\\|T_{u,v}\\|=\\|u\\|\\,\\|v\\|$ ([[def-bounded-linear-operator]], [[def-operator-norm]]), and the assignment $(u,v)\\mapsto T_{u,v}$ is linear in $u$ and conjugate-linear in $v$;\n\n(b) $T_{u,v}$ is trace class ([[def-trace-class-operator]]) with $\\|T_{u,v}\\|_1=\\|u\\|\\,\\|v\\|$ and $\\operatorname{tr}(T_{u,v})=\\langle u,v\\rangle$;\n\n(c) $T_{u,v}^*=T_{v,u}$ ([[def-hilbert-space-adjoint]]); $T_{x,x}$ is a positive bounded operator in the sense of [[def-self-adjoint-positive-unitary-and-normal-operator]], with $\\langle T_{x,x}y,y\\rangle=|\\langle y,x\\rangle|^2\\ge0$ for every $y\\in H$, and $\\operatorname{tr}(T_{x,x})=\\|x\\|^2$, $\\|T_{x,x}\\|_1=\\|x\\|^2$;\n\n(d) for bounded $B\\in\\mathcal B(H)$, $BT_{u,v}=T_{Bu,v}$ and $T_{u,v}B=T_{u,B^*v}$;\n\n(e) for trace-class $S$, $ST_{u,v}=T_{Su,v}$, $T_{u,v}S=T_{u,S^*v}$ and $\\operatorname{tr}(ST_{x,y})=\\langle Sx,y\\rangle=\\operatorname{tr}(T_{x,y}S)$;\n\n(f) the map $(u,v)\\mapsto T_{u,v}$ is continuous $H\\times H\\to\\mathcal S_1(H)$ for the trace norm, so in particular $v\\mapsto T_{v,v}$ and $v\\mapsto T_{u,v}$ are trace-norm continuous for fixed $u$.\n\n*Scope.* Only the rank-one calculus is asserted; no spectral, compactness or ideal statement beyond (b) is claimed, and no physical interpretation is attached.",
          "strategy": "Finite-rank membership and the one-term nuclear representation give the trace-class property, trace norm and trace; the adjoint, positivity and product identities are direct pairing computations; continuity follows from bilinearity and the trace-norm triangle inequality.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "A. W. Knapp, Advanced Real Analysis, Chapter II §5 (rank-one operators, trace class and the trace norm)",
                "url": "https://www.math.stonybrook.edu/~aknapp/download/a2-realanal-inside.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Topics in Real and Functional Analysis (November 17, 2017), §3.6, Lemmas 3.27–3.29, printed pp. 96–98 (Hilbert-Schmidt and trace class operators)",
                "url": "https://uomustansiriyah.edu.iq/media/lectures/9/9_2018_12_07!10_23_44_AM.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "aliases": []
        },
        {
          "id": "lem-nrqm-composites-bounded-tensor-maps",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Bounded tensor maps: extension, norm estimate, adjoint and commutation",
          "reference": "inventory.json#nrqm-composites-bounded-tensor-maps; proof module M1 (scaffold/mathematical-prerequisites.md)",
          "design_state": "reserved-local-prerequisite; complete-conditional-argument",
          "dependency_level": 1,
          "deps": [
            "lem-nrqm-composites-hilbert-tensor-construction",
            "thm-extension-of-a-bounded-map-from-a-dense-subspace",
            "def-bounded-linear-operator",
            "def-operator-norm",
            "def-hilbert-space-adjoint",
            "thm-hilbert-adjoint-properties",
            "def-countable-choice"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "lem-nrqm-composites-hilbert-tensor-construction": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-extension-of-a-bounded-map-from-a-dense-subspace": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-bounded-linear-operator": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-operator-norm": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-hilbert-space-adjoint": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-hilbert-adjoint-properties": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $H,H',K,K'$ be complex Hilbert spaces and let $S\\in\\mathcal B(H,H')$, $T\\in\\mathcal B(K,K')$ be bounded linear operators ([[def-bounded-linear-operator]]). Write $H\\widehat\\otimes K$ for the completion of the algebraic tensor product constructed in [[lem-nrqm-composites-hilbert-tensor-construction]], with inclusion $\\kappa$.\n\n(a) There is a unique bounded linear operator $S\\otimes T: H\\widehat\\otimes K\\to H'\\widehat\\otimes K'$ with $(S\\otimes T)\\kappa(u\\otimes v)=\\kappa'(Su\\otimes Tv)$ for all $u\\in H$, $v\\in K$, and it satisfies $\\|S\\otimes T\\|\\le\\|S\\|\\,\\|T\\|$ ([[def-operator-norm]]).\n\n(b) For Hilbert spaces $H'',K''$ and bounded $S':H''\\to H$, $T':K''\\to K$, one has $(S\\otimes T)(S'\\otimes T')=(SS')\\otimes(TT')$. In particular, for endomorphisms $S:H\\to H$, $T:K\\to K$, the endomorphisms $S\\otimes I_K$ and $I_H\\otimes T$ commute and their composite is $S\\otimes T$.\n\n(c) The Hilbert adjoint ([[def-hilbert-space-adjoint]]) is $(S\\otimes T)^*=S^*\\otimes T^*$.\n\n(d) If $S,T$ are unitary, then so is $S\\otimes T$. No extension of unbounded maps, and no algebraic manipulation of domains of unbounded operators, is asserted.",
          "strategy": "Define S⊗T on elementary tensors, estimate ‖(S⊗I)z‖ and ‖(I⊗T)z‖ in orthonormal coordinates, extend by density and bounded extension, then transfer adjoint, product and commutation identities from the dense elementary tensors.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics, 1st edition 2009, §1.4 pp. 45-47 (tensor products of operators)",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-schroe/schroe.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "MIT 8.05 Quantum Physics II (Fall 2013), Chapter 8 'Multiparticle States and Tensor Products', §1 pp. 1-4",
                "url": "https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/8-05-quantum-physics-ii-fall-2013/ffe665c0cba2eae19a83e88dec42925c_MIT8_05F13_Chap_08.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "aliases": [
            "nrqm-composites-bounded-tensor-maps"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "lem-nrqm-composites-density-and-scalar-spectral-probability",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Density operators and scalar spectral probability",
          "reference": "inventory.json#nrqm-composites-density-and-scalar-spectral-probability; proof module M2 (scaffold/mathematical-prerequisites.md)",
          "design_state": "reserved-local-prerequisite; complete-conditional-argument",
          "dependency_level": 1,
          "deps": [
            "def-trace-class-operator",
            "def-trace-of-a-trace-class-operator",
