          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-trace-class-operator": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-trace-of-a-trace-class-operator": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-rank-one-operator-calculus": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-nuclear-series-characterizes-trace-norm": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-spectral-theorem-for-compact-self-adjoint-operators": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-trace-of-a-positive-operator-is-the-sum-of-its-eigenvalues": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-trace-class-is-a-two-sided-banach-operator-ideal": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-trace-is-absolutely-convergent-and-basis-independent": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-self-adjoint-positive-unitary-and-normal-operator": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-projection-valued-measure": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-scalar-and-complex-measures-from-a-pvm": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-bounded-borel-pvm-integral": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-unbounded-integral-against-a-pvm": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-spectral-theorem-for-unbounded-self-adjoint-operators": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-monotone-convergence-for-the-integral": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-dominated-convergence": "mathematical-premise",
            "cor-finite-dimensional-inner-product-spaces-have-orthonormal-bases": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-measure": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-probability-measure": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-hilbert-space": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-axiom-of-choice": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]) and let $H$ be a nonzero complex Hilbert space ([[def-hilbert-space]]). Recall that $T_{u,v}\\in\\mathcal B(H)$ denotes the rank-one operator $T_{u,v}x=\\langle x,v\\rangle u$ ([[lem-nrqm-composites-rank-one-operator-calculus]]).\n\n(a) A **density operator** on $H$ is a self-adjoint positive trace-class operator $\\rho$ with $\\operatorname{tr}\\rho=1$ ([[def-trace-class-operator]], [[def-trace-of-a-trace-class-operator]], [[def-self-adjoint-positive-unitary-and-normal-operator]]). If $(u_n)_{n\\in J}$ is a finite or countable orthonormal family, with $J$ a finite initial segment of the positive integers or all positive integers, and $w_n\\ge0$ with $\\sum_nw_n=1$, then the sum $\\rho:=\\sum_nw_nT_{u_n,u_n}$ converges in trace norm to a density operator with $\\operatorname{tr}\\rho=\\sum_nw_n=1$. Conversely every density operator $\\rho$ admits such an expansion whose weights are its positive eigenvalues counted with multiplicity and whose vectors are orthonormal eigenvectors; distinct expansions of the same $\\rho$ exist when a positive eigenspace has dimension at least two.\n\n(b) Let $E$ be a projection-valued measure on a measurable space $(X,\\Sigma)$ acting on $H$ ([[def-projection-valued-measure]]). Then $\\mu_\\rho(B):=\\operatorname{tr}(\\rho E(B))$ is a well-defined probability measure on $(X,\\Sigma)$ ([[def-measure]], [[def-probability-measure]]); it is given by the absolutely convergent series $\\mu_\\rho(B)=\\sum_nw_n\\|E(B)u_n\\|^2$ in every expansion of (a), and reduces to $\\mu_\\rho(B)=\\|E(B)u\\|^2$ for a pure density operator $\\rho=T_{u,u}$ with $\\|u\\|=1$.\n\n(c) Assume in addition the Axiom of Choice ([[def-axiom-of-choice]]). Let $A$ be a self-adjoint operator with projection-valued measure $E_A$ ([[thm-spectral-theorem-for-unbounded-self-adjoint-operators]]) and let $\\psi\\in H$ have $\\|\\psi\\|=1$ and $\\psi\\in D(A)$. Here $|A|^{1/2}$ denotes the unbounded PVM integral $f(E_A)$ for $f(\\lambda)=|\\lambda|^{1/2}$, with domain $D(f(E_A))=\\{\\psi:\\int |\\lambda|\\,dE_{A,\\psi}<\\infty\\}$ as in [[def-unbounded-integral-against-a-pvm]]. Then\n\n$$\\int_{\\mathbb R}\\lambda\\,dE_{A,\\psi}(\\lambda)=\\langle A\\psi,\\psi\\rangle,\\qquad \\int_{\\mathbb R}\\lambda^2\\,dE_{A,\\psi}(\\lambda)=\\|A\\psi\\|^2 ,$$\n\nwhere $E_{A,\\psi}(B)=\\langle E_A(B)\\psi,\\psi\\rangle$ ([[lem-scalar-and-complex-measures-from-a-pvm]]); moreover $\\int_{\\mathbb R}|\\lambda|\\,dE_{A,\\psi}(\\lambda)<\\infty$ exactly when $\\psi\\in D(|A|^{1/2})$, and then the mean $\\int\\lambda\\,dE_{A,\\psi}$ is finite. No product $A\\rho$ of an unbounded operator with a density operator is used, and no physical interpretation of $\\mu_\\rho$ or of the moments is asserted.",
          "strategy": "Use the compact spectral theorem and trace-class ideal/nuclear estimates for the decomposition and its convergence, test the trace pairing against bounded projections for σ-additivity of μ_ρ, and obtain the moment clauses from the PVM form of the unbounded spectral theorem (choosing the domain where the moment integrals converge).",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics, 1st edition 2009, Section 3.1 pp. 87-98 (spectral calculus and scalar spectral measures), Section 6.2 pp. 136-138 (compact spectral expansions) and Section 6.3 pp. 139-144 (trace class, trace and ideal properties)",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-schroe/schroe.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "J. Binney and D. Skinner, The Physics of Quantum Mechanics, §6.3 pp. 121-128 (density operators)",
                "url": "https://www-thphys.physics.ox.ac.uk/people/JamesBinney/qb.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "aliases": [
            "nrqm-composites-density-and-scalar-spectral-probability"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "lem-nrqm-composites-weak-form-robertson-uncertainty",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Weak-form Robertson uncertainty on a common domain",
          "reference": "inventory.json#nrqm-composites-weak-form-robertson-uncertainty; proof module M5 (scaffold/mathematical-prerequisites.md)",
          "design_state": "reserved-local-prerequisite; complete-conditional-argument",
          "dependency_level": 0,
          "deps": [
            "thm-cauchy-schwarz-for-real-and-complex-inner-product-spaces",
            "def-adjoint-of-a-densely-defined-unbounded-operator",
            "def-symmetric-self-adjoint-and-essentially-self-adjoint",
            "def-schwartz-space-and-its-seminorms",
            "thm-algebra-of-derivatives",
            "thm-integration-by-parts",
            "cor-primitives-of-a-continuous-function",
            "def-improper-integral-at-infinity",
            "def-hilbert-space",
            "def-countable-choice"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "thm-cauchy-schwarz-for-real-and-complex-inner-product-spaces": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-adjoint-of-a-densely-defined-unbounded-operator": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-symmetric-self-adjoint-and-essentially-self-adjoint": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-schwartz-space-and-its-seminorms": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-algebra-of-derivatives": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-integration-by-parts": "mathematical-premise",
            "cor-primitives-of-a-continuous-function": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-improper-integral-at-infinity": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-hilbert-space": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $H$ be a complex Hilbert space ([[def-hilbert-space]]) and let $A,B$ be symmetric densely defined operators on $H$ ([[def-symmetric-self-adjoint-and-essentially-self-adjoint]], [[def-adjoint-of-a-densely-defined-unbounded-operator]]). Let $u\\in D(A)\\cap D(B)$ have $\\|u\\|=1$, and put\n\n$$a:=\\langle Au,u\\rangle,\\qquad b:=\\langle Bu,u\\rangle,\\qquad x:=(A-a)u,\\qquad y:=(B-b)u,\\qquad \\Delta A:=\\|x\\|,\\qquad \\Delta B:=\\|y\\| .$$\n\nThen:\n\n(a) $a$ and $b$ are real, $x,y\\in H$, and $\\Delta A\\Delta B\\ge|\\langle x,y\\rangle|\\ge|\\operatorname{Im}\\langle x,y\\rangle|$;\n\n(b) *(refined form)* $(\\Delta A)^2(\\Delta B)^2\\ge[\\operatorname{Re}\\langle x,y\\rangle]^2+[\\operatorname{Im}\\langle x,y\\rangle]^2$;\n\n(c) if in addition $u\\in D(AB)\\cap D(BA)$, then $([A,B]u,u)=\\langle ABu,u\\rangle-\\langle BAu,u\\rangle=-2i\\operatorname{Im}\\langle Au,Bu\\rangle=-2i\\operatorname{Im}\\langle x,y\\rangle$, and consequently $\\Delta A\\Delta B\\ge\\frac12|([A,B]u,u)|$;\n\n(d) for $c>0$, $H=L^2(\\mathbb R)$ and the operators $Qf(x)=xf(x)$, $Pf(x)=-icf'(x)$ defined on the Schwartz space $\\mathcal S(\\mathbb R)$: every unit $f\\in\\mathcal S(\\mathbb R)$ satisfies $(QP-PQ)f=icf$, the numbers $a_Q=\\int_{\\mathbb R}x|f(x)|^2dx$ and $b_P=\\langle Pf,f\\rangle$ are real, and with $x_Q:=(Q-a_Q)f$, $y_P:=(P-b_P)f$ one has $|\\operatorname{Im}\\langle x_Q,y_P\\rangle|=c/2$; hence $\\Delta Q\\Delta P\\ge c/2$ in the sense of the centered norms.\n\nNo assertion is made about products $AB$ off $D(AB)$ and the statement produces no energy-time inequality.",
          "strategy": "Centre A and B by their real means, apply Cauchy-Schwarz to x=(A−a)u and y=(B−b)u, and extract the imaginary part; verify the commutator pairing identity under the product-domain hypothesis, then compute the Schwartz commutator by the product rule.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "MIT 8.05 Quantum Physics II (Fall 2013), Chapter 5 'Uncertainty Principle and Compatible Observables' (variance identity and Cauchy-Schwarz bound)",
                "url": "https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/8-05-quantum-physics-ii-fall-2013/005979fa741c3ea2e0430456b70caf93_MIT8_05F13_Chap_05.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics, 1st edition 2009, §2.1 pp. 55-57 and §3.1 pp. 88-92 (self-adjoint operators and spectral measures)",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-schroe/schroe.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "aliases": [
            "nrqm-composites-weak-form-robertson-uncertainty"
          ]
        },
