        {
          "id": "lem-nrqm-composites-chsh-and-finite-sampling-law",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "The CHSH bound and the finite-sampling law for independent trials",
          "reference": "inventory.json#nrqm-composites-chsh-and-finite-sampling-law; proof module M7 (scaffold/mathematical-prerequisites.md)",
          "design_state": "reserved-local-prerequisite; complete-conditional-argument",
          "dependency_level": 0,
          "deps": [
            "def-probability-measure",
            "def-random-element-and-real-random-variable",
            "def-expectation-of-a-nonnegative-or-integrable-random-variable",
            "cor-expectation-linearity-monotonicity-and-modulus-bound",
            "def-independence-of-finite-random-variables",
            "def-bernoulli-and-binomial-random-variables",
            "lem-bernoulli-and-binomial-mean-and-variance",
            "def-moments-variance-and-covariance",
            "cor-chebyshev-inequality-for-random-variables",
            "def-multinomial-coefficient",
            "def-measure"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-probability-measure": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-random-element-and-real-random-variable": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-expectation-of-a-nonnegative-or-integrable-random-variable": "mathematical-premise",
            "cor-expectation-linearity-monotonicity-and-modulus-bound": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-independence-of-finite-random-variables": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-bernoulli-and-binomial-random-variables": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-bernoulli-and-binomial-mean-and-variance": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-moments-variance-and-covariance": "mathematical-premise",
            "cor-chebyshev-inequality-for-random-variables": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-multinomial-coefficient": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-measure": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "No choice principle is used. Let $(\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)$ be a probability space ([[def-probability-measure]]).\n\n(a) _CHSH bound._ Let $A_0,A_1,B_0,B_1:\\Omega\\to\\{-1,1\\}$ be random variables with values in $\\{-1,1\\}$ ([[def-random-element-and-real-random-variable]]). Then the four expectations exist and\n\n$$\\bigl|\\mathbb E[A_0B_0]+\\mathbb E[A_0B_1]+\\mathbb E[A_1B_0]-\\mathbb E[A_1B_1]\\bigr|\\le2 .$$\n\n(b) _Positive-probability sequences._ Let $N\\ge1$, $m\\ge1$, $p_1,\\dots,p_m\\ge0$ with $\\sum_{j=1}^mp_j=1$, and let $X_1,\\dots,X_N:\\Omega\\to\\{1,\\dots,m\\}$ be mutually independent with $\\mathbb P(X_k=j)=p_j$ for all $k,j$ ([[def-independence-of-finite-random-variables]]). Then for every sequence $(j_1,\\dots,j_N)\\in\\{1,\\dots,m\\}^N$ with $p_{j_k}>0$ for every $k$,\n\n$$\\mathbb P\\bigl(X_k=j_k\\text{ for every }k\\bigr)=\\prod_{k=1}^Np_{j_k}>0 .$$\n\nConsequently every event disjoint from this outcome has probability at most $1-\\prod_kp_{j_k}<1$: any criterion that rejects at least one such sequence has positive failure probability under this sampling model.\n\n(c) _Binomial frequency._ Let $S$ be binomial$(N,p)$ with $N\\ge1$ and $p\\in[0,1]$ ([[def-bernoulli-and-binomial-random-variables]]). Then the frequency $S/N$ satisfies $\\mathbb E[S/N]=p$, $\\operatorname{Var}(S/N)=p(1-p)/N$, and for every $\\varepsilon>0$\n\n$$\\mathbb P\\bigl(|S/N-p|\\ge\\varepsilon\\bigr)\\le\\frac{p(1-p)}{N\\varepsilon^2}.$$\n\n(d) _Multinomial count law._ The number of sequences $(j_1,\\dots,j_N)$ with prescribed fibre sizes $n_j:=\\#\\{k:j_k=j\\}$ is the multinomial coefficient $\\binom{N}{n_1,\\dots,n_m}$ ([[def-multinomial-coefficient]]), and each such sequence has probability $\\prod_{j=1}^mp_j^{n_j}$; in this displayed product use the zero-count convention $p^0:=1$ for every $p\\in[0,1]$, including $p=0$. Hence the probability that the count vector equals $(n_1,\\dots,n_m)$ is $\\binom{N}{n_1,\\dots,n_m}\\prod_jp_j^{n_j}$.\n\nNo statistical inference, empirical claim or measured frequency is asserted; the lemma only computes probabilities of an explicitly specified independent sampling model.",
          "strategy": "Bound the pointwise CHSH combination by 2 and integrate; compute independent sequence probabilities from the product rule of independence; obtain the binomial frequency moments from the published binomial lemma (or directly by indicator variance addition) and apply Chebyshev; count sequences with prescribed bin counts by the multinomial coefficient.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "J. Binney and D. Skinner, The Physics of Quantum Mechanics, §6.1.4 pp. 113-115 (CHSH inequality for a setting-independent local model)",
                "url": "https://www-thphys.physics.ox.ac.uk/people/JamesBinney/qb.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "MIT 8.05 Quantum Physics II (Fall 2013), Chapter 8 'Multiparticle States and Tensor Products', §5 pp. 16-19",
                "url": "https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/8-05-quantum-physics-ii-fall-2013/ffe665c0cba2eae19a83e88dec42925c_MIT8_05F13_Chap_08.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "aliases": [
            "nrqm-composites-chsh-and-finite-sampling-law"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "thm-nrqm-composites-finite-partial-trace-and-schmidt",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Finite partial trace, Schmidt decomposition and finite no-signalling",
          "reference": "inventory.json#nrqm-composites-finite-partial-trace-and-schmidt; proof module M3 (scaffold/mathematical-prerequisites.md)",
          "design_state": "reserved-local-prerequisite; complete-conditional-argument",
          "dependency_level": 2,
          "deps": [
            "lem-nrqm-composites-hilbert-tensor-construction",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-density-and-scalar-spectral-probability",
            "thm-trace-of-ab-equals-trace-of-ba",
