            "thm-spectral-resolution-and-polynomial-spectral-projections",
            "def-self-adjoint-and-normal-endomorphism",
            "def-non-negative-and-positive-operator",
            "cor-finite-dimensional-inner-product-spaces-have-orthonormal-bases"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "lem-nrqm-composites-hilbert-tensor-construction": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-density-and-scalar-spectral-probability": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-trace-of-ab-equals-trace-of-ba": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-trace-of-an-endomorphism": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-coordinate-column-and-matrix-of-a-linear-map": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-singular-value-decomposition": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-complex-spectral-theorem-for-normal-endomorphisms": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-spectral-resolution-and-polynomial-spectral-projections": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-self-adjoint-and-normal-endomorphism": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-non-negative-and-positive-operator": "mathematical-premise",
            "cor-finite-dimensional-inner-product-spaces-have-orthonormal-bases": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Let $V,W$ be nonzero finite-dimensional complex inner product spaces with orthonormal bases $(e_1,\\dots,e_m)$ of $V$ and $(f_1,\\dots,f_n)$ of $W$, let $V\\otimes W$ be their tensor product with the inner product of [[lem-nrqm-composites-hilbert-tensor-construction]], and let $\\operatorname{tr}$ denote the basis-independent trace of an endomorphism ([[def-trace-of-an-endomorphism]]).\n\n(a) For every endomorphism $R$ of $V\\otimes W$ there is a unique endomorphism $\\operatorname{Tr}_W R$ of $V$ with\n\n$$\\operatorname{tr}\\bigl((\\operatorname{Tr}_WR)A\\bigr)=\\operatorname{tr}\\bigl(R(A\\otimes I_W)\\bigr)\\qquad\\text{for every }A\\in\\operatorname{End}(V),$$\n\nnamely $\\operatorname{Tr}_WR=\\sum_{j=1}^n\\varphi_j\\circ R\\circ\\iota_j$, where $\\iota_j(v)=v\\otimes f_j$ and $\\varphi_j(x\\otimes w)=\\langle w,f_j\\rangle x$; it does not depend on the orthonormal basis $(f_j)$ of $W$, and the analogous definition gives $\\operatorname{Tr}_V R$ with $\\operatorname{tr}((\\operatorname{Tr}_VR)B)=\\operatorname{tr}(R(I_V\\otimes B))$.\n\n(b) $\\operatorname{Tr}_W$ is linear, positive (it maps positive endomorphisms to positive endomorphisms) and trace preserving on density matrices: if $R\\ge0$ and $\\operatorname{tr}R=1$ then $\\operatorname{Tr}_WR\\ge0$ and $\\operatorname{tr}\\operatorname{Tr}_WR=1$; and $\\operatorname{Tr}_W T_{\\Psi,\\Psi}=CC^*$ for every $\\Psi\\in V\\otimes W$, where $C:W\\to V$ is the coefficient map determined by $\\Psi=\\sum_jCf_j\\otimes f_j$.\n\n(c) *Schmidt decomposition.* Every $\\Psi\\in V\\otimes W$ admits an expansion\n\n$$\\Psi=\\sum_{r=1}^{k}s_r\\,v_r\\otimes u_r,$$\n\nwith $k\\le\\min(m,n)$, orthonormal families $(v_r)\\subseteq V$, $(u_r)\\subseteq W$ and $s_1\\ge\\cdots\\ge s_k>0$ uniquely determined by $\\Psi$ as the positive singular values of the coefficient map; moreover $\\|\\Psi\\|^2=\\sum_rs_r^2$. For $\\|\\Psi\\|=1$ the reduced density $\\rho=\\operatorname{Tr}_W T_{\\Psi,\\Psi}$ satisfies $\\operatorname{tr}\\rho^2=\\sum_rs_r^4$, and $\\operatorname{tr}\\rho^2=1$ holds exactly when $k=1$, i.e. exactly when $\\Psi$ is a product vector; mixed-state separability is not decided by this criterion.\n\n(d) *Finite nonselective no-signalling.* If $(M_a)_{a=1}^p$ are endomorphisms of $W$ with $\\sum_aM_a^*M_a=I_W$ then for every endomorphism $R$ of $V\\otimes W$\n\n$$\\operatorname{Tr}_W\\Bigl(\\sum_a(I_V\\otimes M_a)R(I_V\\otimes M_a^*)\\Bigr)=\\operatorname{Tr}_WR .$$\n\nThis is an identity for the specified finite local instrument; selective conditioning (dividing one summand by its nonzero trace) is not covered.",
          "strategy": "Define the partial trace by the finite sum formula, prove the pairing identity by expanding in matrix units and invoke finite trace cyclicity for uniqueness, positivity and trace preservation; construct the Schmidt decomposition from the finite singular value decomposition of the coefficient matrix, and verify the no-signalling identity by testing against A.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "MIT 8.05 Quantum Physics II (Fall 2013), Chapter 8 'Multiparticle States and Tensor Products', §§1-3 pp. 1-12",
                "url": "https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/8-05-quantum-physics-ii-fall-2013/ffe665c0cba2eae19a83e88dec42925c_MIT8_05F13_Chap_08.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "J. Binney and D. Skinner, The Physics of Quantum Mechanics, §6.1 pp. 105-111 and §6.3 pp. 121-128 (reduced states, nonunique mixtures)",
                "url": "https://www-thphys.physics.ox.ac.uk/people/JamesBinney/qb.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "aliases": [
            "nrqm-composites-finite-partial-trace-and-schmidt"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "lem-nrqm-composites-finite-effects-and-instruments",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Finite effects and instruments: normalization and non-determination of the update",
          "reference": "inventory.json#nrqm-composites-finite-effects-and-instruments; proof module M4 (scaffold/mathematical-prerequisites.md)",
          "design_state": "reserved-local-prerequisite; complete-conditional-argument",
          "dependency_level": 2,
          "deps": [
            "lem-nrqm-composites-density-and-scalar-spectral-probability",
            "def-non-negative-and-positive-operator",
            "thm-complex-spectral-theorem-for-normal-endomorphisms",
            "thm-spectral-resolution-and-polynomial-spectral-projections",
            "def-functional-calculus-for-a-normal-endomorphism",
            "def-self-adjoint-and-normal-endomorphism",
            "def-adjoint-of-a-linear-map-between-inner-product-spaces",
            "thm-trace-of-ab-equals-trace-of-ba",
            "def-trace-of-an-endomorphism",
            "def-hilbert-space",
            "thm-hilbert-adjoint-properties",
            "def-linear-isometry-and-orthogonal-or-unitary-operator",
