          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $H$ be a complex Hilbert space, $n\\ge1$, and $H^{\\otimes n}$ the $n$-fold completed tensor power ($H^{\\otimes1}:=H$, $H^{\\otimes(k+1)}:=H^{\\otimes k}\\widehat\\otimes H$ as in [[lem-nrqm-composites-hilbert-tensor-construction]]). For $v_0,\\dots,v_{n-1}\\in H$ write $v_0\\otimes\\cdots\\otimes v_{n-1}\\in H^{\\otimes n}$ for the iterated elementary tensor.\n\n(a) For every $\\pi$ in the symmetric group $S_n$ ([[def-finite-symmetric-group-and-permutation-notation]]) there is a unique unitary $U_\\pi\\in\\mathcal B(H^{\\otimes n})$ with\n\n$$U_\\pi(v_0\\otimes\\cdots\\otimes v_{n-1})=v_{\\pi^{-1}(0)}\\otimes\\cdots\\otimes v_{\\pi^{-1}(n-1)},$$\n\nand $U_\\pi U_\\sigma=U_{\\pi\\sigma}$, $U_{\\pi}^*=U_{\\pi^{-1}}$.\n\n(b) The operators\n\n$$P_+:=\\frac1{n!}\\sum_{\\pi\\in S_n}U_\\pi,\\qquad P_-:=\\frac1{n!}\\sum_{\\pi\\in S_n}\\operatorname{sgn}(\\pi)U_\\pi$$\n\n(with $\\operatorname{sgn}$ the sign homomorphism, [[thm-sign-is-a-homomorphism]]) are orthogonal projections.\n\n(c) $U_\\pi P_+=P_+U_\\pi=P_+$ and $U_\\pi P_-=P_-U_\\pi=\\operatorname{sgn}(\\pi)P_-$ for every $\\pi$; consequently the range of $P_+$ is the subspace of vectors fixed by every $U_\\pi$, and the range of $P_-$ is the subspace of vectors transforming by $\\operatorname{sgn}$.\n\n(d) If $v_0,\\dots,v_{n-1}$ have a repeated factor, that is, $v_i=v_j$ for some distinct $i,j\\in\\{0,\\dots,n-1\\}$, then $P_-(v_0\\otimes\\cdots\\otimes v_{n-1})=0$.\n\nSelecting the symmetric or antisymmetric sector for a particle species is a physical postulate, not a theorem of this construction; no spin-statistics statement is proved here.",
          "strategy": "Prove unitarity of each U_π and the composition law from the tensor norm, then verify idempotence and self-adjointness by group reindexing; derive the range description from U_πP_±=±P_± and the two-equal-factors vanishing from the transposition that fixes the product.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "D. Skinner, Principles of Quantum Mechanics (Cambridge Part II, Michaelmas 2021), Chapter 7 'Identical Particles', pp. 1-10",
                "url": "https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/dbs26/PQM/chap7.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "MIT 8.05 Quantum Physics II (Fall 2013), Chapter 8 'Multiparticle States and Tensor Products'",
                "url": "https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/8-05-quantum-physics-ii-fall-2013/ffe665c0cba2eae19a83e88dec42925c_MIT8_05F13_Chap_08.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "aliases": [
            "nrqm-composites-permutation-sector-projections"
          ]
        },
