          "id": "lem-nrqm-composites-nuclear-bounded-cyclicity",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Nuclear bounded cyclicity for trace-class operators",
          "reference": "inventory.json#nrqm-composites-nuclear-bounded-cyclicity; proof module M9 (scaffold/mathematical-prerequisites.md)",
          "design_state": "reserved-local-prerequisite; complete-conditional-argument",
          "dependency_level": 1,
          "deps": [
            "thm-hilbert-adjoint-properties",
            "def-trace-class-operator",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-rank-one-operator-calculus",
            "lem-nuclear-series-characterizes-trace-norm",
            "thm-trace-class-is-a-two-sided-banach-operator-ideal",
            "thm-trace-is-absolutely-convergent-and-basis-independent",
            "def-hilbert-space-adjoint",
            "def-bounded-linear-operator",
            "def-operator-norm",
            "def-hilbert-space",
            "def-countable-choice"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "thm-hilbert-adjoint-properties": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-trace-class-operator": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-rank-one-operator-calculus": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-nuclear-series-characterizes-trace-norm": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-trace-class-is-a-two-sided-banach-operator-ideal": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-trace-is-absolutely-convergent-and-basis-independent": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-hilbert-space-adjoint": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-bounded-linear-operator": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-operator-norm": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-hilbert-space": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $H$ be a complex Hilbert space ([[def-hilbert-space]]) and for $u,v\\in H$ let $T_{u,v}x=\\langle x,v\\rangle u$ ([[lem-nrqm-composites-rank-one-operator-calculus]]).\n\n(a) For every bounded $B\\in\\mathcal B(H)$ ([[def-bounded-linear-operator]]),\n\n$$BT_{u,v}=T_{Bu,v},\\qquad T_{u,v}B=T_{u,B^*v},$$\n\nwith the Hilbert adjoint $B^*$ ([[def-hilbert-space-adjoint]]).\n\n(b) Let $T\\in\\mathcal B(H)$ be trace class and let $T=\\sum_jT_{u_j,v_j}$ be a nuclear representation, i.e. the partial sums converge to $T$ in operator norm and $\\sum_j\\|u_j\\|\\,\\|v_j\\|<\\infty$ ([[lem-nuclear-series-characterizes-trace-norm]], [[def-trace-class-operator]]). Then for every bounded $B$\n\n$$\\operatorname{tr}(BT)=\\sum_j\\langle Bu_j,v_j\\rangle,\\qquad \\operatorname{tr}(TB)=\\sum_j\\langle u_j,B^*v_j\\rangle,$$\n\nboth series converging absolutely with $\\bigl|\\operatorname{tr}(BT)\\bigr|\\le\\|B\\|\\sum_j\\|u_j\\|\\,\\|v_j\\|$, and $\\operatorname{tr}(BT)=\\operatorname{tr}(TB)$ ([[thm-trace-is-absolutely-convergent-and-basis-independent]]). In particular $\\operatorname{tr}(BT)=\\operatorname{tr}(TB)$ for every trace-class $T$ and bounded $B$, and $\\operatorname{tr}(T_{u,v})=\\langle u,v\\rangle$. No cyclic permutation of unbounded operators is asserted.",
          "strategy": "Compute the rank-one identities and |tr(T_{v,u})|≤‖v‖‖u‖ first, pass to nuclear series by absolute convergence and the trace-class ideal estimates, and then to bounded multipliers with the bound ‖B‖Σ‖v_j‖‖u_j‖; the Lipschitz clause follows from the rank-one norm and nuclear estimates.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Topics in Real and Functional Analysis (2017), §3.6 pp. 93-96 (trace class, nuclear series and cyclicity)",
                "url": "https://www.uomustansiriyah.edu.iq/media/lectures/9/9_2018_12_07!10_23_44_AM.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "A. W. Knapp, Advanced Real Analysis, Chapter II §5 (trace-class operators and their ideal properties)",
                "url": "https://www.math.stonybrook.edu/~aknapp/download/a2-realanal-inside.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "aliases": [
            "nrqm-composites-nuclear-bounded-cyclicity"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "lem-nrqm-composites-complex-gaussian-continuation",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Complex Gaussian continuation",
          "reference": "inventory.json#nrqm-composites-complex-gaussian-continuation; proof module M28 (scaffold/mathematical-prerequisites.md)",
          "design_state": "reserved-local-prerequisite; complete-conditional-argument",
          "dependency_level": 0,
          "deps": [
            "lem-euclidean-gaussian-fourier-transform-with-two-pi-normalization",
            "thm-dominated-convergence",
            "def-complex-differentiability-holomorphic-and-entire",
            "def-complex-domain",
            "def-complex-logarithms-principal-logarithm-and-complex-powers",
            "cor-principal-logarithm-is-holomorphic-on-the-slit-plane",
            "thm-chain-rule-for-complex-derivatives",
            "thm-complex-exponential-is-entire-with-derivative-itself",
