          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $H,K$ be nonzero complex Hilbert spaces ([[def-hilbert-space]]) and let $H\\widehat\\otimes K$ be their completed tensor product ([[lem-nrqm-composites-hilbert-tensor-construction]]); write $T_{x,z}x'=\\langle x',z\\rangle x$ for rank-one operators ([[lem-nrqm-composites-rank-one-operator-calculus]]) and $\\operatorname{tr}$ for the trace of a trace-class operator ([[thm-trace-is-absolutely-convergent-and-basis-independent]]).\n\n(a) There is a unique linear map $\\operatorname{Tr}_K:\\mathcal S_1(H\\widehat\\otimes K)\\to\\mathcal S_1(H)$ with\n\n$$\\operatorname{tr}\\bigl((\\operatorname{Tr}_KT)A\\bigr)=\\operatorname{tr}\\bigl(T(A\\otimes I_K)\\bigr)$$\n\nfor every trace-class $T$ and every $A\\in\\mathcal B(H)$; it satisfies $\\|\\operatorname{Tr}_KT\\|_1\\le\\|T\\|_1$ and is independent of any chosen orthonormal basis of $K$.\n\n(b) $\\operatorname{Tr}_K$ maps self-adjoint positive trace-class operators to self-adjoint positive trace-class operators (positivity in the bounded-operator sense of [[def-self-adjoint-positive-unitary-and-normal-operator]]), is trace preserving ($\\operatorname{tr}\\operatorname{Tr}_KT=\\operatorname{tr}T$), and maps density operators to density operators ([[lem-nrqm-composites-density-and-scalar-spectral-probability]]).\n\n(c) On rank-one operators, $\\operatorname{Tr}_KT_{u\\otimes v,u'\\otimes v'}=\\langle v,v'\\rangle_K\\,T_{u,u'}$.\n\nThe analogous map $\\operatorname{Tr}_H$ satisfies $\\operatorname{tr}((\\operatorname{Tr}_HT)A)=\\operatorname{tr}(T(I_H\\otimes A))$ for $A\\in\\mathcal B(K)$. No claim is made about instruments or conditioning.",
          "strategy": "Define Tr_K on rank-one maps by the basis formula, prove trace-norm convergence of the resulting series (nuclear representation), establish the trace-pairing identity for rank-one maps and extend by absolute convergence, deduce uniqueness from testing against rank-one A, and get positivity by testing against x∈H.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Topics in Real and Functional Analysis (2017), §3.6 pp. 93-96 (trace-class operators and partial traces)",
                "url": "https://www.uomustansiriyah.edu.iq/media/lectures/9/9_2018_12_07!10_23_44_AM.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "MIT 8.05 Quantum Physics II (Fall 2013), Chapter 8 'Multiparticle States and Tensor Products', §3 pp. 9-12",
                "url": "https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/8-05-quantum-physics-ii-fall-2013/ffe665c0cba2eae19a83e88dec42925c_MIT8_05F13_Chap_08.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "aliases": [
            "nrqm-composites-separable-partial-trace"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "lem-nrqm-composites-countable-kraus-normalization",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Countable Kraus normalization and trace-norm convergence",
          "reference": "inventory.json#nrqm-composites-countable-kraus-normalization; proof module M9 (scaffold/mathematical-prerequisites.md)",
          "design_state": "reserved-local-prerequisite; complete-conditional-argument",
          "dependency_level": 2,
          "deps": [
            "lem-nuclear-series-characterizes-trace-norm",
