            "thm-trace-is-absolutely-convergent-and-basis-independent": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-self-adjoint-positive-unitary-and-normal-operator": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-hilbert-space": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $H$ be a complex Hilbert space ([[def-hilbert-space]]) and let $(M_a)_{a\\ge1}$ be bounded operators on $H$ with\n\n$$\\sum_{a=1}^NM_a^*M_a\\longrightarrow I\\qquad\\text{strongly as }N\\to\\infty .$$\n\nThen:\n\n(a) $\\sum_{a\\ge1}\\|M_ax\\|^2=\\|x\\|^2$ for every $x\\in H$;\n\n(b) for every self-adjoint positive trace-class $\\rho$ (positivity as in [[def-self-adjoint-positive-unitary-and-normal-operator]]) the series $\\sum_{a\\ge1}M_a\\rho M_a^*$ converges in trace norm to a self-adjoint positive trace-class operator $\\Phi(\\rho)$ with $\\operatorname{tr}\\Phi(\\rho)=\\operatorname{tr}\\rho$;\n\n(c) $\\Phi$ extends uniquely to a linear positive map $\\Phi:\\mathcal S_1(H)\\to\\mathcal S_1(H)$ with $\\operatorname{tr}\\Phi(\\rho)=\\operatorname{tr}\\rho$ for all trace-class $\\rho$ and $\\|\\Phi(\\rho)\\|_1\\le\\|\\rho\\|_1$ for self-adjoint $\\rho$; it maps density operators to density operators. No claim is made that every positive trace-preserving map has such a family.",
          "strategy": "Verify the norm identity Σ‖M_a x‖²=‖x‖² from strong convergence of the partial sums, express a positive trace-class ρ by its spectral expansion, bound the trace norm of the tail by the tail of Σ tr(M_aρM_a*) via monotone convergence, and extend to general trace-class inputs by the four positive parts.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Topics in Real and Functional Analysis (2017), §3.6 pp. 93-96 (trace-norm convergence and positivity)",
                "url": "https://www.uomustansiriyah.edu.iq/media/lectures/9/9_2018_12_07!10_23_44_AM.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "MIT 8.05 Quantum Physics II (Fall 2013), Chapter 8 'Multiparticle States and Tensor Products', §3 (local operations and reduced states)",
                "url": "https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/8-05-quantum-physics-ii-fall-2013/ffe665c0cba2eae19a83e88dec42925c_MIT8_05F13_Chap_08.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "aliases": [
            "nrqm-composites-countable-kraus-normalization"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "lem-nrqm-composites-finite-ancilla-complete-positivity",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Finite-ancilla complete positivity of countable Kraus maps",
          "reference": "inventory.json#nrqm-composites-finite-ancilla-complete-positivity; proof module M9 (scaffold/mathematical-prerequisites.md)",
          "design_state": "reserved-local-prerequisite; complete-conditional-argument",
          "dependency_level": 3,
          "deps": [
            "lem-nrqm-composites-hilbert-tensor-construction",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-bounded-tensor-maps",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-nuclear-bounded-cyclicity",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-countable-kraus-normalization",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-density-and-scalar-spectral-probability",
            "thm-trace-class-is-a-two-sided-banach-operator-ideal",
            "def-trace-class-operator",
            "def-self-adjoint-positive-unitary-and-normal-operator",
            "def-hilbert-space",
            "def-countable-choice"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "lem-nrqm-composites-hilbert-tensor-construction": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-bounded-tensor-maps": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-nuclear-bounded-cyclicity": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-countable-kraus-normalization": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-density-and-scalar-spectral-probability": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-trace-class-is-a-two-sided-banach-operator-ideal": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-trace-class-operator": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-self-adjoint-positive-unitary-and-normal-operator": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-hilbert-space": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $H$ be a complex Hilbert space ([[def-hilbert-space]]), let $(M_a)_{a\\ge1}$ be bounded operators on $H$ with $\\sum_{a\\le N}M_a^*M_a\\to I$ strongly, and let $\\Phi(\\rho)=\\sum_aM_a\\rho M_a^*$ be the map of [[lem-nrqm-composites-countable-kraus-normalization]]. Here a map on trace-class operators is **completely positive on finite-dimensional ancillas** when, for every finite-dimensional complex inner product space $C$, its matrixwise amplification $I_C\\otimes\\Phi$ preserves self-adjoint positive trace-class operators on $C\\widehat\\otimes H$. Then for every finite-dimensional complex inner product space $C$ the amplification\n\n$$I_C\\otimes\\Phi:S_1(C\\widehat\\otimes H)\\to S_1(C\\widehat\\otimes H)$$\n\nis well defined by the trace-norm convergent series $\\sum_a(I_C\\otimes M_a)R(I_C\\otimes M_a^*)$ and preserves positivity: every self-adjoint positive trace-class $R$ (positivity in the sense of [[def-self-adjoint-positive-unitary-and-normal-operator]]) has $I_C\\otimes\\Phi(R)$ self-adjoint positive. Hence $\\Phi$ is completely positive on every finite-dimensional ancilla in the stated sense.",
          "strategy": "On the dense span of elementary tensors the amplification of each summand is a positive map and the sum converges in trace norm by the nuclear estimates; positivity passes to the trace-norm limit, and the finite-dimensional statements reduce to finite sums.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Topics in Real and Functional Analysis (2017), §3.6 pp. 93-96 (trace-class amplification)",
                "url": "https://www.uomustansiriyah.edu.iq/media/lectures/9/9_2018_12_07!10_23_44_AM.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "MIT 8.05 Quantum Physics II (Fall 2013), Chapter 8 'Multiparticle States and Tensor Products' (composite systems and amplification)",
                "url": "https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/8-05-quantum-physics-ii-fall-2013/ffe665c0cba2eae19a83e88dec42925c_MIT8_05F13_Chap_08.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "aliases": [
            "nrqm-composites-finite-ancilla-complete-positivity"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "lem-nrqm-composites-local-trace-preserving-no-signalling",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Local trace-preserving Kraus maps do not change the opposite reduced state",
          "reference": "inventory.json#nrqm-composites-local-trace-preserving-no-signalling; proof module M9 (scaffold/mathematical-prerequisites.md)",
          "design_state": "reserved-local-prerequisite; complete-conditional-argument",
          "dependency_level": 4,
          "deps": [
            "lem-nrqm-composites-nuclear-bounded-cyclicity",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-separable-partial-trace",
