            "thm-trace-is-absolutely-convergent-and-basis-independent": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-trace-class-is-a-two-sided-banach-operator-ideal": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-self-adjoint-positive-unitary-and-normal-operator": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-bounded-tensor-maps": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-hilbert-tensor-construction": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-nuclear-bounded-cyclicity": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $H,K$ be complex Hilbert spaces, let $(M_a)_{a\\ge1}$ be bounded operators on $K$ with $\\sum_{a\\le N}M_a^*M_a\\to I_K$ strongly, and let $R$ be a trace-class operator on $H\\widehat\\otimes K$. In this statement, $R\\ge0$ means that $R$ is self-adjoint and $\\langle Rx,x\\rangle\\ge0$ for every $x$, as in [[def-self-adjoint-positive-unitary-and-normal-operator]]. Then the series (when either factor is $\\{0\\}$, use the zero partial-trace maps $\\operatorname{Tr}_K:\\mathcal S_1(\\{0\\})\\to\\mathcal S_1(H)$ and $\\operatorname{Tr}_H:\\mathcal S_1(\\{0\\})\\to\\mathcal S_1(K)$; when both factors are nonzero, use the partial traces of [[lem-nrqm-composites-separable-partial-trace]])\n\n$$\\sum_{a\\ge1}(I_H\\otimes M_a)R(I_H\\otimes M_a^*)$$\n\nconverges in trace norm, its sum $\\Phi(R)$ is trace class with $\\operatorname{tr}\\Phi(R)=\\operatorname{tr}R$ and $\\Phi(R)\\ge0$ if $R\\ge0$, and the reduced state on $H$ is unchanged:\n\n$$\\operatorname{Tr}_K\\Phi(R)=\\operatorname{Tr}_KR .$$\n\nBy symmetry, a local map $R\\mapsto\\sum_a(N_a\\otimes I_K)R(N_a^*\\otimes I_K)$ on the first factor also leaves $\\operatorname{Tr}_HR$ fixed. Selective conditioning (one summand normalized by its nonzero trace) is not covered.",
          "strategy": "Test the identity against an arbitrary bounded A on H, use the defining property of the partial trace to move A⊗I, cyclicity for bounded operators and the completeness identity Σ_a M_a*M_a=I, and density of the relevant operators.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
