          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]) and let $H,K$ be nonzero complex Hilbert spaces ([[def-hilbert-space]]) with $H\\widehat\\otimes K$ their completed tensor product ([[lem-nrqm-composites-hilbert-tensor-construction]]). A **product vector** means an elementary tensor $v\\otimes u$ with $v\\in H$ and $u\\in K$. Then for every $\\Psi\\in H\\widehat\\otimes K$ there are an at most countable index set $J$, orthonormal families $(v_r)_{r\\in J}\\subseteq H$ and $(u_r)_{r\\in J}\\subseteq K$, and numbers $s_r>0$ with\n\n$$\\Psi=\\sum_{r\\in J}s_r\\,v_r\\otimes u_r\\qquad\\text{(norm convergence in }H\\widehat\\otimes K),$$\n\nand $\\|\\Psi\\|^2=\\sum_rs_r^2$. The $s_r$ are the positive square roots of the nonzero eigenvalues of $CC^*$, where $C:\\overline{K_0}\\to H_0$ is the linear coefficient operator on countable closed factor supports of $\\Psi$, defined below; if $J$ is infinite then $s_r\\to0$. For $\\|\\Psi\\|=1$ the reduced density $\\rho=\\operatorname{Tr}_KT_{\\Psi,\\Psi}$ has $\\operatorname{tr}\\rho^2=\\sum_rs_r^4$, and $\\operatorname{tr}\\rho^2=1$ holds exactly when exactly one $s_r$ is nonzero, i.e. exactly when $\\Psi$ is a product vector. No assertion about separability of mixed density operators is made here.\n\nFor clarity, choose finite algebraic tensors converging to $\\Psi$ and let $H_0\\subseteq H$, $K_0\\subseteq K$ be the closed spans of their factor vectors. These supports have finite/countable orthonormal bases, and $\\Psi\\in H_0\\widehat\\otimes K_0$. The conjugate Hilbert space $\\overline{K_0}$ consists of symbols $\\bar z$, with $a\\bar z:=\\overline{\\bar a z}$ and $\\langle\\bar z,\\bar w\\rangle_{\\overline{K_0}}:=\\langle w,z\\rangle_{K_0}$. For an orthonormal basis $(f_j)$ of $K_0$, write $\\Psi=\\sum_jh_j\\otimes f_j$ and set $C\\bar f_j=h_j$, extending linearly and continuously. The positive singular values and the nonzero spectrum of $CC^*$ are independent of these supports and bases, as the reduced-state identity proved below shows.",
          "strategy": "Expand Ψ against an orthonormal basis of K to obtain coefficient vectors h_j, build the compact coefficient operator C:ℓ²→H and diagonalize the positive compact operator CC*; define the partners v_r with the coefficient identities and verify orthonormality, completeness and norm convergence, then read the reduced eigenvalues off the partial trace.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics, 1st edition 2009, §1.4 pp. 45-47 and Ch. 3 (compact operators and spectral decomposition)",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-schroe/schroe.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "MIT 8.05 Quantum Physics II (Fall 2013), Chapter 8 'Multiparticle States and Tensor Products', §§1-3",
                "url": "https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/8-05-quantum-physics-ii-fall-2013/ffe665c0cba2eae19a83e88dec42925c_MIT8_05F13_Chap_08.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "aliases": [
            "nrqm-composites-infinite-schmidt-decomposition"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "lem-nrqm-composites-general-trace-class-instrument-and-effect-duality",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Abstract trace-class instruments: effects and Heisenberg duality",
          "reference": "inventory.json#nrqm-composites-general-trace-class-instrument-and-effect-duality; proof module M32 (scaffold/mathematical-prerequisites.md)",
          "design_state": "reserved-local-prerequisite; complete-conditional-argument",
          "dependency_level": 2,
          "deps": [
            "lem-nrqm-composites-nuclear-bounded-cyclicity",
