          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $(X,\\Sigma,\\mu)$ be a $\\sigma$-finite measure space, $H$ a nonzero separable complex Hilbert space, and $(M_r)_{r\\ge1}$ bounded operator-valued maps on $X$ such that:\n\n(i) for every $\\psi\\in H$ the map $x\\mapsto M_r(x)\\psi$ is strongly measurable for each $r$ ([[def-strongly-measurable-banach-valued-function]]) and\n\n$$\\int_X\\sum_{r\\ge1}\\|M_r(x)\\psi\\|^2\\,d\\mu(x)=\\|\\psi\\|^2\\qquad(\\psi\\in H).$$\n\nHere $E:=\\ell^2(H)$ is the space of sequences $z=(z_r)_{r\\ge1}$ with $\\sum_r\\|z_r\\|^2<\\infty$, with inner product $\\langle z,w\\rangle_E:=\\sum_r\\langle z_r,w_r\\rangle_H$. Define $L^2(X,\\mu;E)$ as the vector space of strongly measurable fields $f:X\\to E$ with $\\int_X\\|f(x)\\|_E^2d\\mu<\\infty$, modulo equality almost everywhere; its inner product is $\\langle[f],[g]\\rangle:=\\int_X\\langle f(x),g(x)\\rangle_Ed\\mu$. The proof establishes that both spaces are Hilbert spaces before using adjoints or PVMs on this target.\n\nThen:\n\n(a) the formula $W\\psi(x):=(M_r(x)\\psi)_r$ defines a linear isometry $W:H\\to L^2(X,\\mu;\\ell^2(H))$;\n\n(b) for $B\\in\\Sigma$ the multiplication operator $P(B)$ by $\\mathbf 1_B$ is a projection-valued measure on $(X,\\Sigma)$, and $F(B):=W^*P(B)W$ is a normalized POVM. Here a POVM is a weakly countably additive map $F:\\Sigma\\to\\mathcal B(H)$ whose values are self-adjoint positive contractions, with $F(\\varnothing)=0$ and $F(X)=I$; positivity is in the sense of [[def-self-adjoint-positive-unitary-and-normal-operator]];\n\n(c) for every self-adjoint positive trace-class $\\rho=\\sum_nw_nT_{u_n,u_n}$ ([[def-self-adjoint-positive-unitary-and-normal-operator]], [[def-trace-class-operator]], [[lem-nrqm-composites-density-and-scalar-spectral-probability]]) the Bochner integral\n\n$$I_B(\\rho):=\\sum_{n\\ge1}w_n\\int_B\\sum_{r\\ge1}T_{M_r(x)u_n,M_r(x)u_n}\\,d\\mu(x)$$\n\nconverges in trace norm and defines a positive trace-class operator with $\\operatorname{tr}I_B(\\rho)=\\operatorname{tr}(\\rho F(B))$; the map $B\\mapsto I_B(\\rho)$ is countably additive in trace norm and $I_X$ is trace preserving, so $I$ is an abstract instrument in the sense of [[lem-nrqm-composites-general-trace-class-instrument-and-effect-duality]]; moreover $\\operatorname{tr}(I_B(\\rho)A)=\\sum_r\\int_B\\operatorname{tr}(M_r(x)\\rho M_r(x)^*A)\\,d\\mu(x)$ for bounded $A$, and finite-dimensional ancilla amplifications preserve positivity;\n\n(d) the conditional update at an event $B$ with $p(B)=\\operatorname{tr}(\\rho F(B))>0$ is $I_B(\\rho)/p(B)$. The normalization is integrated over events; no pointwise identity $\\sum_rM_r(x)^*M_r(x)=I$ is assumed. Universal normal-instrument representation is not claimed.",
          "strategy": "Prove the isometry from the normalization hypothesis, define the PVM and POVM by compression, construct I_B from rank-one contributions with Bochner measurability and Tonelli bounds, and establish well-definedness, positivity, additivity and trace preservation by testing against bounded A.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Topics in Real and Functional Analysis (2017), Ch. 1-3 (Bochner integration, trace-class Banach space and duality)",
                "url": "https://www.uomustansiriyah.edu.iq/media/lectures/9/9_2018_12_07!10_23_44_AM.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "MIT 8.05 Quantum Physics II (Fall 2013), Chapter 4 'Dirac's Bra and Ket Notation' (POVM formulation)",
                "url": "https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/8-05-quantum-physics-ii-fall-2013/4de6d044fa9d7e5b8998c5f8ca984a42_MIT8_05F13_Chap_04.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "aliases": [
