      "items": [
        {
          "id": "ex-nrqm-composites-bell-reduced-state",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Bell reduced state",
          "reference": "inventory.json#nrqm-composites-example-bell-reduced-state; leaf example reservation",
          "design_state": "leaf-example; complete-exact-conditional-argument",
          "dependency_level": 3,
          "deps": [
            "lem-nrqm-composites-hilbert-tensor-construction",
            "thm-nrqm-composites-finite-partial-trace-and-schmidt",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-rank-one-operator-calculus"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "lem-nrqm-composites-hilbert-tensor-construction": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-nrqm-composites-finite-partial-trace-and-schmidt": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-rank-one-operator-calculus": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Let $V=W=\\mathbb C^2$ with the standard inner product and orthonormal basis $e_+=\\binom{1}{0}$, $e_-=\\binom{0}{1}$ ([[lem-nrqm-composites-hilbert-tensor-construction]]), and let\n\n$$\\Psi:=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt2}\\bigl(e_+\\otimes e_--e_-\\otimes e_+\\bigr)\\in V\\otimes W .$$\n\nHere a **product vector** means an elementary tensor $v\\otimes u$ with $v\\in V$ and $u\\in W$; $T_{\\Psi,\\Psi}$ is the rank-one density operator determined by the unit vector $\\Psi$.\n\nThen:\n\n(a) $\\|\\Psi\\|=1$, and the coefficient matrix of $\\Psi$ in the bases $(e_+,e_-)$ is $C=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt2}\\begin{pmatrix}0&1\\\\-1&0\\end{pmatrix}$;\n\n(b) the partial traces satisfy $\\operatorname{Tr}_WT_{\\Psi,\\Psi}=CC^*=\\tfrac12 I_V$ and $\\operatorname{Tr}_VT_{\\Psi,\\Psi}=C^*C=\\tfrac12 I_W$, so both reduced states are the maximally mixed matrix $\\tfrac12 I$;\n\n(c) the reduced density $\\rho=\\tfrac12 I$ has eigenvalues $\\tfrac12,\\tfrac12$ and trace-square $\\operatorname{tr}\\rho^2=\\tfrac12$, while $\\operatorname{tr}(T_{\\Psi,\\Psi}^2)=1$; the Schmidt coefficients of $\\Psi$ are $s_1=s_2=\\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt2}$, and $\\Psi$ is not a product vector.",
          "strategy": "Compute the matrix of Ψ in the standard product basis, apply the partial-trace formula by summing the relevant index pairs, and read eigenvalues and purity directly.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-generated",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "generation": {
            "role": "example"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "MIT 8.05 Quantum Physics II (Fall 2013), Chapter 8 'Multiparticle States and Tensor Products', §§1-3",
                "url": "https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/8-05-quantum-physics-ii-fall-2013/ffe665c0cba2eae19a83e88dec42925c_MIT8_05F13_Chap_08.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "J. Binney and D. Skinner, The Physics of Quantum Mechanics, §6.1 pp. 105-115",
                "url": "https://www-thphys.physics.ox.ac.uk/people/JamesBinney/qb.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "aliases": [
            "nrqm-composites-example-bell-reduced-state"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "ex-nrqm-composites-nonunique-mixed-ensemble",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Nonunique mixed ensemble",
          "reference": "inventory.json#nrqm-composites-example-nonunique-mixed-ensemble; leaf example reservation",
          "design_state": "leaf-example; complete-exact-conditional-argument",
          "dependency_level": 2,
          "deps": [
            "lem-nrqm-composites-density-and-scalar-spectral-probability",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-rank-one-operator-calculus"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "lem-nrqm-composites-density-and-scalar-spectral-probability": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-rank-one-operator-calculus": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "On $H=\\mathbb C^2$ with the standard inner product and orthonormal basis $e_1=\\binom10$, $e_2=\\binom01$, put $e_\\pm:=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt2}(e_1\\pm e_2)$ ([[lem-nrqm-composites-density-and-scalar-spectral-probability]]). Then the maximally mixed density operator $\\frac12 I$ admits the two orthonormal convex decompositions\n\n$$\\frac12 I=\\frac12T_{e_1,e_1}+\\frac12T_{e_2,e_2}=\\frac12T_{e_+,e_+}+\\frac12T_{e_-,e_-},$$\n\nwhere $(e_1,e_2)$ and $(e_+,e_-)$ are distinct orthonormal bases of $H$. Thus the same density operator has two distinct orthonormal convex decompositions into rank-one density operators.",
          "strategy": "Compute both convex combinations with the rank-one trace formula and the orthonormality of the two bases.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-generated",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "generation": {
            "role": "example"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "J. Binney and D. Skinner, The Physics of Quantum Mechanics, §6.3 pp. 121-128 (density operators and their nonunique decompositions)",
                "url": "https://www-thphys.physics.ox.ac.uk/people/JamesBinney/qb.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "D. Skinner, Principles of Quantum Mechanics (Cambridge Part II, Michaelmas 2021), Chapter 10 'Interpreting Quantum Mechanics', pp. 1-12",
                "url": "https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/dbs26/PQM/chap10.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "aliases": [
            "nrqm-composites-example-nonunique-mixed-ensemble"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "cex-nrqm-composites-selective-conditioning-counterexample",
          "kind": "counterexample",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Selective-conditioning counterexample",
          "reference": "inventory.json#nrqm-composites-example-selective-conditioning-counterexample; leaf counterexample reservation",
          "design_state": "leaf-example; complete-refutation",
          "dependency_level": 5,
          "deps": [
