            "lem-nrqm-composites-local-trace-preserving-no-signalling": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "**False claim:** for every density operator $\\rho$ on a tensor product $H\\otimes K$ of finite-dimensional complex inner product spaces and every finite local family $(M_a)$ on $K$ with $\\sum_aM_a^*M_a=I_K$, the conditional reduced state on $H$ after the outcome $a$ is again $\\operatorname{Tr}_K\\rho$ whenever its probability is positive.\n\nThe claim confuses the *nonselective* identity $\\operatorname{Tr}_K\\bigl(\\sum_a(I\\otimes M_a)\\rho(I\\otimes M_a^*)\\bigr)=\\operatorname{Tr}_K\\rho$ of [[lem-nrqm-composites-local-trace-preserving-no-signalling]] with the corresponding statement for one selected outcome. The displayed unit vector in $\\mathbb C^2\\otimes\\mathbb C^2$ and one outcome of the explicitly defined projection instrument below refute the selective claim.",
          "strategy": "Compute the unnormalized conditional matrix from the partial-trace formula, normalize by its trace, compare with the unconditional maximally mixed reduced state, and verify the nonselective identity from the no-signalling lemma.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-generated",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "generation": {
            "role": "counterexample"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "J. Binney and D. Skinner, The Physics of Quantum Mechanics, §6.3 pp. 121-128",
                "url": "https://www-thphys.physics.ox.ac.uk/people/JamesBinney/qb.pdf"
              },
