            "thm-algebra-of-derivatives",
            "thm-ftc-second-part",
            "def-hilbert-space",
            "def-countable-choice"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "lem-nrqm-oscillator-diagonal-adjoint-and-graph-core-lemma": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-nrqm-oscillator-diagonal-spectrum": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-nrqm-oscillator-hermite-recurrence": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-nrqm-oscillator-hermite-orthogonality": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-nrqm-oscillator-hermite-completeness": "mathematical-premise",
            "cor-c-one-change-of-variables-for-l-one-functions": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-l-p-space-as-a-quotient-by-null-functions": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-complex-lp-and-euclidean-test-function-conventions": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-test-function-space-d-of-an-open-set": "mathematical-premise",
            "cor-cauchy-schwarz-inequality-for-l-two": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-chain-rule": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-algebra-of-derivatives": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-ftc-second-part": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-hilbert-space": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Fix real parameters $m>0$, $\\omega>0$, $\\hbar>0$, put $\\ell:=\\sqrt{\\hbar/(m\\omega)}>0$, and let $g_0,P,(g_n)_{n\\in\\mathbb N}$ be the Hermite data of [[thm-nrqm-oscillator-hermite-recurrence]] in $L^2(\\mathbb R,dy)$, so that $(g_n)$ is a complete orthonormal family by [[thm-nrqm-oscillator-hermite-completeness]]. Define\n\n$$D:L^2(\\mathbb R,dy)\\to L^2(\\mathbb R,dx),\\qquad (Df)(x):=\\ell^{-1/2}f(x/\\ell),$$\n\nand let $A$ be the self-adjoint diagonal operator of [[lem-nrqm-oscillator-diagonal-adjoint-and-graph-core-lemma]] for the complete orthonormal family $(g_n)$ and the eigenvalues $\\lambda_n=2n+1$, with the core $P$ and spectrum $\\{2n+1:n\\in\\mathbb N\\}$ ([[thm-nrqm-oscillator-diagonal-spectrum]]).\n\nThen:\n\n(a) $D$ is a linear isometry of $L^2(\\mathbb R,dy)$ onto $L^2(\\mathbb R,dx)$ with two-sided inverse $(D^{-1}g)(y)=\\ell^{1/2}g(\\ell y)$; the functions $\\psi_n:=Dg_n$, $\\psi_n(x)=\\ell^{-1/2}g_n(x/\\ell)$, form a complete orthonormal family of $L^2(\\mathbb R,dx)$;\n\n(b) the operator\n\n$$H_{\\mathrm{osc}}:=\\frac{\\hbar\\omega}{2}\\,DAD^{-1},\\qquad D(H_{\\mathrm{osc}}):=\\{f\\in L^2(\\mathbb R,dx):D^{-1}f\\in D(A)\\},$$\n\nis self-adjoint, satisfies $H_{\\mathrm{osc}}\\psi_n=\\hbar\\omega(n+\\tfrac12)\\psi_n$ for every $n$, and has\n\n$$D(H_{\\mathrm{osc}})=\\Bigl\\{f:\\sum_n\\hbar^2\\omega^2(n+\\tfrac12)^2|c_n|^2<\\infty\\Bigr\\},\\qquad H_{\\mathrm{osc}}f=\\sum_n\\hbar\\omega(n+\\tfrac12)c_n\\psi_n,$$\n\nwhere $c_n:=\\langle D^{-1}f,g_n\\rangle=\\langle f,\\psi_n\\rangle$; its spectrum is $\\sigma(H_{\\mathrm{osc}})=\\{\\hbar\\omega(n+\\tfrac12):n\\in\\mathbb N\\}$, its ground energy is $\\hbar\\omega/2$ with eigenvector $\\psi_0$, and $\\langle H_{\\mathrm{osc}}f,f\\rangle\\ge\\frac{\\hbar\\omega}{2}\\|f\\|^2$ for every $f\\in D(H_{\\mathrm{osc}})$;\n\n(c) $D(P)=\\operatorname{span}\\{\\psi_n\\}$ is a core for $H_{\\mathrm{osc}}$, and for every polynomial $p$ the function $f:=D(pg_0)$ is $C^\\infty$ on $\\mathbb R$ with\n\n$$H_{\\mathrm{osc}}f=-\\frac{\\hbar^2}{2m}f''+\\frac{m\\omega^2}{2}x^2f$$\n\npointwise on $\\mathbb R$;\n\n(d) for every $f\\in D(H_{\\mathrm{osc}})$ and every test function $\\varphi\\in C_c^\\infty(\\mathbb R)$,\n\n$$\\int_{\\mathbb R}(H_{\\mathrm{osc}}f)(x)\\varphi(x)\\,dx=\\int_{\\mathbb R}f(x)\\Bigl(-\\frac{\\hbar^2}{2m}\\varphi''(x)+\\frac{m\\omega^2}{2}x^2\\varphi(x)\\Bigr)dx,$$\n\nso $H_{\\mathrm{osc}}$ is the self-adjoint realization of the differential expression $-\\frac{\\hbar^2}{2m}\\frac{d^2}{dx^2}+\\frac{m\\omega^2}{2}x^2$ in the weak sense; no identification of $D(H_{\\mathrm{osc}})$ with a separately defined maximal differential-operator domain is asserted.\n\nAll parameters enter as positive real numbers; no physical identification of $m,\\omega,\\hbar$ with measured quantities is made.",
          "strategy": "Complete conditional argument authored locally from the published mathematical suppliers and the batch-35 tensor layer; see the item body for the numbered steps.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics, 1st edition 2009, §8.3 pp. 177-179 (H = H0 + omega^2 x^2, essential self-adjointness and Theorem 8.5)",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-schroe/schroe.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "J. Binney and D. Skinner, The Physics of Quantum Mechanics, §3.1 pp. 37-41 (oscillator Hamiltonian, length scale and stationary states)",
                "url": "https://www-thphys.physics.ox.ac.uk/people/JamesBinney/qb.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
