          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice and Countable Choice ([[def-axiom-of-choice]],\n[[def-countable-choice]]). Let $0<L<\\infty$ and $\\theta\\in[0,2\\pi)$. Put\n$D_\\theta:=\\{u\\in H^1(0,L):u^*(L)=e^{i\\theta}u^*(0)\\},\\qquad\nP_\\theta u:=-i\\,Du,$\nwith $H^1$ and the trace $u^*$ of [[def-nrqm-intervals-hilbert-sobolev-spaces]]\nand [[lem-nrqm-intervals-integration-by-parts]] clause (b). Then:\n\n(a) $D_\\theta$ is dense in $L^2(0,L;\\mathbb C)$, $P_\\theta$ is symmetric and\nself-adjoint;\n\n(b) the functions\n$\\varphi_n(x):=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt L}e^{i(2\\pi n+\\theta)x/L}\\qquad(n\\in\\mathbb Z)$\nform a complete orthonormal family of $L^2(0,L;\\mathbb C)$, each\n$\\varphi_n\\in D_\\theta$, and $P_\\theta\\varphi_n=\\kappa_n\\varphi_n$ with\n$\\kappa_n:=\\frac{2\\pi n+\\theta}{L};$\nthe eigenvalues $\\kappa_n$ are simple and\n$\\sigma(P_\\theta)=\\{\\kappa_n:n\\in\\mathbb Z\\}$;\n\n(c) $P_\\theta$ is the unique self-adjoint extension of the symmetric operator\n$P_\\theta$ restricted to the finite linear span of the $\\varphi_n$, and its\ndomain is exactly\n$D_\\theta=\\Bigl\\{\\sum_nc_n\\varphi_n:\\sum_n\\kappa_n^2|c_n|^2<\\infty\\Bigr\\}.$",
          "strategy": "Complete conditional argument authored on this page; see the item body for the numbered steps.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics, 1st edition 2009, Section 9.1 pp. 181-186 (second-order Sturm-Liouville operators and boundary forms; Problem 9.3 treats first-order adjoints), and Section 9.2 pp. 187-188 (second-order self-adjoint boundary conditions); the first-order twisted-periodic theorem is proved locally",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-schroe/schroe.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "Haim Brezis, Functional Analysis, Sobolev Spaces and Partial Differential Equations (Springer Universitext 2011), Section 8.2 Theorem 8.2 p. 204 (continuous Sobolev representatives), and Section 8.6 Theorem 8.22 pp. 231-232 (second-order Dirichlet spectral decomposition and the sine basis); the twisted Fourier basis is derived locally",
                "url": "https://www.math.toronto.edu/almut/Brezis.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "aliases": [
            "nrqm-intervals-and-contacts-twisted-periodic-momentum-domain"
          ]
