          "id": "thm-nrqm-intervals-regular-ivp-parameter-series",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Regular interval IVP: existence, a priori bound and entire spectral-parameter dependence",
          "reference": "inventory.json#nrqm-intervals-and-contacts-regular-ivp-parameter-series; proof module M19 (scaffold/mathematical-prerequisites.md)",
          "design_state": "reserved-local-prerequisite; complete-conditional-argument",
          "dependency_level": 0,
          "deps": [
            "thm-banach-fixed-point",
            "thm-gronwall-integral-inequality",
            "lem-fundamental-theorem-of-calculus-for-banach-valued-continuous-curves",
            "thm-tonelli-and-fubini-for-completed-product-measures",
            "thm-continuous-implies-integrable",
            "def-banach-space",
            "def-countable-choice"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "thm-banach-fixed-point": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-gronwall-integral-inequality": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-fundamental-theorem-of-calculus-for-banach-valued-continuous-curves": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-tonelli-and-fubini-for-completed-product-measures": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-continuous-implies-integrable": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-banach-space": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $0<L<\\infty$ and let\n$V\\in C([0,L];\\mathbb C)$ with $M:=\\|V\\|_{C^0}=\\max_{[0,L]}|V|$. For\n$z\\in\\mathbb C$, $x_0\\in[0,L]$ and $c_0,c_1\\in\\mathbb C$ consider the\ninitial value problem\n$\\text{(IVP)}\\qquad -u''+Vu=zu,\\qquad u(x_0)=c_0,\\quad u'(x_0)=c_1,$\nfor $u\\in C^2([0,L];\\mathbb C)$. Then:\n\n(a) (IVP) has exactly one solution $u(\\cdot\\,;z,x_0,c_0,c_1)$; it is the\nunique continuous solution of the Volterra equation\n$u(x)=c_0+c_1(x-x_0)+\\int_{x_0}^x(x-t)\\bigl(V(t)-z\\bigr)u(t)\\,dt\n\\qquad(x\\in[0,L]),$\nthe integral over $[x_0,x]$ for $x<x_0$ carrying the negative orientation, and\n$\\sup_{[0,L]}|u|\\le\\bigl(|c_0|+|c_1|L\\bigr)e^{(M+|z|)L^2};$\n\n(b) for fixed $x_0,c_0,c_1$, put $p(x):=c_0+c_1(x-x_0)$ and, for\n$f\\in C([0,L];\\mathbb C)$, define\n$\\mathcal K_zf(x):=\\int_{x_0}^x(x-t)(V(t)-z)f(t)\\,dt$. Then\n$$u(x;z)=\\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty}(\\mathcal K_z^np)(x)$$\nand the termwise $x$-derivative series converge uniformly on\n$[0,L]\\times\\{z\\in\\mathbb C:|z|\\le R\\}$ for every $R>0$. In particular,\n$(x,z)\\mapsto(u(x;z),u'(x;z))$ is continuous, and for each fixed $x$ both\n$u(x;\\cdot)$ and $u'(x;\\cdot)$ are entire functions of $z$. The derivative\n$w:=\\partial_zu(\\cdot\\,;z)$ is the unique $C^2$ solution on $[0,L]$ of\n$-w''+Vw-zw=u(\\cdot\\,;z),\\qquad w(x_0)=0,\\quad w'(x_0)=0 .$\nIt satisfies the associated Volterra equation\n$w(x)=\\int_{x_0}^x(x-t)\\bigl[(V(t)-z)w(t)-u(t)\\bigr]dt$.",
          "strategy": "Complete conditional argument authored on this page; see the item body for the numbered steps.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics, 1st edition 2009, Theorem 9.1 p. 183 (existence, uniqueness and entire dependence on the spectral parameter for regular Sturm-Liouville problems)",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-schroe/schroe.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "Gerald Teschl, Ordinary Differential Equations and Dynamical Systems (American Mathematical Society, Graduate Studies in Mathematics 140), Chapter 2 pp. 25-54 (linear systems, Gronwall estimates and continuous dependence)",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-ode/ode.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
