          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-axiom-of-choice": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-nrqm-intervals-hilbert-sobolev-spaces": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-nrqm-intervals-weak-derivative-ac-representative": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-nrqm-intervals-endpoint-trace-and-half-line-decay": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-nrqm-intervals-regular-ivp-parameter-series": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-nrqm-intervals-prufer-energy-monotonicity": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-sine-and-cosine-derivatives": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-sine-cosine-zero-sets-and-fundamental-period": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-gronwall-integral-inequality": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-intermediate-value": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-continuous-implies-integrable": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice and Countable Choice\n([[def-axiom-of-choice]], [[def-countable-choice]]). Let $0<L<\\infty$ and let\n$V\\in C([0,L];\\mathbb R)$, with $V_{\\min}:=\\min_{[0,L]}V$ and\n$V_{\\max}:=\\max_{[0,L]}V$. For $E\\in\\mathbb R$ let $u(\\cdot,E)$ be the\nsolution of $-u''+Vu=Eu$, $u(0)=0$, $u'(0)=1$, and let $\\theta(\\cdot,E)$ be\nits Prufer angle, as in [[thm-nrqm-intervals-prufer-energy-monotonicity]].\nCall $E$ a **Dirichlet eigenvalue** when there is a nonzero\n$w\\in H^2(0,L)$ ([[def-nrqm-intervals-hilbert-sobolev-spaces]]) with\n$w^*(0)=w^*(L)=0$ satisfying $-w''+Vw=Ew$, $w^*$ the continuous\nrepresentative of [[lem-nrqm-intervals-weak-derivative-ac-representative]].\nThen:\n\n(a) $E$ is a Dirichlet eigenvalue if and only if $\\theta(L,E)=k\\pi$ for some\ninteger $k\\ge1$;\n\n(b) for every $k\\ge1$ the equation $\\theta(L,E)=k\\pi$ has exactly one\nsolution $E_k$; the sequence $(E_k)_{k\\ge1}$ is strictly increasing,\n$E_k\\to\\infty$, and it is exactly the sequence of Dirichlet eigenvalues, each\nwith one-dimensional eigenspace:\n$\\ker(-\\tfrac{d^2}{dx^2}+V-E_k)=\\mathbb Cu(\\cdot,E_k)$;\n\n(c) bounds: for every $k\\ge1$,\n$\\Bigl(\\frac{k\\pi}{L}\\Bigr)^2+V_{\\min}\\le E_k\\le\n\\Bigl(\\frac{k\\pi}{L}\\Bigr)^2+V_{\\max};$\n\n(d) nodal count: for every $E$, the number of zeros of $u(\\cdot,E)$ in\n$(0,L]$ equals $\\lfloor\\theta(L,E)/\\pi\\rfloor$; consequently the $k$-th\neigenfunction $u(\\cdot,E_k)$ has exactly $k-1$ zeros in $(0,L)$, and the same\nholds for every nonzero eigenfunction with eigenvalue $E_k$.",
          "strategy": "Complete conditional argument authored on this page; see the item body for the numbered steps.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics, 1st edition 2009, Section 9.7, Theorem 9.39 p. 218 (Sturm comparison background; the regular finite-interval nodal count and energy bounds are proved locally)",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-schroe/schroe.pdf"
              },
