            "def-axiom-of-choice": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice and Countable Choice ([[def-axiom-of-choice]],\n[[def-countable-choice]]). Fix $\\alpha\\in\\mathbb R$. Let $D(A_\\alpha)$ be\nthe set of classes $u\\in H^1(\\mathbb R)$ whose restrictions to $(0,\\infty)$\nand $(-\\infty,0)$ have representatives of class $H^2$ on each half-line\n([[def-nrqm-intervals-hilbert-sobolev-spaces]]) and which satisfy the\n**interface condition**\n$u'^*(0+)-u'^*(0-)=\\alpha\\,u^*(0),$\nwhere $u^*$ is the continuous representative of [[lem-nrqm-intervals-weak-derivative-ac-representative]]\nand $u'^*(0\\pm)$ are the one-sided traces of the representative of the weak\nderivative, which exist by\n[[lem-nrqm-intervals-endpoint-trace-and-half-line-decay]]. For\n$u\\in D(A_\\alpha)$ define $A_\\alpha u$ to be the class equal to $-D^2u$ on\neach half-line. Then:\n\n(a) $D(A_\\alpha)$ is a dense linear subspace of $L^2(\\mathbb R;\\mathbb C)$\nand $A_\\alpha:D(A_\\alpha)\\to L^2(\\mathbb R)$ is a well-defined linear\noperator;\n\n(b) $A_\\alpha$ is symmetric;\n\n(c) $A_\\alpha$ is self-adjoint; explicitly, for $z\\in\\mathbb C\\setminus\\mathbb R$\nthe operator $A_\\alpha-z$ is a bijection $D(A_\\alpha)\\to L^2(\\mathbb R)$.",
          "strategy": "Complete conditional argument authored on this page; see the item body for the numbered steps.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Sarang Gopalakrishnan, Self-Adjointness and the Renormalization of Singular Potentials (2006), Section 1.2 pp. 16-18 and Section 8.2.5 pp. 129-130 (one-dimensional derivative jump, attractive bound-state calculation and extension background; rigorous operator and resolvent proofs are supplied locally)",
                "url": "https://math.ucr.edu/home/baez/gopalkrishnan.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics (2009), Section 2.6, Lemma 2.29 pp. 83-84 (differences of extension resolvents; point-interface results are proved locally)",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-schroe/schroe.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "aliases": [
            "nrqm-intervals-and-contacts-delta-interface-operator"
          ],
          "repair_confidence": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "thm-nrqm-intervals-delta-rank-one-resolvent",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Rank-one resolvent formula for the delta interface operator",
          "reference": "inventory.json#nrqm-intervals-and-contacts-delta-rank-one-resolvent; proof module M19 (scaffold/mathematical-prerequisites.md)",
          "design_state": "reserved-local-prerequisite; complete-conditional-argument",
          "dependency_level": 6,
          "deps": [
            "def-nrqm-intervals-hilbert-sobolev-spaces",
            "thm-nrqm-intervals-delta-interface-operator",
            "lem-nrqm-intervals-free-line-resolvent",
            "lem-nrqm-intervals-endpoint-trace-and-half-line-decay",
            "lem-nrqm-intervals-integration-by-parts",
            "lem-nrqm-intervals-weak-derivative-ac-representative",
            "thm-cauchy-schwarz-for-real-and-complex-inner-product-spaces",
            "def-bounded-linear-operator",
            "def-hilbert-space",
