            "def-axiom-of-choice"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-nrqm-intervals-hilbert-sobolev-spaces": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-nrqm-intervals-delta-interface-operator": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-nrqm-intervals-free-line-resolvent": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-nrqm-intervals-endpoint-trace-and-half-line-decay": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-nrqm-intervals-integration-by-parts": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-nrqm-intervals-weak-derivative-ac-representative": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-cauchy-schwarz-for-real-and-complex-inner-product-spaces": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-bounded-linear-operator": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-hilbert-space": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-axiom-of-choice": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice and Countable Choice ([[def-axiom-of-choice]],\n[[def-countable-choice]]). Let $\\alpha\\in\\mathbb R$ and let $A_\\alpha$ be the\nself-adjoint delta interface operator of\n[[thm-nrqm-intervals-delta-interface-operator]]; write $A_0$ for the\noperator with $\\alpha=0$, so that $D(A_0)=H^2(\\mathbb R)$ and\n$A_0u=-D^2u$. For $z\\in\\mathbb C\\setminus\\mathbb R$ let $k$ with $k^2=-z$,\n$\\operatorname{Re}k>0$, let $G_z(t)=(2k)^{-1}e^{-k|t|}$, and define the\nbounded linear functional\n$\\ell_z(f):=\\int_{\\mathbb R}G_z(y)f(y)\\,dy\\qquad(f\\in L^2(\\mathbb R)).$\nThen for every $z\\in\\mathbb C\\setminus\\mathbb R$:\n\n(a) $1+\\alpha G_z(0)=1+\\alpha/(2k)\\ne0$, and\n$(A_\\alpha-z)^{-1}f=(A_0-z)^{-1}f-\\frac{\\alpha\\,\\ell_z(f)}{1+\\alpha G_z(0)}\\,G_z\n\\qquad(f\\in L^2(\\mathbb R));$\n\n(b) the difference\n$K_z:=(A_\\alpha-z)^{-1}-(A_0-z)^{-1}$ is a bounded operator of rank at most one (rank one if $\\alpha\\ne0$, and zero if $\\alpha=0$),\n$K_zf=-\\dfrac{\\alpha}{1+\\alpha G_z(0)}\\,\\ell_z(f)\\,G_z$, its range is\ncontained in $\\mathbb C G_z$, and\n$\\|K_z\\|\\le\\frac{|\\alpha|\\,\\|G_z\\|_{L^2}^2}{|1+\\alpha G_z(0)|}\n=\\frac{|\\alpha|}{4|k|^2\\operatorname{Re}k\\,\\bigl|1+\\alpha/(2k)\\bigr|}\\,;$\nconsequently\n$\\bigl\\|(A_\\alpha-z)^{-1}\\bigr\\|\\le\n\\bigl\\|(A_0-z)^{-1}\\bigr\\|+\\|K_z\\| .$",
          "strategy": "Complete conditional argument authored on this page; see the item body for the numbered steps.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Sarang Gopalakrishnan, Self-Adjointness and the Renormalization of Singular Potentials (2006), Section 1.2 pp. 16-18 and Section 8.2.5 pp. 129-130 (one-dimensional derivative jump, attractive bound-state calculation and extension background; rigorous operator and resolvent proofs are supplied locally)",
                "url": "https://math.ucr.edu/home/baez/gopalkrishnan.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics (2009), Section 2.6, Lemma 2.29 pp. 83-84 (differences of extension resolvents; point-interface results are proved locally)",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-schroe/schroe.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "aliases": [
            "nrqm-intervals-and-contacts-delta-rank-one-resolvent"
          ],
          "repair_confidence": 1
        },
