            "lem-nrqm-intervals-weak-derivative-ac-representative": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-nrqm-intervals-endpoint-trace-and-half-line-decay": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-nrqm-intervals-regular-ivp-parameter-series": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-nrqm-composites-real-multipliers-and-free-bounded-potential-operators": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-complex-exponential": "mathematical-premise",
            "cor-complex-trigonometric-and-hyperbolic-addition-formulas": "mathematical-premise",
            "cor-complex-trigonometric-and-hyperbolic-derivatives": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-derivative-of-exponential": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-cauchy-schwarz-for-real-and-complex-inner-product-spaces": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-hilbert-space": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-axiom-of-choice": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice and Countable Choice ([[def-axiom-of-choice]],\n[[def-countable-choice]]). Let $a>0$, $U>0$, $m,\\hbar>0$ and put\n$K:=\\sqrt{2mU}/\\hbar>0$. Let $V:\\mathbb R\\to\\mathbb R$ be $V(x)=-U$ for\n$|x|\\le a$ and $V(x)=0$ for $|x|>a$, and let\n$H\\psi:=-\\frac{\\hbar^2}{2m}\\psi''+V\\psi,\\qquad D(H):=H^2(\\mathbb R),$\nwith $H^2$ of [[def-nrqm-intervals-hilbert-sobolev-spaces]]. Then:\n\n(a) $H$ is self-adjoint on $H^2(\\mathbb R)$;\n\n(b) *root conditions.* $E\\in\\mathbb R$ with $-U<E<0$ is an eigenvalue of $H$\nif and only if, writing $E=-\\varepsilon$, $\\kappa:=\\sqrt{2m\\varepsilon}/\\hbar$\nand $k:=\\sqrt{2m(U-\\varepsilon)}/\\hbar$ (so that $k,\\kappa>0$ and\n$k^2+\\kappa^2=K^2$), the pair $(k,\\kappa)$ satisfies\n$k\\tan(ka)=\\kappa\\qquad\\text{(even case)}\\qquad\\text{or}\\qquad\n-k\\cot(ka)=\\kappa\\qquad\\text{(odd case)} .$\nEvery such eigenvalue is simple, and its eigenfunction is, up to a nonzero\nscalar, $x\\mapsto\\cos(kx)$ on $(-a,a)$ continued by $ce^{-\\kappa|x|}$ outside\nin the even case and $x\\mapsto\\sin(kx)$ on $(-a,a)$ continued by\n$c\\,\\operatorname{sgn}(x)e^{-\\kappa|x|}$ outside in the odd case;\n\n(c) *range of energies.* There are no eigenvalues $E\\le-U$ and no eigenvalues\n$E\\ge0$; hence all eigenvalues of $H$ lie in $(-U,0)$ and are given by (b);\n\n(d) *bound count.* The number of negative eigenvalues of $H$ equals\n$\\Bigl\\lceil\\frac{2aK}{\\pi}\\Bigr\\rceil,$\nand more precisely the equations of (b) have exactly one solution $k$ in each\ninterval $\\bigl(\\frac{n\\pi}{2a},\\frac{(n+1)\\pi}{2a}\\bigr)$, $n\\ge0$, whose\nleft endpoint satisfies $\\frac{n\\pi}{2a}<K$, and no solution in $(0,K)$\nelsewhere; the solutions are alternatively of even type ($n$ even) and odd\ntype ($n$ odd).",
          "strategy": "Complete conditional argument authored on this page; see the item body for the numbered steps.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics, 1st edition 2009, Section 9.7, Corollary 9.43 p. 219 (finiteness background for short-range negative spectra; the square-well roots and exact count are proved locally)",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-schroe/schroe.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "J. Binney and D. Skinner, The Physics of Quantum Mechanics, Section 5.1 pp. 75-77, equations (5.3)-(5.8) (even/odd square-well matching; the potential is shifted by -U here, and threshold counting is proved locally)",
                "url": "https://www-thphys.physics.ox.ac.uk/people/JamesBinney/qb.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
