      "items": [
        {
          "id": "def-nrqm-coulomb-ltwo-kernel-operators",
          "kind": "definition",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "L^2 kernel operators and Hilbert-Schmidt operators on R^3",
          "dependency_level": 0,
          "deps": [
            "def-l-p-space-as-a-quotient-by-null-functions",
            "def-complex-lp-and-euclidean-test-function-conventions",
            "def-hilbert-space",
            "def-countable-choice",
            "thm-tonelli-and-fubini-for-completed-product-measures"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-l-p-space-as-a-quotient-by-null-functions": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-complex-lp-and-euclidean-test-function-conventions": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-hilbert-space": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-tonelli-and-fubini-for-completed-product-measures": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "aliases": [
            "nrqm-coulomb-ltwo-kernel-operators"
          ],
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "not-applicable"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics, 1st edition 2009, Section 6.3 pp. 139-145 (Hilbert-Schmidt operators defined as integral operators with L^2 kernels)",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-schroe/schroe.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "Theo Buehler and Dietmar A. Salamon, Functional Analysis (ETH lecture notes, 2017), Section 5.2.3 pp. 224-227 (the spectrum of a compact operator; finite-rank and norm-limit structure)",
                "url": "https://sci.mu.edu.iq/wp-content/uploads/2021/08/FUNCTIONAL-ANALYSIS-freebookcenter.net_.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Write\n$L^2=L^2(\\mathbb R^3;\\mathbb C)$ for the complex Hilbert space of Lebesgue\n(equivalence classes of) square-integrable functions with inner product\n$\\langle f,g\\rangle=\\int_{\\mathbb R^3}f\\overline g$ linear in the first\nargument ([[def-l-p-space-as-a-quotient-by-null-functions]],\n[[def-complex-lp-and-euclidean-test-function-conventions]],\n[[def-hilbert-space]]), and write $L^2(\\mathbb R^3\\times\\mathbb R^3;\\mathbb C)$\nfor the same construction over the product with Lebesgue measure; identify\nLebesgue measure on $\\mathbb R^6$ with the completion of the product of\nLebesgue measures on the two $\\mathbb R^3$ factors.\n\n**Kernel data and sections.** Let $k\\in L^2(\\mathbb R^3\\times\\mathbb R^3;\\mathbb C)$, an almost-everywhere equivalence class, and choose a finite-valued Lebesgue-measurable representative $k_0:\\mathbb R^3\\times\\mathbb R^3\\to\\mathbb C$. When $f\\in L^2$ is used, choose likewise a finite-valued Lebesgue-measurable representative $f_0:\\mathbb R^3\\to\\mathbb C$. For almost every $x\\in\\mathbb R^3$, the section $k_x(y):=k_0(x,y)$ is measurable, by applying the completed-product Fubini theorem to the positive and negative parts of the real and imaginary components of $k_0$ ([[thm-tonelli-and-fubini-for-completed-product-measures]]).\n\n**Domain and action.** For $f\\in L^2$ say that the integral defining $T_kf$\n*exists at* $x\\in\\mathbb R^3$ if the section product\n$y\\mapsto k_0(x,y)f_0(y)$ is measurable and lies in $L^1(\\mathbb R^3;\\mathbb C)$, and at such points put\n$$(T_kf)(x):=\\int_{\\mathbb R^3}k_0(x,y)f_0(y)\\,dy .$$\nDefine\n$$D(T_k):=\\Bigl\\{f\\in L^2:\\ x\\mapsto(T_kf)(x)\\ \\text{exists for almost every }x\\text{ and agrees a.e. with a class in }L^2\\Bigr\\},$$\nand for $f\\in D(T_k)$ let $T_kf$ denote that class. The assignment\n$f\\mapsto T_kf$ is called the *$L^2$-kernel operator with kernel $k$*.\n\nThis definition is independent of both representative choices. If $k_1$ is\nanother representative of $k$, its disagreement set with $k_0$ is null for the\ncompleted product Lebesgue measure. Fubini applied to the indicator of that\nset gives $k_0(x,\\cdot)=k_1(x,\\cdot)$ almost everywhere for almost every\n$x$. For each such $x$ and any representative of $f$, the two section products\ntherefore have the same $L^1$ status and, when integrable, the same integral.\nReplacing $f_0$ by another representative changes the section product only on\na null set of $y$, so it too preserves integrability and the integral.\nConsequently the almost-everywhere sections, the subset $D(T_k)\\subseteq L^2$,\nand the resulting output class are unchanged by either representative choice.\n\n**Hilbert-Schmidt operators.** A linear operator $T$ on $L^2$ is called a\n*Hilbert-Schmidt operator* if there is\n$k\\in L^2(\\mathbb R^3\\times\\mathbb R^3;\\mathbb C)$ with $D(T)=D(T_k)$ and\n$T=T_k$; such a $k$ is called an *$L^2$ kernel* of $T$.\n\nThis definition asserts nothing about whether $D(T_k)$ is all of $L^2$,\nwhether $T_k$ is bounded, or whether $T_k$ is compact; those properties are\nproved in [[lem-nrqm-coulomb-ltwo-kernel-operators-bounded-and-compact]]. A\nfinite product kernel $\\sum_{i=1}^nf_i(x)\\overline{g_i(y)}$ with\n$f_i,g_i\\in L^2$ is also a class in $L^2(\\mathbb R^3\\times\\mathbb R^3;\\mathbb C)$,\nas the same lemma records, so $T_k$ is defined for it whenever that membership\nis used.",
          "strategy": "Complete conditional argument authored on this page; see the item body for the numbered steps.",
          "inventory_expansion_required": true,
          "reference": "local prerequisite added by this batch (closure of the reserved claims)",
          "design_state": "batch-local prerequisite; complete-conditional-argument"
        },
        {
          "id": "lem-nrqm-coulomb-ltwo-kernel-operators-bounded-and-compact",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "L^2 kernel operators are bounded and compact",
          "dependency_level": 1,
          "deps": [
            "def-nrqm-coulomb-ltwo-kernel-operators",
            "cor-cauchy-schwarz-inequality-for-l-two",
            "thm-tonelli-and-fubini-for-completed-product-measures",
            "thm-rational-box-step-functions-form-a-countable-dense-subset-of-l-p-of-rn",
            "lem-finite-rank-operators-are-compact",
            "thm-norm-limit-of-compact-operators-is-compact",
            "def-compact-linear-operator",
            "def-bounded-linear-operator",
            "def-operator-norm",
            "def-l-p-space-as-a-quotient-by-null-functions",
            "def-complex-lp-and-euclidean-test-function-conventions",
            "def-hilbert-space",
            "def-countable-choice"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-nrqm-coulomb-ltwo-kernel-operators": "mathematical-premise",
            "cor-cauchy-schwarz-inequality-for-l-two": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-tonelli-and-fubini-for-completed-product-measures": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-rational-box-step-functions-form-a-countable-dense-subset-of-l-p-of-rn": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-finite-rank-operators-are-compact": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-norm-limit-of-compact-operators-is-compact": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-compact-linear-operator": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-bounded-linear-operator": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-operator-norm": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-l-p-space-as-a-quotient-by-null-functions": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-complex-lp-and-euclidean-test-function-conventions": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-hilbert-space": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "aliases": [
            "nrqm-coulomb-ltwo-kernel-operators-bounded-and-compact"
          ],
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics, 1st edition 2009, Section 6.3 pp. 139-145 (an integral operator with L^2 kernel is bounded with norm at most the L^2 norm of its kernel and is compact)",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-schroe/schroe.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "Theo Buehler and Dietmar A. Salamon, Functional Analysis (ETH lecture notes, 2017), Section 5.2.3 pp. 224-227 (finite-rank operators are compact; norm limits of compact operators are compact)",
                "url": "https://sci.mu.edu.iq/wp-content/uploads/2021/08/FUNCTIONAL-ANALYSIS-freebookcenter.net_.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let\n$L^2=L^2(\\mathbb R^3;\\mathbb C)$ and let\n$k\\in L^2(\\mathbb R^3\\times\\mathbb R^3;\\mathbb C)$, with $T_k$ the\n$L^2$-kernel operator of [[def-nrqm-coulomb-ltwo-kernel-operators]]. Then:\n\n(a) $D(T_k)=L^2$; $T_k$ is linear and bounded with\n$\\|T_kf\\|_2\\le\\|k\\|_{L^2(\\mathbb R^3\\times\\mathbb R^3)}\\|f\\|_2$ for every\n$f\\in L^2$, so $\\|T_k\\|\\le\\|k\\|_{L^2(\\mathbb R^3\\times\\mathbb R^3)}$;\n\n(b) if $n\\ge1$, $f_1,\\dots,f_n,g_1,\\dots,g_n\\in L^2$ and\n$k(x,y)=\\sum_{i=1}^nf_i(x)\\overline{g_i(y)}$ a.e., then $k$ is a class in\n$L^2(\\mathbb R^3\\times\\mathbb R^3;\\mathbb C)$, the range of $T_k$ is contained\nin $\\operatorname{span}\\{f_1,\\dots,f_n\\}$, and $T_k$ is compact;\n\n(c) $T_k$ is compact; and\n\n(d) for every sequence $(k_m)$ in\n$L^2(\\mathbb R^3\\times\\mathbb R^3;\\mathbb C)$ with\n$\\|k_m-k\\|_{L^2(\\mathbb R^3\\times\\mathbb R^3)}\\to0$ one has\n$T_{k_m}-T_k=T_{k_m-k}$ and\n$\\|T_{k_m}-T_k\\|\\le\\|k_m-k\\|_{L^2(\\mathbb R^3\\times\\mathbb R^3)}\\to0$; in\nparticular $T_k$ is the operator-norm limit of finite-rank kernel operators.\n\nNo statement is made about the spectrum of $T_k$, about its singular values,\nor about $L^2$ kernels of a given compact operator.",
          "strategy": "Complete conditional argument authored on this page; see the item body for the numbered steps.",
          "inventory_expansion_required": true,
          "reference": "local prerequisite added by this batch (closure of the reserved claims)",
          "design_state": "batch-local prerequisite; complete-conditional-argument"
        },
        {
          "id": "def-nrqm-coulomb-closed-semibounded-forms",
