          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "lem-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-cc-separable-spectral-calculus": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-self-adjoint-resolvent-estimate": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-orthogonal-decomposition-by-a-closed-subspace": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-symmetric-self-adjoint-and-essentially-self-adjoint": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-hilbert-space": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics, spectral calculus and unitary groups",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-schroe/schroe.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "aliases": [],
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $H$ be an arbitrary\ncomplex Hilbert space, with inner product linear in the first variable,\nand let $A=A^*$ be a densely defined self-adjoint operator on $H$.\nThere is no separability or supplied-basis hypothesis on $H$.\n\nThere is a unique regular projection-valued Borel measure $E_A$ on\n$\\mathbb R$ representing $A$, with $E_A(\\mathbb R)=I$, strong countable\nadditivity and\n\n$$D(A)=\\{x:\\int\\lambda^2d\\mu_x(\\lambda)<\\infty\\},\\qquad \\|Ax\\|^2=\\int\\lambda^2d\\mu_x,\\qquad \\mu_x(B)=\\langle E_A(B)x,x\\rangle.$$\n\nRegularity means compact inner and open outer approximation of each finite\nscalar measure $\\mu_x$. For bounded Borel $b$, its calculus satisfies\n$\\|b(A)\\|\\le\\sup|b|$, $(bc)(A)=b(A)c(A)$ and\n$\\overline b(A)=b(A)^*$. For finite-valued, possibly unbounded complex Borel\n$b$, there is a closed densely defined operator $b(A)$ on exactly\n$\\{x:\\int|b|^2d\\mu_x<\\infty\\}$, with norm given by that integral and\nconvergence of the bounded cutoffs on its domain.\n\nThe PVM is concentrated on $\\sigma(A)$, and a real $\\lambda$ belongs to $\\sigma(A)$ exactly when every neighborhood of $\\lambda$ has nonzero spectral projection. For $z\\notin\\sigma(A)$, the bounded resolvent is the multiplier $(\\lambda-z)^{-1}$, maps into exactly $D(A)$, and has norm at most $\\operatorname{dist}(z,\\sigma(A))^{-1}$ (with the zero-space convention $1/\\infty=0$).\n\nThe operators $U_A(t)=e^{itA}$ form a strongly continuous unitary group on\nall of $H$, with the exact derivative criterion\n\n$$\\lim_{t\\to0}\\frac{U_A(t)x-x}{t}\\text{ exists in }H\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad x\\in D(A),\\qquad \\left.\\frac{d}{dt}U_A(t)x\\right|_{t=0}=iAx.$$\n\nThey preserve $D(A)$ and its graph norm and commute with $A$ on that domain.\nThe group with this exact generator is unique. PVMs, Borel calculus and\ngroups transport under unitary intertwiners, and an isometry intertwining\nthe groups for all real times has a reducing closed range and intertwines\nthe PVMs. The construction uses countably generated subspaces attached to\neach finite tuple of vectors and their uniquely determined compatible\ncalculus; it does not choose an arbitrary global cyclic decomposition or\nan orthonormal basis of $H$.",
          "strategy": "Compatible vector-local Cayley restrictions; complete CC PVM/domain/group assembly and explicit spectrum support proved locally.",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "reference": "Exact root-authorized arbitrary-H CC prerequisite for contour/Feshbach repair",
          "design_state": "authored-local-prerequisite; full native stages pending"
        },
        {
          "id": "thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-allowed-region-wkb-coefficient-equation",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Allowed-region WKB coefficient equation",
          "dependency_level": 0,
          "deps": [
            "def-derivative",
            "def-continuity-real",
            "thm-chain-rule"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-derivative": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-continuity-real": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-chain-rule": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "aliases": [
            "nrqm-controlled-dynamics-allowed-region-wkb-coefficient-equation"
          ],
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "R. Fitzpatrick, Quantum Mechanics (University of Texas at Austin, author-hosted course text), The WKB Approximation pp. 70-73 (WKB wavefunctions in the classically allowed region and the second-order correction)",
                "url": "https://farside.ph.utexas.edu/teaching/qmech/qmech.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "F. W. J. Olver, Asymptotics and Special Functions, Chapter 6 (Liouville-Green approximation and error bounds; survey recorded via DLMF Chapter 2, https://dlmf.nist.gov/2)",
                "url": "https://dlmf.nist.gov/2"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Let $a<b$ be real numbers, let $p\\in C^2([a,b])$ with $p(x)>0$ for all\n$x\\in[a,b]$, let $h>0$, put $\\theta(x):=\\int_a^xp(s)\\,ds$ and\n$$w_\\pm(x):=p(x)^{-1/2}e^{\\pm i\\theta(x)/h},\\qquad q(x):=\\frac{3p'(x)^2}{4p(x)^2}-\\frac{p''(x)}{2p(x)}.$$\nThen:\n\n(a) $w_\\pm\\in C^2([a,b])$ and $w_\\pm''+\\dfrac{p^2}{h^2}w_\\pm=q\\,w_\\pm$ pointwise on\n$[a,b]$.\n\n(b) The Wronskian $W:=w_+w_-'-w_+'w_-$ equals $-2i/h$ on $[a,b]$.\n\n(c) Let $y\\in C^2([a,b])$ solve $y''+\\dfrac{p^2}{h^2}y=0$, let\n$M(x):=\\begin{pmatrix}w_+(x)&w_-(x)\\\\ w_+'(x)&w_-'(x)\\end{pmatrix}$ and\n$c(x):=\\bigl(c_+(x),c_-(x)\\bigr)^{\\mathsf T}:=M(x)^{-1}\\bigl(y(x),y'(x)\\bigr)^{\\mathsf T}$\n(well defined by (b)). Then $c\\in C^1([a,b];\\mathbb C^2)$ and $c'=B(x)c$ with\n$$B(x)=\\frac{q(x)}{W}\\begin{pmatrix}w_+(x)w_-(x)&w_-(x)^2\\\\ -w_+(x)^2&-w_+(x)w_-(x)\\end{pmatrix},$$\nand with $\\|\\cdot\\|_1$ the $\\ell^1$ norm on $\\mathbb C^2$ one has\n$\\|B(x)\\|_1=\\dfrac{h|q(x)|}{p(x)}$ for every $x\\in[a,b]$.\n\nIn particular $y=w_+c_++w_-c_-$, and the coefficient system is a nonsingular\nlinear ODE with explicitly bounded coefficients. No approximation of $y$ and no\nphysical interpretation is asserted here.",
          "strategy": "Complete conditional argument authored on this page; see the item body for the numbered steps.",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "reference": "reserved claim of the qm-math-controlled-dynamics design reservation; complete-conditional-argument",
          "design_state": "reserved-closure; complete-conditional-argument"
        },
        {
          "id": "thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-common-domain-nonautonomous-evolution",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Common-domain nonautonomous evolution",
          "dependency_level": 0,
