          ],
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics, 1st edition 2009, Chapter 5 pp. 123-131 (generators of unitary groups) and Section 6.6 pp. 153-159 (norm resolvent convergence)",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-schroe/schroe.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "T. Kato, Linear Operators and Their Applications, Chapter 2 (evolution equations with a constant domain; standard reference for the propagator construction)",
                "url": "https://sci.mu.edu.iq/wp-content/uploads/2021/08/FUNCTIONAL-ANALYSIS-freebookcenter.net_.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $H$ be a\ncomplex Hilbert space, let $Y$ be a dense linear subspace of $H$ that is itself\na Hilbert space continuously embedded in $H$ (for instance $Y=D(A_0)$ with the\ngraph norm of a self-adjoint $A_0$), let $T>0$, and let $A(t)$ for\n$t\\in[0,T]$ be an operator with $D(A(t))=Y$, self-adjoint as an operator on $H$,\nsuch that $t\\mapsto A(t)$ belongs to $C^1([0,T];\\mathcal B(Y,H))$\n([[def-bounded-linear-operator]], [[def-operator-norm]],\n[[def-symmetric-self-adjoint-and-essentially-self-adjoint]]). Put $L:=\\sup_t\\|A'(t)\\|_{\\mathcal B(Y,H)}$.\nThen:\n\n(a) *Existence and uniqueness of a strong propagator.* There is a family\n$U(t,s)$, $0\\le s\\le t\\le T$, of unitary operators on $H$ with:\n$U(s,s)=I$; $U(t,s)U(s,r)=U(t,r)$; $(t,s)\\mapsto U(t,s)\\xi$ continuous on\n$\\{s\\le t\\}$ for each $\\xi\\in H$; $U(t,s)Y=Y$ with\n$\\|U(t,s)y\\|_Y\\le C_T\\|y\\|_Y$ for a constant $C_T$ independent of\n$(s,t)\\in[0,T]^2$; and for every $y\\in Y$ the map $t\\mapsto U(t,s)y$ is $C^1$\nin $H$ with\n$$i\\,\\partial_tU(t,s)y=A(t)U(t,s)y,\\qquad s\\le t\\le T.$$\n\n(b) *Uniqueness.* If $V(t,s)$ is another family of bounded linear operators on $H$ with the same strong equation\non $Y$, $V(s,s)=I$ and $\\sup_{r}\\|V(r,s)y\\|_{H}<\\infty$, then $V=U$.\n\n(c) *Equations for the reverse and adjoint.* $U(t,s)Y=Y$ for all $0\\le s\\le t\\le T$\nand $U(s,t):=U(t,s)^{-1}$ satisfies $i\\partial_sU(s,t)y=A(s)U(s,t)y$ for\n$y\\in Y$; $U(t,s)^*=U(s,t)$. Equivalently, differentiating the second\nargument of the forward propagator gives $i\\partial_sU(t,s)y=-U(t,s)A(s)y$.\nThe domain maps are jointly strongly continuous in $Y$.\n\nThe theorem is stated for the abstract family $A$; a physical generator is\nobtained by $A=H_{\\mathrm{energy}}/\\hbar$ after choosing a time unit.",
          "strategy": "Complete conditional argument authored on this page; see the item body for the numbered steps.",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "reference": "reserved claim of the qm-math-controlled-dynamics design reservation; complete-conditional-argument",
          "design_state": "reserved-closure; complete-conditional-argument"
        },
        {
          "id": "thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-norm-dyson-series-and-uniqueness",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Norm Dyson series and uniqueness",
          "dependency_level": 0,
          "deps": [
            "thm-riesz-representation-for-hilbert-space",
            "lem-fundamental-theorem-of-calculus-for-banach-valued-continuous-curves",
