          },
          "aliases": [
            "nrqm-controlled-dynamics-dyson-truncation-bound"
          ],
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics, 1st edition 2009, Chapter 5 pp. 123-131 (quantum dynamics; existence, uniqueness and norm bounds for time-ordered evolution)",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-schroe/schroe.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "R. Fitzpatrick, Quantum Mechanics (University of Texas at Austin, author-hosted course text), Perturbation Expansion pp. 180-182 (the Dyson-type expansion and its truncation as an approximation scheme)",
                "url": "https://farside.ph.utexas.edu/teaching/qmech/qmech.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]) and adopt the hypotheses and corrected latest-time-left notation of [[thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-norm-dyson-series-and-uniqueness]]: $H$ is an arbitrary complex Hilbert space, $I=[a,b]$ a nonempty compact interval, $\\hbar>0$, and $\\mathcal H:I\\to\\mathcal B(H)$ is norm-continuous with bounded self-adjoint values. Write $A(r)=-i\\mathcal H(r)/\\hbar$, $K=\\sup_{r\\in I}\\|A(r)\\|$, $U_0=I_H$, and $U_{n+1}(t,s)=\\int_s^tA(r)U_n(r,s)dr$ with oriented integrals. The norm-convergent sum $U=\\sum_{n\\ge0}U_n$ is the unitary propagator of that supplier. For $N\\in\\mathbb N_0$, put $R_N(t,s)=U(t,s)-\\sum_{n=0}^NU_n(t,s)$. Then for all $s,t\\in I$:\n\n(a) *Exact oriented remainder.*\n$$R_N(t,s)=\\int_s^t dr_1\\int_s^{r_1}dr_2\\cdots\\int_s^{r_N}dr_{N+1}\\,A(r_1)\\cdots A(r_{N+1})U(r_{N+1},s).$$\nFor $N=0$ this means the single integral $\\int_s^tA(r_1)U(r_1,s)dr_1$. For $s\\le t$, relabeling $t_j=r_{N+2-j}$ gives the corrected ordered-simplex identity\n$$R_N(t,s)=\\Bigl(\\frac{-i}{\\hbar}\\Bigr)^{N+1}\\int_{s<t_1<\\cdots<t_{N+1}<t}\\mathcal H(t_{N+1})\\cdots\\mathcal H(t_1)U(t_1,s)\\,dt_1\\cdots dt_{N+1},$$\nwhere $t_{N+1}$ is outermost, $t_1$ innermost, and the residual propagator is evaluated at the **earliest** integration time on the right. The universal nested formula specifies signs and operator order for $t<s$ as well.\n\n(b) *Truncation bound.* With $\\tau=|t-s|$,\n$$\\|R_N(t,s)\\|\\le e^{K\\tau}\\frac{(K\\tau)^{N+1}}{(N+1)!}.$$\nIn fact unitarity under the actual stated self-adjoint hypotheses also gives the stronger bound $\\|R_N(t,s)\\|\\le(K\\tau)^{N+1}/(N+1)!$. The original exponential estimate is retained for every $s\\le t$.\n\nIn particular $\\|U(t,s)-I_H-U_1(t,s)\\|\\le e^{K\\tau}(K\\tau)^2/2$. If the family is scaled to $\\lambda\\mathcal H(t)$ with a real coupling $\\lambda$, the same conclusion holds with $K$ replaced by $|\\lambda|K$, so the first-order error is $O(|\\lambda|^2\\tau^2)$ uniformly when $|\\lambda|K\\tau$ remains bounded, with explicit multiplier $e^{|\\lambda|K\\tau}/2$. The stronger bound has multiplier $1/2$. Both time orientations, negative absolute times, $t=s$, $K=0$, the zero Hilbert space and a singleton $I$ are included.",
          "strategy": "Complete conditional argument authored on this page; see the item body for the numbered steps.",
