          },
          "aliases": [
            "nrqm-controlled-dynamics-airy-contour-and-fresnel-normalization"
          ],
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "NIST Digital Library of Mathematical Functions, Section 9.2 'Differential Equation' (Airy's equation A''=zA and its solutions)",
                "url": "https://dlmf.nist.gov/9.2"
              },
              {
                "title": "NIST Digital Library of Mathematical Functions, Section 9.5 'Integral Representations' (Airy contour integrals and Fresnel normalization)",
                "url": "https://dlmf.nist.gov/9.5"
              },
              {
                "title": "F. W. J. Olver, Asymptotics and Special Functions (1974), Chapters 4 and 11 (Airy functions and their asymptotics) — classical monograph treatment consulted through the DLMF survey of the same theory",
                "url": "https://dlmf.nist.gov/9.7"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $C$ be the\ncontour in $\\mathbb C$ from $\\infty e^{-i\\pi/3}$ through $0$ to $\\infty e^{i\\pi/3}$\nand define\n$$A(z):=\\frac1{2\\pi i}\\int_Ce^{t^3/3-zt}\\,dt .$$\nThen:\n\n(a) the integral converges absolutely on compact sets and $A$ is entire with\n$A''(z)=zA(z)$;\n\n(b) for real $z$, after deforming each ray to the imaginary axis,\n$$A(z)=\\frac1{2\\pi}\\int_{\\mathbb R}e^{i(t^3/3+zt)}\\,dt$$\nas a convergent oscillatory improper integral. Its first $z$-derivative also\nconverges uniformly on compact real sets. Higher derivatives are defined by\nthe absolutely convergent contour representation in (a), or equivalently by\ndifferentiating the oscillatory representation as a distribution; they are\nnot asserted to be ordinary convergent improper integrals;\n\n(c) as $Z\\to+\\infty$,\n$$A(Z)=\\frac1{2\\sqrt\\pi}Z^{-1/4}e^{-2Z^{3/2}/3}\\bigl(1+O(Z^{-3/2})\\bigr),\\qquad A'(Z)=-\\frac1{2\\sqrt\\pi}Z^{1/4}e^{-2Z^{3/2}/3}\\bigl(1+O(Z^{-3/2})\\bigr);$$\n\n(d) as $Z\\to+\\infty$, with $\\Theta:=2Z^{3/2}/3+\\pi/4$,\n$$A(-Z)=\\frac1{\\sqrt\\pi}Z^{-1/4}\\bigl(\\sin\\Theta+O(Z^{-3/2})\\bigr),\\qquad A'(-Z)=-\\frac1{\\sqrt\\pi}Z^{1/4}\\bigl(\\cos\\Theta+O(Z^{-3/2})\\bigr).$$\n\nThe error terms are absolute envelope errors and are not relative errors at the\nzeros of $A(-Z)$.",
          "strategy": "Complete conditional argument authored on this page; see the item body for the numbered steps.",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "reference": "reserved claim of the qm-math-controlled-dynamics design reservation; complete-conditional-argument",
          "design_state": "reserved-closure; complete-conditional-argument"
        },
        {
          "id": "thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-contour-perturbation-projection",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Contour perturbation projection",
          "dependency_level": 2,
          "deps": [
            "lem-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-cc-arbitrary-hilbert-spectral-calculus",
            "thm-circle-integrals-of-integer-monomials",
