            "def-bounded-linear-operator": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-operator-norm": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-cauchy-integral-formula-circle": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-symmetric-self-adjoint-and-essentially-self-adjoint": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-hilbert-space": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "aliases": [
            "nrqm-controlled-dynamics-contour-perturbation-projection"
          ],
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics, 1st edition 2009, Section 6.6 pp. 153-159 (strong and norm resolvent convergence; analytic perturbation via contour integrals)",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-schroe/schroe.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "T. Kato, Perturbation Theory for Linear Operators, Chapter II (analytic perturbation theory of isolated eigenvalues, surveyed via Buehler-Salamon, Functional Analysis, ETH lecture notes 2017, Section 5.3)",
                "url": "https://sci.mu.edu.iq/wp-content/uploads/2021/08/FUNCTIONAL-ANALYSIS-freebookcenter.net_.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $H$ be an arbitrary complex Hilbert space, let $H_0$ be self-adjoint on its exact dense domain, and use the resolvent convention $R_0(z)=(z-H_0)^{-1}$. Let $E\\in\\mathbb R$ be an isolated eigenvalue with $\\operatorname{dist}(E,\\sigma(H_0)\\setminus\\{E\\})\\ge g>0$, and suppose its orthogonal spectral projection $P_0=E_{H_0}(\\{E\\})$ has rank one. Let $V\\in\\mathcal B(H)$ be self-adjoint with $v=\\|V\\|>0$, put $H_\\lambda=H_0+\\lambda V$ on $D(H_0)$, and let $\\lambda\\in\\mathbb C$ satisfy $q=2|\\lambda|v/g<1$. Write $\\Gamma$ for the counterclockwise circle $|z-E|=g/2$. Then:\n\n(a) $H_\\lambda$ is closed and densely defined. For every $z\\in\\Gamma$, $z-H_\\lambda$ is a bijection from $D(H_0)$ onto $H$, with\n$$R_\\lambda(z)=(z-H_\\lambda)^{-1}=R_0(z)\\sum_{k\\ge0}(\\lambda VR_0(z))^k,\\qquad \\|R_\\lambda(z)\\|\\le\\frac{2/g}{1-q},\\qquad \\|R_\\lambda(z)-R_0(z)\\|\\le\\frac{2}{g}\\frac{q}{1-q}.$$\nThe series converges in operator norm uniformly on $\\Gamma$ and locally uniformly in the complex disk $|\\lambda|<g/(2v)$.\n\n(b) The operator\n$$P_\\lambda=\\frac1{2\\pi i}\\oint_\\Gamma R_\\lambda(z)dz$$\nis an operator-norm holomorphic, rank-one Riesz projection throughout that disk. Its range lies in $D(H_0)$ and is invariant under $H_\\lambda$, and it commutes with $H_\\lambda$ on $D(H_0)$. There is exactly one spectral value $E_\\lambda$ inside $\\Gamma$; it is an eigenvalue of algebraic multiplicity one, with $\\operatorname{ran}P_\\lambda=\\ker(H_\\lambda-E_\\lambda)$. The function $\\lambda\\mapsto E_\\lambda$ is holomorphic.\n\n(c) $\\|P_\\lambda-P_0\\|\\le q/(1-q)$. Rank one holds for every $q<1$, including when this bound is at least one. Whenever two projections $P_\\lambda,P_\\mu$ have distance less than one, the restrictions $P_\\mu|_{\\operatorname{ran}P_\\lambda}$ and $P_\\lambda|_{\\operatorname{ran}P_\\mu}$ are injective; local comparisons along the path $t\\lambda$, $0\\le t\\le1$, preserve the rank throughout the full disk.\n\n(d) For real $\\lambda$, $H_\\lambda$ is self-adjoint on $D(H_0)$, $E_\\lambda$ is real, and $P_\\lambda=E_{H_\\lambda}(\\{E_\\lambda\\})$ is its orthogonal spectral projection. For complex $\\lambda$, $P_\\lambda$ is the Riesz projection; self-adjointness or orthogonality is not asserted.\n\nNo separability or Axiom of Choice assumption on $H$ is added. Degenerate clusters are outside this rank-one statement.",
          "strategy": "Complete conditional argument authored on this page; see the item body for the numbered steps.",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "reference": "reserved claim of the qm-math-controlled-dynamics design reservation; complete-conditional-argument",
          "design_state": "reserved-closure; complete-conditional-argument"
        },
        {
          "id": "thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-cook-domain-criterion",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Cook domain criterion",
          "dependency_level": 0,
          "deps": [
            "thm-self-adjoint-resolvent-estimate",
            "thm-riesz-representation-for-hilbert-space",
            "def-symmetric-self-adjoint-and-essentially-self-adjoint",
            "def-adjoint-of-a-densely-defined-unbounded-operator",
