          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "thm-self-adjoint-resolvent-estimate": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-riesz-representation-for-hilbert-space": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-symmetric-self-adjoint-and-essentially-self-adjoint": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-adjoint-of-a-densely-defined-unbounded-operator": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-hilbert-space": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-fundamental-theorem-of-calculus-for-banach-valued-continuous-curves": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "aliases": [
            "nrqm-controlled-dynamics-cook-domain-criterion"
          ],
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics, 1st edition 2009, Lemma 12.3 p. 248 (Cook's criterion) and Section 5.1 pp. 123-126 (Stone's theorem)",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-schroe/schroe.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "R. Fitzpatrick, Quantum Mechanics (University of Texas at Austin, author-hosted course text), Scattering Theory pp. 209-211 (scattering states and the scattering operator)",
                "url": "https://farside.ph.utexas.edu/teaching/qmech/qmech.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). To distinguish the Hilbert space from the interacting operator,\nwrite the space as $\\mathcal H$, the free operator as $A_0$, and the\ninteracting operator as $A$. Both are self-adjoint, with\n$D(A_0)\\subseteq D(A)$. Let $D\\subseteq D(A_0)$ be a dense linear\nsubspace of $\\mathcal H$, invariant under $e^{-itA_0}$ for every real $t$.\nFor every $\\psi\\in D$, suppose\n$b_\\psi(t)=(A-A_0)e^{-itA_0}\\psi$ is norm-continuous on $\\mathbb R$,\nand its norm is integrable on both half-lines. Define\n\n$$F(t)=e^{itA}e^{-itA_0}.$$\n\nThen $\\Omega_\\pm\\psi=\\lim_{t\\to\\pm\\infty}F(t)\\psi$ exist on $D$ and,\nfor every $s\\ge0$, satisfy the full original estimates\n\n$$\\|\\Omega_+\\psi-F(s)\\psi\\|\\le\\int_s^\\infty\\|b_\\psi(t)\\|dt,\\qquad \\|\\Omega_-\\psi-F(-s)\\psi\\|\\le\\int_{-\\infty}^{-s}\\|b_\\psi(t)\\|dt.$$\n\nThey extend uniquely to bounded linear isometries on all $\\mathcal H$,\nwith $\\Omega_\\pm^*\\Omega_\\pm=I$, injectivity and closed ranges. The\nextensions are the full strong limits of $F(t)$ in the two time directions.\nNo separability, AC, range equality, spectral-type conclusion or asymptotic\ncompleteness is imposed or inferred.\n\nFor the consuming intertwining/domain argument, the same construction also\nproves the consequence\n\n$$e^{-i\\tau A}\\Omega_\\pm=\\Omega_\\pm e^{-i\\tau A_0},\\qquad D(A)\\cap\\operatorname{ran}\\Omega_\\pm=\\Omega_\\pm D(A_0),\\qquad A\\Omega_\\pm\\eta=\\Omega_\\pm A_0\\eta\\quad(\\eta\\in D(A_0)).$$\n\nThis last displayed domain equality is restricted to the wave range; it\ndoes not assert that $\\Omega_\\pm$ is onto $\\mathcal H$.",
          "strategy": "Complete conditional argument authored on this page; see the item body for the numbered steps.",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "reference": "reserved claim of the qm-math-controlled-dynamics design reservation; complete-conditional-argument",
          "design_state": "reserved-closure; complete-conditional-argument"
        },
        {
          "id": "thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-finite-gapped-adiabatic-estimate",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Finite gapped adiabatic estimate",
          "dependency_level": 0,
          "deps": [
            "thm-cauchy-integral-formula-circle",
            "def-self-adjoint-and-normal-endomorphism",
            "def-operator-norm",
            "def-bounded-linear-operator",
