          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "thm-cauchy-integral-formula-circle": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-self-adjoint-and-normal-endomorphism": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-operator-norm": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-bounded-linear-operator": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-hilbert-space": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "aliases": [
            "nrqm-controlled-dynamics-finite-gapped-adiabatic-estimate"
          ],
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "R. Fitzpatrick, Quantum Mechanics (University of Texas at Austin, author-hosted course text), Two-State System pp. 153-155 (adiabatic evolution as the slow limit)",
                "url": "https://farside.ph.utexas.edu/teaching/qmech/qmech.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "T. Kato, Perturbation Theory for Linear Operators, Chapter II.4 (adiabatic theorem for a nondegenerate isolated level; standard analytic perturbation treatment)",
                "url": "https://sci.mu.edu.iq/wp-content/uploads/2021/08/FUNCTIONAL-ANALYSIS-freebookcenter.net_.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let\n$H:[0,1]\\to\\operatorname{Herm}(\\mathbb C^d)$ be a map of class $C^2$ into the\nHermitian $d\\times d$ matrices, let $P(s)$ be the spectral projection of $H(s)$\nfor a spectral cluster $\\sigma_P(s)$ that is separated from the complementary\nspectrum by a uniform gap: $\\operatorname{dist}(\\sigma_P(s),\\sigma(H(s))\\setminus\\sigma_P(s))\\ge g>0$\nfor all $s\\in[0,1]$. Require that the cluster is followed coherently:\n$P(s)$ is continuous in operator norm (equivalently, it follows the local\nRiesz continuation of its initial cluster). Fix $T>0$. Let $U_T$ solve\n$i\\,\\partial_sU_T(s)=TH(s)U_T(s)$, $U_T(0)=I$\nby the finite matrix construction below, and let\n$U_A$ solve $i\\,\\partial_sU_A(s)=\\bigl(TH(s)+i[P'(s),P(s)]\\bigr)U_A(s)$,\n$U_A(0)=I$ (equivalently $U_A'=(-iTH+K)U_A$ with $K=[P',P]$). Then:\n\n(a) $P\\in C^2([0,1];\\operatorname{End}(\\mathbb C^d))$ and $K=[P',P]$ is\nanti-Hermitian of class $C^1$ with $[K,P]=P'$.\n\n(b) There is a $C^1$ Hermitian $X:[0,1]\\to\\operatorname{End}(\\mathbb C^d)$ with\n$[H(s),X(s)]=K(s)$ for all $s$.\n\n(c) *Intertwining.* $P(s)U_A(s)=U_A(s)P(0)$ for all $s$.\n\n(d) *Adiabatic estimate.* With\n$C:=2\\sup_s\\|X(s)\\|+\\int_0^1\\bigl(\\|X'(s)\\|+\\|K(s)\\|\\|X(s)\\|\\bigr)ds$ one has\n$$\\bigl\\|(I-P(s))U_T(s)P(0)\\bigr\\|\\le\\frac CT\\qquad(s\\in[0,1]).$$\n\nThe estimate is finite-dimensional and conditional on the uniform positive gap;\ngap-closing families and unbounded families are not covered.",
          "strategy": "Complete conditional argument authored on this page; see the item body for the numbered steps.",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "reference": "reserved claim of the qm-math-controlled-dynamics design reservation; complete-conditional-argument",
          "design_state": "reserved-closure; complete-conditional-argument"
        },
        {
          "id": "thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-free-gaussian-dispersive-kernel",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Free Gaussian dispersive kernel",
          "dependency_level": 1,
          "deps": [
