          },
          "aliases": [
            "nrqm-controlled-dynamics-free-gaussian-dispersive-kernel"
          ],
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics, 1st edition 2009, Section 7.2 pp. 167-171 (the free Schrodinger operator, its propagator kernel and the resolvent)",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-schroe/schroe.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "R. Fitzpatrick, Quantum Mechanics (University of Texas at Austin, author-hosted course text), Evolution of Wave Packets pp. 29-32 (the spreading Gaussian free packet)",
                "url": "https://farside.ph.utexas.edu/teaching/qmech/qmech.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let\n$H_0=-\\Delta$ on $L^2(\\mathbb R^3;\\mathbb C)$ with $D(H_0)=W^{2,2}(\\mathbb R^3;\\mathbb C)$\n([[thm-fourier-characterisation-of-integer-order-hilbert-sobolev-spaces]]),\nlet $\\mathcal F_2$ be the Plancherel transform with\n$\\widehat f(\\xi)=\\int f(x)e^{-2\\pi ix\\cdot\\xi}dx$ on $L^1$\n([[def-fourier-transform-on-l-one-of-rn]], [[thm-plancherel]]), so that\n$H_0=\\mathcal F_2^*M_{4\\pi^2|\\xi|^2}\\mathcal F_2$, and let $t\\in\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{0\\}$. Define, for\n$\\psi\\in L^1\\cap L^2(\\mathbb R^3)$ and a.e. $x$,\n$$(K_t\\psi)(x):=(4\\pi it)^{-3/2}\\int_{\\mathbb R^3}e^{i|x-y|^2/(4t)}\\psi(y)\\,dy,$$\nwhere $(4\\pi it)^{-3/2}:=\\exp\\bigl(-\\tfrac32\\operatorname{Log}(4\\pi it)\\bigr)$\nis the principal branch ([[def-complex-logarithms-principal-logarithm-and-complex-powers]]).\nThen:\n\n(a) $K_t\\psi\\in L^2$ and $\\|K_t\\psi\\|_2=\\|\\psi\\|_2$; consequently $K_t$ extends\nuniquely to a unitary operator $\\widehat U_t$ on $L^2$, and\n$\\widehat U_t=e^{-itH_0}$ in the sense of the functional calculus of the free\noperator.\n\n(b) For every $\\psi\\in L^1\\cap L^2$ the representative $K_t\\psi$ is\neverywhere defined and bounded with\n$$\\|K_t\\psi\\|_\\infty\\le(4\\pi|t|)^{-3/2}\\|\\psi\\|_1.$$\n\n(c) For every $\\psi\\in D(H_0)$ one has $e^{-itH_0}\\psi\\in D(H_0)$ and\n$\\|H_0e^{-itH_0}\\psi\\|_2=\\|H_0\\psi\\|_2$.\n\nNo physical interpretation and no point-particle trajectory is asserted.",
          "strategy": "Complete conditional argument authored on this page; see the item body for the numbered steps.",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "reference": "reserved claim of the qm-math-controlled-dynamics design reservation; complete-conditional-argument",
          "design_state": "reserved-closure; complete-conditional-argument"
        },
