        {
          "id": "thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-two-level-rabi-model",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Two-level Rabi model",
          "dependency_level": 1,
          "deps": [
            "prop-nrqm-orbital-and-spin-finite-spin-matrices",
            "def-bounded-linear-operator",
            "def-operator-norm",
            "def-hilbert-space"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "prop-nrqm-orbital-and-spin-finite-spin-matrices": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-bounded-linear-operator": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-operator-norm": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-hilbert-space": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "aliases": [
            "nrqm-controlled-dynamics-two-level-rabi-model"
          ],
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "R. Fitzpatrick, Quantum Mechanics (University of Texas at Austin, author-hosted course text), Two-State System pp. 153-155 and Spin Magnetic Resonance pp. 178-180 (exact two-level evolution and Rabi oscillations)",
                "url": "https://farside.ph.utexas.edu/teaching/qmech/qmech.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "C. Cohen-Tannoudji, B. Diu, F. Laloe, Quantum Mechanics I, Chapter IV (two-level systems and the Rabi formula; standard textbook reference)"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Let $\\sigma_x,\\sigma_y,\\sigma_z$ be the Pauli matrices of\n[[prop-nrqm-orbital-and-spin-finite-spin-matrices]] (e), acting on\n$\\mathbb C^2$, and let $\\hbar>0$, $\\delta,\\Omega\\in\\mathbb R$. Put\n$$H:=\\frac{\\hbar}{2}\\bigl(\\delta\\sigma_z+\\Omega\\sigma_x\\bigr),\\qquad b:=\\sqrt{\\delta^2+\\Omega^2}.$$\nThen:\n\n(a) $H^2=\\frac{\\hbar^2b^2}{4}I$ and the unitary group generated by $-iH/\\hbar$ is\n$$U(t)=\\cos\\!\\Bigl(\\frac{bt}{2}\\Bigr)I-\\frac{i}{b}\\sin\\!\\Bigl(\\frac{bt}{2}\\Bigr) \\bigl(\\delta\\sigma_z+\\Omega\\sigma_x\\bigr),$$\nwhich solves $i\\hbar U'(t)=HU(t)$, $U(0)=I$; if $b=0$ the formula is read as\n$U(t)=I$.\n\n(b) *Squared transition amplitude.* Put $e_{\\uparrow}=(1,0)^{\\mathsf T}$ and\n$e_{\\downarrow}=(0,1)^{\\mathsf T}$, and use the inner product linear in its\nfirst argument from the Pauli supplier. Define the squared transition amplitude by\n$$p_{\\downarrow}(t)=\\bigl|\\langle e_{\\downarrow},U(t)e_{\\uparrow}\\rangle\\bigr|^2 =\\frac{\\Omega^2}{b^2}\\sin^2\\!\\Bigl(\\frac{bt}{2}\\Bigr)\\qquad(b>0).$$\nFor $b=0$ it is $p_{\\downarrow}(t)=0$ for every real $t$.\n\n(c) *Periodicity.* For $b>0$ one has $U(t+2\\pi/b)=-U(t)$; the propagator is\n$2\\pi/b$-periodic up to the central sign $-I$, and every squared transition amplitude\nis $2\\pi/b$-periodic.\n\nThese are the exact mathematical dynamics of the stipulated finite matrix model;\nno physical identification of $\\delta,\\Omega$ with a field or detuning and no\nmeasurement statistics is asserted.",
          "strategy": "Complete conditional argument authored on this page; see the item body for the numbered steps.",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "reference": "reserved claim of the qm-math-controlled-dynamics design reservation; complete-conditional-argument",
          "design_state": "reserved-closure; complete-conditional-argument"
        },
        {
          "id": "thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-wkb-explicit-error",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "WKB explicit error",
          "dependency_level": 1,
          "deps": [
