          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "R. Fitzpatrick, Quantum Mechanics (University of Texas at Austin, author-hosted course text), The WKB Approximation pp. 70-73 (validity of the WKB approximation in the classically allowed region)",
                "url": "https://farside.ph.utexas.edu/teaching/qmech/qmech.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "F. W. J. Olver, Asymptotics and Special Functions, Chapter 6 (error bounds for the Liouville-Green approximation; survey via DLMF Chapter 2, https://dlmf.nist.gov/2)",
                "url": "https://dlmf.nist.gov/2"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Adopt the hypotheses and notation of\n[[thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-allowed-region-wkb-coefficient-equation]]: $p\\in\nC^2([a,b])$ positive, $h>0$, $\\theta(x)=\\int_a^xp$, $w_\\pm=p^{-1/2}e^{\\pm\ni\\theta/h}$, $q=\\frac{3p'^2}{4p^2}-\\frac{p''}{2p}$, $M$ the fundamental matrix\nof $(w_+,w_-)$ and $c=M^{-1}(y,y')^{\\mathsf T}$ the coefficient curve of an exact\nsolution $y\\in C^2([a,b])$ of $y''+\\frac{p^2}{h^2}y=0$. Then for every\n$x\\in[a,b]$:\n\n(a) *Growth bound.* $\\|c(x)\\|_1\\le\\|c(a)\\|_1\\exp\\Bigl(h\\displaystyle\\int_a^x\n\\frac{|q(s)|}{p(s)}\\,ds\\Bigr)$.\n\n(b) *Deviation bound.*\n$$\\|c(x)-c(a)\\|_1\\le\\|c(a)\\|_1\\Bigl(\\exp\\Bigl(h\\int_a^x\\frac{|q(s)|}{p(s)}\\,ds\\Bigr)-1\\Bigr).$$\n\n(c) *Pointwise wavefunction error.* With $\\Psi(x):=c_+(a)w_+(x)+c_-(a)w_-(x)$\nthe leading WKB wave,\n$$|y(x)-\\Psi(x)|\\le p(x)^{-1/2}\\|c(a)\\|_1\\Bigl(\\exp\\Bigl(h\\int_a^x\\frac{|q(s)|}{p(s)}\\,ds\\Bigr)-1\\Bigr).$$\n\nThe estimate degenerates as $p\\to0$ (turning points are excluded by the\nhypotheses) and asserts nothing about connecting asymptotics across a turning\npoint; it is an explicit finite-interval error bound of Gronwall type.",
          "strategy": "Complete conditional argument authored on this page; see the item body for the numbered steps.",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "reference": "reserved claim of the qm-math-controlled-dynamics design reservation; complete-conditional-argument",
          "design_state": "reserved-closure; complete-conditional-argument"
        },
        {
          "id": "thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-airy-envelopes-and-asymptotic-coefficients",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Airy envelopes and asymptotic coefficients",
          "dependency_level": 2,
          "deps": [
            "thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-airy-contour-and-fresnel-normalization",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-complex-gaussian-continuation",
