            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "aliases": [
            "nrqm-controlled-dynamics-airy-envelopes-and-asymptotic-coefficients"
          ],
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "NIST Digital Library of Mathematical Functions, Sections 9.2, 9.7 (Airy function integral representations, Wronskians and asymptotic expansions)",
                "url": "https://dlmf.nist.gov/9.7"
              },
              {
                "title": "F. W. J. Olver, Asymptotics and Special Functions, Chapter 11 (uniform Airy asymptotics; standard monograph)",
                "url": "https://dlmf.nist.gov/9.7"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $A$ be the\nentire Airy function of\n[[thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-airy-contour-and-fresnel-normalization]] and\ndefine, for real $z$,\n$$B(z):=\\frac1\\pi\\int_0^\\infty\\Bigl[\\exp\\bigl(-t^3/3+zt\\bigr)+\\sin\\bigl(t^3/3+zt\\bigr)\\Bigr]dt .$$\nThen:\n\n(a) $B$ is well defined and smooth on $\\mathbb R$, extends to an entire\nsolution of $B''=zB$, and the Wronskian identity\n$$A(z)B'(z)-A'(z)B(z)=\\frac1\\pi$$\nholds for all complex $z$;\n\n(b) as $Z\\to+\\infty$, with $\\Theta=2Z^{3/2}/3+\\pi/4$,\n$$B(Z)=\\frac1{\\sqrt\\pi}Z^{-1/4}e^{2Z^{3/2}/3}\\bigl(1+O(Z^{-3/2})\\bigr),\\quad B'(Z)=\\frac1{\\sqrt\\pi}Z^{1/4}e^{2Z^{3/2}/3}\\bigl(1+O(Z^{-3/2})\\bigr),$$\n$$B(-Z)=\\frac1{\\sqrt\\pi}Z^{-1/4}\\bigl(\\cos\\Theta+O(Z^{-3/2})\\bigr),\\quad B'(-Z)=\\frac1{\\sqrt\\pi}Z^{1/4}\\bigl(\\sin\\Theta+O(Z^{-3/2})\\bigr);$$\n\n(c) *Envelopes.* With $p(z):=1+|z|$ and $S(z):=\\frac23(z_+)^{3/2}$ there is a\nconstant $C<\\infty$ with\n$$|A(z)|\\le Cp(z)^{-1/4}e^{-S(z)},\\quad|B(z)|\\le Cp(z)^{-1/4}e^{S(z)},\\quad |A'(z)|\\le Cp(z)^{1/4}e^{-S(z)},\\quad|B'(z)|\\le Cp(z)^{1/4}e^{S(z)}$$\nfor all real $z$, and there is $c>0$ with\n$A(z)\\ge cp(z)^{-1/4}e^{-S(z)}$ for $z\\ge0$.",
          "strategy": "Complete conditional argument authored on this page; see the item body for the numbered steps.",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "reference": "reserved claim of the qm-math-controlled-dynamics design reservation; complete-conditional-argument",
          "design_state": "reserved-closure; complete-conditional-argument"
        },
        {
