          ],
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics, 1st edition 2009, Section 12.3 pp. 253-256 (existence of wave operators for short-range potentials via Cook's criterion)",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-schroe/schroe.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "M. Reed and B. Simon, Methods of Modern Mathematical Physics III: Scattering Theory, Section XI.3 (short-range potentials and asymptotic completeness; standard treatment of the L^2 class)",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-schroe/schroe.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let\n$V\\in L^2(\\mathbb R^3;\\mathbb R)$ be real, let $H_0=-\\Delta$ on\n$D(H_0)=W^{2,2}(\\mathbb R^3;\\mathbb C)$, and let $H=H_0+M_V$ be the\nself-adjoint operator on $D(H_0)$ of\n[[thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-l2-potential-infinitesimal-kinetic-bound]] (c).\nThen:\n\n(a) For every Schwartz function $\\psi$\n$$\\int_0^\\infty\\bigl\\|Ve^{-itH_0}\\psi\\bigr\\|_2\\,dt<\\infty,\\qquad \\int_{-\\infty}^0\\bigl\\|Ve^{-itH_0}\\psi\\bigr\\|_2\\,dt<\\infty.$$\n\n(b) Consequently the wave operators\n$\\Omega_\\pm:=\\operatorname*{s-lim}_{t\\to\\pm\\infty}e^{itH}e^{-itH_0}$ exist as\nbounded linear isometries on $L^2(\\mathbb R^3)$ by\n[[thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-cook-domain-criterion]], with\n$\\Omega_\\pm e^{-isH_0}=e^{-isH}\\Omega_\\pm$ and\n$H\\Omega_\\pm\\psi=\\Omega_\\pm H_0\\psi$ for $\\psi\\in D(H_0)$.\n\n(c) *Free absolute continuity.* $H_0$ has purely absolutely continuous\nspectrum: for every $\\psi\\in L^2$ the scalar spectral measure of $H_0$ is\nabsolutely continuous with respect to Lebesgue measure, with density\n$\\frac{\\sqrt E}{2(2\\pi)^3}\\int_{S^2}|\\mathcal F_2\\psi(\\frac{\\sqrt E}{2\\pi}\\Omega)|^2d\\sigma(\\Omega)$\nfor almost every $E>0$, using any measurable Fourier representative. This nonnegative density lies in $L^1(0,\\infty)$ with integral $\\|\\psi\\|_2^2$, and the measure gives zero mass to $\\{0\\}$ and to $(-\\infty,0)$.\nHence $L^2=H_{\\mathrm{ac}}(H_0)$.\n\nAssertions about the ranges of $\\Omega_\\pm$, asymptotic completeness or the\nS-matrix are not made here; they are separate theorems\n([[thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-compact-support-asymptotic-completeness]]).",
          "strategy": "Complete conditional argument authored on this page; see the item body for the numbered steps.",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "reference": "reserved claim of the qm-math-controlled-dynamics design reservation; complete-conditional-argument",
          "design_state": "reserved-closure; complete-conditional-argument"
        },
        {
          "id": "thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-cook-isometry-and-intertwining",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Cook isometry and intertwining",
          "dependency_level": 1,
          "deps": [
