          ],
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "F. W. J. Olver, Asymptotics and Special Functions (1974), Chapter 11 (Liouville transformation and turning-point theory) — classical monograph treatment consulted through the DLMF survey of Airy-type asymptotics",
                "url": "https://dlmf.nist.gov/9.7"
              },
              {
                "title": "NIST Digital Library of Mathematical Functions, Sections 9.2 and 9.7 (Airy's differential equation and Airy-type connection formulas)",
                "url": "https://dlmf.nist.gov/9.2"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Let $J=[-x_-,x_+]$ with $x_-,x_+>0$, and let $q\\in C^5(J;\\mathbb R)$ have a single simple zero at $0$:\n$q(0)=0$, $q'(0)>0$, $q(x)$ has the sign of $x$, and $q\\ne0$ on\n$[-x_-,0)\\cup(0,x_+]$. Let $h>0$ and define\n$$\\zeta(x):=\\operatorname{sign}(x)\\Bigl[\\frac32\\Bigl|\\int_0^x\\sqrt{|q(s)|}\\,ds\\Bigr|\\Bigr]^{2/3}.$$\nThen:\n\n(a) $\\zeta\\in C^4$, $\\zeta(\\zeta')^2=q$, $\\zeta'>0$ with\n$\\min\\zeta'>0$. Define $a(x):=(\\zeta'(x))^{-1/2}$; then $a>0$ is $C^3$;\n\n(b) For each $u\\in C^2(J;\\mathbb C)$ solving $u''(x)=q(x)u(x)/h^2$ on $J$, define $w:\\zeta(J)\\to\\mathbb C$ by\n$$w(y):=\\frac{u(\\zeta^{-1}(y))}{a(\\zeta^{-1}(y))};$$\nthis is well-defined by (a), and $u(x)=a(x)w(\\zeta(x))$. The function $w$ is $C^2$ and satisfies $w''(\\zeta)=\\bigl[\\zeta/h^2+R(\\zeta)\\bigr]w(\\zeta)$ with\n$$R(\\zeta(x))=-\\frac{a''(x)}{a(x)\\,(\\zeta'(x))^2},$$\nwhere $a''$ denotes the second derivative with respect to $x$; the formula defines a continuous bounded real function on $\\zeta([-x_-,x_+])$ through the invertible map $x\\mapsto\\zeta(x)$;\n\n(c) the constants implicit in (a)–(b) depend only on $q$ and the interval.",
          "strategy": "Complete conditional argument authored on this page; see the item body for the numbered steps.",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "reference": "reserved claim of the qm-math-controlled-dynamics design reservation; complete-conditional-argument",
          "design_state": "reserved-closure; complete-conditional-argument"
        },
        {
          "id": "thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-quadratic-free-packet-decay",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Quadratic free-packet decay",
          "dependency_level": 2,
          "deps": [
            "thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-free-gaussian-dispersive-kernel",
