            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "R. Fitzpatrick, Quantum Mechanics (University of Texas at Austin, author-hosted course text), Evolution of Wave Packets pp. 29-32 (spreading and decay of free packets)",
                "url": "https://farside.ph.utexas.edu/teaching/qmech/qmech.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "E. M. Stein, Harmonic Analysis: Real-Variable Methods, Orthogonality and Oscillatory Integrals, Chapter VIII (stationary phase and decay of oscillatory integrals; standard monograph treatment)",
                "url": "https://dlmf.nist.gov/2"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let\n$a\\in C_c^\\infty(\\mathbb R^3;\\mathbb C)$ and put, for $t\\in\\mathbb R$ and\n$x\\in\\mathbb R^3$,\n$$\\psi_t(x):=\\int_{\\mathbb R^3}e^{i(k\\cdot x-t|k|^2)}a(k)\\,dk$$\n(the free evolution of the momentum-space amplitude $a$). Let\n$K\\subseteq\\mathbb R^3$ be compact with $v/2\\in\\operatorname{int}\\operatorname{supp}a$\nfor every $v\\in K$. Then there is a constant $C_K<\\infty$ such that\n$$\\sup_{v\\in K}|\\psi_t(tv)|\\le C_K|t|^{-3/2}\\qquad(|t|\\ge1).$$\nMoreover on every compact set $K'$ with\n$K'\\cap\\{2k:k\\in\\operatorname{supp}a\\}=\\varnothing$ and for every integer $N$\nthere is $C_{K',N}$ with\n$\\sup_{v\\in K'}|\\psi_t(tv)|\\le C_{K',N}|t|^{-N}$ for $|t|\\ge1$.\n\nThese are conditional estimates for the specified free model; no statement about\nbeams, detectors or measured intensities is made.",
          "strategy": "Complete conditional argument authored on this page; see the item body for the numbered steps.",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "reference": "reserved claim of the qm-math-controlled-dynamics design reservation; complete-conditional-argument",
          "design_state": "reserved-closure; complete-conditional-argument"
        },
        {
          "id": "thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-rotating-wave-finite-time-error",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Rotating-wave finite-time error",
          "dependency_level": 1,
          "deps": [
            "lem-fundamental-theorem-of-calculus-for-banach-valued-continuous-curves",
            "lem-bochner-integral-norm-inequality",
