          },
          "aliases": [
            "nrqm-controlled-dynamics-analytic-perturbation-remainder"
          ],
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics, 1st edition 2009, Section 6.6 pp. 153-159 (analytic perturbation with remainder control via Cauchy estimates)",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-schroe/schroe.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "E. B. Saff and A. D. Snider, Fundamentals of Complex Analysis, Chapter 4 (Cauchy estimates and Taylor remainder bounds; standard reference for the coefficient estimate used here)",
                "url": "https://sci.mu.iq/wp-content/uploads/2021/08/FUNCTIONAL-ANALYSIS-freebookcenter.net_.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]) and the hypotheses of [[thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-simple-level-reduced-resolvent-coefficients]] on an arbitrary complex Hilbert space $H$, with inner product linear in the first variable: $H_0$ is self-adjoint on its exact dense domain, $E$ is an isolated simple eigenvalue with gap at least $g>0$, $\\psi_0$ is a normalized eigenvector, and $V=V^*$ is bounded with $v=\\|V\\|$. Let $P_\\lambda,E_\\lambda$ be the contour projection and eigenvalue, $Q=I-P_0$, $S=\\iota_Q(H_0|_{D(H_0)\\cap QH}-E)^{-1}Q$ the actual reduced inverse, and $\\psi(\\lambda)$ the gauge-fixed eigenvector with $\\langle\\psi(\\lambda),\\psi_0\\rangle=1$.\n\nFor $v>0$ put $R=g/(8v)$. On the full complex disk $|\\lambda|<R$:\n\n(a) $q=2|\\lambda|v/g\\le1/4$, $\\|P_\\lambda-P_0\\|\\le1/3$, $\\|\\psi(\\lambda)\\|\\le2$, and the holomorphic scalar energy identity is\n$$E_\\lambda=\\langle(H_0+\\lambda V)\\psi(\\lambda),\\psi_0\\rangle=E+\\lambda\\langle V\\psi(\\lambda),\\psi_0\\rangle.$$\n\n(b) The exact coefficients are\n$$E'(0)=\\langle V\\psi_0,\\psi_0\\rangle,\\qquad \\psi'(0)=-SV\\psi_0,\\qquad E''(0)=-2\\langle VSV\\psi_0,\\psi_0\\rangle,$$\nwith bounds $|E'(0)|\\le v$, $\\|\\psi'(0)\\|\\le v/g$ and $|E''(0)|\\le2v^2/g$. The whole complementary spectral subspace, including its continuum, contributes through $S$. The cubic remainder satisfies\n$$\\left|E_\\lambda-E-\\lambda E'(0)-\\frac{\\lambda^2}{2}E''(0)\\right|\\le\\frac{Rv\\,(|\\lambda|/R)^3}{1-|\\lambda|/R}.$$\nAt $|\\lambda|=R/2$ the displayed bound is $Rv/4=g/32$. For $|\\lambda|\\le R/2$ it is at most $128v^3|\\lambda|^3/g^2$.\n\n(c) If $v=0$, then $V=0$ and $P_\\lambda=P_0$, $E_\\lambda=E$, $\\psi(\\lambda)=\\psi_0$ for every complex $\\lambda$; no radius involving division by $v$ is used in this branch.\n\nThese conclusions are conditional on the strict positive gap and bounded perturbation, and do not assert an unbounded or degenerate perturbation theorem.",
          "strategy": "Complete conditional argument authored on this page; see the item body for the numbered steps.",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "reference": "reserved claim of the qm-math-controlled-dynamics design reservation; complete-conditional-argument",
          "design_state": "reserved-closure; complete-conditional-argument"
        },
        {
          "id": "thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-mellin-incoming-and-outgoing-propagation",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Mellin incoming and outgoing propagation",
          "dependency_level": 0,
          "deps": [
            "thm-plancherel",
            "def-projection-valued-measure",
            "def-schwartz-space-and-its-seminorms",
            "def-hilbert-space",
            "def-countable-choice"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "thm-plancherel": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-projection-valued-measure": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-schwartz-space-and-its-seminorms": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-hilbert-space": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "aliases": [
            "nrqm-controlled-dynamics-mellin-incoming-and-outgoing-propagation"
          ],
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics (scattering-theory context; local Mellin estimates proved here)",
                "url": "https://www.math.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-schroe/schroe.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics, 1st edition 2009, Chapter 12 pp. 245-256 (scattering theory and asymptotic estimates)",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-schroe/schroe.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $H_0=-\\Delta$ on $L^2(\\mathbb R^3;\\mathbb C)$, with domain $H^2(\\mathbb R^3)$, and let\n$$U(s)\\psi(x):=e^{-3s/2}\\psi(e^{-s}x)\\qquad(s\\in\\mathbb R)$$\nbe the unitary dilation group. Use the convention $U(s)=e^{-isD}$. Then:\n\n(a) $U$ is strongly continuous and its self-adjoint generator $D$ has $D\\psi=-i(x\\cdot\\nabla+3/2)\\psi$ on the core $C_c^\\infty(\\mathbb R^3)$. The unitary position-log map $T_x\\psi(\\rho,\\omega)=e^{3\\rho/2}\\psi(e^\\rho\\omega)$ takes $D$ to $-i\\partial_\\rho$ on $L^2(\\mathbb R\\times S^2,d\\rho\\,d\\sigma)$, with domain consisting of functions whose weak $\\rho$ derivative belongs to $L^2$. The unitary transform $\\mathcal G u(\\eta,\\omega)=(2\\pi)^{-1/2}\\int_{\\mathbb R}e^{-i\\eta\\rho}u(\\rho,\\omega)\\,d\\rho$ takes this operator to multiplication by $\\eta$. In momentum-log coordinates the sign reverses: if $\\mathcal F_p\\psi(p)=(2\\pi)^{-3/2}\\int e^{-ip\\cdot x}\\psi(x)\\,dx$ and $W=\\mathcal G T_p\\mathcal F_p$, with $T_p$ given by the same polar-log formula, then $WDW^*=M_{-\\eta}$, on $\\{h:\\eta h\\in L^2\\}$.\n\n(b) With $P_\\pm:=\\mathbf 1_{(0,\\infty)}(\\pm D)$ ([[def-projection-valued-measure]]) one has $P_++P_-=I$. In the $W$ representation these are multiplication by $\\mathbf 1_{\\eta<0}$ and $\\mathbf 1_{\\eta>0}$, respectively; the spectral projection of $D$ at $0$ vanishes.\n\n(c) For every $f\\in C_c^\\infty((0,\\infty))$ with $\\operatorname{supp}f\\subseteq(a^2,b^2)$, $0<a<b$, and every nonnegative integer $N$, there is $C_N$ such that\n$$\\bigl\\|\\mathbf 1_{\\{|x|<2at\\}}e^{-itH_0}f(H_0)P_+\\bigr\\|\\le C_Nt(1+t)^{-N}\\qquad(t\\ge1),$$\n$$\\bigl\\|\\mathbf 1_{\\{|x|<2a|t|\\}}e^{-itH_0}f(H_0)P_-\\bigr\\|\\le C_N|t|(1+|t|)^{-N}\\qquad(t\\le-1).$$\nConsequently $P_+f(H_0)e^{-itH_0}\\to0$ strongly as $t\\to-\\infty$ and $P_-f(H_0)e^{-itH_0}\\to0$ strongly as $t\\to+\\infty$. The bounds also hold for any integer $N<0$ after enlarging its constant.",
          "strategy": "Complete conditional argument authored on this page; see the item body for the numbered steps.",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "reference": "reserved claim of the qm-math-controlled-dynamics design reservation; complete-conditional-argument",
          "design_state": "reserved-closure; complete-conditional-argument"
        },
        {
          "id": "thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-stable-weighted-airy-volterra-connection",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Stable weighted Airy Volterra connection",
          "dependency_level": 3,
          "deps": [
            "thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-liouville-turning-point-transformation",
            "thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-airy-envelopes-and-asymptotic-coefficients",
