          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-liouville-turning-point-transformation": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-airy-envelopes-and-asymptotic-coefficients": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-airy-contour-and-fresnel-normalization": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-fundamental-theorem-of-calculus-for-banach-valued-continuous-curves": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-bochner-integrable-function": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "aliases": [
            "nrqm-controlled-dynamics-stable-weighted-airy-volterra-connection"
          ],
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "F. W. J. Olver, Asymptotics and Special Functions (1974), Chapter 11 (error bounds for Airy-type Volterra equations near turning points) — classical monograph treatment consulted through the DLMF survey of asymptotics and error bounds",
                "url": "https://dlmf.nist.gov/9.7"
              },
              {
                "title": "NIST Digital Library of Mathematical Functions, Section 9.7 (connection formulas for Airy functions)",
                "url": "https://dlmf.nist.gov/9.7"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Adopt the hypotheses and notation of\n[[thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-liouville-turning-point-transformation]]: $q\\in C^5$\nwith a single simple zero at $0$, $q'(0)>0$, transformed equation\n$w''=[\\zeta/h^2+R(\\zeta)]w$ on $\\zeta([-x_-,x_+])$, $a>0$ the Liouville factor\nand $R$ continuous bounded. Put $b:=-\\zeta(-x_-)>0$ and $c:=\\zeta(x_+)>0$,\nso the transformed interval is $[-b,c]$. Let\n$A_h(\\zeta):=A(\\zeta/h^{2/3})$, $B_h(\\zeta):=B(\\zeta/h^{2/3})$ for the Airy\nfunctions of\n[[thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-airy-envelopes-and-asymptotic-coefficients]]\n(Wronskian $A_hB_h'-A_h'B_h=h^{-2/3}/\\pi$), and define the envelopes\n$$e_h(\\zeta):=\\bigl(1+|\\zeta|/h^{2/3}\\bigr)^{-1/4}\\exp\\Bigl(-\\frac{2(\\zeta_+)^{3/2}}{3h}\\Bigr),\\qquad d_h(\\zeta):=h^{-2/3}\\bigl(1+|\\zeta|/h^{2/3}\\bigr)^{1/4}\\exp\\Bigl(-\\frac{2(\\zeta_+)^{3/2}}{3h}\\Bigr).$$\nThen:\n\n(a) *Volterra representation.* For $h$ small the unique solution with Airy terminal data $w(c)=A_h(c)$, $w'(c)=A_h'(c)$ at the right endpoint $\\zeta=c$ satisfies\n$$w(\\zeta)=A_h(\\zeta)+\\pi h^{2/3}\\int_\\zeta^c\\bigl[A_h(\\zeta)B_h(v)-B_h(\\zeta)A_h(v)\\bigr]R(v)w(v)\\,dv .$$\n\n(b) *Stable weighted estimate.* There is a constant $C_A$ with\n$|w(\\zeta)-A_h(\\zeta)|\\le C_Ae_h(\\zeta)(e^{\\varepsilon_h}-1)$ and\n$|w'(\\zeta)-A_h'(\\zeta)|\\le C_Ad_h(\\zeta)(e^{\\varepsilon_h}-1)$, where\n$$\\varepsilon_h:=Ch\\int_{-b}^c\\frac{|R(v)|}{\\sqrt{|v|+h^{2/3}}}\\,dv\\le C'h$$\nfor constants depending only on $q$ and the interval.\n\n(c) *Growing branch and connection.* The solution with terminal data\n$(B_h,B_h')$ at $\\zeta=0$ obeys the analogous bound with $e_h$ replaced by its\ngrowing analogue on the full interval; consequently, for fixed $\\zeta>0$ and\n$\\zeta<0$ away from zero, the forbidden-side solution\n$q^{-1/4}\\exp(-\\frac1h\\int_0^x\\sqrt q)$ corresponds to\n$2(-q)^{-1/4}\\sin(\\frac1h\\int_x^0\\sqrt{-q}+\\pi/4)$ on the allowed side, and the\ngrowing forbidden solution to the corresponding cosine, with absolute errors bounded by the envelopes times $C(\\varepsilon_h+h/|\\zeta|^{3/2})$.",
