          "aliases": [
            "nrqm-controlled-dynamics-dollard-integrable-remainder"
          ],
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "J. D. Dollard, Asymptotic convergence and the Coulomb interaction, Journal of Mathematical Physics 5 (1964) 729-738 (modified Coulomb wave operators; primary source)",
                "url": "https://doi.org/10.1063/1.1704171"
              },
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics, 1st edition 2009, Chapter 12 pp. 245-256 (long-range modifications of Cook's criterion)",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-schroe/schroe.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let\n$\\gamma>0$, $H_0=-\\Delta$ on $L^2(\\mathbb R^3;\\mathbb C)$ and\n$H_\\gamma:=-\\Delta-\\gamma/|\\cdot|$ on $D(H_\\gamma)=H^2(\\mathbb R^3)$, the\nself-adjoint Coulomb operator established below on this exact domain, with\nessential spectrum $[0,\\infty)$ as proved by the local compact-resolvent argument. Use the physical-momentum Fourier transform $\\mathcal F_pf(p)=(2\\pi)^{-3/2}\\mathcal F_2f(p/(2\\pi))$, unitary by the dilation change of variables, equivalently $(2\\pi)^{-3/2}\\int e^{-ip\\cdot x}f(x)dx$ on Schwartz functions. Let $P_j=\\mathcal F_p^*M_{p_j}\\mathcal F_p=-i\\partial_j$ on its maximal weak-derivative domain; thus $H_0=\\mathcal F_p^*M_{|p|^2}\\mathcal F_p$. Set $a(p)=\\gamma/(2|p|)$ for $p\\ne0$ and $a(0)=0$, and $a(P)=\\mathcal F_p^*M_a\\mathcal F_p$ on the maximal multiplier domain. For $|t|\\ge1$ define the\nDollard-modified free evolution\n$$U_D(t):=e^{-itH_0}e^{i\\,\\operatorname{sign}(t)\\,a(P)\\log|t|}$$\n(the two factors commute, being functions of $P$; extend to $|t|\\le1$ by\n$U_D(t):=e^{-itH_0}$). Then:\n\n(a) $U_D(t)$ is unitary for every $t$ and strongly continuous in $t$ away from $t=0$; on the dense set of momentum $C_c^\\infty$ vectors supported in an annulus $0<a_0\\le|p|\\le b_0<\\infty$ it is differentiable for $|t|>1$, with the exterior one-sided derivatives at $t=\\pm1$, and\n$$i\\,U_D'(t)=\\Bigl[H_0-\\frac{\\gamma}{2|t|\\,|P|}\\Bigr]U_D(t)\\qquad(|t|>1).$$\n\n(b) *Integrable remainder.* For every vector $\\psi$ in that dense set one has\n$$\\int_1^\\infty\\Bigl\\|\\Bigl[\\frac{\\gamma}{|\\cdot|}-\\frac{\\gamma}{2|t|\\,|P|}\\Bigr]U_D(t)\\psi\\Bigr\\|_2dt<\\infty,$$\nand the same integral with $|t|$ in the comparison denominator over $(-\\infty,-1]$ is finite. More precisely, for each such $\\psi$ there are $T_\\psi\\ge1$ and $C_\\psi<\\infty$ such that for both signs of $t$, $|t|\\ge T_\\psi$ implies $\\|[\\gamma/|\\cdot|-\\gamma/(2|t|\\,|P|)]U_D(t)\\psi\\|_2\\le C_\\psi(1+\\log|t|)/|t|^2$.\n\nNo empirical claim, no Rutherford cross-section and no photon interpretation is\nasserted; the logarithmic phase is a comparison construction for the\nlong-range generator.",
          "strategy": "Complete conditional argument authored on this page; see the item body for the numbered steps.",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "reference": "reserved claim of the qm-math-controlled-dynamics design reservation; complete-conditional-argument",
          "design_state": "reserved-closure; complete-conditional-argument"
