            "def-countable-choice"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-stable-weighted-airy-volterra-connection": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-liouville-turning-point-transformation": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-wkb-explicit-error": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-airy-envelopes-and-asymptotic-coefficients": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-bochner-integrable-function": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "aliases": [
            "nrqm-controlled-dynamics-two-turn-barrier-tunnelling-error"
          ],
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "F. W. J. Olver, Asymptotics and Special Functions, Chapter 11 (connection formulas and barrier penetration; standard monograph)",
                "url": "https://dlmf.nist.gov/11"
              },
              {
                "title": "R. Fitzpatrick, Quantum Mechanics (University of Texas at Austin, author-hosted course text), Square Potential Barrier and Cold Emission pp. 64-73 (WKB barrier transmission)",
                "url": "https://farside.ph.utexas.edu/teaching/qmech/qmech.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Fix $m>0$. Let $V\\in C_c^5(\\mathbb R;\\mathbb R)$ be fixed and let $E>0$ be such that\n$V-E$ has exactly two simple zeros $a<b$, is positive on $(a,b)$ and negative\noutside $[a,b]$ with nonvanishing derivative at $a,b$. Set $q(x):=2m(V(x)-E)$\nand consider the explicitly parameterized family\n$$u_h''(x)=\\frac{q(x)}{h^2}u_h(x),\\qquad h>0.$$\nThe quantities and $h$ are nondimensional after fixed scales have been chosen;\nthe physical reading is the scaled family, with the physical $\\hbar$ fixed.\nChoose $L>0$ with $\\operatorname{supp}V\\subset(-L,L)$ and put\n$p_0:=\\sqrt{2mE}$. Define the scattering amplitudes $r(h),t(h)$ by the exact\nsolution with one incoming wave from the left and none from the right:\n$$u_h(x)=p_0^{-1/2}\\bigl(e^{ip_0x/h}+r(h)e^{-ip_0x/h}\\bigr)\\quad(x\\le-L),\\qquad u_h(x)=p_0^{-1/2}t(h)e^{ip_0x/h}\\quad(x\\ge L).$$\nHere the conserved dimensionless current is $J_h(u):=h\\operatorname{Im}(\\overline u\\,u')$;\nthe exterior waves $p_0^{-1/2}e^{\\pm ip_0x/h}$ have currents $\\pm1$.\nThe transmission coefficient is the transmitted-to-incoming current ratio\n$T(h):=|t(h)|^2$. The proof establishes existence and uniqueness of these\namplitudes. Put $B:=\\int_a^b\\sqrt{2m(V-E)}\\,dx$ and $S:=B/h$. Then there are $h_0>0$, an\n$\\varepsilon(h)\\le Ch$ for $0<h<h_0$, and a constant $C_0$ such that the transmission\ncoefficient is\n$$T(h)=e^{-2S}\\bigl[1+O\\bigl(\\varepsilon(h)+e^{-2S}\\bigr)\\bigr],$$\nquantitatively\n$$|T(h)e^{2S}-1|\\le\\frac{C_0[\\varepsilon(h)+e^{-2S}]}{1-C_0[\\varepsilon(h)+e^{-2S}]}$$\nwhenever the denominator is positive. The bound holds for fixed $V,E$ with the\nstated separated simple turning points; rectangular walls, coalescing turning\npoints, barrier-top uniformity and resonant multiwell interference are excluded.",
          "strategy": "Complete conditional argument authored on this page; see the item body for the numbered steps.",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "reference": "reserved claim of the qm-math-controlled-dynamics design reservation; complete-conditional-argument",
          "design_state": "reserved-closure; complete-conditional-argument"
        },
        {
          "id": "thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-radial-carleman-estimate",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "domain": "mathematics",
