          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "D. Jerison and C. E. Kenig, Unique continuation and absence of positive eigenvalues for Schrodinger operators, Annals of Mathematics 121 (1985) 463-494 (Carleman estimates for the Laplacian; primary research source)",
                "url": "https://doi.org/10.2307/1971319"
              },
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics, 1st edition 2009, Chapter 7 pp. 161-172 (polar coordinates and the Laplacian in three dimensions)",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-schroe/schroe.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $s\\ge1$ be\nan integer, $\\tau:=s+1$, and let $u\\in C_c^\\infty(\\mathbb R^3\\setminus\\{0\\})$\n([[lem-smooth-compactly-supported-functions-are-dense-in-ltwo-of-an-open-set]]).\nWrite $r=|x|$ and $\\Delta$ for the Laplacian. Then\n$$\\bigl\\|r^{-\\tau}u\\bigr\\|_{L^2(\\mathbb R^3)}\\le\\frac2s\\bigl\\|r^{-\\tau+2}\\Delta u\\bigr\\|_{L^2(\\mathbb R^3)}.$$\nThe inequality extends to every compactly supported $H^2$ function that vanishes\nin a neighborhood of the origin.",
