              {
                "title": "H. Brezis, Functional Analysis, Sobolev Spaces and Partial Differential Equations, Chapter 9 (local H^2 calculus and cut-off products)",
                "url": "https://www.math.toronto.edu/almut/Brezis.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let\n$\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^3$ be open and connected, let\n$B\\in L^\\infty_{\\mathrm{loc}}(\\Omega;\\mathbb C)$, and let\n$\\psi\\in H^2_{\\mathrm{loc}}(\\Omega)$ satisfy $\\Delta\\psi=B\\psi$ in the\ndistributional sense on $\\Omega$ ([[def-sobolev-space-wkp-and-its-norm]]). If\n$\\psi=0$ almost everywhere on some nonempty open subset of $\\Omega$, then\n$\\psi=0$ almost everywhere on $\\Omega$.",
