            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-common-domain-nonautonomous-evolution": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-nrqm-oscillator-hermite-recurrence": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-plancherel": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-weak-derivatives-are-polynomial-fourier-multipliers": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-dominated-convergence": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-adjoint-of-a-densely-defined-unbounded-operator": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-unbounded-adjoint-is-well-defined-and-closed": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-cauchy-schwarz-for-real-and-complex-inner-product-spaces": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-complex-lp-completeness-density-and-inner-product": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "aliases": [
            "nrqm-controlled-dynamics-driven-oscillator-common-domain"
          ],
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics, 1st edition 2009, Section 6.1 pp. 133-136 (Kato-Rellich) and Chapter 8 pp. 173-180 (algebraic oscillator methods)",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-schroe/schroe.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "R. Fitzpatrick, Quantum Mechanics (University of Texas at Austin, author-hosted course text), Simple Harmonic Oscillator pp. 80-84 (ladder operators and the ground state)",
                "url": "https://farside.ph.utexas.edu/teaching/qmech/qmech.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let\n$m,\\omega,\\hbar>0$, let $\\ell:=\\sqrt{\\hbar/(m\\omega)}$, let\n$H_{\\mathrm{osc}}=\\frac{\\hbar\\omega}{2}DAD^{-1}$ be the oscillator of\n[[thm-nrqm-oscillator-oscillator-scaling-and-exact-realization]] with\northonormal eigenbasis $(\\psi_n)_{n\\ge0}$ and ladder operators\n$a_\\psi,a_\\psi^\\dagger,N_\\psi$ of [[lem-nrqm-oscillator-closed-ladder-domains]]\ntransported to $L^2(\\mathbb R,dx)$. Work with $\\langle u,v\\rangle=\\int u\\overline v$, linear in its first argument, and define $N_\\psi^{1/2}$ by the coefficient action $\\sqrt n\\,c_n$ on $D(N_\\psi^{1/2})=\\{\\psi:\\sum_n n|c_n|^2<\\infty\\}$, where $c_n=\\langle\\psi,\\psi_n\\rangle$. Use the negative-sign $2\\pi$ Fourier convention $\\widehat u(\\xi)=\\int e^{-2\\pi i x\\xi}u(x)\\,dx$ on integrable inputs and its Plancherel extension $\\mathcal F_2$. Let\n$Q=M_x$, $P=\\mathcal F_2^*M_{2\\pi\\hbar\\xi}\\mathcal F_2$ be the maximal\nposition and momentum operators (their self-adjointness is proved below), with\n$D(Q)=\\{\\psi:x\\psi\\in L^2\\}$ and\n$D(P)=\\{\\psi:\\xi\\mathcal F_2\\psi\\in L^2\\}$, with\n$H_{\\mathrm{osc}}=\\hbar\\omega(N_\\psi+\\frac12I)$ and the couplings\n$$Q=\\frac{\\ell}{\\sqrt2}(a_\\psi+a_\\psi^\\dagger),\\qquad P=\\frac{\\hbar}{i\\ell\\sqrt2}(a_\\psi-a_\\psi^\\dagger)$$\non the common domain $D(N_\\psi^{1/2})$. Let $f:[a,b]\\to\\mathbb R$ be of class\n$C^1$. Put $Y:=D(H_{\\mathrm{osc}})=D(N_\\psi)$ with graph norm\n$\\|\\psi\\|_Y^2:=\\|\\psi\\|^2+\\|H_{\\mathrm{osc}}\\psi\\|^2$. Then:\n\n(a) *Ladder bounds.* For every $\\psi\\in D(N_\\psi^{1/2})$,\n$$\\|Q\\psi\\|\\le\\ell\\bigl(2\\|N_\\psi^{1/2}\\psi\\|^2+\\|\\psi\\|^2\\bigr)^{1/2},\\qquad \\|P\\psi\\|\\le\\frac{\\hbar}{\\ell}\\bigl(2\\|N_\\psi^{1/2}\\psi\\|^2+\\|\\psi\\|^2\\bigr)^{1/2}.$$\n\n(b) *Infinitesimal bound.* For every $\\eta>0$ there is $b_\\eta<\\infty$ with\n$\\|Q\\psi\\|\\le\\eta\\|H_{\\mathrm{osc}}\\psi\\|+b_\\eta\\|\\psi\\|$ for\n$\\psi\\in Y=D(H_{\\mathrm{osc}})$; hence $-f(t)Q$ is\n$H_{\\mathrm{osc}}$-bounded with relative bound $0$ for every fixed $t$\n([[def-relative-boundedness-with-respect-to-an-operator]]).\n\n(c) *Common domain.* For every $t\\in[a,b]$ the operator\n$H(t):=H_{\\mathrm{osc}}-f(t)Q$ is self-adjoint on the single domain $Y$\n(independent of $t$); moreover $t\\mapsto H(t)$ belongs to\n$C^1([a,b];\\mathcal B(Y,L^2))$ with derivative $-f'(t)Q$, so the family has a\ncommon domain and satisfies the regularity hypothesis of\n[[thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-common-domain-nonautonomous-evolution]].",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "reference": "reserved claim of the qm-math-controlled-dynamics design reservation; complete-conditional-argument",
          "design_state": "reserved-closure; complete-conditional-argument"
        },
        {
          "id": "thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-explicit-unbounded-oscillator-propagator",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Explicit unbounded oscillator propagator",
          "dependency_level": 5,
          "deps": [
            "thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-driven-oscillator-common-domain",
            "thm-nrqm-oscillator-oscillator-scaling-and-exact-realization",
            "lem-nrqm-oscillator-closed-ladder-domains",
