          },
          "aliases": [
            "nrqm-controlled-dynamics-controlled-born-amplitude-error"
          ],
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "R. Fitzpatrick, Quantum Mechanics (University of Texas at Austin, author-hosted course text), Born Approximation pp. 211-213 (first Born approximation and its validity condition)",
                "url": "https://farside.ph.utexas.edu/teaching/qmech/qmech.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics, 1st edition 2009, Chapter 12 pp. 245-256 (Neumann series for the scattering amplitude)",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-schroe/schroe.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Adopt the\nhypotheses and notation of\n[[thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-stationary-outgoing-integral-and-flux]]: real\n$V$ bounded with $\\operatorname{supp}V\\subseteq B_R$, $k>0$, $d\\in S^2$, the\ncompact operator $K_k$, and write $q:=\\|K_k\\|$. Then:\n\n(a) *Neumann control.* If $q<1$ then $u=(I+K_k)^{-1}e_{\\mathrm{inc}}$ satisfies\n$$\\bigl\\|u-e_{\\mathrm{inc}}\\bigr\\|_{L^2(B_R)}\\le\\frac{q}{1-q}\\, \\bigl\\|e_{\\mathrm{inc}}\\bigr\\|_{L^2(B_R)}.$$\n\n(b) *First Born amplitude.* Under the same condition $q<1$, with\n$f_B(\\Omega):=-\\frac1{4\\pi}\\int_{B_R}e^{ik(d-\\Omega)\\cdot y}V(y)\\,dy$ one has,\nuniformly in $\\Omega\\in S^2$,\n$$\\bigl|f_k(\\Omega)-f_B(\\Omega)\\bigr|\\le\\frac{\\|V\\|_\\infty|B_R|^{1/2}}{4\\pi}\\, \\frac{q}{1-q}\\,\\bigl\\|e_{\\mathrm{inc}}\\bigr\\|_{L^2(B_R)}.$$\n\n(c) *Scaling form.* For $V_\\eta=\\eta V$ with $|\\eta|q<1$, put $K_{k,\\eta}=\\eta K_k$, $u_\\eta=(I+\\eta K_k)^{-1}e_{\\mathrm{inc}}$, and define the corresponding amplitudes by the same integrals. Then\n$$\\|u_\\eta-e_{\\mathrm{inc}}\\|_2\\le\\frac{|\\eta|q}{1-|\\eta|q}\\|e_{\\mathrm{inc}}\\|_2,$$\n$$\\sup_{\\Omega,d\\in S^2}|f_{k,\\eta}(\\Omega;d)-\\eta f_B(\\Omega;d)|\\le\\frac{|\\eta|^2\\|V\\|_\\infty|B_R|q}{4\\pi(1-|\\eta|q)}.$$\nThis applies to every real $\\eta$ in the original real stationary model. For complex $\\eta$ the same Neumann construction and amplitude integrals give the same algebraic estimate, without asserting the real-potential flux conclusions. No base condition $q<1$ is needed in (c). These give controlled weak-coupling Born estimates in the actual operator norm, uniformly in both incident and outgoing directions.",
          "strategy": "Complete conditional argument authored on this page; see the item body for the numbered steps.",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "reference": "reserved claim of the qm-math-controlled-dynamics design reservation; complete-conditional-argument",
          "design_state": "reserved-closure; complete-conditional-argument"
        },
