            ]
          },
          "statement": "Let\n$$w_n:=\\begin{cases}0,&n\\in\\{0,1\\},\\\\[2mm]\\dfrac1{C\\,n\\,(\\log n)^2},&n\\ge2,\\end{cases}\\qquad C:=\\sum_{n\\ge2}\\frac1{n(\\log n)^2},$$\nwhere $\\log$ is the natural logarithm. This example verifies concretely that:\n\n(a) the normalizing constant is finite and positive,\n$C\\in(0,\\infty)$, so that $\\sum_{n\\ge0}w_n=1$ ([[def-series-and-absolute-convergence-in-a-normed-space]]);\n\n(b) the entropy of the weight family diverges,\n$$s(w):=-\\sum_{n\\ge0}w_n\\log w_n=\\sum_{n\\ge0}w_n\\log\\frac1{w_n}=+\\infty,$$\nwhere the sum is the nonnegative extended sum of the nonnegative terms\n$w_n\\log(1/w_n)$; for a zero weight, both expressions $-w_n\\log w_n$ and $w_n\\log(1/w_n)$ are defined to have value $0$. Thus the two zero weights at $n=0,1$ contribute $0$ rather than requiring a logarithm or reciprocal at zero;\n\n(c) Consequently, a probability weight on a countable set can have infinite entropy, while every finite probability vector $p=(p_1,\\ldots,p_d)$ with $p_i\\ge0$ and $\\sum_ip_i=1$ has entropy $s_d(p):=-\\sum_{i:p_i>0}p_i\\log p_i\\le\\log d$ (zero entries contribute $0$). The finite bound is verified below.",
          "strategy": "Complete conditional argument authored on this page; see the item body for the numbered steps.",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "reference": "reserved claim of the qm-math-fock-and-equilibrium design reservation; complete-conditional-argument",
          "design_state": "reserved-closure; complete-conditional-argument"
        },
        {
          "id": "thm-nrqm-fock-and-equilibrium-variational-ground-gap-overlap",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Variational ground gap overlap",
          "dependency_level": 2,
          "deps": [
