          },
          "aliases": [
            "nrqm-fock-and-equilibrium-variational-ground-gap-overlap"
          ],
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics, 1st edition 2009, Chapter 3 and Chapter 4 (spectral theorem, functional calculus) and Sections 4.3-4.4 pp. 117-120 (variational methods and spectral projection estimates)",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-schroe/schroe.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "S. Pratt, Lecture Notes on Quantum Mechanics (Michigan State University, PHY 851/852; retrieved via the Internet Archive snapshot of 2024-04-21), Section 6.2 pp. 87-89 (variational theory and ground-state estimates)",
                "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20240421090356/http://web.archive.org/web/20240421090356/https://web.pa.msu.edu/people/pratts/phy851/lectures/lectures_full.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice and the Axiom of Countable Choice\n([[def-axiom-of-choice]], [[def-countable-choice]]). Let $H$ be a self-adjoint\noperator on a nonzero complex Hilbert space $\\mathfrak H$\n([[def-symmetric-self-adjoint-and-essentially-self-adjoint]],\n[[def-hilbert-space]]) which is bounded below, let\n$E_0:=\\inf\\sigma(H)\\in\\mathbb R$, let $E$ be the projection-valued measure of\n$H$ ([[thm-spectral-theorem-for-unbounded-self-adjoint-operators]],\n[[def-projection-valued-measure]]), put $P:=E(\\{E_0\\})$, and assume that\n$g>0$ is a spectral gap:\n$$\\sigma(H)\\cap(E_0,E_0+g)=\\varnothing .$$\nFor $u\\in D(|H|^{1/2})$ write $E_u(B):=\\langle E(B)u,u\\rangle$ for Borel sets\n$B\\subseteq\\mathbb R$ ([[lem-scalar-and-complex-measures-from-a-pvm]]) and put\n$q_H[u]:=\\int_{\\mathbb R}\\lambda\\,dE_u(\\lambda)$; by\n[[lem-nrqm-composites-density-and-scalar-spectral-probability]] (c) this\nintegral exists for $u\\in D(|H|^{1/2})$, and for $u\\in D(H)$ it equals\n$\\langle Hu,u\\rangle$. Then for every $u\\in D(|H|^{1/2})$ with $\\|u\\|=1$:\n\n(a) $q_H[u]-E_0=\\displaystyle\\int_{\\mathbb R}(\\lambda-E_0)\\,dE_u(\\lambda)\\ \\ge\\ g\\,\\|(I-P)u\\|^2$;\n\n(b) if $q_H[u]\\le E_0+\\varepsilon$ for some $\\varepsilon\\ge0$, then\n$\\|(I-P)u\\|^2\\le\\varepsilon/g$; in particular, if $\\varepsilon<g$ then $Pu\\ne0$.\n\nNo claim is made about the existence of a ground eigenvector, about $E_0$\nbeing an eigenvalue, or about any physical interpretation of the trial vector.",
          "strategy": "Complete conditional argument authored on this page; see the item body for the numbered steps.",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "reference": "reserved claim of the qm-math-fock-and-equilibrium design reservation; complete-conditional-argument",
          "design_state": "reserved-closure; complete-conditional-argument"
        },
