          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "I. Burmistrov and A. Lunkin, Lecture Notes on Statistical Mechanics (HSE, 2023), Sections 1.1.1-1.1.3 pp. 12-14 (density matrix, Gibbs distribution, entropy; relaxation to equilibrium is an additional assumption)",
                "url": "http://home.itp.ac.ru/~burmi/HSE/Lectures-StatPhys-temp.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics, 1st edition 2009, Sections 3.1 and 5.1 (the spectral theorem; Stone's theorem and unitary dynamics)",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-schroe/schroe.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice and the Axiom of Choice. Let $\\omega>0$,\n$\\hbar>0$, let $F(\\mathbb C)$ be the one-mode Fock space with its complete\northonormal family $(e_n)_{n\\in\\mathbb N}$, number operator $N$ and operators\n$A_\\pm(1)$ as in [[thm-nrqm-fock-and-equilibrium-fixed-mode-number-law]] and\n[[thm-nrqm-fock-and-equilibrium-number-operator-domain]], and let\n$$A:=\\omega N,\\qquad U(t):=e^{-itA/\\hbar}=\\int_{\\mathbb R}e^{-it\\lambda/\\hbar}\\,dE(\\lambda),$$\nthe unitary group generated by the self-adjoint $A$ with spectral projection\nvalued measure $E$ ([[thm-spectral-theorem-for-unbounded-self-adjoint-operators]],\n[[lem-self-adjoint-operator-generates-a-strongly-continuous-unitary-group]]).\nPut\n$$\\psi_0:=\\frac{e_0+e_1}{\\sqrt2},\\qquad \\psi(t):=U(t)\\psi_0,\\qquad Y:=A_+(1)+A_-(1),\\qquad D(Y):=D(A_+(1))\\cap D(A_-(1)).$$\nThen $\\|\\psi_0\\|=1$, $\\psi(t)\\in D(Y)$ for every $t$, and with\n$\\theta:=\\omega t/\\hbar$:\n\n(a) $\\psi(t)=\\dfrac{e_0+e^{-i\\theta}e_1}{\\sqrt2}$;\n\n(b) the expectation $t\\mapsto\\langle\\psi(t),Y\\psi(t)\\rangle$ equals\n$\\cos(\\omega t/\\hbar)$; consequently it tends to no limit as $t\\to+\\infty$,\nsince it equals $1$ at $t=2\\pi\\hbar n/\\omega$ and $-1$ at\n$t=(2n+1)\\pi\\hbar/\\omega$;\n\n(c) the state itself has no norm limit: $\\|\\psi(t)-\\psi(s)\\|^2\n=1-\\cos\\bigl(\\omega(t-s)/\\hbar\\bigr)$, so $\\|\\psi(t_n)-\\psi(s_n)\\|=\\sqrt2$ for\nthe two sequences of (b);\n\n(d) in contrast, the weight operator $G_\\beta$ and the density operator\n$\\rho_\\beta=G_\\beta/Z(\\beta)$ of\n[[thm-nrqm-fock-and-equilibrium-single-mode-thermal-trace]] are invariant under\nthe same dynamics:\n$$U(t)G_\\beta U(t)^*=G_\\beta,\\qquad U(t)\\rho_\\beta U(t)^*=\\rho_\\beta\\qquad(t\\in\\mathbb R,\\ \\beta>0).$$\n\nThus a stationary equilibrium weight is available on this space, but the\nunitary dynamics of the non-stationary unit vector $\\psi_0$ produces no\nconvergence of the state or of the displayed expectation: equilibration is not\na consequence of unitary evolution alone. No physical interpretation of\n$\\psi_0$, $Y$, $\\beta$ or $\\rho_\\beta$ is asserted; in particular no thermal\nstate is derived, and the example does not assert that any physical\npreparation oscillates.",
          "strategy": "Complete conditional argument authored on this page; see the item body for the numbered steps.",
