        {
          "id": "ex-nrqm-fock-and-equilibrium-example-repeated-orbital-fermion-exclusion",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Repeated-orbital fermion exclusion",
          "dependency_level": 6,
          "deps": [
            "thm-nrqm-fock-and-equilibrium-slater-direct-and-exchange-calculation",
            "thm-nrqm-fock-and-equilibrium-hilbert-direct-sum-construction",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-permutation-sector-projections",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-hilbert-tensor-construction",
            "def-orthonormal-family-complete-orthonormal-system-and-hilbert-basis",
            "def-hilbert-space",
            "def-countable-choice",
            "def-axiom-of-choice"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "thm-nrqm-fock-and-equilibrium-slater-direct-and-exchange-calculation": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-nrqm-fock-and-equilibrium-hilbert-direct-sum-construction": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-permutation-sector-projections": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-hilbert-tensor-construction": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-orthonormal-family-complete-orthonormal-system-and-hilbert-basis": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-hilbert-space": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-axiom-of-choice": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "aliases": [
            "nrqm-fock-and-equilibrium-example-repeated-orbital-fermion-exclusion"
          ],
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "F. H. L. Essler, Advanced Quantum Theory (Oxford lecture notes, 2017/18), Sections 1.1-1.2 pp. 1-6 (many-particle antisymmetric states and Pauli exclusion)",
                "url": "http://www-thphys.physics.ox.ac.uk/courses/C6/C6_2017/C6Notes/lecturenotes2017AQT.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "S. Pratt, Lecture Notes on Quantum Mechanics (Michigan State University, PHY 851/852; retrieved via the Internet Archive snapshot of 2024-04-21), Chapter 11 Sections 11.1-11.3 pp. 161-168 (spin statistics, multi-particle symmetrization and Slater determinants)",
                "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20240421090356/http://web.archive.org/web/20240421090356/https://web.pa.msu.edu/people/pratts/phy851/lectures/lectures_full.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "**Slot convention.** For $\\ell\\ge1$, $S_\\ell$ acts on $\\{0,\\dots,\\ell-1\\}$ as in [[lem-nrqm-composites-permutation-sector-projections]]. On one-based tuple positions use $\\widehat{\\pi}(k):=1+\\pi(k-1)$ for $1\\le k\\le\\ell$. Conjugation by $k\\mapsto k-1$ gives $\\widehat{\\pi\\sigma}=\\widehat{\\pi}\\circ\\widehat{\\sigma}$ and $\\widehat{\\pi^{-1}}=\\widehat{\\pi}^{-1}$; thus the supplier's tensor action becomes $U_\\pi(v_1\\otimes\\cdots\\otimes v_\\ell)=v_{\\widehat{\\pi}^{-1}(1)}\\otimes\\cdots\\otimes v_{\\widehat{\\pi}^{-1}(\\ell)}$. The parameters of $U_\\pi$ and $\\operatorname{sgn}(\\pi)$ remain canonical zero-based permutations.\n\nAssume the Axiom of Countable Choice and the Axiom of Choice. Let $H$ be a\ncomplex Hilbert space, let $H^{\\otimes n}$ be its completed tensor powers with\nthe unitaries $U_\\pi$ and projections $P_\\pm^{(n)}$ of\n[[lem-nrqm-composites-permutation-sector-projections]]. Fix $n\\ge2$ and vectors $u_1,\\ldots,u_n\\in H$, and let\n$$S(u_1,\\dots,u_n):=\\frac1{\\sqrt{n!}}\\sum_{\\sigma\\in S_n}\\operatorname{sgn}(\\sigma)\\, u_{\\widehat{\\sigma}(1)}\\otimes\\cdots\\otimes u_{\\widehat{\\sigma}(n)}$$\nbe the Slater vector of\n[[thm-nrqm-fock-and-equilibrium-slater-direct-and-exchange-calculation]]. This\nexample verifies concretely that:\n\n(a) for every $u\\in H$ the antisymmetrised two-particle tensor vanishes,\n$$P_-^{(2)}(u\\otimes u)=0,$$\nbecause the canonical transposition $\\tau=(0\\,1)\\in S_2$ of the two tensor factors satisfies\n$U_\\tau(u\\otimes u)=u\\otimes u$ and $P_-^{(2)}=\\tfrac12(\\mathrm{id}-U_\\tau)$;\n\n(b) consequently the Slater vector with a repeated orbital is the zero vector,\n$$S(u,u)=\\frac1{\\sqrt2}\\bigl(u\\otimes u-u\\otimes u\\bigr)=0\\qquad(u\\in H),$$\nand the norm-one conclusion of\n[[thm-nrqm-fock-and-equilibrium-slater-direct-and-exchange-calculation]] (a)\ndoes not apply to the degenerate list $(u,u)$: orthonormality of $u_1,\\dots,u_n$\nis an essential hypothesis, not a convenience; for orthonormal $u_1,u_2$ one\nhas $\\|S(u_1,u_2)\\|=1$;\n\n(c) exclusion is a property of the *state* and not only of basis labels:\nfor $H=\\mathbb C^2$ with orthonormal basis $e_1,e_2$ and the non-basis vector\n$u:=e_1+e_2$ the antisymmetric part still vanishes. Indeed $u\\otimes u\n=e_1\\otimes e_1+e_1\\otimes e_2+e_2\\otimes e_1+e_2\\otimes e_2$, and\n$P_-^{(2)}$ annihilates the two diagonal tensors while exchanging the two\ncrossed tensors with opposite sign, so $P_-^{(2)}(u\\otimes u)=0$;\n\n(d) in the actual tensor space $H^{\\otimes2}$, the two-particle antisymmetric sector $\\operatorname{ran}P_-^{(2)}$ contains no **nonzero** vector of the form $P_-^{(2)}(u\\otimes u)$: every repeated-orbital projection is zero, and zero belongs to this sector as it does to every linear subspace. Thus a nonvanishing antisymmetric two-particle vector cannot be built from two copies of the same one-particle vector. This sector is distinct from the symmetric two-particle sector of the bosonic $F(H)$ in [[thm-nrqm-fock-and-equilibrium-hilbert-direct-sum-construction]].\n\nThe antisymmetric sector and its projection are mathematical objects; as\nrecorded in the cited suppliers, selecting this sector for a species is a\npostulate and no spin-statistics statement is proved here.",
