        {
          "id": "def-nrqm-magnetic-and-detection-magnetic-schrodinger-operator",
          "kind": "definition",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Bounded-coefficient magnetic Schrodinger operator",
          "reference": "local prerequisite added by this batch (closure of the reserved claims)",
          "design_state": "batch-local prerequisite; complete-conditional-argument",
          "dependency_level": 2,
          "deps": [
            "def-nrqm-magnetic-and-detection-position-and-momentum-operators",
            "lem-nrqm-magnetic-and-detection-weak-product-rule",
            "lem-nrqm-magnetic-and-detection-momentum-operators-self-adjoint",
            "def-sobolev-space-wkp-and-its-norm",
            "def-weak-derivative-of-a-locally-integrable-function",
            "def-countable-choice",
            "def-axiom-of-choice"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-nrqm-magnetic-and-detection-position-and-momentum-operators": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-nrqm-magnetic-and-detection-weak-product-rule": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-nrqm-magnetic-and-detection-momentum-operators-self-adjoint": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-sobolev-space-wkp-and-its-norm": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-weak-derivative-of-a-locally-integrable-function": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-axiom-of-choice": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": true,
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice and the Axiom of Countable Choice\n([[def-axiom-of-choice]], [[def-countable-choice]]). Fix $\\hbar>0$, $m>0$ and\n$q\\in\\mathbb R$, and work on $L^2(\\mathbb R^3;\\mathbb C)$ with the position\nand momentum operators $Q_j,P_j$ of\n[[def-nrqm-magnetic-and-detection-position-and-momentum-operators]].\n\n**Admissible magnetic data.** Call the pair $(A,\\Phi)$ **admissible** when\n$A=(A_1,A_2,A_3)$ is a triple of real-valued classes\n$A_j\\in L^\\infty(\\mathbb R^3;\\mathbb R)$ having weak first derivatives\n$D_kA_j\\in L^\\infty(\\mathbb R^3;\\mathbb R)$ for all $j,k\\in\\{1,2,3\\}$, and\n$\\Phi\\in L^\\infty(\\mathbb R^3;\\mathbb R)$ is a real-valued bounded class\n([[def-weak-derivative-of-a-locally-integrable-function]],\n[[def-sobolev-space-wkp-and-its-norm]]). Write $|A|^2:=A_1^2+A_2^2+A_3^2$\nand $\\operatorname{div}A:=D_1A_1+D_2A_2+D_3A_3$ for chosen representatives;\nboth are bounded classes.\n\n**Magnetic momentum operators.** For admissible $(A,\\Phi)$ and\n$j\\in\\{1,2,3\\}$ define the $\\mathbb C$-linear operator\n$$P_{A,j}:=P_j-qA_j,\\qquad D(P_{A,j}):=D(P_j)=\\{f\\in L^2:\\ D_jf\\in L^2\\},$$\nwhere $A_j$ acts as multiplication; this is well defined into $L^2$ because\n$A_j\\in L^\\infty$ and $f\\in L^2$. The self-adjointness of $P_{A,j}$ is proved\nlater on this page, not asserted here.\n\n**The operator.** Put $D(K_{A,\\Phi}):=W^{2,2}(\\mathbb R^3;\\mathbb C)$ and\n$$K_{A,\\Phi}u:=\\frac1{2m}\\sum_{j=1}^3P_{A,j}\\bigl(P_{A,j}u\\bigr)+q\\,\\Phi u \\qquad(u\\in D(K_{A,\\Phi})).$$\nThis is well defined: if $u\\in W^{2,2}$ and $(A,\\Phi)$ is admissible, then\n$P_{A,j}u=P_ju-qA_ju\\in W^{1,2}(\\mathbb R^3;\\mathbb C)$ by\n[[lem-nrqm-magnetic-and-detection-weak-product-rule]] together with\n$P_ju\\in W^{1,2}$, so $P_{A,j}u\\in D(P_{A,j})$ and every summand lies in\n$L^2$. Write $K_0:=K_{(0,0)}$ for the **free operator**, so that\n$K_0u=\\frac1{2m}\\sum_jP_j(P_ju)$ on $W^{2,2}$. The same formula shows\n$K_{A,\\Phi}$ is $\\mathbb C$-linear. Its symmetry, self-adjointness, expansion\nin the magnetic momenta and relative boundedness with respect to $K_0$ are the\ncontent of\nthe self-adjointness theorem on this page,\nnot asserted here.",
          "strategy": "Complete conditional argument authored on this page; see the item body for the numbered steps.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "not-applicable"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics, first edition 2009, Section 6.1 printed pp. 133-135 (PDF pp. 145-147), Theorem 6.4 p. 135: relative boundedness and Kato-Rellich; Section 7.2 printed pp. 167-168 (PDF pp. 179-180): the free operator on H2. Background only; the bounded-coefficient magnetic operator and its weak-derivative domain construction are supplied locally.",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-schroe/schroe.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "J. Binney and D. Skinner, The Physics of Quantum Mechanics, Section 3.3 printed p. 45 equation (3.31), and Section 3.3.1 printed pp. 46-47 equations (3.40)-(3.45) (PDF pp. 53-55): minimal coupling and time-independent magnetic gauge phase algebra. The bounded-coefficient Sobolev-domain hypotheses are supplied locally.",
                "url": "https://www-thphys.physics.ox.ac.uk/people/JamesBinney/qb.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "aliases": [
            "nrqm-magnetic-and-detection-magnetic-schrodinger-operator"
          ]
        },
