          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice and the Axiom of Countable Choice\n([[def-axiom-of-choice]], [[def-countable-choice]]). Fix $\\hbar>0$, $m>0$,\n$q\\in\\mathbb R$, admissible magnetic data $(A,\\Phi)$ on $\\mathbb R^3$ and a\ngauge function $\\chi:\\mathbb R^3\\times I\\to\\mathbb R$ as in\n[[thm-nrqm-magnetic-and-detection-gauge-h2-domain-preservation]], with\nunderlying open interval $I\\subseteq\\mathbb R$. Put\n$A'_j(\\cdot,t):=A_j+D_j\\chi(\\cdot,t)$, $\\Phi'(\\cdot,t):=\\Phi-\\partial_t\\chi(\\cdot,t)$\nand, for $t\\in I$,\n$$H'(t):=K_{A'(t),\\Phi'(t)},\\qquad G(t):=\\text{multiplication by }e^{i\\frac q\\hbar\\chi(\\cdot,t)} ,$$\nso that $(A'(t),\\Phi'(t))$ is admissible for every $t$ and $H'(t)$ is\nself-adjoint with domain $W^{2,2}(\\mathbb R^3;\\mathbb C)$ by\n[[thm-nrqm-magnetic-and-detection-bounded-coefficient-magnetic-operator]].\nLet $K:=K_{A,\\Phi}$ and $U(\\tau):=e^{-i\\tau K/\\hbar}$ for $\\tau\\in\\mathbb R$,\nthe strongly continuous unitary group generated by $-iK/\\hbar$\n([[lem-self-adjoint-operator-generates-a-strongly-continuous-unitary-group]],\n[[def-unbounded-integral-against-a-pvm]]).\n\n(a) For every $t\\in I$ one has the operator identity on $W^{2,2}$\n$$H'(t)=G(t)\\,K\\,G(t)^{-1}-q\\,\\partial_t\\chi(\\cdot,t),$$\nwhere the last term is multiplication by $-q\\,\\partial_t\\chi(\\cdot,t)$;\nexplicitly, $G(t)KG(t)^{-1}=K_{A'(t),\\Phi}$ is the magnetic operator with the\ntransported vector potential and the original scalar potential $\\Phi$.\n\n(b) For every $u_0\\in W^{2,2}$ and $s\\in I$ the curve\n$$u(t):=G(t)\\,U(t-s)\\,G(s)^{-1}u_0\\qquad(t\\in I)$$\nlies in $W^{2,2}$ for every $t$, is differentiable into $L^2$ on $I$, and\nsatisfies $u(s)=u_0$ and $i\\hbar\\,u'(t)=H'(t)u(t)$ for every $t\\in I$. It is\nthe unique such curve: if $v:I\\to W^{2,2}$ is continuous into\n$W^{2,2}(\\mathbb R^3;\\mathbb C)$, differentiable into $L^2$, with\n$i\\hbar\\,v'(t)=H'(t)v(t)$ for all $t$ and $v(s)=u_0$, then $v=u$.\n\n(c) The two-parameter family\n$$U'(t,s):=G(t)\\,U(t-s)\\,G(s)^{-1}\\qquad(t,s\\in I)$$\nconsists of unitary operators mapping $W^{2,2}$ onto $W^{2,2}$, satisfies\n$U'(t,t)=I$ and the composition law\n$U'(t,r)U'(r,s)=U'(t,s)$ for all $t,r,s\\in I$, and\n$u(t)=U'(t,s)u_0$ is the solution of (b).\n\nThe theorem provides dynamics for the transformed coefficient class only; it\nasserts no general well-posedness for arbitrary time-dependent unbounded\ngenerators.",
          "strategy": "Complete conditional argument authored on this page; see the item body for the numbered steps.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
