          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice and the Axiom of Countable Choice\n([[def-axiom-of-choice]], [[def-countable-choice]]). Let $\\mathcal H$ be a\nnonzero complex Hilbert space ([[def-hilbert-space]]), let $K$ be a\nself-adjoint operator on $\\mathcal H$ with spectral projection-valued measure\n$E=E_K$ on the Borel subsets of $\\mathbb R$\n([[thm-spectral-theorem-for-unbounded-self-adjoint-operators]],\n[[def-projection-valued-measure]]), and put\n$U(t):=e^{-itK/\\hbar}=\\int_{\\mathbb R}e^{-it\\lambda/\\hbar}\\,dE(\\lambda)$ for\n$\\hbar>0$, the strongly continuous unitary group generated by $-iK/\\hbar$\n([[lem-self-adjoint-operator-generates-a-strongly-continuous-unitary-group]],\n[[def-unbounded-integral-against-a-pvm]]).\n\n(a) If a bounded operator $B\\in\\mathcal B(\\mathcal H)$ satisfies\n$BE(C)=E(C)B$ for every Borel set $C\\subseteq\\mathbb R$, then\n$BU(t)=U(t)B$ for every $t\\in\\mathbb R$.\n\n(a') If a bounded self-adjoint operator $S$ satisfies $SK\\subseteq KS$ — that\nis $S(Kx)=K(Sx)$ for every $x\\in D(K)$ — then $SU(t)=U(t)S$ for every $t$.\n\n(b) Let $F$ be a projection-valued measure on a measurable space\n$(Y,\\Sigma)$ with $F(S)E(C)=E(C)F(S)$ for all $S\\in\\Sigma$ and all Borel\n$C\\subseteq\\mathbb R$. Then:\n\n(i) $F(S)U(t)=U(t)F(S)$ for all $t$ and $S$;\n\n(ii) for every density operator $\\rho$ on $\\mathcal H$ — a self-adjoint\npositive trace-class operator with $\\operatorname{tr}\\rho=1$\n([[def-trace-class-operator]],\n[[lem-nrqm-composites-density-and-scalar-spectral-probability]] clause (a)) —\nthe numbers $\\operatorname{tr}(\\rho F(S))$ are independent of $t$:\n$$\\operatorname{tr}\\bigl(U(t)\\rho U(t)^*F(S)\\bigr)=\\operatorname{tr}\\bigl(\\rho F(S)\\bigr) \\qquad(t\\in\\mathbb R,\\ S\\in\\Sigma);$$\n\n(iii) for every unit vector $\\psi\\in\\mathcal H$ and every $S$,\n$\\|F(S)U(t)\\psi\\|^2=\\|F(S)\\psi\\|^2$ for all $t$;\n\n(c) applying (b) with $F=E$: for every density operator $\\rho$ the energy law\n$\\operatorname{tr}(\\rho E(C))$ is independent of $t$, for every unit $\\psi$\nthe law $\\|E(C)U(t)\\psi\\|^2=\\|E(C)\\psi\\|^2$ is independent of $t$, and if\n$\\psi\\in D(K)$ then both existing scalar moments are conserved:\n$$\\int_{\\mathbb R}\\lambda^k\\,dE_{K,U(t)\\psi}(\\lambda) =\\int_{\\mathbb R}\\lambda^k\\,dE_{K,\\psi}(\\lambda),\\qquad k=1,2,$$\nwith the integrals finite at $t=0$ and equal to $\\langle K\\psi,\\psi\\rangle$\nand $\\|K\\psi\\|^2$ respectively; moments that are infinite at $t=0$ remain\noutside the assertion;\n\n(d) if $K\\psi=\\lambda\\psi$ for some $\\lambda\\in\\mathbb R$ and unit\n$\\psi\\in D(K)$, then $U(t)\\psi=e^{-it\\lambda/\\hbar}\\psi$ for every $t$, and\nevery $S\\mapsto\\|F(S)\\psi\\|^2$ of (b) agrees with\n$S\\mapsto\\|F(S)U(t)\\psi\\|^2$.\n\nNo equilibration, relaxation or convergence of the law of an arbitrary state\nis asserted, and no moment beyond those finite at $t=0$ is claimed.",
          "strategy": "Complete conditional argument authored on this page; see the item body for the numbered steps.",
