        {
          "id": "post-nrqm-framework-autonomous-dynamics",
          "kind": "postulate",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "Autonomous dynamics postulate P4: self-adjoint generators and unitary evolution",
          "statement": "Adopt as physical assumptions of the framework the following statement of isolated autonomous dynamics. Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice and the Axiom of Choice ([[def-countable-choice]], [[def-axiom-of-choice]]), which are the choice hypotheses of the cited spectral and group suppliers.\n\n**(i) Energy operator.** An **isolated autonomous system** of the sector has a declared **energy operator** $H_{\\mathrm{op}}:D(H_{\\mathrm{op}})\\subset H\\to H$ that is self-adjoint ([[def-adjoint-of-a-densely-defined-unbounded-operator]], [[def-symmetric-self-adjoint-and-essentially-self-adjoint]]) and a declared energy unit in which its spectral coordinate is read. The energy operator is part of the model specification of the system; for a massive particle it is fixed by the kinematics postulate P5, and singular or unbounded model Hamiltonians require their own self-adjointness statements.\n\n**(ii) Evolution.** The time evolution of the model is the strongly continuous one-parameter unitary group\n$$U(t):=\\exp\\!\\Bigl(-\\frac{i}{\\hbar}tH_{\\mathrm{op}}\\Bigr)\\qquad(t\\in\\mathbb R),\\qquad U(t+s)=U(t)U(s),\\quad U(t)^{*}=U(t)^{-1},$$\ndefined by the spectral calculus of the self-adjoint generator ([[thm-spectral-theorem-for-unbounded-self-adjoint-operators]], [[def-unbounded-integral-against-a-pvm]], [[lem-self-adjoint-operator-generates-a-strongly-continuous-unitary-group]], [[def-strongly-continuous-one-parameter-unitary-group]]). The energy unit enters the argument of the exponential so that $H_{\\mathrm{op}}t/\\hbar$ acts in the dimensionless spectral variable.\n\n**(iii) State evolution.** A vector state evolves continuously, $\\psi(t):=U(t)\\psi(0)$ for every $\\psi(0)\\in H$, and the Schroedinger equation\n$$i\\hbar\\,\\frac{d}{dt}\\psi(t)=H_{\\mathrm{op}}\\psi(t)$$\nholds in the norm-differentiable sense exactly for initial vectors $\\psi(0)\\in D(H_{\\mathrm{op}})$, where the derivative is the norm limit of the difference quotients; for other vectors the equation is not asserted, although the evolution remains continuous. A density-operator preparation evolves as $\\rho(t)=U(t)\\rho(0)U(t)^{*}$, which is a density operator for every $t$ and satisfies $\\operatorname{tr}\\rho(t)=1$ ([[lem-nrqm-composites-density-and-scalar-spectral-probability]]).\n\n**(iv) Time-dependent families.** A prescribed time-dependent family $t\\mapsto H(t)$ of self-adjoint operators is a different model assumption: a norm-continuous finite-dimensional Hermitian family is used only through the unitary two-time propagator that its family defines, and the exponential of the integral of $H(t)$ is not identified with that propagator unless the family commutes with itself at different times. The general unbounded time-dependent case requires a separate existence and domain theorem of its own and is not adopted by this postulate; the driven-dynamics page states its own assumptions for the models it treats.\n\n**(v) Open systems.** A non-unitary evolution of the reduced description of a system coupled to an environment is an extension obtained from an explicitly chosen environment model and a declared reduction, not a replacement for clause (ii); no environment model is adopted by this postulate.\n\n**(vi) Status.** Clauses (i)-(v) are adopted assumptions of the isolated-system idealization. They assert nothing about the origin of the energy operator of a concrete system, about the accuracy of the idealization for a laboratory preparation, or about which laboratory interactions realize an isolated evolution; those are tested identifications in the sense of P7.",
          "strategy": "A postulate, not a theorem: it adopts the self-adjoint energy operator, the unitary evolution it generates, the Schroedinger equation on the operator domain, and the separation of driven and open-system evolution.",
          "deps": [
            "def-adjoint-of-a-densely-defined-unbounded-operator",
            "def-symmetric-self-adjoint-and-essentially-self-adjoint",
            "def-strongly-continuous-one-parameter-unitary-group",
