          "dependency_level": 6,
          "physical_scope": "The autonomous-dynamics assumption of the framework: an isolated system's energy is a self-adjoint operator with a declared energy unit, the state of a vector or density operator evolves by the unitary group it generates, and the Schroedinger equation holds on the operator domain. Adoption is a model assumption of the isolated-system idealization; driven and open systems are excluded and require their own assumptions, and no claim is made that any laboratory system is exactly isolated.",
