          "dependency_level": 7,
          "physical_scope": "A refutation, on an explicit normalized state in the one-dimensional specialization of the P1 state assignment and P2 position-probability rule, of the claim that every normalized preparation has a finite position mean. The displayed state has unit norm but neither a finite second moment nor a finite first absolute moment. The item defines the mean as the Lebesgue expectation and states its absolute-integrability condition; it asserts no measured value and no empirical claim.",
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics, 1st edition 2009, Section 2.1, printed pages 55-58 (PDF pages 67-70): the probability interpretation, expectation values and the moment conditions for position",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-schroe/schroe.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "B. Zwiebach, MIT 8.05 Quantum Physics II (Fall 2013), Chapter 1 'Wave Mechanics', Section 1, printed pages 1-4: normalization of wave functions and the probability density",
                "url": "https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/8-05-quantum-physics-ii-fall-2013/61bc31b8d8bf0680c322733910a71aa0_MIT8_05F13_Chap_01.pdf"
