            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "dependency_level": 8,
          "physical_scope": "A worked computation in the framework's two-level state space showing that two distinct statistical mixtures of pure preparations, with different members and different weights, determine the same mixed preparation: the diagonal state with eigenvalues 3/4 and 1/4 arises both as the orthonormal spectral ensemble with weights 3/4, 1/4 and as the uniform mixture of two non-orthogonal pure states. The item shows that the state does not determine the ensemble; it asserts no measurement probability, no apparatus realization and no empirical result, and it makes no claim of physical incompleteness.",
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "J. Preskill, Lecture Notes for Ph219/CS219: Quantum Information, Chapter 2 (updated July 2015), Sections 2.5.1-2.5.2 and 2.5.5, printed pages 26-29 and 34-36: the ambiguity of the ensemble interpretation and the ensemble preparation of convex combinations",
                "url": "https://preskill.caltech.edu/ph219/chap2_15.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "J. Binney and D. Skinner, The Physics of Quantum Mechanics, Section 6.3, printed pages 121-125: the density operator of a mixture in two different bases, and the non-uniqueness of the expansion of a density operator",
                "url": "https://www-thphys.physics.ox.ac.uk/people/JamesBinney/qb.pdf"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "cex-nrqm-state-geometry-zero-vector-is-not-a-preparation",
          "kind": "counterexample",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "The zero vector determines no pure preparation and no state",
          "statement": "Adopt the state postulate of the framework, and let $H\\ne\\{0\\}$ be the Hilbert space assigned to a declared system. Then: **every** vector of $H$ determines a pure preparation of the system; the zero vector determines the zero operator $0$, which is the state of the system when no preparation is made, and the normalization convention $0/\\|0\\|=0$ supplies the unit representative of its ray.",
          "strategy": "Direct refutation of the claim that every vector determines a pure preparation: no unit representative exists for the zero vector, the normalization is undefined, and the zero operator is not a density operator.",
          "deps": [
            "post-nrqm-framework-state-and-composition",
            "def-nrqm-state-geometry-framework-state-space",
            "def-nrqm-state-geometry-state-vectors-and-rays",
            "lem-nrqm-state-geometry-ray-to-rank-one-projection",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-rank-one-operator-calculus",
            "cor-inner-product-induces-a-norm",
            "def-field",
            "def-complex-numbers-and-arithmetic",
            "thm-complex-numbers-form-a-field",
            "def-countable-choice"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "post-nrqm-framework-state-and-composition": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-nrqm-state-geometry-framework-state-space": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-nrqm-state-geometry-state-vectors-and-rays": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-nrqm-state-geometry-ray-to-rank-one-projection": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-rank-one-operator-calculus": "mathematical-premise",
            "cor-inner-product-induces-a-norm": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-field": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-complex-numbers-and-arithmetic": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-complex-numbers-form-a-field": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "dependency_level": 7,
          "physical_scope": "A refutation, inside the framework's state semantics, of the claim that every vector of the assigned Hilbert space determines a pure preparation with the zero vector corresponding to the zero operator: the zero vector has no unit representative, the normalization map is undefined at it, and the zero operator has trace zero and is not a density operator, so under the state postulate no preparation and no state is assigned to it. The item refutes that specific informal claim; it asserts no empirical result and no claim about nature.",
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "J. Preskill, Lecture Notes for Ph219/CS219: Quantum Information, Chapter 2 (updated July 2015), Section 2.1, printed page 4: positivity of the inner product is stated for |psi> not equal to 0, and a ray is an equivalence class of nonzero vectors",
                "url": "https://preskill.caltech.edu/ph219/chap2_15.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics, 1st edition 2009, Section 2.1, printed pages 55-56 (PDF pages 66-67): the states are the vectors of norm one, so the zero vector is not a state",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-schroe/schroe.pdf"
