        {
          "id": "lem-nrqm-observables-spectral-measure-atoms-and-eigenvalues",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Atoms of the spectral measure and eigenvalues of a self-adjoint operator",
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice and the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-axiom-of-choice]], [[def-countable-choice]]). Let $H\\ne\\{0\\}$ be a complex Hilbert space ([[def-hilbert-space]]), let $A$ be a self-adjoint operator on $H$ with spectral projection-valued measure $E_A$ on the Borel $\\sigma$-algebra of $\\mathbb R$ ([[thm-spectral-theorem-for-unbounded-self-adjoint-operators]], [[def-projection-valued-measure]]), and let $E_{A,x}(B):=\\langle E_A(B)x,x\\rangle$ be its scalar measures ([[lem-scalar-and-complex-measures-from-a-pvm]]). For $\\lambda\\in\\mathbb R$ say that $\\lambda$ is an **eigenvalue** of $A$ when $Ax=\\lambda x$ for some nonzero $x\\in D(A)$, the domain-restricted reading of [[def-eigenvalue-eigenvector-eigenspace-and-spectrum]]. Then:\n\n(a) The orthogonal projection $E_A(\\{\\lambda\\})$ is the projection of $H$ onto the eigenspace $\\ker(A-\\lambda)=\\{x\\in D(A):Ax=\\lambda x\\}$; in particular $E_A(\\{\\lambda\\})\\ne0$ if and only if $\\lambda$ is an eigenvalue of $A$.\n\n(b) For every density operator $\\rho$ on $H$, that is every self-adjoint positive trace-class $\\rho$ with $\\operatorname{tr}\\rho=1$ ([[lem-nrqm-composites-density-and-scalar-spectral-probability]] clause (a)), the number $\\mu^{A}_{\\rho}(\\{\\lambda\\})=\\operatorname{tr}(\\rho E_{A}(\\{\\lambda\\}))$ is the weight that the scalar law $\\mu^{A}_{\\rho}$ assigns to the singleton $\\{\\lambda\\}$: it vanishes for every $\\rho$ whenever $\\lambda$ is not an eigenvalue of $A$, and it equals $1$ for the pure state $T_{u,u}$ of every unit eigenvector $u\\in\\ker(A-\\lambda)$.\n\n(c) If $A$ has no eigenvalues at all, then $\\mu^{A}_{\\rho}(\\{\\lambda\\})=0$ for every density operator $\\rho$ and every $\\lambda\\in\\mathbb R$: the scalar law of every state carries no point mass, while its values on general Borel sets remain $\\operatorname{tr}(\\rho E_{A}(B))$.\n\nClauses (a)-(c) are mathematical statements about $A$, $E_A$ and the density operators; no physical interpretation of $\\mu^{A}_{\\rho}$ is asserted here.",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "deps": [
            "def-axiom-of-choice",
            "def-countable-choice",
            "def-eigenvalue-eigenvector-eigenspace-and-spectrum",
            "def-hilbert-orthogonal-projection",
