        {
          "id": "lem-nrqm-observables-outcome-law-affinity-and-trace-norm-continuity",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Affinity and trace-norm continuity of the scalar spectral law",
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]) and let $H$ be a nonzero complex Hilbert space ([[def-hilbert-space]]). Let $A$ be a self-adjoint operator on $H$ with spectral projection-valued measure $E_A$ ([[def-projection-valued-measure]]). For a self-adjoint trace-class operator $T$ on $H$ ([[def-trace-class-operator]], [[def-trace-of-a-trace-class-operator]]) and a Borel set $B\\subseteq\\mathbb R$ put\n$$\\Phi_T(B):=\\operatorname{tr}\\bigl(TE_A(B)\\bigr)\\in\\mathbb C .$$\nThen:\n\n(a) $|\\Phi_T(B)|\\le\\|T\\|_1$ for every Borel set $B$; the map $T\\mapsto\\Phi_T(B)$ is real-linear on the self-adjoint trace-class operators; and for every density operator $\\rho$ one has $0\\le\\Phi_\\rho(B)\\le1$, so that $\\mu^{A}_\\rho:=\\Phi_\\rho$ is a probability measure on the Borel sets with $\\mu^{A}_\\rho(\\mathbb R)=1$ ([[lem-nrqm-composites-density-and-scalar-spectral-probability]] clause (b)).\n\n(b) If $\\rho=\\sum_nw_n\\rho_n$ is a statistical mixture of density operators $\\rho_n$ with weights $w_n\\ge0$, $\\sum_nw_n=1$, the trace-norm convergent sum of [[lem-nrqm-state-geometry-density-set-convex-and-complete]], then for every Borel set $B$\n$$\\mu^{A}_{\\rho}(B)=\\sum_nw_n\\,\\mu^{A}_{\\rho_n}(B),$$\nthe series converging absolutely.\n\n(c) For density operators $\\rho,\\sigma$ one has\n$$\\sup\\{\\,|\\mu^{A}_{\\rho}(B)-\\mu^{A}_{\\sigma}(B)|:\\ B\\subseteq\\mathbb R\\ \\text{Borel}\\,\\}\\le\\|\\rho-\\sigma\\|_1,$$\nand if density operators $\\rho_k$ converge to $\\rho$ in trace norm, then $\\mu^{A}_{\\rho_k}(B)\\to\\mu^{A}_{\\rho}(B)$ uniformly over all Borel sets $B$.",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "deps": [
            "def-countable-choice",
            "def-hilbert-space",
            "def-projection-valued-measure",
            "def-trace-class-operator",
