        {
          "id": "lem-nrqm-observables-states-separated-by-bounded-projections",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Distinct density operators are separated by the law of a bounded rank-one projection",
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]); the Axiom of Choice is used only where the spectral theorem for unbounded self-adjoint operators is invoked ([[def-axiom-of-choice]]). Let $H$ be a nonzero complex Hilbert space ([[def-hilbert-space]]) and let $\\rho,\\sigma$ be density operators on $H$ with $\\rho\\ne\\sigma$ ([[lem-nrqm-composites-density-and-scalar-spectral-probability]] clause (a)). Then:\n\n(a) There is a unit vector $w\\in H$ with $\\langle\\rho w,w\\rangle\\ne\\langle\\sigma w,w\\rangle$.\n\n(b) For the rank-one orthogonal projection $P:=T_{w,w}$ of [[lem-nrqm-composites-rank-one-operator-calculus]] ([[def-hilbert-orthogonal-projection]]), whose spectral projection-valued measure assigns $P$ to the Borel set $\\{1\\}$, the two scalar laws of [[lem-nrqm-composites-density-and-scalar-spectral-probability]] clause (b) satisfy\n$$\\mu^{P}_{\\rho}(\\{1\\})=\\operatorname{tr}(\\rho P)=\\langle\\rho w,w\\rangle,\\qquad \\mu^{P}_{\\sigma}(\\{1\\})=\\operatorname{tr}(\\sigma P)=\\langle\\sigma w,w\\rangle,$$\nso the bounded sharp observable $P$ assigns different outcome probabilities to $\\rho$ and $\\sigma$.\n\n(c) For every unit vector $w$ and every self-adjoint trace-class $T$ one has $|\\operatorname{tr}(TT_{w,w})|\\le\\|T\\|_1$; in particular $|\\langle\\rho w,w\\rangle-\\langle\\sigma w,w\\rangle|\\le\\|\\rho-\\sigma\\|_1$.",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "deps": [
            "def-axiom-of-choice",
