          "id": "lem-nrqm-measurement-selective-luders-update",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "The selective Lueders update by an orthogonal projection",
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $H$ be a nonzero complex Hilbert space ([[def-hilbert-space]]), let $P$ be an orthogonal projection on $H$ ([[def-hilbert-orthogonal-projection]]) and let $\\rho$ be a density operator with $p:=\\operatorname{tr}(\\rho P)>0$ ([[lem-nrqm-composites-density-and-scalar-spectral-probability]] clause (a)). Define the **selective update**\n$$\\rho_{P}:=\\frac{P\\rho P}{p}.$$\nThen:\n\n(a) $P\\rho P$ is a positive trace-class operator with $\\operatorname{tr}(P\\rho P)=p$, so $\\rho_{P}$ is a density operator;\n\n(b) $\\operatorname{tr}(\\rho_{P}P)=1$ and\n$$P\\rho_{P}P=\\rho_{P}=P\\rho_{P}=\\rho_{P}P;$$\nin particular $\\rho_{P}$ commutes with $P$ and is fixed by compression with $P$;\n\n(c) if $Q$ is an orthogonal projection with $QP=0$, then $\\operatorname{tr}(\\rho_{P}Q)=0$ and $Q\\rho_{P}Q=0$;\n\n(d) if $\\rho=T_{u,u}$ for a unit vector $u$ with $Pu\\ne0$, where $T_{u,u}x=\\langle x,u\\rangle u$ ([[lem-nrqm-composites-rank-one-operator-calculus]]), then $\\rho_{P}=T_{Pu,Pu}/\\|Pu\\|^{2}$, the pure state of the normalized vector $Pu$; the value depends only on the ray of $Pu$, meaning its equivalence class of nonzero vectors under $x\\sim y$ if $y=zx$ for some $z\\in\\mathbb C\\setminus\\{0\\}$.\n\nNo physical interpretation of the update is asserted.",
