          "physical_scope": "A conditional consequence of the adopted ideal conditional-measurement postulate P3 for a declared ideal sharp measurement: the Born outcome probabilities, the selective Lueders conditional states, the certainty of an immediately repeated outcome, the discarded-outcome state as the outcome-weighted mixture of the conditional states, invariance of bounded quantities compatible with the declared measurement under discarding, and the loss of coherence between non-selected branches. The theorem asserts nothing about any laboratory apparatus, about outcome uniqueness or about measurements outside the declared class."
        },
        {
          "id": "pthm-nrqm-measurement-degenerate-eigenspace-update",
          "kind": "physics-theorem",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "The Lueders update on a degenerate eigenspace preserves intra-eigenspace coherence",
          "statement": "Adopt the state postulate P1, the observable and probability postulate P2 and the ideal conditional-measurement postulate P3 ([[post-nrqm-framework-state-and-composition]], [[post-nrqm-framework-observable-and-probability]], [[post-nrqm-framework-ideal-conditional-measurement]]), and assume the Axiom of Countable Choice and the Axiom of Choice, the hypotheses of the cited spectral mathematics. Let $A$ be a bounded assigned sharp observable of a system with state space $D(H)$ ([[def-nrqm-observables-framework-observable-and-outcome-law]]), with spectral projection-valued measure $E_{A}$ ([[lem-nrqm-observables-spectral-measure-atoms-and-eigenvalues]]), and let $\\lambda$ be an eigenvalue of $A$ with eigenspace $K=\\ker(A-\\lambda I)$ and $P:=E_{A}(\\{\\lambda\\})$, the orthogonal projection of $H$ onto $K$. Declare the two-outcome ideal sharp measurement $(P,I-P)$, the **$\\lambda$-readout** of $A$. Let $\\psi\\in K$ with $\\|\\psi\\|=1$ and let $\\rho=T_{\\psi,\\psi}$ be the pure state of $\\psi$. Then:\n\n**(a) Certainty and trivial update.** $p_{\\lambda}=\\operatorname{tr}(\\rho P)=1$, and the conditional state after the outcome $\\lambda$ is $\\rho_{\\lambda}=\\rho$: the $\\lambda$-readout leaves this preparation unchanged.\n\n**(b) No disturbance inside the eigenspace.** For every assigned sharp observable $C$ and every Borel set $S\\subseteq\\mathbb R$, the outcome law of $C$ computed in the conditional state equals its law computed in $\\rho$ ([[def-nrqm-observables-framework-observable-and-outcome-law]] clause (b)); in particular the $\\lambda$-readout induces no decoherence or disturbance within the eigenspace.\n\n**(c) Degenerate case: coherence is retained.** If $\\dim K\\ge2$ and $\\psi=\\alpha u+\\beta v$ with $u,v$ orthonormal vectors of $K$ and $\\alpha,\\beta\\in\\mathbb C\\setminus\\{0\\}$, then the conditional state is the coherent superposition $T_{\\psi,\\psi}$, not the mixture $|\\alpha|^{2}T_{u,u}+|\\beta|^{2}T_{v,v}$: for the bounded assigned sharp observable\n$$W:=T_{w,w}-T_{w',w'},\\qquad w:=\\frac{u+v}{\\sqrt2},\\qquad w'=\\frac{u-v}{\\sqrt2},$$\nwith $W$ declared dimensionless (spectral unit $1$), the conditional state assigns probability $1$ to the value $+1$ of $W$ whenever $\\alpha=\\beta=1/\\sqrt2$, i.e. whenever $\\psi=w$, while the mixture $|\\alpha|^{2}T_{u,u}+|\\beta|^{2}T_{v,v}$ assigns probability $1/2$ to each of the values $+1$ and $-1$ of $W$.\n\n**(d) Scope.** The update used here is the Lueders update with the eigenspace projection $P$ itself, as adopted in P3; no physical apparatus is asserted to perform the $\\lambda$-readout without disturbance, and a declared apparatus that resolves the eigenspace further (a finer family of projections inside $K$) is a different declared measurement, not the coarse $\\lambda$-readout.",
