            ]
          },
          "physical_scope": "A conditional statement about the declared ideal sharp measurement of a bounded assigned sharp observable at a degenerate eigenvalue: the Lueders update by the eigenspace projection leaves a pure preparation inside that eigenspace unchanged, so no decoherence is induced inside the eigenspace and subsequent laws are those of the unmodified preparation. It asserts no apparatus realization and does not claim that a laboratory eigenvalue readout preserves coherence or that it resolves or fails to resolve the degeneracy in any particular device."
        },
        {
          "id": "pthm-nrqm-measurement-instrument-updates-not-determined-by-effects",
          "kind": "physics-theorem",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "Outcome effects do not determine the conditional update, and general instruments need not be repeatable",
          "statement": "Adopt the state postulate P1, the observable and probability postulate P2 and the ideal conditional-measurement postulate P3 ([[post-nrqm-framework-state-and-composition]], [[post-nrqm-framework-observable-and-probability]], [[post-nrqm-framework-ideal-conditional-measurement]]), and assume the Axiom of Countable Choice. Let a declared two-level system have state space $D(\\mathbb C^{2})$ with orthonormal basis $(e_{1},e_{2})$ of $\\mathbb C^{2}$ ([[def-nrqm-measurement-framework-declared-measurements-and-instruments]], [[def-nrqm-state-geometry-framework-state-space]]), write $P_{i}:=T_{e_{i},e_{i}}$ for the rank-one projections and $W:=T_{e_{2},e_{1}}+T_{e_{1},e_{2}}$ for the swap, and declare the dimensionless sharp observable $B:=P_{1}-P_{2}$ (its spectral values have unit $1$). Then:\n\n**(a) Two normalized instruments with equal effects.** The families\n$$\\bigl(M_{0},M_{1}\\bigr)=\\bigl(P_{1},P_{2}\\bigr),\\qquad \\bigl(M_{0}',M_{1}'\\bigr)=\\bigl(WP_{1},P_{2}\\bigr)$$\nare both normalized declared instruments on $\\mathbb C^{2}$, and both have the effects $F_{0}=F_{0}'=P_{1}$, $F_{1}=F_{1}'=P_{2}$.\n\n**(b) Different updates and different predictions.** For every state $\\rho$ with $p_{0}=\\operatorname{tr}(\\rho P_{1})>0$ the conditional state after the outcome $0$ is $T_{e_{1},e_{1}}$ for the first instrument and $T_{e_{2},e_{2}}$ for the second. Consequently, for the bounded assigned sharp observable $B=P_{1}-P_{2}$, the probability of the value $+1$ after the outcome $0$ is $1$ under the first instrument and $0$ under the second, although the two instruments have identical outcome effects and identical outcome probabilities $p_{0},p_{1}$ in every preparation. Hence the effects do not determine the conditional update; the update is part of the declared apparatus model (clause (v) of P3, [[lem-nrqm-composites-finite-effects-and-instruments]] clause (d)).\n\n**(c) A non-repeatable declared instrument.** The family\n$$N_{+}:=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt2}I,\\qquad N_{-}:=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt2}B$$\nis a normalized declared instrument with effects $F_{+}=F_{-}=\\tfrac12 I$. Its outcome probabilities are $\\tfrac12,\\tfrac12$ in every preparation, and conditioned on either outcome an immediate repetition of the same declared instrument again yields each outcome with probability $\\tfrac12$; the probability of repeating the same outcome is $\\tfrac12$, not $1$. So declared instruments need not be repeatable, in contrast to the projective Lueders case of [[pthm-nrqm-measurement-projective-outcomes-and-discarded-ensembles]] clause (b).\n\n**(d) Scope.** Clauses (a)-(c) are statements about the declared instruments displayed; they assert no property of any laboratory device, no uniqueness of recorded outcomes and no dynamics of an apparatus. Whether a device is described by one of these instruments is a tested identification with uncertainty under P7.",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "deps": [
            "def-bounded-linear-operator",
            "def-countable-choice",
            "def-hilbert-orthogonal-projection",
            "def-hilbert-space",
