          "physical_scope": "A declared-instrument statement on the two-level model: two normalized instruments with identical outcome effects have different conditional updates and therefore different predictions for a subsequent measurement, and a third instrument with effects proportional to the identity is not repeatable. The theorem is a statement about declared apparatus models under P2(iv) and P3(v); it asserts no apparatus realization and no empirical fact."
        },
        {
          "id": "pthm-nrqm-measurement-finite-effects-dilation",
          "kind": "physics-theorem",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "A declared finite effect family is realised by a dilated ideal projective measurement",
          "statement": "Adopt the state postulate P1, the observable and probability postulate P2 and the ideal conditional-measurement postulate P3 ([[post-nrqm-framework-state-and-composition]], [[post-nrqm-framework-observable-and-probability]], [[post-nrqm-framework-ideal-conditional-measurement]]), and assume the Axiom of Countable Choice and the Axiom of Choice. Let $H$ be the nonzero complex Hilbert space assigned to a declared system, and let $(F_{a})_{a=1}^{n}$ be a declared finite family of effects on $H$ in the general-H sense of [[def-nrqm-measurement-framework-declared-measurements-and-instruments]] clause (d): each $F_a$ is bounded and self-adjoint, $0\\le\\langle F_ax,x\\rangle\\le\\|x\\|^{2}$ for every $x\\in H$, and $\\sum_{a}F_{a}=I$. The outcome probabilities are those of clause (iv) of P2. Let $C=\\mathbb C^{n}$ with orthonormal basis $(e_{a})_{a=1}^{n}$, form the completed tensor product $H\\widehat\\otimes C$ ([[lem-nrqm-composites-hilbert-tensor-construction]]), and define\n$$W:H\\to H\\widehat\\otimes C,\\qquad W\\psi:=\\sum_{a=1}^{n}F_{a}^{1/2}\\psi\\otimes e_{a},\\qquad P_{a}:=I_{H}\\otimes T_{e_{a},e_{a}},$$\nwhere $F_{a}^{1/2}$ is the positive square root supplied by the continuous functional calculus ([[thm-continuous-functional-calculus-for-bounded-self-adjoint-operators]]) and $T_{x,x}$ is the rank-one projection of [[lem-nrqm-composites-rank-one-operator-calculus]]. Then:\n\n**(a) The dilation.** $W$ is a linear isometry, the operators $P_{a}$ are pairwise orthogonal orthogonal projections on $H\\widehat\\otimes C$ with strong sum $I$, and $W^{*}P_{a}W=F_{a}$ for every $a$.\n\n**(b) Realised outcome probabilities.** For every state $\\rho$ on $H$ the operator $\\widetilde\\rho:=W\\rho W^{*}$ is a state on $H\\widehat\\otimes C$, and the declared ideal sharp measurement $(P_{a})_{a=1}^{n}$ on the composite model space has outcome probabilities\n$$\\operatorname{tr}\\bigl(\\widetilde\\rho\\,P_{a}\\bigr)=\\operatorname{tr}(\\rho F_{a})\\qquad(a=1,\\dots,n).$$\n\n**(c) The induced instrument.** Let $\\Lambda$ be the trace-preserving map $\\Lambda(\\sigma)=\\sum_{b=1}^{n}F_{b}^{1/2}\\sigma F_{b}^{1/2}$ (the square-root Kraus map of the effect family). If $p_{a}:=\\operatorname{tr}(\\rho F_{a})>0$, the conditional composite state after the outcome $a$ is $\\widetilde\\rho_{a}=P_{a}\\widetilde\\rho P_{a}/p_{a}$, and its reduction to $H$ is the state\n$$\\operatorname{Tr}_{C}\\widetilde\\rho_{a}=\\frac{1}{p_{a}}F_{a}^{1/2}\\rho F_{a}^{1/2}.$$\nThe non-selective composite state reduces to $\\operatorname{Tr}_{C}\\sum_{a}P_{a}\\widetilde\\rho P_{a}=\\sum_{a}F_{a}^{1/2}\\rho F_{a}^{1/2}=\\Lambda(\\rho)$. Thus this dilation induces on $H$ the declared square-root instrument with one Kraus operator $M_{a}=F_{a}^{1/2}$ for each outcome $a$ and effects $F_{a}$ ([[def-nrqm-measurement-framework-declared-measurements-and-instruments]] clause (d)).\n\n**(d) Projective case and scope of the update.** If the effects are pairwise orthogonal projections, $F_{a}=P_{a}^{\\circ}$ with $P_{a}^{\\circ}P_{b}^{\\circ}=0$ for $a\\ne b$, then the induced update of clause (c) is the Lueders update $P_{a}^{\\circ}\\rho P_{a}^{\\circ}/p_{a}$. For general effects, clause (c) identifies the update selected by this particular dilation; the effects alone do not determine the update among all declared instruments, as shown by [[pthm-nrqm-measurement-instrument-updates-not-determined-by-effects]].\n\n**(e) Scope.** The ancilla register $C$ and the isometry $W$ are mathematical objects of a declared composite model space; the theorem asserts no physical ancilla, no physical realisation of the dilated projective measurement and no preferred outcome. Whether a laboratory device realises the declared effects or either update is a tested identification with uncertainty under P7.",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "deps": [
            "def-axiom-of-choice",
            "def-bounded-linear-operator",
            "def-countable-choice",
            "def-spectrum-and-resolvent-of-a-bounded-operator",
            "def-hilbert-space-adjoint",
            "def-hilbert-orthogonal-projection",
            "def-self-adjoint-positive-unitary-and-normal-operator",
            "def-nrqm-measurement-framework-declared-measurements-and-instruments",
            "def-nrqm-state-geometry-framework-state-space",
            "def-nrqm-state-geometry-pure-mixed-states-and-purity",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-bounded-tensor-maps",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-density-and-scalar-spectral-probability",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-hilbert-tensor-construction",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-nuclear-bounded-cyclicity",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-rank-one-operator-calculus",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-separable-partial-trace",
