                "url": "https://www-thphys.physics.ox.ac.uk/people/JamesBinney/qb.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "physical_scope": "A conditional model statement: a declared finite family of bounded effects on a system is realised as the outcome probabilities of a declared ideal sharp measurement on an enlarged model space carrying a finite ancilla register, and the induced conditional reduced states are given explicitly. The construction is an idealisation within the declared composite model space; it asserts no physical apparatus, no physical ancilla and no preferred outcome."
        },
        {
          "id": "pthm-nrqm-measurement-countable-kraus-instruments",
          "kind": "physics-theorem",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "Declared countable instruments: normalization, discarded ensembles and the repeatability criterion",
          "statement": "Adopt the state postulate P1, the observable and probability postulate P2 and the ideal conditional-measurement postulate P3 ([[post-nrqm-framework-state-and-composition]], [[post-nrqm-framework-observable-and-probability]], [[post-nrqm-framework-ideal-conditional-measurement]]), and assume the Axiom of Countable Choice, the hypothesis of the cited mathematics. Let $H$ be the nonzero complex Hilbert space assigned to a declared system ([[def-nrqm-state-geometry-framework-state-space]]), and let $(M_{a})_{a\\ge1}$ be a declared normalized countable Kraus family on $H$: bounded operators with\n$$\\sum_{a=1}^{N}M_{a}^{*}M_{a}\\longrightarrow I\\qquad\\text{strongly as }N\\to\\infty .$$\nDeclare the countable instrument with outcome set $\\{1,2,\\dots\\}$, effects $F_{a}:=M_{a}^{*}M_{a}$, outcome probabilities $p_{a}:=\\operatorname{tr}(\\rho F_{a})$, conditional updates $\\rho_{a}:=M_{a}\\rho M_{a}^{*}/p_{a}$ for $p_{a}>0$, and discarded-outcome map $\\Phi(\\rho):=\\sum_{a\\ge1}M_{a}\\rho M_{a}^{*}$ ([[def-nrqm-measurement-framework-declared-measurements-and-instruments]] clause (d)). Then:\n\n**(a) POVM and discarded ensemble.** Each $F_{a}$ is an effect, $0\\le F_{a}\\le I$; for every state $\\rho$ one has $p_{a}\\ge0$ and $\\sum_{a}p_{a}=1$; $\\Phi$ is a positive trace-preserving linear map of the trace-class operators and maps states to states; and $\\Phi(\\rho)=\\sum_{a:p_{a}>0}p_{a}\\rho_{a}$, a trace-norm convergent mixture of the conditional states.\n\n**(b) Repeatability criterion.** The declared instrument is **repeatable**, i.e. for every state $\\rho$ and every $a$ with $p_{a}>0$ an immediate repetition of the same declared instrument returns the outcome $a$ with probability $1$ and every $b\\ne a$ with probability $0$, if and only if\n$$M_{b}M_{a}=0\\qquad\\text{for all }a,b\\text{ with }b\\ne a .$$\nEquivalently, $M_a^*F_aM_a=F_a$ for every $a$. If $H$ is finite-dimensional, this criterion also forces each $F_a$ to be an orthogonal projection; the projection condition is not imposed for general $H$.\n\n**(c) Projective case.** For a declared ideal sharp measurement $(P_{a})$ the Kraus family $M_{a}=P_{a}$ satisfies the criterion of (b) and is repeatable, in agreement with [[pthm-nrqm-measurement-projective-outcomes-and-discarded-ensembles]] clause (b); a general normalized Kraus family need not satisfy it ([[pthm-nrqm-measurement-instrument-updates-not-determined-by-effects]] clause (c)).\n\n**(d) Non-determination.** The effects $(F_{a})$ determine the outcome probabilities but not the conditional updates; the Kraus family is part of the declared instrument (clause (v) of P3, [[pthm-nrqm-measurement-instrument-updates-not-determined-by-effects]] clause (b)).\n\n**(e) Scope.** Clauses (a)-(d) are conditional statements about the declared countable instrument; they assert no apparatus realization, no outcome uniqueness and no empirical fact, and no claim is made that every positive trace-preserving map admits such a Kraus family ([[lem-nrqm-composites-countable-kraus-normalization]] clause (c)).",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "deps": [
