        {
          "id": "lem-nrqm-autonomous-dynamics-stationary-ray-characterization",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Stationary rays of a self-adjoint flow are exactly the eigenrays",
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice and the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-axiom-of-choice]], [[def-countable-choice]]). Let $H\\ne\\{0\\}$ be a complex Hilbert space ([[def-hilbert-space]], [[def-inner-product-space]]), let $T$ be self-adjoint ([[def-symmetric-self-adjoint-and-essentially-self-adjoint]]) with spectral projection-valued measure $E$ ([[thm-spectral-theorem-for-unbounded-self-adjoint-operators]], [[def-projection-valued-measure]]), let $U(t)=e^{itT}=\\int e^{it\\lambda}\\,dE(\\lambda)$ be the generated strongly continuous unitary group ([[def-strongly-continuous-one-parameter-unitary-group]], [[def-unbounded-integral-against-a-pvm]]), and let $\\psi\\in H$ with $\\psi\\ne0$. Then the following are equivalent:\n\n(i) for every $t\\in\\mathbb R$ the vector $U(t)\\psi$ is a complex multiple of $\\psi$ (the ray of $\\psi$ is invariant under the flow);\n\n(ii) $\\psi\\in D(T)$ and $T\\psi=\\lambda\\psi$ for some $\\lambda\\in\\mathbb R$ (the ray of $\\psi$ is an eigenray of $T$).\n\nIf these hold for the eigenvalue $\\lambda$, then $U(t)\\psi=e^{it\\lambda}\\psi$ for every $t\\in\\mathbb R$.",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "deps": [
            "cor-finite-dimensional-subspaces-are-closed",
