                "title": "J. Binney and D. Skinner, The Physics of Quantum Mechanics, Sections 2.2 and 4.3-4.4, printed pages 21-23 and 68-71 (time evolution, conserved quantities, stationary states and the Heisenberg picture)",
                "url": "https://www-thphys.physics.ox.ac.uk/people/JamesBinney/qb.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "physical_scope": "The evolution vocabulary of the framework's autonomous-dynamics postulate P4: the assigned energy observable and its unit, the unitary flow it generates, the Schroedinger-picture evolution of state vectors and density operators, the Heisenberg-picture representative of a bounded assigned sharp observable, stationarity of pure preparations, and compatibility (conservation) of an assigned sharp observable with the energy. This item fixes readings and terminology of P4 together with P1 and P2; it adopts no assumption beyond those postulates and the cited mathematics, asserts no evolution for driven or open systems, no measurement or apparatus realization, no isolation claim about any laboratory system, and no empirical result."
        },
        {
          "id": "pthm-nrqm-autonomous-dynamics-schrodinger-picture-flow",
          "kind": "physics-theorem",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "The Schroedinger-picture flow: unitarity, domain invariance and the domain-qualified equation",
          "statement": "Adopt the state and composition postulate [[post-nrqm-framework-state-and-composition]] (P1), the observable and probability postulate in the reading of [[def-nrqm-observables-framework-observable-and-outcome-law]], and the autonomous-dynamics postulate [[post-nrqm-framework-autonomous-dynamics]] (P4), and assume the Axiom of Countable Choice and the Axiom of Choice ([[def-countable-choice]], [[def-axiom-of-choice]]), the choice hypotheses of the cited spectral suppliers. Let $H$ be the state space assigned to a declared isolated system of the massive-matter sector ([[def-nrqm-state-geometry-framework-state-space]]), let $(H_{\\mathrm{op}},u_H)$ be its assigned energy observable with spectral projection-valued measure $E_H$ ([[def-nrqm-autonomous-dynamics-framework-evolution]] clause (a)), and let\n$$U(t)=\\exp\\!\\Bigl(-\\frac{i}{\\hbar}tH_{\\mathrm{op}}\\Bigr)=\\int_{\\mathbb R}e^{-it\\lambda/\\hbar}\\,dE_H(\\lambda),\\qquad \\psi(t):=U(t)\\psi(0),\\qquad \\rho(t):=U(t)\\rho(0)U(t)^{*}$$\nbe the flow and the state evolutions of clauses (b) and (c) of [[def-nrqm-autonomous-dynamics-framework-evolution]], with $\\hbar>0$ and the energy unit in the sense of [[def-nrqm-framework-quantities-and-units]]. Then:\n\n(a) **Unitary flow.** $U$ is a strongly continuous one-parameter unitary group ([[def-strongly-continuous-one-parameter-unitary-group]]) with $U(0)=I$, $U(t+s)=U(t)U(s)$ and $U(t)^{*}=U(t)^{-1}=U(-t)$; every orbit has constant norm, $\\|\\psi(t)\\|=\\|\\psi(0)\\|$, so for $\\psi(0)\\ne0$ the ray $[\\psi(t)]$ is a pure preparation of the model for every $t$ ([[def-nrqm-state-geometry-pure-mixed-states-and-purity]]).\n\n(b) **Domain invariance.** $U(t)D(H_{\\mathrm{op}})=D(H_{\\mathrm{op}})$ for every $t$ and $H_{\\mathrm{op}}U(t)=U(t)H_{\\mathrm{op}}$ on $D(H_{\\mathrm{op}})$: the flow preserves the energy domain and commutes with the energy there.\n\n(c) **Schroedinger equation on the domain.** For $\\psi(0)\\in D(H_{\\mathrm{op}})$ the curve $t\\mapsto\\psi(t)$ is norm-differentiable at every $t\\in\\mathbb R$, it stays in $D(H_{\\mathrm{op}})$, and\n$$i\\hbar\\,\\frac{d}{dt}\\psi(t)=H_{\\mathrm{op}}\\psi(t)=H_{\\mathrm{op}}U(t)\\psi(0);$$\nfor $\\psi(0)\\in H\\setminus D(H_{\\mathrm{op}})$ the curve is norm-differentiable at no $t\\in\\mathbb R$, so the equation is not asserted there, although the evolution $t\\mapsto\\psi(t)$ remains continuous.\n\n(d) **Density-operator evolution.** For every preparation $\\rho$ ([[def-nrqm-state-geometry-framework-state-space]]) and every $t$ the operator $\\rho(t)=U(t)\\rho(0)U(t)^{*}$ is again a preparation: self-adjoint, positive, trace class with $\\operatorname{tr}\\rho(t)=1$ ([[def-trace-class-operator]], [[def-self-adjoint-positive-unitary-and-normal-operator]]). Moreover for every bounded operator $B$ the identity $\\operatorname{tr}\\bigl(\\rho(t)B\\bigr)=\\operatorname{tr}\\bigl(\\rho(0)U(t)^{*}BU(t)\\bigr)$ holds.\n\n(e) **Status.** Clauses (a)-(d) are conditional consequences of P1 and P4 and the cited mathematics. They assert no evolution for a prescribed time-dependent Hamiltonian, no non-unitary reduced dynamics, no measurement, apparatus or detector model, no claim that any laboratory system is isolated, and no empirical result.",
          "strategy": "direct",
