          "physical_scope": "A conditional consequence of the autonomous-dynamics postulate P4 and the observable and probability postulate P2 in the reading of this page for a declared isolated system: the Heisenberg representative of a bounded assigned sharp observable is again a bounded assigned sharp observable with the same unit, norm and spectrum, the two pictures assign the same outcome laws to every preparation, the domain-qualified Heisenberg equation holds, and energy-compatible bounded observables are frozen in the Heisenberg picture. No measurement, apparatus, detector, driven-dynamics or open-system claim is made, and no empirical result is asserted."
        },
        {
          "id": "pthm-nrqm-autonomous-dynamics-stationary-states-and-energy-conservation",
          "kind": "physics-theorem",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "Energy conservation, conserved sharp observables and the stationary eigenrays",
          "statement": "Adopt the state and composition postulate [[post-nrqm-framework-state-and-composition]] (P1), the observable and probability postulate in the reading of [[def-nrqm-observables-framework-observable-and-outcome-law]] (P2), and the autonomous-dynamics postulate [[post-nrqm-framework-autonomous-dynamics]] (P4), and assume the Axiom of Countable Choice and the Axiom of Choice ([[def-countable-choice]], [[def-axiom-of-choice]]). Let $(H_{\\mathrm{op}},u_H)$ be the assigned energy observable of a declared isolated system with state space $H$ ([[def-nrqm-state-geometry-framework-state-space]]), spectral projection-valued measure $E_H$ and flow $U(t)=\\exp(-itH_{\\mathrm{op}}/\\hbar)$ ([[def-nrqm-autonomous-dynamics-framework-evolution]]), and write $\\rho(t)=U(t)\\rho(0)U(t)^{*}$. Then:\n\n(a) **Energy law and moments.** For every preparation $\\rho$, every Borel set $B\\subseteq\\mathbb R$ and every $t$,\n$$\\mu^{H_{\\mathrm{op}}}_{\\rho(t)}(B)=\\operatorname{tr}\\bigl(\\rho(t)E_H(B)\\bigr)=\\operatorname{tr}\\bigl(\\rho(0)E_H(B)\\bigr)=\\mu^{H_{\\mathrm{op}}}_{\\rho(0)}(B);$$\nfor the pure preparation of a unit vector $\\psi$ likewise $\\|E_H(B)U(t)\\psi\\|^{2}=\\|E_H(B)\\psi\\|^{2}$. If $\\psi(0)\\ne0$ and $\\psi(0)\\in D(H_{\\mathrm{op}})$, the mean and second moment of the energy law of the pure preparation $[\\psi(0)]$ are finite and time-independent. For any nonzero representative $\\psi(0)$ their time-zero values are\n$$\\frac{\\langle H_{\\mathrm{op}}\\psi(0),\\psi(0)\\rangle}{\\|\\psi(0)\\|^{2}}\\qquad\\text{and}\\qquad\\frac{\\|H_{\\mathrm{op}}\\psi(0)\\|^{2}}{\\|\\psi(0)\\|^{2}},$$\nrespectively. The displayed conservation of moments makes no assertion that these moments are finite for preparations outside this domain hypothesis.\n\n(b) **Conserved sharp observables.** Let $(A,u_A)$ be a bounded assigned sharp observable that is compatible with the energy ([[def-nrqm-autonomous-dynamics-framework-evolution]] clause (f)). Then its outcome law is time-independent: for every preparation $\\rho$, every Borel set $B$ and every $t$,\n$$\\mu^{A}_{\\rho(t)}(B)=\\mu^{A}_{\\rho(0)}(B).$$\n\n(c) **Stationary states are exactly the eigenrays.** Let $\\psi\\in H$, $\\psi\\ne0$. The pure preparation $[\\psi]$ is stationary, that is $[\\psi(t)]=[\\psi(0)]$ for every $t$, if and only if $\\psi$ is an eigenvector of $H_{\\mathrm{op}}$: $\\psi\\in D(H_{\\mathrm{op}})$ and $H_{\\mathrm{op}}\\psi=\\lambda\\psi$ for some $\\lambda\\in\\mathbb R$. In that case $\\psi(t)=e^{-it\\lambda/\\hbar}\\psi(0)$ for every $t$, and every assigned sharp observable has a time-independent outcome law in this preparation: $\\mu^{A}_{[\\psi(t)]}(B)=\\mu^{A}_{[\\psi(0)]}(B)$ for every $(A,u_A)$, every Borel $B$ and every $t$.\n\n(d) **Status and exclusions.** No equilibration, relaxation, decay or convergence of the law of an arbitrary preparation is asserted; no moment beyond those finite at time zero is claimed; the converse of (b) — constancy of the law of a bounded observable in every preparation implying strong spectral compatibility with the energy — is not asserted for a general (possibly unbounded) $H_{\\mathrm{op}}$; and the item is conditional on the isolated-system idealization of P4, asserting no apparatus realization and no empirical result.",
          "strategy": "direct",
