          },
          "physical_scope": "A conditional consequence of the autonomous-dynamics postulate P4 and the observable and probability postulate P2 in the reading of this page for a declared isolated system: the outcome law of the assigned energy observable is time-independent in every preparation; for a pure preparation represented by a nonzero vector in the energy domain, its finite first and second energy moments, evaluated on a unit representative, are conserved; every bounded assigned sharp observable compatible with the energy has a time-independent outcome law; and a pure preparation is stationary exactly when it is an eigenray of the energy, in which case all its outcome laws are time-independent. No relaxation, equilibration or decay is asserted; no converse of the compatibility criterion is claimed for unbounded energy operators; no measurement, apparatus or empirical claim is made."
        },
        {
          "id": "rem-nrqm-autonomous-dynamics-scope-and-empirical-status",
          "kind": "remark",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "What the autonomous-dynamics page adopts, proves and does not claim",
          "statement": "**What the page adopts.** The single physical assumption materialized here is the autonomous-dynamics postulate [[post-nrqm-framework-autonomous-dynamics]] (P4), read in the vocabulary of [[def-nrqm-autonomous-dynamics-framework-evolution]] for an isolated system of the framework with state space of the type fixed by [[def-nrqm-state-geometry-framework-state-space]]. In particular the assigned energy observable $(H_{\\mathrm{op}},u_H)$, its energy unit and the reduced Planck constant entering the phase are model specifications in the sense of [[def-nrqm-framework-quantities-and-units]]; no numerical value of any of them is produced by this page.\n\n**What is proved.** [[pthm-nrqm-autonomous-dynamics-schrodinger-picture-flow]] draws, from P4 and the local mathematics [[lem-nrqm-autonomous-dynamics-flow-calculus]], the unitary flow, the invariance of the energy domain, the domain-qualified Schroedinger equation and the evolution of density-operator preparations. [[pthm-nrqm-autonomous-dynamics-heisenberg-picture]], using [[lem-nrqm-autonomous-dynamics-heisenberg-flow]], identifies the Heisenberg representative of a bounded assigned sharp observable and proves that the two pictures assign the same outcome laws, together with the domain-qualified Heisenberg equation and the freezing of energy-compatible bounded observables. [[pthm-nrqm-autonomous-dynamics-stationary-states-and-energy-conservation]] reads the conservation of the energy law and its finite moments, the conservation of any bounded energy-compatible observable, and the equivalence of stationary pure preparations with the eigenrays of the energy; the mathematical core of that equivalence is [[lem-nrqm-autonomous-dynamics-stationary-ray-characterization]]. All statements are conditional consequences of the adopted postulates and the cited mathematics; none of them is an empirical claim.\n\n**What is not claimed.** (i) The page treats only the autonomous case: a prescribed time-dependent family $t\\mapsto H(t)$ and the propagator problems it raises are not covered by P4(ii) and are deferred to the driven-dynamics development, and an open or reduced non-unitary evolution is an extension requiring an environment model, in the sense of clauses (iv) and (v) of P4. (ii) No measurement, collapse, conditioning or apparatus model is introduced; the outcome law of [[def-nrqm-observables-framework-observable-and-outcome-law]] is used only to read statistics of a preparation, and the state after an outcome is not treated. (iii) No relaxation, equilibration or convergence of the law of a general preparation is asserted. (iv) The converse of the conservation criterion — that a bounded observable whose law is constant in every preparation must be strongly spectrally compatible with the energy — is not proved for a general possibly unbounded $H_{\\mathrm{op}}$ and is therefore not claimed. (v) The equation of motion is asserted exactly on the operator domain; for vectors outside the domain only the unitary flow, not the differential equation, is available.\n\n**Empirical status.** Whether a concrete laboratory system realizes P4's isolated-system idealization, and whether a concrete apparatus realizes a preparation of the type used here, are tested identifications with uncertainty, in the sense of the framework's preparation and apparatus assumptions; they are not consequences of P4. This pair records no measurement, apparatus, calibration or data, and the worked companion page contains finite model computations only.",
          "strategy": "n/a",
          "deps": [
            "def-axiom-of-choice",
            "def-countable-choice",
