          "dependency_level": 12,
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "B. Zwiebach, MIT 8.05 Quantum Physics II (Fall 2013), Chapter 7 'Two State Systems', Sections 2-3, chapter pages 2-6 (two-state precession: superpositions of energy eigenstates with distinct energies have time-dependent expectation values, while eigenstates do not)",
                "url": "https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/8-05-quantum-physics-ii-fall-2013/7c376a3b5b27e5ea586a7e37b85a05d3_MIT8_05F13_Chap_07.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "J. Binney and D. Skinner, The Physics of Quantum Mechanics, Sections 2.2 and 2.2.1, printed pages 21-24 (only states of well-defined energy have time-independent expectation values of all time-independent operators; superpositions generally do not)",
                "url": "https://www-thphys.physics.ox.ac.uk/people/JamesBinney/qb.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "physical_scope": "A refutation, inside the framework's autonomous-dynamics reading, of the informal claim that every superposition of two or more distinct energy eigenrays of an isolated system is a stationary state with time-independent outcome laws: in the explicit two-level model with two distinct energies, an equal-weight superposition carries the bounded flip observable with an outcome probability oscillating between one and zero. The item refutes that specific universal claim; it asserts no apparatus, no measurement statistics from a laboratory and no empirical result, and it does not deny that individual eigenrays are stationary or that special superpositions can be stationary."
        },
        {
          "id": "rem-nrqm-autonomous-dynamics-examples-scope-limits",
          "kind": "remark",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "What the worked items of the companion page establish",
          "statement": "**Two-level precession.** [[ex-nrqm-autonomous-dynamics-two-level-precession]] computes, on the explicit two-dimensional state space, the spectral measure and flow of the assigned energy observable $E_{1}T_{u_{1},u_{1}}+E_{2}T_{u_{2},u_{2}}$ with $E_{1}\\ne E_{2}$, the exact phases of an evolved preparation, the outcome probabilities and expectations of three bounded observables, and the rotation of the expectation-value triple about the third axis with angular frequency $\\omega=(E_{2}-E_{1})/\\hbar$. The computation verifies the flow and law of [[def-nrqm-autonomous-dynamics-framework-evolution]] and [[def-nrqm-observables-framework-observable-and-outcome-law]] on finite data, and it confirms the energy conservation of [[pthm-nrqm-autonomous-dynamics-stationary-states-and-energy-conservation]] clause (a) in the model. No apparatus realization, detector resolution or measured frequency is asserted.\n\n**Finite superpositions.** [[ex-nrqm-autonomous-dynamics-finite-stationary-superposition]] computes the evolution of a nonzero finite superposition of orthogonal energy eigenrays, the trigonometric-polynomial form of the outcome laws of a bounded assigned sharp observable, the exact return-time criterion $(\\lambda_{m}-\\lambda_{n})T/\\hbar\\in2\\pi\\mathbb Z$ for $m,n$ in the support of the coefficients, the existence criterion for a positive return time via a common frequency, and the two-energy specialization with least return time $2\\pi\\hbar/|\\lambda_{1}-\\lambda_{2}|$. These are exact model statements under the flow of [[pthm-nrqm-autonomous-dynamics-schrodinger-picture-flow]].\n\n**A failed universal claim.** [[cex-nrqm-autonomous-dynamics-superposition-with-distinct-energies-is-not-stationary]] refutes the informal universal statement that every superposition of distinct energy eigenrays is stationary: on the two-level model with $\\psi_{0}=(u_{1}+u_{2})/\\sqrt2$ the outcome law of the flip observable takes the values $1$ at $t=0$ and $0$ at $t=\\pi/|\\omega|$. The refutation isolates the relative phase as the mechanism and is consistent with the exact stationarity criterion of [[pthm-nrqm-autonomous-dynamics-stationary-states-and-energy-conservation]] clause (c): the individual eigenrays are stationary, the equal-weight superposition of distinct eigenrays is not.\n\n## What the page does not establish\n\nNone of the three items is an experiment: no counts, calibration, resolution, efficiency, background, uncertainty or data comparison appears anywhere on the page, and no energy value is measured. The two-level system is an abstract model and is not identified with a spin, a magnetic moment, a photon polarization or any other species; the coupling of spin to a magnetic field belongs to the corresponding model pages, and driven or resonant dynamics is deferred to the driven-dynamics development, which adopts its own time-dependent assumptions. The return-time and precession results are statements about the model's flow and outcome law, not about the stability, decoherence or control of any laboratory preparation.",
          "strategy": "n/a",
          "deps": [
            "cex-nrqm-autonomous-dynamics-superposition-with-distinct-energies-is-not-stationary",
            "def-nrqm-autonomous-dynamics-framework-evolution",
