          "physical_scope": "The detection laws of the declared two-path preparation model of the massive spin-s model of the framework: the normalized coherent bin law with its amplitude cross term, the which-path (incoherent) bin law, and the criterion under which the two declared laws coincide on every bin, with the phase-zero criterion conditional on the coherent preparation being admissible at phase zero. The statement is a conditional consequence of P1, P2, P5 and P6, the declared apparatus and preparation assignment in the sense of P7, and the cited published mathematics plus the local calculations in its proof. It asserts no which-path ontology, no entanglement or marker interaction, no detector response, no dynamics and no empirical result; the coherent and the which-path law are properties of two declared preparation models, and the identification of a concrete arrangement with either model is a tested identification with uncertainty.",
          "relations": {
