                "url": "https://www-thphys.physics.ox.ac.uk/people/JamesBinney/qb.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "physical_scope": "The spin-one-half internal factor of the massive particle model: the exact identity for the sum of the three component spreads in every unit state, the resulting lower bound hbar^2/2 and the impossibility of a state with all three component spreads small, the failure of spectral compatibility for every pair of spin components with the explicit projection witness, and the saturation of the Robertson bound in the S_z eigenstates. The statement is a conditional consequence of P1, P2, P5 and P6, under the Axiom of Choice and Countable Choice required by the cited spectral and moment suppliers, and the cited finite-dimensional mathematics; it asserts no measurement, apparatus, dynamics, empirical value or claim about angular momentum in space."
        },
        {
          "id": "cex-nrqm-uncertainty-commutator-zero-on-a-core-is-not-spectral-compatibility",
          "kind": "counterexample",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "A commutator vanishing on a dense invariant domain does not imply strong spectral commutation",
          "statement": "Let $H\\ne\\{0\\}$ be a complex Hilbert space, let $A,B$ be self-adjoint\noperators on $H$, and let $D\\subseteq D(A)\\cap D(B)$ be a dense linear\nsubspace with $AD\\subseteq D(B)$ and $BD\\subseteq D(A)$. If $ABu=BAu$ for\nevery $u\\in D$, then the spectral projection-valued measures of $A$ and $B$\nstrongly commute in the sense of\n[[def-nrqm-uncertainty-strong-spectral-commutation]] clause (b).",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "deps": [
            "def-axiom-of-choice",
            "def-complex-exponential",
            "def-countable-choice",
            "def-hilbert-space",
            "def-hilbert-orthogonal-projection",
            "def-nrqm-intervals-hilbert-sobolev-spaces",
