          "physical_scope": "A finite check in the declared line model of the pair: the rectangular barrier with height twice the incident energy and a width scaling chosen so that the barrier exponent is the natural logarithm of ten. The example computes the exact transmission and reflection coefficients as rational numbers, brackets them by rationals, compares the exact value with the thick-barrier approximation and verifies the theorem's error bound. It is a computation in the model, not a measurement; it reports no count, no apparatus and no empirical value, and it makes no claim about nature."
