      "items": [
        {
          "id": "lem-nrqm-oscillator-diagonal-eigenspaces",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Eigenspaces of the diagonal operator",
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $H$ be a complex Hilbert space ([[def-hilbert-space]]), let $(e_n)_{n\\in\\mathbb N}$ be a complete orthonormal family of $H$ ([[def-orthonormal-family-complete-orthonormal-system-and-hilbert-basis]]), let $(\\lambda_n)_{n\\in\\mathbb N}\\subseteq\\mathbb R$, and let $A$ be the self-adjoint diagonal operator of [[lem-nrqm-oscillator-diagonal-adjoint-and-graph-core-lemma]]:\n$$D(A)=\\Bigl\\{x\\in H:\\sum_n\\lambda_n^2|\\langle x,e_n\\rangle|^2<\\infty\\Bigr\\},\\qquad Ax=\\sum_n\\lambda_n\\langle x,e_n\\rangle e_n .$$\nThen:\n\n(a) for every $\\lambda\\in\\mathbb R$ the eigenspace of $A$ at $\\lambda$ is the closed linear span of the basis vectors carrying the eigenvalue $\\lambda$:\n$$\\ker(A-\\lambda I)=\\overline{\\operatorname{span}}\\{e_n:\\lambda_n=\\lambda\\};$$\nin particular $\\lambda$ is an eigenvalue of $A$ exactly when $\\lambda=\\lambda_n$ for some $n$;\n\n(b) if $\\lambda_m\\ne\\lambda_n$ whenever $m\\ne n$, then $\\ker(A-\\lambda_nI)=\\mathbb Ce_n$ for every $n$: every eigenspace is one-dimensional with eigenvector $e_n$, the eigenspaces are pairwise orthogonal, and every nonzero eigenvector of $A$ is a nonzero multiple of some $e_n$;\n\n(c) in the situation of (b) the linear span of all eigenspaces of $A$ is $\\operatorname{span}\\{e_n:n\\in\\mathbb N\\}$, which is dense in $H$.",
          "deps": [
            "lem-nrqm-oscillator-diagonal-adjoint-and-graph-core-lemma",
            "def-orthonormal-family-complete-orthonormal-system-and-hilbert-basis",
            "thm-parseval-equivalences-for-a-complete-orthonormal-family",
            "def-hilbert-space",
            "def-countable-choice"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
