        {
          "id": "lem-nrqm-oscillator-unitary-transport-of-spectral-pvms",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Transport of spectral projection-valued measures along isometric bijections",
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice and the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-axiom-of-choice]], [[def-countable-choice]]). Let $H,K$ be complex Hilbert spaces ([[def-hilbert-space]], [[def-inner-product-space]]) and let $U:H\\to K$ be a bijective linear map with\n$$\\langle Ux,Uy\\rangle_K=\\langle x,y\\rangle_H\\qquad\\text{for all }x,y\\in H .$$\nLet $T$ be a self-adjoint operator on $H$ with spectral projection-valued measure $E_T$ on the Borel $\\sigma$-algebra of $\\mathbb R$ ([[thm-spectral-theorem-for-unbounded-self-adjoint-operators]], [[def-projection-valued-measure]], [[def-symmetric-self-adjoint-and-essentially-self-adjoint]]), and define\n$$D(T'):=U D(T),\\qquad T'(Ux):=U(Tx)\\quad(x\\in D(T)).$$\nThen:\n\n(a) $T'$ is well defined, linear, densely defined and self-adjoint on $K$;\n\n(b) the assignment $E(B):=U E_T(B) U^{-1}$ on Borel sets $B\\subseteq\\mathbb R$ is a regular projection-valued measure on the Borel $\\sigma$-algebra of $\\mathbb R$, and it is the spectral projection-valued measure of $T'$;\n\n(c) for every unit vector $x\\in H$ the scalar laws of the two operators agree,\n$$\\mu^{T'}_{Ux}(B):=\\|E(B)Ux\\|_K^2=\\|E_T(B)x\\|_H^2=:\\mu^{T}_x(B)\\qquad(B\\subseteq\\mathbb R\\ \\text{Borel});$$\n\n(d) $\\sigma(T')=\\sigma(T)$.\n\n",
          "deps": [
            "def-resolvent-and-spectrum-of-a-closed-unbounded-operator",
            "def-axiom-of-choice",
            "def-countable-choice",
            "def-hilbert-space",
            "def-inner-product-space",
            "def-symmetric-self-adjoint-and-essentially-self-adjoint",
            "def-adjoint-of-a-densely-defined-unbounded-operator",
            "def-projection-valued-measure",
            "lem-scalar-and-complex-measures-from-a-pvm",
            "thm-spectral-theorem-for-unbounded-self-adjoint-operators",
            "def-unbounded-integral-against-a-pvm",
            "lem-nrqm-observables-spectral-support-and-outcome-law",
            "thm-cauchy-schwarz-for-real-and-complex-inner-product-spaces"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-resolvent-and-spectrum-of-a-closed-unbounded-operator": "mathematical-premise",
