        {
          "id": "def-nrqm-oscillator-framework-quadratic-potential-model",
          "kind": "definition",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "The quadratic-potential oscillator model of the framework",
          "statement": "**(a) Adopted framework assumptions.** Adopt the state and composition postulate P1, the observable and probability postulate P2, the autonomous-dynamics postulate P4 and the kinematics and massive-particle model postulate P5, in the readings of [[def-nrqm-state-geometry-framework-state-space]], [[def-nrqm-observables-framework-observable-and-outcome-law]], [[def-nrqm-autonomous-dynamics-framework-evolution]] and [[def-nrqm-kinematics-framework-massive-spin-s-model]] ([[post-nrqm-framework-state-and-composition]], [[post-nrqm-framework-observable-and-probability]], [[post-nrqm-framework-autonomous-dynamics]], [[post-nrqm-framework-nonrelativistic-kinematics-and-massive-particle]]). Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice and the Axiom of Choice ([[def-countable-choice]], [[def-axiom-of-choice]]). Fix real model parameters $m>0$ (mass parameter, unit $\\mathrm{kg}$), $\\omega>0$ (angular frequency, unit $\\mathrm s^{-1}$) and the action constant $\\hbar>0$ (unit $\\mathrm J\\,\\mathrm s$) of [[def-nrqm-framework-quantities-and-units]] clause (d)4, and put\n$$\\ell:=\\sqrt{\\frac{\\hbar}{m\\omega}}>0\\qquad\\text{(unit }\\mathrm m\\text{),}$$\nthe model's length scale.\n\n**(b) One-dimensional realization.** Write $\\mathcal H_1:=L^{2}(\\mathbb R,dx;\\mathbb C)$ for the model's one-dimensional state space, the complex Hilbert space of almost-everywhere classes with inner product linear in the first argument, taken in the scalar reading $r=1$ of the component-valued space of [[lem-nrqm-kinematics-componentwise-position-and-momentum]] for $d=1$. The model's **position** and **momentum** are the operators of that lemma at $d=1$, $r=1$, namely\n$$Q:=M_x,\\qquad D(Q)=\\{f\\in\\mathcal H_1:xf\\in L^{2}\\},\\qquad (Qf)(x)=xf(x),$$\n$$P:=-i\\hbar D_x,\\qquad D(P)=\\{f\\in\\mathcal H_1:\\text{the weak derivative }D_xf\\text{ lies in }L^{2}\\},\\qquad Pf=-i\\hbar D_xf,$$\nwhich are densely defined and self-adjoint with exactly these domains; the model assigns to $(Q,\\mathrm m)$ and to $(P,\\mathrm{kg}\\,\\mathrm m\\,\\mathrm s^{-1})$ the status of assigned sharp observables in the sense of [[def-nrqm-observables-framework-observable-and-outcome-law]] clause (a), with outcome laws read from P2.\n\n**(c) Energy and excitation-number observables.** Let $g_0,(g_n)_{n\\in\\mathbb N}$ and the unitary $D:L^{2}(\\mathbb R,dy)\\to L^{2}(\\mathbb R,dx)$ be the Hermite data and scaling map of [[thm-nrqm-oscillator-oscillator-scaling-and-exact-realization]] clauses (a), (b) for the parameters $m,\\omega,\\hbar$. Put $\\mathscr P_y:=\\{p g_0:p\\in\\mathbb C[y]\\}\\subseteq L^{2}(\\mathbb R,dy)$; the Hermite recurrence [[thm-nrqm-oscillator-hermite-recurrence]] identifies this polynomial-Gaussian space with $\\operatorname{span}\\{g_n:n\\in\\mathbb N\\}$, and its scaled image $\\mathscr P_x:=D(\\mathscr P_y)=\\operatorname{span}\\{\\psi_n:n\\in\\mathbb N\\}$ is the core supplied by the scaling theorem. Let $A$ be the diagonal operator of [[lem-nrqm-oscillator-diagonal-adjoint-and-graph-core-lemma]] for the family $(g_n)$ and eigenvalues $2n+1$. The model's **energy operator** is\n$$H_1:=\\frac{\\hbar\\omega}{2}\\,D A D^{-1},\\qquad D(H_1):=\\{f\\in\\mathcal H_1:D^{-1}f\\in D(A)\\},$$\nthe operator of [[thm-nrqm-oscillator-oscillator-scaling-and-exact-realization]] clause (b); its exact domain, action, spectrum and eigenbasis are those established there. The model assigns to $(H_1,\\mathrm J)$ the status of assigned energy observable of the isolated system in the sense of [[def-nrqm-autonomous-dynamics-framework-evolution]] clauses (a) and (b): the model's flow is $U(t)=\\exp(-itH_1/\\hbar)$ and the model's Schroedinger dynamics is the one of that definition. Let $N$ be the self-adjoint number operator on $L^{2}(\\mathbb R,dy)$ of [[lem-nrqm-oscillator-closed-ladder-domains]] for the Hermite family $(g_n)$, and set $N_\\psi:=DND^{-1}$. Its transported domain and action are\n$$D(N_\\psi)=\\Bigl\\{f\\in\\mathcal H_1:\\sum_n n^2|\\langle f,\\psi_n\\rangle|^2<\\infty\\Bigr\\},\\qquad N_\\psi f=\\sum_n n\\langle f,\\psi_n\\rangle\\psi_n,$$\nwith the series converging in $\\mathcal H_1$; it is self-adjoint by [[lem-nrqm-oscillator-unitary-transport-of-spectral-pvms]] clauses (a), (d). The model assigns to $(N_\\psi,1)$ the status of its dimensionless excitation-number observable; here $1$ is the dimensionless unit, and the spectral coordinate $n$ records the number of excitations, and its outcome laws are read by P2. On the scaled polynomial-Gaussian core $\\mathscr P_x$ the operator $H_1$ is the self-adjoint realization of the quadratic expression: for every $f\\in\\mathscr P_x$,\n$$H_1f=-\\frac{\\hbar^{2}}{2m}f''+\\frac{m\\omega^{2}}{2}x^{2}f$$\npointwise, and for every $f\\in D(H_1)$ the weak identity $\\int (H_1f)\\varphi\\,dx=\\int f\\bigl(-\\frac{\\hbar^{2}}{2m}\\varphi''+\\frac{m\\omega^{2}}{2}x^{2}\\varphi\\bigr)dx$ holds for every $\\varphi\\in C_c^{\\infty}(\\mathbb R)$ ([[thm-nrqm-oscillator-oscillator-scaling-and-exact-realization]] clauses (c), (d)). The formal differential expression $-\\frac{\\hbar^{2}}{2m}\\frac{d^{2}}{dx^{2}}+\\frac{m\\omega^{2}}{2}x^{2}$ is the model's **quadratic potential energy plus kinetic energy** reading; no identification of $D(H_1)$ with any independently defined maximal differential-operator domain, and no separate quadratic-form-domain characterization, is asserted.\n\n**(d) Three-dimensional isotropic realization.** For the spinless reading $s=0$ of the massive-particle model of [[def-nrqm-kinematics-framework-massive-spin-s-model]], with state space $\\mathcal H_3:=L^{2}(\\mathbb R^{3},dx;\\mathbb C)$, position operators $Q_j$ and momentum operators $P_k$ ($j,k\\in\\{1,2,3\\}$) with the domains and units of that definition, the model with common frequency $\\omega$ has **energy operator** $H_3$ equal to the diagonal operator $H$ of [[thm-nrqm-oscillator-multidimensional-oscillator-completeness]] clause (c) for $d=3$, $m_j=m$, $\\omega_j=\\omega$, a self-adjoint operator on $\\mathcal H_3$ with the domain, spectrum and core displayed there. The model assigns to $(H_3,\\mathrm J)$ the status of assigned energy observable in the reading of clause (c); its eigenbasis and the identity $H_3=\\sum_{j=1}^{3}\\bigl(-\\frac{\\hbar^{2}}{2m}\\partial_{x_j}^{2}+\\frac{m\\omega^{2}}{2}x_j^{2}\\bigr)$ on the core are those of that theorem, and the one-dimensional realization of clauses (b) and (c) is the coordinate specialization of this one.\n\n**(e) Physical reading and scope.** Clause (c) defines the model quantities that the page calls the energy and excitation number; it is a **model assumption** that the energy of the declared isolated particle is the assigned observable $(H_1,\\mathrm J)$ and that $(N_\\psi,1)$ is its excitation-number observable. The additive constant of the potential energy is removed at the minimum: for a one-dimensional potential-energy function $V:\\mathbb R\\to\\mathbb R$ of class $C^2$, with values in joules for position $x$ in metres, suppose $V$ has a non-degenerate local minimum at $0$, meaning $V'(0)=0$ and $V''(0)>0$. Taylor's theorem gives $V(x)-V(0)=\\frac{1}{2}V''(0)x^{2}+o(x^{2})$ as $x\\to0$; the oscillator model approximates this shifted potential-energy function by its quadratic term and sets $m\\omega^{2}=V''(0)$. The oscillator's quantum ground energy in this convention is $\\hbar\\omega/2$. With only the stated $C^2$ regularity, the remainder is $o(x^2)$; no quantitative finite-amplitude error bound is asserted on this page (Binney §3.1, cited in the references). No measured value, no laboratory identification and no derivation of $m$ or $\\omega$ from any microscopic or environmental theory is asserted. The model contains no damping, no external driving, no time-dependent parameters, no coupling to electromagnetic fields or radiation, no spin-dependent force, no anharmonic term, no relativistic correction and no boundary or many-body effect; those are separate model assumptions belonging to their own items. The parameters $m$ and $\\omega$ are model parameters of dimensions $\\mu$ and $\\tau^{-1}$ in the conventions of [[def-nrqm-framework-quantities-and-units]], and all displayed quantities are read in the units fixed there.\n\n**(f) Status.** Clauses (a)-(e) fix the objects used by the theorems of this page and record the readings of P1, P2, P4 and P5 in the model's terminology. They assert no preparation or apparatus model, no detection model, no joint outcome law of position and momentum and no empirical result.\n\n",
          "deps": [
            "post-nrqm-framework-state-and-composition",
            "post-nrqm-framework-observable-and-probability",
