          "strategy": "direct",
          "physical_scope": "The energy and excitation-number observables of the quadratic-potential oscillator model: for the one-dimensional realization with parameters m>0, omega>0 and hbar>0 the exact energy eigenvalue list hbar omega (n+1/2) under the convention that subtracts the potential-energy value V(0), with quantum ground energy hbar omega/2, one-dimensional eigenspaces spanned by the Hermite eigenbasis, completeness of that basis, the energy gap hbar omega, the assigned dimensionless excitation-number observable in unit 1 and the atomic outcome laws; and for the isotropic three-dimensional realization of the spinless massive particle the energy spectrum hbar omega (M+3/2) with multiplicity (M+1)(M+2)/2. The statement is a conditional consequence of the postulates P1, P2, P4 and P5, of the adopted oscillator model and of the cited mathematics; it asserts no measured spectral line, no value of m, omega or hbar and no empirical result."
        },
        {
          "id": "def-nrqm-oscillator-coherent-states",
          "kind": "definition",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "The coherent states of the oscillator model",
          "statement": "**(a) Setting.** Adopt the state and composition postulate P1 in the reading of [[def-nrqm-state-geometry-framework-state-space]] ([[post-nrqm-framework-state-and-composition]]) and the one-dimensional oscillator model of [[def-nrqm-oscillator-framework-quadratic-potential-model]] clauses (a), (b), (c), with parameters $m>0$, $\\omega>0$, action constant $\\hbar>0$ and length scale $\\ell=\\sqrt{\\hbar/(m\\omega)}$. Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $(g_n)_{n\\in\\mathbb N}$ be the Hermite family of $L^{2}(\\mathbb R,dy)$, let $D:L^{2}(\\mathbb R,dy)\\to L^{2}(\\mathbb R,dx)$ be the scaling unitary and $(\\psi_n)$ the scaled eigenbasis of [[thm-nrqm-oscillator-oscillator-scaling-and-exact-realization]] clauses (a), (b), with $\\psi_n=Dg_n$; let $a_\\psi=DaD^{-1}$ be the transported annihilation operator of [[lem-nrqm-oscillator-closed-ladder-domains]], and let $N_\\psi=DND^{-1}$ be the model's assigned excitation-number observable of [[def-nrqm-oscillator-framework-quadratic-potential-model]] clause (c), with its stated domain and unit $1$.\n\n**(b) The family.** For $z\\in\\mathbb C$ let $\\psi^{(y)}_z$ be the coherent vector of [[thm-nrqm-oscillator-coherent-state-convergence]] clause (a),\n$$\\psi^{(y)}_z:=e^{-|z|^{2}/2}\\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty}\\frac{z^{n}}{\\sqrt{n!}}\\,g_n\\in L^{2}(\\mathbb R,dy),$$\nthe series converging in $L^{2}(\\mathbb R,dy)$, and define the model's **coherent state** with label $z$ by\n$$\\Psi_z:=D\\psi^{(y)}_z=e^{-|z|^{2}/2}\\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty}\\frac{z^{n}}{\\sqrt{n!}}\\,\\psi_n\\in\\mathcal H_1 .$$\nThe family $(\\Psi_z)_{z\\in\\mathbb C}$ is the model's **coherent-state family**, and $z$ is its **amplitude-phase label**.\n\n**(c) Basic properties.** The following properties of the family are those established in the cited items and are recorded here as part of the definition's reading: the series for $\\Psi_z$ converges and $\\|\\Psi_z\\|=1$, so by P1 the ray $[\\Psi_z]$ is a pure preparation of the model when it is declared as one; $\\Psi_z\\in D(N_\\psi^{k})$ for every $k\\in\\mathbb N$; $a_\\psi\\Psi_z=z\\Psi_z$, so $\\Psi_z$ is a unit eigenvector of the annihilation operator with eigenvalue $z$; $\\langle\\Psi_z,\\Psi_w\\rangle=e^{-(|z|^{2}+|w|^{2})/2+z\\overline w}$, with modulus $e^{-|z-w|^{2}/2}$ for all $z,w$, so distinct labels define distinct preparations (their overlap modulus is less than $1$, whereas unit vectors on the same ray have overlap modulus $1$) and no two members of the family are orthogonal; and $\\Psi_0=\\psi_0$ is the ground eigenvector of the energy operator. ([[thm-nrqm-oscillator-coherent-state-convergence]] clauses (a), (b), (c), (d), (e), transported by the unitary $D$ of [[thm-nrqm-oscillator-oscillator-scaling-and-exact-realization]] clause (a).)\n\n**(d) Reading of the label.** The label $z$ is dimensionless (it is a complex number, not a quantity with a physical dimension). Its amplitude is $|z|$; when $z\\ne0$, its phase is the class $\\arg z\\in\\mathbb R/(2\\pi\\mathbb Z)$, while $z=0$ has zero amplitude and no phase label. The mathematical coherent-state series gives the quadratic-form value $\\langle N_\\psi\\Psi_z,\\Psi_z\\rangle=|z|^{2}$ for the assigned, dimensionless excitation-number observable $(N_\\psi,1)$; this is the number coordinate intended by the model's P2 reading. Under the model's flow, [[thm-nrqm-oscillator-coherent-evolution-and-variance]] clauses (c), (e), (f) gives $U(t)\\Psi_z=e^{-i\\omega t/2}\\Psi_{ze^{-i\\omega t}}$ and the position and momentum means $\\sqrt2\\ell\\operatorname{Re}(ze^{-i\\omega t})$ and $\\sqrt2\\hbar\\operatorname{Im}(ze^{-i\\omega t})/\\ell$, respectively; thus the mean pair, in coordinates scaled by $\\sqrt2\\ell$ and $\\sqrt2\\hbar/\\ell$, rotates with the phase label at angular frequency $\\omega$. Clause (d) records this interpretation of the label, not an outcome of measuring the label itself.\n\n**(e) Scope.** The definition declares a one-parameter family of preparations of the one-dimensional model and fixes its notation. It does not assert that the coherent states are the only preparations with time-independent position or momentum spreads, it does not assert minimality of any uncertainty product (that is a separate result for this family), it does not construct a displacement operator, an overcompleteness relation or a resolution of unity, and it makes no measurement, apparatus or empirical claim. The two presentations of the family -- as eigenvectors of the annihilation operator, as in clause (b), and as translated ground states -- are not identified here; only the former is defined.\n\n",
          "deps": [
