          "physical_scope": "The coherent states of the one-dimensional quadratic-potential oscillator model of the framework: for each complex dimensionless label z the unit vector Psi_z obtained by transporting the coherent vector of the Hermite oscillator basis along the model's scaling unitary, its properties as a preparation of the model (normalization, annihilation-operator eigenvalue z, non-orthogonality), and the amplitude and phase reading of z together with its operator-expectation excitation-number coordinate in the assigned unit 1. The definition asserts no measurement procedure, no uniqueness or minimality property among preparations, no overcompleteness or resolution of unity, no apparatus realization and no empirical result."
        },
        {
          "id": "pthm-nrqm-oscillator-coherent-state-fluctuations",
          "kind": "physics-theorem",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "Fluctuations of the oscillator coherent states and the position-momentum relation of the model",
          "statement": "Adopt the state and composition postulate P1, the observable and probability postulate P2 and the kinematics and massive-particle model postulate P5, read through the one-dimensional oscillator model of [[def-nrqm-oscillator-framework-quadratic-potential-model]] clauses (a), (b), (c), and the coherent-state family of [[def-nrqm-oscillator-coherent-states]]; assume the Axiom of Countable Choice and the Axiom of Choice ([[def-countable-choice]], [[def-axiom-of-choice]]). Let $Q$ and $P$ be the model's position and momentum observables with their declared units ($\\mathrm m$ and $\\mathrm{kg}\\,\\mathrm m\\,\\mathrm s^{-1}$), let $\\ell=\\sqrt{\\hbar/(m\\omega)}$, let $\\Delta_{\\rho}A$ be the preparation spread of an assigned sharp observable in the reading of [[def-nrqm-uncertainty-preparation-spread]], and write $\\langle A\\rangle_z:=\\langle A\\Psi_z,\\Psi_z\\rangle$ for the model's coherent preparation of label $z$. Then:\n\n(a) **Coherent spreads.** For every $z\\in\\mathbb C$ the vector $\\Psi_z$ lies in $D(Q)\\cap D(P)$, the preparation spreads of $Q$ and $P$ in the pure preparation of $\\Psi_z$ exist, and\n$$\\Delta_{\\Psi_z}Q=\\frac{\\ell}{\\sqrt2},\\qquad \\Delta_{\\Psi_z}P=\\frac{\\hbar}{\\ell\\sqrt2},\\qquad \\Delta_{\\Psi_z}Q\\,\\Delta_{\\Psi_z}P=\\frac{\\hbar}{2};$$\n\n(b) **Position-momentum relation of the model.** Every unit vector $f\\in D(Q)\\cap D(P)$ satisfies\n$$\\Delta_{f}Q\\,\\Delta_{f}P\\ge\\frac{\\hbar}{2},$$\nread in the product unit $\\mathrm{kg}\\,\\mathrm m^{2}\\mathrm s^{-1}$; consequently the value $\\hbar/2$ attained in (a) is the minimum over the common domain, and it is attained by every coherent preparation;\n\n(c) **Saturation.** For every $z\\in\\mathbb C$, with the centered vectors\n$$x_z:=(Q-\\langle Q\\rangle_zI)\\Psi_z,\\qquad y_z:=(P-\\langle P\\rangle_zI)\\Psi_z,$$\none has $\\langle x_z,y_z\\rangle=-i\\hbar/2$; in particular $\\operatorname{Re}\\langle x_z,y_z\\rangle=0$ and $x_z,y_z$ are linearly dependent, so $\\|x_z\\|\\,\\|y_z\\|=|\\langle x_z,y_z\\rangle|=\\hbar/2$;\n\n(d) **Status.** Clauses (a)-(c) are conditional consequences of P1, P2, P5, the adopted oscillator model, the cited preparation-moment and uncertainty results and the cited mathematics. They concern the spreads of the two separately assigned outcome laws of $Q$ and $P$ in one preparation; they introduce no joint outcome law of position and momentum, no measurement error, no disturbance of the preparation, no dynamics and no empirical value. Whether a laboratory preparation and apparatus realize the pair of observables and produce this spread is a tested identification under the preparation and apparatus postulate P7.",
