          "strategy": "direct",
          "physical_scope": "The ladder operators of the one-dimensional oscillator model applied to the first excited eigenstates: the explicit ladder norms up to the second excited level, the outcome laws of the assigned dimensionless excitation-number observable in unit 1 and of the energy observable in the eigenstate preparations, and the warning that the annihilation and creation operators are not assigned sharp observables of the model. The example is a conditional computation inside the adopted model and asserts no measured excitation number, apparatus realisation or empirical value."
        },
        {
          "id": "ex-nrqm-oscillator-coherent-trajectory",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "A coherent-state trajectory: period, phase-space ellipse and constant spreads",
          "statement": "Adopt the state and composition postulate P1, the observable and probability postulate P2, the autonomous-dynamics postulate P4 and the kinematics and massive-particle model postulate P5, read through the one-dimensional oscillator model of [[def-nrqm-oscillator-framework-quadratic-potential-model]] clauses (a), (b), (c), and the coherent-state family of [[def-nrqm-oscillator-coherent-states]]; assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Fix a label $z=z_1+iz_2$ with $|z|>0$, let $x_0:=\\sqrt2\\,\\ell z_1$, $p_0:=\\frac{\\sqrt2\\,\\hbar}{\\ell}z_2$, let $\\Psi_z(t):=U(t)\\Psi_z$ be the evolved coherent state, and write $x(t):=\\langle Q\\Psi_z(t),\\Psi_z(t)\\rangle$, $p(t):=\\langle P\\Psi_z(t),\\Psi_z(t)\\rangle$. Then:\n\n(a) the preparation is periodic with period $\\frac{2\\pi}{\\omega}$ in the sense that the prepared state is the same pure preparation at times $t$ and $t+\\frac{2\\pi}{\\omega}$:\n$$[U(2\\pi/\\omega)\\Psi_z]=[\\Psi_z],\\qquad [\\Psi_z(t+2\\pi/\\omega)]=[\\Psi_z(t)]\\quad(t\\in\\mathbb R);$$\n\n(b) the mean pair is\n$$x(t)=x_0\\cos\\omega t+\\frac{p_0}{m\\omega}\\sin\\omega t,\\qquad p(t)=p_0\\cos\\omega t-m\\omega x_0\\sin\\omega t,$$\nso that $x(0)=x_0$, $p(0)=p_0$, and at the quarter period $x\\bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{2\\omega}\\bigr)=\\frac{p_0}{m\\omega}$, $p\\bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{2\\omega}\\bigr)=-m\\omega x_0$; the phase-space ellipse\n$$\\frac{x(t)^{2}}{2\\ell^{2}}+\\frac{\\ell^{2}p(t)^{2}}{2\\hbar^{2}}=|z|^{2}$$\nis invariant along the motion;\n\n(c) the position and momentum spreads and their product are constant along the motion:\n$$\\Delta_{\\Psi_z(t)}Q=\\frac{\\ell}{\\sqrt2},\\qquad \\Delta_{\\Psi_z(t)}P=\\frac{\\hbar}{\\ell\\sqrt2},\\qquad \\Delta_{\\Psi_z(t)}Q\\,\\Delta_{\\Psi_z(t)}P=\\frac{\\hbar}{2}\\quad(t\\in\\mathbb R);$$\n\n(d) the displayed $x(t)$ and $p(t)$ are preparation means of the model's position and momentum observables in the evolving coherent preparation; they are not the coordinates of a measured particle trajectory, and no measurement record, apparatus or empirical value is asserted.",
          "deps": [
            "post-nrqm-framework-state-and-composition",
            "post-nrqm-framework-observable-and-probability",
