          "strategy": "direct",
          "physical_scope": "The trajectory of a coherent preparation of the one-dimensional oscillator model with nonzero label: the exact period 2 pi/omega of the preparation, the quarter-period phase-space values, the invariant ellipse of the preparation means, and the constancy of the position and momentum spreads and their product hbar/2. The example is a conditional computation inside the adopted model; the mean values are preparation means and are not the coordinates of a measured particle trajectory."
        },
        {
          "id": "rem-nrqm-oscillator-examples-scope-limits",
          "kind": "remark",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "What the worked oscillator examples establish",
          "statement": "## What the worked items establish\n\n**Ground state.** [[ex-nrqm-oscillator-ground-state-gaussian]] fixes the explicit Gaussian representative $\\psi_0(x)=\\ell^{-1/2}\\pi^{-1/4}e^{-x^{2}/(2\\ell^{2})}$ of the ground vector, its unit norm, the eigenvalue equation $H_1\\psi_0=\\frac{\\hbar\\omega}{2}\\psi_0$, the position law with density $\\ell^{-1}\\pi^{-1/2}e^{-x^{2}/\\ell^{2}}$ and variance $\\ell^{2}/2$, the momentum law with density $\\frac{\\ell}{\\hbar\\sqrt\\pi}e^{-\\ell^{2}p^{2}/\\hbar^{2}}$ and variance $\\hbar^{2}/(2\\ell^{2})$, and the saturation $\\Delta_{\\psi_0}Q\\,\\Delta_{\\psi_0}P=\\hbar/2$ of the model's position-momentum relation.\n\n**Ladder and excitation structure.** [[ex-nrqm-oscillator-ladder-norms]] computes the first ladder images and their norms, the ladder matrix elements $\\langle\\psi_m,a_\\psi\\psi_n\\rangle=\\sqrt n\\,\\delta_{m,n-1}$ and $\\langle\\psi_m,a^\\dagger_\\psi\\psi_n\\rangle=\\sqrt{n+1}\\,\\delta_{m,n+1}$, and the excitation and energy laws $\\mu^{N_\\psi}_{\\psi_n}(\\{n\\})=1$, $\\mu^{H_1}_{\\psi_n}(\\{E_n\\})=1$ of the eigenstate preparations, with the warning that $a_\\psi$ and $a^\\dagger_\\psi$ are not assigned sharp observables.\n\n**Coherent motion.** [[ex-nrqm-oscillator-coherent-trajectory]] shows that a nonzero-label coherent preparation is periodic with period $2\\pi/\\omega$, that its mean pair traces the invariant phase-space ellipse $\\frac{x^{2}}{2\\ell^{2}}+\\frac{\\ell^{2}p^{2}}{2\\hbar^{2}}=|z|^{2}$ with the quarter-period values $x(\\frac{\\pi}{2\\omega})=\\frac{p_0}{m\\omega}$, $p(\\frac{\\pi}{2\\omega})=-m\\omega x_0$, and that the position and momentum spreads and their product $\\hbar/2$ are constant along the motion.\n\n## What they do not establish\n\nEvery computation above is conditional on the adopted oscillator model of [[def-nrqm-oscillator-framework-quadratic-potential-model]] and on the postulates P1, P2, P4 and P5 read through it; none of them reports a measurement. In particular: no numerical value of $m$, $\\omega$ or $\\hbar$ is extracted; no laboratory state is identified with $\\psi_0$, with an eigenstate $\\psi_n$ or with a coherent state; the mean functions $x(t),p(t)$ are preparation means of the model's observables under the evolving preparation and are not the coordinates of a measured trajectory; and the periodicity of clause (a) of the coherent-trajectory example is a statement about the pure preparation (a ray), not about a measured signal. The harmonic approximation's range, anharmonic corrections, damping, driving, time-dependent parameters and coupling to electromagnetic fields or radiation are outside the examples, as is the displacement-operator presentation of the coherent family. The one-dimensional non-normalizable formal solution of the ground-state equation is authored on the mathematical companion `qm-math-oscillator-examples` and is linked there, not duplicated here.\n",
          "deps": [
            "def-nrqm-oscillator-framework-quadratic-potential-model",
            "def-nrqm-oscillator-coherent-states",
            "pthm-nrqm-oscillator-energy-spectrum-and-completeness",
            "pthm-nrqm-oscillator-coherent-state-fluctuations",
            "pthm-nrqm-oscillator-coherent-state-evolution",
            "ex-nrqm-oscillator-ground-state-gaussian",
            "ex-nrqm-oscillator-ladder-norms",
            "ex-nrqm-oscillator-coherent-trajectory",
            "def-nrqm-framework-quantities-and-units"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
