      "items": [
        {
          "id": "lem-nrqm-symmetries-unitary-conjugation-and-commutation-calculus",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Unitary conjugation, generator transport and strong commutation of self-adjoint observables",
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice, the Axiom of Countable Choice and the Axiom of\nDependent Choice ([[def-axiom-of-choice]], [[def-countable-choice]],\n[[def-dependent-choice]]), the choice hypotheses of the cited spectral and\nBochner suppliers. Fix $\\hbar>0$, let $H\\ne\\{0\\}$ be a complex Hilbert space\n([[def-hilbert-space]]), let $K$ and $A$ be self-adjoint operators on $H$ with\nspectral projection-valued measures $E_K$ and $E_A$\n([[def-symmetric-self-adjoint-and-essentially-self-adjoint]],\n[[thm-spectral-theorem-for-unbounded-self-adjoint-operators]],\n[[def-projection-valued-measure]]), let $W\\in\\mathcal B(H)$ be unitary\n([[def-bounded-linear-operator]],\n[[def-self-adjoint-positive-unitary-and-normal-operator]]), and put\n$$U_K(t):=e^{-itK/\\hbar},\\qquad U_A(s):=e^{-isA/\\hbar}\\qquad(s,t\\in\\mathbb R)$$\nin the spectral calculus of [[def-unbounded-integral-against-a-pvm]], which are\nstrongly continuous one-parameter unitary groups\n([[lem-self-adjoint-operator-generates-a-strongly-continuous-unitary-group]],\n[[def-strongly-continuous-one-parameter-unitary-group]]). Write\n$\\Phi_K(g)=\\int g\\,dE_K$ for bounded Borel $g:\\mathbb R\\to\\mathbb C$\n([[thm-bounded-borel-pvm-integral]]), and let\n$K_W:=WKW^{*}$ with $D(K_W):=WD(K)$. Then:\n\n(a) $K_W$ is self-adjoint with spectral projection-valued measure\n$$E_{K_W}(B)=WE_K(B)W^{*}\\qquad(B\\subseteq\\mathbb R\\ \\text{Borel}),$$\nits flow satisfies $e^{-itK_W/\\hbar}=WU_K(t)W^{*}$ for every $t$, and the\nconjugated family $s\\mapsto WU_A(s)W^{*}$ is a strongly continuous\none-parameter unitary group whose infinitesimal generator is\n$-\\frac{i}{\\hbar}WAW^{*}$ with domain $WD(A)$\n([[def-infinitesimal-generator-of-a-unitary-group]]);\n\n(b) the following are equivalent:\n\n  (i) $U_A(s)U_K(t)=U_K(t)U_A(s)$ for all $s,t\\in\\mathbb R$;\n\n  (ii) $E_A(B)E_K(C)=E_K(C)E_A(B)$ for all Borel sets $B,C\\subseteq\\mathbb R$;\n\n  (iii) $U_K(t)D(A)=D(A)$ and $U_K(t)AU_K(t)^{*}=A$ for every $t\\in\\mathbb R$;\n\n(c) if a bounded $B\\in\\mathcal B(H)$ satisfies $BU_K(t)=U_K(t)B$ for every\n$t\\in\\mathbb R$, then $B\\Phi_K(g)=\\Phi_K(g)B$ for every bounded Borel\n$g:\\mathbb R\\to\\mathbb C$; in particular $BE_K(C)=E_K(C)B$ for every Borel\n$C\\subseteq\\mathbb R$;\n\n(d) if (i)-(iii) of (b) hold, then $E_A(B)U_K(t)=U_K(t)E_A(B)$ for every Borel\n$B\\subseteq\\mathbb R$ and every $t\\in\\mathbb R$.",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "deps": [
            "def-axiom-of-choice",
            "def-bounded-linear-operator",
            "def-countable-choice",
