          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "not-applicable"
          },
          "dependency_level": 9,
          "physical_scope": "The symmetry and conservation vocabulary of the declared framework model: symmetries of the dynamics of a declared isolated system as unitaries preserving the energy domain and commuting with the energy operator, unitary symmetry groups and their strong continuity, one-parameter symmetry groups and their Stone generators, and the reading of a conserved sharp observable as one whose outcome law is time-independent in every preparation. The item fixes terminology and candidate actions of the model (translations, spatial rotations, parity, and explicitly defined gauge phase multipliers on the spinless scalar space); it asserts no symmetry of any concrete model potential or external coupling, no antiunitary or superselection structure, no apparatus realization and no empirical result.",
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "J. Binney and D. Skinner, The Physics of Quantum Mechanics, Sections 4.1-4.3, printed pages 58-70 (PDF pages 66-78): unitary transformation operators, generators of continuous transformations, symmetries and conservation laws",
                "url": "https://www-thphys.physics.ox.ac.uk/people/JamesBinney/qb.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "B. Zwiebach, MIT 8.05 Quantum Physics II (Fall 2013), Chapter 6 'Quantum Dynamics', Sections 3.1-3.2, printed pages 18-22 (PDF pages 18-22): Heisenberg operators, conserved operators commuting with the Hamiltonian and their constant time dependence",
                "url": "https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/8-05-quantum-physics-ii-fall-2013/79a8091ef4f18d8e3ff76a097e8db33c_MIT8_05F13_Chap_06.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics, 1st edition 2009, Section 4.2 printed pages 115-117 (PDF pages 127-129) and Theorem 8.1 printed page 174 (PDF page 186): commuting self-adjoint operators and the Noether-type conservation statement",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-schroe/schroe.pdf"
              }
            ]
