          "dependency_level": 12,
          "physical_scope": "A model computation for the massive spin-s model with an even real bounded measurable potential: the parity invariance of every energy eigenspace, the definite parity of nondegenerate eigenstates, and the vanishing of the position matrix element between two states of the same parity. The item is a conditional identity about the model's operators and assigned position observables; it computes no transition rate, models no measurement and records no empirical result.",
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "J. Binney and D. Skinner, The Physics of Quantum Mechanics, Sections 4.1.4 and 4.2, printed pages 62-67 (PDF pages 70-75): the parity operator and its eigenvalues, the commutation of parity with the Hamiltonian for an even potential (equation (4.43)) and the vanishing of matrix elements of a vector operator between states of equal definite parity (equation (4.42), printed page 67); PDF page = printed page + 8",
                "url": "https://www-thphys.physics.ox.ac.uk/people/JamesBinney/qb.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "D. Tong, Quantum Mechanics (author-hosted lecture set), Sections 2.2-2.3.1, printed pages 39-47 (PDF pages 42-50): parity of energy eigenfunctions for even potentials (printed page 39) and the even and odd bound-state solutions of the finite potential well; PDF page = printed page + 3",
                "url": "https://davidtong.org/pdfs/teaching/quantum-mechanics/qm.pdf"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "ex-nrqm-symmetries-free-translation-and-momentum",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "The free model: translation symmetries and conserved momentum in the momentum representation",
          "statement": "Adopt the postulates P1, P2, P4, P5 and P6 in the readings of\n[[def-nrqm-kinematics-framework-massive-spin-s-model]],\n[[def-nrqm-observables-framework-observable-and-outcome-law]],\n[[def-nrqm-autonomous-dynamics-framework-evolution]] and\n[[def-nrqm-symmetries-framework-symmetry-groups-and-conservation]] for a\ndeclared particle of mass parameter $m>0$ and spin label $s$, with state space\n$H_{s}=L^{2}(\\mathbb R^{3};\\mathbb C^{r})$, $r=2s+1$, componentwise operators\n$Q_{j},P_{k}$ and translations $T_{a}$\n([[lem-nrqm-kinematics-componentwise-position-and-momentum]] clause (c));\nassume the Axiom of Choice, the Axiom of Countable Choice and the Axiom of\nDependent Choice ([[def-axiom-of-choice]], [[def-countable-choice]],\n[[def-dependent-choice]]). Consider the **free model**, the bounded-potential\nmodel with $V\\equiv0$:\n$$H_{0}:=\\frac{1}{2m}\\sum_{k=1}^{3}P_{k}^{2},\\qquad D(H_{0})=W^{2,2}(\\mathbb R^{3};\\mathbb C^{r}),$$\nwith flow $U(t)=\\exp(-itH_{0}/\\hbar)$, momentum unitary $U^{(r)}$\n([[lem-nrqm-kinematics-momentum-representation]]) and\n$f_{t}(p):=e^{-it|p|^{2}/(2m\\hbar)}$. Then:\n\n(a) for every $a\\in\\mathbb R^{3}$ the translation $T_{a}$ is a symmetry of\n$H_{0}$ in the sense of\n[[def-nrqm-symmetries-framework-symmetry-groups-and-conservation]] clause (b),\nand\n$$T_{a}\\,e^{-itH_{0}/\\hbar}\\,T_{a}^{-1}=e^{-itH_{0}/\\hbar}\\qquad(a\\in\\mathbb R^{3},\\ t\\in\\mathbb R);$$\n\n(b) in the momentum representation the two actions are the multipliers\n$$U^{(r)}T_{a}U^{(r)-1}=M_{e^{-ia\\cdot p/\\hbar}},\\qquad U^{(r)}e^{-itH_{0}/\\hbar}U^{(r)-1}=M_{f_{t}},$$\nwhich commute; consequently $T_{a}U(t)=U(t)T_{a}$ for all $a,t$;\n\n(c) **Momentum conservation.** For every $k$ the momentum component $P_{k}$ is\na conserved observable of the free model: for every preparation $\\rho$, Borel\n$B\\subseteq\\mathbb R$ and $t$,\n$$\\mu^{P_{k}}_{\\rho(t)}(B)=\\mu^{P_{k}}_{\\rho(0)}(B),$$\nand for a unit vector $\\psi(0)\\in D(P_{k})$ the mean and second moment of the\nlaw of $P_{k}$ are finite and independent of $t$, with time-zero values\n$\\langle P_{k}\\psi,\\psi\\rangle$ and $\\|P_{k}\\psi\\|^{2}$; the coordinate\ntranslations satisfy $T_{te_{k}}=e^{-itP_{k}/\\hbar}$, so the momentum\ncomponents are the generators of the translational symmetry groups;\n\n(d) the modulus of the momentum representative is invariant in time:\n$$\\bigl|\\bigl(U^{(r)}e^{-itH_{0}/\\hbar}\\psi\\bigr)(p)\\bigr|=\\bigl|\\bigl(U^{(r)}\\psi\\bigr)(p)\\bigr|\\qquad\\text{for almost every }p\\ \\text{and every }\\psi\\in H_{s};$$\nconsequently the squared modulus of the momentum representative is the same\nalmost-everywhere function of $p$ at every time;\n\n(e) **Scope.** The statement concerns the free model $V\\equiv0$ only. For a\nnonconstant bounded potential the translations need not be symmetries and\nmomentum need not be conserved; that failure is exhibited on this page. No\ntrajectory in space, no classical limit, no measurement model and no empirical\nresult is asserted.",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "deps": [
            "def-axiom-of-choice",
            "def-countable-choice",
            "def-dependent-choice",
            "def-hilbert-space",
            "def-l-p-space-as-a-quotient-by-null-functions",
            "def-nrqm-autonomous-dynamics-framework-evolution",
            "def-nrqm-framework-quantities-and-units",
            "def-nrqm-kinematics-framework-massive-spin-s-model",
            "def-nrqm-observables-framework-observable-and-outcome-law",
            "def-nrqm-state-geometry-framework-state-space",
            "def-nrqm-symmetries-framework-symmetry-groups-and-conservation",
            "lem-nrqm-kinematics-componentwise-position-and-momentum",
            "lem-nrqm-kinematics-momentum-representation",
            "lem-nrqm-symmetries-free-flow-multiplier-form",
            "post-nrqm-framework-autonomous-dynamics",
            "post-nrqm-framework-identical-particles-and-spin",
            "post-nrqm-framework-nonrelativistic-kinematics-and-massive-particle",
            "post-nrqm-framework-observable-and-probability",
            "post-nrqm-framework-state-and-composition",
            "pthm-nrqm-symmetries-translation-invariance-and-momentum-conservation",
            "thm-nrqm-composites-real-multipliers-and-free-bounded-potential-operators"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-axiom-of-choice": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
