          "dependency_level": 12,
          "physical_scope": "A model computation for the free massive spin-s model, V identically zero: the translations are symmetries and commute with the free flow, the momentum components are conserved sharp observables with conserved law and moments, and the free flow acts in the momentum representation as a unimodular multiplier leaving the modulus of the momentum representative fixed. The item asserts nothing for nonconstant potentials, no trajectory, no measured distribution, and no apparatus model.",
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "J. Binney and D. Skinner, The Physics of Quantum Mechanics, Sections 4.1.1-4.1.2 and 4.3, printed pages 59-62 and 68-70 (PDF pages 67-70 and 76-78): translating kets, momentum as the generator of translations and translational invariance with conservation of momentum; PDF page = printed page + 8",
                "url": "https://www-thphys.physics.ox.ac.uk/people/JamesBinney/qb.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics, 1st edition 2009, Sections 7.2-7.3, printed pages 167-169 (PDF pages 179-181), equations (7.24) and (7.27): the free Hamiltonian and evolution as Fourier multipliers in the convention hbar=1, m=1/2; Section 8.1, printed pages 173-175 (PDF pages 185-187), equations (8.3)-(8.7): translations, momentum generators and conservation",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-schroe/schroe.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "B. Zwiebach, MIT 8.05 Quantum Physics II (Fall 2013), Chapter 6 'Quantum Dynamics', Section 3.2, printed pages 20-22 (PDF pages 20-22): constant Heisenberg operators for observables commuting with the Hamiltonian",
                "url": "https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/8-05-quantum-physics-ii-fall-2013/79a8091ef4f18d8e3ff76a097e8db33c_MIT8_05F13_Chap_06.pdf"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "cex-nrqm-symmetries-nonconstant-potential-breaks-translation",
          "kind": "counterexample",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "A bounded nonconstant potential with no nontrivial translational symmetry",
          "statement": "Let $V:\\mathbb R^{3}\\to\\mathbb R$ be any real, bounded, measurable, nonconstant\npotential energy, expressed in joules. Then for every nonzero $a\\in\\mathbb R^{3}\\setminus\\{0\\}$ the\ntranslation $T_{a}$ is a symmetry of the declared bounded-potential dynamics\nwith energy $H_{V}$.",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "deps": [
            "def-axiom-of-choice",
            "def-countable-choice",
            "def-dependent-choice",
            "def-euclidean-inner-product",
            "def-metric-ball",
            "def-measure-null-set-and-almost-everywhere",
            "def-nrqm-framework-quantities-and-units",
            "def-nrqm-kinematics-framework-massive-spin-s-model",
            "def-nrqm-symmetries-framework-symmetry-groups-and-conservation",
            "lem-euclidean-balls-have-positive-finite-lebesgue-measure",
            "lem-every-norm-on-rn-is-continuous-for-the-euclidean-metric",
