      "items": [
        {
          "id": "lem-nrqm-angular-momentum-product-flow-generator",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Self-adjointness and the flow of a self-adjoint operator perturbed by a bounded operator commuting with its flow",
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice and the Axiom of Countable Choice\n([[def-axiom-of-choice]], [[def-countable-choice]]). Let $H$ be a nonzero\ncomplex Hilbert space ([[def-hilbert-space]]), let $A$ be a self-adjoint\noperator on $H$ with domain $D(A)$\n([[def-adjoint-of-a-densely-defined-unbounded-operator]],\n[[def-symmetric-self-adjoint-and-essentially-self-adjoint]]), and let $B$ be a\nbounded self-adjoint operator on $H$\n([[def-bounded-linear-operator]],\n[[def-self-adjoint-positive-unitary-and-normal-operator]]) with\n$$B\\,e^{isA}=e^{isA}B\\qquad(s\\in\\mathbb R),$$\nwhere $e^{isA}=\\int_{\\mathbb R}e^{is\\lambda}\\,dE_A(\\lambda)$ is the unitary\ngroup of $A$ in the spectral calculus\n([[lem-self-adjoint-operator-generates-a-strongly-continuous-unitary-group]],\n[[thm-bounded-borel-pvm-integral]],\n[[def-projection-valued-measure]]). Put $A+B$ on its natural domain\n$D(A+B):=D(A)\\cap D(B)=D(A)$. Then:\n\n(a) $A+B$ is self-adjoint;\n\n(b) $e^{isB}e^{itA}=e^{itA}e^{isB}$ for all $s,t\\in\\mathbb R$; the flows of\n$A$ and of the bounded $B$ commute;\n\n(c) the family $s\\mapsto P(s):=e^{isA}e^{isB}$ is a strongly continuous\none-parameter unitary group\n([[def-strongly-continuous-one-parameter-unitary-group]]), and its\ninfinitesimal generator $G$\n([[def-infinitesimal-generator-of-a-unitary-group]]) is $G=i(A+B)$: the\nquotient $\\frac1s\\bigl(P(s)x-x\\bigr)$ converges as $s\\to0$ exactly for\n$x\\in D(A)$, with limit $i(A+B)x$. Consequently $P(s)=e^{is(A+B)}$ for every\n$s\\in\\mathbb R$.",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "deps": [
            "def-adjoint-of-a-densely-defined-unbounded-operator",
            "def-axiom-of-choice",
            "def-bounded-linear-operator",
