        {
          "id": "lem-nrqm-angular-momentum-orbital-casimir-identity",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "The orbital Casimir identity: the restrictions of the orbital generators to the degree-l blocks are spin-l models",
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Work in the\nnotation of\n[[thm-nrqm-orbital-and-spin-orbital-self-adjoint-generators]] and\n[[thm-nrqm-orbital-and-spin-sphere-laplacian-diagonal-domain]]: $S^2$ with its\npolar measure $\\sigma$, the Hilbert space $L^{2}(S^2,\\sigma)$ with inner\nproduct linear in the first argument\n([[def-l-p-space-as-a-quotient-by-null-functions]],\n[[def-complex-lp-and-euclidean-test-function-conventions]],\n[[def-hilbert-space]], [[def-inner-product-space]]), the complete orthonormal\nfamily $(Y_{lm})_{l\\ge0,\\,-l\\le m\\le l}$\n([[thm-nrqm-orbital-and-spin-sphere-onb]]), the blocks\n$V_{l}:=\\operatorname{span}\\{Y_{l,-l},\\dots,Y_{ll}\\}$, the finite span $H$,\nthe self-adjoint operators $L_{1},L_{2},L_{3}$ with $L_{3}=L_{z}$ and\n$L_{i}Y_{lm}\\in V_{l}$ for all $l,m,i$, and the diagonal sphere Laplacian $A$\nwith $AY_{lm}=l(l+1)Y_{lm}$. Then for every $l\\ge0$:\n\n(a) each $L_{i}$ leaves $V_{l}$ invariant, and the restriction\n$L_{i}|_{V_{l}}$ is a self-adjoint endomorphism of the finite-dimensional\ninner product space $V_{l}$\n([[def-self-adjoint-and-normal-endomorphism]]), with\n$L_{3}Y_{lm}=\\hbar mY_{lm}$ for $-l\\le m\\le l$;\n\n(b) the triple $\\bigl((1/\\hbar)L_{1}|_{V_{l}},(1/\\hbar)L_{2}|_{V_{l}},(1/\\hbar)L_{3}|_{V_{l}}\\bigr)$\nis unitarily equivalent to the spin-$l$ matrices of\n[[prop-nrqm-orbital-and-spin-finite-spin-matrices]]; in particular\n$$\\sum_{i=1}^{3}L_{i}^{2}F=\\hbar^{2}l(l+1)F\\qquad(F\\in V_{l});$$\n\n(c) for every $F$ in the finite span $H$ one has\n$\\sum_{i=1}^{3}L_{i}^{2}F=\\hbar^{2}AF$.\n\nThe statement is a mathematical statement about the operators on\n$L^{2}(S^2,\\sigma)$; no physical interpretation as angular momentum of a\nparticle is asserted.",
          "strategy": "direct",
