          "dependency_level": 9,
          "physical_scope": "The effective magnetic-moment coupling of the framework's massive spin-s particle model in a declared inertial frame, for a prescribed real bounded measurable magnetic field profile and a declared real gyromagnetic parameter gamma_s: the magnetic moment mu = gamma_s S with unit J T^-1, the Zeeman energy operator H_Z on the domain of the free operator, its units and the autonomous unitary evolution assigned to it by P4, and the status of gamma_s and of the static field profile as empirical or externally prescribed model inputs. The item asserts no Maxwell equation, no source model, no derivation of gamma_s from charge and mass, no spin-orbit or relativistic correction, no time-dependent or open-system dynamics and no measured value; it is a model assumption adopted on this page only.",
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "J. Binney and D. Skinner, The Physics of Quantum Mechanics, Section 7.4, printed pages 158-169 (PDF pages 166-177): spin angular momentum, the magnetic moment of a spin-half particle, the Stern-Gerlach coupling and magnetic precession",
                "url": "https://www-thphys.physics.ox.ac.uk/people/JamesBinney/qb.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "B. Zwiebach, MIT 8.05 Quantum Physics II (Fall 2013), Chapter 2 'Spin One-Half, Bras, Kets, and Operators', Section 1, printed pages 1-7 (the magnetic dipole in a nonuniform magnetic field and the two-peak Stern-Gerlach idealization) and Section 4, printed pages 16-19 (the spin operator in an arbitrary direction and its two eigenvalues)",
                "url": "https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/8-05-quantum-physics-ii-fall-2013/a56c316e4ec548d8bd0a554fac9a74e8_MIT8_05F13_Chap_02.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "B. Zwiebach, MIT 8.05 Quantum Physics II (Fall 2013), Chapter 7 'Two State Systems', Sections 2-3, chapter pages 2-6 (spin precession in a uniform magnetic field and the precession frequency)",
                "url": "https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/8-05-quantum-physics-ii-fall-2013/7c376a3b5b27e5ea586a7e37b85a05d3_MIT8_05F13_Chap_07.pdf"
              }
            ]
          }
