        {
          "id": "lem-nrqm-composites-pure-state-separability-criterion",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Pure-state separability is equivalent to being a product: a Schmidt overlap witness",
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $H,K$ be arbitrary nonzero complex Hilbert spaces, with inner products linear in the first argument, and put $L=H\\widehat\\otimes K$ with the isometric inclusion $\\kappa$ of [[lem-nrqm-composites-hilbert-tensor-construction]]. Write $T_{x,y}z=\\langle z,y\\rangle x$ as in [[lem-nrqm-composites-rank-one-operator-calculus]]. Set\n$$\\mathcal P=\\{T_{\\kappa(a\\otimes b),\\kappa(a\\otimes b)}:\\|a\\|=\\|b\\|=1\\},\\qquad \\mathcal S=\\overline{\\operatorname{conv}\\mathcal P}^{\\|\\cdot\\|_1},$$\nwith trace class as in [[def-trace-class-operator]], where the convex hull consists of finite convex combinations, and the closure is taken in the trace-class operators on $L$. For each unit $\\Psi\\in L$, let $P_\\Psi=T_{\\Psi,\\Psi}$. Then\n$$P_\\Psi\\in\\mathcal S\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad \\Psi=\\kappa(a\\otimes b)\\text{ for some unit }a\\in H,\\ b\\in K.$$\n\nMore precisely, let $\\Psi=\\sum_{r\\in J}s_r\\kappa(v_r\\otimes u_r)$ be any finite or countably infinite positive Schmidt expansion from [[thm-nrqm-composites-infinite-schmidt-decomposition]], and put $\\lambda_r=s_r^2$. The number $m=\\max_{r\\in J}\\lambda_r$ exists. Every pair of unit vectors $a,b$ satisfies $|\\langle\\Psi,\\kappa(a\\otimes b)\\rangle|^2\\le m$, with equality at a Schmidt pair whose weight is $m$. Every $\\sigma\\in\\mathcal S$ satisfies $\\operatorname{tr}(\\sigma P_\\Psi)\\le m$, whereas $\\operatorname{tr}(P_\\Psi^2)=1$. If $\\Psi$ is non-product then $m<1$ and, for every $\\sigma\\in\\mathcal S$,\n$$\\|P_\\Psi-\\sigma\\|_1\\ge 1-m>0.$$\nThe factors need not be separable; only the support of the single tensor vector has a countable Schmidt expansion. These are mathematical trace pairings, with no measurement or Born-rule assumption.",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "deps": [
            "def-countable-choice",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-hilbert-tensor-construction",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-rank-one-operator-calculus",
            "thm-nrqm-composites-infinite-schmidt-decomposition",
            "def-trace-class-operator",
            "thm-trace-class-is-a-two-sided-banach-operator-ideal",
            "thm-trace-is-absolutely-convergent-and-basis-independent"
          ],
