          "physical_scope": "The declared local instruments of one factor of a composite of two distinguishable subsystems: a declared finite or countable instrument on one factor leaves the reduced preparation, and hence every local outcome law, of the other factor unchanged once its classical record is discarded; conditioning on the record displays the correlation through the conditional reduced preparations, whose probability-weighted average is the original reduced preparation. The statement is a conditional consequence of the framework's measurement readings and the cited mathematics; it asserts no relativistic causality principle, no disturbance of the other factor by any particular apparatus, no apparatus realization and no empirical fact."
