            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "dependency_level": 0,
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "J. Binney and D. Skinner, The Physics of Quantum Mechanics, Section 11.6 printed pages 253-254 (PDF pages 261-262): the WKBJ equation d^2 psi/dx^2 = -k^2 psi with k^2 = 2m(E-V)/hbar^2 and the phase phi(x) = int k dx",
                "url": "https://www-thphys.physics.ox.ac.uk/people/JamesBinney/qb.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "R. Fitzpatrick, Quantum Mechanics (University of Texas at Austin, author-hosted course text), Section 5.4 'WKB Approximation' printed and PDF pages 70-72 (the one-dimensional WKB solution with the local wavenumber and the phase integral, in the same reduced equation)",
                "url": "https://farside.ph.utexas.edu/teaching/qmech/qmech.pdf"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "lem-nrqm-approximations-finite-rank-gapped-cluster-projection",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Finite-rank gapped spectral cluster under a bounded perturbation",
          "deps": [
            "def-countable-choice",
            "def-hilbert-space",
            "def-symmetric-self-adjoint-and-essentially-self-adjoint",
            "def-bounded-linear-operator",
            "def-operator-norm",
            "def-resolvent-and-spectrum-of-a-closed-unbounded-operator",
            "def-projection-valued-measure",
            "lem-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-cc-arbitrary-hilbert-spectral-calculus",
            "cor-finite-dimensional-inner-product-spaces-have-orthonormal-bases",
            "thm-circle-integrals-of-integer-monomials",
            "thm-cauchy-integral-formula-circle"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-hilbert-space": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-symmetric-self-adjoint-and-essentially-self-adjoint": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-bounded-linear-operator": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-operator-norm": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-resolvent-and-spectrum-of-a-closed-unbounded-operator": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-projection-valued-measure": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-cc-arbitrary-hilbert-spectral-calculus": "mathematical-premise",
            "cor-finite-dimensional-inner-product-spaces-have-orthonormal-bases": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-circle-integrals-of-integer-monomials": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-cauchy-integral-formula-circle": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "dependency_level": 2,
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $H$ be an arbitrary complex Hilbert space ([[def-hilbert-space]]) and $H_0=H_0^*$ a self-adjoint operator on its exact dense domain $D=D(H_0)$ ([[def-symmetric-self-adjoint-and-essentially-self-adjoint]]). Let $E\\in\\mathbb R$ be an isolated eigenvalue with $\\operatorname{dist}(E,\\sigma(H_0)\\setminus\\{E\\})\\ge g>0$, and let its orthogonal spectral projection $P_0=E_{H_0}(\\{E\\})$ have finite rank $r\\ge1$. The PVM and gap calculus are those of [[lem-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-cc-arbitrary-hilbert-spectral-calculus]]. Let $V=V^*\\in\\mathcal B(H)$ and $v=\\|V\\|\\ge0$ ([[def-bounded-linear-operator]], [[def-operator-norm]]). Put $H_\\lambda=H_0+\\lambda V$ on $D$, and define\n$$\\Omega_v=\\begin{cases}\\{\\lambda\\in\\mathbb C:|\\lambda|<g/(2v)\\},&v>0,\\\\\\mathbb C,&v=0.\\end{cases}$$\nFor $\\lambda\\in\\Omega_v$ write $q_\\lambda=2|\\lambda|v/g<1$, $\\Gamma=\\{z:|z-E|=g/2\\}$ oriented counterclockwise, and $\\Delta=\\{z:|z-E|<g/2\\}$.\n\n**(a) Resolvent and exact domain.** $H_\\lambda$ is closed and densely defined on $D$. Every $z\\in\\Gamma$ is a resolvent point, with the convention $R_\\lambda(z)=(z-H_\\lambda)^{-1}:H\\to D$ of [[def-resolvent-and-spectrum-of-a-closed-unbounded-operator]], and\n$$R_\\lambda(z)=R_0(z)\\sum_{k\\ge0}(\\lambda VR_0(z))^k,\\qquad \\|R_\\lambda(z)\\|\\le\\frac{2/g}{1-q_\\lambda},\\qquad \\|R_\\lambda(z)-R_0(z)\\|\\le\\frac2g\\frac{q_\\lambda}{1-q_\\lambda}.$$\nThe series converges in operator norm uniformly on $\\Gamma$ and locally uniformly in $\\lambda\\in\\Omega_v$.\n\n**(b) Finite-rank holomorphic cluster.** The norm contour integral\n$$P_\\lambda=\\frac1{2\\pi i}\\oint_\\Gamma R_\\lambda(z)\\,dz$$\nis a bounded idempotent of rank exactly $r$ throughout $\\Omega_v$, with $P_{\\lambda=0}=P_0$ and $\\|P_\\lambda-P_0\\|\\le q_\\lambda/(1-q_\\lambda)$. It is holomorphic in operator norm. Its range $M_\\lambda=P_\\lambda H$ lies in $D$ and is invariant under $H_\\lambda$, and $P_\\lambda H_\\lambda=H_\\lambda P_\\lambda$ on $D$. Both $H_\\lambda P_\\lambda\\in\\mathcal B(H)$ and $P_\\lambda:H\\to(D,\\|x\\|+\\|H_0x\\|)$ are holomorphic in their respective operator norms.\n\n**(c) Exactly the enclosed spectrum.** Let $A_\\lambda=H_\\lambda|_{M_\\lambda}:M_\\lambda\\to M_\\lambda$. Then\n$$\\sigma(H_\\lambda)\\cap\\Delta=\\sigma(A_\\lambda)\\subset\\Delta.$$\nThis is a nonempty finite set of at most $r$ eigenvalues. The restriction of $w-H_\\lambda$ to $\\ker P_\\lambda$ has a bounded two-sided inverse on its exact domain $D\\cap\\ker P_\\lambda$ for every $w\\in\\Delta$. Consequently all generalized eigenvectors at an enclosed eigenvalue belong to $M_\\lambda$; their eigenspaces and generalized eigenspaces are those of this finite-dimensional restriction.\n\n**(d) Real coupling and zero perturbation.** For real $\\lambda$, $H_\\lambda$ is self-adjoint on $D$. For real $\\lambda\\in\\Omega_v$, $P_\\lambda=E_{H_\\lambda}((E-g/2,E+g/2))$ is the orthogonal projection on the entire enclosed spectral cluster ([[def-projection-valued-measure]]). If $v=0$, then $V=0$, $H_\\lambda=H_0$ and $P_\\lambda=P_0$ for every complex coupling, with $A_\\lambda=E I_{M_0}$ and enclosed spectrum $\\{E\\}$.\n\nNo separability or arbitrary-index Axiom of Choice is assumed. The claim supplies a cluster and its finite restriction; for $r>1$ it supplies no ordering or individually holomorphic scalar eigenvalue branches.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics, 1st edition 2009, Section 6.6: contour perturbation; finite-rank extension proved locally here",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-schroe/schroe.pdf"
              }
            ]
          }
