          "physical_scope": "The static finite-level electric-dipole coupling model of the declared two-body Coulomb pair: the relative-coordinate dipole operator with components -q Q_j on their maximal L^2 domains, a declared finite-dimensional subspace of the relative-coordinate space, the compressed Hermitian dipole matrix, the uniform static field value and the bounded interaction -E . D added to the compressed Coulomb energy on the subspace. The postulate is a model assumption for the declared finite-level truncation; it asserts no Maxwell equation or source model, no propagation, no derivation of the truncation or of the field, no semibounded uncompressed model (the common test-domain expectations of H_kappa - E_ext . D are shown unbounded below for every nonzero uniform field), no transition rate and no measured shift."
