        {
          "id": "pthm-nrqm-approximations-turning-point-connection",
          "kind": "physics-theorem",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "Airy connection across a single simple turning point of the declared regime model, with envelope error control",
          "statement": "Adopt the declared WKB regime model of\n[[def-nrqm-approximations-framework-wkb-regime-model]] with its data\n$V,m,\\hbar,\\ell,E_\\star,W,\\lambda,h$, and assume hypothesis (W3) at a\nturning point $\\xi_{0}$ with $W'(\\xi_{0})>0$: on an interval\n$[\\xi_{0}-r_{0},\\xi_{0}+s_{0}]$ with $r_{0},s_{0}>0$ the function\n$W-\\lambda$ has the single zero $\\xi_{0}$, is strictly negative on\n$[\\xi_{0}-r_{0},\\xi_{0})$ (allowed side) and strictly positive on\n$(\\xi_{0},\\xi_{0}+s_{0}]$ (forbidden side). Write, for the two sides,\n$$\\theta(\\xi):=\\frac1h\\int_{\\xi}^{\\xi_{0}}\\sqrt{\\lambda-W(\\xi')}\\,d\\xi' \\quad(\\xi<\\xi_{0}),\\qquad \\Sigma(\\xi):=\\frac1h\\int_{\\xi_{0}}^{\\xi}\\sqrt{W(\\xi')-\\lambda}\\,d\\xi' \\quad(\\xi>\\xi_{0}),$$the nonnegative dimensionless phase and exponent measured from the turning point into the allowed and forbidden sides. Let$$\\zeta(\\xi):=\\operatorname{sign}(\\xi-\\xi_{0})\\Bigl[\\frac32\\Bigl|\\int_{\\xi_{0}}^{\\xi}\\sqrt{|W(\\xi')-\\lambda|}\\,d\\xi'\\Bigr|\\Bigr]^{2/3}$$be the Liouville coordinate. Write $R$ for the continuous remainder in the transformed equation $w''=[\\zeta/h^{2}+R(\\zeta)]w$ and put $\\eta_-:=\\zeta(\\xi_{0}-r_{0})$, $\\eta_+:=\\zeta(\\xi_{0}+s_{0})$. Define$$\\varepsilon(h):=C_{\\mathrm{ker}}h\\int_{\\eta_-}^{\\eta_+}\\frac{|R(v)|}{\\sqrt{|v|+h^{2/3}}}\\,dv,$$where $C_{\\mathrm{ker}}$ is the kernel constant of [[thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-stable-weighted-airy-volterra-connection]]; boundedness of $R$ on the fixed transformed interval gives $\\varepsilon(h)\\le C_{1}h$ for some $C_{1}>0$ depending only on the fixed data. There are constants $0<C_{0}<\\infty$ and $0<C_{\\mathrm{err}}<\\infty$, depending only on $W,\\lambda,\\xi_{0},r_{0},s_{0}$ (not on $h$), and $h_0>0$, such that for every $0<h<h_0$:  (a) *Decaying connection.* There is an exact solution $u_{\\mathrm{dec}}$ of the model equation $u''=(W-\\lambda)u/h^{2}$ on $[\\xi_{0}-r_{0},\\xi_{0}+s_{0}]$ and a real constant $C\\ne0$ with$$u_{\\mathrm{dec}}(\\xi)=C\\,(W(\\xi)-\\lambda)^{-1/4} e^{-\\Sigma(\\xi)}\\bigl(1+\\delta_{\\mathrm{f}}(\\xi)\\bigr)\\qquad(\\xi>\\xi_{0}),$$$$u_{\\mathrm{dec}}(\\xi)=2C\\,(\\lambda-W(\\xi))^{-1/4} \\Bigl(\\sin\\bigl(\\theta(\\xi)+\\tfrac{\\pi}{4}\\bigr)+\\delta_{\\mathrm{a}}(\\xi)\\Bigr) \\qquad(\\xi<\\xi_{0}),$$ where the absolute errors obey, for $\\xi\\ne\\xi_{0}$ away from the turning point,$$|\\delta_{\\mathrm{f}}(\\xi)|\\le C_{0}\\bigl(\\varepsilon(h)+h/|\\zeta(\\xi)|^{3/2}\\bigr), \\qquad \\bigl|\\delta_{\\mathrm{a}}(\\xi)\\bigr|\\le C_{0}\\bigl(\\varepsilon(h)+h/|\\zeta(\\xi)|^{3/2}\\bigr),$$(b) *Growing connection.* There is a second exact solution $u_{\\mathrm{grow}}$, linearly independent of $u_{\\mathrm{dec}}$, with$$u_{\\mathrm{grow}}(\\xi)=C'\\,(W(\\xi)-\\lambda)^{-1/4} e^{+\\Sigma(\\xi)}\\bigl(1+\\delta_{\\mathrm{f,grow}}(\\xi)\\bigr)\\qquad(\\xi>\\xi_{0}),$$$$u_{\\mathrm{grow}}(\\xi)=C'\\,(\\lambda-W(\\xi))^{-1/4} \\Bigl(\\cos\\bigl(\\theta(\\xi)+\\tfrac{\\pi}{4}\\bigr)+\\delta_{\\mathrm{a,grow}}(\\xi)\\Bigr) \\qquad(\\xi<\\xi_{0}),$$ for a real constant $C'\\ne0$, with $|\\delta_{\\mathrm{f,grow}}(\\xi)|,|\\delta_{\\mathrm{a,grow}}(\\xi)| \\le C_{0}(\\varepsilon(h)+h/|\\zeta(\\xi)|^{3/2})$ away from $\\xi_{0}$;  (c) *Derivative and envelope control.* Let $A_h(\\zeta):=A(\\zeta/h^{2/3})$ and $B_h(\\zeta):=B(\\zeta/h^{2/3})$ be the Airy functions in [[thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-airy-envelopes-and-asymptotic-coefficients]], let $a(\\xi):=(\\zeta'(\\xi))^{-1/2}$, and put$$\nf_h(\\zeta):=(1+|\\zeta|/h^{2/3})^{-1/4},\\qquad \\phi_h(\\zeta):=\\frac{2(\\zeta_+)^{3/2}}{3h}.\n$$\nDefine the decaying and growing envelopes by\n$$\ne_h^-(\\zeta):=f_h(\\zeta)e^{-\\phi_h(\\zeta)},\\quad d_h^-(\\zeta):=h^{-2/3}f_h(\\zeta)^{-1}e^{-\\phi_h(\\zeta)},\\quad e_h^+(\\zeta):=f_h(\\zeta)e^{\\phi_h(\\zeta)},\\quad d_h^+(\\zeta):=h^{-2/3}f_h(\\zeta)^{-1}e^{\\phi_h(\\zeta)}.\n$$For each transformed coordinate $\\eta\\in\\zeta([\\xi_0-r_0,\\xi_0+s_0])$, define $w_{\\mathrm{dec}}(\\eta):=u_{\\mathrm{dec}}(\\zeta^{-1}(\\eta))/a(\\zeta^{-1}(\\eta))$ and $w_{\\mathrm{grow}}(\\eta):=u_{\\mathrm{grow}}(\\zeta^{-1}(\\eta))/a(\\zeta^{-1}(\\eta))$. For the solutions chosen as in the proof, the following transformed derivative error bounds hold on the full transformed interval, with an error constant $C_{\\mathrm{err}}$ depending only on the fixed data and not on $h$: $ |w_{\\mathrm{dec}}'-A_h'|\\le C_{\\mathrm{err}} d_h^-(e^{\\varepsilon(h)}-1),\\qquad |w_{\\mathrm{grow}}'-B_h'|\\le C_{\\mathrm{err}} d_h^+(e^{\\varepsilon(h)}-1). $ Here $\\varepsilon(h):=\\varepsilon_h$ is the control parameter of [F3] and satisfies $\\varepsilon(h)\\le C_1h$; the corresponding value errors are bounded by $C_{\\mathrm{err}}e_h^-(e^{\\varepsilon(h)}-1)$ and $C_{\\mathrm{err}}e_h^+(e^{\\varepsilon(h)}-1)$. Here primes on $w_{\\mathrm{dec}},w_{\\mathrm{grow}},A_h,B_h$ denote $\\eta$-derivatives, and primes on $a,\\zeta$ denote $\\xi$-derivatives. Consequently,$$\n|u_{\\mathrm{dec}}'(\\xi)-a'(\\xi)A_h(\\zeta(\\xi))-a(\\xi)\\zeta'(\\xi)A_h'(\\zeta(\\xi))|\\le C_{\\mathrm{err}}\\bigl(|a'(\\xi)|e_h^-(\\zeta(\\xi))+|a(\\xi)|\\zeta'(\\xi)d_h^-(\\zeta(\\xi))\\bigr)(e^{\\varepsilon(h)}-1),\n$$$$ |u_{\\mathrm{grow}}'(\\xi)-a'(\\xi)B_h(\\zeta(\\xi))-a(\\xi)\\zeta'(\\xi)B_h'(\\zeta(\\xi))|\\le C_{\\mathrm{err}}\\bigl(|a'(\\xi)|e_h^+(\\zeta(\\xi))+|a(\\xi)|\\zeta'(\\xi)d_h^+(\\zeta(\\xi))\\bigr)(e^{\\varepsilon(h)}-1).$$\nFor $\\rho(\\xi):=W(\\xi)-\\lambda>0$ on the forbidden side and\n$p(\\xi):=\\sqrt{\\lambda-W(\\xi)}>0$ on the allowed side, the scaled slope\nforms on every compact section bounded away from $\\xi_0$ are\n$$h\\rho(\\xi)^{-1/4}u_{\\mathrm{dec}}'(\\xi)=C e^{-\\Sigma(\\xi)}\\bigl(-1+\\delta_{\\mathrm{f,dec}}^{(1)}(\\xi)\\bigr),\\qquad h\\rho(\\xi)^{-1/4}u_{\\mathrm{grow}}'(\\xi)=C'e^{\\Sigma(\\xi)}\\bigl(1+\\delta_{\\mathrm{f,grow}}^{(1)}(\\xi)\\bigr),$$\n$$hp(\\xi)^{-1/2}u_{\\mathrm{dec}}'(\\xi)=2C\\bigl(-\\cos(\\theta(\\xi)+\\tfrac{\\pi}{4})+\\delta_{\\mathrm{a,dec}}^{(1)}(\\xi)\\bigr),\\qquad hp(\\xi)^{-1/2}u_{\\mathrm{grow}}'(\\xi)=C'\\bigl(\\sin(\\theta(\\xi)+\\tfrac{\\pi}{4})+\\delta_{\\mathrm{a,grow}}^{(1)}(\\xi)\\bigr).$$\nEach new slope error is absolute and satisfies\n$|\\delta_{\\mathrm{f,dec}}^{(1)}|,|\\delta_{\\mathrm{f,grow}}^{(1)}|,\n|\\delta_{\\mathrm{a,dec}}^{(1)}|,|\\delta_{\\mathrm{a,grow}}^{(1)}|\n\\le C_0(\\varepsilon(h)+h/|\\zeta(\\xi)|^{3/2})$; in particular no relative\nerror at a sine or cosine zero is asserted.\n\n(d) *Content of the connection.* The factors $2$ in the decaying allowed-side\nform of (a) and $1$ in the growing allowed-side form of (b) are the amplitude\nrelations of the exact Airy pair: the forbidden-side data determine the\nconstants $C$ and $C'$, and the allowed-side oscillations are the sine and\ncosine forms with phase $\\pi/4$ measured from the turning point into the\nallowed region. The statement excludes rectangular walls, coalescing or\nmultiple turning points, multi-turn resonances and barrier-top uniformity; it\nasserts no transmission or reflection coefficient (that is a separate\nstatement requiring hypothesis (W2)), no wave packet, no detector and no\nmeasured value; the errors are absolute and blow up as the turning point is\napproached, as displayed by the $h/|\\zeta|^{3/2}$ term.",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "deps": [
            "def-nrqm-approximations-framework-wkb-regime-model",
            "lem-nrqm-approximations-scaled-line-model-correspondence",
