            "references": [
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics, 1st edition 2009, Chapter 5 printed pages 123-131 (PDF pages 135-143): quantum dynamics and the Dyson expansion of the unitary propagator of a norm-continuous bounded family",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-schroe/schroe.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "B. Zwiebach, MIT 8.05 Quantum Physics II (Fall 2013), Chapter 6 'Quantum Dynamics', Section 2.3 printed pages 15-17 (PDF pages 15-17): the time-ordered exponential series of a time-dependent Hamiltonian and its truncation",
                "url": "https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/8-05-quantum-physics-ii-fall-2013/79a8091ef4f18d8e3ff76a097e8db33c_MIT8_05F13_Chap_06.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "physical_scope": "The bounded norm-continuous driven model of the declared system: existence, uniqueness and unitarity of the two-time propagator with its operator-norm Schroedinger equation, the Dyson truncation bound as an explicit error budget for the truncated propagator, the reading of evolved preparations at the running time, and the bound comparing exact Born probabilities to unnormalized truncated quadratic estimates. The theorem is conditional on the bounded norm-continuous class; it asserts no unbounded or common-domain family, no laboratory realization, no measurement model, no long-time limit and no empirical result.",
          "empirical_premises": []
        },
        {
          "id": "pthm-nrqm-driven-dynamics-mild-propagator-and-pictures",
          "kind": "physics-theorem",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "The bounded-control driven model: mild propagator, interaction-picture evolution and equivalence of the two readings",
          "statement": "Adopt the framework data and the declared driven model of [[def-nrqm-driven-dynamics-framework-driven-model]] in the **bounded-control class** of clause (b)(ii): $\\mathfrak H$ is the model's state space, $H_{0}$ is self-adjoint on $D(H_{0})$ ([[def-symmetric-self-adjoint-and-essentially-self-adjoint]]), $V:I\\to\\mathcal B(\\mathfrak H)$ is strongly continuous with self-adjoint values and $v:=\\sup_{t\\in I}\\|V(t)\\|<\\infty$ ([[def-bounded-linear-operator]], [[def-operator-norm]]), $H(t)=H_{0}+V(t)$ on $D(H_{0})$, and adopt the interaction-picture readings of [[def-nrqm-driven-dynamics-framework-interaction-picture]]: $E(t)=e^{-itH_{0}/\\hbar}$, $V_{I}(t)=E(-t)V(t)E(t)$, $U_{I}(t,s)=E(-t)U(t,s)E(s)$. Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice and the Axiom of Choice ([[def-countable-choice]], [[def-axiom-of-choice]]), the latter for the outcome-law reading of P2. Let $U(t,s)$ be the mild propagator constructed by [[thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-strong-bounded-interaction-picture]]. Then:\n\n(a) *Well-posedness of the declared model.* $U$ is the unique family of unitary operators on $\\mathfrak H$, jointly strongly continuous on $I\\times I$, with $U(s,s)=I$, $U(t,s)^{*}=U(s,t)$ and the cocycle $U(t,r)=U(t,s)U(s,r)$, satisfying the vectorwise mild Schroedinger identity\n$$U(t,s)\\psi=E(t-s)\\psi-\\frac{i}{\\hbar}\\int_{s}^{t}E(t-r)V(r)U(r,s)\\psi\\,dr\\qquad(\\psi\\in\\mathfrak H,\\ s,t\\in I);$$\nso the model's clause (c)(ii) declaration has exactly one solution. For $\\psi,\\varphi\\in D(H_{0})$ the scalar curve $t\\mapsto\\langle U(t,s)\\psi,\\varphi\\rangle$ is continuously differentiable on $I$ with\n$$\\frac{d}{dt}\\bigl\\langle U(t,s)\\psi,\\varphi\\bigr\\rangle=-\\frac{i}{\\hbar}\\Bigl[\\bigl\\langle U(t,s)\\psi,H_{0}\\varphi\\bigr\\rangle+\\bigl\\langle V(t)U(t,s)\\psi,\\varphi\\bigr\\rangle\\Bigr].$$\nNo invariance of $D(H_{0})$ under $U$, no strong full Schroedinger equation for its domain vectors, and no operator-norm differentiability of $U$ with respect to the unbounded generator are asserted.\n\n(b) *Interaction picture.* For every $s,t\\in I$ and every $\\psi\\in\\mathfrak H$ the interaction state $\\psi_{I}(t):=E(-t)U(t,s)\\psi(s)$ satisfies $\\psi_{I}(t)=U_{I}(t,s)\\psi_{I}(s)$, and its first-endpoint map is strongly differentiable with $i\\hbar\\partial_{t}\\psi_{I}(t)=V_{I}(t)\\psi_{I}(t)$; the interaction propagator is unitary with the cocycle and $U_{I}(t,s)^{*}=U_{I}(s,t)$, and its strong truncation bound is $\\|U_{I}(t,s)-\\sum_{n=0}^{N}D_{n}(t,s)\\|\\le e^{K(t-s)}(K(t-s))^{N+1}/(N+1)!$ for $s\\le t$ with $K=v/\\hbar$.\n\n(c) *Equivalence of the two readings.* For every preparation $\\rho$ specified at time $s$, every assigned sharp observable $(A,u_{A})$ with $A$ bounded, every $t\\in I$ and every Borel set $B\\subseteq\\mathbb R$, the Schroedinger reading and the interaction reading give the same outcome probability:\n$$\\mu^{A}_{\\rho(t)}(B)=\\mu^{A_{I}(t)}_{\\rho_{I}(t)}(B),\\qquad A_{I}(t)=E(-t)AE(t),\\quad \\rho_{I}(t)=E(-t)\\rho(t)E(t),$$\nand for pure preparations $\\|\\psi_{I}(t)\\|=\\|\\psi(t)\\|=\\|\\psi(s)\\|$. For eigenvectors $\\varphi_{a},\\varphi_{b}$ of $H_{0}$ as in clause (e) of the model, the transition probabilities of the two pictures agree,\n$$p_{ba}(t,s)=\\bigl|\\bigl\\langle U(t,s)\\varphi_{a},\\varphi_{b}\\bigr\\rangle\\bigr|^{2}=\\bigl|\\bigl\\langle U_{I}(t,s)\\varphi_{a},\\varphi_{b}\\bigr\\rangle\\bigr|^{2}.$$\n\n(d) *Scope.* The theorem is conditional on the bounded-control class; the mild identity, not a strong equation on $D(H_{0})$, is the evolution equation it establishes, and it asserts nothing about unbounded controls, invariant domains, measurement records, detectors, rates or empirical data.",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "deps": [
            "def-nrqm-driven-dynamics-framework-driven-model",
            "def-nrqm-driven-dynamics-framework-interaction-picture",
            "def-nrqm-autonomous-dynamics-framework-evolution",
