          "dependency_level": 10,
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics, 1st edition 2009, Chapter 5 printed pages 123-131 (PDF pages 135-143) and Section 9.1: strong evolution equations with a common domain of the generators",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-schroe/schroe.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "B. Zwiebach, MIT 8.05 Quantum Physics II (Fall 2013), Chapter 6 'Quantum Dynamics', Section 4.3-4.5 printed pages 30-39 (PDF pages 30-39): the forced harmonic oscillator, its translation operator and the classical response of coherent states",
                "url": "https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/8-05-quantum-physics-ii-fall-2013/79a8091ef4f18d8e3ff76a097e8db33c_MIT8_05F13_Chap_06.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "physical_scope": "The common-domain driven model of the declared system: existence and uniqueness of a strong two-time propagator for a C^1 family of self-adjoint operators on a fixed dense domain Y, invariance of Y with a uniform graph bound, the strong Schroedinger equation on Y, the reverse and adjoint equations, and the admissibility of the declared driven oscillator family H(t) = H_osc - f(t) Q as an instance. The theorem is conditional on the common-domain regularity class; it asserts no laboratory realization, no measurement, no long-time or asymptotic statement and no empirical result.",
          "empirical_premises": []
        },
        {
          "id": "pthm-nrqm-driven-dynamics-circular-drive-exact-rabi",
          "kind": "physics-theorem",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "The circularly driven two-level model: exact rotating-frame reduction, Rabi populations, resonance and inversion times",
          "statement": "Adopt the framework data and the **declared circular two-level drive model** of clause (f) of [[def-nrqm-driven-dynamics-framework-driven-model]]: $\\mathfrak H=\\mathbb C^{2}$ with the orthonormal basis $(e_{\\uparrow},e_{\\downarrow})$ and the Pauli matrices $(\\sigma_x,\\sigma_y,\\sigma_z)$ of [[prop-nrqm-orbital-and-spin-finite-spin-matrices]] clause (e), real parameters $\\omega_{0},\\Omega_{1},\\omega$ and\n$$H_{\\mathrm c}(t):=\\frac{\\hbar}{2}\\Bigl(\\omega_{0}\\sigma_{z}+\\Omega_{1}\\bigl(\\cos(\\omega t)\\sigma_{x}+\\sin(\\omega t)\\sigma_{y}\\bigr)\\Bigr),\\qquad t\\in I=[t_{0},t_{1}],$$\nread as the model's energy family in the bounded norm-continuous class, with $U_{\\mathrm c}(t,s)$ its unique unitary propagator ([[pthm-nrqm-driven-dynamics-bounded-norm-propagator]] clause (a)). Put $\\Delta:=\\omega_{0}-\\omega$, $b:=\\sqrt{\\Delta^{2}+\\Omega_{1}^{2}}$, let $R(t):=\\cos(\\omega t/2)I+i\\sin(\\omega t/2)\\sigma_{z}$ be the rotating frame of [[lem-nrqm-driven-dynamics-two-level-rotating-frame]] and let $P_{\\uparrow},P_{\\downarrow}$ be the projections onto $\\mathbb Ce_{\\uparrow},\\mathbb Ce_{\\downarrow}$, with populations $p_{\\bullet}(t):=\\langle P_{\\bullet}\\psi(t),\\psi(t)\\rangle$ of the evolved vector. Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice and the Axiom of Choice ([[def-countable-choice]], [[def-axiom-of-choice]]). Then:\n\n(a) *Exact rotating-frame reduction.* For every solution $\\psi$ of $i\\hbar\\psi'(t)=H_{\\mathrm c}(t)\\psi(t)$ the rotating-frame vector $\\psi_{R}(t):=R(t)\\psi(t)$ satisfies exactly\n$$i\\hbar\\psi_{R}'(t)=\\frac{\\hbar}{2}\\bigl(\\Delta\\sigma_{z}+\\Omega_{1}\\sigma_{x}\\bigr)\\psi_{R}(t),$$\nwith the constant matrix $\\frac{\\hbar}{2}(\\Delta\\sigma_{z}+\\Omega_{1}\\sigma_{x})$; equivalently\n$$U_{\\mathrm c}(t,s)=R(t)^{*}\\,e^{-i(t-s)(\\Delta\\sigma_{z}+\\Omega_{1}\\sigma_{x})/2}\\,R(s)\\qquad(s,t\\in I).$$\n\n(b) *Rabi populations.* Let $\\psi(s)=e_{\\uparrow}$ at time $s$. Define $p_{\\bullet}^{R}(\\tau):=\\langle P_{\\bullet}\\psi_R(s+\\tau),\\psi_R(s+\\tau)\\rangle$ for $\\tau\\in I-s:=\\{t-s:t\\in I\\}$. Then for $\\tau:=t-s$\n$$p_{\\downarrow}(t)=p_{\\downarrow}^{R}(\\tau)=\\Bigl|\\bigl\\langle e_{\\downarrow},e^{-i\\tau(\\Delta\\sigma_{z}+\\Omega_{1}\\sigma_{x})/2}e_{\\uparrow}\\bigr\\rangle\\Bigr|^{2}=\\frac{\\Omega_{1}^{2}}{b^{2}}\\sin^{2}\\!\\Bigl(\\frac{b\\tau}{2}\\Bigr)\\qquad(b>0),$$\nand $p_{\\uparrow}(t)=1-p_{\\downarrow}(t)$; the populations of the rotating-frame vector $\\psi_{R}(t)$ are the same numbers.\n\n(c) *Resonance and inversion times.* At resonance $\\Delta=0$ one has $p_{\\downarrow}(t)=\\sin^{2}(\\Omega_{1}\\tau/2)$; when $\\Omega_1\\ne0$, the drive inverts the population fully at the **pi-pulse** time $\\tau=\\pi/|\\Omega_{1}|$ and returns it to the initial level at $\\tau=2\\pi/|\\Omega_{1}|$; for $b>0$ the population is exactly periodic in $\\tau$ with period $2\\pi/b$. For $\\Omega_{1}=0$ the populations are constant, $p_{\\downarrow}\\equiv0$ and $p_{\\uparrow}\\equiv1$.\n\n(d) *Scope.* The statements are exact for the declared finite model and its declared parameters; the rotating frame is a change of description of the same model and does not change the populations. The theorem asserts no damping or relaxation, no decoherence, no measurement record, no identification of $\\omega_{0},\\Omega_{1}$ with laboratory fields or of the two levels with a species, and no empirical value.",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "deps": [
            "def-nrqm-driven-dynamics-framework-driven-model",
            "pthm-nrqm-driven-dynamics-bounded-norm-propagator",
            "lem-nrqm-driven-dynamics-two-level-rotating-frame",
