          "id": "ex-nrqm-driven-dynamics-circular-drive-exact-populations",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "Worked Rabi populations of the circularly driven two-level model: quarter-inversion, pi-pulse and detuned checks",
          "statement": "Adopt P1, P2 and P4 in the readings of the declared driven model ([[def-nrqm-driven-dynamics-framework-driven-model]] clause (a)) and the **circular two-level drive model** of its clause (f) with $\\mathbb C^{2}$, the basis $(e_{\\uparrow},e_{\\downarrow})$ and the Pauli matrices of [[prop-nrqm-orbital-and-spin-finite-spin-matrices]] clause (e). All angular frequencies below are declared model parameters read in $\\mathrm{s^{-1}}$ ([[def-nrqm-framework-quantities-and-units]]); no value is attributed to a laboratory system. For the numerical substitutions below, frequency symbols denote their numerical values in $\\mathrm{s^{-1}}$ and $t,s$ denote numerical time values in seconds; thus a displayed elapsed time $t-s=\\pi/2$ means a physical duration $(\\pi/2)\\,\\mathrm s$, and the displayed sine arguments are dimensionless. Define $\\sigma_{\\pm}:=(\\sigma_x\\pm i\\sigma_y)/2$. Three declared parameter sets are used:\n\n1. **Resonant set.** $\\omega_{0}=\\omega=1$, $\\Omega_{1}=2$, so $\\Delta=0$ and $b=2$;\n2. **Detuned set.** $\\omega_{0}=1+\\sqrt3$, $\\omega=1$, $\\Omega_{1}=1$, so $\\Delta=\\sqrt3$ and $b=2$;\n3. **Undriven set.** $\\Omega_{1}=0$ and arbitrary $\\omega_{0},\\omega$.\n\nIn each set let $U_{\\mathrm c}(t,s)$ be the model's propagator and let $p_{\\downarrow}(t)=\\langle P_{\\downarrow}U_{\\mathrm c}(t,s)e_{\\uparrow},U_{\\mathrm c}(t,s)e_{\\uparrow}\\rangle$ be the down-population of the initially up state. Then:\n\n(a) for the resonant set, $p_{\\downarrow}(t)=\\sin^{2}(t-s)$, so $p_{\\downarrow}=1/2$ at the **quarter-inversion time** $t-s=\\pi/4$, $p_{\\downarrow}=1$ at the **pi-pulse** time $t-s=\\pi/2$, and $p_{\\downarrow}=0$ again at $t-s=\\pi$;\n\n(b) for the detuned set, $p_{\\downarrow}(t)=\\frac14\\sin^{2}(t-s)$, so $p_{\\downarrow}=1/4$ at $t-s=\\pi/2$ and the population is exactly $\\pi$-periodic in $t-s$;\n\n(c) for the undriven set, $p_{\\downarrow}(t)\\equiv0$ and $p_{\\uparrow}(t)\\equiv1$ for all $t$, while the transverse coherences $\\langle\\sigma_{\\pm}\\rangle(t):=\\langle\\sigma_{\\pm}U_{\\mathrm c}(t,s)e_{\\uparrow},U_{\\mathrm c}(t,s)e_{\\uparrow}\\rangle$ rotate with phase $e^{\\pm i\\omega_{0}(t-s)}$: the general coherence transforms by this phase at the splitting frequency $\\omega_0$, while the specified initial up state has both transverse coherences zero;\n\n(d) in every set the population is the outcome probability of the projection $P_{\\downarrow}$ in the evolved preparation in the reading of P2; no damping, decoherence, measurement record or laboratory identification is asserted.",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "deps": [
