        {
          "id": "ex-nrqm-driven-dynamics-linear-drive-rotating-wave-budget",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "Worked rotating-wave error budget for the linearly driven two-level model: dimensionless instantiation and averaged Rabi check",
          "statement": "Adopt P1, P2 and P4 in the readings of the declared driven model ([[def-nrqm-driven-dynamics-framework-driven-model]] clause (a)) and the **linear two-level drive model** of its clause (f) with $\\mathbb C^{2}$, the basis $(e_{\\uparrow},e_{\\downarrow})$ and the Pauli matrices of [[prop-nrqm-orbital-and-spin-finite-spin-matrices]] clause (e). Declare angular-frequency parameters $\\omega>0$, $\\Delta=\\omega_{0}-\\omega=0$ (resonance) and $\\Omega_{1}=\\omega/50$, so that the dimensionless frequency ratio is $\\Omega_{1}/|\\omega|=1/50$; all angular frequencies are declared model parameters read in $\\mathrm{s^{-1}}$ ([[def-nrqm-framework-quantities-and-units]]), and no value is attributed to a laboratory system. Let $p_{\\downarrow}(t)$ be the exact down-population of the initially up state under the model's propagator, $p_{\\downarrow}^{\\mathrm{avg}}(\\tau)=\\sin^{2}(|\\Omega_{1}|\\tau/4)$ the averaged-model Rabi population of the page's error contract, and $\\varepsilon(\\tau)=\\frac{|\\Omega_{1}|}{2|\\omega|}[1+\\tau(|\\Delta|/2+3|\\Omega_{1}|/4)]$. Then:\n\n(a) the rotating-wave error contract reads $\\varepsilon(\\tau)=\\frac{1}{100}(1+\\frac{3\\omega\\tau}{200})$, so that $\\varepsilon=1/100$ at $\\omega\\tau=0$, $\\varepsilon=5/200=1/40$ at $\\omega\\tau=100$, and $\\varepsilon=1/25$ at $\\omega\\tau=200$; the corresponding population-difference bounds $2\\varepsilon$ are $2/100$, $1/20$ and $2/25$;\n\n(b) at the declared elapsed time $\\omega\\tau=100\\pi/3$ one has $\\Omega_{1}\\tau/4=\\pi/6$ and the averaged-model population is exactly $p_{\\downarrow}^{\\mathrm{avg}}=1/4$;\n\n(c) for the **circular** drive of the companion theorem with the same $\\omega_{0},\\omega,\\Omega_{1}$ the model's exact population obeys the same Rabi-type formula with no rotating-wave error, so the non-zero bound of (a) is specific to the linear polarization;\n\n(d) the numbers in (a)-(b) are outputs of the declared model and its error contract; they are not measured values, and clause (a)'s bound is conservative (at $\\tau=0$ the two propagators coincide while the bound is $1/50$).",
          "strategy": "direct",
