            ]
          },
          "physical_scope": "A conditional computation in the declared driven oscillator model H(t) = H_osc - f(t) Q with a C^1 real drive: the exact mean position and momentum of a coherent preparation follow the classical forced oscillator through the free rotation plus the zero-data forced response, and the position and momentum spreads stay at their oscillator values. The example is a model computation; it asserts no laboratory oscillator, no measured amplitude or phase, no damping or driving source and no measurement record."
        },
        {
          "id": "rem-nrqm-driven-dynamics-examples-scope-limits",
          "kind": "remark",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "What the examples check, what they do not contain, and the empirical status of the companion page",
          "statement": "## What the examples check\n\n[[ex-nrqm-driven-dynamics-circular-drive-exact-populations]] checks the exact Rabi populations of the declared circular two-level model at rational multiples of the Rabi period, including the quarter-inversion value $1/2$, the pi-pulse value $1$, the return value $0$ and a detuned value $1/4$; [[ex-nrqm-driven-dynamics-linear-drive-rotating-wave-budget]] evaluates the rotating-wave error contract of [[pthm-nrqm-driven-dynamics-linear-drive-rotating-wave-error]] at declared dimensionless times, including one exact rational averaged population and the observation that the contract is conservative at the initial time; [[ex-nrqm-driven-dynamics-ammonia-two-level-resonance]] matches the declared linear model onto an inversion-doublet family with an oscillating field, computes the averaged inversion probability and its pulse time and evaluates the error contract there for a declared coupling ratio; and [[ex-nrqm-driven-dynamics-driven-oscillator-coherent-response]] checks the exact classical mean response and the stationary fluctuations of a coherent preparation of the driven oscillator of [[pthm-nrqm-driven-dynamics-common-domain-propagator]] clause (c).\n\n## What the examples do not contain\n\nThe examples contain no measured frequency, energy, population, rate or lifetime; no apparatus, detector, calibration, sampling model or uncertainty record; no damping, relaxation, decoherence or environmental coupling; no identification of a laboratory spin, molecule, cavity or oscillator with the declared models or of a laboratory field with the declared drive parameters; and no claim that any declared parameter value is realized in nature. They also contain no Fermi golden rule, no continuum density of states and no long-time limit, in agreement with the scope of the companion A page ([[rem-nrqm-driven-dynamics-scope-and-empirical-status]]).\n\n## Empirical status\n\nAll four examples are conditional computations inside declared models: their inputs are declared parameters, the cited mathematics and the postulates P1, P2 and P4. The sources cited are mathematical and textbook treatments, not experimental reports, so no empirical premise and no statistical inference enters any statement of the page. Comparing any of these model outputs with a laboratory oscillation or pulse would require a separately declared preparation and apparatus model with its own uncertainty and would test the combined model and apparatus assumptions; it is a tested identification in the sense of P7 ([[post-nrqm-framework-preparation-and-apparatus]]), not a consequence of the computations here.\n",
          "strategy": "n/a",
          "deps": [
            "ex-nrqm-driven-dynamics-circular-drive-exact-populations",
            "ex-nrqm-driven-dynamics-linear-drive-rotating-wave-budget",
            "ex-nrqm-driven-dynamics-ammonia-two-level-resonance",
            "ex-nrqm-driven-dynamics-driven-oscillator-coherent-response",
