        {
          "id": "lem-nrqm-many-body-cc-bounded-spatial-realization",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "title": "CC realization of the bounded spatial operator on a finite-component H² domain",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "dependency_level": 0,
          "deps": [
            "def-countable-choice",
            "def-hilbert-space",
            "def-l-p-space-as-a-quotient-by-null-functions",
            "def-sobolev-space-wkp-and-its-norm",
            "def-adjoint-of-a-densely-defined-unbounded-operator",
            "def-symmetric-self-adjoint-and-essentially-self-adjoint",
            "def-fourier-transform-on-l-one-of-rn",
            "thm-plancherel",
            "thm-fourier-characterisation-of-integer-order-hilbert-sobolev-spaces",
            "lem-weak-derivatives-are-polynomial-fourier-multipliers",
            "cor-compactly-supported-smooth-functions-are-dense-in-wkp-of-rn",
            "thm-dominated-convergence"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-hilbert-space": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-l-p-space-as-a-quotient-by-null-functions": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-sobolev-space-wkp-and-its-norm": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-adjoint-of-a-densely-defined-unbounded-operator": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-symmetric-self-adjoint-and-essentially-self-adjoint": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-fourier-transform-on-l-one-of-rn": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-plancherel": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-fourier-characterisation-of-integer-order-hilbert-sobolev-spaces": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-weak-derivatives-are-polynomial-fourier-multipliers": "mathematical-premise",
            "cor-compactly-supported-smooth-functions-are-dense-in-wkp-of-rn": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-dominated-convergence": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Fix integers $N,M\\ge1$, $a>0$, and a real measurable function $V:\\mathbb R^{3N}\\to\\mathbb R$ with $v=\\operatorname{ess\\,sup}|V|<\\infty$. Put\n$$\\mathcal H=L^2(\\mathbb R^{3N};\\mathbb C^M),\\qquad Y=W^{2,2}(\\mathbb R^{3N};\\mathbb C^M)=H^2(\\mathbb R^{3N};\\mathbb C^M),$$\nwhere the vector space, pairing and Sobolev norm are the finite component sums of the scalar conventions of [[def-hilbert-space]], [[def-l-p-space-as-a-quotient-by-null-functions]] and [[def-sobolev-space-wkp-and-its-norm]]. Use the componentwise Plancherel unitary of [[thm-plancherel]], with the negative-sign $2\\pi$ convention of [[def-fourier-transform-on-l-one-of-rn]]. Define\n$$w(\\xi)=4\\pi^2a|\\xi|^2,\\qquad K=\\mathcal F_2^{-1}M_w\\mathcal F_2,\\qquad D(K)=\\{u:w\\mathcal F_2u\\in\\mathcal H\\}.$$\nThen $D(K)=Y$, and $Ku=-a\\Delta u$ for every $u\\in Y$, with the distributional Laplacian acting componentwise. The operator\n$$H=K+M_V=-a\\Delta+V,\\qquad D(H)=Y,$$\nis densely defined and self-adjoint on exactly $Y$, and $H\\ge-v$. Both $K$ and $H$ have graph norms equivalent to the stated Sobolev norm, and $C_c^\\infty(\\mathbb R^{3N};\\mathbb C^M)$ is a core for both. For $z=\\pm i\\mu$ with $\\mu>v$, there is the concrete two-sided inverse\n$$R_H(z)=(H-z)^{-1}=R_0(z)\\sum_{k\\ge0}(-M_VR_0(z))^k,\\qquad R_0(z)=\\mathcal F_2^{-1}M_{(w-z)^{-1}}\\mathcal F_2,$$\nwith range exactly $Y$ and $\\|R_H(z)\\|\\le(\\mu-v)^{-1}$.\n\nThis realizes the equal-mass bounded spatial operator used at fixed $N$ by setting $a=\\hbar^2/(2m)$ and any finite spin multiplicity $M$; for an $N$-fold spin-$s$ tensor the full multiplicity is $M=(2s+1)^N$. The lemma makes no statement about Coulomb potentials, unequal-mass operators, thermodynamic limits, or physical assignments. It uses no Axiom of Choice or Kato–Rellich theorem.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics, bounded perturbations of the free operator; concrete CC realization proved locally here",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-schroe/schroe.pdf"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "lem-nrqm-many-body-finite-spin-product-identification",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "title": "Finite spin components of an N-fold spatial tensor product",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "dependency_level": 4,
          "deps": [
            "def-sobolev-space-wkp-and-its-norm",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-euclidean-l2-product-unitary",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-hilbert-tensor-construction",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-bounded-tensor-maps",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-permutation-sector-projections",
            "lem-nrqm-kinematics-component-valued-wavefunction-identifications",
            "thm-nrqm-fock-and-equilibrium-permutation-restricted-self-adjointness",
            "def-countable-choice"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-sobolev-space-wkp-and-its-norm": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-euclidean-l2-product-unitary": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-hilbert-tensor-construction": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-bounded-tensor-maps": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-permutation-sector-projections": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-nrqm-kinematics-component-valued-wavefunction-identifications": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-nrqm-fock-and-equilibrium-permutation-restricted-self-adjointness": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "statement": "**Slot convention.** For $\\ell\\ge1$, $S_\\ell$ acts on $\\{0,\\dots,\\ell-1\\}$ as in [[lem-nrqm-composites-permutation-sector-projections]]. On one-based tuple positions use $\\widehat{\\pi}(k):=1+\\pi(k-1)$ for $1\\le k\\le\\ell$. Conjugation by $k\\mapsto k-1$ gives $\\widehat{\\pi\\sigma}=\\widehat{\\pi}\\circ\\widehat{\\sigma}$ and $\\widehat{\\pi^{-1}}=\\widehat{\\pi}^{-1}$; thus the supplier's tensor action becomes $U_\\pi(v_1\\otimes\\cdots\\otimes v_\\ell)=v_{\\widehat{\\pi}^{-1}(1)}\\otimes\\cdots\\otimes v_{\\widehat{\\pi}^{-1}(\\ell)}$. The parameters of $U_\\pi$ and $\\operatorname{sgn}(\\pi)$ remain canonical zero-based permutations.\n\nAssume Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $N,r\\ge1$ be integers, $H=L^2(\\mathbb R^3;\\mathbb C^r)$, $\\mathcal S_N=(\\mathbb C^r)^{\\otimes N}$, and $M=r^N$. In the product basis $e_a=e_{a_1}\\otimes\\cdots\\otimes e_{a_N}$ indexed by $a\\in\\{1,\\dots,r\\}^N$, identify $\\mathcal S_N$ with $\\mathbb C^M$ and write $\\mathcal L_N=L^2(\\mathbb R^{3N};\\mathbb C^M)$. Then:\n\n(a) There is a unique unitary $\\Theta_N:H^{\\otimes N}\\to\\mathcal L_N$ such that\n$$[\\Theta_N(f_1\\otimes\\cdots\\otimes f_N)]_a(x_1,\\dots,x_N)=\\prod_{j=1}^N[f_j(x_j)]_{a_j}.$$\n\n(b) For $\\pi\\in S_N$, let $U_\\pi$ be the permutation of the complete one-particle factors and $R_\\pi e_a=e_{a_{\\widehat{\\pi}^{-1}(1)}}\\otimes\\cdots\\otimes e_{a_{\\widehat{\\pi}^{-1}(N)}}$ the permutation of spin factors. With $X^\\pi=(x_{\\widehat{\\pi}(1)},\\dots,x_{\\widehat{\\pi}(N)})$, the conjugate permutation is\n$$\\mathcal U_\\pi:=\\Theta_NU_\\pi\\Theta_N^{-1},\\qquad (\\mathcal U_\\pi\\Psi)(X)=R_\\pi\\Psi(X^\\pi).$$\nIn particular $[\\mathcal U_\\pi\\Psi]_a(X)=\\Psi_{(a_{\\widehat{\\pi}(1)},\\dots,a_{\\widehat{\\pi}(N)})}(X^\\pi)$; averaging this combined action gives $\\mathcal P_\\pm=\\Theta_NP_\\pm^{(N)}\\Theta_N^{-1}$.\n\n(c) The component domain $\\mathcal D_N=W^{2,2}(\\mathbb R^{3N};\\mathbb C^M)$ is the set of tuples with every scalar component in $W^{2,2}(\\mathbb R^{3N};\\mathbb C)$. If a scalar self-adjoint $T$ has this scalar domain and its domain is preserved by every spatial block permutation, commuting with that permutation on the domain, its finite direct sum $T_M\\Psi=(T\\Psi_a)_a$ on $\\mathcal D_N$ is self-adjoint, retains every scalar lower bound $T\\ge cI$, and commutes with the combined permutations on that domain. The restrictions of $T_M$ to $\\operatorname{ran}\\mathcal P_\\pm$, with domain $\\mathcal D_N\\cap\\operatorname{ran}\\mathcal P_\\pm$, are self-adjoint when the sector is nonzero; on the zero sector the unique zero operator has domain $\\{0\\}$.\n\n(d) For matrices $A_j\\in\\mathcal B(\\mathbb C^r)$, the constant spin action $A_1\\otimes\\cdots\\otimes A_N$ preserves $\\mathcal D_N$ and commutes with $T_M$. Its permutation covariance is\n$$R_\\pi(A_1\\otimes\\cdots\\otimes A_N)R_\\pi^{-1}=A_{\\widehat{\\pi}^{-1}(1)}\\otimes\\cdots\\otimes A_{\\widehat{\\pi}^{-1}(N)}.$$\nThus a common internal unitary $A^{\\otimes N}$ commutes with $\\mathcal U_\\pi$, preserves both sectors and commutes with their restricted operators. This is a tensor identity and asserts no physical spin-statistics assignment. For $r=1$ all spin actions are scalar and $\\Theta_N$ is the iterated scalar product unitary; for $N=1$ it is the identity component identification.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "G. Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics, Section 1.4 (finite tensor products and orthogonal sums); local derivation from the declared suppliers",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-schroe/schroe.pdf"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "lem-nrqm-many-body-fixed-n-countable-mode-partition-criterion",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "title": "Fixed-particle-number occupation bases and the countable-mode partition criterion",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "dependency_level": 4,
          "deps": [
            "lem-finite-rank-operators-are-compact",
            "thm-norm-limit-of-compact-operators-is-compact",
            "thm-cauchy-schwarz-in-an-inner-product-space",
