            "thm-nrqm-identical-particles-occupation-number-basis": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-parseval-equivalences-for-a-complete-orthonormal-family": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-adjoint-of-a-densely-defined-unbounded-operator": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-symmetric-self-adjoint-and-essentially-self-adjoint": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-projection-valued-measure": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-bounded-borel-pvm-integral": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-nuclear-series-characterizes-trace-norm": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-trace-is-absolutely-convergent-and-basis-independent": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-unbounded-integral-against-a-pvm": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-unbounded-pvm-integral-is-well-defined-and-closed": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "statement": "**Slot convention.** For $\\ell\\ge1$, $S_\\ell$ acts on $\\{0,\\dots,\\ell-1\\}$ as in [[lem-nrqm-composites-permutation-sector-projections]]. On one-based tuple positions use $\\widehat{\\pi}(k):=1+\\pi(k-1)$ for $1\\le k\\le\\ell$. Conjugation by $k\\mapsto k-1$ gives $\\widehat{\\pi\\sigma}=\\widehat{\\pi}\\circ\\widehat{\\sigma}$ and $\\widehat{\\pi^{-1}}=\\widehat{\\pi}^{-1}$; thus the supplier's tensor action becomes $U_\\pi(v_1\\otimes\\cdots\\otimes v_\\ell)=v_{\\widehat{\\pi}^{-1}(1)}\\otimes\\cdots\\otimes v_{\\widehat{\\pi}^{-1}(\\ell)}$. The parameters of $U_\\pi$ and $\\operatorname{sgn}(\\pi)$ remain canonical zero-based permutations.\n\nAssume Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $H$ be a complex Hilbert space with a supplied countably infinite orthonormal basis $(e_j)_{j\\ge1}$, let $N\\ge1$ be an integer, and let $\\varepsilon_j\\in\\mathbb R$ with $\\varepsilon_j\\ge b$ for a fixed $b\\in\\mathbb R$. Use the completed tensor power and permutation-sector projections of [[lem-nrqm-composites-hilbert-tensor-construction]] and [[lem-nrqm-composites-permutation-sector-projections]], and write $\\mathfrak H_N^\\sigma:=\\operatorname{ran}P_\\sigma^{(N)}$ for $\\sigma\\in\\{+,-\\}$. Then:\n\n(a) For every finitely supported sequence $n=(n_j)_{j\\ge1}$ of nonnegative integers with $\\sum_jn_j=N$, put $\\operatorname{orb}(n):=\\{(i_1,\\ldots,i_N):\\#\\{k:i_k=j\\}=n_j\\text{ for every }j\\}$ and\n$$b_n^+:=|\\operatorname{orb}(n)|^{-1/2}\\sum_{i\\in\\operatorname{orb}(n)}e_{i_1}\\otimes\\cdots\\otimes e_{i_N}.$$\nFor every $N$-element subset $J=\\{j_1<\\cdots<j_N\\}$ of the positive integers, put\n$$b_J^-:=\\frac1{\\sqrt{N!}}\\sum_{\\pi\\in S_N}\\operatorname{sgn}(\\pi)e_{j_{\\widehat{\\pi}(1)}}\\otimes\\cdots\\otimes e_{j_{\\widehat{\\pi}(N)}}.$$\nThese are orthonormal bases of the symmetric and antisymmetric sectors respectively. Denote their countable index sets by $\\mathcal C_N^+$ and $\\mathcal C_N^-$, and write $b_c^\\sigma$ for the corresponding vector. Define $E_n:=\\sum_jn_j\\varepsilon_j$ and $E_J:=\\sum_{j\\in J}\\varepsilon_j$.\n\n(b) The fixed-$N$ free energy operator is the self-adjoint diagonal operator\n$$D(H_N^\\sigma):=\\left\\{\\psi=\\sum_{c\\in\\mathcal C_N^\\sigma}a_cb_c^\\sigma:\\sum_c|E_c|^2|a_c|^2<\\infty\\right\\},\\qquad H_N^\\sigma\\psi:=\\sum_cE_ca_cb_c^\\sigma.$$\nIt is bounded below by $Nb$, and is the closure of its action on finite occupation sums. On elementary tensors of modes it agrees with the restriction of the labelled energy sum $\\sum_{k=1}^N\\varepsilon_{i_k}$, with the same diagonal-domain closure. Its spectral PVM is\n$$E_N^\\sigma(B)\\psi=\\sum_c\\mathbf1_B(E_c)a_cb_c^\\sigma.$$\n\n(c) For $\\beta>0$, let $q_j:=e^{-\\beta\\varepsilon_j}>0$, so $q_j\\le e^{-\\beta b}$. Define the extended positive trace of a bounded positive operator as its nonnegative diagonal sum in the supplied occupation basis; its independence of any other supplied orthonormal basis is proved below. With this trace (allowed to be $+\\infty$),\n$$Z_N^+(\\beta):=\\operatorname{Tr}e^{-\\beta H_N^+}=h_N(q):=\\sum_{1\\le i_1\\le\\cdots\\le i_N}q_{i_1}\\cdots q_{i_N},$$\n$$Z_N^-(\\beta):=\\operatorname{Tr}e^{-\\beta H_N^-}=e_N(q):=\\sum_{1\\le i_1<\\cdots<i_N}q_{i_1}\\cdots q_{i_N}.$$\nAll sums are nonnegative-series sums. For either sign,\n$$\\left(\\prod_{k=1}^{N-1}q_k\\right)\\sum_{j=N}^\\infty q_j\\le Z_N^\\sigma(\\beta)\\le\\left(\\sum_{j=1}^\\infty q_j\\right)^N.$$\nFor $N=1$ the product is $1$, the tail starts at $1$, and both partition sums equal $\\sum_jq_j$. Consequently, for every fixed $N\\ge1$ and either statistics,\n$$0<Z_N^\\sigma(\\beta)<\\infty\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\sum_j e^{-\\beta\\varepsilon_j}<\\infty.$$\nThe bounded positive operator $e^{-\\beta H_N^\\sigma}$ is trace class exactly in this case, and its ordinary trace then equals the displayed occupation sum. This is a fixed-$N$ criterion, not a trace over all particle numbers.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "F. H. L. Essler, Advanced Quantum Theory, Chapter 1: finite occupation configurations; the countable fixed-N extension and trace bounds are proved locally here",
                "url": "http://www-thphys.physics.ox.ac.uk/courses/C6/C6_2017/C6Notes/lecturenotes2017AQT.pdf"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
