            "proof": "not-applicable"
          },
          "physical_scope": "The adopted radiation extension of the non-relativistic quantum framework: a fixed propagation-mode one-photon polarisation model with a two-dimensional transverse internal space, and a quantised free transverse radiation sector with bosonic Fock space and the mode assignments omega=c|k|, photon energy E=hbar*omega and photon momentum p=hbar*k in a declared inertial laboratory chart. The extension is an explicitly adopted model assumption; it is not derived from classical Maxwell theory, from special relativity, or from the massive-particle model by a mass-to-zero limit, and no Lorentz transformation law for the mode labels and no Galilean covariance of the radiation sector are claimed. Detection, coupling to matter and spontaneous emission are not supplied by this postulate.",
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "J. Binney and D. Skinner, The Physics of Quantum Mechanics, Section 1.3.6 printed pages 14-15 (PDF pages 22-23): photon polarisation, the two transverse states, individual photons transmitted or absorbed, and the agreement of the transmitted fraction cos^2(theta) with the classical Malus law",
                "url": "https://www-thphys.physics.ox.ac.uk/people/JamesBinney/qb.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "B. Zwiebach, MIT 8.05 Quantum Physics II (Fall 2013), Chapter 6 'Quantum Dynamics', Section 5.3 printed pages 48-50: a single electromagnetic field mode, its field amplitudes q and p, the oscillator Hamiltonian, photon number and energy hbar*omega, and the classical standing-wave expectation of a coherent state",
                "url": "https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/8-05-quantum-physics-ii-fall-2013/79a8091ef4f18d8e3ff76a097e8db33c_MIT8_05F13_Chap_06.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "Robert G. Littlejohn, Physics 221B 2021-22 Notes 41, The Quantized Electromagnetic Field, Section 7, equations (21)-(33), printed pages 8-10: for the free field, derives the normal-ordered momentum operator P=sum_lambda hbar*k*a_lambda^dagger*a_lambda and reads occupation-number states as carrying the corresponding photon momentum hbar*k; the derivation uses Gaussian units, Coulomb gauge and box normalization",
                "url": "https://bohr.physics.berkeley.edu/classes/221/notes/quantemf.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "S. Pratt, Lecture Notes on Quantum Mechanics (Michigan State University, PHY 851/852; retrieved via the Internet Archive snapshot of 2024-04-21), Chapter 9 Section 9.2 printed pages 135-138: creation and destruction operators in coordinate space, the field operator expansion and the energy of free modes",
                "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20240421090356/https://web.pa.msu.edu/people/pratts/phy851/lectures/lectures_full.pdf"
              },
              {
