          "physical_scope": "The declared ideal detection models of the radiation sector: the ideal total-number counting model with the Fock sector projections as outcome structure and the Born law of P2, the ideal energy-window model with the spectral projections of the free-field energy, and the polarisation analyser of the fixed-mode model. The declaration fixes vocabulary only; it asserts no laboratory counter, no absorption instrument, no efficiency, no dark counts, no dead time, no background, no calibration and no sampling model, and repeated trials require a separately declared statistical model.",
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "J. Binney and D. Skinner, The Physics of Quantum Mechanics, Section 1.3.6 printed pages 14-15 (PDF pages 22-23): individual photons either passing or being absorbed by an analyser, read as the outcome structure of an idealised polarisation measurement",
                "url": "https://www-thphys.physics.ox.ac.uk/people/JamesBinney/qb.pdf"
              },
