          "physical_scope": "The adopted assumption that a preparation described as a declared finite-level model in its upper level with no quanta in the declared transverse radiation sector is represented by the ray of v_a tensor Omega and evolves under the declared cutoff dipole model, together with the model reading of vacuum-initiated emission as the model's one-photon projection probability, and the explicit absence of any environment, thermal radiation, extra modes, detector or rate law from the postulate. The postulate is an adopted model assumption: it is not derived, and it asserts no measured emission, lifetime, linewidth or rate.",
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "J. Binney and D. Skinner, The Physics of Quantum Mechanics, Box 9.2 printed page 218 (PDF page 226): spontaneous emission as emission stimulated by the zero-point energy, the explicit statement that the classical treatment of the field omits it, and Einstein's A/B relation as an added argument rather than a deduction of the spontaneous rate",
                "url": "https://www-thphys.physics.ox.ac.uk/people/JamesBinney/qb.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "S. Pratt, Lecture Notes on Quantum Mechanics (Michigan State University, PHY 851/852; Internet Archive snapshot of 2024-04-21), Chapter 14 Section 14.3 printed page 221: a classical current coupled to the field radiates coherent states and is unaffected by the emission, in contrast to an atom that changes state when it emits",
                "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20240421090356/https://web.pa.msu.edu/people/pratts/phy851/lectures/lectures_full.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "D. Tong, Quantum Mechanics (author-hosted lecture set), Section 4.4.2 printed pages 119-122 (PDF pages 122-125): coupling to radiation and energy transfer as separately scoped extensions, and the photon energy relation as extra input",
                "url": "https://davidtong.org/pdfs/teaching/quantum-mechanics/qm.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "dependency_level": 16
        },
        {
          "id": "pthm-nrqm-light-matter-first-order-emission-and-absorption-coefficients",
          "kind": "physics-theorem",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "First-order emission and absorption amplitudes of the cutoff dipole model, and the exact model probability of the one-photon level-b projection up to the Dyson tail",
          "statement": "Adopt the model of\n[[def-nrqm-light-matter-framework-finite-level-coupled-model]] with its data\n$d$, $H_{a}$, $D_j^{\\mathrm{ch}}$, $\\Lambda$, $g_{j}$, $\\eta_{0}$, and a declared upward\nlevel pair $(a,b)$ with transition energy $\\Delta=E_{a}-E_{b}>0$ and page\ncoefficients $c_{j}=\\langle D_j^{\\mathrm{ch}}v_{a},v_{b}\\rangle$, mode vector $M$ and\nphoton density $\\nu_{b}$ of\n[[def-nrqm-light-matter-framework-spectral-transition-and-detection]] clauses\n(b),(c). Write $H_{0}:=H_{a}\\otimes I+I\\otimes H_{f}$ and\n$B:=\\eta_{0}\\sum_{j}D_j^{\\mathrm{ch}}\\otimes\\phi(g_{j})$, so that $H_{\\mathrm{LM}}=H_{0}+B$\non $\\mathbb C^{d}\\otimes D(H_{f})$. Assume the Axioms of Countable Choice and\nof Choice ([[def-countable-choice]], [[def-axiom-of-choice]]). Fix $T>0$,\nput\n$$C:=\\frac{2}{\\hbar}\\sum_{j=1}^{J}\\|D_j^{\\mathrm{ch}}\\|\\,\\|g_{j}\\|_{\\mathfrak h}, \\qquad \\varepsilon_{2}(t):=\\sum_{n\\ge2}\\frac{(|\\eta_{0}|Ct)^{n}}{\\sqrt{n!}}\\qquad(0\\le t\\le T),$$\nand let $\\Psi_{0}:=v_{a}\\otimes\\Omega$. For $t\\ge0$ let $\\Psi_{1}(t)$ denote the\nfirst interaction-picture Dyson term of the model with initial vector\n$\\Psi_{0}$, as in\n[[thm-nrqm-fock-and-equilibrium-vacuum-emission-dyson-convergence]] clause (b).\nThen:\n\n(a) (single-vertex emission vector) the component of $\\Psi_{1}(t)$ in the\none-photon sector at level $b$ is\n$$v_{b}\\otimes A_{b}(\\cdot,t),$$\nwith $A_{b}(\\cdot,t)$ the single-vertex emission vector of\n[[def-nrqm-light-matter-framework-spectral-transition-and-detection]] clause\n(d) and\n[[lem-nrqm-light-matter-first-order-photon-energy-law]]; consequently the\nsingle-vertex emission coefficient of the model is\n$$\\gamma_{b}(t)=\\eta_{0}^{2}\\,t\\int_{\\mathbb R}K_{t}(E-\\Delta)\\,d\\nu_{b}(E) \\qquad(t>0);$$\n\n(b) (exact model probability up to the Dyson tail) let\n$Q_{b}:=|v_{b}\\rangle\\langle v_{b}|\\otimes\\Pi_{1}$ and let\n$$p_{b}(t):=\\|Q_{b}\\,e^{-itH_{\\mathrm{LM}}/\\hbar}\\Psi_{0}\\|^{2}$$\nbe the model's probability of the spectral value $1$ of the assigned sharp\nobservable $(Q_{b},1)$ in the evolved preparation of $\\Psi_{0}$ at time $t$\n(the reading of P2, [[post-nrqm-framework-observable-and-probability]],\n[[def-nrqm-observables-framework-observable-and-outcome-law]]). Then for\n$0\\le t\\le T$,\n$$\\bigl|p_{b}(t)-\\gamma_{b}(t)\\bigr|\\le \\varepsilon_{2}(t)\\bigl(2\\|A_{b}(\\cdot,t)\\|_{\\mathfrak h}+\\varepsilon_{2}(t)\\bigr);$$\nin particular the exact probability equals the single-vertex coefficient up to\nthe explicit Dyson tail, which is not asserted to be small;\n\n(c) (absorption mirror) let $g\\in\\mathfrak h$ be a unit vector, let\n$\\Psi_1^g(t)$ be the first interaction-picture Dyson term with initial\nvector $\\Phi_0=v_b\\otimes g$, defined as a norm integral using the\nfinite-photon-sector creation/contraction action, and define the physical\ntransition amplitudes with the output vector in the first slot,\n$$\\alpha_{\\mathrm{em}}(t):=\\langle\\Psi_1(t),v_b\\otimes g\\rangle,\\qquad \\alpha_{\\mathrm{abs}}(t):=\\langle\\Psi_1^g(t),v_a\\otimes\\Omega\\rangle.$$\nThen for every $t\\ge0$,\n$$\\alpha_{\\mathrm{em}}(t)=-\\frac{i\\eta_0}{\\hbar}\\int_0^te^{-i\\Delta s/\\hbar}\\langle M,e^{-is\\varepsilon/\\hbar}g\\rangle_{\\mathfrak h}\\,ds,\\qquad \\alpha_{\\mathrm{abs}}(t)=-\\frac{i\\eta_0}{\\hbar}\\int_0^te^{+i\\Delta s/\\hbar}\\overline{\\langle M,e^{-is\\varepsilon/\\hbar}g\\rangle_{\\mathfrak h}}\\,ds,$$\nand hence\n$$\\alpha_{\\mathrm{abs}}(t)=-\\overline{\\alpha_{\\mathrm{em}}(t)},\\qquad |\\alpha_{\\mathrm{abs}}(t)|=|\\alpha_{\\mathrm{em}}(t)|.$$\nThis compares the reverse transitions for the same level pair, the same\nunit one-photon vector $g$ and the same real coupling $\\eta_0$, retaining\narbitrary complex Hermitian dipole matrices and transverse mode vectors;\n\n(d) (scope) clauses (a)-(c) are statements about the model's first-order Dyson\nterms and about one projection probability of the exact model evolution. No\nrate, exponential decay, linewidth, environment, sampling model or measurement\nrecord is asserted; the identification of a laboratory preparation with\n$\\Psi_{0}$ and of a laboratory detector with the observable $Q_{b}$ is a tested\nidentification with uncertainty under P7\n([[post-nrqm-framework-preparation-and-apparatus]]); and no value of\n$\\eta_{0}$, $D_j^{\\mathrm{ch}}$, $g_{j}$ or $\\Lambda$ is asserted.",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "deps": [
            "def-nrqm-light-matter-framework-finite-level-coupled-model",
