        {
          "id": "def-oriented-minkowski-volume-form",
          "kind": "definition",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "The oriented volume form epsilon and the permutation symbols of an inertial frame",
          "statement": "Let (A,V,eta,C^+) be an oriented time-oriented affine Minkowski space and let (o;e_0,...,e_3) be an inertial frame. For v_0,...,v_3 in V let [v_j^a] be the 4x4 matrix whose j-th column lists the coordinates of v_j in the ordered basis (e_0,...,e_3), and define epsilon(v_0,v_1,v_2,v_3) := det([v_j^a]) in the sense of the determinant of a square matrix. Then epsilon is an alternating 4-linear form on V, called the oriented volume form of the model. Its components in the inertial frame are the permutation symbols epsilon_{abcd}, with epsilon_{0123} = +1 and epsilon_{abcd} the sign of the permutation taking (0,1,2,3) to (a,b,c,d) (zero if two indices repeat). The raised components are epsilon^{abcd} := eta^{aa'} eta^{bb'} eta^{cc'} eta^{dd'} epsilon_{a'b'c'd'}, where eta^{ab} is the inverse of the matrix eta_{ab}; epsilon^{0123} = -1. The spatial permutation symbol epsilon_{ijk} for i,j,k in {1,2,3} is defined by epsilon_{123} = +1 together with alternation.",
          "strategy": "epsilon is the determinant of the coordinate matrix of (v_0,...,v_3); the determinant is multilinear and alternating in the columns, hence epsilon is an alternating 4-linear form. Its components in the frame are by definition the determinant values, i.e. the permutation-sign symbols; epsilon^{0123} computes to eta^{00}eta^{11}eta^{22}eta^{33} epsilon_{0123} = (-1)(+1)(+1)(+1)(+1) = -1 because the inverse metric is diagonal in an eta-orthonormal frame. Well-definedness of epsilon as a form of the model, independent of the inertial frame used, is proved in the frame-independence lemma.",
          "deps": [
            "def-inertial-frame-and-inertial-chart",
            "def-determinant-of-a-square-matrix",
            "def-alternating-k-linear-map",
            "def-lorentz-form-and-inertia",
            "thm-determinant-is-the-unique-normalized-alternating-multilinear-function"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-inertial-frame-and-inertial-chart": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-determinant-of-a-square-matrix": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-alternating-k-linear-map": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-lorentz-form-and-inertia": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-determinant-is-the-unique-normalized-alternating-multilinear-function": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "justified_by": [
            "lem-volume-form-is-independent-of-the-oriented-frame"
          ],
          "provenance": {
