          "dependency_level": 5
        },
        {
          "id": "lem-volume-form-is-independent-of-the-oriented-frame",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "The oriented volume form is independent of the positively oriented inertial frame",
          "statement": "The alternating $4$-linear form $\\epsilon$ of\n[[def-oriented-minkowski-volume-form]] does not depend on the inertial frame\nused to define it. Explicitly, if $(e_0,e_1,e_2,e_3)$ and\n$(e'_0,e'_1,e'_2,e'_3)$ are inertial frames with\n$e'_a=\\sum_bM^b_ae_b$ for the change-of-basis matrix $M$, then $\\det M=+1$\n(both ordered bases are positively oriented), and the coordinate matrices $X$,\n$X'$ of any tuple $(v_0,v_1,v_2,v_3)$ in the two frames satisfy $X'=M^{-1}X$,\nso that $\\det X'=\\det(M^{-1})\\det X=\\det X$. Consequently\n$\\epsilon(e_0,e_1,e_2,e_3)=1$ for every inertial frame, $\\epsilon$ is the unique\nalternating $4$-linear form on $V$ taking the value $1$ on every positively\noriented $\\eta$-orthonormal ordered basis, and in every inertial frame the\nraised component $\\epsilon^{0123}$ equals $-1$.",
          "strategy": "From eta(e'_a,e'_b) = eta_{ab} and e'_a = sum_b M^b_a e_b one gets the matrix identity M^T eta M = eta; taking determinants and using det eta = -1 gives (det M)^2 = 1, so det M = +1 or -1, and the orientation clause selects det M = +1. The coordinate columns of a fixed tuple in the two bases are related by X' = M^{-1} X, so multiplicativity of the determinant and det(M^{-1}) = (det M)^{-1} give det X' = det X; this is exactly the frame independence, and it also shows the normalized value 1 on the frame itself. Uniqueness of the normalized alternating 4-linear form is the uniqueness clause for the determinant as a normalized alternating multilinear function, transported to V by the coordinate isomorphism E. The raised component computation is the diagonal evaluation given in the definition.",
          "deps": [
            "def-oriented-minkowski-volume-form",
            "thm-determinant-multiplicative",
            "cor-determinant-of-an-inverse",
            "thm-determinant-is-the-unique-normalized-alternating-multilinear-function",
            "thm-determinant-sign-detects-orientation-change",
            "def-lorentz-form-and-inertia",
            "def-inertial-frame-and-inertial-chart",
            "lem-lorentz-form-has-orthonormal-basis",
            "def-orientation-of-a-finite-dimensional-real-vector-space",
            "def-alternating-k-linear-map",
            "def-determinant-of-a-square-matrix"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
