          "dependency_level": 8
        },
        {
          "id": "lem-rapidity-parametrization-of-collinear-boosts",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Rapidity parametrization of collinear boosts",
          "statement": "For $\\beta\\in(-1,1)$ define\n$r(\\beta):=\\tfrac12\\log\\!\\Bigl(\\dfrac{1+\\beta}{1-\\beta}\\Bigr)$, where $\\log$ is\nthe natural logarithm ([[def-natural-logarithm]]); the argument is positive\nbecause $1+\\beta>0$ and $1-\\beta>0$. Then $r$ is a strictly increasing\nbijection of $(-1,1)$ onto $\\mathbb R$. Writing\n$\\sinh(r):=(e^r-e^{-r})/2$, $\\cosh(r):=(e^r+e^{-r})/2$ and\n$\\tanh(r):=\\sinh(r)/\\cosh(r)$ ([[def-real-exponential-function-and-e]]), one\nhas $\\cosh^2(r)-\\sinh^2(r)=1$, where\n$e^x:=\\exp(x)$ for real $x$,\n$\\beta=\\tanh(r(\\beta))$,\n$(1-\\tanh(r)^2)^{-1/2}=\\cosh(r)$, and\n$\\sinh(r)=\\tanh(r)\\cosh(r)=\\beta\\gamma(\\beta)$ at $\\beta=\\tanh(r)$.\nConsequently, for every unit spatial vector $e$ the passive boost acts, in the\nordered pair of directions $(e_0,e)$, as the $2\\times2$ matrix\n$\\begin{pmatrix}\\cosh r&-\\sinh r\\\\ -\\sinh r&\\cosh r\\end{pmatrix}$ and as the\nidentity on the perpendicular complement of the plane\n$\\operatorname{span}(e_0,e)$. Finally, collinear rapidities add: for all\n$r,s\\in\\mathbb R$,\n$B(\\tanh(r)e)\\,B(\\tanh(s)e)=B(\\tanh(r+s)e)$, consistent with\n[[lem-collinear-boost-composition-and-velocity-addition]].",
          "strategy": "Proof plan. (a) r is strictly increasing on (-1,1): the map beta |-> (1 + beta)/(1 - beta) has positive derivative 2/(1 - beta)^2 and log is strictly increasing (def-natural-logarithm is the inverse of the strictly increasing exp, thm-exponential-is-strictly-increasing); the limits are -infinity and +infinity, so r is onto R by the intermediate value property. (b) beta = tanh(r(beta)): let q := e^(2r) = (1 + beta)/(1 - beta), then tanh(r) = (q - 1)/(q + 1) = beta by elementary algebra of the exponential. (c) Setting beta = tanh(r), the identity 1 - tanh^2 r = 1/cosh^2 r follows from cosh^2 r - sinh^2 r = 1 (itself an expansion using the exponential addition formula thm-exponential-addition-formula); since cosh r > 0, (1 - tanh^2 r)^(-1/2) = cosh r, and gamma(tanh r) = cosh r, sinh r = tanh r cosh r. (d) The matrix display is the definition of B(beta) evaluated at beta = tanh r, using gamma = cosh r and gamma beta = sinh r: [[gamma,-gamma beta],[-gamma beta,gamma]] = [[cosh r,-sinh r],[-sinh r,cosh r]]. (e) Finally the composition statement follows either from the matrix product with the addition formulas for sinh and cosh or from the composition lemma together with the addition law of the exponential; the two routes agree. The exponential presentation exp(r N_e) of the same matrix is supplied separately in lem-lorentz-exponential-map-and-rapidity, which depends on this item, so that this item does not presuppose the exponential series for matrices.",
          "deps": [
            "def-lorentz-boost",
            "lem-collinear-boost-composition-and-velocity-addition",
            "lem-boost-is-proper-orthochronous-with-inverse",
            "def-real-exponential-function-and-e",
            "thm-exponential-addition-formula",
            "cor-exponential-is-a-bijection-onto-positive-reals",
