        {
          "id": "lem-sr-piecewise-proper-time-reparametrization-invariance",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Proper time is invariant under regular increasing weak piecewise changes of parameter",
          "statement": "Let c>0 and let x:[a,b]->A be a weak piecewise C^1 future timelike worldline. Let phi:[u,v]->[a,b] be an increasing continuous surjection, C^1 on the open pieces of a finite partition, with phi'>0 at every interior smooth point and finite positive one-sided difference-quotient derivatives at both endpoints of each piece. Then phi is strictly increasing with continuous inverse, y=x composed with phi is a weak piecewise C^1 future timelike worldline, and Delta tau_[u,v](y)=Delta tau_[a,b](x). The same equality holds for every pair of corresponding restricted parameter intervals; based proper-time functions differ only by their base-point constant. The relevant partition is the common refinement of phi's partition and the inverse images of x's partition points. This statement gives worldline/clock consequences only for positive derivatives, including all one-sided endpoint derivatives. It leaves intact the separate global-C^1 curve-integral identities allowing zero tangents in lem-sr-proper-time-reparametrization-invariance; a zero-tangent composition is not asserted to be a worldline.",
          "strategy": "On each closed piece phi is continuous and differentiable inside with phi'>0, so the mean value theorem proves strict increase there; finite concatenation gives global strict increase, and the continuous monotone bijection has continuous inverse. The finite inverse-image refinement separates all x and phi corners. Inside each refined piece componentwise chain rule gives y'=phi' x'(phi), so y' is continuous and future timelike and sqrt(-eta(y',y'))=phi' f(phi), where f=sqrt(-eta(x',x')). At each one-sided endpoint the quotient of y is the product of the corresponding quotient of x and that of phi; strict monotonicity chooses the correct side and both finite limits exist, the latter positive. Thus y has finite future timelike one-sided tangents and lies in the same weak class. On any compact interior truncation [r,s] of a refined piece, f is continuous on the compact image interval and phi' is continuous and integrable on [r,s]; thm-substitution gives integral_r^s phi' f(phi)=integral_phi(r)^phi(s) f. As r and s approach the refined endpoints, continuity and strict monotonicity of phi make the image endpoints approach the corresponding x endpoints. Both improper limits exist by lem-sr-weak-piecewise-causal-integrability for x and y, so the identity passes to the limits. Finite summation and partition independence give the full and restricted interval identities. Oriented additivity gives the based-function constant. No boundedness of the derivative near a corner is assumed and no zero tangent is admitted as a worldline.",
          "deps": [
            "def-sr-piecewise-proper-time",
            "lem-sr-weak-piecewise-causal-integrability",
            "def-sr-regular-causal-curve-and-worldline",
            "def-inertial-frame-and-inertial-chart",
