        {
          "id": "ex-sr-observer-split-worked",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Worked example: splitting a four-velocity in an observer's rest frame",
          "statement": "Worked computation. In an inertial chart with eta_0 = diag(-1,1,1,1) let the observer be n = e_0 = (1,0,0,0) and let u = (5/4, 3/4, 0, 0), a future unit timelike vector: eta(u,u) = -25/16 + 9/16 = -1. Then gamma = -eta(n,u) = 5/4 >= 1, h(u) = u + eta(n,u) n = u - (5/4)(1,0,0,0) = (0, 3/4, 0, 0) lies in n^perp = span(e_1,e_2,e_3), and the relative velocity is w = c h(u)/gamma = (0, 3c/5, 0, 0). One checks u = gamma (n + w/c) = (5/4)(1, 3/5, 0, 0) and |w|^2 = 9c^2/25 = c^2 (1 - gamma^{-2}) = c^2 (1 - 16/25). Also h(h(u)) = h(u) and eta(n,h(u)) = 0. This four-velocity is the one of the clock with coordinate velocity (3c/5, 0, 0) in ex-sr-proper-time-of-a-straight-worldline.",
          "strategy": "Direct evaluation of clauses (c) and (d) of thm-sr-proper-time-and-observer-decomposition on the displayed vectors: the projection, its idempotence and its orthogonality to n, the split u = gamma(n + w/c) and the identity |w|^2 = c^2(1 - gamma^{-2}) are each finite computations with rational numbers.",
          "deps": [
            "thm-sr-proper-time-and-observer-decomposition",
            "def-sr-four-velocity-and-four-acceleration",
            "def-inertial-frame-and-inertial-chart",
