        {
          "id": "lem-sr-radar-midpoint-for-inertial-observer",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "The radar round trip of an inertial observer halves at the midpoint of the reception interval",
          "statement": "Let $n$ be a future unit timelike vector, $\\eta(n,n)=-1$ ([[def-causal-classification-of-lorentz-vectors]], [[def-time-orientation-and-future-causal-sets]]), let $o$ be an event, and let $\\lambda_-<\\lambda_+$ be real numbers; put $e_-:=o+\\lambda_-n$ and $e_+:=o+\\lambda_+n$ ([[def-sr-affine-minkowski-model]]). For an event $q$ the following are equivalent:\n\n(i) $q-e_-$ is future null and $e_+-q$ is future null;\n\n(ii) there is $u\\in n^\\perp$ with $|u|:=\\sqrt{\\eta(u,u)}=(\\lambda_+-\\lambda_-)/2$ such that $q=o+\\tfrac{\\lambda_-+\\lambda_+}{2}n+u$.\n\nIn that case $q-e_-=\\tfrac{\\lambda_+-\\lambda_-}{2}n+u$ and $e_+-q=\\tfrac{\\lambda_+-\\lambda_-}{2}n-u$, the affine midpoint $m:=o+\\tfrac{\\lambda_-+\\lambda_+}{2}n=\\tfrac{e_-+e_+}{2}$ satisfies $\\eta(n,q-m)=0$ (so $q$ lies in the slice $H(m,n)$) and $|q-m|=(\\lambda_+-\\lambda_-)/2$ ([[def-sr-simultaneity-slice-and-rest-distance]]). In particular for fixed $e_-,e_+$ all admissible reflection events $q$ have the same midpoint $m$ and the same rest distance $(\\lambda_+-\\lambda_-)/2$, and differ only in the direction $u$ of $n^\\perp$.",
          "strategy": "Decompose each null leg into its n component and horizontal part. Futurity gives two positive coefficients; their equal squared horizontal norm forces both coefficients to be half the reception interval. Conversely rho n plus/minus u are future null when rho>0 and |u|=rho. The affine midpoint and translated event witness m+rho e/|e| have the stated rest distance.",
          "deps": [
            "thm-sr-proper-time-and-observer-decomposition",
            "def-sr-affine-minkowski-model",
            "def-causal-classification-of-lorentz-vectors",
            "def-time-orientation-and-future-causal-sets",
            "def-lorentz-orthogonality-and-orthogonal-complement",
            "def-sr-simultaneity-slice-and-rest-distance"
          ],
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "B. Crowell, Special Relativity, revision 2020-12-10 (author-published undergraduate textbook, 246 PDF pages): Sections 1.1-1.3 pp. 12-28 (vector representation of observer motion, operational radar calibration, time dilation, length-contraction road-trip example), Sections 3.5 and 3.7 pp. 60-68 (four-velocity, acceleration, projection operator), Section 3.9.3 pp. 73-74 (local failure of accelerated simultaneity), Sections 7.1-7.3 pp. 147-151 (Rindler coordinates and nonuniform proper acceleration), Section 8.1 pp. 165-169 (rotating synchronization), Section 9.5 pp. 205-211 (congruences, expansion, Born rigidity); signature (+---) converted to (-+++) and c = 1 formulas converted to x^0 = c t",
                "url": "https://archive.org/download/sr_20220102/sr.pdf"
