        {
          "id": "thm-sr-local-congruence-adapted-charts-and-frobenius",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Local flow boxes, adapted charts and the Frobenius criterion for rest distributions",
          "statement": "Let $\\Omega$ be a nonempty open subset of $A$ ([[def-sr-affine-minkowski-model]]).\n\n**(i) Flow box.** If $X$ is a smooth vector field on $\\Omega$ ([[def-ck-tensor-field-on-minkowski-space]]) and $X(p)\\ne0$ at a point $p\\in\\Omega$, then there is an open neighbourhood $U$ of $p$ in $\\Omega$ and a chart $(u^0,u^1,u^2,u^3):U\\to\\mathbb R^4$ in which $X=\\partial/\\partial u^0$; the integral curves of $X$ in $U$ are therefore the $u^0$-coordinate lines up to reparametrization. In particular every observer congruence $n$ on $\\Omega$ ([[def-sr-chart-tetrad-and-congruence-distinction]]) admits a local $n$-adapted chart, and in such a chart $n=\\partial/\\partial u^0$.\n\n**(ii) Frobenius criterion.** For a smooth nowhere-zero one-form $\\alpha$ on $\\Omega$ ([[def-closed-and-exact-differential-forms]]) let $D:=\\ker\\alpha$ be the hyperplane distribution $D_p=\\{v\\in V:\\alpha_p(v)=0\\}$. Then $D$ is integrable on $\\Omega$ (through every point there passes a local hypersurface whose tangent space at each of its points is the corresponding $D_p$) if and only if $\\alpha\\wedge d\\alpha=0$ on $\\Omega$ ([[def-wedge-product-of-differential-forms]]).\n\n**(iii) Rest distributions of observer congruences.** Let $n$ be an observer congruence on $\\Omega$ ([[def-sr-chart-tetrad-and-congruence-distinction]]), let $\\alpha:=n^\\flat$, and let $\\theta,\\omega$ be its expansion and vorticity ([[def-sr-observer-congruence-and-kinematics]]). Then:\n\n(a) $d\\alpha=2\\nabla_{[a}n_{b]}$, that is, $d\\alpha(X,Y)=(\\nabla_Xn^\\flat)(Y)-(\\nabla_Yn^\\flat)(X)$ for smooth vector fields $X,Y$;\n\n(b) for every $p$ and all $X,Y$ with $\\alpha(X)=\\alpha(Y)=0$ one has $d\\alpha(X,Y)=2\\omega(X,Y)$; consequently $(\\alpha\\wedge d\\alpha)(p)=0$ if and only if $\\omega(p)=0$, and on an open set $U\\subseteq\\Omega$ the following are equivalent: $\\alpha\\wedge d\\alpha=0$ on $U$, $\\omega=0$ on $U$, and the rest distribution $\\ker\\alpha$ is integrable on $U$;\n\n(c) when the rest distribution is integrable on $U$, its integral hypersurfaces are orthogonal to $n$ at every point and the restriction of $\\eta$ to each of them is positive definite, so they are rest slices of the congruence.\n\n**(iv) Scope.** All statements are local on $\\Omega$; no global foliation, global synchronization, completeness or product structure is asserted, and no claim is made about variable-rank or non-smooth distributions.",
          "strategy": "(i) is the published flow-box theorem (thm-flow-box-theorem) applied on the manifold Omega, together with the identification of the integral curves with coordinate lines: in the chart X = partial/partial u^0, so the spatial coordinates are constant along the flow. (ii) is the published codimension-one Frobenius criterion (cor-codimension-one-frobenius-criterion) applied verbatim on the open subset of the smooth manifold A. (iii)(a) is the exterior-derivative identity d alpha(X,Y) = X(alpha(Y)) - Y(alpha(X)) - alpha([X,Y]) for a one-form (def-exterior-derivative-by-the-invariant-vector-field-formula) combined with the torsion-freeness nabla_X Y - nabla_Y X = [X,Y] of the flat connection (def-flat-covariant-derivative-on-affine-minkowski-space), giving d alpha_{ab} = nabla_a n_b - nabla_b n_a = 2 nabla_{[a}n_{b]}. (iii)(b) for horizontal X,Y the projections in omega_{ab} = h_a{}^c h_b{}^d nabla_{[c}n_{d]} act as the identity on horizontal arguments, so omega(X,Y) = (1/2) d alpha(X,Y); hence alpha wedge d alpha = 0 at a point (which means d alpha vanishes on all pairs of horizontal vectors there) is equivalent to omega = 0 there, and the integrability equivalence on an open set is (ii). (iii)(c) a leaf has tangent space ker alpha_p = n(p)^perp at each of its points, so it is orthogonal to n there, and the restriction of eta to n(p)^perp is positive definite by thm-sr-proper-time-and-observer-decomposition (c). All steps are local algebra plus the two cited theorems; no choice principle is used.",
          "deps": [
            "thm-flow-box-theorem",
            "cor-codimension-one-frobenius-criterion",
            "def-sr-affine-minkowski-model",
            "lem-affine-minkowski-charts-form-a-smooth-atlas",
            "def-sr-chart-tetrad-and-congruence-distinction",
            "def-flat-covariant-derivative-on-affine-minkowski-space",
            "def-sr-observer-congruence-and-kinematics",
            "def-ck-tensor-field-on-minkowski-space",
            "def-exterior-derivative-by-the-invariant-vector-field-formula",
            "def-wedge-product-of-differential-forms",
            "def-closed-and-exact-differential-forms",
            "thm-sr-proper-time-and-observer-decomposition",
            "def-lie-bracket-of-smooth-vector-fields",
            "prop-coordinate-formula-for-the-lie-bracket",
            "def-lorentz-orthogonality-and-orthogonal-complement"
          ],
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "D. Giulini, Algebraic and geometric structures of Special Relativity, arXiv:math-ph/0602018: Section 5.5 pp. 41-49 (Definition 7 and equation (123) of Born rigidity, equations (125)-(126), Proposition 14, Lemma 16, Theorem 15 part 1, Lemmas 17-18, Theorem 19 part 2); signature (+---) converted to (-+++)",
                "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/math-ph/0602018"
              },
