        {
          "id": "lem-sr-closed-one-form-primitive-on-simply-connected-open-sets",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "A closed 1-form on a simply connected open subset of the affine model has a primitive",
          "statement": "Let $(A,V,\\eta,C^+)$ be an oriented time-oriented affine Minkowski space ([[def-sr-affine-minkowski-model]]), let $U\\subseteq A$ be a nonempty open subset which, with the topology of [[lem-affine-minkowski-charts-form-a-smooth-atlas]], is path-connected and simply connected ([[def-simply-connected]]), and let $\\alpha$ be a $C^1$ one-form on $U$ with $d\\alpha=0$ ([[def-closed-and-exact-differential-forms]]); here closedness of a $C^1$ one-form means that in an inertial chart ([[def-inertial-frame-and-inertial-chart]]) one has $\\alpha=\\sum_{i=0}^3 a_i\\,dx^i$ with $\\partial_i a_j=\\partial_j a_i$, the exterior derivative being understood by this coefficient formula ([[def-exterior-derivative-by-the-invariant-vector-field-formula]], [[thm-local-coordinate-formula-for-the-exterior-derivative]]). Then:\n\n(a) there is a $C^2$ function $F:U\\to\\mathbb R$ with $dF=\\alpha$;\n\n(b) for any two piecewise-$C^1$ paths $\\gamma_0,\\gamma_1$ in $U$ ([[def-piecewise-c1-path-connected-conservative-and-path-independent]]) with the same endpoints, the integrals of $\\alpha$ along them are equal, and consequently the integral of $\\alpha$ along every piecewise-$C^1$ loop in $U$ vanishes.\n\nIf $\\alpha$ is smooth, $F$ may be taken smooth.\n\n**Conventions (what the objects mean here).** Fix one inertial chart $x:A\\to\\mathbb R^4$ and put $\\Omega:=x(U)\\subseteq\\mathbb R^4$; by [[lem-affine-minkowski-charts-form-a-smooth-atlas]] the chart $x$ is a diffeomorphism of $A$ onto $\\mathbb R^4$ carrying the model's topology, and every other inertial chart $x'$ satisfies $x'=M^{-1}(x-b)$ for an invertible matrix $M$ and a vector $b$. The $C^1$ one-form $\\alpha$ is represented in the chart as $\\alpha=\\sum_{i=0}^3 a_i\\,dx^i$ with coefficient functions $a_i:\\Omega\\to\\mathbb R$ of class $C^1$; write $A:=(a_0,a_1,a_2,a_3):\\Omega\\to\\mathbb R^4$ for the coefficient field, so that $A$ is $C^1$ and closedness reads $\\partial_i a_j=\\partial_j a_i$ on $\\Omega$. For a piecewise-$C^1$ path $\\gamma$ in $U$ the integral is $\\int_\\gamma\\alpha:=\\int_{x\\circ\\gamma}A\\cdot d\\mathbf r$, the vector-field line integral of [[def-scalar-and-vector-line-integrals-along-piecewise-c1-paths]]. For a $C^1$ function $F:U\\to\\mathbb R$ with $\\tilde F:=F\\circ x^{-1}$, the differential $dF$ is the one-form whose chart coefficients are the partial derivatives $\\partial_i\\tilde F$, and $dF=\\alpha$ means $\\partial_i\\tilde F=a_i$ on $\\Omega$ for all $i$. Under the transition $x'=M^{-1}(x-b)$ the chain rule gives $a'_j=\\sum_i M^i_j a_i$, $\\partial_j\\tilde F'=\\sum_i M^i_j\\,\\partial_i\\tilde F$ and $(x'\\circ\\gamma)'=M^{-1}(x\\circ\\gamma)'$, so the integral $\\int_\\gamma\\alpha$ and the identity $dF=\\alpha$ do not depend on which inertial chart is used; likewise, $F$ being $C^2$, respectively smooth, is chart-independent. It therefore suffices to prove the following statement about the open set $\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^4$ and the $C^1$ closed field $A$: every closed piecewise-$C^1$ path in $\\Omega$ has zero $A$-integral, the $A$-integral is path-independent on $\\Omega$, and there is a $C^2$ function $\\tilde F$ on $\\Omega$ with $\\nabla\\tilde F=A$ which can be taken smooth when $A$ is smooth.",
          "strategy": "Use the exact published C1 closed-field primitive on each convex ball. A continuous based nullhomotopy has compact image and uniformly continuous coordinates, giving a finite mesh whose cell images and chords lie in such balls. Sum zero cell integrals, cancel internal edges, and compare bottom arcs to their chords. Thus loop integrals vanish, including singleton paths. Path independence defines the primitive by a unique integral value without choosing paths; local potential equality gives C2 or smoothness.",
          "deps": [
            "def-simply-connected",
            "def-homotopy-relative-and-path-homotopy",
            "def-nullhomotopic-map-and-contractible-space",
            "def-closed-and-exact-differential-forms",
            "def-exterior-derivative-by-the-invariant-vector-field-formula",
            "thm-heine-borel-rn",
