        {
          "id": "thm-sr-smooth-local-herglotz-noether",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "The smooth local Herglotz-Noether classification of Born-rigid motions",
          "statement": "Let $(A,V,\\eta,C^+)$ be the oriented time-oriented affine Minkowski space ([[def-sr-affine-minkowski-model]]), let $n$ be a smooth future unit timelike field on a nonempty open subset $\\Omega\\subseteq A$ ([[def-sr-chart-tetrad-and-congruence-distinction]]), with acceleration $a=\\nabla_nn$, rest metric $h$, expansion $\\theta$ and vorticity $\\omega$ ([[def-sr-observer-congruence-and-kinematics]]), and assume that $n$ is Born rigid, $\\theta=0$; write $a^\\flat:=\\eta(a,\\cdot)$.\n\n**(i) Preliminary identity.** For every smooth vector field $X$ on $\\Omega$ with $\\eta(n,X)=0$ one has $\\nabla_Xn=0$ if and only if $\\theta(X,\\cdot)=0$ and $\\omega(X,\\cdot)=0$. In particular, if $\\theta=\\omega=0$ on an open set $U\\subseteq\\Omega$, then $\\nabla_Xn=0$ for every vector field $X$ on $U$ tangent to the rest distribution $\\ker n^\\flat$.\n\n**(ii) Rotational case.** Let $U\\subseteq\\Omega$ be a flow box of $n$ with adapted coordinates $(s,y^1,y^2,y^3)$ in which $n=\\partial_s$ ([[thm-sr-local-congruence-adapted-charts-and-frobenius]]), and suppose that $\\omega$ is nowhere zero on $U$. Then the vorticity and the acceleration are **basic** on $U$: they are horizontal and their components in the adapted coframe do not depend on $s$, equivalently $\\mathcal L_n\\omega=0$ and $\\mathcal L_na^\\flat=0$. Moreover $da^\\flat=0$ on $U$, and for every primitive $F$ of the closed one-form $a^\\flat$ on the coordinate product box $U$ ([[thm-poincare-lemma-for-differential-forms-on-star-shaped-domains]]) the field $K:=e^Fn$ is a timelike Killing field, $\\nabla_aK_b+\\nabla_bK_a=0$, equivalently $\\mathcal L_K\\eta=0$. If $U$ is connected and simply connected and $\\omega$ is nowhere zero, then a single positive smooth function $f$ on $U$ satisfies $\\mathcal L_{fn}\\eta=0$ ([[lem-sr-closed-one-form-primitive-on-simply-connected-open-sets]]). Conversely, every future timelike Killing field on a connected open set, normalized as $n=K/\\sqrt{-\\eta(K,K)}$, is Born rigid, and its vorticity is either nowhere zero or identically zero on that set; hence its flow is rotational, in the sense of case (ii), exactly when its vorticity is nowhere zero.\n\n**(iii) Irrotational case.** Suppose $\\theta=\\omega=0$ on $\\Omega$. Then on a sufficiently small neighbourhood $U$ of every point the connected leaves of the rest distribution are open subsets of affine hyperplanes: there are a smooth future timelike curve $z:J\\to A$ with $\\eta(z',z')=-1$ and a smooth function $\\sigma:U\\to J$ such that, with\n\n$$N(x):=1+\\eta\\bigl(z''(\\sigma(x)),\\,x-z(\\sigma(x))\\bigr)>0,$$\n\nthe leaves of the rest distribution in $U$ are open subsets of the hyperplanes $H_s=z(s)+z'(s)^\\perp$, the field is $n=z'\\circ\\sigma$ on $U$, and\n\n$$d\\sigma(v)=-\\frac{\\eta(z'(\\sigma(x)),v)}{N(x)},\\qquad a=\\frac{z''\\circ\\sigma}{N},\\qquad \\nabla n=d\\sigma\\otimes(z''\\circ\\sigma);$$\n\nthe tubular label has derivative $1+\\eta(z''\\circ\\sigma,x-z\\circ\\sigma)$, which is nonzero and is taken positive on $U$. Conversely, for every smooth future timelike curve $z:J\\to A$ with $\\eta(z',z')=-1$, the field $n:=z'\\circ\\sigma$ on any tubular neighbourhood on which the label $\\sigma$ is unique with positive derivative is a smooth future unit irrotational Born-rigid congruence satisfying these same formulas.\n\n**(iv) Scope.** All statements are local on $\\Omega$; no global classification of rigid motions, no global orbit quotient, no completeness and no global restriction on the size of a rigid body is asserted beyond what the local formulas give. No choice principle is used. The rotational case is the local form of the Herglotz-Noether statement that a rotational Born-rigid motion is Killing; the irrotational case describes the orthogonal affine-plane families.",
          "strategy": "Use the complete local coframe/flatness proof, with theta=0 as the standing hypothesis of clause (i). Construct the local quotient metric and basic orthonormal coframe, identify all connection entries by metric/torsion and Koszul identities, derive Rbar=-3omega tensor omega in three rest dimensions and the mixed identity. Differentiate to show vorticity and acceleration basic; contract d2theta0=0 using Cartan to prove da-flat=0. An exact primitive gives the positive Killing rescaling. A connected-domain Killing field is affine with constant skew derivative, whose Lorentzian-plane argument gives the vorticity dichotomy. In the irrotational branch construct connected affine-plane leaf portions and a unit integral curve before the implicit label; apply the choice-free Euclidean inverse theorem to (s,x) mapped to (eta(z-prime(s),x-z(s)),x), giving N>0, d sigma=-n-flat/N and a=z-double-prime/N. Verify the converse by vanishing rest derivatives. No global orbit quotient or AC is assumed.",
          "deps": [
