        {
          "id": "ex-sr-radar-round-trip-3-4-5",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "Worked radar round trip: emission, reflection and reception at exact rational parameters",
          "statement": "Adopt the ideal-clock, ideal-light, available-reflector and SI premises of [[def-sr-operational-radar-protocol]], and calibrate the observer's ideal clock to read $\\tau=0$ at $x^0=0$. In an inertial chart $(x^0,x^1,x^2,x^3)$ of the affine Minkowski model with metric $\\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,1,1)$ let the observer be at rest at the spatial origin, so that its worldline is $x^1=x^2=x^3=0$, let $T>0$, and let $q:=x^{-1}\\bigl(cT,\\tfrac35cT,0,0\\bigr)$, an event of chart time $T$ and spatial coordinate $(3cT/5,0,0)$. With $e_-:=x^{-1}\\bigl(\\tfrac25cT,0,0,0\\bigr)$ and $e_+:=x^{-1}\\bigl(\\tfrac85cT,0,0,0\\bigr)$ one has $q-e_-=\\bigl(\\tfrac35cT,\\tfrac35cT,0,0\\bigr)$ and $e_+-q=\\bigl(\\tfrac35cT,-\\tfrac35cT,0,0\\bigr)$; both displacements have $\\eta$-square $-\\tfrac{9}{25}c^2T^2+\\tfrac{9}{25}c^2T^2=0$ and positive time component, hence are future null, so the radar protocol applies with emission $e_-$, reflection $q$ and reception $e_+$ ([[def-sr-operational-radar-protocol]], [[lem-sr-radar-midpoint-for-inertial-observer]]). Since the observer is inertial, its proper time between the events with temporal coordinates $\\lambda_-=\\tfrac25cT$ and $\\lambda_+=\\tfrac85cT$ (chart times $2T/5$ and $8T/5$) is $(\\lambda_+-\\lambda_-)/c$ with the stated clock calibration, so the radar assignments are $\\tau_{\\mathrm{rad}}(q)=\\tfrac12\\bigl(\\tfrac25T+\\tfrac85T\\bigr)=T$, the chart time of $q$, and $\\rho_{\\mathrm{rad}}(q)=\\tfrac{c}{2}\\bigl(\\tfrac85T-\\tfrac25T\\bigr)=\\tfrac35cT$, the chart distance of $q$ from the observer. The same computation for $q':=x^{-1}\\bigl(cT,\\tfrac45cT,0,0\\bigr)$ gives $e'_-=x^{-1}\\bigl(\\tfrac15cT,0,0,0\\bigr)$, $e'_+=x^{-1}\\bigl(\\tfrac95cT,0,0,0\\bigr)$, radar time $T$ and radar distance $\\tfrac45cT$. Hence the two events $q$ and $q'$ of equal chart time are radar-simultaneous, with radar distances equal to their chart distances, in agreement with [[lem-sr-radar-midpoint-for-inertial-observer]].",
          "strategy": "For T>0 evaluate the two future-null leg pairs and the calibrated readings tau(lambda)=lambda/c. Temporal coordinates 2cT/5 and 8cT/5 give chart times 2T/5 and 8T/5, radar time T and distance 3cT/5. The second pair uses coordinates cT/5 and 9cT/5, giving distance 4cT/5 and the same midpoint and radar time under the exact ideal protocol.",
          "deps": [
            "lem-sr-radar-midpoint-for-inertial-observer",
