        {
          "id": "ex-sr-time-dilation-at-beta-three-fifths",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Worked time dilation at speed 3c/5",
          "statement": "In an inertial chart $x$ with metric $\\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,1,1)$ let $v=3c/5$, $\\gamma=(1-v^2/c^2)^{-1/2}=5/4$, and consider the smooth worldline $y:\\mathbb R\\to A$ whose $x$-coordinates are $y(t)=(ct,\\tfrac{3c}{5}t,0,0)$.\n\n(a) $y'(t)=(c,\\tfrac{3c}{5},0,0)$ and $\\eta(y',y')=-c^2+\\tfrac{9c^2}{25}=-\\tfrac{16}{25}c^2$, so $y$ is future timelike and its proper-time rate is $\\tau'(t)=\\tfrac1c\\sqrt{\\tfrac{16}{25}c^2}=\\tfrac45$: between coordinate times $t_0<t_1$ the model elapsed proper time is $\\tfrac45(t_1-t_0)=(t_1-t_0)/\\gamma$, with rate factor $4/5=1/\\gamma$ ([[def-sr-proper-time]], [[def-inertial-frame-and-inertial-chart]]).\n\n(b) The four-velocity is $U=y'/\\tau'=(\\tfrac{5c}{4},\\tfrac{3c}{4},0,0)$ with $\\eta(U,U)=-\\tfrac{25c^2}{16}+\\tfrac{9c^2}{16}=-c^2$, and the dimensionless velocity is $u=U/c=\\tfrac54(1,\\tfrac35,0,0)=\\gamma\\bigl(e_0+\\tfrac35e_1\\bigr)$ for the chart's first coordinate basis vector $e_0$: this is exactly the boost relation of clause (i) of [[lem-sr-boost-time-length-and-velocity-formulas]] ([[def-sr-four-velocity-and-four-acceleration]], [[thm-sr-proper-time-and-observer-decomposition]]).\n\n(c) Described in the boosted chart $x'$ in which the clock is at rest (boost speed $3c/5$ along the first axis, [[def-lorentz-boost]]), its $x'$-time rate equals its proper-time rate, and the inverse statement $\\Delta t=\\gamma\\,\\Delta\\tau$ holds with $\\gamma=5/4$.",
          "strategy": "On the smooth all-real affine curve (ct,3ct/5,0,0), compute tangent square -16c2/25, proper-time rate 4/5 and U=(5c/4,3c/4,0,0) of square -c2. The passive boost makes the curve stationary and its primed coordinate-time increments equal model proper time; no physical clock reading is inferred from mathematics.",
          "deps": [
            "lem-sr-boost-time-length-and-velocity-formulas",
            "def-lorentz-boost",
            "def-sr-proper-time",
            "def-sr-four-velocity-and-four-acceleration",
            "def-inertial-frame-and-inertial-chart",
