        {
          "id": "ex-sr-length-contraction-of-a-moving-rod",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Worked length contraction of a rod of rest length 5 at speed 3c/5",
          "statement": "In an inertial chart $x$ let the chart $x'$ be related to $x$ by a boost of speed $v=3c/5$ along the first spatial axis, $\\gamma=5/4$, so that $x'^0=\\tfrac54\\bigl(x^0-\\tfrac35x^1\\bigr)$ and $x'^1=\\tfrac54\\bigl(x^1-\\tfrac35x^0\\bigr)$ ([[lem-sr-boost-time-length-and-velocity-formulas]], [[def-lorentz-boost]]). Let $L_0=5$ and let the rod at rest in $x'$ have endpoints on the worldlines $x'^1=0$ and $x'^1=5$, with vanishing transverse coordinates. Solving the transition for $x^1$ as a function of $x^0$ gives $x^1=\\tfrac35x^0$ on the first worldline and $x^1=\\tfrac35x^0+4$ on the second, so at every equal $x$-time the endpoints are separated by $4=L_0/\\gamma$ in the frame $x$. Explicit witness: the events $p:=x^{-1}(5,3,0,0)$ and $r:=x^{-1}(5,7,0,0)$ are simultaneous in $x$ (both have $x^0=5$) and separated by $4$; their $x'$-coordinates are $x'(p)=(4,0,0,0)$ and $x'(r)=(1,5,0,0)$, so they are not simultaneous in $x'$ but their $x'$-separation is $5=L_0$. Comparing events at equal $x'$-time instead: the events of the two worldlines with $x'^0=4$ are $x^{-1}(5,3,0,0)$ and $x^{-1}(35/4,37/4,0,0)$, the second of which has $x'^1=5$; at equal $x'$-time $4$ the endpoints are separated by $5$, the rest length. Thus the frame $x$ assigns length $4$ to a rod of rest length $5$ at rest in $x'$, exactly the contraction $L_0/\\gamma$ of clause (ii) of [[lem-sr-boost-time-length-and-velocity-formulas]], and the comparison uses the simultaneity slice of the measuring frame in the sense of [[def-sr-simultaneity-slice-and-rest-distance]].",
          "strategy": "Exact rational computation: solve the two linear transition relations for x^1 as a function of x^0 on each worldline and subtract; verify the witness events by substituting into the transition, obtaining the exact values 4, 0, 1 and 5; the equal-x'-time event is obtained from x'^0 = 4 on the second worldline x^1 = (3/5)x^0 + 4, which gives x^0 = 35/4, x^1 = 37/4 and x'^1 = 5. All arithmetic is rational.",
          "deps": [
            "lem-sr-boost-time-length-and-velocity-formulas",
            "def-lorentz-boost",
