        {
          "id": "ex-sr-velocity-transformation-worked",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Worked velocity transformation: collinear, transverse and null cases",
          "statement": "Let $x$ and $x'$ be inertial charts related by a boost of parameter $v=3c/5$ along the first axis ($\\gamma=5/4$, [[def-lorentz-boost]], [[def-inertial-frame-and-inertial-chart]]).\n\n(a) **Collinear case.** A worldline with coordinate velocity $w=(4c/5,0,0)$ in $x$ has, by clause (iv) of [[lem-sr-boost-time-length-and-velocity-formulas]], $w'_1=(4c/5-3c/5)/(1-(3/5)(4/5))=(c/5)/(13/25)=5c/13$, so $|w'|=5c/13<c$; the Galilean difference $c/5$ is not the transformed velocity.\n\n(b) **Transverse case.** A worldline with $w=(0,c/2,0)$ has $w'_1=(0-3c/5)/(1-0)=-3c/5$ and $w'_2=(c/2)/((5/4)(1-0))=2c/5$, hence $|w'|=\\sqrt{9/25+4/25}\\,c=(\\sqrt{13}/5)c<c$.\n\n(c) **Null limit.** For $w=(c,0,0)$ the formula gives $w'_1=(c-3c/5)/(1-3/5)=c$ and $|w'|=c$: a null worldline is null in every inertial chart.\n\nIn each case take the affine coordinate curve $t\\mapsto(ct,wt)$ on $\\mathbb R$ with the stated constant $w$; the first two are future timelike and the third future null. The three cases verify the velocity transformation and the subluminality statement of clause (iv) of [[lem-sr-boost-time-length-and-velocity-formulas]].",
          "strategy": "Evaluate the positive-denominator future-causal boost formulas at w=(4c/5,0,0), (0,c/2,0) and (c,0,0). Results are 5c/13, (-3c/5,2c/5,0), and c; the fixed-boost null denominator is 2/5, not zero. Each affine curve is on R. Compare the first result with the passive Galilean difference c/5.",
          "deps": [
            "lem-sr-boost-time-length-and-velocity-formulas",
            "def-lorentz-boost",
            "def-inertial-frame-and-inertial-chart"
          ],
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-generated",
            "proof": "ai-generated"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "B. Crowell, Special Relativity, revision 2020-12-10 (author-published undergraduate textbook, 246 PDF pages): Sections 1.1-1.3 pp. 12-28 (vector representation of observer motion, operational radar calibration, time dilation, length-contraction road-trip example), Sections 3.5 and 3.7 pp. 60-68 (four-velocity, acceleration, projection operator), Section 3.9.3 pp. 73-74 (local failure of accelerated simultaneity), Sections 7.1-7.3 pp. 147-151 (Rindler coordinates and nonuniform proper acceleration), Section 8.1 pp. 165-169 (rotating synchronization), Section 9.5 pp. 205-211 (congruences, expansion, Born rigidity); signature (+---) converted to (-+++) and c = 1 formulas converted to x^0 = c t",
