        {
          "id": "ex-sr-rindler-wedge-congruence-worked",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Worked Rindler wedge congruence: chart, metric, acceleration, rigidity and non-coordinate frame",
          "statement": "In the inertial chart $(x^0,x,y,z)$ with metric $\\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,1,1)$ consider $\\Phi(\\theta,\\rho,y,z):=(\\rho\\sinh\\theta,\\rho\\cosh\\theta,y,z)$ on $\\mathbb R\\times(0,\\infty)\\times\\mathbb R^2$, with $\\theta\\in\\mathbb R$ and $\\rho>0$. Then:\n\n(a) the identities $x^2-(x^0)^2=\\rho^2$ and $x=\\rho\\cosh\\theta>0$ show that the image of $\\Phi$ is the right wedge $W=\\{x>|x^0|\\}$, and the inverse $\\rho=\\sqrt{x^2-(x^0)^2}$, $\\theta=\\tfrac12\\log\\bigl((x+x^0)/(x-x^0)\\bigr)$ is smooth on $W$; both maps are smooth, so $\\Phi$ is a diffeomorphism onto $W$;\n\n(b) differentiating gives $dx^0=\\sinh\\theta\\,d\\rho+\\rho\\cosh\\theta\\,d\\theta$ and $dx=\\cosh\\theta\\,d\\rho+\\rho\\sinh\\theta\\,d\\theta$, so the pullback metric is $-\\rho^2d\\theta^2+d\\rho^2+dy^2+dz^2$;\n\n(c) the field $n:=\\rho^{-1}\\partial_\\theta$ satisfies $\\eta(n,n)=-1$ and is future; computing with the pullback metric, the nonzero connection coefficients are $\\Gamma^\\rho_{\\theta\\theta}=\\rho$ and $\\Gamma^\\theta_{\\theta\\rho}=\\Gamma^\\theta_{\\rho\\theta}=1/\\rho$, so $\\nabla_{\\partial_\\theta}\\partial_\\theta=\\rho\\,\\partial_\\rho$ and the congruence acceleration is $a=\\nabla_nn=\\rho^{-1}\\partial_\\rho$ with $\\eta(a,a)=1/\\rho^2$; for example at $\\rho=2$ one has $|a|=1/2$ in reciprocal-length units;\n\n(d) the slices $\\theta=const$ are open subsets of hyperplanes through the origin with induced metric $d\\rho^2+dy^2+dz^2$, independent of $\\theta$; hence the congruence is Born rigid, and it is irrotational because its rest distribution is the tangent distribution of these slices;\n\n(e) the tetrad field $(n,\\partial_\\rho,\\partial_y,\\partial_z)$ is not a coordinate frame, since $[n,\\partial_\\rho]=[\\rho^{-1}\\partial_\\theta,\\partial_\\rho]=+\\rho^{-2}\\partial_\\theta=+(1/\\rho)n$ is nonzero, whereas the members of a coordinate frame commute.\n\nThis realizes the Rindler congruence of [[thm-sr-fermi-walker-and-rigid-observer-examples]] clause (b) with exact formulas.",
          "strategy": "Verify the explicit two-sided inverse and determinant rho>0, invoking the choice-free smooth inverse theorem. Pull back the flat metric and differentiate the inertial components of the coordinate basis to obtain the three nonzero connection coefficients. Compute a=partial_rho/rho. Restricted slices x0=tanh(theta)x inside the wedge are valid also at theta=0; constant rest metric and vertical brackets give rigidity, while [n,partial_rho]=n/rho excludes a coordinate tetrad.",
          "deps": [
            "thm-sr-fermi-walker-and-rigid-observer-examples",
            "def-sr-observer-congruence-and-kinematics",
            "thm-sr-local-congruence-adapted-charts-and-frobenius",
            "def-inertial-frame-and-inertial-chart",
