          "id": "ex-sr-bell-congruence-fails-born-rigidity",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Worked Bell-type translated congruence: constant launch-frame separation without Born rigidity",
          "statement": "In an inertial chart let $q(t)=\\bigl(\\tfrac12\\alpha t^2,0,0\\bigr)$ with $\\alpha>0$, and consider the congruence of translated worldlines $x_\\xi(t)=\\bigl(ct,q(t)+\\xi\\bigr)$ for $\\xi$ in an open subset of $\\mathbb R^3$, defined while $|q_1'(t)|=\\alpha|t|<c$ ([[thm-sr-fermi-walker-and-rigid-observer-examples]] clause (d), [[def-inertial-frame-and-inertial-chart]]). Then $n=\\gamma\\bigl(1,\\alpha t/c,0,0\\bigr)$ with $\\gamma=(1-\\alpha^2t^2/c^2)^{-1/2}$ is a smooth future unit timelike field, and $s=\\gamma\\bigl(\\alpha t/c,1,0,0\\bigr)$ is a unit vector orthogonal to $n$. Direct computation of the expansion on $s$ gives\n\n$$\\theta(s,s)=s^as^b\\partial_an_b=\\gamma^3\\,\\frac{\\alpha^2t}{c^3},$$\n\nwhich is nonzero for every $t\\ne0$ on the subluminal domain; hence the congruence is not Born rigid on any neighbourhood of a time $t\\ne0$, and the failure is already present at $t=0$ on the two sides, where $\\theta(s,s)$ changes sign. Nevertheless, for every fixed chart time $t$ the separation between the member labelled $\\xi_1$ and the member labelled $\\xi_2$ is $|\\xi_1-\\xi_2|$, constant in $t$: the congruence has constant launch-frame separation while failing Born rigidity. This is the Bell-type translated congruence of the cited theorem; a physical conclusion about a breaking thread or rod would additionally require an elasticity model and a failure criterion and is not drawn here.",
          "strategy": "Put beta=alpha t/c and beta'=alpha/c. With x^0=ct, partial_0 n_0=-gamma^3 alpha^2t/c^3 and partial_0 n_1=gamma^3 alpha/c^2. Contract with s=(gamma alpha t/c,gamma,0,0): theta(s,s)=gamma^5 alpha^2t(1-alpha^2t^2/c^2)/c^3=gamma^3 alpha^2t/c^3. This vanishes exactly at t=0 on the two-sided subluminal domain |t|<c/alpha. At c=1, beta=3/5 and beta'=1 the general contraction is75/64, while the discarded extra factor gives3075/1024. The translated members differ by the constant vector xi_1-xi_2 at a fixed chart time. No elasticity or breaking conclusion is drawn.",
