          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Worked Fermi-Walker transport along uniformly accelerated hyperbolic motion",
          "statement": "In an inertial chart with metric $\\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,1,1)$ let $\\alpha>0$ and consider the smooth worldline $x:\\mathbb R\\to A$ with inertial coordinates $x(\\tau)=\\frac{c^2}{\\alpha}\\bigl(\\sinh(\\alpha\\tau/c),\\cosh(\\alpha\\tau/c),0,0\\bigr)$, parametrized by $\\tau$; write $\\theta:=\\alpha\\tau/c$. Its derivatives are $U:=x'=c(\\cosh\\theta,\\sinh\\theta,0,0)$ and $A:=U'=\\alpha(\\sinh\\theta,\\cosh\\theta,0,0)$, and one computes $\\eta(U,U)=c^2(-\\cosh^2\\theta+\\sinh^2\\theta)=-c^2$, $\\eta(A,A)=\\alpha^2(-\\sinh^2\\theta+\\cosh^2\\theta)=\\alpha^2$ and $\\eta(U,A)=c\\alpha(-\\cosh\\theta\\sinh\\theta+\\sinh\\theta\\cosh\\theta)=0$; thus $\\tau$ is a proper-time parameter (up to an additive constant) and $U$ is the four-velocity of a uniformly accelerated worldline. Put $X_0:=U/c=(\\cosh\\theta,\\sinh\\theta,0,0)$ and $X_1:=(\\sinh\\theta,\\cosh\\theta,0,0)$; then $\\eta(X_0,X_0)=-1$, $\\eta(X_0,X_1)=0$ and $\\eta(X_1,X_1)=1$, so $(X_0,X_1)$ is an orthonormal pair. A direct substitution into the Fermi-Walker rule shows that both are Fermi-Walker transported: $X_0'=A/c$ equals $\\frac1{c^2}\\bigl(\\eta(A,X_0)U-\\eta(U,X_0)A\\bigr)=\\frac1{c^2}\\bigl(0+cA\\bigr)=A/c$, and $X_1'=\\frac{\\alpha}{c}X_0$ equals $\\frac1{c^2}\\bigl(\\eta(A,X_1)U-\\eta(U,X_1)A\\bigr)=\\frac1{c^2}\\bigl(\\alpha U-0\\bigr)=\\frac{\\alpha}{c}X_0$. Moreover $X_1$ is not parallel transported, since $X_1'=\\frac{\\alpha}{c}X_0\\ne0$ for $\\alpha>0$; Fermi-Walker transport therefore differs from parallel transport for accelerated motion. The norm $\\eta(X_1,X_1)=1$ is constant along the worldline, an instance of the preservation clause of [[thm-sr-fermi-walker-and-rigid-observer-examples]], and adjoining the constant fields $\\partial_y,\\partial_z$ gives a Fermi-Walker transported orthonormal tetrad $\\bigl(U/c,X_1,\\partial_y,\\partial_z\\bigr)$ along the hyperbolic worldline.",
          "strategy": "Exact symbolic computation: differentiate x, U and X_0, X_1; evaluate the diagonal form on all displayed vectors; compare X_0' and X_1' with the two Fermi-Walker right-hand sides. Every step is finite algebra in the hyperbolic functions, using cosh^2 - sinh^2 = 1.",
          "deps": [
            "def-sr-fermi-walker-transport",
            "lem-sr-fermi-walker-transport-existence-and-uniqueness",
