        {
          "id": "ex-sr-parallel-null-displacements-compose-to-null",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Parallel future null displacements compose to a future null displacement",
          "statement": "Worked computation in the chart x of an inertial frame. Let v := (1,1,0,0) and w := (2,2,0,0) be coordinate columns with respect to the basis of the frame. (a) v and w are future null: eta(v,v) = -1 + 1 = 0, eta(w,w) = -4 + 4 = 0, and both have positive time component; w = 2v, so the two directions are parallel. (b) The sum v + w = (3,3,0,0) is again future null, eta(v+w,v+w) = -9 + 9 = 0, and the endpoint q := x^{-1}(3,3,0,0) lies in J^+(p) for p := x^{-1}(0,0,0,0) but not in I^+(p), by the coordinate criterion; the straight path from p to q is a future null straight line of the model. (c) This is the boundary case of the sum clause: the sum of two future causal vectors is future causal, and it is future null exactly when both vectors are future null and positive multiples of one another, as here; by contrast the explicit nonparallel future null pair (1,1,0,0) and (1,−1,0,0) has sum (2,0,0,0), whose squared norm is −4.",
          "strategy": "Evaluate the three displayed norms with eta=diag(−1,1,1,1), and apply the A-page coordinate criterion for the endpoint relation. For the full equality characterization retained in clause(c), let nonzero future causal u=(a,p),v=(b,q), a,b>0 and |p|≤a,|q|≤b. If u+v is null, then a+b=|p+q|≤|p|+|q|≤a+b; all inequalities are equalities. Thus |p|=a,|q|=b and equality in Euclidean triangle forces q=(b/a)p: use p·q=|p||q| and |q−(b/a)p|²=0. Hence v=(b/a)u. Conversely positive multiples of a future null vector sum to future null. The contrasting pair sums to (2,0,0,0), squared norm−4. These are actual A-supplier/coordinate computations; no worked example is a premise, and no choice principle is used.",
          "deps": [
            "def-sr-causal-reachability-in-affine-minkowski-space",
            "lem-sr-future-causal-sums-and-inertial-coordinate-criterion",
            "def-inertial-frame-and-inertial-chart",
