        {
          "id": "ex-sr-boost-makes-spacelike-events-simultaneous",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Worked boost family on the spacelike pair (11,13,0,0): simultaneity at b = 11/13 and both time orders",
          "statement": "Worked computation in the chart x of an inertial frame with eta_0 = diag(-1,1,1,1). Let p := x^{-1}(0,0,0,0) and q := x^{-1}(11,13,0,0); then D := x(q) - x(p) = (11,13,0,0) has eta(D,D) = -121 + 169 = 48 > 0, so q - p is spacelike and |D^0| = 11 < 13 = |D_s| in accordance with lem-sr-spacelike-pairs-have-frame-dependent-time-order(a). (a) With e := D_s/|D_s| = e_1 and b_0 := D^0/|D_s| = 11/13 (so |b_0| < 1), the chart x_{b_0} of the inertial frame built from the passive boost B(b_0 e_1) satisfies x_{b_0}^0(q) - x_{b_0}^0(p) = gamma_{b_0}(11 - (11/13)13) = 0: the two events are simultaneous in that frame, and gamma_{b_0} = (1 - 121/169)^{-1/2} = 13/sqrt(48). (b) With b = 3/5 (gamma = 5/4, below b_0) the time difference is (5/4)(11 - (3/5)13) = (5/4)(16/5) = 4 > 0. (c) With b = 12/13 (gamma = 13/5, above b_0) the time difference is (13/5)(11 - (12/13)13) = (13/5)(-1) = -13/5 < 0. (d) In all three frames the causal character of D is spacelike and |x_b^0(q) - x_b^0(p)| < |x_b^1(q) - x_b^1(p)|; the spatial difference of the pair in the boosted charts is computed from the same matrix and is nonzero. The three charts are the charts of three inertial frames related to x by passive boosts, so the time-order sign of a spacelike-separated pair is an artifact of the frame, not of the pair.",
          "strategy": "Exact rational computation with the passive boost formula x'^0 = gamma(x^0 - b x^1), x'^1 = gamma(x^1 - b x^0) of def-lorentz-boost restricted to the (0,1)-plane, which is the case beta = b e_1. (a)-(c) substitute the three values b = 11/13, 3/5, 12/13, each with |b| < 1, and evaluate the displayed expression gamma_b (11 - 13b) exactly: gamma_{11/13} = 13/sqrt(48) > 0, gamma_{3/5} = 5/4, gamma_{12/13} = 13/5. The frames exist by lem-sr-spacelike-pairs-have-frame-dependent-time-order(d) (basis e'_a = B(b e_1)^{-1} e_a), and the strict inequalities |b_0| < 1, 3/5 < 11/13 < 12/13 < 1 are elementary. (d) The spacelike character is invariant under the boost (lem-lorentz-map-preserves-metric-and-causal-structure) and the boosted spatial difference is gamma(13 - 11b) in the e_1 direction, which is nonzero for the three values; hence |time difference| < |spatial difference| holds in each chart, as (a) of the lemma requires. No choice principle is used.",
          "deps": [
            "lem-sr-spacelike-pairs-have-frame-dependent-time-order",
