        {
          "id": "cex-sr-spacelike-time-order-is-not-absolute",
          "kind": "counterexample",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Counterexample: the temporal order of a spacelike-separated pair is not the same in every inertial frame",
          "statement": "Statement refuted: 'for any two distinct events p,q of the affine Minkowski model, the sign of the time-coordinate difference x^0(q) - x^0(p) is independent of the inertial frame.' Counterexample: in the chart x of an inertial frame let p := x^{-1}(0,0,0,0) and q := x^{-1}(11,13,0,0). Then q - p is spacelike (eta = 48 > 0) and the chart x_{3/5} of the frame related to x by the passive boost with parameter b = 3/5 gives x_{3/5}^0(q) - x_{3/5}^0(p) = 4 > 0, while the chart x_{12/13} of the frame related to x by the passive boost with parameter b = 12/13 gives x_{12/13}^0(q) - x_{12/13}^0(p) = -13/5 < 0. Both frames are inertial frames of the model and the two coordinate differences refer to the same pair of events, so the refuted statement is false. The counterexample does not touch causal pairs: by thm-sr-future-cone-and-flat-domain-of-dependence(d) every inertial frame gives a positive time difference to a pair with q - p future causal, so the failure of frame independence is confined to spacelike-separated pairs.",
          "strategy": "Use the passive boost formula x_b^0=gamma_b(x^0−b x^1) supplied by def-lorentz-boost. For b=3/5, gamma=5/4 and gamma(11−13b)=(5/4)(16/5)=4. For b=12/13, gamma=13/5 and gamma(11−13b)=−13/5. Each |b|<1, so the A lemma lem-boost-is-proper-orthochronous-with-inverse supplies a proper orthochronous boost, hence an inertial chart by the A affine-frame construction. The displacement squared norm is −121+169=48>0. Opposite time signs refute the stated frame-independence assertion. The causal coordinate criterion retains positive time difference for nonzero future causal pairs. No worked example is a premise and no choice principle is used.",
          "deps": [
