        {
          "id": "ex-sr-superluminal-sweep-has-no-causal-connection",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "A prearranged sweep with superluminal coordinate speed: successive events are spacelike separated and can be made simultaneous",
          "statement": "Worked computation in the chart x of an inertial frame with x^0 in metres and c > 0. Fix w > c and consider the family E_xi := x^{-1}((c/w) xi, xi, 0, 0), xi in R: a prearranged array of devices at x^1 = xi triggered at coordinate time t = xi/w, so the pattern is a sweep of coordinate speed w > c along the row. (a) For xi < eta the displacement is E_eta - E_xi = ((c/w)(eta - xi), eta - xi, 0, 0), whose interval is (eta - xi)^2 (1 - c^2/w^2) > 0, so successive events are spacelike separated; in particular no event E_eta lies in J^+(E_xi) or J^-(E_xi) for eta not equal to xi by the coordinate criterion. (b) Let b := c/w in (0,1). The passive boost with parameter b e_1 maps the displacement to time component gamma_b((c/w)(eta - xi) - b(eta - xi)) = gamma_b(eta - xi)(c/w - c/w) = 0, so in the boosted chart x_b the whole family consists of events simultaneous at one coordinate time; taking b > c/w produces the opposite sign, so the apparent temporal order of the sweep runs forward, frozen or backward in different inertial frames even though no event of the family is causally related to another. (c) No signal statement is made or needed: the computation is a property of the spacetime locations of independently triggered events, and it exhibits the class of spacelike-separated patterns that a kinematic superluminal speed bound cannot exclude. The computation isolates the geometry of the pattern: it is a statement about the locations of the events and asserts nothing about any of them being the reception of a signal, and it does not model the fixed-speed relay kinematics of the hypothetical superluminal model treated on the A page.",
          "strategy": "Direct evaluation. (a) is the diagonal-form computation of eta on the displacement and the sign inspection of def-causal-classification-of-lorentz-vectors, together with the coordinate criterion lem-sr-future-causal-sums-and-inertial-coordinate-criterion(c). (b) substitutes the displacement into the passive boost x'^0 = gamma(x^0 - bx^1) of def-lorentz-boost for b = c/w, where gamma_b = (1 - c^2/w^2)^{-1/2} is finite because w > c; the case b > c/w is the same substitution with the resulting factor gamma_b(eta - xi)(c/w - b) < 0. Both boosted charts are charts of inertial frames by lem-sr-spacelike-pairs-have-frame-dependent-time-order(d). (c) is a scope delimitation of the example. All arithmetic is real algebra of one linear expression; no choice principle is used.",
          "deps": [
            "lem-sr-spacelike-pairs-have-frame-dependent-time-order",
            "lem-sr-future-causal-sums-and-inertial-coordinate-criterion",
            "def-sr-causal-reachability-in-affine-minkowski-space",
