        {
          "id": "lem-sr-reverse-cauchy-schwarz-for-future-timelike-vectors",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "The reversed Cauchy-Schwarz inequality for future timelike vectors",
          "statement": "Let (A,V,eta,C^+) be the oriented time-oriented affine Minkowski space and let v,w in V be future timelike vectors. Put a := sqrt(-eta(v,v)) > 0 and b := sqrt(-eta(w,w)) > 0, the timelike lengths of v and w. Then: (i) -eta(v,w) >= a b > 0; (ii) equality -eta(v,w) = a b holds if and only if v and w are positive proportional, that is w = t v for some real t > 0 or v = t w for some real t > 0; (iii) consequently -eta(v,w) > a b whenever v and w are not positive proportional, and eta(v,w) < 0 in every case; (iv) for two past timelike vectors v,w the same inequality -eta(v,w) >= sqrt(-eta(v,v)) sqrt(-eta(w,w)) holds, with equality if and only if they are positive proportional, because -v and -w are future timelike and eta(-v,-w) = eta(v,w). The statement uses only eta and the future cone C^+ and involves no chart, frame or choice principle.",
          "strategy": "Proof strategy, in an arbitrary inertial frame. Fix an inertial frame (o;e_0,e_1,e_2,e_3) (lem-future-oriented-inertial-frames-exist, def-inertial-frame-and-inertial-chart) and write v = v^0 e_0 + v_s, w = w^0 e_0 + w_s with v_s,w_s in the spatial three-space S. Future timelikeness of v and w is, in these coordinates, v^0 > |v_s| and w^0 > |w_s| (lem-timelike-cone-has-two-convex-components, whose coordinate description applies because e_0 is future). Bilinearity gives -eta(v,w) = v^0 w^0 - delta(v_s,w_s) where delta is the Euclidean form on S (def-spatial-euclidean-structure-of-an-inertial-frame), and the finite Cauchy-Schwarz inequality (thm-cauchy-schwarz-finite) gives delta(v_s,w_s) <= |v_s| |w_s|, so -eta(v,w) >= v^0 w^0 - |v_s| |w_s|. The algebraic identity (v^0 w^0 - |v_s||w_s|)^2 - ((v^0)^2 - |v_s|^2)((w^0)^2 - |w_s|^2) = (v^0 |w_s| - w^0 |v_s|)^2, together with a = sqrt((v^0)^2 - |v_s|^2) and b = sqrt((w^0)^2 - |w_s|^2) (def-rational-power, thm-of-square-roots), shows that v^0 w^0 - |v_s| |w_s| is a nonnegative real whose square dominates (ab)^2; monotonicity of squaring on the nonnegatives (lem-of-square-monotone) gives (i). For (ii), equality in the two-step estimate forces both delta(v_s,w_s) = |v_s||w_s| and v^0 |w_s| = w^0 |v_s|. The equality case of the finite Cauchy-Schwarz inequality (thm-cauchy-schwarz-finite) makes v_s and w_s nonnegatively proportional; if one of them is 0 then the second equality forces the other to be 0 as well and v,w are positive multiples of e_0; otherwise v_s = t w_s with t > 0 and v^0 |w_s| = w^0 t |w_s| gives v^0 = t w^0, hence v = t w. The converse is a direct substitution: eta(t w, w) = t eta(w,w) gives -eta(t w,w) = t b^2 = (t b) b. Clause (iv) applies (i)-(ii) to -v,-w, using that the negative of a past timelike vector is future timelike (def-time-orientation-and-future-causal-sets). No step uses the Axiom of Choice: the frame is finite-dimensional and the only inequality is the finite-sum Cauchy-Schwarz theorem.",
          "deps": [
            "def-lorentz-form-and-inertia",
            "def-causal-classification-of-lorentz-vectors",
            "def-time-orientation-and-future-causal-sets",
            "lem-timelike-cone-has-two-convex-components",
