        {
          "id": "ex-sr-rest-frame-of-a-timelike-displacement-worked",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Worked rest frame of the future timelike displacement (5,3,0,0)",
          "statement": "Worked computation in an inertial frame with eta = diag(-1,1,1,1). Let d := (5,3,0,0), future timelike with -eta(d,d) = 25 - 9 = 16, T := 4 and n := d/T = (5/4,3/4,0,0). (a) n is future unit timelike: eta(n,n) = -25/16 + 9/16 = -1 and n^0 = 5/4 > 3/4 = |n_vec|. (b) The boost parameter beta := n_vec/n^0 = (3/5,0,0) has |beta| = 3/5 < 1 and gamma = 5/4; the passive boost B(beta) of def-lorentz-boost sends n to e_0, as clause (iv) of lem-boost-is-proper-orthochronous-with-inverse requires, since gamma(1, 3/5, 0, 0) = (5/4, 3/4, 0, 0) = n. (c) The basis (e'_0, e'_1, e'_2, e'_3) := (n, B(-beta)e_1, B(-beta)e_2, B(-beta)e_3) has coordinate vectors e'_0 = (5/4,3/4,0,0), e'_1 = (3/4,5/4,0,0), e'_2 = (0,0,1,0), e'_3 = (0,0,0,1); the checks eta(e'_0,e'_0) = -1, eta(e'_1,e'_1) = -9/16 + 25/16 = 1, eta(e'_0,e'_1) = -(5/4)(3/4) + (3/4)(5/4) = 0, eta(e'_2,e'_2) = eta(e'_3,e'_3) = 1 and eta(e'_i,e'_j) = 0 for the remaining pairs show that (o;e'_0,e'_1,e'_2,e'_3) is an inertial frame with first vector n. (d) Its chart x' assigns to d the coordinates (4,0,0,0): d = 4n = 4 e'_0, so E'^{-1}(d) = (4,0,0,0); in particular the two endpoints of any displacement 4n have equal spatial coordinates in x' and time coordinates differing by 4.",
          "strategy": "Finite computations: the coordinates of B(-beta)e_1 are obtained from the coordinate action of def-lorentz-boost (x''^0 = gamma(x^0 + beta x^1), x''^1 = gamma(x^1 + beta x^0) at (0,1,0,0)), giving (gamma beta, gamma, 0, 0) = (3/4, 5/4, 0, 0); the orthonormality checks are exact rational evaluations of the diagonal form; and the chart value is the definition x'(p) = E'^{-1}(p - o) with E'(1,0,0,0) = e'_0. The example is the concrete instance of lem-sr-rest-frame-of-a-future-timelike-displacement.",
          "deps": [
