        {
          "id": "lem-sr-future-causal-pairing-negative",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "A future timelike vector pairs negatively with every nonzero future causal vector",
          "statement": "Let (A,V,eta,C^+) be the oriented time-oriented affine Minkowski space, let n, v be in V, and recall that a nonzero v with eta(v,v) <= 0 is causal (def-causal-classification-of-lorentz-vectors, def-time-orientation-and-future-causal-sets). Then: (a) if n is future timelike and v is nonzero future causal, then eta(n,v) < 0; (b) if n is future timelike and v is nonzero past causal, then eta(n,v) > 0; (c) consequently, for a nonzero null vector v and any future timelike n, v is future null if and only if eta(n,v) < 0, and v is past null if and only if eta(n,v) > 0; the sign of eta(n,v) does not depend on the choice of the future timelike n; (d) if n_hat := n / sqrt(-eta(n,n)) is the normalization of a future timelike n, then n_hat is future unit timelike (eta(n_hat,n_hat) = -1) and eta(n,v) = sqrt(-eta(n,n)) eta(n_hat,v) for every v, so the sign statements hold for n_hat as well. The statement is pure affine Minkowski geometry and no choice principle is used.",
          "strategy": "Proof strategy. Choose an inertial frame (o;e_0,e_1,e_2,e_3), which exists by lem-future-oriented-inertial-frames-exist with first vector e_0 in C^+; write x = x^0 e_0 + x_vec, where x_vec := sum_{i=1}^3 x^i e_i belongs to S = span(e_1,e_2,e_3), with delta:S x S -> R the restriction of eta and |x_vec| = sqrt(sum_i (x^i)^2) (def-spatial-euclidean-structure-of-an-inertial-frame). By lem-timelike-cone-has-two-convex-components, the future timelike set is {x : x^0 > |x_vec|}, the closed future cone is {x : x^0 >= |x_vec|}, and the closed past cone is {x : x^0 <= -|x_vec|}. Hence n^0 > |n_vec| >= 0 for future timelike n, and for nonzero future causal v one has v^0 >= |v_vec| and v^0 > 0 (if v^0 = 0 then |v_vec| = 0 and v = 0, excluded). Then eta(n,v) = -n^0 v^0 + delta(n_vec,v_vec) <= -n^0 v^0 + |n_vec||v_vec| by the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality for delta (thm-cauchy-schwarz-finite), and |v_vec| <= v^0 gives eta(n,v) <= -(n^0 - |n_vec|) v^0 < 0 because n^0 - |n_vec| > 0 and v^0 > 0. This proves (a); (b) applies (a) to -v, which is nonzero future causal exactly when v is nonzero past causal, and eta(n,-v) = -eta(n,v). (c) For a nonzero null v exactly one of 'v future' and 'v past' holds (the closed cones meet only at 0 and every nonzero causal vector is future or past); (a) and (b) then identify the sign cases; the 'for every/some' uniformity is immediate because (a) applies to every future timelike n once v is known to be future. (d) eta(n,n) < 0 makes the square root real and positive, n_hat is future timelike by convexity of the cone and has unit norm, and eta is homogeneous in each argument. Scope note: no physical claim; no choice principle is used.",
          "deps": [
            "def-lorentz-form-and-inertia",
            "def-causal-classification-of-lorentz-vectors",
            "def-time-orientation-and-future-causal-sets",
            "lem-timelike-cone-has-two-convex-components",
            "lem-future-oriented-inertial-frames-exist",
            "def-inertial-frame-and-inertial-chart",
