            "thm-cauchy-schwarz-finite": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "B. Crowell, Special Relativity, revision 2020-12-10 (author-published undergraduate textbook, 246 PDF pages): Section 3.2 'The stretch factor is the Doppler shift' pp. 55-57, Section 3.3 'Combination of velocities' pp. 57-59, Section 6.4 'Duality' pp. 134-137 (the frequency covector and its dual), Section 6.5.1 'Doppler shift' p. 137, Section 6.5.2 'Aberration' pp. 137-139 and Section 6.6.1 'Phase velocity' pp. 140-141; signature (+---) converted to (-+++) and c = 1 formulas converted to x^0 = c t",
                "url": "https://archive.org/download/sr_20220102/sr.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "dependency_level": 6
        },
        {
          "id": "lem-sr-null-covector-frame-data",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Frame data of a future null wave covector: the unique pair (varpi, s) with |s| = 1",
          "statement": "Let (A,V,eta,C^+) be the oriented time-oriented affine Minkowski space, let k be a future null wave covector (def-sr-affine-phase-and-wave-covector) and let (o;e_0,e_1,e_2,e_3) be an inertial frame with inertial chart x. Define varpi := -k(e_0) and s_i := k(e_i)/varpi for i = 1,2,3, and write s := (s_1,s_2,s_3) in R^3 with Euclidean norm |s|. Then: (a) varpi > 0. (b) |s| = 1. (c) for every v = v^0 e_0 + v^1 e_1 + v^2 e_2 + v^3 e_3 in V one has k(v) = varpi(-v^0 + s_1 v^1 + s_2 v^2 + s_3 v^3); equivalently the components of k in the frame are (k_0,k_1,k_2,k_3) = (-varpi, varpi s_1, varpi s_2, varpi s_3). (d) the raised vector is k^sharp = varpi(e_0 + s_1 e_1 + s_2 e_2 + s_3 e_3), with frame coordinates varpi(1,s_1,s_2,s_3); it is nonzero and future null, and k(k^sharp) = eta(k^sharp,k^sharp) = 0. (e) conversely, if a covector k in V* has frame components (-varpi, varpi s_1, varpi s_2, varpi s_3) with varpi > 0 and |s| = 1 in some inertial frame, then k is a future null wave covector and the construction of (a)-(b) applied to k in that frame returns the same varpi and s. (f) the pair (varpi,s) is uniquely determined by k and the frame; it is the complete frame description of a future null wave covector. No choice principle is used.",
          "strategy": "Proof strategy. (a) k(e_0) = eta(k^sharp,e_0) by the defining property of k^sharp (lem-sr-metric-duality-on-lorentz-vector-space), and eta(k^sharp,e_0) < 0 by lem-sr-future-causal-pairing-negative applied to the future timelike vector e_0 and the nonzero future null vector k^sharp; hence varpi = -k(e_0) > 0. (b) By lem-sr-metric-duality-on-lorentz-vector-space(d), the nullness eta(k^sharp,k^sharp) = 0 reads -(k_0)^2 + (k_1)^2 + (k_2)^2 + (k_3)^2 = 0; with k_0 = -varpi and k_i = k(e_i) = varpi s_i this is varpi^2(-1 + |s|^2) = 0, and varpi > 0 gives |s| = 1. (c) is linearity of k along the unique basis expansion (thm-unique-coordinates-with-respect-to-an-ordered-basis). (d) The component formula of the duality lemma gives k^sharp = -k_0 e_0 + sum_i k_i e_i = varpi e_0 + varpi sum_i s_i e_i; evaluating eta(k^sharp,k^sharp) with the diagonal matrix and using (b) gives 0, and k^sharp = varpi(1,s) in the frame has positive time component varpi > 0 equal to the norm of its spatial part, which is future null by lem-timelike-cone-has-two-convex-components. (e) With the displayed components the duality lemma gives the vector varpi(1,s), which is nonzero future null by the same closed-cone description, and applying (a)-(b) to it returns varpi and s by construction. (f) Uniqueness is immediate because the components k_a = k(e_a) are determined by k and the frame and (a)-(c) invert them. Scope: pure algebra of eta in one inertial frame; no physical interpretation and no choice principle.",
          "deps": [
            "def-sr-affine-phase-and-wave-covector",
            "lem-sr-metric-duality-on-lorentz-vector-space",
            "lem-sr-future-causal-pairing-negative",
            "def-causal-classification-of-lorentz-vectors",
            "def-time-orientation-and-future-causal-sets",
            "def-inertial-frame-and-inertial-chart",
            "def-spatial-euclidean-structure-of-an-inertial-frame",
            "lem-timelike-cone-has-two-convex-components",
            "thm-unique-coordinates-with-respect-to-an-ordered-basis",
            "def-euclidean-inner-product"
          ],
