        {
          "id": "lem-sr-null-covector-boost-transformation",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Transformation of the frame data of a future null wave covector under a passive boost",
          "statement": "Let (A,V,eta,C^+) be the oriented time-oriented affine Minkowski space, let x and x' be inertial charts whose transition is x' = B(beta) x + b for some beta in R^3 with |beta| < 1 and some b in R^4, where B(beta) is the passive boost of def-lorentz-boost and gamma := (1 - |beta|^2)^(-1/2), and let k be a future null wave covector with frame-x data (varpi,s) as in lem-sr-null-covector-frame-data, so that k has components (k_0,k_1,k_2,k_3) = (-varpi, varpi s_1, varpi s_2, varpi s_3) in x. Then: (i) the components of the same covector k in x' are k'_a = (B(-beta))^b_a k_b, that is k'_0 = gamma(k_0 + beta . k_vec) and k'_vec = k_vec + ((gamma - 1)/|beta|^2)(beta . k_vec) beta + gamma beta k_0 for beta nonzero (and k' = k for beta = 0), where k_vec := (k_1,k_2,k_3). (ii) With varpi' := -k'_0 and s'_i := k'_i/varpi' the frame-x' data is varpi' = gamma(1 - beta . s) varpi > 0 and s' = [s + ((gamma - 1)/|beta|^2)(beta . s) beta - gamma beta] / [gamma(1 - beta . s)] for beta nonzero (and s' = s for beta = 0); moreover |s'| = 1, so k'_a = (-varpi', varpi' s'_1, varpi' s'_2, varpi' s'_3) in x'. (iii) In the axis case beta = b e_1 with b in (-1,1): s'_1 = (s_1 - b)/(1 - b s_1), s'_2 = s_2/(gamma(1 - b s_1)) and s'_3 = s_3/(gamma(1 - b s_1)). (iv) beta . s' = (beta . s - |beta|^2)/(1 - beta . s); in particular beta . s' = 0 if and only if beta . s = |beta|^2, and beta . s' = -|beta|^2 if and only if beta . s = 0. (v) applying the transformation with beta replaced by -beta returns the original data (varpi,s), since B(-beta) is the inverse of B(beta). The statement is pure algebra of eta and the boost; no choice principle is used.",
          "strategy": "Proof strategy. (i) The transition x' = B(beta)x + b has linear part Lambda = B(beta), which is a proper orthochronous Lorentz matrix representing the inertial frame change (lem-inertial-chart-transitions-are-affine-lorentz, def-lorentz-map-and-lorentz-group); the covector component law k'_a = (Lambda^{-1})^b_a k_b is clause (ii) of thm-sr-tensor-and-current-transformation (for the constant covector field k, of class C^infinity in the sense of def-ck-tensor-field-on-minkowski-space). By lem-boost-is-proper-orthochronous-with-inverse, Lambda^{-1} has entries (B(-beta))^0_0 = gamma, (B(-beta))^0_i = (B(-beta))^i_0 = gamma beta_i and (B(-beta))^i_j = delta^i_j + ((gamma - 1)/|beta|^2) beta_i beta_j (for beta nonzero), which gives the displayed component formulas. (ii) Insert k_0 = -varpi and k_i = varpi s_i: k'_0 = gamma(-varpi + varpi beta . s) = -gamma(1 - beta . s) varpi, so varpi' = gamma(1 - beta . s) varpi; positivity follows from |beta| < 1 and |s| = 1 via the Cauchy-Schwarz bound beta . s <= |beta| < 1 (thm-cauchy-schwarz-finite), so 1 - beta . s >= 1 - |beta| > 0. The numerator for k'_vec is k_vec + ((gamma - 1)/|beta|^2)(beta . k_vec) beta + gamma beta k_0 = varpi[s + ((gamma - 1)/|beta|^2)(beta . s) beta - gamma beta], so dividing by varpi' gives the displayed s'. Finally |s'| = 1 is not assumed but follows from part (b) of lem-sr-null-covector-frame-data applied in the inertial frame x': the same covector k is future null (k^sharp is unchanged by a change of frame; only its components change), and the lemma's construction in x' returns precisely (varpi', s') as computed. (iii) Substituting beta = b e_1 and |beta|^2 = b^2 gives s'_1 = (s_1 - b)/(1 - b s_1) and s'_j = s_j/(gamma(1 - b s_1)) for j = 2,3. (iv) beta . s' = [beta . s + ((gamma - 1)/|beta|^2)(beta . s)|beta|^2 - gamma|beta|^2]/[gamma(1 - beta . s)] = [gamma(beta . s) - gamma|beta|^2]/[gamma(1 - beta . s)] = (beta . s - |beta|^2)/(1 - beta . s); the two equivalences follow since |beta| < 1. (v) By lem-boost-is-proper-orthochronous-with-inverse B(-beta) is the inverse of B(beta), so applying the component law twice returns k'' = k; equivalently substituting -beta in (ii) inverts the explicit formulas. Scope note: pure algebra; the item asserts no physical Doppler statement (that is pthm-sr-null-wave-doppler-and-aberration) and no choice principle is used.",
          "deps": [
            "def-sr-affine-phase-and-wave-covector",
            "lem-sr-metric-duality-on-lorentz-vector-space",
            "lem-sr-future-causal-pairing-negative",
