        {
          "id": "lem-sr-phase-rate-along-worldline",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "The phase rate along a curve, a worldline and an ideal observer",
          "statement": "Let theta be an affine phase function with wave covector k (def-sr-affine-phase-and-wave-covector). (a) For every C^1 curve gamma: I -> A one has (theta o gamma)'(s) = k(gamma'(s)) for all s in I. (b) If x: I -> A is a future timelike worldline (def-sr-regular-causal-curve-and-worldline) with proper-time function tau (def-sr-proper-time) and four-velocity U = dx/dtau (def-sr-four-velocity-and-four-acceleration), then d(theta o x)/dtau = k(U) along the worldline (the derivative is taken in the proper-time parametrization; the inverse proper-time parametrization exists by lem-sr-proper-time-parametrization). (c) If k is moreover a future null wave covector, then k(U) < 0 at every point, so theta is strictly decreasing in proper time along every future timelike worldline; the positive number -k(U) is the quantity given physical meaning in def-sr-null-wave-covector-and-observer-frequency. (d) If x is the straight worldline of an inertial observer, so that U = c n for a future unit timelike vector n with eta(n,n) = -1, then k(U) = c k(n) and -k(U) = -c k(n) > 0; conversely every future timelike worldline has eta(U,U) = -c^2 (thm-sr-proper-time-and-observer-decomposition(a)). No choice principle is used.",
          "strategy": "Proof strategy. (a) In an inertial chart theta is the affine function x |-> k_a x^a + theta_0; composing with gamma and differentiating is the chain rule (thm-chain-rule, def-derivative), and the derivative of the affine part is the constant covector k applied to gamma'. (b) Write the worldline in proper-time parametrization, x = x(tau); then theta o x has derivative k(x'(tau)) = k(U(tau)) by (a) applied to the reparametrized curve, with the chain rule and the positivity of dtau/ds (lem-sr-proper-time-parametrization). (c) U is nonzero future timelike and k^sharp is nonzero future null, so eta(k^sharp,U) < 0 by lem-sr-future-causal-pairing-negative; by the defining property of k^sharp, k(U) = eta(k^sharp,U) < 0. (d) For an inertial observer, thm-sr-proper-time-and-observer-decomposition(a),(d) gives eta(U,U) = -c^2 and the unit vector n = U/c; linearity gives k(U) = c k(n), and positivity is (c). Scope note: the item is conditional geometry along worldlines; it asserts no clock reading and no frequency measurement, and no choice principle is used.",
          "deps": [
            "def-sr-affine-phase-and-wave-covector",
            "lem-sr-future-causal-pairing-negative",
