        {
          "id": "rem-sr-doppler-dimensional-restoration",
          "kind": "remark",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "Units, coordinate conventions and c restoration for the wave and Doppler formulas",
          "statement": "Remark on the conventions of def-sr-si-units-and-coordinate-conventions and def-sr-null-wave-covector-and-observer-frequency, for use with pthm-sr-null-wave-doppler-and-aberration. (a) Units in the adopted coordinates x^0 = c t: the phase theta is dimensionless; the coordinates x^a, the wavelength lambda and all distances are in metres; the components k_a of a wave covector, the wave vector kappa and varpi = -k(e_0) are in m^-1; the angular frequencies omega and omega_n and the linear frequencies nu are in s^-1 (nu also in hertz); c is in m s^-1; and s, beta, beta_w and gamma are dimensionless. (b) Two coordinate forms. In the adopted coordinates theta = -omega t + kappa . x_vec + const and k_a = (-omega/c, (omega/c)s); in a chart whose time coordinate is t in seconds directly, so that the metric component g_tt = -c^2 carries m^2 s^-2 and the time-space components carry m s^-1, the same phase is theta = -omega t + kappa . x_vec + const with the same omega and kappa, and the component tuple (-omega, (omega/c)s) carries mixed units; formulas derived in one convention are not reused unchanged in the other. This is the general warning of def-sr-si-units-and-coordinate-conventions specialized to the wave covector. (c) Natural units and restoration. In natural units c = 1 with x^0 = t one has k_a = (-omega, omega s), lambda = 2 pi/omega, and the Doppler and aberration factors gamma(1 - beta . s) and sqrt((1 -/+ |beta|)/(1 +/- |beta|)) are unchanged; restoring dimensions means replacing k_0 by -omega/c, k_i by (omega/c)s_i, writing every velocity as v = c beta with the dimensionless beta, and replacing lambda by 2 pi c/omega = c/nu. The dimensionless factors gamma(1 - beta . s) and the longitudinal square roots need no c restoration because they contain only beta, s and gamma; the c restoration affects the map between omega, nu, lambda and the components of k, not the shift factors themselves. (d) This remark introduces no quantum identification of energy with hbar omega, no amplitude or intensity content and no measurement claim; it is a units and convention statement carrying the scope of the items it cites.",
          "strategy": "A conventions and units remark, not a theorem. (a) Each unit is read off from the definitions in def-sr-si-units-and-coordinate-conventions and def-sr-null-wave-covector-and-observer-frequency: the phase is dimensionless by (theta(p) = k(p - q) + theta_0 with k in m^-1 and displacements in m), and the wave quantities inherit their units from k, c and the definitions omega = c varpi, kappa = (omega/c)s, lambda = c/nu. (b) Substituting x^0 = c t into k_a x^a gives -omega t + kappa . x_vec; the metric-component statement is the convention clause of def-sr-si-units-and-coordinate-conventions for a chart with time coordinate in seconds, and the mixed-unit tuple is displayed to prevent copying formulas across conventions. (c) The natural-unit form is the substitution c = 1 in the same formulas (with x^0 = t), and the restoration list is the inverse substitution; the factors gamma(1 - beta . s) and sqrt((1 -/+ |beta|)/(1 +/- |beta|)) are functions of the dimensionless quantities beta, s, gamma alone, which is why they are invariant under the restoration. (d) The exclusions repeat the scope of the cited items; no step proves a physical claim and no choice principle is used.",
