        {
          "id": "ex-sr-phase-level-sets-and-null-generators",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Worked geometry of the phase level sets of a future null wave covector",
          "statement": "Worked example for def-sr-affine-phase-and-wave-covector and lem-sr-null-covector-frame-data. Let (A,V,eta,C^+) be the oriented time-oriented affine Minkowski space, let k be a future null wave covector with frame data (varpi,s) in an inertial frame, so varpi > 0, |s| = 1 and k has components k_a = (-varpi, varpi s_1, varpi s_2, varpi s_3), and let theta be the affine phase with wave covector k. Then: (a) k(k^sharp) = eta(k^sharp,k^sharp) = 0, since the raised vector is k^sharp = varpi(e_0 + s_1 e_1 + s_2 e_2 + s_3 e_3), so theta is constant on every line p + R k^sharp. (b) The direction subspace ker k = {v : k(v) = 0} = {v : v^0 = s . v_vec} is 3-dimensional; for v in ker k one has eta(v,v) = |v_vec|^2 - (s . v_vec)^2 >= 0 by the finite Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, with equality exactly when v_vec is a real multiple of s, i.e. exactly when v lies in the line span(k^sharp); hence the restriction of eta to ker k is positive semidefinite with radical the line span(k^sharp), and the only null direction contained in ker k is the line through k^sharp (with future ray k^sharp and past ray -k^sharp). (c) Every nonempty level set Sigma = {p : theta(p) = theta(p_0)} is the affine hyperplane p_0 + ker k through p_0, whose normal covector is the null covector k; it contains the two null rays p_0 + R_{\\ge 0} k^sharp and p_0 + R_{\\le 0} k^sharp, and all its other direction vectors are spacelike. The verification is exact algebra; no choice principle is used.",
          "strategy": "Verification by explicit computation. (a) k^sharp = varpi(1,s) by lem-sr-null-covector-frame-data(d); then k(k^sharp) = -varpi^2 + varpi^2|s|^2 = 0 because |s| = 1, and homogeneity gives theta(p + lambda k^sharp) = theta(p) + lambda k(k^sharp) = theta(p) by the displayed identity of def-sr-affine-phase-and-wave-covector(b). (b) The kernel of the nonzero functional k is 3-dimensional; substituting v^0 = s . v_vec into eta gives eta(v,v) = -(s . v_vec)^2 + |v_vec|^2, and the finite Cauchy-Schwarz inequality (thm-cauchy-schwarz-finite) gives |s . v_vec| <= |s||v_vec| = |v_vec| with equality exactly when v_vec lies in the span of s; for such v one has v = (v^0, v_vec) = (lambda, lambda s) = lambda(1,s) in span(k^sharp), and for all other nonzero v in ker k the form is strictly positive, i.e. spacelike. (c) The level set is a coset of ker k by def-sr-affine-phase-and-wave-covector(b), its normal covector is k (the level sets are exactly the affine hyperplanes with direction ker k), and the null directions in it are those of (b); membership of the two rays follows from (a). The sign of the normal covector's null character is the definition of a null wave covector; no physical interpretation of the level sets is used in the verification. No choice principle is used.",
