        {
          "id": "ex-sr-null-covector-frame-data-worked",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Worked frame data of a future null wave covector and its boost",
          "statement": "Worked example for lem-sr-null-covector-frame-data and lem-sr-null-covector-boost-transformation. In an inertial frame (o;e_0,e_1,e_2,e_3) let varpi > 0 and s = (0, 3/5, 4/5), and let k be the covector with frame components (k_0,k_1,k_2,k_3) = (-varpi, 0, 3varpi/5, 4varpi/5). Then: (a) |s| = 1 and k is a future null wave covector; its raised vector is k^sharp = varpi(e_0 + (3/5)e_2 + (4/5)e_3) and k(k^sharp) = 0. (b) Let x' be the inertial chart with x' = B(beta)x + b and beta = (3/5)e_1. The frame-x' data of the same covector is (varpi',s') with varpi'/varpi = gamma(1 - beta . s) = (5/4)(1 - 0) = 5/4 and s' = (-3/5, 12/25, 16/25), since s'_1 = (s_1 - beta)/(1 - beta s_1) = (0 - 3/5)/1 = -3/5, s'_2 = s_2/(gamma(1 - beta s_1)) = (3/5)/(5/4) = 12/25 and s'_3 = s_3/(gamma(1 - beta s_1)) = (4/5)/(5/4) = 16/25; one checks |s'|^2 = 9/25 + 144/625 + 256/625 = 9/25 + 400/625 = 9/25 + 16/25 = 1. (c) Applying the transformation with beta replaced by -beta to (varpi',s') returns (varpi,s): varpi''/varpi' = gamma(1 + (3/5)(-3/5)) = (5/4)(16/25) = 4/5, so varpi'' = (4/5)(5/4)varpi = varpi, and s'' = (0, 3/5, 4/5) by the same axis formulas. The verification is exact rational algebra; no physical interpretation of the data is used and no choice principle is used.",
          "strategy": "Verification by substitution. (a) |s|^2 = 9/25 + 16/25 = 1; k has the components required by lem-sr-null-covector-frame-data(e), so it is a future null wave covector and the duality lemma gives k^sharp = -k_0 e_0 + k_1 e_1 + k_2 e_2 + k_3 e_3 = varpi e_0 + (3varpi/5)e_2 + (4varpi/5)e_3; then k(k^sharp) = -varpi^2 + varpi^2(9/25 + 16/25) = 0. (b) The transformation formulas of lem-sr-null-covector-boost-transformation(ii)-(iii) with s_1 = 0, beta = 3/5 and gamma = 5/4 give the displayed varpi' and s'; the norm check is exact arithmetic. (c) Same formulas with -beta: 1 - (-beta) . s' = 1 + (3/5)(-3/5) = 16/25, gamma = 5/4, so varpi'' = (5/4)(16/25)(5/4)varpi = (4/5)(5/4)varpi = varpi; s''_1 = (s'_1 + 3/5)/(1 + (3/5)(3/5)) = 0 and s''_2 = s'_2/((5/4)(16/25)) = (12/25)/(4/5) = 3/5, s''_3 = (16/25)/(4/5) = 4/5. No choice principle is used.",
          "deps": [
            "lem-sr-null-covector-frame-data",
            "lem-sr-null-covector-boost-transformation",
