        {
          "id": "lem-sr-finite-future-causal-sums",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "title": "Finite sums of future causal vectors and additivity of observer energy and momentum",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "statement": "Let $(A,V,\\eta,C^+)$ be the oriented time-oriented affine Minkowski model\n([[def-sr-affine-minkowski-model]]) and $c>0$.\n\n**(a)** If $v,w\\in\\mathrm{cl}(C^+)$, then $v+w\\in\\mathrm{cl}(C^+)$; if in\naddition $v\\in C^+$ or $w\\in C^+$, then $v+w\\in C^+$. Moreover\n$-\\eta(v,w)\\ge0$ for $v,w\\in\\mathrm{cl}(C^+)$, with equality if and only if\n$v=0$, or $w=0$, or both $v$ and $w$ are nonzero future null and\n$w=\\lambda v$ for some $\\lambda>0$.\n\n**(b)** If $P_1,\\dots,P_N$ with $N\\ge1$ are nonzero future causal vectors,\nthen $P_{\\mathrm{tot}}=\\sum_{i=1}^{N}P_i$\n([[def-sr-total-four-momentum-and-invariant-mass]]\\,(a)) is a nonzero future\ncausal vector; if at least one $P_i$ is future timelike, then\n$P_{\\mathrm{tot}}$ is future timelike. The converse implication does not\nhold: two future null vectors that are not parallel have a future timelike\nsum.\n\n**(c)** For every future unit $n$ ([[def-lorentz-form-and-inertia]]) and all\n$P_1,\\dots,P_N\\in\\mathrm{cl}(C^+)$,\n\n$$E_n\\Bigl(\\sum_{i=1}^{N}P_i\\Bigr)=\\sum_{i=1}^{N}E_n(P_i),\\qquad q_n\\Bigl(\\sum_{i=1}^{N}P_i\\Bigr)=\\sum_{i=1}^{N}q_n(P_i),$$\n\nwhere $E_n,q_n$ are the observer quantities of\n[[def-sr-observed-energy-momentum-and-kinetic-energy]]; if the $P_i$ are\nnonzero future causal, then $E_n(P_{\\mathrm{tot}})>0$.",
          "strategy": "Work in an $\\eta$-orthonormal basis whose first vector lies in $C^+$ ([[lem-lorentz-form-has-orthonormal-basis]], [[lem-future-oriented-inertial-frames-exist]]), so that $\\mathrm{cl}(C^+)=\\{v:v^0\\ge|v_s|\\}$ and $C^+=\\{v:v^0>|v_s|\\}$ by [[lem-timelike-cone-has-two-convex-components]]. For (a), $(v+w)^0=v^0+w^0\\ge|v_s|+|w_s|\\ge|v_s+w_s|$ by the triangle inequality, with strict first inequality if one summand is timelike; $-\\eta(v,w)=v^0w^0-v_s\\cdot w_s\\ge|v_s||w_s|-v_s\\cdot w_s\\ge0$ by Cauchy-Schwarz ([[thm-cauchy-schwarz-finite]]), and equality forces $v_s,w_s$ collinear with $v^0=|v_s|$, $w^0=|w_s|$ unless a vector vanishes, i.e. both are null and parallel. For (b), apply (a) repeatedly by induction on $N$ ([[thm-induction-principle]], [[def-finite-sum-in-a-commutative-monoid]]); nonzeroness follows from $\\mathrm{cl}(C^+)\\cap(-\\mathrm{cl}(C^+))=\\{0\\}$ of [[def-time-orientation-and-future-causal-sets]]: if $P_{\\mathrm{tot}}=0$ then $P_N=-\\sum_{i<N}P_i$ lies in $\\mathrm{cl}(C^+)$ and in $-\\mathrm{cl}(C^+)$, hence is zero, contradicting the hypothesis. For the failure of the converse, in an orthonormal basis take $P_1=(1,1,0,0)$ and $P_2=(1,0,1,0)$ times a common positive energy over $c$: both are future null and not parallel, and their sum $(2,1,1,0)$ times that factor has $v^0=2>\\sqrt2=|v_s|$, hence is future timelike. For (c), $\\eta(\\cdot,n)$ and $h$ are linear ([[def-sr-observed-energy-momentum-and-kinetic-energy]], [[thm-sr-proper-time-and-observer-decomposition]]\\,(c), [[def-linear-map]]); positivity is [[lem-sr-energy-momentum-observer-identities]]\\,(a) applied to the nonzero future causal total of (b). No choice principle is used.",
          "deps": [
