        {
          "id": "ex-sr-four-momentum-boost-to-rest",
          "kind": "example",
          "title": "A passive boost that brings a moving particle to rest",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "statement": "In the setting of [[ex-sr-four-momentum-at-beta-three-fifths]], let $B(\\beta)$ be the passive boost of [[def-lorentz-boost]] with parameter $\\beta=3/5$ along $e_1$, and let $P'$ be the components of $P$ after the coordinate change $x'=B(\\beta)x$ with $v=3c/5$. Then $P'=(mc,0,0,0)$: the energy becomes $E'=mc^2$ and the spatial momentum vanishes, and the mass shell gives $E'^2-c^2|\\mathbf p'|^2=m^2c^4$. The observer energy of the same particle thus changes from $5mc^2/4$ to $mc^2$ while the invariant mass stays $m$; in particular $T_{e'_0}(P)=0$ in the new frame, the frame of the particle's rest.",
          "strategy": "Substitute $\\gamma_v=5/4$, $E=5mc^2/4$, $p_\\parallel=3mc/4$ into the boost transformation of [[lem-sr-four-momentum-in-inertial-frame]]\\,(c): $E'=\\gamma_v(E-vp_\\parallel)=5/4\\,(5mc^2/4-9mc^2/20)=mc^2$ and $p'_\\parallel=\\gamma_v(p_\\parallel-vE/c^2)=0$. Check the mass shell and read the rest-frame property from [[lem-sr-energy-momentum-observer-identities]]\\,(b).",
          "deps": [
            "ex-sr-four-momentum-at-beta-three-fifths",
            "lem-sr-four-momentum-in-inertial-frame",
            "lem-sr-energy-momentum-observer-identities",
