        {
          "id": "ex-sr-null-pair-invariant-mass",
          "kind": "example",
          "title": "Collective mass of a pair of oppositely directed massless momenta",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "statement": "Let $e_0,e_1$ be the first two vectors of an inertial frame, $E_1,E_2>0$, and\nlet $P_1=(E_1/c)(e_0+e_1)$, $P_2=(E_2/c)(e_0-e_1)$. Both are nonzero future\nnull vectors with $E_{e_0}(P_i)=E_i$, and their total is\n$Q=((E_1+E_2)/c)e_0+((E_1-E_2)/c)e_1$, a future timelike vector with\ninvariant mass $M=2\\sqrt{E_1E_2}/c^2$; for $E_1=E_2=E$ this gives\n$Q=(2E/c)e_0$ and $M=2E/c^2$. If instead $P_2=(E_2/E_1)P_1$ (parallel\nmomenta), then $Q$ is future null, $M=0$ by convention and there is no\ncenter-of-momentum frame. In the opposite-direction case with $E_1\\ne E_2$\nthe first basis vector is not the center-of-momentum vector; the\ncenter-of-momentum frame exists by [[lem-sr-center-of-momentum-frame]] but\ndiffers from the displayed frame. The arithmetic is exact and no measurement\nis asserted.",
          "strategy": "Verify nullness, observer energies and the sum componentwise; compute $-c^2\\eta(Q,Q)=(E_1+E_2)^2-(E_1-E_2)^2=4E_1E_2$ and apply [[def-sr-total-four-momentum-and-invariant-mass]]; the parallel case is the null-total clause of [[lem-sr-collision-necessary-conditions]]\\,(d). Exact arithmetic, no measurement.",
          "deps": [
            "lem-sr-energy-momentum-observer-identities",
            "def-sr-observed-energy-momentum-and-kinetic-energy",
            "def-sr-total-four-momentum-and-invariant-mass",
