            "proof": "not-applicable"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "B. Crowell, Special Relativity, revision 2020-12-10 (author-published undergraduate textbook, 246 PDF pages); signature (+---) converted to (-+++) and c = 1 formulas converted to x^0 = c t; Chapter 9 pp. 179-197: 9.1 pp. 179-182 (current vector, flux, charge conservation), 9.2 pp. 183-191 (stress-energy tensor, conservation and flux, symmetry, dust, rank-2 transformation law, pressure, perfect fluid, worked examples, energy conditions), 9.3 pp. 192-197 (Gauss's theorem, integral conservation laws, the energy-momentum vector, angular momentum); the printed 9.2.8 dominant energy condition p. 191 has the defective |P| > rho and is not used",
                "url": "https://archive.org/download/sr_20220102/sr.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "D. Tong, General Relativity, University of Cambridge Part III Mathematical Tripos (Michaelmas Term 2019); c = 1 formulas converted to x^0 = c t; 4.5.1-4.5.5 printed pp. 181-191: scalar-field action (4.42)-(4.43) and equation of motion, Hilbert energy-momentum tensor (4.46), diffeomorphism invariance and conservation (4.50), flat-space Noether form, scalar tensor (4.51), Maxwell tensor (4.52), perfect fluid (4.53) with conservation equations (4.54)-(4.55), and the flat-space conserved-charge box argument of 4.5.5",
                "url": "https://davidtong.org/pdfs/teaching/general-relativity/gr.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "S. M. Carroll, Lecture Notes on General Relativity, arXiv:gr-qc/9712019v1 (1997), Chapter 1 printed pp. 28-30 (energy-momentum tensor, dust T^{mu nu}=rho U^mu U^nu (1.106), perfect fluid (1.107)-(1.110), scalar and Maxwell tensors (1.111)-(1.112), conservation (1.113) with the remark that the proof follows from each matter model's equations of motion) and Chapter 5 printed pp. 138-139 (on-shell conservation from diffeomorphism invariance with compact-support variations, (5.34)-(5.38))",
                "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/gr-qc/9712019"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "lem-sr-observer-stress-energy-decomposition",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "title": "Observer decomposition of a symmetric stress-energy tensor",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "statement": "Let $(A,V,\\eta,C^+)$ be the affine Minkowski model, $c>0$, $\\Omega\\subseteq A$ open, and let $T$ be a continuous symmetric type-$(2,0)$ tensor field on $\\Omega$ ([[def-sr-stress-energy-tensor-and-force-density]]). Let $n\\in V$ be future unit, $\\eta(n,n)=-1$, with rest projection $h(v)=v+\\eta(n,v)n$ and $h^a{}_b=\\delta^a{}_b+n^an_b$ as in [[thm-sr-proper-time-and-observer-decomposition]]\\,(c). At a point $p\\in\\Omega$ define $\\varepsilon:=T^{ab}n_an_b$, $\\pi^a:=-c^{-1}h^a{}_bT^{bc}n_c$ and $S^{ab}:=h^a{}_ch^b{}_dT^{cd}$. Then: (a) $\\pi$ lies in $n^\\perp$, $S$ is symmetric and horizontal in both slots ($S^{ab}n_b=n_aS^{ab}=0$), and $$T^{ab}=\\varepsilon\\,n^an^b+c\\,(n^a\\pi^b+\\pi^an^b)+S^{ab}.$$ (b) Contracting with $n$ gives $T^{ab}n_b=-\\varepsilon n^a-c\\pi^a$; hence $\\varepsilon$ and $\\pi$ are determined by $T$ and $n$, and the decomposition is unique among decompositions $T^{ab}=\\varepsilon' n^an^b+c(n^a\\pi'^b+\\pi'^an^b)+S'^{ab}$ with $\\pi'\\in n^\\perp$ and $S'$ symmetric horizontal: $\\varepsilon'=\\varepsilon$, $\\pi'=\\pi$, $S'=S$. (c) In any adapted inertial orthonormal frame with $n=e_0$, the numerical components of this decomposition are $\\varepsilon=T^{00}$, $\\pi^0=0$, $\\pi^i=T^{0i}/c$ and $S^{0a}=S^{a0}=0$, $S^{ij}=T^{ij}$ for $i,j=1,2,3$. Define isotropic rest stress to mean $S^{ab}=p h^{ab}$ for a real scalar $p$, where $h^{ab}:=\\eta^{ab}+n^an^b$. Thus $S=0$ means vanishing rest stress, and is the isotropic case $p=0$; isotropy permits any $p$, including nonzero pressure or tension. These are numerical tensor identities. Physical adoption of the energy/momentum-density reading is a separate model premise; this mathematical lemma asserts no observer measurement. No choice principle is used.",
          "strategy": "Pointwise linear algebra. Since $h$ is the projection of [[thm-sr-proper-time-and-observer-decomposition]]\\,(c) with image $n^\\perp$ and kernel $\\operatorname{span}(n)$, and $\\delta^a{}_c=h^a{}_c-n^an_c$, expand $T^{ab}=(h^a{}_c-n^an_c)(h^b{}_d-n^bn_d)T^{cd}$ and use symmetry of $T$ to obtain (a) with the stated signs. For (b), contract (a) with $n_b$ using $n_bn^b=-1$, $n_b\\pi^b=0$ and $S^{ab}n_b=0$; uniqueness follows by contracting a general decomposition with $n_an_b$ (gives $\\varepsilon'=\\varepsilon$), with $h_{ac}h_{bd}$ (gives $S'=S$), and with $n_b$ (gives $\\pi'=\\pi$). No choice principle is used. For (c), in the adapted frame $n^a=\\delta^a_0$, $n_a=-\\delta_a^0$ and $h^a{}_b=\\operatorname{diag}(0,1,1,1)$. Substituting these components into the definitions gives the stated entries. The rest-stress convention $S=p h$ gives $S^{ij}=p\\delta^{ij}$ in that frame; it does not force $p=0$. The decomposition needs only continuity of $T$ and its pointwise symmetric tensor structure; no derivative or physical identification is used.",
          "deps": [
            "def-ck-tensor-field-on-minkowski-space",
            "def-lorentz-form-and-inertia",
            "def-sr-affine-minkowski-model",
            "def-sr-stress-energy-tensor-and-force-density",
            "thm-sr-proper-time-and-observer-decomposition"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-ck-tensor-field-on-minkowski-space": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-lorentz-form-and-inertia": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-sr-affine-minkowski-model": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-sr-stress-energy-tensor-and-force-density": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-sr-proper-time-and-observer-decomposition": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "dependency_level": 12,
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "B. Crowell, Special Relativity, revision 2020-12-10 (author-published undergraduate textbook, 246 PDF pages); signature (+---) converted to (-+++) and c = 1 formulas converted to x^0 = c t; Chapter 9 pp. 179-197: 9.1 pp. 179-182 (current vector, flux, charge conservation), 9.2 pp. 183-191 (stress-energy tensor, conservation and flux, symmetry, dust, rank-2 transformation law, pressure, perfect fluid, worked examples, energy conditions), 9.3 pp. 192-197 (Gauss's theorem, integral conservation laws, the energy-momentum vector, angular momentum); the printed 9.2.8 dominant energy condition p. 191 has the defective |P| > rho and is not used",
                "url": "https://archive.org/download/sr_20220102/sr.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "D. Tong, General Relativity, University of Cambridge Part III Mathematical Tripos (Michaelmas Term 2019); c = 1 formulas converted to x^0 = c t; 4.5.1-4.5.5 printed pp. 181-191: scalar-field action (4.42)-(4.43) and equation of motion, Hilbert energy-momentum tensor (4.46), diffeomorphism invariance and conservation (4.50), flat-space Noether form, scalar tensor (4.51), Maxwell tensor (4.52), perfect fluid (4.53) with conservation equations (4.54)-(4.55), and the flat-space conserved-charge box argument of 4.5.5",
                "url": "https://davidtong.org/pdfs/teaching/general-relativity/gr.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "S. M. Carroll, Lecture Notes on General Relativity, arXiv:gr-qc/9712019v1 (1997), Chapter 1 printed pp. 28-30 (energy-momentum tensor, dust T^{mu nu}=rho U^mu U^nu (1.106), perfect fluid (1.107)-(1.110), scalar and Maxwell tensors (1.111)-(1.112), conservation (1.113) with the remark that the proof follows from each matter model's equations of motion) and Chapter 5 printed pp. 138-139 (on-shell conservation from diffeomorphism invariance with compact-support variations, (5.34)-(5.38))",
                "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/gr-qc/9712019"
              }
            ]
