        },
        {
          "id": "lem-sr-compact-variation-and-fundamental-lemma",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "title": "Compact-support variation: the fundamental lemma, integration by parts and differentiation under the integral sign",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "statement": "Work in an inertial chart $x$ of the affine Minkowski model, identifying a nonempty open $\\Omega\\subseteq A$ with its image in $\\mathbb R^4$; all integrals are Riemann (Darboux) integrals. (a) If $g:\\Omega\\to\\mathbb R$ is continuous and $\\int_\\Omega g\\,\\psi\\,d^4x=0$ for every smooth compactly supported $\\psi:\\Omega\\to\\mathbb R$, then $g=0$ on $\\Omega$. (b) If $f:\\Omega\\to\\mathbb R$ is $C^1$ and compactly supported and $g:\\Omega\\to\\mathbb R$ is $C^1$, then for each $a$, $\\int_\\Omega(\\partial_af)g\\,d^4x=-\\int_\\Omega f(\\partial_ag)\\,d^4x$, provided $g$ is $C^1$ on $\\Omega$ and the products are extended by zero outside $\\operatorname{supp}f$. (c) Let $s_0>0$. If $F:(-s_0,s_0)\\times\\Omega\\to\\mathbb R$ is continuous with continuous $\\partial_sF$ and there is a compact $K\\Subset\\Omega$ with $F(s,z)=0$ for $z\\notin K$ and all $s$, then $s\\mapsto\\int_\\Omega F(s,z)\\,d^4z$ is $C^1$ on $(-s_0,s_0)$ with derivative $\\int_\\Omega\\partial_sF(s,z)\\,d^4z$. The lemma is choice-free and is stated for the exact Riemann integration theory on bounded rectangles; no distribution theory, no $L^1_{\\mathrm{loc}}$ hypothesis and no choice principle is used.",
          "strategy": "(a) Suppose g(p) is nonzero. Set sigma=+1 if g(p)>0 and sigma=-1 if g(p)<0. By continuity there is a closed nondegenerate box Q compactly inside Omega on which sigma*g>=a>0. Choose a smaller closed nondegenerate box Qprime in int(Q). Apply [[lem-euclidean-bump-for-a-compact-set-inside-an-open-set]] to Qprime inside int(Q) to obtain a smooth bump rho with 0<=rho<=1, rho=1 on Qprime and support inside int(Q). Its finite-ball construction gives compact support. Use the signed test psi=sigma*rho. Its integral satisfies integral g*psi=integral (sigma*g)*rho >=a*vol(Qprime)>0, contrary to the hypothesis. Both signs of g(p) are thereby covered.\n(b) The products fg, f partial_a g, and g partial_a f have compact support inside Omega. Their extensions by zero are respectively C1 and continuous on R4: near every point outside Omega they vanish on a neighbourhood, because supp(f) is a compact subset of Omega. Choose a bounding rectangle with this support in its interior. On each coordinate line the integral of partial_a(fg) is zero by FTC, since fg vanishes at the endpoints. Apply [[thm-riemann-fubini-on-product-rectangles]] repeatedly to the continuous functions, and expand the product derivative to obtain the displayed integration-by-parts identity.\n(c) Extend F and partial_s F by zero outside Omega. Since the common support K is compactly inside Omega, both extensions are continuous on each compact parameter interval times a bounding rectangle, and differentiation in s gives the extended partial_s F. The imported [[thm-differentiation-under-the-integral-sign-on-a-compact-rectangle]] has a one-spatial-variable public interface; apply it four times to the iterated coordinate integrals, using Fubini for continuous functions at each stage. Continuity of each integrated derivative follows from uniform continuity on the compact product and the bound |integral u|<=vol(R)*sup|u|. This proves C1 parameter dependence on each compact subinterval of (-s0,s0), hence everywhere there. The compactly supported integral does not depend on its bounding rectangle by [[lem-compactly-supported-riemann-integral-is-well-defined]]. All choices are finite; no AC or countable choice is used.",
          "deps": [
            "def-directional-and-partial-derivatives",
            "def-inertial-frame-and-inertial-chart",
            "def-multidimensional-darboux-integral",
            "def-sr-affine-minkowski-model",
            "def-support-and-compactly-supported-riemann-integral-in-rn",
            "lem-algebra-of-continuous-real-maps-on-a-space",
            "lem-compactly-supported-riemann-integral-is-well-defined",
            "lem-euclidean-bump-for-a-compact-set-inside-an-open-set",
            "thm-algebra-of-derivatives",
            "thm-continuous-on-a-rectangle-is-riemann-integrable",
            "thm-differentiation-under-the-integral-sign-on-a-compact-rectangle",
            "thm-ftc-second-part",
            "thm-heine-cantor-metric",
            "thm-jordan-content-and-indicator-integrability",
            "thm-multidimensional-integral-properties",
            "thm-riemann-fubini-on-product-rectangles",
            "thm-heine-borel-rn"
