            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "not-applicable"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "B. Crowell, Special Relativity, revision 2020-12-10 (author-published undergraduate textbook, 246 PDF pages); signature (+---) converted to (-+++) and c = 1 formulas converted to x^0 = c t; Chapter 9 pp. 179-197: 9.1 pp. 179-182 (current vector, flux, charge conservation), 9.2 pp. 183-191 (stress-energy tensor, conservation and flux, symmetry, dust, rank-2 transformation law, pressure, perfect fluid, worked examples, energy conditions), 9.3 pp. 192-197 (Gauss's theorem, integral conservation laws, the energy-momentum vector, angular momentum); the printed 9.2.8 dominant energy condition p. 191 has the defective |P| > rho and is not used",
                "url": "https://archive.org/download/sr_20220102/sr.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "D. Tong, General Relativity, University of Cambridge Part III Mathematical Tripos (Michaelmas Term 2019); c = 1 formulas converted to x^0 = c t; 4.5.1-4.5.5 printed pp. 181-191: scalar-field action (4.42)-(4.43) and equation of motion, Hilbert energy-momentum tensor (4.46), diffeomorphism invariance and conservation (4.50), flat-space Noether form, scalar tensor (4.51), Maxwell tensor (4.52), perfect fluid (4.53) with conservation equations (4.54)-(4.55), and the flat-space conserved-charge box argument of 4.5.5",
                "url": "https://davidtong.org/pdfs/teaching/general-relativity/gr.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "physical_scope": "The isolation premise of the flat-spacetime continuum framework: total stress-energy, a bounded region of one inertial chart with vanishing side flux and finite slice integrals. Excludes leakage or radiation through the region boundary, noncompact and asymptotic settings, gravitational binding energy (no gravity here) and any claim about real apparatus; the premise is adopted, not empirically established."
        },
        {
          "id": "pthm-sr-local-stress-energy-conservation",
          "kind": "physics-theorem",
          "title": "Local conservation of stress-energy for the adopted matter models",
          "domain": "physics",
          "statement": "Under the adopted matter premises of [[post-sr-matter-models-and-evolution]] on a nonempty open $\\Omega$: (a) If $\\varphi$ is a smooth scalar field solving the adopted field equation $\\Box\\varphi=V'(\\varphi)$ on $\\Omega$, then the Hilbert stress-energy tensor of the scalar-field action ([[lem-sr-scalar-field-hilbert-stress-energy]]) satisfies $\\partial_aT^{ab}=0$ on $\\Omega$, in every inertial chart. (b) If $\\rho>0$ and the future unit field $n$ satisfy the adopted dust equations, then $T=\\rho\\,n\\otimes n$ satisfies $\\partial_aT^{ab}=0$; conversely if $\\partial_aT^{ab}=0$ and $\\rho>0$ then the dust equations hold. (c) If $\\varepsilon,P$ and the future unit field $n$ satisfy the adopted fluid equations, then $T=(\\varepsilon+P)n\\otimes n+P\\eta^{-1}$ satisfies $\\partial_aT^{ab}=0$; conversely conservation of that $T$ implies the two fluid equations. (d) For a $C^1$ symmetric tensor field prescribed on $\\Omega$ that is not obtained from one of the adopted models together with its field equations, no conservation is asserted; a conservation statement about such a field is an additional explicit premise. (e) The theorem is a conditional deduction from the adopted model equations; it asserts no interaction, force law, cross section, measurement or empirical fact, and its conclusions inherit the scope of the postulate. Under the already stated homogeneous dust reading, the tensor boost computation has the conditional physical interpretation $T'^{00}=\\gamma^2\\rho$. For comoving identical massive particles with fixed rest mass $m$, rest number density $\\nu$ and $\\rho=\\nu mc^2$, a rest rectangular parcel has boosted simultaneous volume $1/\\gamma$ times its rest volume (the parallel length contracts and transverse lengths are unchanged), so its particle density is $\\gamma\\nu$; the adopted massive-particle reading gives each particle energy $\\gamma mc^2$. Thus the two factors in $\\gamma^2\\rho$ correspond respectively to particle energy and volume/density. This is conditional model interpretation for that homogeneous particle realization, not a derivation of the continuum from microscopic dynamics, a claim about arbitrary tensors, or empirical evidence.\n\nFor the postulate's separate mathematical branch $\\Omega=\\varnothing$, the scalar, dust and fluid component formulas define the unique empty symmetric tensor field and its coordinate derivatives are empty maps. Thus each pointwise conservation equation and each pointwise dust/fluid equivalence in (a)–(c) is vacuously valid; no Hilbert-tensor, stress-energy, action-stationarity or physical-reading supplier is applied to this branch, and no nonempty parcel realization in (e) exists.",
          "strategy": "Clause (a) is [[lem-sr-scalar-field-stress-divergence-identity]] evaluated on the solutions of the adopted field equation; clause (b) is [[lem-sr-dust-conservation-equivalence]]; clause (c) is [[lem-sr-perfect-fluid-conservation-equations]]. Clause (d) records the absence of any derivation for arbitrary prescribed tensors: the local balance $\\partial_aT^{ab}=f^b$ of [[def-sr-stress-energy-tensor-and-force-density]] is a definition, and no hypothesis in this page forces $f=0$ for an arbitrary $T$. Clause (e) restates the physical scope. No empirical premise is used and the conclusions inherit only the adopted ideal model readings, with no reported measurement or empirical support. For the preserved dust energy/volume explanation, use the massive-particle energy formula of [[lem-sr-four-momentum-in-inertial-frame]] and the parallel/transverse length formulas of [[lem-sr-boost-time-length-and-velocity-formulas]] on the stipulated homogeneous rest rectangular parcel. Divide its same particle count by the contracted simultaneous volume and multiply by the particle energy. The exact tensor computation itself is $T'^{00}=\\rho(\\Lambda^0{}_0)^2=\\gamma^2\\rho$ from [[thm-sr-tensor-and-current-transformation]](iii). This physical explanation is restricted to the explicitly interpreted homogeneous dust and introduces no interaction, statistical or measured claim.",
