      "items": [
        {
          "id": "ex-sr-dust-stress-energy-under-a-boost",
          "kind": "example",
          "title": "Dust stress-energy in a boosted inertial frame",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "statement": "In an inertial frame $x$ let dust at rest have constant rest coefficient $\\rho>0$, so $T^{ab}=\\rho\\,\\delta^a_0\\delta^b_0$; the only nonzero component is $T^{00}=\\rho$. Consider the passive boost of [[def-lorentz-boost]] along the $x^1$ axis with parameter $\\beta$, $|\\beta|<1$, $\\gamma=(1-\\beta^2)^{-1/2}$: $x'^0=\\gamma(x^0-\\beta x^1)$, $x'^1=\\gamma(x^1-\\beta x^0)$, $x'^2=x^2$, $x'^3=x^3$. By the component law of [[thm-sr-tensor-and-current-transformation]]\\,(iii), $$T'^{00}=\\gamma^2\\rho,\\quad T'^{01}=T'^{10}=-\\gamma^2\\beta\\rho,\\quad T'^{11}=\\gamma^2\\beta^2\\rho,\\quad T'^{22}=T'^{33}=0,$$ all remaining components zero; equivalently $T'=\\rho\\,n'\\otimes n'$ where $n'$ is the image of $e_0$ under the boost, $n'^0=\\gamma$, $n'^1=-\\gamma\\beta$, the future unit direction of the dust in the primed frame. The primed coordinate coefficient $T'^{00}=\\gamma^2\\rho$ is the numerical factorization $\\gamma^2\\rho=\\gamma(\\gamma\\rho)$. Its source interpretation as one energy factor and one volume factor belongs to the separately adopted dust model reading; it is not an empirical identification proved by this component calculation. All primed components are constant, so $\\partial'_aT'^{ab}=0$, consistently with [[lem-sr-dust-conservation-equivalence]]. The example is a component computation; it asserts no measurement and no dynamics.",
          "strategy": "Compute $T'^{ab}=\\Lambda^a{}_c\\Lambda^b{}_dT^{cd}$ with the boost matrix $\\Lambda$ of [[def-lorentz-boost]]: only $T^{00}=\\rho$ contributes, giving the displayed components; the identification $T'=\\rho n'\\otimes n'$ follows from $n'=\\Lambda e_0$. Constancy and conservation are immediate. Source: Crowell Example 5 p. 185 and (1.106) of Carroll. No choice principle is used.",
          "deps": [
            "def-inertial-frame-and-inertial-chart",
            "def-lorentz-boost",
            "def-lorentz-form-and-inertia",
            "def-rational-power",
            "def-sr-affine-minkowski-model",
            "def-sr-stress-energy-tensor-and-force-density",
            "lem-boost-is-proper-orthochronous-with-inverse",
