        {
          "id": "ex-sr-box-flux-balance-worked",
          "kind": "example",
          "title": "The box balance identity checked on an explicit stress-energy field",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "statement": "In an inertial chart define the smooth symmetric type-$(2,0)$ field by $T^{00}=x^0$, $T^{01}=T^{10}=x^1$, $T^{11}=x^0$, with every other component zero. Its force density is $f^0=2$, $f^1=f^2=f^3=0$. Let $t_1<t_2$, $x_1<x_2$, $c_2<d_2$, $c_3<d_3$, and set $A=(d_2-c_2)(d_3-c_3)>0$, $B=[t_1,t_2]\\times[x_1,x_2]\\times[c_2,d_2]\\times[c_3,d_3]$. For $b=0$, the full four-dimensional identity of [[thm-sr-stress-balance-and-finite-flux]] reads $\\int_B f^0\\,d^4x=2A(t_2-t_1)(x_2-x_1)$. The temporal-face difference is $A(t_2-t_1)(x_2-x_1)$ and the axis-one-face difference is $A(t_2-t_1)(x_2-x_1)$; all transverse face terms vanish because $T^{2b}=T^{3b}=0$. For $b=1$, the temporal face integrals $\\pm A\\int_{x_1}^{x_2}x^1\\,dx^1$ cancel, as do the axis-one face integrals $\\pm A\\int_{t_1}^{t_2}x^0\\,dx^0$, so both sides vanish; $b=2,3$ vanish identically. For example, transverse area $A=6$, temporal length $2$ and axis-one length $3$ give bulk integral $72$ and the nonzero face differences $36+36$. This verifies the finite-box identity on a field with nonzero force density and nonzero net side flux; no physical matter model is asserted.",
          "strategy": "Compute all integrals as three-dimensional face or four-dimensional volume Riemann integrals. Repeated integration of each transverse constant factor gives A, then the FTC computes the remaining integrals. For b=0 the two nonzero face differences add; for b=1 the two opposite-face pairs separately cancel; b=2,3 and all transverse faces vanish. The full finite-box theorem supplies the sign convention and repeated-integration framework. No choice principle is used.",
