                "title": "M. Blau, Lecture Notes on General Relativity (University of Bern, last update October 5, 2026, 1052 PDF pages): Section 1.3 pp. 36-40 (Rindler metric, lines of constant rho and eta, the boundary eta = +-infinity, the lightcone equation d eta = +- rho^{-1} d rho, and item 6: the past lightcone of the accelerated observer covers asymptotically only the region xi^0 < xi^1, so every event above xi^0 = xi^1 is forever invisible) and Section 3.4 pp. 90-93 (Rindler coordinates, their ranges and the right Rindler wedge)",
                "url": "http://www.blau.itp.unibe.ch/newlecturesGR.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "Wikipedia, 'Rindler coordinates' (encyclopedia article consulted as a secondary treatment): section 'The Rindler horizon' (no observer of the congruence can receive signals from events with T >= X nor send signals to events with T <= -X) and section 'Notions of distance' (the null geodesic equation t - t_0 = log(x/x_0), the radar distance x_0 log(1 + h/x_0) between observers at x_0 and x_0 + h, the comparison with the ruler distance, and the caution that radar distance need not be symmetric under interchange)",
