          "physical_scope": "A conditional kinematic thought experiment in flat classical special relativity about two prescribed rocket worldlines with equal chart-frame accelerations and a thread whose material points are modelled as following the translated congruence. It contains no dynamical or elastic model, no material failure criterion, no force law, no measurement and no empirical claim; breaking or tension of a real thread is explicitly not asserted, and no experimental data are used or invented. The preserved C2 worldline branch uses first-order C1 kinematics and an explicit C2 four-dimensional material family. Internal length gamma(t)L is compared with gamma(0)L; initial-rest stretch is a special case, and finite endpoint simultaneity distance is not identified without a separate construction.",
          "dependency_level": 15
        }
      ],
