        {
          "id": "ex-sr-bell-congruence-rest-separation-worked",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Bell congruence worked: internal material length gamma(t)L and constant chart separation",
          "statement": "Worked computation of the internal material length for the Bell congruence of [[thm-sr-fermi-walker-and-rigid-observer-examples]] (d) and the material metric of [[lem-sr-connecting-field-stretching]]. Fix $c > 0$ and $\\alpha > 0$, let $J := (-c/\\alpha, c/\\alpha)$, put $q(t) := \\frac12 \\alpha t^2$ on $J$ and let $x_\\xi(t) := x^{-1}(c t, q(t) + \\xi, 0, 0)$ for $\\xi$ in an open interval containing $[0,L]$, $L > 0$, in the inertial chart $x$ with $x^0 = c t$. Then $|q'(t)| = \\alpha|t| < c$ on the two-sided domain $J$; write $\\beta(t) := \\alpha t/c$ and $\\gamma(t) := (1 - \\beta(t)^2)^{-1/2}$.\n\n(a) The translated congruence field is $n = \\gamma (1, \\beta, 0, 0)$ and the material field $e := \\partial_\\xi$ is the constant $(0,1,0,0)$; since $\\eta(n,e) = \\gamma \\beta$, the $h$-length of $e$ is $|e|_h = \\sqrt{\\eta(e,e) + \\eta(n,e)^2} = \\sqrt{1 + \\gamma^2 \\beta^2} = \\gamma(t)$ ([[lem-sr-connecting-field-stretching]] (a), [[thm-sr-fermi-walker-and-rigid-observer-examples]] (d)). Hence the internal longitudinal material-metric length between labels $0$ and $L$ is $|e|_h L = \\gamma(t) L > L$ for every $t \\neq 0$, with minimum $L$ at $t = 0$, while the chart-frame separation is $q(t) + L - q(t) = L$ for every $t$ in $J$.\n\n(b) The longitudinal expansion of the translated congruence is $\\theta(s,s) = \\gamma^3 q' q''/c^3 = \\gamma^3 \\alpha^2 t/c^3$, with unit rest vector $s = \\gamma(\\beta,1,0,0)$ ([[thm-sr-fermi-walker-and-rigid-observer-examples]] (d)); it vanishes at $t = 0$ and is nonzero for every $t \\neq 0$, negative for $t < 0$ and positive for $t > 0$. By [[lem-sr-connecting-field-stretching]] (b) the internal longitudinal material metric component is $G_{11} = h(e,e) = \\gamma(t)^2$ and its derivatives in geometric proper length $\\sigma = c \\tau$ are $d/d\\sigma G_{11} = 2 \\theta(e,e)$ and $d/d\\tau G_{11} = 2 c \\theta(e,e)$; with horizontal unit direction $h(e)/\\gamma = s$, equivalently the fractional rate of change of the rest separation per unit proper time is $d/d\\tau \\log\\gamma = c \\theta(s,s) = \\gamma^3 \\alpha^2 t/c^2$, and $d(\\gamma L)/d \\tau = \\gamma^4 L \\alpha^2 t/c^2$.\n\n(c) Explicit check at $\\alpha t = 3c/5$, i.e. $t = 3c/(5\\alpha)$ in $J$: $\\beta = 3/5$, $\\gamma = 5/4$ and $\\sinh$ and $\\cosh$ are not needed; the rest separation is $5L/4 > L$, the internal metric component is $G_{11} = 25/16 > 1$, the expansion is $\\theta(s,s) = (125/64)(3\\alpha/(5c^2)) = 75\\alpha/(64c^2)$, and using [L7], the fractional rest-separation rate is $c \\theta(s,s) = 75\\alpha/(64c)$. At $t = 0$ the rest separation takes its minimum $L$ and the expansion vanishes; the domain is the two-sided interval $(-c/\\alpha, c/\\alpha)$, so both the decelerating branch $t < 0$ (negative expansion) and the accelerating branch $t > 0$ (positive expansion) are included.\n\n(d) **Scope.** The length $\\gamma(t)L$ is the integral of the local rest metric over the material-label segment at common flow parameter; no finite endpoint-hyperplane distance is inferred. The computation is exact kinematics of the specified family: it uses no elasticity, no material failure criterion, no force law, no measurement and no empirical claim, and it draws no conclusion about real threads; no choice principle is used.",
          "strategy": "First use the full material family rather than a one-label-only domain: set tau(t)=integral_0^t gamma(v)^(-1)dv, sigma=c tau and Phi(sigma,xi,y,z)=(ct(sigma),q(t(sigma))+xi,y,z) with (xi,y,z) in an open subset of R^3 containing the prescribed endpoint labels and transverse zero labels. The positive derivative tauprime=1/gamma and the inverse argument in [[lem-sr-proper-time-parametrization]] give a C2 inverse (smooth here by repeating the derivative bootstrap with polynomial q), dt/dsigma=gamma/c, partial_sigma Phi=n, and four independent derivative columns. Thus [[lem-sr-connecting-field-stretching]] applies exactly before restriction to y=z=0. Direct evaluation of the family in the two-sided subluminal domain. (a) Differentiating the members with the chain rule gives tangent (c, q'(t), 0, 0) = (c/gamma) n, so the flow field is n = gamma(1, beta, 0, 0) and each member is future timelike (def-sr-four-velocity-and-four-acceleration, thm-sr-proper-time-and-observer-decomposition, thm-chain-rule); the h-length computation is eta(e,e) = 1 and eta(n,e) = gamma beta, whence h(e,e) = 1 + gamma^2 beta^2 = gamma^2 (1 - beta^2 + beta^2) = gamma^2 by gamma^{-2} = 1 - beta^2 (def-sr-observer-congruence-and-kinematics (a), lem-sr-connecting-field-stretching (a)). (b) The expansion formula is clause (d) of thm-sr-fermi-walker-and-rigid-observer-examples; the material-metric statements are clauses (b) and (c) of lem-sr-connecting-field-stretching applied to e, with theta(e,e) = gamma^2 theta(s,s) because h(e) = gamma s and theta is horizontal, although e/gamma generally differs from s. The logarithmic rate identity follows from d/dtau = gamma d/dt (while d/dsigma = (gamma/c) d/dt for sigma = c tau) and d gamma/dt = gamma^3 beta beta' = gamma^3 q'q''/c^2 (thm-chain-rule, def-derivative). (c) Substituting alpha t = 3c/5 gives beta = 3/5, gamma^{-2} = 1 - 9/25 = 16/25, gamma = 5/4, gamma^2 = 25/16, and theta(s,s) = gamma^3 alpha^2 t/c^3 = (125/64)(alpha^2 (3c/(5alpha))/c^3) = (125/64)(3alpha/(5c^2)) = 75alpha/(64c^2), so c theta(s,s) = 75alpha/(64c); the remaining values are substitutions. (d) Scope only. No choice principle is used.",
          "deps": [
