              {
                "title": "S. M. Carroll, Lecture Notes on General Relativity, arXiv:gr-qc/9712019v1 (1997), Ch. 2, 'the metric again' and the tensor transformation law, printed pp. 47-51 (PDF pp. 54-58)",
                "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/gr-qc/9712019"
              },
              {
                "title": "H. S. Reall, Part III General Relativity (Cambridge, October 12, 2022 revision), sections 1.7-1.8 on tensors and tensor fields, printed pp. 16-21 (PDF pp. 17-22)",
                "url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20230323191108id_/https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/hsr1000/part3_gr_lectures.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "J. M. Lee, Introduction to Smooth Manifolds, 2nd ed., Ch. 12 (tensor fields on manifolds)",
                "url": "https://julianchaidez.net/materials/reu/lee_smooth_manifolds.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "D. Tong, General Relativity (Cambridge Part III Mathematical Tripos, Michaelmas 2019), section 2.3.3 on tensors and tensor fields, printed pp. 72-75 (PDF pp. 79-82)",
                "url": "https://web.archive.org/web/2023id_/https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/gr/gr.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "dependency_level": 0
        },
        {
          "id": "lem-gr-covariant-two-tensor-transformation-law",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Chart independence and the transformation law of a smooth covariant 2-tensor field",
          "statement": "Let $M$ be a smooth $n$-manifold and let $A=(A_p)_{p\\in M}$ be a family\nassigning to each $p$ a covariant $2$-tensor at $p$\n([[def-gr-smooth-covariant-two-tensor-field]]). Suppose that the component\nfunctions of $A$ are $C^\\infty$ in the charts of one smooth atlas of $M$. Let\n$(U,x)$ and $(V,y)$ be overlapping smooth charts of the maximal smooth atlas and\nlet $A_{cd}$ and $A'_{ab}$ denote their coordinate representatives in the\ncharts $x$ and $y$ as specified in [[def-gr-smooth-covariant-two-tensor-field]].\nFor $q\\in U\\cap V$ put $u=y(q)$ and write $x(u):=(x\\circ y^{-1})(u)$. Then\n\n$$A'_{ab}(u) = \\sum_{c,d\\in I_n}\\frac{\\partial x^c}{\\partial y^a}(u)\\,\\frac{\\partial x^d}{\\partial y^b}(u)\\,A_{cd}\\bigl(x(u)\\bigr),$$\n\nwhere $\\partial x^c/\\partial y^a$ are the entries of the total derivative\n$D(x\\circ y^{-1})(u)$; $I_n$ is the label set of the supplier,\nso in dimension four the sum runs from $0$ through $3$. In particular $A$ is a smooth covariant $2$-tensor field\non $M$: its components are $C^\\infty$ in every chart of the maximal smooth\natlas.",
          "strategy": "Direct computation: the chain rule expresses the coordinate derivations of one chart in the other, bilinearity of each A_p converts the change of frame into the displayed double-sum law, and smoothness of the transition and its Jacobian plus closure of C^∞ maps under products give chart-independence of smoothness.",
          "deps": [
            "def-gr-smooth-covariant-two-tensor-field",
            "def-smoothly-compatible-charts",
            "def-c-r-and-smooth-maps-between-smooth-manifolds",
            "lem-coordinate-derivations-are-well-defined-derivations",
            "thm-chain-rule-for-total-derivatives",
            "thm-ck-euclidean-maps-closed-under-algebra-and-composition"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-gr-smooth-covariant-two-tensor-field": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-smoothly-compatible-charts": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-c-r-and-smooth-maps-between-smooth-manifolds": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-coordinate-derivations-are-well-defined-derivations": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-chain-rule-for-total-derivatives": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-ck-euclidean-maps-closed-under-algebra-and-composition": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "provenance": {
