          "kind": "counterexample",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "A torsion-free connection that is not metric-compatible",
          "statement": "Statement refuted: \"every torsion-free affine connection on the flat\nLorentzian four-manifold $(M,A)$ of\n[[ex-gr-minkowski-chart-as-a-lorentzian-manifold]] is compatible with the\nmetric $A$\" ([[def-gr-metric-selected-connection]]).",
          "strategy": "Explicit witness: the connection with Gamma^0_{01} = Gamma^0_{10} = 1 and all other coefficients zero is verified to be an affine connection with symmetric coefficients, hence torsion-free, while the compatibility identity fails at every point because the left side is 0 and the right side is -2.",
