        {
          "id": "ex-gr-reversing-the-timelike-field-reverses-future",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Reversing the time orientation reverses the future cone",
          "statement": "Let $(M,g,N)$ be a time-oriented smooth Lorentzian four-manifold\n([[def-gr-smooth-lorentzian-objects]]) and put $N':=-N$. Then $(M,g,N')$ is\nagain a time-oriented smooth Lorentzian four-manifold, and at every $p\\in M$\nthe future-directed causal vectors of $N'$ are exactly the past-directed causal\nvectors of $N$; equivalently $C_p^+(N')=C_p^-(N)$. In the flat model of\n[[ex-gr-minkowski-chart-as-a-lorentzian-manifold]] with $N=\\partial_0$, the\nvector $\\partial_0$ is future-directed for $N$ and past-directed for $-N$.",
          "strategy": "Direct: -N is smooth and timelike, so it is a time orientation; the pairing g(N,-N) = -g(N,N) is positive everywhere, which by the two-orientation lemma means the future cones are opposite; the flat-model evaluation on partial_0 exhibits a future vector of N that is past for -N.",
          "deps": [
