          "kind": "theorem",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Existence of a smooth future-directed tetrad field near every event",
          "statement": "Let $(M,g,N)$ be a time-oriented smooth Lorentzian four-manifold and let\n$p\\in M$ ([[def-gr-smooth-lorentzian-objects]]). Then there is an open\nneighborhood $U\\subseteq M$ of $p$ and a smooth future-directed tetrad field\n$(E_0,E_1,E_2,E_3)$ on $U$\n([[def-gr-local-frame-and-tetrad-fields]]), i.e.\n$g_q(E_A(q),E_B(q))=\\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,1,1)_{AB}$ for all $q\\in U$ with\n$E_0(q)$ future-directed for every $q\\in U$.",
          "strategy": "Construct the tetrad from constant-coefficient fields of a future orthonormal basis at the point, then normalize and orthogonalize inside the rest space with successive shrinking; smoothness of the square root and reciprocal is supplied by the injective-regular-map theorem and the derivative rules.",
