      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "ex-gr-mixed-tensor-transformation-and-contraction",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "A mixed tensor field: components in two charts and the invariance of its trace",
          "statement": "Let $M=\\mathbb R^4$ carry the flat Lorentzian metric\n$g=\\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,1,1)$ and the time orientation $N=\\partial_0$, so\nthat $(M,g,N)$ is a time-oriented smooth Lorentzian four-manifold\n([[def-gr-smooth-lorentzian-objects]]); here $g$ and $N$ enter only to place\nthe charts and the tensor field in the setting of the cited definition and\ntake no part in the computation. Let $x=(x^0,x^1,x^2,x^3)$ be the identity\nchart and let the chart $y=(y^0,y^1,y^2,y^3)$ be defined by\n\n$$y^0=x^0,\\qquad y^1=x^1+x^0,\\qquad y^2=x^2,\\qquad y^3=x^3 .$$\n\nDefine a type $(1,1)$ tensor field $T$ on $M$ by its components in the $x$\nchart,\n\n$$T^0{}_1:=1,\\qquad T^2{}_3:=x^1,\\qquad T^a{}_b:=0\\text{ otherwise}.$$\n\nThen $T$ is a smooth type $(1,1)$ tensor field. Its components in the chart\n$y$ are\n\n$$T'^0{}_0=-1,\\quad T'^0{}_1=1,\\quad T'^1{}_0=-1,\\quad T'^1{}_1=1,\\quad T'^2{}_3=y^1-y^0,\\quad\\text{others }0,$$\n\nand its trace computed in the two charts agrees: it is $0$ in both, as the\nchart-independence of contraction requires.",
          "strategy": "Compute the affine chart change and its constant Jacobians, transform a mixed tensor's components by the component law, and compare its traces in the two charts.",
          "deps": [
            "def-gr-tensor-fields-and-components",
            "def-gr-smooth-lorentzian-objects",
            "lem-gr-tensor-component-transformation-law",
            "lem-gr-contraction-of-smooth-tensor-fields"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-gr-tensor-fields-and-components": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-gr-smooth-lorentzian-objects": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-gr-tensor-component-transformation-law": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-gr-contraction-of-smooth-tensor-fields": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-generated"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "S. M. Carroll, Lecture Notes on General Relativity, arXiv:gr-qc/9712019v1 (1997), Ch. 2 'the tensor transformation law' (printed pp. 46-47; PDF pp. 53-54) and Ch. 1 'index manipulation' (printed pp. 17-19; PDF pp. 24-26)",
                "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/gr-qc/9712019"
              },
              {
                "title": "J. M. Lee, Introduction to Smooth Manifolds, 2nd ed., Ch. 12 'Tensors and Tensor Fields on Manifolds', printed pp. 316-324",
                "url": "https://julianchaidez.net/materials/reu/lee_smooth_manifolds.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "dependency_level": 5
        },
        {
          "id": "ex-gr-boosted-constant-tetrad-field",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "A constant boosted tetrad field on flat spacetime and an adapted chart",
          "statement": "Let $M=\\mathbb R^4$ carry the identity chart $x=(x^0,x^1,x^2,x^3)$ and the\nflat Lorentzian metric $g=\\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,1,1)$, with time\norientation $N=\\partial_0$. Let $\\beta\\in(-1,1)$ and let\n$\\gamma:=(1-\\beta^2)^{-1/2}>0$. Define the constant-coefficient fields\n\n$$E_0:=\\gamma(\\partial_0+\\beta\\partial_1),\\qquad E_1:=\\gamma(\\beta\\partial_0+\\partial_1),\\qquad E_2:=\\partial_2,\\qquad E_3:=\\partial_3 .$$\n\nThen $(E_0,E_1,E_2,E_3)$ is a smooth future-directed tetrad field on $M$, and\n$n:=E_0$ is an observer congruence whose integral curves have\n$x^1-\\beta x^0$, $x^2$ and $x^3$ constant; hence\n$u:=(x^0,\\,x^1-\\beta x^0,\\,x^2,\\,x^3)$ is an $n$-adapted chart. In that chart\n$n=\\gamma\\,\\partial_{u^0}$, so the coordinate field of an adapted chart need\nnot equal the congruence.",
          "strategy": "Verify that the constant boosted fields are smooth, orthonormal and future-directed, and exhibit an adapted chart for the resulting parallel congruence with an explicit inverse.",
          "deps": [
            "def-gr-local-frame-and-tetrad-fields",
            "def-gr-observer-congruence-and-adapted-charts",
            "def-gr-smooth-lorentzian-objects",
            "prop-smoothness-of-a-vector-field-is-equivalent-to-smooth-coordinate-components"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-gr-local-frame-and-tetrad-fields": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-gr-observer-congruence-and-adapted-charts": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-gr-smooth-lorentzian-objects": "mathematical-premise",
            "prop-smoothness-of-a-vector-field-is-equivalent-to-smooth-coordinate-components": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "S. M. Carroll, Lecture Notes on General Relativity, arXiv:gr-qc/9712019v1 (1997), Ch. 1 'Lorentz transformations' including boosts (printed pp. 5-7; PDF pp. 12-14) and 'four-velocity' (printed pp. 26-27; PDF pp. 33-34)",
                "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/gr-qc/9712019"
              },
              {
                "title": "H. S. Reall, Part III General Relativity (Cambridge, October 12, 2022 revision), section 1.9 on integral curves (printed pp. 21-22; PDF pp. 22-23) and section 2.3 on the 4-velocity (2.14) (printed p. 28; PDF p. 29)",
                "url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20230323191108id_/https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/hsr1000/part3_gr_lectures.pdf"
              }
            ]
