        {
          "id": "ex-gr-shearing-congruence-tetrad-and-adapted-chart",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "A shearing observer congruence on flat spacetime: tetrad, adapted chart and non-coordinate frame",
          "statement": "Let $M=\\mathbb R^4$ carry the identity chart $x$ and the flat Lorentzian metric\n$g=\\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,1,1)$ with time orientation $N=\\partial_0$. Fix\n$\\lambda>0$ and put\n\n$$W:=\\{(x^0,x^1,x^2,x^3):\\lvert\\lambda x^1\\rvert<1/2\\},\\qquad \\Omega:=\\lambda x^1,\\qquad \\gamma:=(1-\\Omega^2)^{-1/2}>0 .$$\n\nDefine the smooth fields on $W$\n\n$$E_0:=\\gamma(\\partial_0+\\Omega\\partial_2),\\quad E_1:=\\partial_1,\\quad E_2:=\\gamma(\\Omega\\partial_0+\\partial_2),\\quad E_3:=\\partial_3 .$$\n\nThen $(E_0,E_1,E_2,E_3)$ is a future-directed tetrad field on $W$, its first\nmember $n:=E_0$ is an observer congruence, the chart\n$u:=(x^0,\\,x^1,\\,x^2-\\Omega(x^1)x^0,\\,x^3)$ is $n$-adapted with\n$\\partial_{u^0}=n/\\gamma$, and the tetrad is not the coordinate frame of any\nchart, because\n$[E_0,E_1]=-\\gamma'\\partial_0-(\\gamma\\Omega)'\\partial_2$ is nonzero at every\npoint of $W$ with $x^1\\neq0$, where $\\gamma'=\\gamma^3\\lambda^2x^1$.",
          "strategy": "Construct the shearing congruence and its tetrad from a positive smooth gamma, verify orthonormality, produce an explicit adapted chart with inverse, and compute the bracket showing the frame is not a coordinate frame.",
          "deps": [
            "def-gr-observer-congruence-and-adapted-charts",
            "def-gr-local-frame-and-tetrad-fields",
            "def-gr-smooth-lorentzian-objects",
            "prop-smoothness-of-a-vector-field-is-equivalent-to-smooth-coordinate-components",
            "thm-ck-euclidean-maps-closed-under-algebra-and-composition",
            "thm-algebra-of-derivatives",
            "cor-injective-regular-ck-map-is-a-ck-diffeomorphism-onto-its-image",
            "prop-coordinate-formula-for-the-lie-bracket"
          ],
