        {
          "id": "ex-gr-observer-relative-velocity-of-a-boost",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "The relative-velocity decomposition of a boost, checked in an explicit tetrad",
          "statement": "Let $(\\mathbb R^4,g)$ and the constant boosted tetrad field\n$(E_0,E_1,E_2,E_3)$ be as in [[ex-gr-boosted-constant-tetrad-field]], with\n$E_0=n$ future unit timelike, $E_1$ unit spacelike and $g(E_0,E_1)=0$. Let\n$\\beta\\in(-1,1)$, $\\gamma=(1-\\beta^2)^{-1/2}$ and $c>0$, and set\n\n$$w:=\\beta c\\,E_1,\\qquad u:=\\gamma\\Bigl(n+\\frac{w}{c}\\Bigr)=\\gamma(E_0+\\beta E_1).$$\n\nThen $u$ is future unit timelike, $-g(n,u)=\\gamma\\ge1$, $h_n(u)=\\gamma\\beta E_1$,\n$w=c\\,h_n(u)/\\gamma$, and $g(w,w)=\\beta^2c^2=c^2(1-\\gamma^{-2})<c^2$ whenever\n$\\beta\\neq0$. This verifies the relative-velocity decomposition theorem of the\ntensors page in an explicit family.",
          "strategy": "Evaluate the relative-velocity theorem on the explicit family u = gamma(n + beta E_1), computing the metric, gamma and the spatial projection directly.",
          "deps": [
            "ex-gr-boosted-constant-tetrad-field",
            "thm-gr-observer-relative-velocity-decomposition",
            "def-gr-observer-and-rest-space",
