      "items": [
        {
          "id": "ex-gr-flat-metric-in-cylindrical-coordinates",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "A flat metric with nowhere-zero Christoffel coefficients: flat space in cylindrical coordinates",
          "statement": "On the open set $\\Omega:=\\{x\\in\\mathbb R^4:x^1>0\\}$ with the identity chart\n$x=(x^0,x^1,x^2,x^3)$ consider the metric\n$$g:=-(dx^0)^2+(dx^1)^2+(x^1)^2(dx^2)^2+(dx^3)^2,\\qquad N:=\\partial_0 ,$$\nand let $\\nabla$ be its metric-selected connection and $R$ its curvature\n([[def-gr-smooth-lorentzian-objects]], [[def-gr-metric-selected-connection]],\n[[thm-gr-nondegenerate-levi-civita-and-tensor-derivative]],\n[[def-gr-curvature-tensor-and-derived-tensors]]). Writing\n$X:=x^1\\cos x^2$ and $Y:=x^1\\sin x^2$, the chain rule gives\n$dX=\\cos x^2\\,dx^1-x^1\\sin x^2\\,dx^2$ and\n$dY=\\sin x^2\\,dx^1+x^1\\cos x^2\\,dx^2$, hence\n$dX^2+dY^2=(dx^1)^2+(x^1)^2(dx^2)^2$: the displayed metric is the flat metric\n$-(dx^0)^2+dX^2+dY^2+(dx^3)^2$ pulled back by the map\n$(x^0,x^1,x^2,x^3)\\mapsto(x^0,X,Y,x^3)$. This map is a local diffeomorphism\non all of $\\Omega$, so the metric is locally the flat Minkowski metric. It is\nnot globally injective because $x^2\\in\\mathbb R$ is an unwrapped angular\ncoordinate; on every restriction where $x^2$ ranges over an interval of\nlength less than $2\\pi$, it gives genuine cylindrical coordinates. The\ncomponent verification below uses only the displayed metric.\n\n1. The only nonzero Christoffel symbols of $\\nabla$ in this chart are\n   $$\\Gamma^1{}_{22}=-x^1,\\qquad \\Gamma^2{}_{12}=\\Gamma^2{}_{21}=\\frac{1}{x^1},$$\n   so these three coefficients are nonzero at every point of $\\Omega$,\n   while all other Christoffel symbols vanish identically.\n2. The curvature vanishes identically, $R=0$, even though the chart has\n   nonvanishing Christoffel symbols everywhere.\n3. Consequently $R(T,J)T=0$ for every geodesic tangent $T$ and every field\n   $J$ along it: for every smooth family of affinely parametrized geodesics\n   the deviation equation reads $D_s^2J=0$, with no tidal term.",
          "strategy": "Compute the Christoffel symbols of the flat metric in cylindrical coordinates and verify, by the coordinate formula and a finite case check, that the curvature vanishes identically although no connection coefficient does.",
          "deps": [
            "def-gr-smooth-lorentzian-objects",
            "def-gr-metric-selected-connection",
            "thm-gr-nondegenerate-levi-civita-and-tensor-derivative",
            "def-christoffel-symbols-of-an-affine-connection",
