        {
          "id": "lem-gr-hilbert-tensor-uniqueness",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Uniqueness of the Hilbert stress-energy tensor",
          "statement": "Let $(M,g,N)$ be an oriented time-oriented smooth Lorentzian four-manifold,\nlet $c>0$, let $S:\\mathcal D\\to\\mathbb R$ and $\\varphi$ be as in\n[[def-gr-hilbert-stress-energy-tensor]]; in particular, $\\mathcal D$ admits\nevery compactly supported metric direction at $(g,\\varphi)$. Suppose that $T$\nand $T'$ are both Hilbert stress-energy tensors of $S$ at $(g,\\varphi)$ with\nrespect to $c$ relative to the metric volume form of\n[[def-gr-metric-volume-form-and-current-flux]]. Then $T=T'$ on $M$; hence the\ndefinite article in \"the Hilbert stress-energy tensor\" is justified.",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "deps": [
