        {
          "id": "rem-gr-schwarzschild-horizon-and-singularity",
          "kind": "remark",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "Horizon versus singularity in the Schwarzschild model: a chart breakdown, a smooth null surface and a curvature obstruction",
          "statement": "The exterior datum of [[def-gr-schwarzschild-exterior-model]] is defined on the\nopen domain $r>s$ only. In its product charts the component\n$g_{11}=f(r)^{-1}=(1-s/r)^{-1}$ diverges as $r\\downarrow s$, and the chart\nframe becomes degenerate in the same limit: $g(\\partial_1,\\partial_1)=f^{-1}$,\nwhile the frame is $g$-orthogonal. This is a statement about the components of\nthe metric in one chart, not an invariant: the metric tensor field itself is\nsmooth and nondegenerate on $r>s$ ([[lem-gr-schwarzschild-extension-chart]]),\nand component divergence in a chart is not a geometric obstruction.",
          "deps": [
            "def-gr-schwarzschild-exterior-model",
            "lem-gr-schwarzschild-curvature-and-kretschmann-scalar",
