      "items": [
        {
          "id": "ex-gr-flrw-flat-power-law-check",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Direct check of the flat power-law data against the Friedmann-system equations",
          "statement": "Fix real constants $c>0$, $G_N>0$, $A>0$, $t_*>0$, $t_0\\in\\mathbb R$ and\n$w>-1$, and put\n\n$$q:=\\frac{2}{3(1+w)},\\qquad I:=(t_0,\\infty),\\qquad a(t):=A\\Bigl(\\frac{t-t_0}{t_*}\\Bigr)^{q},\\qquad \\varepsilon(t):=\\frac{3c^2q^2}{8\\pi G_N\\,(t-t_0)^2},\\qquad p(t):=w\\,\\varepsilon(t),$$\n\nwith real powers in the sense of [[def-real-power]]. Then:\n\n1. The functions $a,\\varepsilon,p$ are smooth on $I$, $a(t)>0$ and\n   $\\varepsilon(t)>0$ for every $t\\in I$, and on $I$\n\n$$H(t)=\\frac{q}{t-t_0},\\qquad \\frac{\\ddot a(t)}{a(t)}=\\frac{q(q-1)}{(t-t_0)^2}.$$\n\n2. The Friedmann-system datum $(c,G_N,0,I,0,a,\\varepsilon,p)$ satisfies the\n   Friedmann equation (F), the acceleration equation (A), the continuity\n   equation (C) and the spatial-component equation (S) of\n   [[def-gr-flrw-friedmann-system]] on $I$. In particular $w=0$ gives\n   $q=\\tfrac23$ and $w=\\tfrac13$ gives $q=\\tfrac12$.",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "deps": [
            "def-gr-flrw-friedmann-system",
            "def-real-power",
            "thm-real-power-continuity-and-derivatives",
            "def-derivative",
            "thm-algebra-of-derivatives",
            "thm-chain-rule",
            "lem-derivative-of-a-power",
            "thm-real-power-laws"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
