            "proof": "ai-generated"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "S. M. Carroll, Lecture Notes on General Relativity, arXiv:gr-qc/9712019v1 (1997), Ch. 8 (8.21)-(8.23), (8.49) and (8.53): the equation of state p = w rho, the density scaling and the flat dust and radiation power laws, printed pp. 221-222, 226-227 (PDF pp. 228-229, 233-234)",
                "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/gr-qc/9712019"
              },
              {
                "title": "D. Tong, General Relativity (Cambridge Part III Mathematical Tripos, Michaelmas 2019), section 4.6.2: the flat single-fluid power-law solutions and the dust and radiation exponents, printed p. 203 (PDF p. 210)",
                "url": "https://web.archive.org/web/2023id_/https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/gr/gr.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "dependency_level": 4
        },
        {
          "id": "ex-gr-flrw-de-sitter-system-check",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Direct check of the flat vacuum data with a cosmological parameter against the Friedmann-system equations",
          "statement": "Fix real constants $c>0$, $G_N>0$, $A>0$, $t_0\\in\\mathbb R$ and\n$\\Lambda\\in\\mathbb R$. Then:\n\n1. If $\\Lambda>0$, put $H_\\Lambda:=c\\sqrt{\\Lambda/3}$ and define\n   $a:\\mathbb R\\to(0,\\infty)$ by\n   $a(t):=A\\exp\\bigl(H_\\Lambda(t-t_0)\\bigr)$, together with\n   $\\varepsilon:=0$ and $p:=0$ on $I:=\\mathbb R$. Then the Friedmann-system\n   datum $(c,G_N,\\Lambda,I,0,a,\\varepsilon,p)$ satisfies (F), (A), (C) and\n   (S) of [[def-gr-flrw-friedmann-system]] on all of $I$.\n2. If $\\Lambda<0$, then for every nonempty open interval $I\\subseteq\\mathbb R$\n   and every smooth $a:I\\to(0,\\infty)$ the datum\n   $(c,G_N,\\Lambda,I,0,a,0,0)$ fails the Friedmann equation (F) at every point\n   of $I$; in particular no such flat vacuum datum satisfies the\n   Friedmann-system equations.",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "deps": [
