          "id": "cex-gr-flat-slab-coordinate-time-flow-incomplete",
          "kind": "counterexample",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Counterexample: on the flat slab the coordinate time has Cauchy levels but an incomplete gradient flow",
          "statement": "Statement refuted: \"on every globally hyperbolic time-oriented smooth\nLorentzian four-manifold, for every temporal function $T$ in the sense of\n[[def-gr-causal-conditions-and-global-hyperbolicity]] clause (e) the vector\nfield $X=\\nabla T/g(\\nabla T,\\nabla T)$ is complete, that is, every maximal\nintegral curve of $X$ is defined on all of $\\mathbb R$\n([[def-complete-vector-field]]).\"",
