        {
          "id": "lem-gr-galerkin-second-time-derivative-bound",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Uniform H^{s-2} Lipschitz bound for the time derivative of a Galerkin solution",
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $s\\ge5$, let $I_0$ be a compact interval inside the coefficient time domain, and let $K\\subseteq O$ be compact. Let $u_N:J\\to X_N$ be a Galerkin solution, with $J\\subseteq I_0$, values in $K$ and $\\|u_N\\|_{H^s}\\le R$. Then, uniformly in $N$,\n$$\\|\\partial_t^2u_N(t)\\|_{H^{s-2}}\\le C(A^\\mu,B,K,R,s,I_0),$$\nand consequently\n$$\\|\\partial_tu_N(t)-\\partial_tu_N(t')\\|_{H^{s-2}}\\le C(A^\\mu,B,K,R,s,I_0)|t-t'|.$$\nNo convexity of $K$ is required.",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "deps": [
