        {
          "id": "thm-gr-dust-subsidiary-and-residual-vanishing",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Subsidiary system of the dust reduction: Cartan identities, closed homogeneous residual system and vanishing of the residuals",
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]) and Dependent Choice ([[def-dependent-choice]]), carrying the analytic uniqueness and causal-curve supplier hypotheses.\n\nLet $(M,g,N)$ be the smooth time-oriented Lorentzian spacetime of [[def-gr-dust-reduction-variables-and-gauge]], with $\\gamma=-g$, and let $\\Omega\\subseteq M$ be an open solution region. Let a smooth reduced dust solution on $\\Omega$ have a nondegenerate tentative orthonormal frame for $\\gamma$ of signature $(+---)$, a metric-compatible tentative connection, reconstructed algebraic Weyl tensor $C$, prescribed curvature $\\overline R$, and dust Schouten tensor $S$ as in [[def-gr-dust-reduction-variables-and-gauge]] and [[def-gr-dust-electric-magnetic-weyl-variables-and-schouten]]. Let $\\Sigma\\subseteq\\Omega$ be a smooth spacelike embedded hypersurface for $g$, with future unit normal $\\mathfrak n$. Interpret the metric domain relative to $\\Omega$: $D_\\Omega^+(\\Sigma)$ consists of points in $\\Omega$ such that every past-inextendible causal curve in $\\Omega$ through the point meets $\\Sigma$, and $D_\\Omega^-(\\Sigma)$ is defined with future-inextendible curves ([[def-gr-spacelike-hypersurfaces-and-cauchy-sets]] clause (d), with $\\Omega$ as ambient region). Allow $r\\geq0$, with a smooth unit timelike $U$ prescribed also where $r=0$. Assume the parallel-comoving gauge and precisely the reduced equations\n$$e_0=U,\\quad\\Gamma_0{}^i{}_j=0,\\quad T^i{}_{0a}=0,\\quad\\Delta^i{}_{j0a}=0,\\quad P_{ab}=Q_{ab}=0,\\quad q=U(r)+r\\chi=0.$$\nHere $a,b=1,2,3$, the first torsion index is the output index, and $P_{ab},Q_{ab}$ are the symmetric tracefree evolution projections of [[lem-gr-dust-reduced-evolution-equations]]. No spatial torsion or spatial curvature residual is assumed zero. Define $F_{jkl}=\\nabla^i(C_{ijkl}-\\gamma_{i[k}S_{l]j})$, $P_a=F_{0a0}$, and $Q_a=-\\epsilon_a{}^{bc}F_{0bc}/2$. Then the spatial components of $(T,\\Delta)$ and the vectors $(P,Q)$ satisfy the explicit closed linear homogeneous system constructed in the proof. Its principal part is transport along $U$ for $T,\\Delta$ and the curl pair\n$$e_0(P_a)+\\tfrac12\\epsilon_a{}^{bc}e_b(Q_c),\\qquad e_0(Q_a)-\\tfrac12\\epsilon_a{}^{bc}e_b(P_c).$$\nIt is symmetric hyperbolic on every spacelike initial hypersurface, including one tilted relative to $U$. If all residuals vanish initially, they vanish on the metric domain of determination of that surface relative to $\\Omega$, namely $D_\\Omega^+(\\Sigma)\\cup D_\\Omega^-(\\Sigma)$ as in [[def-gr-spacelike-hypersurfaces-and-cauchy-sets]], with causal curves taken inside the open solution region $\\Omega$. Consequently the tentative connection is Levi--Civita, its actual curvature equals $\\overline R$, and the resulting metric satisfies the full Einstein-dust equation. The conclusion uses neither division by $r$ nor hypersurface orthogonality of $U$.",
