        {
          "id": "thm-gr-scalar-field-local-evolution",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Local Einstein-scalar evolution: smooth constrained data admit a local development, unique up to a data-fixing isometry",
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice and Dependent Choice ([[def-countable-choice]], [[def-dependent-choice]]). Fix $\\Lambda\\in\\mathbb R$, $\\kappa>0$ and one scalar model $(\\varphi,V,K_\\phi)$ of [[def-gr-scalar-field-matter-model]], with its fixed smooth potential and normalization. Let $\\Sigma$ be a smooth three-manifold with smooth Riemannian metric $h$, symmetric tensor $K_2$ and complete scalar data $(\\varphi_0,\\pi_0)$. Suppose the constraints of [[thm-gr-constraint-equations-in-normal-frame]] hold for the scalar stress computed from these data, with $\\pi_0$ the prescribed future-normal derivative. Then there is a smooth local Einstein-scalar development\n$$G_{ab}+\\Lambda g_{ab}=\\kappa T_{ab},\\qquad \\Box_g\\varphi-V'(\\varphi)=0,$$\nwith induced geometric data $(h,K_2)$, $\\varphi|_\\Sigma=\\varphi_0$ and $n(\\varphi)|_\\Sigma=\\pi_0$. The neighborhood may have position-dependent time width. The initial surface is interior to its intrinsic domain of dependence; restricting to the interior Cauchy neighborhood gives a globally hyperbolic development. Every two developments of this same fixed model and complete data are related near the entire initial surface by a data-fixing time-orientation-preserving isometry matching $\\varphi$. No potential positivity, mass sign, global existence or uniform noncompact slab is asserted ([[thm-gr-local-geometric-development]]).",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "deps": [
            "def-gr-scalar-field-matter-model",
            "lem-gr-scalar-einstein-symmetric-hyperbolic-reduction",
            "thm-gr-local-geometric-development",
            "thm-gr-constraint-equations-in-normal-frame",
            "lem-gr-harmonic-initial-data-construction",
            "def-countable-choice",
