          "id": "cex-gr-sobolev-embedding-needs-s-minus-m-above-three-halves",
          "kind": "counterexample",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "The H^1 to C^0 bound fails at s minus m equal to one: dyadic shells have an unbounded C^0/H^1 ratio",
          "statement": "Refuted statement: \"for $s=1$ and $m=0$ on $\\mathbb T^3_{2\\pi}$ (so that\n$s-m=1<\\tfrac32$) there is a constant $C$ with $\\|u\\|_{C^0}\\le C\\|u\\|_{H^1}$\nfor every $u\\in H^1$.\"",
