        {
          "id": "ex-gr-periodic-energy-method-check",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Worked E0 check: constant-coefficient transport on the three-torus, explicit solution and conserved energy",
          "statement": "On $\\mathbb T^3_{2\\pi}$ take $m=1$, $A^0=1$, $A^1=2$, $A^2=A^3=0$, $B=0$,\nso the system $(\\star)$ of [[def-gr-periodic-symmetric-hyperbolic-system]]\nreads $\\partial_tu+2\\partial_1u=0$, with $u_0\\in H^s$ real-valued and $s\\ge5$.\nThis example exhibits the explicit solution on the periodic domain,\n$u(t,x)=u_0(x^1-2t,x^2,x^3)$, verifies that it is the E0 solution, and checks\nthe weighted energy identity $e'(t)=0$ for the energy\n$e(t)=\\int u(t)^2\\,d\\mu$ directly.",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "deps": [
