        {
          "id": "ex-gr-fluid-principal-symbol-radiation",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Worked fluid symbol: eigenvalues of the principal matrix for the radiation equation of state at an explicit timelike covector",
          "statement": "Take the smooth barotropic equation of state $p:J\\to\\mathbb R$, $J=(0,\\infty)$, $p(\\epsilon)=\\tfrac13\\epsilon$, at any state $\\epsilon_0\\in J$. Then $\\epsilon+p=4\\epsilon/3>0$ on $J$ and $p'=1/3\\in(0,1)$ (so\n$c_s=1/\\sqrt3$) and at a point choose a rest frame $n$ with spatial frame\n$(e_1,e_2,e_3)$ and the future-directed timelike covector\n$\\zeta=-n^\\flat+\\tfrac12 e_1^\\flat$ (in the notation\n$\\zeta_0=\\zeta(n)=1$, $\\zeta_\\perp=\\tfrac12e_1$, so\n$\\zeta_0=1>\\tfrac12=|\\zeta_\\perp|$).\nThis example computes the matrix $A(\\zeta)$ of\n[[lem-gr-barotropic-fluid-symmetric-hyperbolic-system]] and verifies its\neigenvalues and positive definiteness explicitly.",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "deps": [
            "def-gr-barotropic-enthalpy-variable",
