          "id": "lem-gr-partial-cauchy-development",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "The causal domain of dependence of a partial Cauchy hypersurface is an open causally convex manifold on which the hypersurface is Cauchy",
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice and Dependent Choice ([[def-countable-choice]], [[def-dependent-choice]]). Let $(W,g,N)$ be a time-oriented smooth Lorentzian four-manifold and let $S\\subseteq W$ be a closed acausal edgeless embedded topological hypersurface of codimension one. Here acausality forbids causal relations between distinct points of $S$ as in [[def-gr-spacelike-hypersurfaces-and-cauchy-sets]]; **edgeless** means that no $s\\in S$ has the following property: every open neighborhood $U$ of $s$ admits $a\\in I^-_U(s)$, $b\\in I^+_U(s)$ and a timelike curve in $U$ from $a$ to $b$ avoiding $S$. All curves and inextendibility use [[def-gr-causal-curves-and-reachability]], so an inextendible end has no point limit in the specified ambient manifold. Define the ambient causal domains by\n$$D^+(S)=\\{p\\in W:\\text{every past-inextendible causal curve in }W\\text{ through }p\\text{ meets }S\\},$$\n$$D^-(S)=\\{p\\in W:\\text{every future-inextendible causal curve in }W\\text{ through }p\\text{ meets }S\\},\\qquad D(S)=D^+(S)\\cup D^-(S),$$\nas in [[def-gr-spacelike-hypersurfaces-and-cauchy-sets]]. Then:\n\n**(a)** $D(S)$ is open, contains $S$, and $D^\\pm(S)\\setminus S\\subseteq I^\\pm(S)$.\n\n**(b)** Every causal curve in $W$ with endpoints in $D(S)$ lies in $D(S)$.\n\n**(c)** Every causal curve in the induced open submanifold $D(S)$ which is inextendible there meets $S$ at exactly one parameter value. No smoothness or spacelikeness of the topological hypersurface is required.",
          "strategy": "direct",
