        {
          "id": "lem-gr-development-quotient-dense-set",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "A countable dense subset of the universal development by rational timelike exponential steps from a dense subset of the initial surface",
          "statement": "Assume the Axioms of Countable Choice and Dependent Choice\n([[def-countable-choice]], [[def-dependent-choice]]). Let $(Q,\\bar g,\\bar N,\\bar j,\\bar\\psi)$ and the\nfamily of member maps $\\pi|_{U_\\alpha}:U_\\alpha\\to Q_\\alpha\\subseteq Q$ be as\nin [[lem-gr-universal-development]] clauses (c)-(d), so that $Q$ is a\nHausdorff locally Euclidean smooth four-manifold with a smooth Lorentzian\nmetric $\\bar g$, the sets $Q_\\alpha$ are open and cover $Q$, and\n$\\bar j(\\Sigma)\\subseteq Q$ is the embedded initial surface. Then there is a\ncountable subset $D\\subseteq Q$ with:\n\n**(a)** $D\\cap\\bar j(\\Sigma)$ is dense in $\\bar j(\\Sigma)$; and\n\n**(b)** $D$ is dense in $Q$.\n\nMoreover $D$ can be chosen of the following explicit form: with\n$D_0:=S_0$ a countable dense subset of $\\bar j(\\Sigma)$, and having chosen\nonce at its first occurrence for every $x\\in D_n$ a basis $(e_1(x),\\dots,e_4(x))$ of $T_xQ$ and defined\n$$V_x^{\\mathrm{rat}}:=\\Bigl\\{\\sum_{i=1}^4q_ie_i(x):\\ q_i\\in\\mathbb Q\\Bigr\\},$$\none sets\n$$D_{n+1}:=D_n\\cup\\bigl\\{\\exp_x(v):\\ x\\in D_n,\\ v\\in V_x^{\\mathrm{rat}}\\text{ timelike, with }\\exp_x(v)\\text{ defined}\\bigr\\},\\qquad D:=\\bigcup_{n\\in\\mathbb N}D_n.$$",
          "strategy": "constructive",
          "deps": [
            "def-dependent-choice",
            "lem-gr-universal-development",
            "def-gr-development-and-data-fixing-isometry",
            "thm-gr-smooth-cauchy-temporal-splitting",
            "thm-gr-convex-normal-neighborhoods",
            "lem-gr-convex-normal-causality",
            "lem-gr-joint-exponential-diffeomorphism",
            "thm-gr-local-geodesics-and-exponential-map",
            "thm-second-countable-implies-separable",
            "def-separable-space",
            "def-second-countable-space",
            "thm-countable-union-of-countable",
            "def-countable-choice",
            "def-countable",
