                "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/cond-mat/9708200v2"
              }
            ]
          },
          "dependency_level": 3,
          "library": "physics",
          "physical_scope": "Process records with equilibrium endpoints and fixed-chart energy bookkeeping in the nonrelativistic macroscopic thermodynamic framework; trajectories may include nonequilibrium configurations and carry no regularity assumption unless a subclass adds one."
        },
        {
          "id": "post-td-bulk-additivity",
          "kind": "postulate",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "Additive separated systems and tagged bulk scaling",
          "statement": "Let $A$ and $B$ be two named subsystems with disjoint physical regions as in [[def-td-system-and-permitted-exchanges]], combined as a compound system $A\\sqcup B$ inside a declared outer boundary. The model's admitted separated pairs form a specified subset $\\mathcal C_{AB}\\subseteq D_A\\times D_B$ using [[def-subset-and-proper-subset]] and [[def-cartesian-product]]. For every pair $(x_A,x_B)\\in\\mathcal C_{AB}$, the composition map $\\kappa_{AB}:\\mathcal C_{AB}\\to D_{A\\sqcup B}$ is a function ([[def-function-space]]) adopted so the dimensioned coordinates of its output satisfy\n$$U_{A\\sqcup B}(\\kappa_{AB}(x_A,x_B))=U_A(x_A)+U_B(x_B),\\qquad V_{A\\sqcup B}(\\kappa_{AB}(x_A,x_B))=V_A(x_A)+V_B(x_B),\\qquad n_{A\\sqcup B,j}(\\kappa_{AB}(x_A,x_B))=n_{A,j}(x_A)+n_{B,j}(x_B).$$\nHere each coordinate function is the dimensioned map of [[def-td-equilibrium-state-domain]] for its material constitution, with SI units as in [[def-td-si-quantities]].\n\nHere “extensive coordinates” means precisely the named coordinates declared additive by this postulate. Amount coordinates are aligned by species label; when a species is absent from one subsystem, its zero amount is in a separately declared composition boundary, not the positive-mole chart of [[def-td-equilibrium-state-domain]]. This is an idealized composition rule: cross-interface and long-range interaction energy is omitted from $U_{A\\sqcup B}$, rather than asserted to vanish in nature. The postulate does not assert that every pair of subsystem states is physically admissible.\n\nThe framework's bulk family is a tagged family of material types. For each dimensionless scale $\\lambda>0$ the model may designate a tag $c^{(\\lambda)}$ and a subset $B_{c,\\lambda}\\subseteq D_c$ of states admitting a scaled copy, with inclusion as in [[def-subset-and-proper-subset]]. For $x=(\\hat U,\\hat V,\\hat n_1,\\ldots,\\hat n_r)\\in B_{c,\\lambda}$, the scaling map is the function $\\delta_\\lambda:B_{c,\\lambda}\\to D_{c^{(\\lambda)}}$ ([[def-function-space]]) given by $\\delta_\\lambda(x)=(\\lambda\\hat U,\\lambda\\hat V,\\lambda\\hat n_1,\\ldots,\\lambda\\hat n_r)$. The tag matters: $c^{(\\lambda)}$ is not silently identified with $c$. This postulate specifies the coordinate scaling model and energy additivity only; it does not postulate entropy additivity or exact scaling for every finite physical body.\n\nThis is an adopted physical composition rule, not a deduction from SI units or from the mathematics of Cartesian products.",
          "deps": [
            "def-td-equilibrium-state-domain",
            "def-td-system-and-permitted-exchanges",
            "def-td-si-quantities",
            "def-cartesian-product",
            "def-function-space",
            "def-subset-and-proper-subset"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-td-equilibrium-state-domain": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-td-system-and-permitted-exchanges": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-td-si-quantities": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-cartesian-product": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-function-space": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-subset-and-proper-subset": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "not-applicable"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Lieb and Yngvason, The Physics and Mathematics of the Second Law of Thermodynamics, §II.A",
                "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/cond-mat/9708200v2"
              },
              {
                "title": "Ling, Moebs, and Sanny, University Physics Volume 2, §3.1 Thermodynamic Systems",
                "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/3-1-thermodynamic-systems"
              }
            ]
          },
          "dependency_level": 3,
          "library": "physics",
          "physical_scope": "Separated macroscopic subsystems in the declared bulk family when interface and long-range interaction energy are excluded; no claim is made for interacting, surface-dominated, or gravitational systems."
        },
        {
          "id": "post-td-first-law-energy",
          "kind": "postulate",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "First-law energy balance for closed process records",
          "statement": "For every admitted $P\\in\\mathcal P_{\\mathrm{cl}}(s)$ with equilibrium endpoints $x_P^-,x_P^+\\in D_c$, fixed material constitution, zero change in center-of-mass kinetic energy, and zero change in separately tracked external-field potential energy in the fixed chart selected by the process model, the adopted model balance is\n$$U_c(x_P^+)-U_c(x_P^-)=Q[P]+W_{\\mathrm{on}}[P],$$\nwhere $U_c$ is the dimensioned energy-coordinate map of [[def-td-equilibrium-state-domain]].\n\nHere the internal-energy coordinate is evaluated in the center-of-mass rest frame as in [[def-td-galilean-rest-frame]], while $Q[P]$ and $W_{\\mathrm{on}}[P]$ are the protocol transfers defined by [[def-td-process-and-protocol]], in joules as in [[def-td-si-quantities]]. The sign convention is positive $Q$ into the system and positive $W_{\\mathrm{on}}$ for work done on it. If $P$ is adiabatic, its defining condition is $Q[P]=0$, so the same adopted balance gives $W_{\\mathrm{on}}[P]=U_c(x_P^+)-U_c(x_P^-)$.\n\nThis equation is an adopted physical postulate of the stated framework. It is not deduced here from a mechanical model or from experimental observations. Records with matter exchange or nonzero changes in omitted kinetic or external-field energy require a separately specified balance and are outside this item.",
          "deps": [
            "def-td-equilibrium-state-domain",
            "def-td-galilean-rest-frame",
            "def-td-process-and-protocol",
            "def-td-si-quantities"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-td-equilibrium-state-domain": "formulation-prerequisite",
