          "physical_scope": "Positive-temperature simple-compressible equilibrium charts coupled to a quasistatic, frictionless planar piston of constant area; other work coordinates and nonequilibrium force laws are excluded.",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "dependency_level": 6,
          "library": "physics"
        },
        {
          "id": "pthm-td-local-energy-representation",
          "kind": "physics-theorem",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "Local energy representation and thermodynamic conjugates",
          "statement": "Let $c$ be a material constitution with $r$ named species, and let $O\\subseteq D_c$ be an open dimensionless single-phase subset from [[def-td-equilibrium-state-domain]]. Its physical SI chart is $\\Omega=\\Phi_c(O)$ under the diagonal unit map $\\Phi_c$ defined in [[def-td-temperature-pressure-chemical-potential]]. Let $(U_0,V_0,n_{0,1},\\ldots,n_{0,r})\\in\\Omega$, with $U$ in joules, $V>0$ in cubic metres, and each $n_j>0$ in moles ([[def-td-si-quantities]]). On $\\Omega$, write $S_c(U,V,n)$ for the physical-coordinate representative $S_c\\circ\\Phi_c^{-1}$; its physical-coordinate partials include the unit factors as specified in [[post-td-concave-fundamental-entropy]]. Assume this representative is $C^2$ and $S_{c,U}(U_0,V_0,n_0)>0$. Then there are open neighborhoods of $(S_c(U_0,V_0,n_0),V_0,n_0)$ and $(U_0,V_0,n_0)$ on which the equation\n\n$$S_c(U,V,n)=s$$\n\nhas a unique solution $U=\\mathcal U_c(s,V,n)$ of class $C^2$. On this local chart,\n\n$$\\mathcal U_{c,s}=T_c,\\qquad \\mathcal U_{c,V}=-p_c,\\qquad \\mathcal U_{c,n_j}=\\mu_{c,j},$$\n\nwith the intensive functions defined by [[def-td-temperature-pressure-chemical-potential]]. This is a local representation only: it asserts neither global injectivity or domain coverage nor differentiability at a nonsmooth phase boundary.",
          "deps": [
            "def-td-equilibrium-state-domain",
            "def-td-si-quantities",
