        {
          "id": "pthm-td-interior-exchange-equilibrium",
          "kind": "physics-theorem",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "Interior exchange conditions from entropy maximization",
          "statement": "Consider two independent separated subsystems $A,B$ of fixed material constitutions, with states in domains $D_{c_A},D_{c_B}$ as in [[def-td-equilibrium-state-domain]], and additive total energy, volume, and aligned mole amounts as in [[post-td-bulk-additivity]] using SI coordinates ([[def-td-si-quantities]]). Let $S_{\\mathrm{tot}}=S_A+S_B$ be their adopted total entropy, and let $\\mathcal F$ be the exact feasible endpoint set fixed by the totals, retained partitions, and permitted exchanges in [[def-td-isolated-compound-feasible-set]]. Suppose $x_*=(x_A^*,x_B^*)\\in\\mathcal F$ is a stable equilibrium attaining the global entropy maximum adopted by [[post-td-entropy-maximum]]. Assume both subsystems lie in open $C^2$ single-phase charts with finite positive temperatures, and assume every exchange direction named below is locally feasible for both signs at $x_*$. Then:\n\n- If energy exchange is permitted, $T_A=T_B$.\n- If volume exchange is permitted, then $p_A/T_A=p_B/T_B$; if energy exchange is also permitted, this gives $p_A=p_B$.\n- If species $j$ can be exchanged, then $\\mu_{A,j}/T_A=\\mu_{B,j}/T_B$; if energy exchange is also permitted, this gives $\\mu_{A,j}=\\mu_{B,j}$.\n\nThe pressure equality concerns the derivative-defined pressures of [[def-td-temperature-pressure-chemical-potential]]. It is equality of mechanical piston pressures only when the coupling of [[post-td-mechanical-conjugate-identification]] applies. A retained volume or species constraint supplies no corresponding equality.",
          "deps": [
            "def-td-equilibrium-state-domain",
            "def-td-si-quantities",
            "def-td-isolated-compound-feasible-set",
            "def-td-thermal-contact-constraints",
