            "post-td-common-bulk-constitutive-law": "physical-assumption",
            "lem-tdmath-concave-affine-maximizer-and-hessian": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-chain-rule-for-total-derivatives": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-generated"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "David Tong, Statistical Physics, complete lecture notes, §1.4.3",
                "url": "https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/statphys/statmechhtml/S1.html"
              },
              {
                "title": "Daniel Arovas, Lecture Notes on Thermodynamics and Statistical Mechanics, Chapter 2, §§2.9.1–2.9.2",
                "url": "https://courses.physics.ucsd.edu/2025/Spring/physics210a/LECTURES/CH02.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "physical_scope": "C2 single-phase entropy charts and explicitly convex affine slices of permitted exchange coordinates; the radial-curvature conclusion applies only to the separately designated common-constitutive-law bulk cone with its adopted entropy transport and common reference conventions.",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "dependency_level": 6,
          "library": "physics",
          "proof_strategy": "direct"
        },
        {
          "id": "def-td-response-functions",
          "kind": "definition",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "Thermodynamic response functions on valid local charts",
          "statement": "Fix a constitution $c$ and an open dimensionless subset $O\\subseteq D_c$ in the single-phase region of [[def-td-equilibrium-state-domain]]. Its physical chart is $\\Omega=\\Phi_c(O)$, where $\\Phi_c$ is the SI coordinate map defined in [[def-td-temperature-pressure-chemical-potential]]. For fixed physical amounts $n=(n_1,\\ldots,n_r)$ with nonempty slice $\\Omega_n:=\\{(U,V):(U,V,n)\\in\\Omega\\}$, this slice is open in $\\mathbb R^2$. Use $T,p$ from [[def-td-temperature-pressure-chemical-potential]] as functions of the physical coordinates on $\\Omega_n$. For a response derivative, restrict to an open neighborhood in $\\Omega_n$ where the required natural-coordinate map is a $C^1$ diffeomorphism onto an open image, so its inverse expresses the physical $(U,V)$ as $C^1$ functions of those natural coordinates ([[def-ck-euclidean-maps-and-diffeomorphisms]]). Specifically, $C_V$ uses $(U,V)\\mapsto(T,V)$ at fixed $n$, while $C_p$, $\\kappa_T$, and $\\alpha_p$ use $(U,V)\\mapsto(T,p)$ at fixed $n$. The existence of each such local chart is a hypothesis for its response derivative, not a consequence of this definition. Each derivative uses the indicated natural variables and holds all other listed coordinates fixed.\n\nThe **constant-volume heat capacity** and **constant-pressure heat capacity** of the whole system are, where the derivatives exist and are finite,\n\n$$C_V:=\\left(\\frac{\\partial U}{\\partial T}\\right)_{V,n},\\qquad H:=U+pV,\\qquad C_p:=\\left(\\frac{\\partial H}{\\partial T}\\right)_{p,n}.$$\n\nHere $H$ is the enthalpy in joules; both heat capacities are in $\\mathrm{J\\,K^{-1}}$, not per mole. The **isothermal compressibility** and **isobaric thermal expansion coefficient** are\n\n$$\\kappa_T:=-\\frac{1}{V}\\left(\\frac{\\partial V}{\\partial p}\\right)_{T,n},\\qquad \\alpha_p:=\\frac{1}{V}\\left(\\frac{\\partial V}{\\partial T}\\right)_{p,n}.$$\n\nSince $V>0$ and the coordinates use SI units ([[def-td-si-quantities]]), $\\kappa_T$ has units $\\mathrm{Pa^{-1}}$ and $\\alpha_p$ has units $\\mathrm{K^{-1}}$. This definition asserts no sign for any response, no identity among them, and no finite value at a critical or otherwise singular chart.",
          "deps": [
            "def-td-equilibrium-state-domain",
            "def-td-si-quantities",
            "def-td-temperature-pressure-chemical-potential",
            "def-ck-euclidean-maps-and-diffeomorphisms"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-td-equilibrium-state-domain": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-td-si-quantities": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-td-temperature-pressure-chemical-potential": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-ck-euclidean-maps-and-diffeomorphisms": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "provenance": {
