      "items": [
        {
          "id": "ex-td-local-response-chart",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "Response functions in a formal logarithmic entropy chart",
          "statement": "Fix a constitution $c$ and an open dimensionless single-phase subset $O\\subseteq D_c$ whose physical chart is $\\Omega=\\Phi_c(O)$ under [[def-td-temperature-pressure-chemical-potential]]. Fix positive amounts $n=(n_1,\\ldots,n_r)$ for which the slice $\\Omega_n:=\\{(U,V):(U,V,n)\\in\\Omega\\}$ is nonempty, and assume $\\Omega_n\\subseteq\\{(U,V):U,V>0\\}$. Let $a,b>0$ have units $\\mathrm{J\\,K^{-1}}$, with reference values $U_0>0$ joules and $V_0>0$ cubic metres. Stipulate the smooth physical-coordinate entropy representative on $\\Omega_n$ (denoted by $S_c(U,V,n)$ as in [[def-td-temperature-pressure-chemical-potential]]) by\n\n$$S(U,V)=a\\ln(U/U_0)+b\\ln(V/V_0).$$\n\nApplying the definitions on this chart gives\n\n$$T=U/a,\\qquad p=bT/V,\\qquad C_V=a,\\qquad C_p=a+b,\\qquad \\kappa_T=1/p,\\qquad \\alpha_p=1/T.$$\n\nThis is a formal chart calculation, not measured data and not a claim that this entropy satisfies the track's tagged bulk-scaling postulate for a fixed material type.",
          "deps": [
            "def-td-temperature-pressure-chemical-potential",
            "def-td-response-functions",
            "def-natural-logarithm",
            "thm-logarithm-derivative-and-integral"
