      "items": [
        {
          "id": "ex-td-response-chart-failure",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "A smooth chart with no isothermal pressure inverse",
          "statement": "Fix the amount of substance and stipulate the local entropy representative\n\n$$S(U,V)=C\\ln(U/U_*)+aV+S_0$$\n\non the open domain $U>0$, $V>0$, where $C>0$ has units $\\mathrm{J\\,K^{-1}}$, $U_*>0$ has units joules, $a>0$ has units $\\mathrm{J\\,K^{-1}\\,m^{-3}}$, and $S_0$ has units $\\mathrm{J\\,K^{-1}}$. This chart is finite, C2, concave, and has $S_U>0$. It illustrates that a smooth positive-temperature chart need not admit pressure as a local coordinate at fixed temperature.\n\nThe displayed entropy is $S^{\\rm SI}$ in physical SI coordinates. For this constructed local model, choose the positive-amount open neighborhood stated here (or any positive neighborhood of the fixed amount, extending this entropy independently of amount) and let $O_c$ be the numerical preimage of that product patch under $\\Phi_c(\\hat U,\\hat V,\\hat n)=(\\hat U\\,\\mathrm J,\\hat V\\,\\mathrm{m^3},\\hat n\\,\\mathrm{mol})$. Declare $O_c$ as the model's local state-domain patch and set $S_c=S^{\\rm SI}\\circ\\Phi_c$. The derivatives below are those of $S^{\\rm SI}=S_c\\circ\\Phi_c^{-1}$ on $\\Phi_c(O_c)$, exactly as in [[def-td-temperature-pressure-chemical-potential]]. This supplies the numerical-to-SI chart identification for the formal witness, with no assertion of a measured material or a global constitutive extension.",
          "deps": [
            "def-td-si-quantities",
            "def-td-temperature-pressure-chemical-potential",
            "def-td-response-functions",
            "def-natural-logarithm",
            "thm-logarithm-derivative-and-integral"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-td-si-quantities": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-td-temperature-pressure-chemical-potential": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-td-response-functions": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-natural-logarithm": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-logarithm-derivative-and-integral": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-generated"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Daniel Arovas, Thermodynamics and Statistical Mechanics, §2.10.5",
                "url": "https://phys.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Thermodynamics_and_Statistical_Mechanics/Book:_Thermodynamics_and_Statistical_Mechanics_(Arovas)/02:_Thermodynamics/2.10:_Applications_of_Thermodynamics"
              }
            ]
          },
          "dependency_level": 7,
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "physical_scope": "Constructed local concave entropy chart at fixed composition, used only to show failure of a response-coordinate inverse; it is not a measured material equation of state or a complete bulk-family model.",
          "generation": {
            "role": "example"
          },
          "library": "physics",
          "proof_strategy": "direct"
        },
        {
          "id": "ex-td-nonzero-isothermal-work-loop",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "Nonzero pressure work around a closed model cycle",
          "statement": "Fix a material constitution and amount $n$ and stipulate, on $U>0$ and $0<V<1/b$, the entropy chart\n\n$$S(U,V)=C\\ln(U/U_*)+aV-\\frac{ab}{2}V^2+S_0,$$\n\nwhere $C>0$ is in $\\mathrm{J\\,K^{-1}}$, $U_*>0$ is in joules, $a>0$ is in $\\mathrm{J\\,K^{-1}\\,m^{-3}}$, $b>0$ is in $\\mathrm{m^{-3}}$, and $S_0$ is in $\\mathrm{J\\,K^{-1}}$. Consider a piecewise-C1 quasistatic cycle with isotherms $T_1>T_2>0$ and volumes $0<V_1<V_2<1/b$, joined by isochoric legs. The ideal frictionless piston load tracks the equilibrium pressure, controlled heat exchange is permitted along the path, and no other work coordinate acts. The calculation shows that the pressure-work integral is not an endpoint increment.\n\nThe displayed entropy is $S^{\\rm SI}$ in physical SI coordinates. For this constructed local model, choose the positive-amount open neighborhood stated here (or any positive neighborhood of the fixed amount, extending this entropy independently of amount) and let $O_c$ be the numerical preimage of that product patch under $\\Phi_c(\\hat U,\\hat V,\\hat n)=(\\hat U\\,\\mathrm J,\\hat V\\,\\mathrm{m^3},\\hat n\\,\\mathrm{mol})$. Declare $O_c$ as the model's local state-domain patch and set $S_c=S^{\\rm SI}\\circ\\Phi_c$. The derivatives below are those of $S^{\\rm SI}=S_c\\circ\\Phi_c^{-1}$ on $\\Phi_c(O_c)$, exactly as in [[def-td-temperature-pressure-chemical-potential]]. This supplies the numerical-to-SI chart identification for the formal witness, with no assertion of a measured material or a global constitutive extension.",
          "deps": [
            "def-td-equilibrium-state-domain",
            "def-td-si-quantities",
            "def-td-process-and-protocol",
            "def-td-temperature-pressure-chemical-potential",
