          "id": "ex-td-carnot-engine-600-300",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "A symbolic 600 K and 300 K engine bound",
          "statement": "Consider a hypothetical ideal-reservoir engine cycle with $T_h=600\\,\\mathrm K$ and $T_c=300\\,\\mathrm K$, with all the assumptions of [[pthm-td-carnot-engine-bound]]. Its efficiency is at most $1/2$. This is a model calculation, not an observed performance.",
