          "justified_by": [],
          "proof_strategy": "direct",
          "statement": "For the finite or explicitly enumerated countable index set $I$ of [[def-tdmath-diagonal-operator-model]], the inner-product space $\\ell^2(I)$ is complete and therefore a complex Hilbert space, with inner product linear in the first variable. For any real family $(E_i)$, the displayed domain $D(H_E)$ is a linear subspace containing every finite-support vector, is dense in $\\ell^2(I)$, and $x\\mapsto(E_ix_i)_i$ is a linear map from that domain into $\\ell^2(I)$. These assertions also hold for the empty finite index set."
        },
