          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Let $\\Omega_0$ be a nonempty finite set, let $E:\\Omega_0\\to\\mathbb R$, and fix $\\beta\\in\\mathbb R$. Define $Z_1=\\sum_{i\\in\\Omega_0}e^{-\\beta E_i}$ and the canonical law $q_i=e^{-\\beta E_i}/Z_1$, and define $\\bar E:=\\sum_iq_iE_i$. For $N\\ge1$, on $\\Omega_0^N$ define $H_N(i_1,\\ldots,i_N)=\\sum_{k=1}^NE_{i_k}$ with the product law. Then $Z_N=Z_1^N$, $\\mathbb E[H_N/N]=\\bar E$, and $\\operatorname{Var}(H_N/N)=\\operatorname{Var}_q(E)/N$. Consequently, for every $\\varepsilon>0$, $\\mathbb P(|H_N/N-\\bar E|\\ge\\varepsilon)\\le\\operatorname{Var}_q(E)/(N\\varepsilon^2)$. If $\\beta\\ne0$, the mathematical free-energy density $-\\beta^{-1}N^{-1}\\log Z_N$ is exactly $-\\beta^{-1}\\log Z_1$ for every $N$.",
          "strategy": "proof_strategy: direct; complete numbered argument is in items/thm-tdmath-independent-bulk-limit.md and its proof contract.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "David Tong, Statistical Physics, author-hosted complete HTML chapter text",
                "url": "https://davidtong.org/teaching/statistical-physics/statmechhtml/S1",
                "locator": "Full author-hosted HTML chapter text read; canonical/grand-canonical ensembles §§1.3–1.4 pp.17–30; two-state model §1.2.3 pp.11–14; 1D Ising §5.3.1 pp.156–157."
