            "thm-exponential-beats-every-polynomial": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-logarithm-derivative-and-integral": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-natural-logarithm-laws": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-nth-roots-exist": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-real-power-continuity-and-derivatives": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Fix $\\beta>0$ and $J,h\\in\\mathbb R$. For $N\\ge2$, let $s_i\\in\\{-1,1\\}$, $s_{N+1}=s_1$, $H_N(s)=-J\\sum_{i=1}^Ns_is_{i+1}-h\\sum_{i=1}^Ns_i$, and $Z_N=\\sum_se^{-\\beta H_N(s)}$. Define $\\cosh x:=(e^x+e^{-x})/2$, $\\sinh x:=(e^x-e^{-x})/2$, and $T_{s,t}:=e^{\\beta Jst+\\beta h(s+t)/2}$. Then $Z_N=\\operatorname{tr}(T^N)=\\lambda_+^N+\\lambda_-^N$, where $\\lambda_\\pm=e^{\\beta J}\\cosh(\\beta h)\\pm\\sqrt{e^{2\\beta J}\\sinh^2(\\beta h)+e^{-2\\beta J}}$ and $\\lambda_+>|\\lambda_-|$. Therefore $N^{-1}\\log Z_N\\to\\log\\lambda_+$. On every compact subset of $(0,\\infty)\\times\\mathbb R^2$ in $(\\beta,J,h)$, the limit and its derivatives of every fixed finite order converge uniformly. This is a result for the specified one-dimensional periodic two-state model only.",
          "strategy": "proof_strategy: direct; complete numbered argument is in items/thm-tdmath-ising-chain-limit.md and its proof contract.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
