          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "For the lattice models of [[thm-tdmath-finite-range-lattice-pressure-limit]], write $p_L(\\gamma)=L^{-d}\\log Z_L(\\gamma)$ and let $p(\\gamma)=\\lim_Lp_L(\\gamma)$ on an open interval $J\\subseteq(0,\\infty)$. At finite $L$, use the canonical law $\\mathbb P_{\\gamma,L}(s):=e^{-\\gamma H_L(s)}/Z_L(\\gamma)$ and its finite expectation $\\mathbb E_{\\gamma,L}$. If $p$ is differentiable at $\\beta\\in J$, then $\\mathbb E_{\\beta,L}[H_L]/L^d\\to e:=-p'(\\beta)$. For every $\\varepsilon>0$ there are $c>0$ and $L_0$ such that for $L\\ge L_0$, $\\mathbb P_{\\beta,L}(|H_L/L^d-e|\\ge\\varepsilon)\\le2e^{-cL^d}$. No energy-density limit is asserted at a nondifferentiability point.",
          "strategy": "proof_strategy: direct; complete numbered argument is in items/thm-tdmath-limiting-derivative-and-concentration.md and its proof contract.",
