        {
          "id": "lem-tdmath-conditional-memory-entropy",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Conditional entropy of finite memory given side information",
          "reference": "research/physics-td-qft-rpm-62-2026-10-14-batch-11.notes.md#item-inventory",
          "design_state": "Complete draft proof recorded; scoped checks and independent review remain pending.",
          "dependency_level": 0,
          "deps": [
            "def-finite-probability-space-and-event",
            "def-finite-sum",
            "def-natural-logarithm",
            "thm-natural-logarithm-laws"
          ],
          "justified_by": [],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-finite-probability-space-and-event": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-finite-sum": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-natural-logarithm": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-natural-logarithm-laws": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Let $M$ and $R$ take values in finite sets under a joint probability law $p(m,r)\\ge0$ with $\\sum_{m,r}p(m,r)=1$. For any finite random variable $Y$ with law $p_Y$, define its Shannon entropy by $H(Y):=-\\sum_{y:p_Y(y)>0}p_Y(y)\\log p_Y(y)$; for a pair, $H(M,R)$ means this definition applied to its joint law. Put $a_r:=\\sum_m p(m,r)$ and, when $a_r>0$, $q(m|r):=p(m,r)/a_r$. Thus $H(R)=-\\sum_{r:a_r>0}a_r\\log a_r$. Define $H(M|R):=\\sum_{r:a_r>0}a_r[-\\sum_{m:q(m|r)>0}q(m|r)\\log q(m|r)]$. Then $H(M,R)=H(R)+H(M|R)$ and $H(M|R)\\ge0$.",
          "strategy": "proof_strategy: direct; complete numbered argument is in items/lem-tdmath-conditional-memory-entropy.md and its proof contract.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "David Tong, Statistical Physics, author-hosted complete HTML chapter text",
                "url": "https://davidtong.org/teaching/statistical-physics/statmechhtml/S1",
                "locator": "Full author-hosted HTML chapter text read; canonical/grand-canonical ensembles §§1.3–1.4 pp.17–30; two-state model §1.2.3 pp.11–14; 1D Ising §5.3.1 pp.156–157."
              },
              {
                "title": "Daniel Arovas, Lecture Notes on Thermodynamics and Statistical Mechanics (work in progress, dated 12 October 2026)",
                "url": "https://courses.physics.ucsd.edu/2025/Spring/physics210a/LECTURES/STATMECH.pdf",
                "locator": "Complete 635-page PDF retrieved; ensembles and traces §§4.2–4.6 pp.192–217; Bose/Fermi models §§5.6–5.7 pp.277–303; 1D Ising §6.2.2 pp.330–333."
              }
            ]
          },
          "library": "mathematics",
          "proof_strategy": "direct"
        },
        {
          "id": "lem-tdmath-mutual-information",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Mutual information of finite random variables",
          "reference": "research/physics-td-qft-rpm-62-2026-10-14-batch-11.notes.md#item-inventory",
          "design_state": "Complete draft proof recorded; scoped checks and independent review remain pending.",
          "dependency_level": 1,
          "deps": [
            "cor-mean-value-theorem",
            "def-finite-probability-space-and-event",
            "def-finite-sum",
            "def-natural-logarithm",
            "lem-tdmath-conditional-memory-entropy",
            "thm-logarithm-derivative-and-integral"
          ],
          "justified_by": [],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "cor-mean-value-theorem": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-finite-probability-space-and-event": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-finite-sum": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-natural-logarithm": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-tdmath-conditional-memory-entropy": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-logarithm-derivative-and-integral": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "For finite random variables $M,R$ with joint law $p(m,r)$ and marginals $p_M,p_R$, use the entropy definition $H(Y)$ of [[lem-tdmath-conditional-memory-entropy]] for $Y=M,R,(M,R)$. Define $I(M;R):=\\sum_{p(m,r)>0}p(m,r)\\log\\frac{p(m,r)}{p_M(m)p_R(r)}$. Then $I(M;R)=H(M)+H(R)-H(M,R)=H(M)-H(M|R)\\ge0$, with equality exactly when $p(m,r)=p_M(m)p_R(r)$ for every pair.",
          "strategy": "proof_strategy: direct; complete numbered argument is in items/lem-tdmath-mutual-information.md and its proof contract.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
