          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $\\mathcal H\\ne\\{0\\}$ be a complex Hilbert space and let $A$ be self-adjoint with regular Borel projection-valued measure $E$ from [[thm-spectral-theorem-for-unbounded-self-adjoint-operators]], with $E((-\\infty,a))=0$ for finite $a\\in\\mathbb R$. For each $\\gamma>0$, define the bounded Gibbs operator $K_\\gamma:=\\Phi_E(f_\\gamma)$ using the bounded Borel PVM integral of [[thm-bounded-borel-pvm-integral]], where $f_\\gamma(\\lambda)=e^{-\\gamma\\lambda}$ for $\\lambda\\ge a$ and $f_\\gamma(\\lambda)=e^{-\\gamma a}$ for $\\lambda<a$. Fix $\\beta>0$ and suppose $K_\\beta$ is trace class in the sense of [[def-trace-class-operator]]. Then $K_\\beta$ is injective and has a finite or countable orthonormal basis $(u_j)$ of $\\mathcal H$ with $Au_j=E_ju_j$, $E_j\\ge a$, and $K_\\beta u_j=e^{-\\beta E_j}u_j$. Its partition function $Z_\\beta:=\\operatorname{Tr}K_\\beta=\\sum_j e^{-\\beta E_j}$ is positive and finite, and $\\rho_\\beta:=K_\\beta/Z_\\beta$ is positive with $\\operatorname{Tr}\\rho_\\beta=1$. For every $B\\in\\mathcal B(\\mathcal H)$, $\\operatorname{Tr}(\\rho_\\beta B)=\\sum_j(e^{-\\beta E_j}/Z_\\beta)\\langle Bu_j,u_j\\rangle$ absolutely. Further, let $J\\subset(0,\\infty)$ be open and suppose that for every compact $C\\subset J$ there is a summable family $a_j\\ge0$ with $(1+|E_j|^2)e^{-\\gamma E_j}\\le a_j$ for all $j$ and $\\gamma\\in C$. Then for each $\\gamma\\in J$, $K_\\gamma$ is trace class with partition function $Z_\\gamma:=\\operatorname{Tr}K_\\gamma=\\sum_j e^{-\\gamma E_j}$. With $p_j(\\gamma):=e^{-\\gamma E_j}/Z_\\gamma$, define $\\bar E_\\gamma:=\\sum_jp_j(\\gamma)E_j$, $\\operatorname{Var}_\\gamma(E):=\\sum_jp_j(\\gamma)(E_j-\\bar E_\\gamma)^2$, and $S_\\gamma:=-\\sum_jp_j(\\gamma)\\log p_j(\\gamma)$. These quantities are finite and satisfy $-\\partial_\\gamma\\log Z_\\gamma=\\bar E_\\gamma$, $\\partial_\\gamma^2\\log Z_\\gamma=\\operatorname{Var}_\\gamma(E)$, and $S_\\gamma=\\log Z_\\gamma+\\gamma\\bar E_\\gamma$ as in [[thm-tdmath-summable-canonical-differentiation]]. Countable nonnegative sums use the finite-subsum supremum convention of [[def-tdmath-countable-canonical-model]].",
          "strategy": "proof_strategy: direct; complete numbered argument is in items/thm-tdmath-general-trace-gibbs-model.md and its proof contract.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
