          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "For $q\\in(0,1)$, the bosonic geometric law on $n\\in\\mathbb N_0$ with weights $(1-q)q^n$ has mean $q/(1-q)$ and variance $q/(1-q)^2=\\mathbb E[n](1+\\mathbb E[n])$; its relative standard deviation tends to $1$ as $q\\uparrow1$. The fermionic two-state law on $n\\in\\{0,1\\}$ with weights $1/(1+q)$ and $q/(1+q)$ has mean $q/(1+q)$ and variance $q/(1+q)^2=\\mathbb E[n](1-\\mathbb E[n])$. Here Bose and Fermi name these explicitly specified counting laws; no claim about a physical preparation is made.",
          "strategy": "proof_strategy: direct; complete numbered argument is in items/lem-tdmath-bose-fermi-mode-fluctuations.md and its proof contract.",
