        {
          "id": "def-tdmath-regular-energy-shell",
          "kind": "definition",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Regular energy shell and weighted area measure",
          "reference": "items/def-tdmath-regular-energy-shell.md#definition",
          "design_state": "Complete draft carrier authored; scoped checks and independent review remain pending.",
          "dependency_level": 0,
          "deps": [
            "def-lebesgue-measure-and-the-lebesgue-sigma-algebra",
            "thm-euclidean-implicit-function-theorem"
          ],
          "justified_by": [],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-lebesgue-measure-and-the-lebesgue-sigma-algebra": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-euclidean-implicit-function-theorem": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Let $O\\subset\\mathbb R^m$, $m\\ge2$, be open, let $H\\in C^2(O,\\mathbb R)$, and let $J\\subset\\mathbb R$ be open. An energy $E\\in J$ is **regular** if $\\nabla H(x)\\ne0$ for every $x\\in\\Sigma_E:=H^{-1}(\\{E\\})$. By the implicit-function theorem, a neighborhood of each point of a nonempty regular level is a graph $x_i=h(z)$.\n\nIn a graph chart, use the local area density $\\sqrt{1+|\\nabla h(z)|^2}\\,dz$, where $dz$ is $(m-1)$-dimensional Lebesgue measure. A **graph partition** on $\\Sigma_E$ is a locally finite graph-chart cover with nonnegative smooth functions $\\chi_a$ supported in their respective charts and summing to one on the level. Whenever such a partition is supplied, define the candidate weighted shell integral by\n$$\\mu_E(g):=\\sum_a\\int g(z,h_a(z))\\chi_a(z,h_a(z))|\\partial_iH(z,h_a(z))|^{-1}\\,dz$$\nfor nonnegative Borel $g$. Its independence from the chosen chart partition, and its equality with $\\int_{\\Sigma_E}g|\\nabla H|^{-1}dA_E$, are proved in the theorem on this page. If $0<\\mu_E(1)<\\infty$, the **microcanonical shell probability** is $\\widehat\\mu_E:=\\mu_E/\\mu_E(1)$.\n\nThis is an explicit chart-based definition, not a formal delta distribution $\\delta(H-E)$. Critical levels are excluded.",
          "strategy": "Definition carrier is in items/def-tdmath-regular-energy-shell.md.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "not-applicable"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "David Tong, Statistical Physics, complete author-hosted lecture text",
