          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Fix dimension $d\\ge1$, particle mass $m>0$, action reference $h>0$, inverse energy $\\beta>0$, and positive cube volumes $V_N$ with $N/V_N\\to\\rho\\in(0,\\infty)$. For $N$ indistinguishable classical noninteracting particles in a cube of volume $V_N$, use the phase-space reference $dq\\,dp/(N!h^{dN})$ and Hamiltonian $H_N(q,p)=\\sum_{i=1}^N|p_i|^2/(2m)$. Define $\\lambda_\\beta=h\\sqrt{\\beta/(2\\pi m)}$. Then the dimensionless partition integral and free-energy limits are\n$$Z_N=\\frac{V_N^N}{N!\\lambda_\\beta^{dN}},\\quad\\frac{-\\beta^{-1}\\log Z_N}{N}\\longrightarrow\\beta^{-1}[\\log(\\rho\\lambda_\\beta^d)-1],\\quad\\frac{-\\beta^{-1}\\log Z_N}{V_N}\\longrightarrow\\beta^{-1}\\rho[\\log(\\rho\\lambda_\\beta^d)-1].$$\nThere is also the following finite-momentum-block limit. Let $M=dN$, let $G_1,\\ldots,G_M$ be independent standard normal variables, set $A_N=M^{-1}\\sum_{a=1}^MG_a^2$, and define canonical momenta $P_a^{\\rm can}=\\sqrt{m/\\beta}\\,G_a$ and shell-prepared momenta $P_a^{\\rm sh}=\\sqrt{m/\\beta}\\,G_a/\\sqrt{A_N}$. The shell-prepared vector has exactly energy $dN/(2\\beta)$, and for every fixed $r$ and bounded continuous $\\psi:\\mathbb R^r\\to\\mathbb R$,\n$$\\mathbb E\\psi(P_1^{\\rm sh},\\ldots,P_r^{\\rm sh})\\longrightarrow\\mathbb E\\psi(P_1^{\\rm can},\\ldots,P_r^{\\rm can}).$$\nThis is weak convergence for each fixed block in this free-particle model. The shell preparation is the stated normalized-Gaussian construction, and no finite-width shell or interacting-gas equivalence is asserted.",
          "strategy": "proof_strategy: direct; complete argument is in items/thm-tdmath-continuous-ideal-gas-block-limit.md and its proof contract.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
