        {
          "id": "thm-tdmath-hamiltonian-measure-and-recurrence",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Hamiltonian volume, recurrence, and ergodic scope",
          "reference": "items/thm-tdmath-hamiltonian-measure-and-recurrence.md#statement",
          "design_state": "Complete draft carrier authored; scoped checks and independent review remain pending.",
          "dependency_level": 0,
          "deps": [
            "cor-birkhoff-ergodic-theorem-for-ergodic-probability-systems",
            "cor-symplectic-manifolds-have-a-canonical-orientation-and-volume-form",
            "def-axiom-of-choice",
            "def-ergodic-measure-preserving-system",
            "def-hamiltonian-vector-field-and-hamiltonian-function",
            "def-integrable-real-and-complex-functions-and-their-integrals",
            "def-measure-preserving-transformation-and-system",
            "def-probability-measure",
            "def-symplectic-form-and-symplectic-manifold",
            "thm-birkhoff-ergodic-theorem",
            "thm-integrals-are-invariant-under-measure-preserving-maps",
            "thm-liouville-volume-preservation",
            "thm-poincare-recurrence-for-finite-measure-preserving-systems"
          ],
          "justified_by": [],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "cor-birkhoff-ergodic-theorem-for-ergodic-probability-systems": "mathematical-premise",
            "cor-symplectic-manifolds-have-a-canonical-orientation-and-volume-form": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-axiom-of-choice": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-ergodic-measure-preserving-system": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-hamiltonian-vector-field-and-hamiltonian-function": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-integrable-real-and-complex-functions-and-their-integrals": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-measure-preserving-transformation-and-system": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-probability-measure": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-symplectic-form-and-symplectic-manifold": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-birkhoff-ergodic-theorem": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-integrals-are-invariant-under-measure-preserving-maps": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-liouville-volume-preservation": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-poincare-recurrence-for-finite-measure-preserving-systems": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $(M,\\omega)$ be a smooth $2n$-dimensional symplectic manifold and $H\\in C^\\infty(M,\\mathbb R)$, with Hamiltonian field defined by $\\iota_{X_H}\\omega=dH$. Wherever its local flow $\\phi_t$ is defined, it preserves the symplectic form and the volume measure $m$ determined by $\\omega^n/n!$. No completeness is asserted. For a region $R$ on which a nonzero-time map $T=\\phi_\\tau$ and all its iterates are defined, $T$ is a measure-preserving transformation. If $m(R)<\\infty$, then for every measurable $E\\subseteq R$, almost every point of $E$ returns to $E$ infinitely often under forward iteration.\n\nIf $m(R)=1$ and $T$ is ergodic, then for every $f\\in L^1(R,m)$ the averages $N^{-1}\\sum_{j=0}^{N-1}f(T^jx)$ converge almost everywhere and in $L^1$ to $\\int_Rf\\,dm$. Without ergodicity, the limit is the invariant conditional expectation supplied by Birkhoff's theorem, not necessarily the space mean. Finally, if each stated time map $\\phi_t$ is a diffeomorphism of a finite invariant region $R$, a density $p_0\\ge0$ with $\\int_Rp_0\\,dm=1$ and $\\int_R|p_0\\log p_0|\\,dm<\\infty$ transports by $p_t=p_0\\circ\\phi_{-t}$ with conserved fine-grained entropy $-k_B\\int_Rp_t\\log p_t\\,dm$, using $0\\log0=0$. Volume preservation alone does not imply ergodicity or a time-average/ensemble identity.",
          "strategy": "proof_strategy: direct; complete argument is in items/thm-tdmath-hamiltonian-measure-and-recurrence.md and its proof contract.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "David Tong, Kinetic Theory, Part 2",
                "url": "https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/kintheory/two.pdf",
                "locator": "Complete 39-page lecture-note part retrieved and read; §2.1, pp.14–16, Liouville phase-space volume; §§2.2–2.3, pp.20–35, Boltzmann equation and H-theorem."
