            "thm-logarithm-derivative-and-integral": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-natural-logarithm-laws": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Let $A=\\{1,\\ldots,q\\}$, $q\\ge1$, have real energies $e_j$, and fix finite $\\beta\\in\\mathbb R$. Set $Z_1=\\sum_j e^{-\\beta e_j}$, $p_j=e^{-\\beta e_j}/Z_1>0$, and $E=\\sum_jp_je_j$. For each $N\\ge1$, let $\\delta_N\\ge q\\sum_{j=1}^q|e_j|$ and $\\delta_N/N\\to0$. Define the shell $\\Gamma_N=\\{i\\in A^N:|\\sum_{r=1}^Ne_{i_r}-NE|\\le\\delta_N\\}$ and the uniform law on that shell. For probability laws $\\mu,\\nu$ on the finite set $A^k$, total variation distance means $\\frac12\\sum_{x\\in A^k}|\\mu(x)-\\nu(x)|$. Then $\\Gamma_N$ is nonempty for every $N$; for each fixed $k\\ge1$, the first $k$-site marginal (for $N\\ge k$) converges in that distance to $p^{\\otimes k}$; and\n$$\\frac1N\\log|\\Gamma_N|\\longrightarrow H(p):=-\\sum_{j=1}^qp_j\\log p_j.$$\nThe conclusion is for this finite alphabet, additive energy, exact shell width and uniform shell law. It does not assert finite-size equality or equivalence for interacting or continuous models.",
