          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume the filtered probability space, Brownian increment hypothesis, and initial data of [[def-tdmath-ornstein-uhlenbeck-equation]], including $\\mathbb E X_0^2<\\infty$ and future increments independent of $\\mathcal F_0$. For $\\gamma,\\sigma>0$, on every finite time interval the process\n$$X_t=e^{-\\gamma t}X_0+\\sigma e^{-\\gamma t}\\int_0^t e^{\\gamma s}\\,dB_s$$\nhas a continuous adapted version, solves the stated Ornstein–Uhlenbeck integral equation, and is the unique continuous solution driven by the same $(X_0,B)$. Put $V=\\sigma^2/(2\\gamma)$. For $0\\le s<t$, its transition law conditional on $\\mathcal F_s$ is normal with mean $e^{-\\gamma(t-s)}X_s$ and variance $V(1-e^{-2\\gamma(t-s)})$. Consequently\n$$\\mathbb E X_t=e^{-\\gamma t}\\mathbb E X_0,\\qquad\\operatorname{Var}(X_t)=e^{-2\\gamma t}\\operatorname{Var}(X_0)+V(1-e^{-2\\gamma t}).$$\nFrom any such initial law, $X_t$ converges in distribution to $N(0,V)$. If $X_0\\sim N(0,V)$ and is independent of future Brownian increments, the process is stationary Gaussian with covariance $C(\\tau)=Ve^{-\\gamma|\\tau|}$, and its transition kernel satisfies detailed balance with the $N(0,V)$ density. Its transition density solves the Fokker–Planck equation for positive time. Under the convention $S(\\omega)=(2\\pi)^{-1}\\int_{\\mathbb R}C(\\tau)e^{i\\omega\\tau}\\,d\\tau$, the stationary spectrum and time-average bound are\n$$S(\\omega)=\\frac{V\\gamma}{\\pi(\\gamma^2+\\omega^2)},\\qquad\\operatorname{Var}\\!\\left(\\frac1T\\int_0^T X_t\\,dt\\right)\\le\\frac{2V}{\\gamma T}.$$\nAll these statements concern the specified linear stochastic model. An Einstein relation between $\\sigma$ and a physical bath temperature would be an additional physical postulate.",
          "strategy": "proof_strategy: direct; complete argument is in items/thm-tdmath-ornstein-uhlenbeck-model.md and its proof contract.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
