        {
          "id": "thm-tdmath-regular-collision-entropy",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Conditional Boltzmann entropy inequality and equality form",
          "reference": "items/thm-tdmath-regular-collision-entropy.md#statement",
          "design_state": "Complete draft carrier authored; scoped checks and independent review remain pending.",
          "dependency_level": 1,
          "deps": [
            "def-tdmath-elastic-collision-kernel",
            "def-integrable-real-and-complex-functions-and-their-integrals",
            "def-lebesgue-measure-and-the-lebesgue-sigma-algebra",
            "def-product-measure-on-sigma-finite-spaces",
            "thm-chain-rule",
            "cor-mean-value-theorem",
            "thm-dominated-convergence",
            "thm-fubini-theorem-for-l-one-on-sigma-finite-product-spaces",
            "thm-logarithm-derivative-and-integral",
            "thm-sigma-finite-product-measure-exists-is-rectangular-and-is-unique",
            "thm-tonelli-theorem-for-sigma-finite-product-spaces"
          ],
          "justified_by": [],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-tdmath-elastic-collision-kernel": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-integrable-real-and-complex-functions-and-their-integrals": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-lebesgue-measure-and-the-lebesgue-sigma-algebra": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-product-measure-on-sigma-finite-spaces": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-chain-rule": "mathematical-premise",
            "cor-mean-value-theorem": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-dominated-convergence": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-fubini-theorem-for-l-one-on-sigma-finite-product-spaces": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-logarithm-derivative-and-integral": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-sigma-finite-product-measure-exists-is-rectangular-and-is-unique": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-tonelli-theorem-for-sigma-finite-product-spaces": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Let $\\Omega=\\mathbb T^d$ be a spatial rectangle with opposite faces identified, $d\\ge2$, and let $I$ be an open time interval. Suppose $f:\\Omega\\times\\mathbb R^d\\times I\\to(0,\\infty)$ is $C^1$ in space and time and $C^2$ in velocity. Fix a positive reference density $f_{\\rm ref}$ with the same units as $f$. Assume $f$, $f|v|^2$, and $f|\\log(f/f_{\\rm ref})|$ are integrable, and assume an integrable envelope on every compact time interval justifying differentiation of the entropy integral and every displayed collision integral. Let $Q$ and the symmetric collision measure $\\nu$ satisfy the weak identity in [[def-tdmath-elastic-collision-kernel]] for tests $1$ and $\\log(f/f_{\\rm ref})$, with absolute convergence, and suppose\n$$\\partial_t f+v\\cdot\\nabla_r f=Q(f).$$\nThen for $H[f](t)=\\int_\\Omega\\int_{\\mathbb R^d}f\\log(f/f_{\\rm ref})\\,dv\\,dr$,\n$$\\frac{d}{dt}H[f](t)=-\\frac14\\int_\\Omega\\int_{Q_{\\rm el}}(A-B)(\\log A-\\log B)\\,d\\nu\\,dr\\le0,\\qquad A=f(r,v,t)f(r,w,t),\\quad B=f(r,v',t)f(r,w',t).$$\nThe integrand is nonnegative because $\\log$ is strictly increasing. Equality in the entropy-production integral holds exactly when $A=B$ for $\\nu$-almost every collision at almost every $r$. Under the additional assumptions that $\\nu$ is locally finite, has full support on $Q_{\\rm el}$, and $f$ is positive and $C^2$ in $v$, this balance implies for almost every $r$ that\n$$\\log(f(r,v,t)/f_{\\rm ref})=\\alpha(r,t)+b(r,t)\\cdot v+\\frac{\\lambda(r,t)}2|v|^2.$$\nIf $f(r,\\cdot,t)$ is integrable over $\\mathbb R^d$, then $\\lambda(r,t)<0$, so its velocity profile is Maxwellian. Conversely, every profile of this form has zero collision entropy production. The weak collision identity is an explicit model hypothesis; this is not a derivation from reversible many-particle mechanics or a PDE existence theorem.",
          "strategy": "proof_strategy: direct; complete argument is in items/thm-tdmath-regular-collision-entropy.md and its proof contract.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "David Tong, Kinetic Theory, Part 2",
                "url": "https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/kintheory/two.pdf",
                "locator": "Complete 39-page lecture-note part retrieved and read; §2.1, pp.14–16, Liouville phase-space volume; §§2.2–2.3, pp.20–35, Boltzmann equation and H-theorem."
              },
