            "def-lebesgue-measure-and-the-lebesgue-sigma-algebra": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-distance-to-set-is-lipschitz": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-finite-measure-uniqueness-on-a-pi-system": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-c-one-change-of-variables-for-nonnegative-lebesgue-measurable-functions": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-dominated-convergence": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-euclidean-implicit-function-theorem": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-metric-closure-characterisation": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-tdmath-hamiltonian-measure-and-recurrence": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-tonelli-theorem-for-sigma-finite-product-spaces": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume AC. Let $O\\subset\\mathbb R^{2n}$ be open with its canonical symplectic form, let $H\\in C^2(O,\\mathbb R)$, and let $J\\subset\\mathbb R$ be open. Suppose $\\nabla H\\ne0$ on $H^{-1}(J)$ and $H^{-1}(K)$ is compact in $O$ for every compact $K\\subset J$. Define $\\mu_E$ by [[def-tdmath-regular-energy-shell]]. Then for every nonnegative Borel $f$ compactly supported in $H^{-1}(J)$,\n$$\\int_Of(x)\\,dx=\\int_J\\mu_E(f)\\,dE.$$\nFor every $E\\in J$ with nonempty shell $\\Sigma_E=H^{-1}(\\{E\\})$, $0<\\mu_E(1)<\\infty$, and $\\widehat\\mu_E=\\mu_E/\\mu_E(1)$ is a probability measure. Let $\\phi_t$ be a Hamiltonian flow map defined as a diffeomorphism on a full compact energy band containing $\\Sigma_E$ and preserving that band. Then $\\widehat\\mu_E$ is invariant under $\\phi_t$ for every such regular $E$. Critical levels and noncompact bands are outside this statement.",
          "strategy": "proof_strategy: direct; complete argument is in items/thm-tdmath-regular-energy-shell-measure.md and its proof contract.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
