            "def-trace-class-operator": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-finite-rank-compressions-converge-in-trace-norm": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-complex-exponential-addition-and-real-extension": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-cyclicity-of-the-trace": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-trace-class-is-a-two-sided-banach-operator-ideal": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-trace-is-absolutely-convergent-and-basis-independent": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-trace-of-a-positive-operator-is-the-sum-of-its-eigenvalues": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-tdmath-general-trace-gibbs-model": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice and the exact first-clause interface of [[thm-tdmath-general-trace-gibbs-model]]: a nonzero complex Hilbert space has a finite or countable complete orthonormal energy eigenbasis $(u_j)$ for a self-adjoint semibounded $A$, with each energy eigenspace finite-dimensional. The supplier is a current draft whose statement and complete argument have been inspected; this theorem is conditional on that interface and does not claim its independent acceptance. Let $\\hbar>0$, define $U_tu_j=e^{-iE_jt/\\hbar}u_j$, and extend linearly and continuously. For any positive trace-class density operator $\\rho$ with $\\operatorname{Tr}\\rho=1$, set $\\rho_t=U_t\\rho U_t^*$. If $P_E$ denotes the projection onto the full eigenspace of energy $E$, then the trace-norm Riemann average\n$$\\bar\\rho_T:=\\frac1T\\int_0^T\\rho_t\\,dt$$\nconverges as $T\\to\\infty$ to\n$$\\rho_{\\rm diag}:=\\sum_E P_E\\rho P_E$$\nin trace norm. The full degenerate energy blocks are retained. Thus expectations of every bounded observable converge to their diagonal-ensemble values. This asserts Cesàro convergence, not convergence of $\\rho_t$ at individual late times, and is restricted to the stated discrete trace-class spectrum.",
          "strategy": "proof_strategy: direct; complete argument is in items/thm-tdmath-discrete-quantum-cesaro-dephasing.md and its proof contract.",
          "provenance": {
