      "items": [
        {
          "id": "def-td-thermodynamic-limit-contract",
          "kind": "definition",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "Finite-state thermodynamic-limit contract",
          "reference": "items/def-td-thermodynamic-limit-contract.md",
          "design_state": "Step 1 complete draft; readiness recorded separately.",
          "dependency_level": 3,
          "deps": [
            "def-td-equilibrium-state-domain",
            "def-td-si-quantities",
            "def-natural-numbers",
            "def-tdmath-countable-canonical-model"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-td-equilibrium-state-domain": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-td-si-quantities": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-natural-numbers": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-tdmath-countable-canonical-model": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "physical_scope": "A specified sequence of finite-state macroscopic models at positive temperature with a declared density, interactions, boundary conditions, and normalization; no limiting existence, ensemble equivalence, or critical singularity is asserted.",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "A **finite-state thermodynamic-limit contract** specifies a sequence $(X_k,E_k,g_k,V_k,n_k)_{k\\in\\mathbb N}$, where $\\mathbb N$ is the positive-integer index set of [[def-natural-numbers]], each $X_k$ is a finite nonempty state set, $E_k:X_k\\to\\mathbb R$ assigns finite energies in joules, $g_k:X_k\\to(0,\\infty)$ assigns positive dimensionless weights, $V_k>0$ is physical volume in $\\mathrm{m^3}$, and, for one declared species, $n_k>0$ is its amount in moles. A fixed-density sequence has $V_k\\to\\infty$ and $n_k/V_k\\to\\rho\\in(0,\\infty)$ in $\\mathrm{mol\\,m^{-3}}$. Boundary conditions, interaction rules, and the choice of a volume or amount normalization are part of the contract and must be held fixed or explicitly tracked as $k$ varies.\n\nFor $T>0$, set $\\beta:=(k_BT)^{-1}$ in $\\mathrm{J^{-1}}$, with $k_B$ and units from [[def-td-si-quantities]]. The finite-state canonical partition sum is\n\n$$\nZ_k(\\beta):=\\sum_{x\\in X_k}g_k(x)e^{-\\beta E_k(x)},\n$$\n\nas the finite case of [[def-tdmath-countable-canonical-model]]. It is a positive finite real number. Define $F_k(\\beta):=-\\beta^{-1}\\log Z_k(\\beta)$ in joules and $f_k(\\beta):=F_k(\\beta)/V_k$ in $\\mathrm{J\\,m^{-3}}$. The specified thermodynamic-limit value is $f(\\beta,\\rho):=\\lim_{k\\to\\infty} f_k(\\beta)$ **if this limit exists**. A limit per mole or per lattice site is a different normalization and must be stated separately.\n\nThis is a contract for what a limit claim must specify, not a theorem that the limit exists. It asserts no uniformity in $\\beta$, derivative interchange, ensemble equivalence, convergence rate, or nonanalyticity. A finite model's regularity and any limiting singularity require their own arguments; neither is inferred from the word “thermodynamic limit.”",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "not-applicable"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "David Tong, Statistical Physics, author-hosted complete lecture notes, Chapter 5, §5.4.3",
                "url": "https://davidtong.org/teaching/statistical-physics/statmechhtml/S5"
              },
              {
                "title": "Konstantin K. Likharev, Essential Graduate Physics: Statistical Mechanics, §§4.1–4.2",
                "url": "https://phys.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Thermodynamics_and_Statistical_Mechanics/Essential_Graduate_Physics_-_Statistical_Mechanics_%28Likharev%29/04%3A_Phase_Transitions/4.01%3A_First_order_phase_transitions"
              }
            ]
          },
          "library": "physics"
        },
        {
          "id": "pthm-td-fixed-tp-reaction-potential-minimum",
          "kind": "physics-theorem",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "Fixed-temperature and fixed-pressure potential minimum with internal reactions",
          "reference": "items/pthm-td-fixed-tp-reaction-potential-minimum.md",
          "design_state": "Step 1 complete draft; readiness recorded separately.",
          "dependency_level": 7,
          "deps": [
            "def-td-equilibrium-state-domain",
