          "physical_scope": "An exact derivative calculation in the dimensionless reduced van der Waals model below its model critical temperature; no real-fluid measurement or universal equation of state is asserted.",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Adopt the reduced van der Waals equation as a phenomenological model:\n$$\np(v,t)=\\frac{8t}{3v-1}-\\frac{3}{v^2},\\qquad v>\\frac13,\\quad t>0,\n$$\nwhere $p=P/P_c$, $v=V/V_c$, and $t=T/T_c$ use positive model scales $P_c,V_c,T_c$. Define a model critical point by the simultaneous isothermal conditions $\\partial_vp=\\partial_v^2p=0$ in this domain. The equation is a model premise; its extension to liquid-like densities is not a universal physical law.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-generated",
            "proof": "ai-generated"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "David Tong, Statistical Physics, author-hosted complete lecture notes, §5.1.1",
