          "physical_scope": "A constructed one-component, two-phase separated mixture with additive volume and fixed total amount; no coexistence data or measured material values are asserted.",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "At a stipulated common $T,p$, let one mole of a component occupy phase $\\alpha$ with molar volume $v_\\alpha=1.0\\times10^{-3}\\,\\mathrm{m^3\\,mol^{-1}}$ or phase $\\beta$ with $v_\\beta=4.0\\times10^{-3}\\,\\mathrm{m^3\\,mol^{-1}}$. Consider a separated mixture of total amount $N=2\\,\\mathrm{mol}$ and total volume $V=5.0\\times10^{-3}\\,\\mathrm{m^3}$; use the volume convention of [[def-td-phase-and-coexistence-domain]] and additivity of [[post-td-bulk-additivity]].",
