            "pthm-td-clapeyron-local": "physical-result",
            "thm-euclidean-inverse-function-theorem": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "physical_scope": "A constructed pair of smooth one-component Gibbs charts with zero molar-volume jump; it shows why the local nonzero-jump hypothesis cannot be omitted and makes no material claim.",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Equality of two smooth one-component molar Gibbs branches near a coexistence point always defines a unique differentiable pressure graph $p=p(T)$ on an open temperature interval, with slope $\\Delta s/\\Delta v$, even when the molar-volume jump $\\Delta v$ vanishes.",
