      "items": [
        {
          "id": "def-tdmath-stable-power-tempered-particle-model",
          "kind": "definition",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Stable power-tempered pair-potential model",
          "reference": "research/physics-td-qft-rpm-62-2026-10-14-batch-14.notes.md#inventory-dependencies-and-levels",
          "design_state": "Draft definition carrier recorded; scoped checks and independent review remain pending.",
          "dependency_level": 0,
          "deps": [
            "def-borel-sigma-algebra",
            "def-borel-sigma-algebra-on-the-extended-real-line",
            "def-extended-reals",
            "def-euclidean-inner-product",
            "def-natural-numbers",
            "def-real-power"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-borel-sigma-algebra": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-borel-sigma-algebra-on-the-extended-real-line": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-extended-reals": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-euclidean-inner-product": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-natural-numbers": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-real-power": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Fix a positive integer $d$ and use the Euclidean space $\\mathbb R^d$ with norm\n$\\|x\\|_2=\\sqrt{\\langle x,x\\rangle}$ of [[def-euclidean-inner-product]]. A\npair potential is an even Borel-measurable function\n$\\phi:\\mathbb R^d\\to\\overline{\\mathbb R}$ whose image is contained in\n$\\mathbb R\\cup\\{+\\infty\\}$. Here $\\overline{\\mathbb R}$ is the extended real\nline ([[def-extended-reals]]). Borel measurability means the inverse image of\neach Borel subset of $\\overline{\\mathbb R}$ belongs to the Borel sigma-algebra\ngenerated by open sets in the Euclidean topology on $\\mathbb R^d$\n([[def-borel-sigma-algebra-on-the-extended-real-line]],\n[[def-borel-sigma-algebra]]). Even means $\\phi(-x)=\\phi(x)$. The value\n$+\\infty$ represents a forbidden pair separation. Coordinates and\npotential values are numerical values in fixed reference length and energy\nunits.\n\nFor $N\\ge1$ and an ordered configuration $(q_1,\\ldots,q_N)\\in(\\mathbb R^d)^N$,\ndefine its pair energy by\n$$U_N(q_1,\\ldots,q_N):=\\sum_{1\\le i<j\\le N}\\phi(q_i-q_j),$$\nwith an empty sum equal to $0$; also put $U_0=0$. The finite sum is in\n$\\mathbb R\\cup\\{+\\infty\\}$, since each pair term is real or $+\\infty$.\n\nThe pair potential is **stable** if there is a finite constant $B\\ge0$ such\nthat $U_N(q_1,\\ldots,q_N)\\ge-BN$ for every $N\\ge1$ and every configuration.\nIt is **power-tempered** if there are constants $C,R,\\epsilon>0$ such that\n$\\phi(x)\\in\\mathbb R$ whenever $\\|x\\|_2\\ge R$, and, on that set, the ordinary\nreal absolute value $|\\phi(x)|$ satisfies\n$$|\\phi(x)|\\le C\\|x\\|_2^{-d-\\epsilon}.$$\nThe combined model class consists of pair potentials that are both stable and\npower-tempered. No condition is imposed on the positive core, which may be\nunbounded or infinite, and the tail may have either sign.",
          "strategy": "Definition carrier is in items/def-tdmath-stable-power-tempered-particle-model.md; no proof obligation applies.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "not-applicable"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Stefan Adams, Mathematical Statistical Mechanics, MPI Lecture Note 30, §5.2",
                "url": "https://files-www.mis.mpg.de/mpi-typo3/preprints/ln/lecturenote-3006.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "M. E. Fisher and J. L. Lebowitz, Asymptotic Free Energy of a System with Periodic Boundary Conditions, §§II–III",
                "url": "https://cmsr.rutgers.edu/images/people/lebowitz_joel/publications-archived/jll.pub_69.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "D. Ruelle, Classical Statistical Mechanics of a System of Particles",
                "url": "https://www.e-periodica.ch/cntmng?pid=hpa-001%3A1963%3A36%3A%3A1128&bot=1"
              }
            ]
          },
          "library": "mathematics"
        },
        {
          "id": "lem-tdmath-measure-integral-agrees-with-root-lebesgue-integral",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "The thermodynamics measure integral agrees with the shared nonnegative integral",
          "reference": "research/physics-td-qft-rpm-62-2026-10-14-batch-14.notes.md#inventory-dependencies-and-levels",
          "design_state": "Complete conditional proof recorded; scoped checks and independent review remain pending.",
          "dependency_level": 1,
          "deps": [
            "def-tdmath-measure-integral",
            "def-measure",
            "def-nonnegative-lebesgue-integral",
            "def-nonnegative-simple-measurable-function",
            "def-simple-function-and-canonical-representation",
            "def-integral-of-a-nonnegative-simple-function",
            "lem-well-definedness-of-the-simple-integral"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-tdmath-measure-integral": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-measure": "mathematical-premise",
