        {
          "id": "lem-tdmath-particle-exponential-cutoff",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Stability gives finite grand normalization and an exponential particle cutoff",
          "reference": "research/physics-td-qft-rpm-62-2026-10-14-batch-14.notes.md#inventory-dependencies-and-levels",
          "design_state": "Complete conditional proof recorded; scoped checks and independent review remain pending.",
          "dependency_level": 1,
          "deps": [
            "def-tdmath-stable-power-tempered-particle-model",
            "def-tdmath-measure-integral",
            "def-nonnegative-extended-series",
            "def-lebesgue-measure-and-the-lebesgue-sigma-algebra",
            "def-countable-choice",
            "prop-lebesgue-measure-is-sigma-finite-and-finite-on-bounded-sets",
            "thm-lebesgue-measure-of-a-box-of-every-kind",
            "thm-sigma-finite-product-measure-exists-is-rectangular-and-is-unique",
            "thm-borel-products-of-euclidean-spaces-are-euclidean-borel",
            "def-extended-reals",
            "def-borel-sigma-algebra-on-the-extended-real-line",
            "def-extended-real-valued-measurable-function",
            "cor-continuous-functions-are-borel-measurable",
            "thm-composition-with-borel-functions-preserves-measurability",
            "prop-closure-properties-of-measurable-functions-used-by-the-integral",
            "def-real-exponential-function-and-e",
            "lem-exponential-series-has-infinite-radius",
            "thm-exponential-addition-formula",
            "thm-exponential-is-strictly-increasing",
            "def-factorial-and-falling-factorial",
            "def-integer-power",
            "lem-integer-part"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-tdmath-stable-power-tempered-particle-model": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-tdmath-measure-integral": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-nonnegative-extended-series": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-lebesgue-measure-and-the-lebesgue-sigma-algebra": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
            "prop-lebesgue-measure-is-sigma-finite-and-finite-on-bounded-sets": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-lebesgue-measure-of-a-box-of-every-kind": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-sigma-finite-product-measure-exists-is-rectangular-and-is-unique": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-borel-products-of-euclidean-spaces-are-euclidean-borel": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-extended-reals": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-borel-sigma-algebra-on-the-extended-real-line": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-extended-real-valued-measurable-function": "mathematical-premise",
            "cor-continuous-functions-are-borel-measurable": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-composition-with-borel-functions-preserves-measurability": "mathematical-premise",
            "prop-closure-properties-of-measurable-functions-used-by-the-integral": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-real-exponential-function-and-e": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-exponential-series-has-infinite-radius": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-exponential-addition-formula": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-exponential-is-strictly-increasing": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-factorial-and-falling-factorial": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-integer-power": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-integer-part": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$\n([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $d\\ge1$, let $\\phi$ be a stable pair\npotential as in [[def-tdmath-stable-power-tempered-particle-model]] with\nstability constant $B$, and fix $a,\\beta>0$. In fixed reference length and\nenergy units, put $\\Lambda_L=[0,L]^d$ and define, for $N\\ge1$,\n$$Z_{L,N}:=\\frac{a^N}{N!}\\int_{\\Lambda_L^N}e^{-\\beta U_N(q_1,\\ldots,q_N)}\\,d\\lambda_d^{\\otimes N},$$\nwhere $\\lambda_d$ is Lebesgue measure restricted to the Borel subsets of\n$\\mathbb R^d$, $\\lambda_d^{\\otimes N}$ is its $N$-fold product measure. The\nintegrand uses the ordinary real exponential when $U_N<+\\infty$ and is defined\nto be $0$ when $U_N=+\\infty$. Also,\n$\\int_{\\Lambda_L^N}f\\,d\\lambda_d^{\\otimes N}$ abbreviates the nonnegative\nintegral of $f\\mathbf1_{\\Lambda_L^N}$ on the full product space, using\n[[def-tdmath-measure-integral]]. Set $Z_{L,0}=1$.\nDefine $\\Xi_L:=\\sum_{N=0}^{\\infty}Z_{L,N}$ as the nonnegative extended sum of\n[[def-nonnegative-extended-series]]. For $L\\ge1$ put\n$Q:=a e^{\\beta B}$. Choose any real $K>eQ+1$ and set\n$$n_L:=\\lfloor K L^d\\rfloor+1.$$\nwhich satisfies $K L^d<n_L\\le K L^d+1$ by the integer-part lemma\n[[lem-integer-part]]. Let\n$\\Xi_L^{\\mathrm{cut}}:=\\sum_{N=0}^{n_L}Z_{L,N}$. Then\n$$1\\le\\Xi_L\\le e^{Q L^d},\\qquad \\sum_{N>n_L}Z_{L,N}\\le e^{-L^d},\\qquad \\Xi_L^{\\mathrm{cut}}\\ge(1-e^{-L^d})\\Xi_L.$$",
          "strategy": "proof_strategy: direct; complete numbered argument is in items/lem-tdmath-particle-exponential-cutoff.md and its proof contract.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Stefan Adams, Mathematical Statistical Mechanics, MPI Lecture Note 30, §5.2",
                "url": "https://files-www.mis.mpg.de/mpi-typo3/preprints/ln/lecturenote-3006.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "M. E. Fisher and J. L. Lebowitz, Asymptotic Free Energy of a System with Periodic Boundary Conditions, §§II–III, VI",
                "url": "https://cmsr.rutgers.edu/images/people/lebowitz_joel/publications-archived/jll.pub_69.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "library": "mathematics",
          "proof_strategy": "direct"
        },
        {
          "id": "lem-tdmath-separated-cube-tail-bound",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Power tempering bounds interactions between separated cubes",
          "reference": "research/physics-td-qft-rpm-62-2026-10-14-batch-14.notes.md#inventory-dependencies-and-levels",
          "design_state": "Complete conditional proof recorded; scoped checks and independent review remain pending.",
          "dependency_level": 1,
          "deps": [
            "def-tdmath-stable-power-tempered-particle-model",
            "def-integers",
            "def-nonnegative-extended-series",
            "thm-p-series-real-exponents"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-tdmath-stable-power-tempered-particle-model": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-integers": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-nonnegative-extended-series": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-p-series-real-exponents": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Let $d\\ge1$ and let $\\phi$ be power-tempered as in\n[[def-tdmath-stable-power-tempered-particle-model]], with constants\n$C,R,\\epsilon>0$. Define\n$$S_{d,\\epsilon}:=\\sum_{m=1}^{\\infty}\\bigl((2m+1)^d-(2m-1)^d\\bigr)m^{-d-\\epsilon},\\qquad \\|k\\|_\\infty:=\\max_{1\\le r\\le d}|k_r| \\quad(k\\in\\mathbb Z^d).$$\nThis nonnegative series, defined by [[def-nonnegative-extended-series]],\ngroups the lattice terms by shells $\\|k\\|_\\infty=m$.\nThen $S_{d,\\epsilon}<\\infty$. Let $\\ell>0$, $g\\ge R$, and let\n$J\\subset\\mathbb Z^d$ be finite with $M=|J|$. For each $j\\in J$, place at most\n$n$ particles in the cube $C_j=(\\ell+g)j+[0,\\ell]^d$, where $n$ is a\nnonnegative integer. The total absolute inter-cube energy satisfies\n$$\\sum_{\\substack{j,j'\\in J\\;j<j'}}\\;\\sum_{q\\in C_j}\\sum_{q'\\in C_{j'}}|\\phi(q-q')|\\le\\frac C2 M n^2 S_{d,\\epsilon}g^{-d-\\epsilon}.$$\nHere $j<j'$ means any fixed total ordering of the finite set $J$; each\nunordered pair of cubes is counted once.",
          "strategy": "proof_strategy: direct; complete numbered argument is in items/lem-tdmath-separated-cube-tail-bound.md and its proof contract.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Stefan Adams, Mathematical Statistical Mechanics, MPI Lecture Note 30, §5.2",
                "url": "https://files-www.mis.mpg.de/mpi-typo3/preprints/ln/lecturenote-3006.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "M. E. Fisher and J. L. Lebowitz, Asymptotic Free Energy of a System with Periodic Boundary Conditions, §III",
                "url": "https://cmsr.rutgers.edu/images/people/lebowitz_joel/publications-archived/jll.pub_69.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "library": "mathematics",
          "proof_strategy": "direct"
        },
