          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice and Countable Choice and the canonical Gibbs-preparation assumption [[post-nrqm-many-body-canonical-equilibrium-ensemble]]. Restrict to its $G=H$ branch: the declared energy operator $H$ is self-adjoint, bounded below, and measured in joules; $T>0$ is in kelvins, $\\beta=(k_{\\mathrm B}T)^{-1}$ is in $\\mathrm{J^{-1}}$, and $K_\\beta=e^{-\\beta H}$ has $0<Z_\\beta=\\operatorname{Tr}K_\\beta<\\infty$. Suppose also that on an open interval $J_\\beta\\subset(0,\\infty)$ containing $\\beta$, every compact $C\\subset J_\\beta$ admits a summable family $a_j\\ge0$ with $(1+|E_j|^2)e^{-\\gamma E_j}\\le a_j$ for all energy eigenvalues $E_j$ and $\\gamma\\in C$. Let $(u_j)$ be the finite or countable complete orthonormal eigenfamily supplied by [[thm-tdmath-general-trace-gibbs-model]], repeated according to multiplicity, with $Hu_j=E_ju_j$, and put $\\lambda_j=e^{-\\beta E_j}/Z_\\beta$. The supplied trace identity gives $\\sum_j\\lambda_j=1$, and these $\\lambda_j$ are the eigenvalues of $\\rho_\\beta$. Define the spectral mean $\\bar E_\\beta:=\\sum_j\\lambda_jE_j$, the variance $\\operatorname{Var}_\\beta(H):=\\sum_j\\lambda_j(E_j-\\bar E_\\beta)^2$, the dimensionless entropy $s_\\beta:=-\\sum_j\\lambda_j\\log\\lambda_j$, and the physical von Neumann entropy $S_{\\mathrm{vN}}(\\rho_\\beta):=k_{\\mathrm B}s_\\beta$. These are spectral-sum definitions for this commuting Gibbs density; no operator trace of an unbounded product is used. The supplied moment envelope makes these sums finite. Then\n$$-\\partial_\\beta\\log Z_\\beta=\\bar E_\\beta,\\qquad \\partial_\\beta^2\\log Z_\\beta=\\operatorname{Var}_\\beta(H),\\qquad S_{\\mathrm{vN}}(\\rho_\\beta)=k_{\\mathrm B}\\bigl(\\log Z_\\beta+\\beta\\bar E_\\beta\\bigr).$$\nThus $F_{\\mathrm{stat}}=-k_{\\mathrm B}T\\log Z_\\beta=\\bar E_\\beta-T S_{\\mathrm{vN}}(\\rho_\\beta)$. This statement does not extend the Helmholtz interpretation to an effective generator $H-\\mu\\mathcal N$.",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "David Tong, Statistical Physics, complete lecture notes, §§1.3.1–1.3.4 (printed pp. 18–26)",
                "url": "https://davidtong.org/pdfs/teaching/statistical-physics/statphys.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "Daniel Arovas, Lecture Notes on Thermodynamics and Statistical Mechanics, §§4.3–4.4 (printed pp. 199–208)",
                "url": "https://courses.physics.ucsd.edu/2025/Spring/physics210a/LECTURES/STATMECH.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "library": "physics",
          "physical_scope": "A declared quantum model with a semibounded self-adjoint energy operator, trace-class Gibbs exponential, and local first-and-second-moment envelope; the result concerns the adopted Gibbs preparation and does not derive thermalization or a continuum spectrum.",
          "verification": {
            "precheck": "pass"
          },
          "proof_strategy": "direct"
        },
