          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Let a physical Hamiltonian model satisfy [[def-td-regular-hamiltonian-shell-preparation]] on a nonempty compact regular energy band, and adopt its normalized shell law by [[post-td-microcanonical-sampling]]. In addition to the definition's $C^2$ regularity, assume its numerical Hamiltonian $\\hat H$ is $C^\\infty$. Let $\\phi_t$ be the physical Hamiltonian flow defined there, with $t$ measured in seconds, and assume it is an invertible smooth map of the whole band for every real time. Then, conditional on the current batch-12 draft mathematical interfaces [[thm-tdmath-hamiltonian-measure-and-recurrence]] and [[thm-tdmath-regular-energy-shell-measure]], every shell probability $\\nu_{\\hat E}$ is invariant:\n$$\\nu_{\\hat E}(\\phi_t^{-1}(A))=\\nu_{\\hat E}(A)$$\nfor every Borel set $A\\subseteq\\Sigma_{\\hat E}$ and every $t\\in\\mathbb R$. This result asserts no ergodicity, time-average equality, or thermalization.",
