          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Use the finite-alphabet, bounded, translation-invariant finite-range lattice model of [[def-tdmath-bounded-finite-range-lattice]], with physical interaction energies in joules, inverse temperature $\\beta=(k_{\\mathrm B}T)^{-1}>0$, and partition sum $Z_L(\\beta)$. Suppose each site represents a fixed cell of volume $v_0>0$ in $\\mathrm{m^3}$. Define the reduced log-partition density $p_L=L^{-d}\\log Z_L$ and the lattice pressure convention $P_L=(k_{\\mathrm B}T/v_0)p_L$ in pascals. Then $p_L$ and $P_L$ have finite limits as $L\\to\\infty$. If a second boundary-energy model on the same configuration sets differs pointwise by at most $C_bL^{d-1}$ joules for fixed $C_b$, it has the same limit.\n\nThe pressure convention in this statement is assigned to this lattice model. Equating it with a derivative-based macroscopic pressure or a measured mechanical pressure requires a separate model identification.",
