          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Work in the nonzero finite-dimensional fixed-$N$ sector of [[def-nrqm-many-body-framework-entropy-and-free-energy]], with self-adjoint energy $H_N^\\sigma$ in joules and assigned $T>0$ in kelvins. Adopt the Gibbs preparation of [[post-nrqm-many-body-canonical-equilibrium-ensemble]] and its unit convention $\\beta=(k_{\\mathrm B}T)^{-1}$. For $F(\\rho)=\\operatorname{tr}(\\rho H_N^\\sigma)-T S(\\rho)$ over the declared sector density operators, the canonical preparation is the unique minimizer and\n$$\\min_\\rho F(\\rho)=F_{\\mathrm{eq}}=-k_{\\mathrm B}T\\log\\operatorname{tr}(e^{-\\beta H_N^\\sigma}).$$\nThis quantum statistical functional is not identified here with a macroscopic Helmholtz potential without an additional model bridge; its minimum does not establish equilibration.",
