        {
          "id": "pthm-td-finite-mode-occupation-and-trace-formulas",
          "kind": "physics-theorem",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "Finite bosonic and fermionic mode partition and occupation formulas",
          "reference": "items/pthm-td-finite-mode-occupation-and-trace-formulas.md#statement",
          "design_state": "Complete draft carrier authored; scoped checks and prerequisite acceptance remain pending.",
          "dependency_level": 7,
          "deps": [
            "def-axiom-of-choice",
            "def-countable-choice",
            "def-nrqm-many-body-framework-entropy-and-free-energy",
            "def-nrqm-framework-quantities-and-units",
            "def-td-si-quantities",
            "def-tdmath-countable-canonical-model",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-hilbert-tensor-construction",
            "lem-nrqm-oscillator-diagonal-adjoint-and-graph-core-lemma",
            "post-nrqm-many-body-canonical-equilibrium-ensemble",
            "pthm-nrqm-many-body-thermal-occupation-predictions",
            "thm-nrqm-fock-and-equilibrium-single-mode-thermal-trace",
            "lem-nrqm-many-body-two-level-thermal-formulas"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-axiom-of-choice": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-nrqm-many-body-framework-entropy-and-free-energy": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-nrqm-framework-quantities-and-units": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-td-si-quantities": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-tdmath-countable-canonical-model": "mathematical-premise",
            "post-nrqm-many-body-canonical-equilibrium-ensemble": "physical-assumption",
            "pthm-nrqm-many-body-thermal-occupation-predictions": "physical-result",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-hilbert-tensor-construction": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-nrqm-oscillator-diagonal-adjoint-and-graph-core-lemma": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-nrqm-fock-and-equilibrium-single-mode-thermal-trace": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-nrqm-many-body-two-level-thermal-formulas": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume AC and Countable Choice and adopt the quantum Gibbs preparation of [[post-nrqm-many-body-canonical-equilibrium-ensemble]] at assigned temperature $T>0$ kelvins, with $\\beta=(k_{\\mathrm B}T)^{-1}$ in $\\mathrm{J^{-1}}$. A finite independent mode list means an integer $m\\ge1$ and, for each $r\\in\\{1,\\ldots,m\\}$, a declared type B or F and an excitation energy $\\varepsilon_r>0$ joules. For type B take the one-mode Fock Hilbert space with complete number basis $(e_n)_{n\\in\\mathbb N_0}$ and self-adjoint occupation operator $N_re_n=ne_n$ on its exact diagonal domain as in [[thm-nrqm-fock-and-equilibrium-single-mode-thermal-trace]]. For type F take $\\mathcal H_r=\\mathbb C^2$ with orthonormal basis $f_0,f_1$ and $N_rf_n=nf_n$. In either case put $H_r=\\varepsilon_rN_r$, and write $u_{r,n}=e_n$ or $f_n$ according to the factor type. Define $\\mathcal H^{(1)}=\\mathcal H_1$ and recursively $\\mathcal H^{(r+1)}=\\mathcal H^{(r)}\\widehat\\otimes\\mathcal H_{r+1}$ by the completed Hilbert tensor construction of [[lem-nrqm-composites-hilbert-tensor-construction]]; let $\\mathcal H=\\mathcal H^{(m)}$. The canonical orthonormal product basis is $u_{\\mathbf n}=\\bigotimes_r u_{r,n_r}$, indexed by $\\mathbf n=(n_1,\\ldots,n_m)\\in\\mathcal C:=\\prod_r\\mathcal C_r$, where $\\mathcal C_r=\\mathbb N_0$ for type B and $\\mathcal C_r=\\{0,1\\}$ for type F. If all factors are F then $\\mathcal C$ is finite; otherwise it is countably infinite and is enumerated by increasing $\\sum_r n_r$ and lexicographic order within each finite level, which is finite because every $n_r\\le\\sum_r n_r$. For each factor put $\\hat\\varepsilon_r=\\varepsilon_r/(1\\,\\mathrm J)$. Define the numerical energy map $\\hat E:\\mathcal C\\to\\mathbb R$ by $\\hat E(\\mathbf n)=\\sum_{r=1}^m\\hat\\varepsilon_rn_r$ and the physical energy $E(\\mathbf n)=(1\\,\\mathrm J)\\hat E(\\mathbf n)$. Define the numerical self-adjoint diagonal operator $\\hat H$ by $\\hat Hu_{\\mathbf n}=\\hat E(\\mathbf n)u_{\\mathbf n}$ on the exact domain\n$$D(\\hat H)=\\Bigl\\{\\psi\\in\\mathcal H:\\sum_{\\mathbf n\\in\\mathcal C}\\hat E(\\mathbf n)^2|\\langle\\psi,u_{\\mathbf n}\\rangle|^2<\\infty\\Bigr\\};$$\nwhen $\\mathcal C$ is finite, $\\hat H$ is a finite real diagonal endomorphism and is self-adjoint; when $\\mathcal C$ is countably infinite, the diagonal-operator lemma [[lem-nrqm-oscillator-diagonal-adjoint-and-graph-core-lemma]] gives $\\hat H$ self-adjoint for the displayed enumeration. The physical total energy operator is $H=(1\\,\\mathrm J)\\hat H$, with $Hu_{\\mathbf n}=E(\\mathbf n)u_{\\mathbf n}$ and $D(H)=D(\\hat H)$; multiplication by a nonzero real scalar preserves self-adjointness.\nThis sum-energy Hamiltonian with no interaction term is the definition of independence for this quantum model.\n\nFor one bosonic mode with excitation energy $\\varepsilon>0$ joules, let $q=e^{-\\beta\\varepsilon}$ and let $N$ be its dimensionless occupation number. Its partition trace and mean occupation are\n$$Z_B=(1-q)^{-1},\\qquad \\langle N\\rangle_B=\\frac{q}{1-q}=\\frac1{e^{\\beta\\varepsilon}-1}.$$\nFor a fermionic two-level occupation system with energies $0,\\varepsilon$, the partition sum and excited-state occupation are\n$$Z_F=1+q,\\qquad \\langle N\\rangle_F=\\frac{q}{1+q}=\\frac1{e^{\\beta\\varepsilon}+1}.$$\nFor a finite independent collection as defined above, write $K_\\beta=e^{-\\beta H}$ and $Z=\\operatorname{Tr}K_\\beta$. Then $0<Z<\\infty$ and the joint occupation-basis law is $P_\\beta(\\mathbf n):=e^{-\\beta E(\\mathbf n)}/Z$. For each factor $r$, define its marginal law by $P_{\\beta,r}(k):=\\sum_{\\mathbf n\\in\\mathcal C:\\,n_r=k}P_\\beta(\\mathbf n)$. The trace satisfies $Z=\\prod_{r=1}^m Z_r$, the joint law factorizes as $P_\\beta(\\mathbf n)=\\prod_{r=1}^m(q_r^{n_r}/Z_r)$, and each marginal mean is the corresponding one-mode mean displayed above. These are exact model identities under the adopted preparation.",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "David Tong, Statistical Physics, complete lecture notes, §§3.5–3.6 (printed pp. 77–106)",
                "url": "https://davidtong.org/pdfs/teaching/statistical-physics/statphys.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "Daniel Arovas, Lecture Notes on Thermodynamics and Statistical Mechanics, §§5.6–5.7 (printed pp. 277–303)",
                "url": "https://courses.physics.ucsd.edu/2025/Spring/physics210a/LECTURES/STATMECH.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "library": "physics",
          "physical_scope": "Declared finite lists of independent bosonic one-mode Fock systems or fermionic two-level occupation systems at assigned positive temperature; no interacting, infinite-mode, continuum, condensation, measured-occupation, or thermalization conclusion is asserted.",
          "verification": {
            "precheck": "pass"
          },
          "proof_strategy": "direct"
        },
        {
          "id": "pthm-td-qualified-discrete-quantum-dephasing",
          "kind": "physics-theorem",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "Cesaro dephasing for a discrete trace-class quantum model",
          "reference": "items/pthm-td-qualified-discrete-quantum-dephasing.md#statement",
          "design_state": "Complete draft carrier authored; scoped checks and prerequisite acceptance remain pending.",
          "dependency_level": 4,
          "deps": [
            "def-axiom-of-choice",
            "def-countable-choice",
            "def-nrqm-autonomous-dynamics-framework-evolution",
            "post-nrqm-framework-autonomous-dynamics",
            "post-nrqm-many-body-canonical-equilibrium-ensemble",
            "pthm-td-general-quantum-canonical-identities",
            "thm-tdmath-discrete-quantum-cesaro-dephasing"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-axiom-of-choice": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-nrqm-autonomous-dynamics-framework-evolution": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "post-nrqm-framework-autonomous-dynamics": "physical-assumption",
            "post-nrqm-many-body-canonical-equilibrium-ensemble": "physical-assumption",
            "pthm-td-general-quantum-canonical-identities": "physical-result",
            "thm-tdmath-discrete-quantum-cesaro-dephasing": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume AC and Countable Choice. Let $H$ be a self-adjoint quantum Hamiltonian bounded below with a complete discrete energy eigenfamily of finite multiplicity, and let $\\rho_0$ be any positive trace-class density operator of trace one. Let $\\hbar>0$ be the assigned action constant in $\\mathrm{J\\,s}$, adopt the unitary dynamics $U_t=e^{-itH/\\hbar}$ of [[post-nrqm-framework-autonomous-dynamics]], and assume the trace-class Gibbs and local moment conditions of [[pthm-td-general-quantum-canonical-identities]] that supply this discrete eigenfamily. Then, conditional on the current batch-12 draft theorem [[thm-tdmath-discrete-quantum-cesaro-dephasing]], the Cesaro state\n$$\\bar\\rho_\\tau:=\\frac1{\\tau}\\int_0^\\tau U_t\\rho_0U_t^*\\,dt$$\nconverges in trace norm as $\\tau\\to\\infty$ to $\\rho_{\\mathrm{diag}}=\\sum_E P_E\\rho_0P_E$, where $P_E$ is the spectral projection onto the full eigenspace of energy $E$. Coherences inside degenerate energy blocks remain. The limit need not be Gibbs, and no pointwise-in-time convergence or thermalization is asserted.",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "David Tong, Statistical Physics, complete lecture notes, §1.3.1 (printed pp. 18–19)",
                "url": "https://davidtong.org/pdfs/teaching/statistical-physics/statphys.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "Daniel Arovas, Lecture Notes on Thermodynamics and Statistical Mechanics, §§4.3.1 and 4.4.1 (printed pp. 199–206)",
                "url": "https://courses.physics.ucsd.edu/2025/Spring/physics210a/LECTURES/STATMECH.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "library": "physics",
          "physical_scope": "A trace-class initial density and a self-adjoint quantum Hamiltonian with a complete discrete energy eigenfamily of finite multiplicity under the declared unitary dynamics; the result is a time-averaged state limit, not Gibbs preparation or pointwise relaxation.",
          "verification": {
            "precheck": "pass"
          },
          "proof_strategy": "direct"
        },
        {
          "id": "rem-td-ensemble-limit-hypotheses",
          "kind": "remark",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "Scope limits for finite ensembles, shells, pressure and dephasing",
          "reference": "items/rem-td-ensemble-limit-hypotheses.md#remarks",
          "design_state": "Complete draft carrier authored; scoped checks and prerequisite acceptance remain pending.",
          "dependency_level": 8,
          "deps": [
