            "pthm-td-finite-mode-occupation-and-trace-formulas",
            "post-td-canonical-sampling",
            "thm-trace-of-a-positive-operator-is-the-sum-of-its-eigenvalues"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-axiom-of-choice": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-square-summable-family-on-an-arbitrary-index-set": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-td-si-quantities": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-tdmath-countable-canonical-model": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-trace-class-operator": "mathematical-premise",
            "ex-standard-basis-of-ell-two": "mathematical-premise",
            "pthm-td-finite-mode-occupation-and-trace-formulas": "physical-result",
            "post-td-canonical-sampling": "physical-assumption",
            "thm-trace-of-a-positive-operator-is-the-sum-of-its-eigenvalues": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume AC and Countable Choice as required by [[pthm-td-finite-mode-occupation-and-trace-formulas]] and the trace-class suppliers. Take modes indexed by $j\\in\\mathbb N$, each with excitation energy $\\varepsilon>0$ joules, and let $q=e^{-\\beta\\varepsilon}\\in(0,1)$. Let $\\mathcal F$ be the set of finite-support occupation sequences $n=(n_j)_{j\\ge1}$ with $n_j\\in\\mathbb N_0$. Enumerate $\\mathcal F$ by increasing $R(n)=\\sum_{j:n_j>0}(j+n_j)$ and lexicographic order of the finite list of nonzero pairs $(j,n_j)$ within each level. Each level is finite because $j,n_j\\le R(n)$ on its support, and every configuration occurs; skipping empty levels gives a bijection $\\mathbb N\\to\\mathcal F$. Define\n$$\\ell^2(\\mathcal F):=\\Bigl\\{c:\\mathcal F\\to\\mathbb C:\\sum_{n\\in\\mathcal F}|c(n)|^2<\\infty\\Bigr\\},\\qquad \\langle c,d\\rangle:=\\sum_{n\\in\\mathcal F}c(n)\\overline{d(n)}.$$\nThe vector $|n\\rangle$ is the indicator of $\\{n\\}$; these canonical occupation vectors form an orthonormal basis. Relabeling by the displayed enumeration is an isometry with $\\ell^2(\\mathbb N,\\mathbb C)$, which is a Hilbert space with its standard basis by [[ex-standard-basis-of-ell-two]]; the definition of square-summable families and their inner product is [[def-square-summable-family-on-an-arbitrary-index-set]]. Define the bounded positive diagonal Gibbs weight $K_\\beta|n\\rangle=q^{\\sum_jn_j}|n\\rangle$. On the subspace with $n_j=0$ for every $j>M$, the corresponding finite-mode partition sum is the trace of that restriction.",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-generated",
            "proof": "ai-generated"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "David Tong, Statistical Physics, complete lecture notes, §§3.5–3.6",
                "url": "https://davidtong.org/pdfs/teaching/statistical-physics/statphys.pdf"
