            "def-nrqm-framework-quantities-and-units": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-td-si-quantities": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-hilbert-tensor-construction": "mathematical-premise",
            "pthm-td-finite-mode-occupation-and-trace-formulas": "physical-result",
            "post-nrqm-framework-autonomous-dynamics": "physical-assumption",
            "post-nrqm-many-body-canonical-equilibrium-ensemble": "physical-assumption"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume AC and Countable Choice for the canonical mode preparation. Let $\\mathcal H_1=\\mathcal H_2=\\mathbb C^2$ with orthonormal basis $|0\\rangle,|1\\rangle$, and define the factor number maps by $N_r|0\\rangle=0$, $N_r|1\\rangle=|1\\rangle$. The composite Hilbert space is the finite Hilbert tensor product $\\mathcal H_1\\widehat\\otimes\\mathcal H_2\\cong\\mathbb C^4$ from [[lem-nrqm-composites-hilbert-tensor-construction]], with orthonormal product basis $|n_1n_2\\rangle$, $n_r\\in\\{0,1\\}$. On this basis define the site-number operators $\\mathcal N_1|n_1n_2\\rangle=n_1|n_1n_2\\rangle$ and $\\mathcal N_2|n_1n_2\\rangle=n_2|n_1n_2\\rangle$. For $T>0$ kelvins set $\\varepsilon=k_{\\mathrm B}T\\log2$ joules and define the noninteracting total Hamiltonian\n$$H=\\varepsilon(\\mathcal N_1+\\mathcal N_2),\\qquad H|n_1n_2\\rangle=\\varepsilon(n_1+n_2)|n_1n_2\\rangle.$$\nThe quantum Gibbs preparation at $T$ is used for the thermal comparison, and the closed-system unitary evolution is generated by $H$ with $U_t=e^{-itH/\\hbar}$, where $t$ is in seconds and $\\hbar>0$ is in $\\mathrm{J\\,s}$. Start the dynamics in $\\rho_0=|00\\rangle\\langle00|$.",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-generated",
            "proof": "ai-generated"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "David Tong, Statistical Physics, complete lecture notes, §§1.3.1 and 3.6",
                "url": "https://davidtong.org/pdfs/teaching/statistical-physics/statphys.pdf"
              },
