          },
          "proof_strategy": "direct",
          "statement": "On $\\mathbb R^2$ with coordinates $(x,y)$, let $\\omega=dy+y\\,dx$. It is a smooth nowhere-zero one-form because its $dy$ coefficient is $1$. The functions $\\mu(x,y)=e^x$ and $S(x,y)=e^xy$ satisfy $\\mu>0$ and $dS=\\mu\\omega$ globally."
        },
