            "thm-continuous-preimages-of-borel-sets-are-borel": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-borel-sigma-algebra-of-a-subspace-is-the-trace": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "dependency_level": 0,
          "statement": "**Set form.** Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ($\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$, [[def-countable-choice]]), used to establish the Lebesgue measure space of [[thm-lebesgue-measure-is-a-complete-measure]]. Let $K\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n$ be compact, Lebesgue measurable and of finite Lebesgue measure $\\lambda_n(K)<\\infty$, let $a<b$, and let $f$ be a real-valued function, defined and continuous together with its partial derivative $\\partial_tf$ on an open neighbourhood of $K\\times[a,b]$ in $\\mathbb R^{n+1}$. Then $t\\mapsto\\int_Kf(x,t)\\,d\\lambda_n(x)$ is differentiable at every $t\\in(a,b)$ with\n\n$$\\frac{d}{dt}\\int_Kf(x,t)\\,d\\lambda_n(x)=\\int_K\\partial_tf(x,t)\\,d\\lambda_n(x),$$\n\nand at $t=a$ and $t=b$ it has relative (one-sided) derivatives, taken within $[a,b]$, both equal to the same displayed integral. Equivalently, for every $t\\in[a,b]$ and every sequence $h_k\\to0$ with $h_k\\ne0$ and $t+h_k\\in[a,b]$,\n\n$$\\lim_{k\\to\\infty}\\frac{1}{h_k}\\Bigl(\\int_Kf(x,t+h_k)\\,d\\lambda_n(x)-\\int_Kf(x,t)\\,d\\lambda_n(x)\\Bigr)=\\int_K\\partial_tf(x,t)\\,d\\lambda_n(x).$$\n\n**Surface form.** Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ($\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$, [[def-countable-choice]]) for the surface measure of [[def-surface-integral-on-a-compact-c-one-hypersurface]]. Let $S$ be a fixed compact embedded $C^1$ hypersurface in $\\mathbb R^m$, $m\\ge2$, and let $f$ be real-valued, defined and continuous together with $\\partial_tf$ on an open neighbourhood of $S\\times[a,b]$. Then $t\\mapsto\\int_Sf(\\sigma,t)\\,dS(\\sigma)$ is differentiable in the same relative sense with\n\n$$\\frac{d}{dt}\\int_Sf(\\sigma,t)\\,dS(\\sigma)=\\int_S\\partial_tf(\\sigma,t)\\,dS(\\sigma).$$\n\nThe statements are pointwise in $t$ and make no claim about moving parameter sets $K(t)$ or $S(t)$, about singularities crossing $K$ or $S$, about differentiability of $\\partial_tf$, or about differentiation in the spatial variables; only the one-dimensional parameter $t$ is differentiated. Integrals are Lebesgue integrals, and the surface integrals are those of the cited surface measure; the case $K=\\varnothing$ or $\\lambda_n(K)=0$ is included and the two sides vanish.",
          "strategy": "For fixed $x$ the mean value theorem writes $[f(x,t+h)-f(x,t)]/h=\\partial_tf(x,\\tau)$ for some $\\tau$ between $t$ and $t+h$; uniform continuity of $\\partial_tf$ on the compact product bounds the integral of the difference by the sup-error times the finite measure. Iterate on finitely many charts, using the independence of the surface integral from the chart, for the surface clause.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
