                "url": "https://www.math.ucdavis.edu/~hunter/pdes/pde_notes.pdf",
                "locator": "Section 1.10.2-1.12, printed pp. 15-18, for surface integration on compact $C^1$ hypersurfaces and finite piecewise $C^1$ domain presentations; used for the imported mathematical conventions cited by the definition."
              }
            ]
          },
          "physical_scope": "The fixed spatial test geometries of the classical electromagnetic framework in a named inertial laboratory frame: bounded open volumes with specified finite piecewise $C^1$ boundary presentations and outward normals, and oriented regular $C^2$ patches over finite elementary planar regions with induced normals and boundary chains, together with the open box interiors with their compact closures and affine square patches explicitly admitted as instances. The definition is a convention for the integral form of the Maxwell equations; it asserts no field equation, no measurement and no apparatus realisation, and the marked $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ is inherited from the imported boundary and surface-measure definitions."
        },
        {
          "id": "def-em-weak-sources",
          "kind": "definition",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "Distributional Maxwell equations with point and stationary-sheet sources",
          "reference": "definition-contracts.md#def-em-weak-sources",
          "design_state": "explicit-definition-contract; supplier-validation-recorded-separately",
          "dependency_level": 14,
          "deps": [
            "def-em-lab-geometry",
            "def-em-si-conventions",
            "def-em-sources",
            "post-em-vacuum-maxwell",
            "def-distribution",
            "def-distributional-derivative",
            "def-test-function-space-d-of-an-open-set",
            "def-dirac-delta-and-its-derivatives",
            "def-regular-distribution-from-a-locally-integrable-function",
