            "thm-metric-closure-characterisation": "mathematical-premise",
            "cor-euclidean-closed-balls-and-spheres-are-compact": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-ck-euclidean-maps-and-diffeomorphisms": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-every-norm-on-rn-is-continuous-for-the-euclidean-metric": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-componentwise-limits-and-continuity": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Let $H:=\\{x\\in\\mathbb R^3:x_3>0\\}$ be the open upper half-space, let $a>0$ and $p:=a e_3\\in H$. Let $w:\\overline H\\setminus\\{p\\}\\to\\mathbb R$ be a function (closure as in [[def-metric-interior-closure-boundary]]) with:\n(i) $w$ is continuous ([[def-metric-continuity]]) on $\\overline H\\setminus\\{p\\}$ and of class $C^2$ with $\\Delta w=0$ on $H\\setminus\\{p\\}$ ([[def-laplacian-of-a-c2-function]], [[def-ck-euclidean-maps-and-diffeomorphisms]]);\n(ii) $w=0$ on $\\partial H=\\{x_3=0\\}$;\n(iii) $|x-p|w(x)\\to0$ as $x\\to p$, $x\\ne p$;\n(iv) $w(x)\\to0$ as $|x|\\to\\infty$ within $H$: for every $\\varepsilon>0$ there is $R>0$ with $|w(x)|\\le\\varepsilon$ for all $x\\in H\\setminus\\overline B_R(0)$.\nThen $w=0$ on $H\\setminus\\{p\\}$.\nThe conclusion is a uniqueness statement for the stated class only: no removable-singularity theorem, no pole condition beyond the sub-Coulomb growth (iii), no boundary regularity of $\\partial H$ beyond the flat graph, and no claim about $w$ outside $H$ are asserted.",
          "strategy": "Fix $y\\in H\\setminus\\{p\\}$ and $\\eta>0$. Choose $R>\\max(2a,|y|)$ large enough that $|w|\\le\\eta$ on $H\\cap\\{|x|\\ge R\\}$, enlarging the decay threshold slightly; choose $0<\\delta<\\min(a/2,|y-p|,R-|p|)$ so small that $|w(x)|\\le\\eta/|x-p|$ whenever $0<|x-p|\\le\\delta$. On the nonempty bounded open $U=(B_R(0)\\setminus\\overline B_\\delta(p))\\cap H$, the functions $\\pm w-\\eta-\\eta/|x-p|$ are harmonic and continuous on $\\overline U$: the barrier $|x-p|^{-1}$ is harmonic off its pole by [[lem-laplace-fundamental-solution-is-harmonic-off-its-pole]]. On the plane they are nonpositive because $w=0$; on the outer sphere they are nonpositive by decay; on the inner sphere they are nonpositive by the sub-Coulomb pole condition. The weak maximum principle [[thm-weak-maximum-principle-for-the-laplacian]] therefore gives $|w(y)|\\le\\eta(1+|y-p|^{-1})$. Let $\\eta\\downarrow0$ with $y$ fixed to obtain $w(y)=0$. This proves uniqueness for all sub-Coulomb remainders, including arbitrary bounded remainders and the earlier zero-remainder-limit class, without a removable-singularity theorem or extra boundary smoothness assumption.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "John K. Hunter, Notes on Partial Differential Equations (University of California, Davis, 2014)",
                "url": "https://www.math.ucdavis.edu/~hunter/pdes/pde_notes.pdf",
                "locator": "§2.3.1 Theorem 2.17 and following subharmonic extension, printed pp. 27-28 (weak maximum principle for the Laplacian on bounded open sets)."
              },
              {
                "title": "Gerald Teschl, Partial Differential Equations: From Classical to Modern (2025 archived author manuscript)",
                "url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20250601000000id_/https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-pde/pde.pdf",
                "locator": "§5.4, maximum principle and uniqueness discussion, printed pp. 124-128."
              }
            ]
          },
          "dependency_level": 0
        },
        {
          "id": "post-em-electrostatic-conductor-model",
          "kind": "postulate",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "The ideal electrostatic conductor model",
          "reference": "definition-contracts.md#post-em-electrostatic-conductor-model",
          "design_state": "explicit-adopted-postulate-contract; nonproof-source-scope-review",
          "deps": [
            "def-bounded-c-k-domain-and-boundary-charts",
            "def-countable-choice",
            "def-em-electrostatic-regime",
            "def-em-fields",
