            "thm-clairaut-schwarz-mixed-partials": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-divergence-and-curl-are-linear-and-obey-the-scalar-product-rules": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-algebra-of-total-derivatives": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-ck-euclidean-maps-and-diffeomorphisms": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-directional-and-partial-derivatives": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-interval": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Let $c>0$, let $\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^3$ be open, let $I\\subseteq\\mathbb R$ be an interval with at least two elements ([[def-interval]]), let $k\\ge2$ be an integer, let $(\\varphi,A)$ be a potential pair of class $C^k$ jointly on $\\Omega\\times I$ and let $\\chi$ be a gauge function of class $C^k$ jointly on $\\Omega\\times I$, all in the conventions of [[def-em-potential-gauge-and-field-conventions]] and [[def-em-gauge-transformation]]: $E(\\varphi,A)=-\\nabla\\varphi-\\partial_tA$, $B(\\varphi,A)=\\operatorname{curl}A$ and $T_\\chi(\\varphi,A)=(\\varphi-\\partial_t\\chi,\\ A+\\nabla\\chi)$; for a non-open $I$ the joint $C^k$ classes are read in the open-neighbourhood restriction convention of [[lem-em-joint-smooth-potentials]] (for open $I$ this is the ordinary class of [[def-ck-euclidean-maps-and-diffeomorphisms]]).\n\nThen $T_\\chi(\\varphi,A)$ is a potential pair of class $C^{k-1}$ jointly on $\\Omega\\times I$ and its field pair is the field pair of $(\\varphi,A)$:\n\n$$E(T_\\chi(\\varphi,A))=E(\\varphi,A),\\qquad B(T_\\chi(\\varphi,A))=B(\\varphi,A)\\qquad\\text{on }\\Omega\\times I,$$\n\nthe common values being maps $\\Omega\\times I\\to\\mathbb R^3$ of class $C^{k-1}$ jointly, that is, fields of the framework in the sense of [[def-em-fields]]. In particular gauge related potential representations of one field pair have equal field pairs: the electric and magnetic fields are gauge invariants of the framework, and no value of $\\varphi$, of $A$ or of $\\chi$ is asserted to be observable.\n\nThe proof uses only the defining formulas, the vanishing of $\\operatorname{curl}\\nabla\\chi$ for the $C^2$ function $\\chi$ and the equality of the time-space mixed partials $\\partial_t\\partial_i\\chi=\\partial_i\\partial_t\\chi$; no Maxwell equation, no hypothesis on $\\Omega$ beyond openness, and no choice principle is used.",
          "strategy": "Magnetic field: $\\operatorname{curl}(A+\\nabla\\chi)=\\operatorname{curl}A+\\operatorname{curl}\\nabla\\chi=\\operatorname{curl}A$ by linearity of the curl ([[lem-divergence-and-curl-are-linear-and-obey-the-scalar-product-rules]]) and $\\operatorname{curl}\\nabla\\chi=0$ ([[thm-the-curl-of-a-gradient-vanishes]], applicable because $\\chi$ is $C^2$, indeed $C^k$ with $k\\ge2$). Electric field: componentwise, $-\\nabla(\\varphi-\\partial_t\\chi)-\\partial_t(A+\\nabla\\chi)=-\\nabla\\varphi-\\partial_tA+(\\nabla\\partial_t\\chi-\\partial_t\\nabla\\chi)$, where the bracket vanishes by equality of the mixed second partials of the $C^2$ function $\\chi$ ([[thm-clairaut-schwarz-mixed-partials]]) and the componentwise linearity of $\\nabla$ and $\\partial_t$ is [[thm-algebra-of-total-derivatives]] and [[def-directional-and-partial-derivatives]]. Regularity: $\\partial_t\\chi$ and $\\nabla\\chi$ are $C^{k-1}$ ([[def-ck-euclidean-maps-and-diffeomorphisms]]), so the transformed pair is $C^{k-1}$ and the two displayed field expressions are legitimate there; the common value equals the $C^{k-1}$ map $E(\\varphi,A)$, resp. $B(\\varphi,A)$, supplied by [[def-em-potential-gauge-and-field-conventions]]. No further hypothesis is used.",
          "provenance": {
