          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-cross-product-in-r3": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-directional-and-partial-derivatives": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-em-vacuum-stress-momentum": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "lem-em-parameter-integrals": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-em-quadratic-stress-identity": "mathematical-premise",
            "post-em-lorentz-coupling": "physical-assumption",
            "pthm-em-angular-balance": "physical-result",
            "pthm-em-momentum-balance": "physical-result",
            "pthm-em-poynting-balance": "physical-result",
            "thm-algebra-of-derivatives": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-divergence-theorem-for-bounded-piecewise-c-one-domains": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-graphs-of-continuous-functions-have-content-zero": "mathematical-premise",
            "cor-integral-over-a-null-set-vanishes": "mathematical-premise",
            "cor-zero-derivative-implies-constant": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-em-fields": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "post-em-vacuum-maxwell": "physical-assumption"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume the hypotheses of [[pthm-em-poynting-balance]] and\n[[pthm-em-momentum-balance]]: the smooth branch of\n[[post-em-vacuum-maxwell]] and clause (ii) of [[post-em-lorentz-coupling]] on\nthe laboratory region $U\\cong I\\times\\Omega$, jointly $C^1$ fields of\n[[def-em-fields]], continuous sources, the constants of the framework, and the\nfield objects $u,S,g,\\Pi$ of [[def-em-vacuum-stress-momentum]]. Suppose in\naddition that matter fields\n$u_m:\\Omega\\times I\\to\\mathbb R$, $S_m:\\Omega\\times I\\to\\mathbb R^3$,\n$g_m:\\Omega\\times I\\to\\mathbb R^3$ and a symmetric matrix-valued map\n$\\Pi_m:\\Omega\\times I\\to\\mathbb R^{3\\times3}$ are of class $C^1$, with\n$\\Pi_{m,ij}=\\Pi_{m,ji}$ and $(\\operatorname{div}\\Pi_m)_i=\\sum_{j=1}^3\\partial_j\\Pi_{m,ij}$.\nTheir SI units are respectively $\\mathrm J\\,\\mathrm m^{-3}$,\n$\\mathrm W\\,\\mathrm m^{-2}$, $\\mathrm{kg}\\,\\mathrm m^{-2}\\mathrm s^{-1}$ and\n$\\mathrm N\\,\\mathrm m^{-2}$, matching the field quantities added below.\nAssume they satisfy the matter balance equations\n\n$$\\partial_tu_m+\\operatorname{div}S_m=J\\cdot E,\\qquad\\partial_tg_m+\\operatorname{div}\\Pi_m=f,$$\n\npointwise on $\\Omega\\times I$, where $f=\\rho E+J\\times B$ and $J\\cdot E$ are\nthe coupling densities of clause (ii). Put\n$u_{\\mathrm{tot}}:=u+u_m$, $S_{\\mathrm{tot}}:=S+S_m$,\n$g_{\\mathrm{tot}}:=g+g_m$, $\\Pi_{\\mathrm{tot}}:=\\Pi+\\Pi_m$ (symmetric) and\n$\\ell_{\\mathrm{tot}}:=x\\times g_{\\mathrm{tot}}$. Then:\n\n(a) [Local conservation] On $\\Omega\\times I$,\n\n$$\\partial_tu_{\\mathrm{tot}}+\\operatorname{div}S_{\\mathrm{tot}}=0,\\qquad\\partial_tg_{\\mathrm{tot}}+\\operatorname{div}\\Pi_{\\mathrm{tot}}=0,\\qquad\\partial_t\\ell_{\\mathrm{tot}}+\\operatorname{div}(x\\times\\Pi_{\\mathrm{tot}})=0$$\n\ncomponentwise in the last two identities.\n\n(b) [Fixed-volume conservation] Let $\\Omega'\\subseteq\\Omega$ be open with\n$\\overline{\\Omega'}\\subseteq\\Omega$ carrying the finite piecewise $C^1$\npresentation of\n[[thm-divergence-theorem-for-bounded-piecewise-c-one-domains]], let\n$t_0<t_1$ with $(t_0,t_1)\\subseteq I$, assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$\n([[def-countable-choice]]), and let $n$ be the outward unit normal. Then for\nevery $t\\in(t_0,t_1)$,\n\n$$\\frac{d}{dt}\\int_{\\Omega'}u_{\\mathrm{tot}}\\,dx=-\\oint_{\\partial\\Omega'}S_{\\mathrm{tot}}\\cdot n\\,dS,\\qquad\\frac{d}{dt}\\int_{\\Omega'}g_{{\\mathrm{tot}},i}\\,dx=-\\oint_{\\partial\\Omega'}\\Bigl(\\sum_{j=1}^{3}\\Pi_{{\\mathrm{tot}},ij}n_j\\Bigr)dS,\\qquad\\frac{d}{dt}\\int_{\\Omega'}\\ell_{{\\mathrm{tot}},i}\\,dx=-\\oint_{\\partial\\Omega'}\\Bigl(\\sum_{j=1}^{3}(x\\times\\Pi_{\\mathrm{tot}})_{ij}n_j\\Bigr)dS,$$\n\nthe closed-surface integrals being finite face sums of that divergence\ntheorem. Consequently each of the three totals is constant on $(t_0,t_1)$ if\nand only if the corresponding boundary flux integral vanishes for every\n$t\\in(t_0,t_1)$.\n\n(c) [Scope] The matter balances are additional, explicitly stated assumptions,\nnot consequences of the Maxwell postulates: a prescribed current $(\\rho,J)$\ndoes not by itself supply matter fields satisfying them, and \"closed system\" is\na modelling choice about which boundary terms are included. The hypotheses and\nexclusions of the two field theorems are inherited, and no empirical claim is\nmade.",
          "strategy": "direct; add each matter balance to the corresponding field balance to obtain the total energy and momentum identities, obtain the total angular identity by adding the field angular balance to the angular identity implied by the matter momentum balance, and integrate with the divergence theorem.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "L. D. Landau, E. M. Lifshitz, The Classical Theory of Fields, Third Revised English Edition (Course of Theoretical Physics vol. 2, Pergamon Press 1971, 387 pp.)",
                "url": "http://www.elegio.it/mc2/LandauLifshitz_TheClassicalTheoryOfFields_text.pdf",
                "locator": "§33 printed pp. 81-83 (PDF pp. 93-95), eqs. (33.1), (33.3), (33.5)-(33.8): electromagnetic tensor, spatial stress, non-interacting charged-particle matter tensor and cancellation of field/matter divergences. The general smooth matter balances in this item are explicitly assumed. Relevant passages independently read during Step 5a reader-32, 10 October 2026."
              },
              {
                "title": "David Tong, Electromagnetism, University of Cambridge Part II Mathematical Tripos lecture notes (cover dated Lent Term 2015, 236-page PDF)",
                "url": "https://davidtong.org/pdfs/teaching/electromagnetism/electro.pdf",
                "locator": "§5.6.2 printed pp. 130-131 (PDF pp. 138-139): the electromagnetic tensor and its field-only divergence in the presence of current. This section does not supply the matter tensor; the matter balances in this item are additional explicit assumptions. Relevant passages independently read during Step 5a reader-32, 10 October 2026."
              },
              {
                "title": "David J. Griffiths, Introduction to Electrodynamics, 3rd edition (Prentice Hall 1999, 596 pp.; full scanned text)",
                "url": "https://www.hlevkin.com/hlevkin/90MathPhysBioBooks/Physics/Physics/Electrodynamics/David%20J.%20Griffiths%20-%20Introduction%20to%20Electrodynamics-Prentice%20Hall%20(1999).pdf",
                "locator": "§8.2.3-8.2.4 printed pp. 353-360: total momentum and angular momentum of the field-plus-matter system and the role of the boundary terms; read in the stamped scanned full text"
              }
            ]
          },
          "physical_scope": "The conditional total balances obtained by adding explicitly assumed matter balance equations to the vacuum field balances of the same framework: local zero-source identities for total energy, momentum and orbital angular momentum and their fixed-volume boundary-flux forms. The matter balances are additional assumptions about a specified matter model, not consequences of the Maxwell postulates; no closed system, no conservation without flux conditions and no empirical claim is asserted."
        }
      ],
      "scaffold": "research/plan-classical-electromagnetism-track.md",
      "order": 343
    },
