        {
          "id": "lem-em-admittance-interface-solve",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "The two-equation interface admittance system: solution formulas and the normal-flux identity",
          "reference": "core-conditional-proofs.md#K8; scaffold-added necessary prerequisite (see research/physics-em-sr-40-2026-10-08-batch-34.notes.md)",
          "design_state": "new-local-prerequisite; complete-proof-strategy",
          "dependency_level": 3,
          "deps": [
            "def-complex-numbers-and-arithmetic",
            "thm-complex-numbers-form-a-field",
            "def-complex-conjugate-real-imaginary-part-and-modulus",
            "lem-complex-conjugation-and-modulus-laws",
            "lem-em-interface-wave-linear-system",
            "def-ordered-field",
            "lem-of-square-monotone",
            "lem-of-square-positive"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-complex-numbers-and-arithmetic": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-complex-numbers-form-a-field": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-complex-conjugate-real-imaginary-part-and-modulus": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-complex-conjugation-and-modulus-laws": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-em-interface-wave-linear-system": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-ordered-field": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-of-square-monotone": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-of-square-positive": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Let $Y_1,Y_2\\in\\mathbb C$ with $Y_1+Y_2\\ne0$, and let $E_i,E_r,E_t\\in\\mathbb C$ satisfy the two linear equations $$E_i+E_r=E_t,\\qquad Y_1(E_i-E_r)=Y_2E_t.$$ Then: (a) [Solution] If $E_i\\ne0$, then $$r:=\\frac{E_r}{E_i}=\\frac{Y_1-Y_2}{Y_1+Y_2},\\qquad t:=\\frac{E_t}{E_i}=\\frac{2Y_1}{Y_1+Y_2};$$ if $E_i=0$ then $E_r=E_t=0$ and the field ratios are undefined. Throughout (b)-(d), $r,t$ denote the displayed algebraic transfer coefficients $(Y_1-Y_2)/(Y_1+Y_2)$ and $2Y_1/(Y_1+Y_2)$, which are defined independently of $E_i$; when $E_i\\ne0$ they equal the field ratios of (a). (b) [Normal-flux identity] If $Y_1>0$ is real (the incident side admittance), then $$|r|^2+\\frac{\\operatorname{Re}Y_2}{Y_1}\\,|t|^2=1,$$ and explicitly $|t|^2=\\dfrac{4Y_1^2}{|Y_1+Y_2|^2}$ and $|r|^2=1-\\dfrac{4Y_1\\operatorname{Re}Y_2}{|Y_1+Y_2|^2}$. The second summand $(\\operatorname{Re}Y_2/Y_1)|t|^2$ is nonnegative if and only if $\\operatorname{Re}Y_2\\ge0$; it is the normal-flux coefficient of a passive transmitted medium and may be negative for an active one, in which case $|r|>1$ and the identity carries no energy-conservation reading. (c) [Pure-imaginary admittance] If $Y_1>0$ is real and $Y_2$ is purely imaginary, then $|r|=1$, $\\operatorname{Re}Y_2\\,|t|^2=0$ and $|t|^2=\\dfrac{4Y_1^2}{Y_1^2+|Y_2|^2}>0$; in particular $r\\ne0$ and $t\\ne0$. (d) [Real-positive specialisation] If $Y_1,Y_2>0$ are real, then $r=(Y_1-Y_2)/(Y_1+Y_2)$ and $t=2Y_1/(Y_1+Y_2)$ are real and $|r|^2+(Y_2/Y_1)|t|^2=1$; with $Y_j=1/Z_j$, $Z_j>0$, this is $r=(Z_2-Z_1)/(Z_1+Z_2)$, $t=2Z_2/(Z_1+Z_2)$ and $R+T=1$ for $R=|r|^2$, $T=(Z_1/Z_2)|t|^2$, in agreement with [[lem-em-interface-wave-linear-system]]. (e) [Scope] The lemma is pure algebra of $\\mathbb C$; the labels 'incident', 'reflected' and 'transmitted' and the interpretation of the second summand as a flux fraction belong to the consuming physical theorem, not to this lemma.",
          "strategy": "Proof technique: direct; solve the two linear equations by substitution, expand the moduli with $|z|^2=z\\overline z$, and read the sign statements off the ordered-field structure of $\\mathbb R$. 1.1 [Solution of the linear system] Substituting the first equation $E_r=E_t-E_i$ into the second gives $Y_1(2E_i-E_t)=Y_2E_t$, that is $2Y_1E_i=(Y_1+Y_2)E_t$ after expanding and collecting terms by the field arithmetic of [F1]. Since $Y_1+Y_2\\ne0$ is invertible in the field $\\mathbb C$ by [F1], $E_t=2Y_1E_i/(Y_1+Y_2)$, and then $E_r=E_t-E_i=\\bigl(2Y_1-(Y_1+Y_2)\\bigr)E_i/(Y_1+Y_2)=(Y_1-Y_2)E_i/(Y_1+Y_2)$, again by [F1]. [given, F1, algebra] 2.1 [Consequences of the solution] If $E_i\\ne0$, dividing the two identities of step 1.1 by $E_i$ gives $r=E_r/E_i=(Y_1-Y_2)/(Y_1+Y_2)$ and $t=E_t/E_i=2Y_1/(Y_1+Y_2)$. If $E_i=0$, the identities of step 1.1 give $E_t=0$ and $E_r=0$, so no field ratio exists; the algebraic expressions $r=(Y_1-Y_2)/(Y_1+Y_2)$ and $t=2Y_1/(Y_1+Y_2)$ remain defined because $Y_1+Y_2\\ne0$, and they agree with the field ratios whenever the latter exist. This proves (a) and the convention stated before (b). [step 1.1, F1, algebra] 3.1 [Modular expansions] For any $z,w\\in\\mathbb C$, $|z\\pm w|^2=(z\\pm w)(\\overline z\\pm\\overline w)=|z|^2\\pm(z\\overline w+\\overline z w)+|w|^2$, and $z\\overline w+\\overline z w=2\\operatorname{Re}(z\\overline w)$ by [F2]; hence for real $Y_1$ and arbitrary $Y_2$, $|Y_1\\pm Y_2|^2=Y_1^2\\pm2Y_1\\operatorname{Re}Y_2+|Y_2|^2$, and subtraction gives $|Y_1+Y_2|^2-|Y_1-Y_2|^2=4Y_1\\operatorname{Re}Y_2$. Moreover $|r|^2=|Y_1-Y_2|^2/|Y_1+Y_2|^2$ and $|t|^2=4Y_1^2/|Y_1+Y_2|^2$: indeed $|zw|=|z||w|$ and $|z|^2=z\\overline z$ by [F2] applied to the quotients of step 2.1 give $|r|^2=|Y_1-Y_2|^2|Y_1+Y_2|^{-2}$ and $|t|^2=|2Y_1|^2|Y_1+Y_2|^{-2}=4Y_1^2|Y_1+Y_2|^{-2}$ because $(2Y_1)\\overline{(2Y_1)}=4Y_1^2$ for real $Y_1$, and the denominator is nonzero since $Y_1+Y_2\\ne0$. [step 2.1, F2, algebra] 4.1 [The flux identity] Assume $Y_1>0$ real. By [F2] and [F3], $|Y_1+Y_2|^2>0$, so $|t|^2=4Y_1^2/|Y_1+Y_2|^2>0$, and the identity of step 3.1 gives $|r|^2=|Y_1-Y_2|^2/|Y_1+Y_2|^2=1-4Y_1\\operatorname{Re}Y_2/|Y_1+Y_2|^2$; adding $(\\operatorname{Re}Y_2/Y_1)|t|^2=4Y_1\\operatorname{Re}Y_2/|Y_1+Y_2|^2$ cancels the correction and yields $|r|^2+(\\operatorname{Re}Y_2/Y_1)|t|^2=1$, the displayed identity and explicit formulas of (b). [step 3.1, F1, F2, F3, algebra] 5.1 [Sign analysis] Still with $Y_1>0$ real: since $|t|^2>0$ by step 4.1, the second summand $(\\operatorname{Re}Y_2/Y_1)|t|^2$ has the sign of $\\operatorname{Re}Y_2$ by [F3], so it is nonnegative if and only if $\\operatorname{Re}Y_2\\ge0$. If $\\operatorname{Re}Y_2<0$, then $|r|^2=1-4Y_1\\operatorname{Re}Y_2/|Y_1+Y_2|^2>1$, and since $|r|\\ge0$ and $1\\ge0$, [F4] gives $|r|>1$; in that case the identity of step 4.1 has a negative transmitted term and carries no energy-conservation reading, while $|r|>1$ alone is consistent with an active transmitted model. [step 4.1, F3, F4, algebra] 5.2 [Purely imaginary admittance] Assume $Y_1>0$ real and $Y_2=i\\beta$ with $\\beta\\in\\mathbb R$. Then $\\overline{Y_1+Y_2}=Y_1-i\\beta=Y_1-Y_2$ by [F2], so $|Y_1-Y_2|=|\\overline{Y_1+Y_2}|=|Y_1+Y_2|$ by [F2] and step 3.1 gives $|r|=1$; the identity of step 4.1 then gives $\\operatorname{Re}Y_2\\,|t|^2=0$ (multiplying the identity by $Y_1>0$ and using $|r|^2=1$), while $|t|^2=4Y_1^2/|Y_1+Y_2|^2=4Y_1^2/(Y_1^2+\\beta^2)=4Y_1^2/(Y_1^2+|Y_2|^2)>0$ by [F2] and [F3]; hence $r\\ne0$ because $|r|=1$ and $t\\ne0$ because $|t|>0$ by the definiteness of the modulus in [F2]. This proves (c); no division by $\\operatorname{Re}Y_2=0$ is performed, and the case $Y_2=0$ is included with $\\beta=0$. [step 4.1, step 3.1, F2, F3, algebra] 5.3 [Real-positive specialisation] Assume $Y_1,Y_2>0$ real. Then $Y_1-Y_2$ is real and $Y_1+Y_2>0$ is real and nonzero, so $r,t$ of step 2.1 are real by [F1], and step 4.1 gives $|r|^2+(Y_2/Y_1)|t|^2=1$ because $\\operatorname{Re}Y_2=Y_2$. Substituting $Y_j=1/Z_j$ with $Z_j>0$ real, $Y_j$ is invertible and $1/Z_1\\pm1/Z_2=(Z_2\\pm Z_1)/(Z_1Z_2)$ by [F1], so $r=(Z_2-Z_1)/(Z_1+Z_2)$ and $t=2Z_2/(Z_1+Z_2)$ by cancellation of the nonzero factor $Z_1Z_2$; moreover $Y_2/Y_1=Z_1/Z_2$ by [F1], so the balance is $R+T=1$ for $R=|r|^2$ and $T=(Z_1/Z_2)|t|^2$. These are exactly the solution formulas and the balance of [F5], so clause (d) is in agreement with [[lem-em-interface-wave-linear-system]]. [step 4.1, step 2.1, F1, F5, algebra] 6.1 [Scope] Clause (e) holds: the entire argument is algebra in the field $\\mathbb C$ together with the ordered-field arithmetic of the real scalars $Y_1,\\operatorname{Re}Y_2$; no wave model, no labelling of the amplitudes and no interpretation of the second summand is used, and no choice principle occurs, all divisions being by explicitly nonzero field elements. [given, F1, F5, algebra] ∎",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
