            "cor-complex-exponential-cartesian-form-modulus-and-eulers-identity": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume the elementary inertial-rest branch of [[post-em-material-closure]] in the laboratory region $U\\cong I\\times\\Omega$ of [[def-em-lab-geometry]] with the units of [[def-em-si-conventions]], in its isotropic scalar case: the material is at rest in the laboratory frame, and the constitutive relations of [[def-em-polarization-magnetization]] hold with constant scalars $\\varepsilon>0$ (F$\\,$m$^{-1}$), $\\mu>0$ (H$\\,$m$^{-1}$) and $\\sigma\\ge0$ (S$\\,$m$^{-1}$), so that $D=\\varepsilon E$, $B=\\mu H$ and the free current is $J_f=\\sigma E+J_{\\mathrm{ext}}$ for a declared external free current $J_{\\mathrm{ext}}$. Write $c>0$ for the exact vacuum speed of [[def-em-si-conventions]] and let $\\omega>0$ (s$^{-1}$) be an angular frequency. Define: (a) [Lossless parameters] with $\\sqrt{\\cdot}$ the nonnegative square root of [[thm-of-square-roots]], $$v:=(\\varepsilon\\mu)^{-1/2}\\quad(\\mathrm m\\,\\mathrm s^{-1}),\\qquad Z:=\\Bigl(\\frac{\\mu}{\\varepsilon}\\Bigr)^{1/2}\\quad(\\Omega),\\qquad n:=\\frac{c}{v}=c(\\varepsilon\\mu)^{1/2}\\quad(\\text{dimensionless}),\\qquad k(\\omega):=\\frac{\\omega}{v};$$ $v$ is the phase speed, $Z$ the wave impedance, $n$ the refractive index relative to vacuum and $k(\\omega)$ the real wavenumber of the lossless case. (b) [Complex propagation constant] put $a:=\\mu\\varepsilon\\omega^{2}>0$, $b:=\\mu\\sigma\\omega\\ge0$, $r:=\\sqrt{a^{2}+b^{2}}$ and $$p(\\omega):=\\sqrt{\\frac{r+a}{2}},\\qquad q(\\omega):=\\sqrt{\\frac{r-a}{2}},\\qquad \\kappa(\\omega):=p(\\omega)+i\\,q(\\omega).$$ Then $\\kappa(\\omega)$ is the unique $k\\in\\mathbb C$ with $\\operatorname{Re}k\\ge0$, $\\operatorname{Im}k\\ge0$ and $k^{2}=\\varepsilon\\mu\\omega^{2}+i\\mu\\sigma\\omega=a+ib$; in the lossless case $\\sigma=0$ one has $b=0$, $q=0$ and $\\kappa(\\omega)=k(\\omega)=p(\\omega)$ real. (The explicit formula is the one of [[thm-every-complex-number-has-a-square-root]]; the verification $p^{2}-q^{2}=a$, $2pq=b$ and the uniqueness of the root with $\\operatorname{Re}k\\ge0$, $\\operatorname{Im}k\\ge0$ are verified in the well-definedness paragraph below.) (c) [Skin depth] call $\\delta(\\omega):=1/q(\\omega)$ (m) the skin depth if $\\sigma>0$, and set $\\delta(\\omega):=+\\infty$ if $\\sigma=0$: for $\\kappa(\\omega)=p+iq$ and $x_3\\in\\mathbb R$ the modulus of $e^{i(\\kappa x_3-\\omega t)}$ equals $e^{-q x_3}$ ([[cor-complex-exponential-cartesian-form-modulus-and-eulers-identity]]), so $\\delta$ is the distance in which that modulus decays by the factor $1/e$ in the direction of increasing $x_3$; for $\\sigma=0$ there is no attenuation and $\\delta$ is infinite rather than a division by zero. (d) [Status and scope] This item fixes objects, units, branch conventions and terminology only. It asserts no field equation, no dispersion relation for a solution, no attenuation of any concrete field and no material validity. The parameters are declared for the isotropic scalar constant-coefficient branch at rest in the laboratory frame; for $\\varepsilon\\mu<c^{-2}$ the branch is, by [[post-em-material-closure]](b), a declared finite-band effective phase-response model with no universal front-speed claim, while $\\varepsilon\\mu\\ge c^{-2}$ is the exact broadband case. No measured value, precision or empirical statement is included.",
          "strategy": "The material assumptions, the rest-frame clause, the isotropic scalar case and the finite-band caveat are those of [[post-em-material-closure]](a)-(b) read with [[def-em-polarization-magnetization|the polarization and magnetization definitions]]; the unit system and the exact constant $c$ are those of [[def-em-si-conventions]]; the laboratory chart is that of [[def-em-lab-geometry]]. The only content beyond notation is the well-definedness of $\\kappa(\\omega)$ in (b). With $a>0$, $b\\ge0$ and $r=\\sqrt{a^{2}+b^{2}}$ one has $r+a>0$ and $(r-a)(r+a)=b^2\\ge0$, so $r-a\\ge0$ and both defining radicands are nonnegative. If $b>0$, the same identity gives $r-a>0$, hence $q>0$; if $b=0$, uniqueness of nonnegative roots gives $r=a$ and $q=0$. Also $p>0$ because $r+a>0$. Thus $p^{2}-q^{2}=(r+a)/2-(r-a)/2=a$ and $(2pq)^{2}=4\\cdot(r+a)(r-a)/4=r^{2}-a^{2}=b^{2}$, so $2pq=b$ because $p,q\\ge0$ ([[thm-of-square-roots]]); hence $\\kappa^{2}=p^{2}-q^{2}+2ipq=a+ib$, by the field arithmetic of [[def-complex-numbers-and-arithmetic]]. The square roots of $a+ib$ are exactly $\\pm\\kappa$: if $z^2=\\kappa^2$, then $(z-\\kappa)(z+\\kappa)=0$, and the complex field property ([[thm-complex-numbers-form-a-field]]) gives $z=\\kappa$ or $z=-\\kappa$. If $k=u+iv$ with $u,v\\ge0$ and $k^{2}=a+ib$, then $u^{2}-v^{2}=a$, $2uv=b$ and $u^{2}+v^{2}=|k|^{2}=|k^{2}|=\\sqrt{a^{2}+b^{2}}=r$, where $|k^{2}|=|k|^{2}$ is the multiplicativity of the modulus ([[lem-complex-conjugation-and-modulus-laws]]) and $|a+ib|=\\sqrt{a^{2}+b^{2}}$ is the modulus of [[def-complex-conjugate-real-imaginary-part-and-modulus]]; solving gives $u^{2}=(r+a)/2=p^{2}$ and $v^{2}=(r-a)/2=q^{2}$, and since $u,v,p,q\\ge0$ the uniqueness of the nonnegative square root ([[thm-of-square-roots]]) gives $u=p$ and $v=q$, so $k=\\kappa$. In the lossless case $\\sigma=0$ one has $b=0$, $r=a$, $q=0$, $p=\\sqrt a=\\omega(\\varepsilon\\mu)^{1/2}=k(\\omega)$ by [[thm-of-square-roots]]. All divisions are by strictly positive real numbers, $v$ and $q$ are nonzero exactly where defined, and no choice principle is used.",
          "physical_scope": "Terminology, units and branch conventions for homogeneous isotropic materials at rest in the laboratory frame in the constant scalar branch D=eps E, B=mu H, J_f=sigma E+J_ext with eps,mu>0 and sigma>=0: the lossless phase speed, wave impedance, refractive index and wavenumber, the complex propagation constant kappa=p+iq as the unique root with Re,Im>=0 of k^2=eps*mu*omega^2+i*mu*sigma*omega, and the skin depth. Objects, units and conventions only: no field equation, no dispersion relation for a solution, no attenuation of any concrete field and no material validity or measured value.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "not-applicable"
          },
