          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "cor-complex-exponential-cartesian-form-modulus-and-eulers-identity": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-ck-euclidean-maps-and-diffeomorphisms": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-complex-conjugate-real-imaginary-part-and-modulus": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-complex-exponential": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-complex-numbers-and-arithmetic": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-directional-and-partial-derivatives": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-divergence-and-curl-of-a-c1-vector-field": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-algebra-of-derivatives": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-chain-rule-for-total-derivatives": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-complex-exponential-is-entire-with-derivative-itself": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-complex-numbers-form-a-field": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-sine-and-cosine-addition-formulas": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-sine-cosine-zero-sets-and-fundamental-period": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-derivative-of-exponential": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-sine-and-cosine-derivatives": "mathematical-premise",
            "cor-trigonometric-parity-and-pythagorean-identity": "mathematical-premise",
            "cor-exponential-reciprocal-and-positivity": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Let $\\Omega_t\\subseteq\\mathbb R^2$ be open, let $\\beta\\in\\mathbb C$, $\\omega>0$, and let $\\tilde F,\\tilde G:\\Omega_t\\to\\mathbb C^3$ be $C^1$ maps (componentwise, in the sense of [[def-ck-euclidean-maps-and-diffeomorphisms]]). Write $\\theta(x_3,t):=\\beta x_3-\\omega t$ and define $F:\\Omega_t\\times\\mathbb R\\times\\mathbb R\\to\\mathbb R^3$ by $F(x_1,x_2,x_3,t):=\\operatorname{Re}\\bigl(\\tilde F(x_1,x_2)e^{i\\theta(x_3,t)}\\bigr)$ componentwise, and $G$ likewise from $\\tilde G$; here $e^{i\\theta}$ is the complex exponential of [[def-complex-exponential]] and $\\operatorname{Re}$ the real part of [[def-complex-conjugate-real-imaginary-part-and-modulus]]. Then $F$ is $C^1$ and, for every point of the domain:\n(a) $\\partial_{x_j}F=\\operatorname{Re}\\bigl(\\partial_{x_j}\\tilde F\\,e^{i\\theta}\\bigr)$ for $j=1,2$, $\\partial_{x_3}F=\\operatorname{Re}\\bigl(i\\beta\\tilde F e^{i\\theta}\\bigr)$, $\\partial_tF=\\operatorname{Re}\\bigl(-i\\omega\\tilde F e^{i\\theta}\\bigr)$, where the divergence and curl are those of [[def-divergence-and-curl-of-a-c1-vector-field]] and the partial derivatives are those of [[def-directional-and-partial-derivatives]];\n(b) $\\operatorname{div}F=\\operatorname{Re}\\bigl((\\partial_1\\tilde F_1+\\partial_2\\tilde F_2+i\\beta\\tilde F_3)e^{i\\theta}\\bigr)$;\n(c) $\\operatorname{curl}F=\\operatorname{Re}\\bigl((\\partial_2\\tilde F_3-i\\beta\\tilde F_2,\\; i\\beta\\tilde F_1-\\partial_1\\tilde F_3,\\; \\partial_1\\tilde F_2-\\partial_2\\tilde F_1)e^{i\\theta}\\bigr)$;\n(d) [amplitude injectivity] if $C\\in\\mathbb C^3$ and $\\operatorname{Re}\\bigl(Ce^{i\\varphi_1}\\bigr)=\\operatorname{Re}\\bigl(Ce^{i\\varphi_2}\\bigr)=0$ for two real phases with $\\varphi_1-\\varphi_2\\notin\\pi\\mathbb Z$, then $C=0$; consequently, if $F=G$ on a nonempty open subset $U$ of $\\Omega_t\\times\\mathbb R\\times\\mathbb R$, then $\\tilde F=\\tilde G$ on the projection of $U$ to $\\Omega_t$ (a nonempty open subset of $\\Omega_t$).",
          "strategy": "Differentiate each component of $\\operatorname{Re}(we^{i\\theta})$ with $w=\\tilde F_j$ by the product and chain rules for real and imaginary parts ([[thm-algebra-of-derivatives]], [[thm-chain-rule-for-total-derivatives]], [[thm-complex-exponential-is-entire-with-derivative-itself]]), using $\\operatorname{Re}(i\\zeta)=-\\operatorname{Im}\\zeta$ and $\\operatorname{Re}(-i\\zeta)=\\operatorname{Im}\\zeta$; assemble the divergence and curl componentwise. For (d), write $C=a+ib$ with real $a,b$; the two scalar equations $a\\cos\\varphi_j-b\\sin\\varphi_j=0$ ($j=1,2$) form a real $2\\times2$ system of determinant $\\sin(\\varphi_1-\\varphi_2)$ for each component, The determinant is nonzero by [[thm-sine-cosine-zero-sets-and-fundamental-period]]; the determinant identity is the sine subtraction formula of [[thm-sine-and-cosine-addition-formulas]], with real-part encoding justified by [[cor-complex-exponential-cartesian-form-modulus-and-eulers-identity]]. Hence $a_j=b_j=0$. If $F=G$ on an open $U$, then for every $x_t$ in the projection fix one real $x_3$ in that open fibre and vary $t$ on a small open interval. Put $C=(\\tilde F(x_t)-\\tilde G(x_t))e^{i\\beta x_3}$; the exponential is nonzero even for complex $\\beta$. The real time phases $-\\omega t$ contain an interval and hence two values with difference strictly between $0$ and $\\pi$. Clause (d) forces $C=0$ and therefore $\\tilde F(x_t)=\\tilde G(x_t)$. Complex $\\beta$ changes a fixed spatial amplitude factor, not this real time-phase injectivity. The projection of a nonempty open set is nonempty and open.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
