          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Let $e_z$ be a unit vector of $\\mathbb R^3$ and identify $\\mathbb R^3=\\mathbb R^2\\oplus\\mathbb R e_z$ with transverse coordinates $(x_1,x_2)$; write $\\nabla_t h=(\\partial_1h,\\partial_2h)$, $\\Delta_t h=\\partial_1^2h+\\partial_2^2h$ and, for a transverse $C^1$ map $u_t$ with components $(u_1,u_2)$, $\\operatorname{div}_t u_t=\\partial_1u_1+\\partial_2u_2$ and $\\operatorname{curl}_2 u_t=\\partial_1u_2-\\partial_2u_1$; regard $h$, $\\nabla_th$, $u_t$ and $e_z\\times u_t$ as $z$-independent fields on $\\Omega_t\\times\\mathbb R$, with $e_z$ the third basis vector. Let $h:\\Omega_t\\to\\mathbb R$ be $C^2$ and $u_t:\\Omega_t\\to\\mathbb R^2$ be $C^1$. Then, with the divergence, curl, cross product and inner product of [[def-divergence-and-curl-of-a-c1-vector-field]], [[def-cross-product-in-r3]], [[def-euclidean-inner-product]]:\n(a) $\\operatorname{div}(e_z\\times\\nabla_th)=0$; $\\operatorname{curl}(e_z\\times\\nabla_th)=e_z\\,\\Delta_th$; $e_z\\times(e_z\\times\\nabla_th)=-\\nabla_th$; $\\nabla_th\\cdot(e_z\\times\\nabla_th)=0$; $e_z\\cdot(e_z\\times\\nabla_th)=0$; $|e_z\\times\\nabla_th|=|\\nabla_th|$;\n(b) $\\operatorname{curl}(e_zh)=-e_z\\times\\nabla_th$ and $\\operatorname{div}(e_zh)=\\partial_3h$ (which vanishes for $z$-independent $h$);\n(c) $\\operatorname{curl}(u_t)=e_z\\operatorname{curl}_2u_t$, $\\operatorname{div}(u_t)=\\operatorname{div}_tu_t$, and $e_z\\times u_t$ is transverse.",
          "strategy": "Work in the oriented orthonormal basis $(e_1,e_2,e_z)$ and write out the six component formulas: for $v=\\nabla_th$ one has $e_z\\times v=(-\\partial_2h,\\partial_1h,0)$, whence the divergence is $-\\partial_1\\partial_2h+\\partial_2\\partial_1h=0$ by equality of mixed partials ([[thm-clairaut-schwarz-mixed-partials]]), the curl is $(0,0,\\partial_1^2h+\\partial_2^2h)$ and the triple-product and norm identities reduce to $a\\cdot(e_z\\times a)=0$ and $|e_z\\times a|=|a|$ for $a\\perp e_z$ ([[lem-cross-product-is-bilinear-alternating-and-orthogonal]]). For (b) use $\\operatorname{curl}(e_zh)=(\\partial_2h,-\\partial_1h,0)$ and the definition of the curl; for (c) note that a $z$-independent field with zero third component has curl $(0,0,\\partial_1u_2-\\partial_2u_1)$.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "N. Beisert, Elektrodynamik, Vorlesungsskript, ETH Zurich, 2024 FS (German), Chapter 13 'Wellenleiter' and 'Kavitaeten', PDF pp. 153-162 (printed pp. 13.1-13.10); complete 176-page author-hosted PDF and official TeX read, with the conjugate-error in (13.26), the 'Wendepunkt' mislabel and the general group-velocity restriction recorded as source defects not copied",
                "url": "https://people.phys.ethz.ch/~nbeisert/lectures/ED-24FS-Skript.pdf"
