            "cor-complex-exponential-cartesian-form-modulus-and-eulers-identity": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume the elementary inertial-rest branch of [[post-em-material-closure]] in its lossless isotropic scalar case at rest in the laboratory frame: constants $\\varepsilon,\\mu>0$, $\\sigma=0$, $J_{\\mathrm{ext}}=0$, the constitutive relations $D=\\varepsilon E$, $B=\\mu H$ of [[post-em-material-closure]] clause (b), read with the objects $D,H$ of [[def-em-polarization-magnetization]], and the macroscopic equations (b) of [[pthm-em-macroscopic-maxwell]] with $\\rho_f=0$, $J_f=0$ on the guide region; suppose also $\\varepsilon\\mu\\ge c^{-2}$ whenever the broadband interpretation of that branch is used. Let the rectangular guide, its PEC boundary model, the axis $e_z$, the TE/TM/TEM terminology and the separated phasor convention be those of [[def-em-guide-cavity-geometry]] with cross-section $(0,a)\\times(0,b)$, and let $\\omega>0$, $\\beta\\in\\mathbb C$, $k_c^2:=\\omega^2\\varepsilon\\mu-\\beta^2\\in\\mathbb R_{>0}$, $H:=B/\\mu$ and $\\theta:=\\beta x_3-\\omega t$. Write $\\tilde E,\\tilde H$ for the complex amplitudes of the separated real fields $E=\\operatorname{Re}(\\tilde Ee^{i\\theta})$, $H=\\operatorname{Re}(\\tilde He^{i\\theta})$, so that $B=\\mu H$.\n(a) [TE family] For integers $m,n\\ge0$ with $(m,n)\\ne(0,0)$ put $h_{mn}:=\\cos\\frac{m\\pi x_1}{a}\\cos\\frac{n\\pi x_2}{b}$, $k_{mn}^2:=(\\frac{m\\pi}{a})^2+(\\frac{n\\pi}{b})^2$, and require $\\beta^2=\\omega^2\\varepsilon\\mu-k_{mn}^2$; define the complex amplitudes $$\\tilde E:=-\\frac{i\\omega\\mu}{k_{mn}^2}\\,e_z\\times\\nabla_th_{mn},\\qquad \\tilde H:=\\frac{i\\beta}{k_{mn}^2}\\,\\nabla_th_{mn}+e_zh_{mn}.$$ Then the real fields $E=\\operatorname{Re}(\\tilde Ee^{i\\theta})$, $B=\\mu\\operatorname{Re}(\\tilde He^{i\\theta})$ are $C^\\infty$ on the guide region, have $E_z=0$ (TE), satisfy the four source-free macroscopic equations $\\operatorname{div}D=0$, $\\operatorname{div}B=0$, $\\operatorname{curl}E=-\\partial_tB$, $\\operatorname{curl}H=\\partial_tD$, and satisfy $n\\times E=0$ and $n\\cdot B=0$ on every open wall of the guide.\n(b) [TM family] For integers $m,n\\ge1$ put $e_{mn}:=\\sin\\frac{m\\pi x_1}{a}\\sin\\frac{n\\pi x_2}{b}$, $k_{mn}^2:=(\\frac{m\\pi}{a})^2+(\\frac{n\\pi}{b})^2$, require $\\beta^2=\\omega^2\\varepsilon\\mu-k_{mn}^2$, and define $$\\tilde E:=\\frac{i\\beta}{k_{mn}^2}\\nabla_te_{mn}+e_ze_{mn},\\qquad \\tilde H:=\\frac{i\\omega\\varepsilon}{k_{mn}^2}\\,e_z\\times\\nabla_te_{mn}.$$ Then the corresponding real fields are $C^\\infty$, have $B_z=0$ (TM), satisfy the same four equations and the same boundary conditions on the open walls.\n(c) [Index restrictions] For $m=n=0$ one has $\\nabla_th_{00}=0$ and $k_{00}^2=0$ makes the displayed divided reconstruction formulas undefined. A purely longitudinal constant-profile magnetic amplitude with zero electric amplitude cannot be a nonzero monochromatic Maxwell candidate: Faraday gives $0=i\\omega\\mu\\tilde H$, hence $\\tilde H=0$ because $\\omega>0$. At $\\beta=0$ a constant $H_z$ is divergence-free, so divergence alone does not exclude it. Thus $(0,0)$ is excluded by the full field equations and the reconstruction denominator, not by a false divergence claim; for $m=0$ or $n=0$ the TM profile $e_{mn}$ vanishes identically, so TM indices are restricted to $m,n\\ge1$; conversely for $(m,n)\\ne(0,0)$ (resp. $m,n\\ge1$) the displayed profiles and fields are nonzero.\n(d) [Dispersion and cutoff] On the declared family, $k_c^2=\\omega^2\\varepsilon\\mu-\\beta^2$ defines the cutoff $\\omega_c:=k_c/\\sqrt{\\varepsilon\\mu}>0$; real longitudinal wave numbers with $\\beta^2=\\omega^2\\varepsilon\\mu-k_c^2$ exist exactly for $\\omega\\ge\\omega_c$, with $\\beta\\ne0$ exactly for $\\omega>\\omega_c$ and $\\beta=0$ at $\\omega=\\omega_c$; for $\\omega<\\omega_c$ the two algebraic roots are $\\beta=\\pm i\\sqrt{k_c^2-\\varepsilon\\mu\\omega^2}$, and the same verified separated fields have the factor $e^{-\\operatorname{Im}\\beta x_3}$; a declared half-guide may select the decaying sign, and no propagating-power claim is made there.\n(e) [Scope] These are separated candidate modes of the declared lossless model; the theorem asserts no completeness, no uniqueness among fields with the same data, and no lossy, dispersive or open-end behaviour, and it assumes the PEC model of the definition, not the physical infinite-conductivity limit.",
          "strategy": "Under the separated phasor convention, [[lem-em-separated-phasor-calculus]] turns the real field equations into the complex amplitude equations $\\operatorname{div}\\tilde E=0$, $\\operatorname{div}\\tilde H=0$, $\\operatorname{curl}\\tilde E=i\\omega\\mu\\tilde H$, $\\operatorname{curl}\\tilde H=-i\\omega\\varepsilon\\tilde E$; the amplitude injectivity clause makes the reduction an equivalence. Verify these four equations for each family with [[lem-em-transverse-vector-identities]] and the profile identities $\\Delta_th=-k_{mn}^2h$, $\\Delta_te=-k_{mn}^2e$ of [[lem-em-rectangle-mode-profile-identities]]: for the TE family compute $\\operatorname{div}\\tilde E=0$ from $\\operatorname{div}_t(e_z\\times\\nabla_th)=0$, the $z$-curl $\\partial_1\\tilde E_2-\\partial_2\\tilde E_1=i\\omega\\mu h$, and both transverse curls via $e_z\\times(e_z\\times\\nabla_th)=-\\nabla_th$; the TM family is dual with the sign conventions of the definitions. The wall conditions follow because $\\partial_nh=0$ makes the tangential part of $E$ vanish in the TE case, and $e=0$ on $\\partial R$ makes the longitudinal and tangential components of $E$ vanish in the TM case; $n\\cdot B=0$ is verified by the same evaluations. The same derivative calculation of [[lem-em-separated-phasor-calculus]] is valid for complex $\\beta$; all algebraic verifications use $\\beta^2=\\varepsilon\\mu\\omega^2-k_{mn}^2$, not reality of $\\beta$. This supplies the actual below-cutoff imaginary-root branch, with no propagating-power interpretation. The zero TE profile exclusion uses Faraday as stated, while the TM zero-index profile is identically zero. Nondegeneracy follows from the exhibited nonconstant profiles; the cutoff statement is the algebraic solvability of $\\beta^2=\\omega^2\\varepsilon\\mu-k_c^2$. No step uses empirical input.",
          "physical_scope": "The verified separated TE and TM candidate fields of the lossless isotropic scalar constant branch in the straight rectangular perfectly conducting guide with cross-section (0,a)x(0,b), at a declared frequency and longitudinal wave number, including the index exclusions and the cutoff relation. Conditional on the adopted material branch and PEC boundary model; no completeness, lossy or empirical claim.",
