            "thm-algebra-of-function-limits"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-complex-conjugate-real-imaginary-part-and-modulus": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-cross-product-in-r3": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-derivative": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-em-guide-cavity-geometry": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-em-si-conventions": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-euclidean-inner-product": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-cross-product-is-bilinear-alternating-and-orthogonal": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-em-period-average": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-em-rectangle-mode-profile-identities": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-em-transverse-vector-identities": "mathematical-premise",
            "pthm-em-rectangular-mode-candidates": "physical-result",
            "pthm-em-restricted-material-energy": "physical-result",
            "thm-algebra-of-derivatives": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-algebra-of-function-limits": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-chain-rule-for-total-derivatives": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-of-square-roots": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "In the setting of [[pthm-em-rectangular-mode-candidates]] let a TE or TM candidate of part (a) or (b) with $\\beta>0$ and $\\omega>\\omega_c$ be fixed (so $\\beta=\\sqrt{\\omega^2\\varepsilon\\mu-k_c^2}$ is real and nonzero), retain its positive longitudinal amplitude $H_*$ (A m$^{-1}$) in the TE case or $E_*$ (V m$^{-1}$) in the TM case, let $T:=2\\pi/\\omega$, and let $u:=\\frac12(E\\cdot D+B\\cdot H)$ and $S:=E\\times H$ be the stored-energy density and energy-flux vector of [[pthm-em-restricted-material-energy]], with the Euclidean inner and cross products of [[def-euclidean-inner-product]] and [[def-cross-product-in-r3]]. Define the period-averaged stored energy per unit length and the period-averaged longitudinal flux across the cross-section $$U:=\\frac1T\\int_0^T\\!\\!\\int_{R_{ab}}u\\,dx_1dx_2\\,dt,\\qquad \\Phi:=\\frac1T\\int_0^T\\!\\!\\int_{R_{ab}}S\\cdot e_z\\,dx_1dx_2\\,dt,$$ both independent of $z$ and of the starting time. Then:\n(a) [Cross-section identities] $\\int_{R_{ab}}|\\nabla_th_{mn}|^2=k_c^2\\int_{R_{ab}}h_{mn}^2$ and $\\int_{R_{ab}}|\\nabla_te_{mn}|^2=k_c^2\\int_{R_{ab}}e_{mn}^2$, with the boundary terms of the integration by parts vanishing;\n(b) [Energy and flux] for the TE candidate $$U=H_*^2\\frac{\\mu^2\\varepsilon\\omega^2}{2k_c^2}\\int_{R_{ab}}h_{mn}^2,\\qquad \\Phi=H_*^2\\frac{\\omega\\mu\\beta}{2k_c^2}\\int_{R_{ab}}h_{mn}^2,$$ and for the TM candidate $$U=E_*^2\\frac{\\varepsilon^2\\mu\\omega^2}{2k_c^2}\\int_{R_{ab}}e_{mn}^2,\\qquad \\Phi=E_*^2\\frac{\\omega\\varepsilon\\beta}{2k_c^2}\\int_{R_{ab}}e_{mn}^2,$$ with the explicit norms of [[lem-em-rectangle-mode-profile-identities]](c);\n(c) [Energy transport and speed relations] $\\Phi=U\\,\\beta/(\\varepsilon\\mu\\omega)=U\\,v_g$, where $v_g:=d\\omega/d\\beta=\\beta/(\\varepsilon\\mu\\omega)$ is the group speed of the branch $\\omega(\\beta)=\\sqrt{(\\beta^2+k_c^2)/(\\varepsilon\\mu)}$; moreover the phase speed $v_p:=\\omega/\\beta$ satisfies $v_pv_g=1/(\\varepsilon\\mu)$, $v_p>1/\\sqrt{\\varepsilon\\mu}$ and $0<v_g<1/\\sqrt{\\varepsilon\\mu}$ for the declared indices;\n(d) [Finite propagating set] if a candidate with indices $(m,n)$ is propagating at frequency $\\omega$ (that is, $\\beta^2=\\omega^2\\varepsilon\\mu-k_{mn}^2>0$), then $m<\\omega a\\sqrt{\\varepsilon\\mu}/\\pi$ and $n<\\omega b\\sqrt{\\varepsilon\\mu}/\\pi$, so the propagating indices lie in the explicitly bounded index box $\\{m,n\\ge0: m<\\omega a\\sqrt{\\varepsilon\\mu}/\\pi,\\, n<\\omega b\\sqrt{\\varepsilon\\mu}/\\pi\\}$;\n(e) [Scope] This is a lossless separated-guide computation: the period average is over time at fixed position, the flux is through one cross-section, $v_p$ is not asserted to be a signal speed and no bound on information or energy speeds in general dispersive media follows; the material branch and the PEC model are those of the cited theorems.",
          "strategy": "Insert the explicit transverse phasors of [[pthm-em-rectangular-mode-candidates]] into $u$ and $S$ and average the real quadratic expressions with [[lem-em-period-average]] (the common frequency is $\\omega$ and the $z$-dependent phase factors cancel); the cross-section integrals are evaluated with [[lem-em-rectangle-mode-profile-identities]](d) and the pointwise identities $|e_z\\times\\nabla_th|=|\\nabla_th|$, $\\nabla_th\\cdot(e_z\\times\\nabla_th)=0$ and $(e_z\\times\\nabla_th)\\times\\nabla_th=-e_z|\\nabla_th|^2$ of [[lem-em-transverse-vector-identities]]. The positive root $\\omega(\\beta)=\\sqrt{(\\beta^2+k_c^2)/(\\varepsilon\\mu)}$ is well-defined by [[thm-of-square-roots]]. Rationalization gives $|\\omega(\\beta+h)-\\omega(\\beta)|\\le |2\\beta h+h^2|/(\\varepsilon\\mu\\omega(\\beta))$, hence continuity. Its difference quotient is $(2\\beta+h)/[\\varepsilon\\mu(\\omega(\\beta+h)+\\omega(\\beta))]$, whose limit is $\\beta/(\\varepsilon\\mu\\omega(\\beta))$ by [[thm-algebra-of-function-limits]], proving the derivative in [[def-derivative]] and the stated $v_g$ and read off $v_pv_g=1/(\\varepsilon\\mu)$. The local balance $\\partial_tu+\\operatorname{div}S=0$ of [[pthm-em-restricted-material-energy]](a) is consistent with the averaged identities ($\\partial_t\\langle u\\rangle=0$ and $\\partial_z\\langle S\\cdot e_z\\rangle=0$); only the choice-free local clause of that theorem is used. The speed inequalities are the elementary bounds $\\beta^2<\\varepsilon\\mu\\omega^2$ (strict for $k_c>0$). For (d), $k_{mn}^2\\ge(m\\pi/a)^2$ and $k_{mn}^2\\ge(n\\pi/b)^2$ give the two index bounds directly from $k_{mn}^2<\\varepsilon\\mu\\omega^2$. No empirical premise is used.",
          "physical_scope": "The dispersion relation, cutoff branch, phase and group speeds and the cross-section period-averaged energy and Poynting flux of the separated TE/TM candidate modes of the lossless rectangular guide, including the identity of the energy transport ratio with the group speed. Conditional on the adopted lossless material branch and PEC model; no signal-speed or general-dispersion claim.",
