          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "post-em-radiation-selection": "physical-assumption",
            "pthm-em-charge-continuity": "physical-result",
            "lem-em-retarded-wave-kernel": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-em-wave-cauchy-kirchhoff": "mathematical-premise",
            "pthm-em-lorenz-gauge-wave-form": "physical-result",
            "post-em-vacuum-maxwell": "physical-assumption",
            "def-em-sources": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-em-potential-gauge-and-field-conventions": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-em-fields": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-em-lab-geometry": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-em-si-conventions": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "lem-em-parameter-integrals": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-divergence-theorem-for-bounded-c-one-euclidean-domains": "mathematical-premise",
            "cor-c-one-change-of-variables-for-l-one-functions": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-differentiation-under-the-integral-sign": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-linearity-of-the-lebesgue-integral-on-l-one": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-polar-coordinates-formula-for-lebesgue-measure": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-ck-euclidean-maps-and-diffeomorphisms": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ($\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$) as carried by the retarded-kernel and Cauchy suppliers below ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let the laboratory region, chart and units be those of [[def-em-lab-geometry]] and [[def-em-si-conventions]], so that $c>0$, $\\mu_0>0$, $\\varepsilon_0=(\\mu_0c^2)^{-1}$ and $W:=c^{-2}\\partial_t^2-\\Delta$ is the wave expression of [[def-em-potential-gauge-and-field-conventions]]. Let $a>0$, $t_0<T$ and let $\\rho:\\mathbb R^3\\times\\mathbb R\\to\\mathbb R$, $J:\\mathbb R^3\\times\\mathbb R\\to\\mathbb R^3$ be source fields of [[def-em-sources]] that are jointly of class $C^\\infty$ in the sense of [[def-ck-euclidean-maps-and-diffeomorphisms]], vanish identically outside the compact set $\\overline B_a(0)\\times[t_0,T]$, and satisfy the continuity equation $\\partial_t\\rho+\\operatorname{div}J=0$ everywhere --- the compatibility condition that [[pthm-em-charge-continuity]] shows to be forced by the Maxwell system, here assumed for the prescribed source. Define the retarded potentials by the explicit retarded integrals $$\\varphi(x,t):=\\frac{1}{4\\pi\\varepsilon_0}\\int_{\\mathbb R^3}\\frac{\\rho\\bigl(y,t-|x-y|/c\\bigr)}{|x-y|}\\,dy,\\qquad A(x,t):=\\frac{\\mu_0}{4\\pi}\\int_{\\mathbb R^3}\\frac{J\\bigl(y,t-|x-y|/c\\bigr)}{|x-y|}\\,dy,$$ and put $E:=-\\nabla\\varphi-\\partial_tA$, $B:=\\nabla\\times A$ ([[def-em-potential-gauge-and-field-conventions]], [[def-em-fields]]). Then: (a) [Smoothness and wave equations] $\\varphi$ and each component of $A$ are of class $C^\\infty$ on $\\mathbb R^3\\times\\mathbb R$, and $W\\varphi=\\rho/\\varepsilon_0$, $WA=\\mu_0J$ pointwise. (b) [Lorenz gauge] With $G:=\\operatorname{div}A+c^{-2}\\partial_t\\varphi$ one has $G=0$ on $\\mathbb R^3\\times\\mathbb R$: the retarded pair is in Lorenz gauge, the continuity hypothesis supplies this identity and the total-charge conclusion (f). (c) [Maxwell fields] $E$ and $B$ are of class $C^\\infty$ and the tuple $(E,B,\\rho,J)$ satisfies the smooth branch of the vacuum Maxwell equations of [[post-em-vacuum-maxwell]] on the whole of $\\mathbb R^3\\times\\mathbb R$: $\\operatorname{div}E=\\rho/\\varepsilon_0$, $\\operatorname{div}B=0$, $\\nabla\\times E=-\\partial_tB$, $\\nabla\\times B=\\mu_0J+c^{-2}\\partial_tE$. (d) [No field before the source] $E=B=0$ at every event with $t<t_0$ (indeed $\\varphi=A=0$ there): the selected retarded solution carries no field from before the source acted. (e) [Zero-data Cauchy identification] For every $t_1<t_0$ the pair $(\\varphi,A)$ restricted to $\\mathbb R^3\\times[t_1,\\infty)$ is the unique $C^2$ extension solution of the wave Cauchy problem of [[thm-em-wave-cauchy-kirchhoff]] at time $t_1$ with zero Cauchy data and sources $\\rho/\\varepsilon_0$, $\\mu_0J$. (f) [Total charge] The total charge $Q(t):=\\int_{\\mathbb R^3}\\rho(y,t)\\,dy$ is zero for every $t$: a source that is smooth, compactly supported in space and restricted to a compact time interval and satisfies continuity carries zero total charge, so this branch does not model an eternal isolated nonzero charge. (g) [Scope] This is the compact smooth branch with an adopted causal selection; it asserts nothing about point, line or sheet sources, about weak or distributional branches, about finite-energy or decay properties, about radiation reaction or self-force, and no empirical claim. In particular the fields of a prescribed isolated point charge with an eternal worldline are not covered by this theorem and are supplied separately by the point-source items of this page.",
          "strategy": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$. (a) $\\rho,J$ are $C^\\infty$ with compact support, hence $C_c^\\infty(\\mathbb R^3\\times\\mathbb R)$; clause (b) of [[lem-em-retarded-wave-kernel]] applied to $h=\\rho/\\varepsilon_0$ and componentwise to $h=\\mu_0J_k$ states that $(K*h)(x,t)=\\int h(y,t-|x-y|/c)/(4\\pi|x-y|)dy$ is $C^\\infty$ on $\\mathbb R^3\\times\\mathbb R$ and satisfies $W(K*h)=h$ pointwise, which is exactly the display. Note the identification $\\varphi=\\varepsilon_0^{-1}K*\\rho$, $A=\\mu_0K*J$ is the framework's form of the adopted retarded selection of [[post-em-radiation-selection]]; the selected branch is the object being computed, not assumed to exist a priori. (b) Differentiate the explicit retarded integral. In the substitution $y'=x-y$, which leaves the integral unchanged by translation invariance of Lebesgue measure ([[thm-lebesgue-outer-measure-and-measurability-are-translation-invariant]]), the kernel $1/(4\\pi|y'|)$ is independent of $x$, so differentiating under the integral sign in $x$ (direct dominated difference quotients: on each compact (x,t) parameter neighborhood all derivatives of h(x-y',t-|y'|/c) vanish outside one bounded y'-ball and are bounded by their appropriate derivative suprema; each quotient is dominated by that constant times |y'|^-1, integrable by [[thm-polar-coordinates-formula-for-lebesgue-measure]], so [[thm-dominated-convergence]] gives each derivative identity. The smooth nonsingular [[lem-em-parameter-integrals]] is used separately for the charge integral, not at this pole) gives $\\partial_{x^i}(K*h)=K*(\\partial_{y^i}h)$; differentiating in $t$ gives $\\partial_t(K*h)=K*(\\partial_th)$. Therefore $\\operatorname{div}A=\\mu_0K*(\\operatorname{div}J)$ and $c^{-2}\\partial_t\\varphi=c^{-2}\\varepsilon_0^{-1}K*(\\partial_t\\rho)=\\mu_0K*(\\partial_t\\rho)$ because $c^{-2}\\varepsilon_0^{-1}=\\mu_0c^2\\varepsilon_0\\cdot\\varepsilon_0^{-1}c^{-2}$ reduces to $\\mu_0$ (equivalently $\\mu_0c^2\\varepsilon_0=1$, [[def-em-si-conventions]]). Adding, $G=\\mu_0K*(\\partial_t\\rho+\\operatorname{div}J)=0$ by the assumed continuity. (c) $\\varphi,A$ are $C^\\infty$, hence $C^2$, and clause (a) of [[pthm-em-lorenz-gauge-wave-form]] (instantiated at $\\Omega=\\mathbb R^3$, $I=\\mathbb R$) states the exact identities $\\operatorname{div}E=W\\varphi-\\partial_tG$ and $\\nabla\\times B-c^{-2}\\partial_tE=WA+\\nabla G$; with (a) and (b) these read $\\operatorname{div}E=\\rho/\\varepsilon_0$ and $\\nabla\\times B-c^{-2}\\partial_tE=\\mu_0J$. The two source-free equations $\\operatorname{div}B=0$ and $\\nabla\\times E+\\partial_tB=0$ are automatic for a potential pair by the curl-divergence and curl-gradient cancellation recorded in clause (c) of the same item and [[def-em-potential-gauge-and-field-conventions]]. This is the smooth branch of [[post-em-vacuum-maxwell]]. (d) If $t<t_0$ then for every $y$ the retarded argument satisfies $t-|x-y|/c\\le t<t_0$, where $\\rho$ and $J$ vanish; both integrands vanish identically, so $\\varphi(x,t)=A(x,t)=0$ and hence $E=B=0$ at such events. (e) Fix $t_1<t_0$. By (d), $\\varphi(\\cdot,t_1)=0$ and $\\partial_t\\varphi(\\cdot,t_1)=0$, and likewise for $A$; by (a) the pair is $C^\\infty$ on $\\mathbb R^3\\times[t_1,\\infty)$ and solves the sourced wave equations there. Clause (b) of [[thm-em-wave-cauchy-kirchhoff]] (uniqueness for $C^2$ extension solutions of the Cauchy problem with these data) identifies the pair with its zero-data solution; clause (d) of the same theorem gives the corresponding finite-speed support, consistent with (d). (f) $\\int_{\\mathbb R^3}\\partial_t\\rho(y,t)dy=-\\int_{\\mathbb R^3}\\operatorname{div}J(y,t)dy=0$: for a ball $B_R$ with $R>a$ the divergence theorem ([[thm-divergence-theorem-for-bounded-c-one-euclidean-domains]]) converts the integral of $\\operatorname{div}J$ into a boundary flux where $J=0$, and differentiation under the integral sign is licensed by compact support ([[lem-em-parameter-integrals]]); hence $Q$ is constant, and $Q(t)=0$ for $t<t_0$ by (d), so $Q\\equiv0$. (g) records the branch boundaries. No self-force, no product of distributions and no empirical premise is used; the only choice assumption is $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$, inherited from the kernel and Cauchy suppliers through the surface-measure and convergence interfaces cited inside them.",
          "physical_scope": "Retarded potentials and fields of a prescribed smooth conserved source of compact spatial support in a compact time interval, on the whole laboratory spacetime in the framework's inertial chart: Lorenz gauge, the smooth vacuum Maxwell equations, zero field before the source acts, the zero-data Cauchy identification and zero total charge. Excluded: point, line, sheet or non-integrable sources; weak/distributional branches; eternal isolated charges; finite-energy, decay or boundary claims; self-force and radiation reaction; and every empirical or measurement claim.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
