            "thm-divergence-theorem-for-bounded-c-one-euclidean-domains": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-cross-product-is-bilinear-alternating-and-orthogonal": "mathematical-premise",
            "prop-order-and-scalar-rules-for-the-nonnegative-integral": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-cauchy-schwarz-finite": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-euclidean-inner-product": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume the setting and hypotheses of [[thm-em-radiation-asymptotic-flux]] and $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ as carried by its suppliers: $c>0$, $\\mu_0>0$, $a>0$, $t_0<T$, jointly $C^\\infty$ fields $\\rho,J$ vanishing outside $\\overline B_a(0)\\times[t_0,T]$ and satisfying $\\partial_t\\rho+\\operatorname{div}J=0$; let $\\varphi,A$ be the retarded potentials and $E:=-\\nabla\\varphi-\\partial_tA$, $B:=\\nabla\\times A$ the fields, with $S:=E\\times B/\\mu_0$ ([[def-em-vacuum-energy-flux]], [[pthm-em-poynting-balance]]). Adopt the causal selection [[post-em-radiation-selection]]: these retarded fields are the fields of the source model (the compact smooth instance established by [[pthm-em-retarded-potentials]]). Define the **time-dependent electric dipole moment** $$p(u):=\\int_{B_a}y\\,\\rho(y,u)\\,dy\\in\\mathbb R^3$$ (componentwise, about the fixed chart origin of [[def-em-lab-geometry]]; it is the fixed-time analogue of the static source moment of [[def-em-electric-moments]]), and, as in the asymptotic theorem, $I(n,u):=\\int_{B_a}J(y,u+n\\cdot y/c)\\,dy$, $V(n,u):=\\partial_uI(n,u)=\\int_{B_a}J_t(y,u+n\\cdot y/c)\\,dy$ and $$D(u):=\\frac{a}{c}\\int_{B_a}\\sup_{|v-u|\\le a/c}|J_{tt}(y,v)|\\,dy.$$ Then: (a) [Moment identities] $p\\in C^\\infty(\\mathbb R;\\mathbb R^3)$, $p'(u)=\\int_{B_a}J(y,u)\\,dy$, $p''(u)=\\int_{B_a}J_t(y,u)\\,dy$, $\\int_{B_a}\\rho_t(y,u)\\,dy=0$ and the total charge $\\int_{B_a}\\rho(y,u)\\,dy$ vanishes for every $u$. (b) [Dipole replacement error] $|V(n,u)-p''(u)|\\le D(u)$ for every $n\\in S^2$ and every $u\\in[t_0,T]$: the explicit absolute error of the dipole approximation to the source's transverse current moment. (c) [Leading fields] With $\\Gamma_E$, $\\Gamma_B$ the constants of [[thm-em-radiation-asymptotic-flux]](b) (depending only on $a,c,\\mu_0$ and the listed source suprema), for every $n\\in S^2$, $u\\in[t_0,T]$, $r\\ge2a$: $$\\Bigl|E\\bigl(rn,u+\\tfrac rc\\bigr)-\\frac{\\mu_0}{4\\pi r}n\\times(n\\times p''(u))\\Bigr|\\le\\frac{\\Gamma_E}{r^2}+\\frac{\\mu_0D(u)}{4\\pi r},\\qquad \\Bigl|B\\bigl(rn,u+\\tfrac rc\\bigr)-\\frac{n\\times E(rn,u+\\tfrac rc)}{c}\\Bigr|\\le\\frac{\\Gamma_B+\\Gamma_E/c}{r^2}.$$ The displayed dipole field approximates the actual leading far field $E_{\\rm lead}=\\mu_0n\\times(n\\times V)/(4\\pi r)$ with the stated absolute $D(u)/r$ error. Equality of these leading fields requires $n\\times(n\\times(V-p''))=0$; $V=p''$ and, in particular, $D(u)=0$ are sufficient. All errors are uniform in $n$ at fixed $u$. (d) [Retarded-time radiated power] The limit of [[thm-em-radiation-asymptotic-flux]](c) equals $\\mu_0|p''(u)|^2/(6\\pi c)+R(u)$ with the explicit absolute error $$|R(u)|\\le\\frac{\\mu_0\\bigl(2|p''(u)|D(u)+D(u)^2\\bigr)}{4\\pi c},\\qquad\\text{so}\\qquad \\lim_{r\\to\\infty}\\int_{S^2}r^2n\\cdot S\\bigl(rn,u+\\tfrac rc\\bigr)d\\sigma=\\frac{\\mu_0}{6\\pi c}|p''(u)|^2\\ \\text{ whenever } D(u)=0.$$ The evaluation uses the sphere moment $\\int_{S^2}|n\\times p''|^2d\\sigma=(8\\pi/3)|p''|^2$ of [[lem-em-sphere-zonal-moments]](d). The limit is at fixed retarded time $u$, not at fixed observation time. (e) [Scope] The compact smooth source branch only; the dipole error is absolute and explicitly controlled by $D(u)$, and no assertion is made that slow or 'nonrelativistic' source motion alone makes $D(u)$ small -- that is a hypothesis on the source's time variation. No point charge, no moving point source, no radiation reaction, no self-force and no empirical or measurement content; the failure of the correspondence with an oscillator for rapidly varying sources is retained through $D(u)$. Separately retain the sharper actual source estimate $|B(rn,u+r/c)-n\\times E_{\\rm lead}(n,u,r)/c|\\le\\Gamma_B/r^2$, with $E_{\\rm lead}=\\mu_0n\\times(n\\times V)/(4\\pi r)$; the bound against the actual E uses the combined constant displayed in (c).",
          "strategy": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ as carried by [[thm-em-radiation-asymptotic-flux]]. (a) $\\rho$ is $C^\\infty$ with compact support, so $u\\mapsto p(u)$ is $C^\\infty$ by differentiation under the integral sign ([[lem-em-parameter-integrals]]) and $p'(u)=\\int y\\,\\rho_t(y,u)dy$; integrating by parts componentwise over a ball containing the support via the divergence theorem ([[thm-divergence-theorem-for-bounded-c-one-euclidean-domains]], boundary term zero by compact support) gives $\\int y_i\\partial_t\\rho\\,dy=-\\int y_i\\operatorname{div}J\\,dy=\\int J_i\\,dy$, since $\\partial_i(y_iJ_k)$ contributes $J_i$ and the remaining divergence term integrates to zero. Replacing $J$ by $J_t$ (equivalently differentiating in $u$ under the integral sign) gives $p''=\\int J_t$. The vanishing $\\int\\rho_t=0$ is the same divergence theorem with weight $1$ (equivalently clause (f) of [[pthm-em-retarded-potentials]]), and the total charge vanishes because $\\rho$ is supported in $t\\in[t_0,T]$. (b) For fixed $y\\in B_a$ the one-variable function $v\\mapsto J_t(y,v)$ is $C^1$ on the interval between $u$ and $u+n\\cdot y/c$, whose length is at most $a/c$; for nonzero vector difference w choose its fixed unit direction e=w/|w| and apply the scalar mean value theorem ([[cor-mean-value-theorem]]) to e dot J_t; finite Euclidean Cauchy-Schwarz bounds |e dot J_tt| by |J_tt| (the zero difference is immediate), giving $|J_t(y,u+n\\cdot y/c)-J_t(y,u)|\\le(a/c)\\sup_{|v-u|\\le a/c}|J_{tt}(y,v)|$ componentwise, and integrating over $B_a$ with the integral triangle inequality and monotonicity ([[thm-integral-triangle-inequality]], [[prop-order-and-scalar-rules-for-the-nonnegative-integral]]) gives (b). (c) Clause (b) of [[thm-em-radiation-asymptotic-flux]] writes $E(rn,u+r/c)=E_{\\mathrm{lead}}(n,u,r)+$ remainder with $E_{\\mathrm{lead}}=\\mu_0\\,n\\times(n\\times V(n,u))/(4\\pi r)$ and remainder $O(r^{-2})$ bounded by $\\Gamma_E r^{-2}$. Substituting $V=p''+(V-p'')$ and using $|n\\times(n\\times w)|\\le|w|$ ([[lem-cross-product-is-bilinear-alternating-and-orthogonal]]) gives the first bound; The supplier bounds B-n cross E_lead/c by Gamma_B/r² and E-E_lead by Gamma_E/r²; the triangle inequality therefore gives the displayed (Gamma_B+Gamma_E/c)/r² bound against the actual E. D=0 suffices for exact dipole power; no converse is inferred from an error bound. (d) By clause (c) of [[thm-em-radiation-asymptotic-flux]] the limit equals $\\mu_0/(16\\pi^2c)\\int_{S^2}|n\\times V|^2d\\sigma$. Replacing $V$ by $p''$ changes the integrand by at most $(2|p''|D+D^2)$ pointwise (expand $|n\\times V|^2-|n\\times p''|^2$ and use the bound (b), the linearity of the cross product and the integral triangle inequality), so the integral changes by at most $4\\pi(2|p''|D+D^2)$ and the limit by $\\mu_0(2|p''|D+D^2)/(4\\pi c)$. The exact dipole value uses $|n\\times p''|^2=|p''|^2-(n\\cdot p'')^2$ and clause (d) of [[lem-em-sphere-zonal-moments]]: $\\int_{S^2}|n\\times p''|^2d\\sigma=4\\pi|p''|^2-(4\\pi/3)|p''|^2=(8\\pi/3)|p''|^2$, and $\\mu_0/(16\\pi^2c)\\cdot(8\\pi/3)=\\mu_0/(6\\pi c)$. (e) records that the error coefficient $D(u)$ constrains the source's own time variation and that the limit is a fixed-retarded-time limit, as in the supplier; no self-force, point-source, decay or empirical claim is added.",
          "physical_scope": "Far-zone electric-dipole radiation of a prescribed smooth conserved source of compact spatial support and compact time support: the dipole moment identities, the explicit absolute dipole-replacement error $D(u)$, the uniform leading far fields and the retarded-time radiated power with its absolute error. Excluded: point charges; sources without the compact smooth branch; claims that slowness alone controls $D(u)$; observation-time power and signal-speed readings; self-force, radiation reaction and every empirical or measurement claim.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
