            "thm-em-retarded-point-distributional-maxwell",
            "post-em-distributional-vacuum-maxwell",
            "pthm-em-poynting-balance"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-em-retarded-point-geometry": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "pthm-em-retarded-potentials": "physical-result",
            "lem-em-point-retarded-potential-and-fields": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-em-retarded-root-and-fields": "mathematical-premise",
            "post-em-radiation-selection": "physical-assumption",
            "def-em-weak-sources": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-em-potential-gauge-and-field-conventions": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-em-fields": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-em-sources": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-em-relativistic-worldlines-frames": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-em-lab-geometry": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-em-si-conventions": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-euclidean-inner-product": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-em-retarded-point-distributional-maxwell": "mathematical-premise",
            "post-em-distributional-vacuum-maxwell": "physical-assumption",
            "pthm-em-poynting-balance": "physical-result"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ($\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$) as carried by the point-source change-of-variables suppliers below ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let the laboratory region, chart and units be those of [[def-em-lab-geometry]] and [[def-em-si-conventions]] ($c>0$, $\\mu_0>0$, $\\varepsilon_0=(\\mu_0c^2)^{-1}$), let $q\\in\\mathbb R$ and let $z$, $v_*$ be a retarded point-geometry datum of [[def-em-retarded-point-geometry]] (a prescribed $C^3$ uniformly subluminal worldline of a point charge, [[def-em-relativistic-worldlines-frames]], with the constant $C:=q/(4\\pi\\varepsilon_0)$), write $\\Omega:=\\mathbb R^3\\times\\mathbb R$ and $\\Gamma:=\\{(z(s),s):s\\in\\mathbb R\\}$, and let $\\rho,J$ be the point-source distributions of that charge on the worldline in the declared point-source class of [[def-em-weak-sources]](b) (the $C^3$ branch of the point-current construction). Let $(\\varphi,A)$ be the retarded history pairings of [[lem-em-point-retarded-potential-and-fields]](b) -- the framework's retarded construction for this source under the adopted selection [[post-em-radiation-selection]] -- and define $E:=-\\nabla\\varphi-\\partial_tA$, $B:=\\nabla\\times A$ on the off-worldline domain $\\Omega\\setminus\\Gamma$ ([[def-em-potential-gauge-and-field-conventions]], [[def-em-fields]]). Then: (a) [Potentials] $\\varphi=C/(\\kappa r)$ and $A=\\beta\\varphi/c$ on $\\Omega\\setminus\\Gamma$, where $r,\\kappa,\\beta$ are the retarded data of [[def-em-retarded-point-geometry]](b); the zero extensions of $\\varphi,A$ to $\\Gamma$ are locally integrable on $\\Omega$. (b) [Exact fields] On $\\Omega\\setminus\\Gamma$, $$E=E_{\\mathrm{vel}}+E_{\\mathrm{acc}},\\qquad E_{\\mathrm{vel}}=\\frac{C(1-|\\beta|^2)(n-\\beta)}{\\kappa^3r^2},\\qquad E_{\\mathrm{acc}}=\\frac{C\\,n\\times\\bigl((n-\\beta)\\times\\dot\\beta\\bigr)}{c\\,\\kappa^3r},\\qquad B=\\frac{n\\times E}{c},$$ and $E,B$ are of class $C^1$ there; the velocity part obeys $|E_{\\mathrm{vel}}|\\le|C|(1+v_*/c)(1-v_*/c)^{-3}r^{-2}$. (c) [Uniform far-zone remainder] For every emission event $s_0$ and direction $n\\in S^2$, with $x_r:=z(s_0)+rn$, $t_r:=s_0+r/c$, $\\beta_0:=z'(s_0)/c$, $\\dot\\beta_0:=z''(s_0)/c$ and $\\kappa_0:=1-n\\cdot\\beta_0$: $(x_r,t_r)\\in\\Omega\\setminus\\Gamma$, $s(x_r,t_r)=s_0$, and $$E(x_r,t_r)=\\frac{C\\,n\\times\\bigl((n-\\beta_0)\\times\\dot\\beta_0\\bigr)}{c\\,\\kappa_0^3\\,r}+\\rho_E(s_0,n,r),\\qquad|\\rho_E(s_0,n,r)|\\le|C|\\frac{1+v_*/c}{(1-v_*/c)^3}\\,r^{-2},\\qquad B(x_r,t_r)=\\frac{n\\times E(x_r,t_r)}{c};$$ the bound is uniform in $n$ at fixed $s_0$. (d) [Scope] These are the stipulated retarded model fields of the prescribed charge: the item identifies, through the same adopted causal selection used by [[pthm-em-retarded-potentials]] for the compact branch, the point-source potentials and fields of the model, and proves their exact form and bounds. It asserts no value of the fields on the worldline $\\Gamma$ (where the formulas are undefined and the self-field is singular), no integral or energy statement, no self-force and no radiation reaction, and derives no mass. The uniform bound $v_*<c$ and the exclusion of $\\Gamma$ are essential hypotheses; the companion example page shows that a merely pointwise subluminal curve can fail to have a retarded root, and no uniformity in the emission event $s_0$ is claimed ($z''$ is not assumed bounded). The signed constant $C$ is retained in every displayed formula while absolute-value bounds use $|C|$. (e) [Constructed weak solution] Let $\\Phi,\\Upsilon$ be the global regular potential distributions in (a), and let $\\mathcal E=-\\nabla\\Phi-\\partial_t\\Upsilon$, $\\mathcal B=\\operatorname{curl}\\Upsilon$. By [[thm-em-retarded-point-distributional-maxwell]], their representatives are exactly the locally integrable zero extensions of the displayed off-worldline fields. They satisfy all four identities of [[def-em-weak-sources]](e) with the proper all-time point pair $\\rho,J$; the volume source parts are zero. Thus they are an admitted point-source model of the explicit physical adoption [[post-em-distributional-vacuum-maxwell]], under the same retarded selection. The potentials satisfy $W\\Phi=\\rho/\\varepsilon_0$, $W\\Upsilon=\\mu_0J$ and the distributional Lorenz identity. This existence and solution property is supplied by the mathematical theorem, not by the selection postulate or by the compact-source theorem. The zero extensions on the null graph give no physically defined self-field and no nonlinear products there. All original exact field, regularity and uniform far-zone branches remain as stated. On each product neighborhood disjoint from $\\Gamma$ the fields satisfy the smooth source-free Maxwell equations. Consequently any use of [[pthm-em-poynting-balance]] by the radiation items is local on such neighborhoods, with $\\rho=J=0$; it neither applies that smooth theorem across the point source nor forms self-work or a global finite-energy identity.",
          "strategy": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$. The mathematical content is fully supplied by the two cited point-source suppliers, and the physical work of this item is the honest identification and the scope statement. (a) Clause (b) of [[lem-em-point-retarded-potential-and-fields]] identifies the history pairings with the regular distributions of the locally integrable zero extensions of $\\varphi=C/(\\kappa r)$ and $A=\\beta\\varphi/c$ on $\\Omega\\setminus\\Gamma$, and proves finiteness of the pairings for every test and the exact change-of-variables identity with denominator $1-n\\cdot\\beta$. The retarded root and its derivative formulas, and the identification of the same formulas with the $C^3$ branch, are clause (a) of [[thm-em-retarded-root-and-fields]], which also supplies (b) and (c) there: the velocity/acceleration split, $B=n\\times E/c$, the $C^1$ regularity and the velocity bound. (c) is clause (d) of the same theorem, whose remainder is $E_{\\mathrm{vel}}$ evaluated at the emission event with the bound obtained from $1-|\\beta|^2\\le1$, $|n-\\beta|\\le1+v_*/c$ and $\\kappa^3\\ge(1-v_*/c)^3$; the root identification $s(x_r,t_r)=s_0$ is its uniqueness statement. (d) is the physical reading: the retarded construction is the one selected by [[post-em-radiation-selection]], so the model's point-charge fields off $\\Gamma$ are exactly these; the new exact [[thm-em-retarded-point-distributional-maxwell]] separately proves the sourced wave identities, Lorenz condition, all four distributional Maxwell identities and L1loc field representatives. The graph is proper by its time coordinate, so [[def-em-weak-sources]](b),(d),(e) admits precisely this point source and field pair. Under [[post-em-distributional-vacuum-maxwell]] and the explicitly extended retarded selection, these constructed weak fields are the model fields. This supplies the solution property without applying the compact-only theorem to an eternal point source. No self-force, mass derivation, radiation reaction or empirical claim appears. The choice assumption $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ is inherited from the change-of-variables and sphere-integration suppliers cited inside the two point-source items.",
          "physical_scope": "Retarded potentials and fields of a prescribed point charge with charge parameter $q\\in\\mathbb R$ on a uniformly subluminal $C^3$ worldline, off the worldline: exact Lienard-Wiechert split, $B=n\\times E/c$, the velocity-field bound and the uniform-in-direction far-zone remainder at a fixed emission event; and the constructed proper point-source weak Maxwell solution with $L^1_{\\mathrm{loc}}$ field representatives and distributional Lorenz-gauge potentials. Excluded: field values on the worldline and any nonlinear self-interaction (no products of distributions, no self-force, no radiation reaction); energy, flux or power (deferred to the emitted-power items of this page); uniform bounds in the emission event; and every empirical or measurement claim.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "David Tong, Electromagnetism, University of Cambridge Part II Mathematical Tripos lecture notes (author-hosted 236-page PDF, title page dated Lent Term 2015)",
