          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Let $E,B$ be jointly $C^k$ fields of [[def-em-fields]] on the laboratory region $U\\cong I\\times\\Omega$ of an inertial chart $x$ of the framework ([[def-em-lab-geometry]]), $k\\ge1$, with the SI units of [[def-em-si-conventions]], and let $F$ be the electromagnetic two-form of [[def-em-electromagnetic-tensor]] with its fixed components $F_{0i}=-E_i/c$, $F_{ij}=\\epsilon_{ijk}B_k$, $F^{0i}=E_i/c$, $F^{ij}=\\epsilon_{ijk}B_k$. Let $0\\le\\beta<1$, $\\gamma:=(1-\\beta^2)^{-1/2}$, $v:=\\beta c\\,e_1$, and let $\\Lambda_\\beta$ be the explicit boost of [[lem-em-boost-preserves-metric]] with $\\Lambda_\\beta{}^0{}_0=\\Lambda_\\beta{}^1{}_1=\\gamma$, $\\Lambda_\\beta{}^0{}_1=\\Lambda_\\beta{}^1{}_0=-\\gamma\\beta$, $\\Lambda_\\beta{}^2{}_2=\\Lambda_\\beta{}^3{}_3=1$ and all other entries zero. Let $x'=\\Lambda_\\beta x+b$ be the corresponding inertial chart, and for every event $p$ in the overlap of the two chart restrictions define the primed field components by reading the components of the same $F$ in $x'$ through the dictionary of [[def-em-electromagnetic-tensor]], so that $F'_{0i}=-E'_i/c$, $F'_{ij}=\\epsilon_{ijk}B'_k$ at $p$. Then: (a) [Boosted fields] at every such $p$, with $\\parallel$ and $\\perp$ the components along and orthogonal to $e_1$ in the spatial Euclidean structure of the chart, $$E'_1=E_1,\\quad B'_1=B_1,\\qquad E'_\\parallel=E_\\parallel,\\quad B'_\\parallel=B_\\parallel,\\qquad E'_\\perp=\\gamma\\,(E+v\\times B)_\\perp,\\qquad B'_\\perp=\\gamma\\,(B-v\\times E/c^2)_\\perp,$$ equivalently, componentwise, $E'_2=\\gamma(E_2-\\beta cB_3)$, $E'_3=\\gamma(E_3+\\beta cB_2)$, $B'_2=\\gamma(B_2+\\beta E_3/c)$, $B'_3=\\gamma(B_3-\\beta E_2/c)$. (a′) [Arbitrary boost direction] For a velocity vector $v\\in\\mathbb R^3$ with $|v|<c$, use the actual vector boost $B(v/c)$ of [[def-lorentz-boost]], with $\\gamma_v=(1-|v|^2/c^2)^{-1/2}$. If $v\\ne0$, decompose the fields along $\\widehat v=v/|v|$ and its orthogonal complement. Then $E'_\\parallel=E_\\parallel$, $B'_\\parallel=B_\\parallel$, $E'_\\perp=\\gamma_v(E+v\\times B)_\\perp$ and $B'_\\perp=\\gamma_v(B-v\\times E/c^2)_\\perp$. Equivalently, for every $v$, including $v=0$, $$E'=\\gamma_v(E+v\\times B)-\\frac{\\gamma_v^2}{\\gamma_v+1}\\frac{v(v\\cdot E)}{c^2},\\qquad B'=\\gamma_v(B-v\\times E/c^2)-\\frac{\\gamma_v^2}{\\gamma_v+1}\\frac{v(v\\cdot B)}{c^2}.$$ At $v=0$ these are the identity and no preferred parallel direction is assigned.  (b) [Invariants] at every such $p$, $$|B'|^2-\\frac{|E'|^2}{c^2}=|B|^2-\\frac{|E|^2}{c^2},\\qquad E'\\cdot B'=E\\cdot B;$$ equivalently the scalar fields $I_1:=\\tfrac12F_{ab}F^{ab}=|B|^2-|E|^2/c^2$ and $I_2:=F_{ab}(*F)^{ab}=4\\,E\\cdot B/c$ of [[def-em-electromagnetic-tensor]] (b) take the same values whether computed from the components in $x$ or in $x'$. (c) [General proper orthochronous changes] for any proper orthochronous Lorentz matrix $\\Lambda$ with chart $x'=\\Lambda x+b$, the primed components of $F$ are given by the component law of [[thm-sr-tensor-and-current-transformation]] (iii), $F'^{ab}=\\Lambda^a{}_c\\Lambda^b{}_dF^{cd}$; in particular, if $\\Lambda=\\widehat R$ is the extension of a spatial rotation $R$ of the frame ([[def-spatial-rotation-of-an-inertial-frame]]), then $E'=RE$ and $B'=RB$, and by the unique factorization $\\Lambda=B(-\\beta)\\widehat R$ of [[thm-sr-proper-orthochronous-lorentz-algebra]] (iii) every proper orthochronous change acts first by $(E,B)\\mapsto(RE,RB)$ and then by the arbitrary-direction boost law (a′) with velocity $-c\\beta$, where $\\beta$ is the vector parameter of that factorization. The axis-only law (a) is not substituted for a general vector boost. (d) [Form invariance of the Maxwell branch] if $(E,B,\\rho,J)$ satisfy the smooth branch of [[post-em-vacuum-maxwell]] in $x$ on the overlap, and $(\\rho',J')$ are the components of the same four-current in $x'$, then $(E',B',\\rho',J')$ satisfy the same four equations in $x'$, by [[pthm-em-tensor-maxwell-equivalence]]. (e) [Scope] All clauses are pointwise on the overlap $U\\cap U'$ of the two chart restrictions, are conditional on the adopted postulates, and concern the smooth classical flat branch; no accelerating coordinates, curved spacetime, material medium, apparatus or empirical claim is involved; the transformation is exact algebra, and the primed component functions are $C^k$ wherever the overlap is open. The invariants clause uses only the proper orthochronous changes of description adopted in [[post-sr-inertial-covariance]]; orientation-reversing changes are outside the framework's field conventions ([[def-em-fields]]).",
          "strategy": "**Proof technique:** component computation from the transformation law, then the scalar contractions. (a) Apply $F'^{ab}=\\Lambda^a{}_c\\Lambda^b{}_dF^{cd}$ ([[thm-sr-tensor-and-current-transformation]] (iii); $\\Lambda_\\beta$ is a proper orthochronous Lorentz map by [[lem-em-boost-preserves-metric]]) to the raised components: $F'^{01}=\\Lambda^0{}_0\\Lambda^1{}_1F^{01}+\\Lambda^0{}_1\\Lambda^1{}_0F^{10}=\\gamma^2(1-\\beta^2)F^{01}=F^{01}$, $F'^{02}=\\gamma(E_2/c-\\beta B_3)$, $F'^{03}=\\gamma(E_3/c+\\beta B_2)$, $F'^{12}=\\gamma(B_3-\\beta E_2/c)$, $F'^{13}=\\gamma(-B_2-\\beta E_3/c)$, $F'^{23}=F^{23}$. Reading $E'_i=cF'^{0i}$ and $B'_k$ from the appropriate cyclic entries through the dictionary gives the displayed components; the vector form evaluates $v\\times B$ and $v\\times E$ from [[def-cross-product-in-r3]]. (a′) For $v\\ne0$ put $u=v/|v|$. Choose a coordinate vector $e_j$ not parallel to $u$, set $a=(e_j-(e_j\\cdot u)u)/|e_j-(e_j\\cdot u)u|$ and $b=u\\times a$. Direct cross-product coordinates show $(u,a,b)$ is an oriented orthonormal basis. Let $R$ have these vectors as rows, so $Ru=e_1$, $R^{\\mathsf T}R=I$ and $\\det R=1$; only one finite choice is used. Substituting the matrix of [[def-lorentz-boost]] gives $B(v/c)=\\widehat R^{-1}\\Lambda_{|v|/c}\\widehat R$. Apply the rotation component law proved in (c), then the axis computation (a), then rotate back. The determinant-one cofactor identity gives $R(p\\times q)=(Rp)\\times(Rq)$, yielding the parallel/perpendicular formulas. Use $\\gamma_v-1=\\gamma_v^2|v|^2/(c^2(\\gamma_v+1))$ to combine the pieces into the displayed nonsingular vector formulas; at zero the separately defined boost is the identity.  (b) The two expressions are the two independent scalar contractions of the two-form; substituting the component law into $\\tfrac12F_{ab}F^{ab}$ and $F_{ab}(*F)^{ab}$ with $\\eta'=\\eta$ shows invariance, equivalently clauses (c) of [[thm-sr-antisymmetric-observer-decomposition]], and [[def-em-electromagnetic-tensor]] (b) identifies them with $|B|^2-|E|^2/c^2$ and $4E\\cdot B/c$. (c) For the rotation case $\\Lambda^0{}_0=1$, $\\Lambda^0{}_j=\\Lambda^i{}_0=0$, $\\Lambda^i{}_j=R^i{}_j$ give $F'^{0i}=R^i{}_jF^{0j}$ and $F'^{ij}=R^i{}_kR^j{}_lF^{kl}$; reading the dictionary and using $\\det R=1$ in the cofactor identity $\\epsilon_{nij}R^i{}_kR^j{}_lR^n{}_m=\\epsilon_{klm}$ ([[def-determinant-of-a-linear-operator]], [[def-spatial-rotation-of-an-inertial-frame]]) gives $E'=RE$, $B'=RB$. The general case is the actual unique factorization $\\Lambda=B(-\\beta)\\widehat R$ of [[thm-sr-proper-orthochronous-lorentz-algebra]] (iii). Since components transform by multiplication with $\\Lambda$, first apply $\\widehat R$ and then $B(-\\beta)$; the latter uses (a′) with vector velocity $-c\\beta$, not the nonnegative axis parameter of (a). (d) Chain clauses (a)-(c) with [[pthm-em-tensor-maxwell-equivalence]]: clause (a) of that theorem in both charts plus its clause (b) for the pair of descriptions. No potential, no second derivative of the fields, no choice principle and no empirical premise are used.",
          "physical_scope": "Conditional statement on the smooth branch of the framework's Maxwell fields in one inertial chart: the exact passive-boost component formulas for $E,B$ along one spatial axis and in every vector direction (including the zero boost), invariance of $B^2-E^2/c^2$ and $E\\cdot B$ under every proper orthochronous change of inertial description, the rotation and general-factorization laws, and form-invariance of the four Maxwell equations. Excluded: accelerating coordinates, curved spacetime, media, weak or singular fields, orientation-reversing changes, apparatus and any measurement or empirical claim.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "David Tong, Electromagnetism, University of Cambridge Part II Mathematical Tripos lecture notes (2026 author-hosted revision, 236 pp.)",
                "url": "https://davidtong.org/pdfs/teaching/electromagnetism/electro.pdf",
                "locator": "§5.3.2 printed pp. 106-108 (the transformation of $E,B$ under a boost, eqs. (5.16)-(5.18), and the rotation embedding (5.4)) and §5.3.5 printed pp. 111-113 (the two Lorentz scalars (5.23) and (5.25)), read in the full extracted text; signs converted from the source's $(+---)$ dictionary"
              },
