      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "ex-em-stationary-not-minimum",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "Stationary functional need not be a minimum",
          "reference": "worked-example-verifications.md#X8",
          "design_state": "complete-exact-conditional-research-argument",
          "deps": [
            "post-em-stationary-action-model",
            "def-em-field-action-definition",
            "lem-em-compact-field-variation",
            "def-em-lab-geometry",
            "def-em-electromagnetic-tensor",
            "def-em-si-conventions",
            "lem-test-function-cutoffs-and-euclidean-localization",
            "thm-algebra-of-derivatives",
            "thm-chain-rule",
            "thm-newton-leibniz-with-interior-derivative",
            "thm-fubini-theorem-for-l-one-on-sigma-finite-product-spaces",
            "thm-linearity-of-the-lebesgue-integral-on-l-one",
            "thm-substitution",
            "lem-riemann-lebesgue-comparison-for-distribution-test-integrands",
            "prop-order-and-scalar-rules-for-the-nonnegative-integral",
            "lem-em-continuous-localization",
            "cor-archimedean-reciprocal",
            "def-integral-over-a-measurable-set",
            "def-ck-euclidean-maps-and-diffeomorphisms",
            "def-fixed-support-test-function-frechet-space",
            "def-test-function-topology",
            "def-countable-choice",
            "thm-heine-borel-rn"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "post-em-stationary-action-model": "physical-assumption",
            "def-em-field-action-definition": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "lem-em-compact-field-variation": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-em-lab-geometry": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-em-electromagnetic-tensor": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-em-si-conventions": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "lem-test-function-cutoffs-and-euclidean-localization": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-algebra-of-derivatives": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-chain-rule": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-newton-leibniz-with-interior-derivative": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-fubini-theorem-for-l-one-on-sigma-finite-product-spaces": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-linearity-of-the-lebesgue-integral-on-l-one": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-substitution": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-riemann-lebesgue-comparison-for-distribution-test-integrands": "mathematical-premise",
            "prop-order-and-scalar-rules-for-the-nonnegative-integral": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-em-continuous-localization": "mathematical-premise",
            "cor-archimedean-reciprocal": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-integral-over-a-measurable-set": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-ck-euclidean-maps-and-diffeomorphisms": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-fixed-support-test-function-frechet-space": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-test-function-topology": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-heine-borel-rn": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "dependency_level": 16,
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice, inherited from the field-action measure suppliers ([[def-countable-choice]]); no additional choice is used. Work in [[def-em-field-action-definition]] with the coordinate box $U=(-1,1)^4$ lying compactly inside the chosen laboratory chart, constants $c,\\mu_0>0$, $\\varepsilon_0=(\\mu_0c^2)^{-1}$ ([[def-em-si-conventions]]) and $j=0$.\n\n(a) [Coordinate and physical forms] With $x^0=ct$, set $U_t:=\\{(t,x):(ct,x)\\in U\\}=(-1/c,1/c)\\times(-1,1)^3$. The exact field dictionary gives\n$$S[A]=\\frac{1}{2c\\mu_0}\\int_U(|E|^2/c^2-|B|^2)d\\lambda=\\frac12\\int_{U_t}(\\varepsilon_0|E|^2-|B|^2/\\mu_0)dt\\,d^3x.$$\nAlso $S[\\lambda A]=\\lambda^2S[A]$ for every real $\\lambda$.\n\n(b) [Stationarity] $A=0$ is stationary: the actual first-variation coefficient of [[lem-em-compact-field-variation]] is $-\\mu_0^{-1}F^{\\mu\\nu}\\partial_\\mu h_\\nu+j^\\nu h_\\nu$, and the action variation is $c^{-1}$ times its integral. Both terms vanish at $F=0,j=0$.\n\n(c) [Positive direction] Choose $\\theta\\in C_c^\\infty(U)$ with $\\nabla_x\\theta\\not\\equiv0$. Set the covariant components $h_0=\\theta,h_i=0$, equivalently the contravariant variation $h^0=-\\theta,h^i=0$. Then $E=c\\nabla_x\\theta$, $B=0$, and\n$$S[h]=\\frac{1}{2c\\mu_0}\\int_U|\\nabla_x\\theta|^2d\\lambda>0.$$\n\n(d) [Negative directions with a fixed compact support] Choose nonzero nonnegative smooth bumps $\\eta,\\varphi,\\psi_2,\\psi_3\\in C_c^\\infty((-1/2,1/2))$ using [[lem-test-function-cutoffs-and-euclidean-localization]]. Extend them by zero to $\\mathbb R$. For integers $N\\ge1$ define the contravariant variation with only its second spatial component nonzero:\n$$h^{(N)2}(x)=\\eta(x^0)\\varphi(Nx^1)\\psi_2(x^2)\\psi_3(x^3).$$\nAll supports lie in one fixed compact subset of $U$. Writing $f_N=h^{(N)2}$, its fields are $E=-c(\\partial_0f_N)e_2$ and $B=-(\\partial_3f_N)e_1+(\\partial_1f_N)e_3$. Define finite constants, with all one-dimensional integrals over $(-1,1)$,\n$$C_E=(\\int\\eta'^2)(\\int\\varphi^2)(\\int\\psi_2^2)(\\int\\psi_3^2),\\quad C_B=(\\int\\eta^2)(\\int\\varphi'^2)(\\int\\psi_2^2)(\\int\\psi_3^2)>0,$$\n$$C_3=(\\int\\eta^2)(\\int\\varphi^2)(\\int\\psi_2^2)(\\int\\psi_3'^2)\\ge0.$$\nExact substitution and Fubini give\n$$\\int_U|E|^2/c^2d\\lambda=C_E/N,\\qquad\\int_U|B|^2d\\lambda=C_BN+C_3/N,$$\n$$S[h^{(N)}]=\\frac{1}{2c\\mu_0}\\left(\\frac{C_E-C_3}{N}-C_BN\\right)\\longrightarrow-\\infty.$$\nThus a fixed sufficiently large $N$ supplies one negative direction $h_-$; the direction $h_+$ of (c) is positive. For nonzero $\\lambda$, their rescalings keep their respective signs, and each action tends to zero in absolute value as $\\lambda\\to0$. A single fixed negative direction is not claimed to change sign under rescaling.\n\n(e) [Every usual neighbourhood] Fix those two directions before rescaling. For each derivative multi-index, every compact-set supremum of a derivative of $\\lambda h_\\pm$ is $|\\lambda|$ times the finite supremum for that fixed smooth compactly supported direction. Thus both tend to zero in the usual $C^k$, smooth compact-convergence and fixed-support and LF test-function topologies ([[def-fixed-support-test-function-frechet-space]], [[def-test-function-topology]]) (and in any usual function-space topology with continuous scalar multiplication). Every such neighbourhood of zero therefore contains configurations of positive and negative action, arbitrarily small in magnitude. The stationary zero is neither a local minimum nor a local maximum. This is a computation in the declared smooth finite-region model, not a claim about actual fields or measurements; other sources or boundary/variation restrictions require their own analysis.",
          "strategy": "(a) Substitute $\\tfrac12F_{\\mu\\nu}F^{\\mu\\nu}=|B|^2-|E|^2/c^2$ from [[def-em-electromagnetic-tensor]] into the action. The coordinate change $x^0=ct$ has $d\\lambda=c\\,dt\\,d^3x$ and changes the time interval to $(-1/c,1/c)$, so the physical-time formula uses $U_t$, not the unscaled coordinate box. Linearity of $F$ and the quadratic functional give the scaling law. (b) uses the exact raised-field/lowered-test coefficient and the overall factor $c^{-1}$ of the definition; at zero it vanishes pointwise.\n\n(c) Direct differentiation gives the stated electric-only field. The continuous nonnegative integrand is positive on a small box because the spatial gradient is nonzero somewhere, so its integral is positive under the declared field-sector measure convention.\n\n(d) Derive the three displayed field components by the product/chain rules. Every selected bump is smooth with compact support strictly inside $(-1/2,1/2)$, so all $h^{(N)}$ share an interior compact support. The nonzero compact bump $\\varphi$ cannot have $\\varphi'\\equiv0$: FTC would make it constant on $\\mathbb R$, and compact support would then force zero. Thus the continuous square $\\varphi'^2$ is positive on an interval and has a positive integral; all undifferentiated bump-square integrals are likewise positive. For $N\\ge1$, [[thm-substitution]] with the affine map $y=Nx^1$ gives $\\int_{-1}^1\\varphi(Nx^1)^2dx^1=N^{-1}\\int_{-N}^N\\varphi(y)^2dy=N^{-1}\\int_{-1}^1\\varphi(y)^2dy$, and the same identity for $\\varphi'^2$. These are ordinary continuous compactly supported Riemann integrals; [[lem-riemann-lebesgue-comparison-for-distribution-test-integrands]] converts them to the action's Lebesgue integrals under the already-declared Countable Choice. [[thm-fubini-theorem-for-l-one-on-sigma-finite-product-spaces]] factors each smooth compact-support squared product. The time derivative supplies $C_E/N$; the $x^1$ derivative supplies $C_BN$, and the $x^3$ derivative supplies $C_3/N$. No endpoint touching the boundary and no false polynomial lower bound are used. Since $C_B>0$, choose one sufficiently large integer $N$ with negative action. Hold it fixed during rescaling.\n\n(e) Quadratic homogeneity keeps the positive and negative signs separately. On the common fixed compact support, the seminorms $p_m$ of [[def-fixed-support-test-function-frechet-space]] obey $p_m(\\lambda h)=|\\lambda|p_m(h)$. In the LF definition [[def-test-function-topology]], every seminorm similarly obeys $q(\\lambda h)=|\\lambda|q(h)$, and a zero neighbourhood contains finitely many such bounds, so the line also tends to zero there. Scaling each fixed compact direction makes every derivative seminorm tend to zero and makes its action magnitude tend to zero. Hence every stated usual neighbourhood contains both signs, proving the full non-extremum claim without a claim that scaling a negative direction creates a positive one. This local functional counterexample is not a source's numbered physical result or an empirical assertion.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "physical_scope": "Worked computation in the smooth finite-region field action with the box region and no source: the stationary configuration of the adopted model is a saddle of the indefinite quadratic functional, with explicit compact variations of both signs and arbitrarily small magnitude. Excluded: any claim about physical fields or measurements, minimality of the adopted action, and applicability beyond the declared region and functional.",
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "L. D. Landau and E. M. Lifshitz, The Classical Theory of Fields (Course of Theoretical Physics vol. 2, English text, 387 pp.)",
                "url": "http://www.elegio.it/mc2/LandauLifshitz_TheClassicalTheoryOfFields_text.pdf",
                "locator": "§27 printed pp. 68-69: the sign of $(\\partial A/\\partial t)^2$ is discussed through a minimum requirement for $S_f$; eqs. (27.4)-(27.6) on printed p. 69"
              },
              {
                "title": "David Tong, Electromagnetism (University of Cambridge Part II Mathematical Tripos), Chapter 5, §5.5.3",
                "url": "https://davidtong.org/pdfs/teaching/electromagnetism/electro4.pdf",
                "locator": "printed p. 125: expansion $S=\\int dtd^3x\\,(\\varepsilon_0E^2/2-B^2/(2\\mu_0))$ and the kinetic/potential reading"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "ex-em-compact-variation-example",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "A compact test variation and gauge-source sign check",
          "reference": "worked-example-verifications.md#X8",
          "design_state": "complete-exact-conditional-research-argument",
          "deps": [
            "def-em-field-action-definition",
            "lem-em-compact-field-variation",
            "pthm-em-action-gauge-source-compatibility",
            "pthm-em-action-maxwell-variation",
            "def-em-electromagnetic-tensor",
            "def-em-si-conventions",
            "def-em-sources",
            "lem-test-function-cutoffs-and-euclidean-localization",
            "thm-newton-leibniz-with-interior-derivative",
            "thm-fubini-theorem-for-l-one-on-sigma-finite-product-spaces",
