      "items": [
        {
          "id": "def-em-monochromatic-source-free-phasors",
          "kind": "definition",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "Frequency-$\\omega$ source-free vacuum phasor pairs and their real-field encoding",
          "reference": "scaffold-added necessary formulation prerequisite for the vector PEC scattering theorem (see research/physics-em-sr-40-2026-10-08-batch-40.notes.md)",
          "design_state": "new-local-definition-prerequisite; complete-definition-contract",
          "deps": [
            "def-em-si-conventions",
            "def-em-fields",
            "def-complex-exponential",
            "def-complex-conjugate-real-imaginary-part-and-modulus",
            "def-ck-euclidean-maps-and-diffeomorphisms",
            "def-divergence-and-curl-of-a-c1-vector-field",
            "def-em-complex-plane-wave"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-em-si-conventions": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-em-fields": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-complex-exponential": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-complex-conjugate-real-imaginary-part-and-modulus": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-ck-euclidean-maps-and-diffeomorphisms": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-divergence-and-curl-of-a-c1-vector-field": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-em-complex-plane-wave": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Let $\\omega>0$, let $D\\subseteq\\mathbb R^3$ be a nonempty open set, and let $c>0$, $\\mu_0>0$, $\\varepsilon_0=(\\mu_0c^2)^{-1}$ be the vacuum constants of [[def-em-si-conventions]]. (a) [Phasor encoding] For every pair of $C^\\infty$ maps $\\widetilde E,\\widetilde B:D\\to\\mathbb C^3$ ([[def-ck-euclidean-maps-and-diffeomorphisms]]) define the **associated real fields** $$E(x,t):=\\operatorname{Re}\\bigl(\\widetilde E(x)e^{-i\\omega t}\\bigr),\\qquad B(x,t):=\\operatorname{Re}\\bigl(\\widetilde B(x)e^{-i\\omega t}\\bigr)\\qquad((x,t)\\in D\\times\\mathbb R),$$ componentwise, with the complex exponential and real part of [[def-complex-exponential]] and [[def-complex-conjugate-real-imaginary-part-and-modulus]]; this is the encoding convention of [[def-em-complex-plane-wave]] specialized from plane-wave amplitudes to a general $C^\\infty$ amplitude, and the complex fields are not themselves physical fields. (b) [Source-free class] The pair $(\\widetilde E,\\widetilde B)$ is called a **frequency-$\\omega$ source-free vacuum phasor pair on $D$** when it is $C^\\infty$ and satisfies, on $D$, $$\\operatorname{div}\\widetilde E=0,\\qquad \\operatorname{div}\\widetilde B=0,\\qquad \\operatorname{curl}\\widetilde E=i\\omega\\widetilde B,\\qquad \\operatorname{curl}\\widetilde B=-i\\omega\\varepsilon_0\\mu_0\\widetilde E=-i\\omega c^{-2}\\widetilde E,$$ with the divergence and curl of [[def-divergence-and-curl-of-a-c1-vector-field]] applied componentwise to the complex fields. The word 'source-free' records that the displayed equations carry no charge or current term; the associated real fields are read as an electric and a magnetic field of [[def-em-fields]], $\\omega$ is the angular frequency and $T:=2\\pi/\\omega$ the period. (c) [Status and scope] This item fixes the encoding, the four phasor equations and the terminology only. It asserts no equation for the associated real fields, no outgoing or boundary condition, no existence or uniqueness statement, no energy or flux reading and no empirical content. In particular the deduction that the associated real fields satisfy the smooth-branch vacuum Maxwell equations with zero sources is not part of this definition; for the pairs used on this page it is established by the exterior-scattering theorem recorded later on this page. Only $C^\\infty$ pairs on an open set are defined, so no boundary trace, weak or distributional class is introduced here.",
          "strategy": "This is a definition contract assembled from earlier items; well-definedness is discharged by the cited suppliers. (i) The encoding (a) is the real-part-of-complex-amplitude convention of [[def-em-complex-plane-wave]] with a general $C^\\infty$ spatial amplitude; the componentwise real part of [[def-complex-conjugate-real-imaginary-part-and-modulus]] and the complex exponential of [[def-complex-exponential]] are total on $\\mathbb C^3$, so the associated real fields are defined for every $C^\\infty$ pair, with no equation assumed. (ii) The class (b) is cut out by four equations on the open set $D$: the divergence and curl of [[def-divergence-and-curl-of-a-c1-vector-field]] act componentwise on the $C^\\infty$ complex fields, and the two constants satisfy $\\varepsilon_0\\mu_0=c^{-2}$ by [[def-em-si-conventions]]; the displayed third and fourth equations use only complex scalar multiplication, so the class is well-defined without any choice principle. (iii) The physical reading of the associated real fields as an electric and a magnetic field uses [[def-em-fields]]; the units of $\\widetilde E$ are V$\\,$m$^{-1}$ and those of $\\widetilde B$ are T, inherited from that definition. (iv) Clause (c) records exactly what is not asserted; in particular the complex Maxwell-to-real-Maxwell deduction is deliberately left to a consumer, because a definition must not assert the field equations of its associated real fields.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "not-applicable"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "N. Beisert, Elektrodynamik, ETH Zurich 2024 FS, section 13.1 'Wellen in Leitern'",
                "url": "https://people.phys.ethz.ch/~nbeisert/lectures/ED-24FS-Skript.pdf",
                "locator": "printed pp. 13.1-13.3, eqs. (13.10)-(13.11): ideal-conductor waveguide model and the monochromatic phasor convention"
              },
              {
                "title": "J. Peatross and M. Ware, Physics of Light and Optics (Brigham Young University, author-hosted complete 348-page textbook)",
                "url": "https://optics.byu.edu/docs/OpticsBook.pdf",
                "locator": "chapter 10 'Diffraction', printed pp. 261-271, sections 10.1-10.4 and Example 10.4; appendix 10.A"
              }
            ]
          },
          "physical_scope": "Definition of the frequency-$\\omega$ complex phasor encoding $E=\\operatorname{Re}(\\widetilde Ee^{-i\\omega t})$, $B=\\operatorname{Re}(\\widetilde Be^{-i\\omega t})$ of a pair of $C^\\infty$ complex fields on an open spatial region, and of the class of pairs satisfying the four source-free vacuum phasor equations with the SI vacuum constants. Excluded: any assertion that the associated real fields solve Maxwell's equations, any outgoing, boundary, existence, uniqueness, energy, flux or constitutive statement, and every empirical claim; only the $C^\\infty$ open-set class is defined.",
          "dependency_level": 9
        },
        {
          "id": "lem-em-phasor-real-part-calculus-and-equivalence",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Real parts of $e^{-i\\omega t}$ phasors: calculus, injectivity and equivalence with the real Helmholtz-Maxwell system",
          "reference": "scaffold-added necessary mathematical prerequisite for the vector PEC scattering theorem (see research/physics-em-sr-40-2026-10-08-batch-40.notes.md)",
          "design_state": "new-local-prerequisite; complete-proof-strategy",
          "deps": [
            "def-ck-euclidean-maps-and-diffeomorphisms",
            "def-directional-and-partial-derivatives",
            "def-divergence-and-curl-of-a-c1-vector-field",
            "def-complex-exponential",
            "def-complex-conjugate-real-imaginary-part-and-modulus",
            "def-complex-numbers-and-arithmetic",
            "thm-complex-exponential-is-entire-with-derivative-itself",
