          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice ($\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$) as carried by [[lem-em-outgoing-source-helmholtz-and-diffraction]] and [[lem-em-helmholtz-boundary-representation]] ([[def-countable-choice]]), whose trace qualification is used in clause (d); the full-Choice modal branch of the latter is not used. Adopt the scalar aperture model and its notation from [[post-em-scalar-aperture-model]]: frequency $\\omega>0$, $k=\\omega/c$, aperture radius $a>0$, finite complex aperture distribution $\\alpha$ supported in the planar aperture $S\\subset\\{y_3=0\\}\\cap\\{y:|y|\\le a\\}$, model field $u=G_k*\\alpha$, real field $U(x,t)=\\operatorname{Re}(u(x)e^{-i\\omega t})$ and $T=2\\pi/\\omega$ ([[def-em-si-conventions]], [[def-em-lab-geometry]], [[def-complex-exponential]], [[def-complex-conjugate-real-imaginary-part-and-modulus]], [[def-integration-against-a-signed-or-complex-measure]]). Set $I(x):=(1/2)|u(x)|^2$. Then: (a) [Model field and Fraunhofer estimate] $u$ is $C^\\infty$ on the half-space $\\{x_3>0\\}$ and on $\\mathbb R^3\\setminus S$, satisfies $(\\Delta+k^2)u=0$ there, and is outgoing in the sense of [[lem-em-outgoing-source-helmholtz-and-diffraction]]: for $x=rn$ with $r\\ge2a$ and $n\\in S^2$, $$u(rn)=\\frac{e^{ikr}}{4\\pi r}\\int e^{-ikn\\cdot y}\\,d\\alpha(y)+O\\Bigl(\\frac{\\|\\alpha\\|_{\\rm TV}}{r}\\Bigl[\\frac ar+\\frac{ka^2}{r}\\Bigr]\\Bigr)$$ uniformly in direction, and $r(\\partial_ru-iku)=O(r^{-1})$ uniformly. (b) [Fresnel estimate] write $y_t=(y_1,y_2)$ and $\\xi=(\\xi_1,\\xi_2)$ for transverse vectors; for the planar aperture and observation $x=(\\xi_1,\\xi_2,z)$ with $z>0$, $b\\ge0$, $|\\xi|\\le b$ and any declared fixed small-angle range $(a+b)/z\\le\\eta_0<1$, where $0<\\eta_0<1$, the Fresnel approximation replaces $R=|x-y|$ by $z+|\\xi-y_t|^2/(2z)$ and $1/R$ by $1/z$ in the model integral with phase error $O(k(a+b)^4/z^3)$, relative amplitude error $O((a+b)^2/z^2)$ and absolute field error $O(\\|\\alpha\\|_{\\rm TV}z^{-1}[(a+b)^2/z^2+k(a+b)^4/z^3])$. (c) [Intensity and error transfer] at every $x$ with $x_3>0$ the model period average satisfies $\\frac1T\\int_0^TU(x,s)^2\\,ds=I(x)$ ([[lem-em-period-average]]). If $u_{\\rm approx}$ is any approximation of $u$ with $|u_{\\rm approx}(x)-u(x)|\\le\\delta(x)$, then $|\\frac12|u_{\\rm approx}(x)|^2-I(x)|\\le\\frac12\\delta(x)(|u(x)|+|u_{\\rm approx}(x)|)$; if moreover $u(x)\\ne0$ and $|u_{\\rm approx}(x)-u(x)|\\le\\epsilon(x)|u(x)|$, the relative intensity error is at most $2\\epsilon(x)+\\epsilon(x)^2$. In particular the Fraunhofer and Fresnel field errors of (a) and (b) bound the corresponding intensity errors; no new approximation is introduced by passing to $I$. (d) [Trace and scope] the aperture distribution $\\alpha$ is an adopted model datum and is not identified with the exact Maxwell boundary data on the screen; assigning both $u$ and $\\partial_nu$ on the aperture independently does not produce a well-posed exact boundary problem ([[lem-em-helmholtz-boundary-representation]]). The construction ignores polarization and aperture back-reaction, makes no claim that $u$ or $U$ satisfies the Maxwell equations exactly, and makes no measured-intensity, apparatus, sampling or empirical claim; only comparisons of $I$ between observation points are read as model predictions.",
          "strategy": "The theorem instantiates the mathematical field estimates of [[lem-em-outgoing-source-helmholtz-and-diffraction]] at the adopted model datum of [[post-em-scalar-aperture-model]]. (a) The model field is the supplier's convolution. Choose any open containing ball of radius $A>a$ to obtain its off-support smoothness and Helmholtz equation. For the advertised sharp-radius endpoint, argue directly for every $|y|\\le a$ and $r\\ge2a$. Write $R=|rn-y|$, so $R\\ge r-a\\ge r/2$. For $h(s)=|rn-sy|$, the exact norm derivative formula from the supplier gives $|h''(s)|\\le2a^2/(r-a)\\le4a^2/r$; twice FTC therefore gives $|R-r+n\\cdot y|\\le2a^2/r$, and $|r/R-1|\\le2a/r$. The supplier's real phase bound $|e^{i\\theta}-1|\\le|\\theta|$ now gives $$\\left|G_k(rn-y)-\\frac{e^{ikr}e^{-ikn\\cdot y}}{4\\pi r}\\right|\\le\\frac1{2\\pi r}\\left(\\frac ar+\\frac{ka^2}r\\right).$$ For a bounded continuous kernel $f$ on the compact support, $|\\int f\\,d\\alpha|\\le\\sup|f|\\,\\|\\alpha\\|_{\\rm TV}$ follows by [[prop-simple-integrals-are-bounded-by-total-variation]] and uniform finite-simple approximation in [[def-integration-against-a-signed-or-complex-measure]]; hence this pointwise bound proves the original field error, including $r=2a$. The exact derivative $\\partial_rR=(r-n\\cdot y)/R$ has modulus at most1 and $|\\partial_rR-1|\\le2a^2/r^2$. Differentiating the explicit kernel gives $r|\\partial_rG_k-ikG_k|\\le(\\pi r)^{-1}(1+ka^2/r)$; the same finite-measure bound gives the uniform outgoing residual. All derivative passages under the source integral use the supplier's compact-product uniform difference-quotient argument, not an unsupported complex-measure dominated-convergence claim. (b) On the explicitly declared range put $d_0=a+b$ and $s=|\\xi-y_t|^2/z^2\\le\\eta_0^2<1$. The actual supplier proof gives $|\\sqrt{1+s}-1-s/2|\\le s^2/8$ and $|(1+s)^{-1/2}-1|\\le s/2$ by twice FTC. Consequently the phase error is at most $kd_0^4/(8z^3)$ and the relative amplitude error at most $d_0^2/(2z^2)$. The complex-measure kernel bound above gives $$|u-u_{\\rm Fresnel}|\\le\\frac{\\|\\alpha\\|_{\\rm TV}}{4\\pi z}\\left[\\frac{d_0^2}{2z^2}+\\frac{kd_0^4}{8z^3}\\right],$$ which preserves and quantifies all original Fresnel estimates for the closed-support datum. (c) applies [[lem-em-period-average]] with $a=d=u(x)$: $\\operatorname{Re}(u(x)e^{-i\\omega t})^2$ averages to $\\frac12\\operatorname{Re}(u(x)\\overline{u(x)})=\\frac12|u(x)|^2$. The first error bound is the identity $\\frac12\\bigl||u_{\\rm approx}|^2-|u|^2\\bigr|=\\frac12\\bigl||u_{\\rm approx}|-|u|\\bigr|(|u_{\\rm approx}|+|u|)$ together with $\\bigl||u_{\\rm approx}|-|u|\\bigr|\\le|u_{\\rm approx}-u|$, obtained by applying the triangle inequality of [[lem-complex-conjugation-and-modulus-laws]] in both directions; the relative bound is $||u_{\\rm approx}|^2-|u|^2|/|u|^2\\le\\epsilon(2+\\epsilon)$. No choice principle beyond that carried by the suppliers is used. (d) reproduces the trace distinction of [[lem-em-helmholtz-boundary-representation]] and the model-scope declarations of the postulate; the intensity reading is the declared one, so no radiometric claim is added. The Countable Choice hypothesis is inherited from the cited suppliers; the intensity computation of (c) uses only the choice-free period-average lemma.",
          "provenance": {
