          "physical_scope": "Conditional model predictions for scalar aperture diffraction: the outgoing model field $u=G_k*\\alpha$, its Fraunhofer and Fresnel approximations with the explicit field-error terms of the outgoing-source lemma, the transfer of those errors to the model squared field $I=\\frac12|u|^2$, and the trace caveat that the aperture datum is not the exact screen boundary data. Excluded: exact Maxwell validity, vector or polarization content, aperture back-reaction, well-posedness of simultaneously prescribed aperture traces, absolute radiometric calibration, apparatus and sampling models, and every measured or empirical claim.",
          "dependency_level": 18
