            "def-em-fields": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-em-lab-geometry": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-em-si-conventions": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-axiom-of-choice": "mathematical-premise",
            "cor-the-curl-of-a-curl-of-a-c2-field": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-the-divergence-of-a-curl-vanishes": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-divergence-and-curl-are-linear-and-obey-the-scalar-product-rules": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-laplacian-of-a-c2-function": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-divergence-and-curl-of-a-c1-vector-field": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-complex-conjugate-real-imaginary-part-and-modulus": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-cross-product-in-r3": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-euclidean-inner-product": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-cross-product-is-bilinear-alternating-and-orthogonal": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice as carried by [[lem-em-exterior-vector-helmholtz-mixed-boundary-existence]], whose variational, Sobolev-compactness and compact-spectral steps use it; the algebraic computations below use no further choice. Let $O\\subset\\mathbb R^3$ be a bounded open set with $C^\\infty$ boundary, $D:=\\mathbb R^3\\setminus\\overline O$ connected, $k>0$, $\\omega:=ck$ with $c$ the vacuum speed of [[def-em-si-conventions]], and $R>0$ with $\\overline O\\subset B_R(0)$; let $V\\subseteq\\mathbb R^3$ be open with $\\overline D\\subseteq V$, and let $(\\widetilde E_{\\rm inc},\\widetilde B_{\\rm inc})$ be a $C^\\infty$ frequency-$\\omega$ source-free vacuum phasor pair on $V$ ([[def-em-monochromatic-source-free-phasors]], [[def-em-lab-geometry]], [[def-em-fields]], [[def-em-si-conventions]]). Plane-wave instances are provided by [[pthm-em-plane-wave-maxwell]]: if $\\kappa\\cdot e=0$, $b=\\kappa\\times e/\\omega$ and $|\\kappa|=\\omega/c$, then $(\\widetilde E_{\\rm inc},\\widetilde B_{\\rm inc})(x)=(e\\,e^{i\\kappa\\cdot x},b\\,e^{i\\kappa\\cdot x})$ satisfies the four phasor equations on $\\mathbb R^3$ ([[def-em-plane-wave-definition]]). Adopt the ideal perfectly conducting (PEC) boundary model: the tangential component of the total electric field vanishes on $\\partial O$. This is a declared idealization of the stationary interface conditions of [[pthm-em-material-stationary-jumps]] with vanishing fields inside the conductor; it is not one of the finite-conductivity branches of [[post-em-material-closure]], and the induced surface charge and current are neither prescribed nor determined here. Let $e_T$ be the tangential projection of $-\\widetilde E_{\\rm inc}$ on $\\partial O$, and let $\\widetilde E_{\\rm scat}$ be the unique $C^\\infty$ field on $\\overline D$ of [[lem-em-exterior-vector-helmholtz-mixed-boundary-existence]] with $(\\Delta+k^2)\\widetilde E_{\\rm scat}=0$ and $\\operatorname{div}\\widetilde E_{\\rm scat}=0$ on $D$ ([[def-laplacian-of-a-c2-function]], [[def-divergence-and-curl-of-a-c1-vector-field]]), tangential trace $e_T$ on $\\partial O$ and that lemma's outgoing modal condition on $S_R$. Set $\\widetilde B_{\\rm scat}:=(i\\omega)^{-1}\\operatorname{curl}\\widetilde E_{\\rm scat}$ and, on $D$, $\\widetilde E_{\\rm tot}:=\\widetilde E_{\\rm inc}+\\widetilde E_{\\rm scat}$, $\\widetilde B_{\\rm tot}:=\\widetilde B_{\\rm inc}+\\widetilde B_{\\rm scat}$. Then: (a) [Phasor Maxwell] $(\\widetilde E_{\\rm scat},\\widetilde B_{\\rm scat})$ and $(\\widetilde E_{\\rm tot},\\widetilde B_{\\rm tot})$ are $C^\\infty$ frequency-$\\omega$ source-free vacuum phasor pairs on $D$; and for every $C^\\infty$ frequency-$\\omega$ source-free vacuum phasor pair $(\\widetilde E,\\widetilde B)$ on an open set $O'\\subseteq\\mathbb R^3$, the associated real fields of [[def-em-monochromatic-source-free-phasors]] satisfy on $O'\\times\\mathbb R$ the smooth-branch vacuum Maxwell equations of [[post-em-vacuum-maxwell]] with $\\rho\\equiv0$ and $J\\equiv0$. Consequently the associated real total fields $E_{\\rm tot},B_{\\rm tot}$ satisfy those source-free equations on $D\\times\\mathbb R$. (b) [PEC boundary condition] the tangential trace of $\\widetilde E_{\\rm tot}$ on $\\partial O$ vanishes; hence for every unit normal field $n$ of $\\partial O$ the associated real total electric field $E_{\\rm tot}(x,t)=\\operatorname{Re}(\\widetilde E_{\\rm tot}(x)e^{-i\\omega t})$ ([[def-complex-conjugate-real-imaginary-part-and-modulus]]) satisfies $n\\times E_{\\rm tot}=0$ on $\\partial O\\times\\mathbb R$. (c) [Uniqueness] if $(\\widetilde E',\\widetilde B')$ is a $C^\\infty$ frequency-$\\omega$ source-free vacuum phasor pair on an open set $V'\\supseteq\\overline D$ that is outgoing on $S_R$ in the modal sense of the vector Helmholtz lemma and has tangential trace $e_T$ on $\\partial O$, then $(\\widetilde E',\\widetilde B')=(\\widetilde E_{\\rm scat},\\widetilde B_{\\rm scat})$ on $D$; equivalently $(\\widetilde E_{\\rm tot},\\widetilde B_{\\rm tot})$ is the unique total source-free phasor pair in the corresponding $C^\\infty$ closure class with that prescribed incident phasor, vanishing tangential electric trace, and outgoing scattered correction $\\widetilde E_{\\rm tot}-\\widetilde E_{\\rm inc}$ in the lemma's modal class. The total field itself is not required to be outgoing; an incident plane wave is generally not outgoing. (d) [Scope] one positive frequency $\\omega=ck$, one smooth bounded stationary PEC obstacle with connected exterior, and $C^\\infty$ incident and scattered classes only; no lossy, impedance, nonsmooth or dispersive obstacle, no determination of the induced surface charge or current, no radiation-zone amplitude or far-field asymptotics beyond the lemma's outgoing modal class, no point or singular source, no finite-energy or empirical claim.",
          "strategy": "Assume the Axiom of Choice exactly through [[lem-em-exterior-vector-helmholtz-mixed-boundary-existence]] (its symmetry/coercivity, compactness and compact-spectral steps); all other steps are pointwise algebra. (a) For the scattered pair: $\\operatorname{div}\\widetilde E_{\\rm scat}=0$ is the boundary-problem condition; $\\operatorname{curl}\\widetilde E_{\\rm scat}=i\\omega\\widetilde B_{\\rm scat}$ holds by the definition of $\\widetilde B_{\\rm scat}$; $\\operatorname{div}\\widetilde B_{\\rm scat}=(i\\omega)^{-1}\\operatorname{div}(\\operatorname{curl}\\widetilde E_{\\rm scat})=0$ and $\\operatorname{curl}\\widetilde B_{\\rm scat}=(i\\omega)^{-1}\\operatorname{curl}(\\operatorname{curl}\\widetilde E_{\\rm scat})=(i\\omega)^{-1}(\\nabla\\operatorname{div}\\widetilde E_{\\rm scat}-\\Delta\\widetilde E_{\\rm scat})=(i\\omega)^{-1}k^2\\widetilde E_{\\rm scat}=-i\\omega c^{-2}\\widetilde E_{\\rm scat}$ by [[cor-the-curl-of-a-curl-of-a-c2-field]], [[thm-the-divergence-of-a-curl-vanishes]] and $(\\Delta+k^2)\\widetilde E_{\\rm scat}=0$; the sum of two solutions of the linear system is a solution by [[lem-divergence-and-curl-are-linear-and-obey-the-scalar-product-rules]]. The real-field Maxwell statement is clause (c) of [[lem-em-phasor-real-part-calculus-and-equivalence]] with the constant $c$ of [[def-em-si-conventions]], combined with the identification of its real system with the zero-source smooth branch of [[post-em-vacuum-maxwell]]; the incident pair is a pair on $V$, hence on $D$. (b) The tangential traces satisfy $\\widetilde E_{\\rm tot,tang}=\\widetilde E_{\\rm inc,tang}+\\widetilde E_{\\rm scat,tang}=\\widetilde E_{\\rm inc,tang}+e_T=0$ on $\\partial O$; the associated real field is the real part of the tangential trace, hence vanishes (the encoding and real-part calculus are those of [[def-em-monochromatic-source-free-phasors]] and [[lem-em-phasor-real-part-calculus-and-equivalence]]). (c) For a candidate phasor pair, $\\operatorname{curl}\\operatorname{curl}\\widetilde E'=i\\omega\\operatorname{curl}\\widetilde B'=\\omega^2c^{-2}\\widetilde E'=k^2\\widetilde E'$, and $\\operatorname{div}\\widetilde E'=0$. The componentwise real/imaginary curl-curl identity thus gives $(\\Delta+k^2)\\widetilde E'=0$. Its prescribed tangential trace and outgoing correction are the declared boundary class. Hence the candidate $\\widetilde E'$ satisfies all hypotheses of the uniqueness assertion of [[lem-em-exterior-vector-helmholtz-mixed-boundary-existence]] for the same tangential data, so $\\widetilde E'=\\widetilde E_{\\rm scat}$; then $\\widetilde B'=(i\\omega)^{-1}\\operatorname{curl}\\widetilde E'=(i\\omega)^{-1}\\operatorname{curl}\\widetilde E_{\\rm scat}=\\widetilde B_{\\rm scat}$ by the third phasor equation of [[def-em-monochromatic-source-free-phasors]]. For the total-field formulation subtract the fixed incident pair: linearity gives a source-free correction with tangential trace $e_T$, and the required outgoing condition is on that correction. Conversely adding the fixed incident pair recovers the total boundary condition. Thus uniqueness transfers exactly to total-minus-incident outgoing; it does not impose the outgoing class on an incident plane wave or on their total. (d) records the exact scope; in particular the ideal PEC condition is adopted, not derived, and the material-closure branches of [[post-em-material-closure]] contain no $\\sigma\\to\\infty$ branch, while [[pthm-em-material-stationary-jumps]] supplies only the stationary-interface idealization context.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
