          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice ($\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$) as carried by [[pthm-em-dipole-radiation]] and [[lem-em-sphere-zonal-moments]] ([[def-countable-choice]]); the period-average and cross-section algebra itself uses no choice. Adopt the ideal harmonic electric-dipole radiation model of [[def-em-ideal-harmonic-dipole-model]] with frequency $\\omega>0$, wavenumber $k=\\omega/c$ and amplitude $p_0\\in\\mathbb C^3$; let $E_{\\rm d},B_{\\rm d},S_{\\rm d}$ be its fields and model flux. Let $\\kappa\\in\\mathbb R^3\\setminus\\{0\\}$ with $|\\kappa|=\\omega/c$, $e\\in\\mathbb C^3\\setminus\\{0\\}$ with $\\kappa\\cdot e=0$, $b:=\\kappa\\times e/\\omega$ ([[def-cross-product-in-r3]], [[def-euclidean-inner-product]]), and let $(E_{\\rm inc},B_{\\rm inc})$ be the corresponding plane-wave fields of [[def-em-plane-wave-definition]] on $\\mathbb R^3\\times\\mathbb R$; by [[pthm-em-plane-wave-maxwell]] they satisfy the smooth-branch source-free vacuum Maxwell equations, and by [[pthm-em-wave-energy-average]](b) their period-averaged energy flux has magnitude $I_{\\rm inc}=\\frac{\\varepsilon_0c}{2}|e|^2=\\frac{|e|^2}{2\\mu_0c}$ ([[def-em-si-conventions]]). Define the **model differential scattering cross section** by $$\\frac{d\\sigma}{d\\Omega}(n):=\\frac{r^2\\langle S_{\\rm d}(rn,\\cdot)\\cdot n\\rangle}{\\langle S_{\\rm inc}\\cdot\\hat\\kappa\\rangle},\\qquad n\\in S^2,\\ r>0,$$ where $\\hat\\kappa:=\\kappa/|\\kappa|$, $S_{\\rm inc}:=E_{\\rm inc}\\times B_{\\rm inc}/\\mu_0$ ([[def-em-vacuum-energy-flux]]), and $\\langle f\\rangle:=\\frac1T\\int_0^Tf(s)\\,ds$, $T=2\\pi/\\omega$, is the period average at fixed observation point. Then: (a) [Angular pattern] the ratio is independent of $r$ and of the averaging start, and for every $n\\in S^2$ $$\\frac{d\\sigma}{d\\Omega}(n)=\\frac{\\omega^4|n\\times p_0|^2}{16\\pi^2\\varepsilon_0^2c^4|e|^2}=\\frac{\\mu_0^2\\omega^4|n\\times p_0|^2}{16\\pi^2|e|^2}.$$ (b) [Total cross section] with $d\\sigma_{S^2}$ the surface measure of the unit sphere, $\\sigma:=\\int_{S^2}\\frac{d\\sigma}{d\\Omega}\\,d\\sigma_{S^2}$ equals $$\\sigma=\\frac{\\omega^4|p_0|^2}{6\\pi\\varepsilon_0^2c^4|e|^2}=\\frac{\\mu_0^2\\omega^4|p_0|^2}{6\\pi|e|^2};$$ if $p_0=\\alpha e$ for a complex scalar $\\alpha$ (the scalar polarizability, in $\\mathrm F\\,\\mathrm m^2$), then $\\sigma=\\frac{\\omega^4|\\alpha|^2}{6\\pi\\varepsilon_0^2c^4}$ and $\\frac{d\\sigma}{d\\Omega}(n)=\\frac{\\omega^4|\\alpha|^2}{16\\pi^2\\varepsilon_0^2c^4}|n\\times\\hat e|^2$ with $\\hat e:=e/|e|$. (c) [Fidelity for arbitrary actual sources and matched windows] Let an actual compact smooth conserved source satisfy the exact hypotheses of [[pthm-em-dipole-radiation]], with spatial support radius a>0, source-time interval [tau0,tau1], moment p_act(u), variation bound D(u) and constants Gamma_E,Gamma_B. These source data are independent of the prescribed model amplitude p0. Put\n$$p_h(u):=\\operatorname{Re}(p_0e^{-i\\omega u}),\\qquad M(u):=|p_{\\rm act}''(u)-p_h''(u)|.$$\nFor n in S2,u in[tau0,tau1],r>=2a, define\n$$H(u,r):=\\frac{\\Gamma_E}{r^2}+\\frac{\\mu_0}{4\\pi r}[D(u)+M(u)].$$\nThe actual retarded fields and the model fields satisfy, uniformly in n,\n$$|E_{\\rm act}(rn,u+r/c)-E_{\\rm d}(rn,u+r/c)|\\le H(u,r),$$\n$$|B_{\\rm act}(rn,u+r/c)-B_{\\rm d}(rn,u+r/c)|\\le\\frac{\\Gamma_B+\\Gamma_E/c}{r^2}+\\frac{H(u,r)}c.$$\nAlso retain the sharper direct source-leading-field consequence\n$$|B_{\\rm act}-B_{\\rm d}|\\le\\frac{\\Gamma_B}{r^2}+\\frac{\\mu_0[D(u)+M(u)]}{4\\pi cr}$$\nat the same events. If p_act''=p_h'' on a specified finite window, M0 there and these give the full matched dipole bounds; in particular they imply the older coarser electric bound Gamma_E/r²+mu0 D/(2pi r). Neither moment matching nor D0 is automatic. A sound sufficient matched branch is p_act=p_h+a0+b0 u on an open neighborhood of the window (any fixed real vectors a0,b0). Such a branch has actual compact realizations over any finite window: choose a smooth time cutoff eta equal1 near the window, let p_eta=eta(p_h+a0+b0 u), choose a nonnegative smooth spatial bump sigma with support inside B_a and integral1, and set rho=-p_eta dot grad sigma,J=p_eta' sigma. Then continuity holds and the actual moment is p_eta; outside the window it is tapered. Apply the actual theorem with the resulting D and Gamma, retaining every finite-radius/source-variation error. No eternal harmonic moment of a compact-time source is asserted. (d) [Scope] conditional predictions of the adopted ideal model: no measured cross section, no frequency-domain response law (the amplitude $p_0$ is prescribed model data), no magnetic-dipole or higher-multipole content, no self-force, material response, finite-size or empirical claim; the scalar-$\\alpha$ clause records a declared proportional response, not a derived polarizability. In all complex-amplitude formulas |v|²=sum_i |v_i|² is the Hermitian norm square; n cross v is complex-linear for real n. The p0=0 case gives zero scattered fields and cross sections while the nonzero incident intensity still defines the ratios. Actual-source fidelity assumes only the explicitly quantified mismatch and source hypotheses; it does not turn the model cross section into a measured or self-consistent scattering prediction.",
          "strategy": "(a) In the model, $B_{\\rm d}=n\\times E_{\\rm d}/c$ and $n\\cdot E_{\\rm d}=0$, so $S_{\\rm d}\\cdot n=n\\cdot(E_{\\rm d}\\times(n\\times E_{\\rm d}))/(\\mu_0c)=|E_{\\rm d}|^2/(\\mu_0c)$ pointwise; writing $w:=-\\frac{\\mu_0\\omega^2}{4\\pi r}n\\times(n\\times p_0)e^{ikr}$, the model has $E_{\\rm d}=\\operatorname{Re}(we^{-i\\omega t})$, and [[lem-em-period-average]] gives $\\langle|E_{\\rm d}|^2\\rangle=\\frac12|w|^2=\\frac{\\mu_0^2\\omega^4}{32\\pi^2r^2}|n\\times p_0|^2$ ([[def-complex-conjugate-real-imaginary-part-and-modulus]], [[lem-cross-product-is-bilinear-alternating-and-orthogonal]]). Hence $r^2\\langle S_{\\rm d}\\cdot n\\rangle=\\frac{\\mu_0\\omega^4}{32\\pi^2c}|n\\times p_0|^2$, independent of $r$ and of the averaging start. Division by the incident flux $I_{\\rm inc}=\\frac{|e|^2}{2\\mu_0c}$ of [[pthm-em-wave-energy-average]](b) and $\\mu_0^2=\\frac1{\\varepsilon_0^2c^4}$ ([[def-em-si-conventions]]) give the two displayed forms. (b) [[lem-em-sphere-zonal-moments]](d) gives $\\int_{S^2}|n\\times a|^2d\\sigma=\\frac{8\\pi}3|a|^2$ for real $a$, and applying it to the real and imaginary parts of $p_0$ gives the complex case; integrating the pattern of (a) over $S^2$ yields $\\frac{\\mu_0^2\\omega^4}{16\\pi^2|e|^2}\\cdot\\frac{8\\pi}3|p_0|^2=\\frac{\\mu_0^2\\omega^4|p_0|^2}{6\\pi|e|^2}$, i.e. the two displayed forms. For $p_0=\\alpha e$ substitute $|p_0|^2=|\\alpha|^2|e|^2$ and $|n\\times p_0|^2=|\\alpha|^2|e|^2|n\\times\\hat e|^2$ ([[lem-cross-product-is-bilinear-alternating-and-orthogonal]]). (c) At t=u+r/c the SIGNED model leading field is mu0 n cross(n cross p_h''(u))/(4pi r). The actual source theorem bounds E_act against the leading field of p_act'' by Gamma_E/r²+mu0 D/(4pi r). The real unit-direction double-cross projection has norm at most1, so the difference of the two leading fields is bounded by mu0 M/(4pi r). Adding gives H, including the zero actual source countercheck: then D=Gamma0 but M=|p_h''|, which exactly accounts for a nonzero prescribed model. The source theorem's B-n cross E_act/c bound is (Gamma_B+Gamma_E/c)/r²; add c^-1 times H to obtain the retained magnetic bound. Separately its stronger B-leading(V_act) estimate is Gamma_B/r²; |V_act-p_h''|<=D+M gives the sharper direct magnetic estimate. For the compact-window construction, smooth nonnegative cutoffs from [[lem-test-function-cutoffs-and-euclidean-localization]] may be normalized and scaled to give sigma ([[def-mollifier-family-generated-by-a-unit-mass-smooth-bump]] for the scaling convention). Continuity is rho_t=-p_eta' dot grad sigma and div J=p_eta' dot grad sigma. Integration by parts on a bounding rectangle gives integral rho0 and integral y_i rho=(p_eta)_i integral sigma=(p_eta)_i, using [[thm-integration-by-parts]], [[thm-riemann-fubini-on-product-rectangles]] and the Countable-Choice comparison [[lem-riemann-lebesgue-comparison-for-distribution-test-integrands]]. Choose source-time endpoints outside the taper support, so all compact smooth hypotheses are met. Moment matching on the window removes M, but D and Gamma remain the actual finite-source quantities. (d) records the scope; no measured or material content is added ([[def-em-si-conventions]] only fixes units and constants). No choice principle beyond that carried by [[pthm-em-dipole-radiation]] and [[lem-em-sphere-zonal-moments]] (Countable Choice, as stated there) is used. The Countable Choice hypothesis is inherited from the actual compact-source and sphere-moment suppliers; the finite period-average calculation and cross-section algebra are choice-free. Complex norms mean |v|²=sum_i |v_i|². Real unit n acts complex-linearly by cross products; all norm identities used in(a),(b) follow by summing the real and imaginary norm identities. The minus sign in w agrees with the model definition; squaring for its flux does not erase a sign mismatch in the field identity. Period averaging adds no choice; Countable Choice here is precisely the actual source/sphere-integral premise.",
          "provenance": {
