          },
          "physical_scope": "Symbolic flat-Minkowski example of the adopted external-field massive charged test-body action, on finite fixed-endpoint timelike segments and under the inherited countable-choice hypothesis. The pure-gauge potential changes a local canonical covector without changing the kinetic momentum or producing a Lorentz force. No self-field, radiation reaction, measured energy, empirical finding or interaction mechanism is asserted.",
          "empirical_premises": [],
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-generated",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "generation": {
            "role": "example"
          },
          "statement": "Use flat affine Minkowski spacetime $(\\mathcal A,V,\\eta,C^+)$ with signature $(-,+,+,+)$ in one named inertial chart $(x^0,x^1,x^2,x^3)$, $x^0=ct$, with coordinates in metres. Adopt the external charged test-body action of [[post-rpm-external-charge-action]], the model quantities of [[def-rpm-charge-spin-model]], and the countable-choice hypothesis $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ of [[def-countable-choice]] required by the final action-equivalence supplier; no full Axiom of Choice is assumed. Fix $m>0$ kilograms, $q\\in\\mathbb R$ coulombs and $c>0$ metres per second. For a chosen constant $b\\in\\mathbb R$ in tesla, put\n\n$$\\chi(x)=\\frac b2(x^1)^2,\\qquad A=d\\chi=b x^1\\,dx^1.$$\n\nHere $\\chi$ has units tesla metre squared and the covector components $A_a$ have units tesla metres. Then $F=dA=0$. On every finite $C^2$ future-timelike segment $z:[\\tau_0,\\tau_1]\\to\\mathcal A$ with $\\tau_0<\\tau_1$, proper-time parameter in seconds and fixed endpoint events $X_0,X_1$, the action differs from its zero-potential value by\n\n$$S_A[z]-S_0[z]=q\\bigl(\\chi(X_1)-\\chi(X_0)\\bigr).$$\n\nThus its stationary curves are precisely the free massive straight timelike curves on these segments. Their kinetic momentum $P=mU$, $U=dz/d\\tau$, is constant. With $p=mU^\\flat$ and the local canonical covector $\\pi_A=p+qA$ of [[lem-rpm-charge-gauge-boundary]],\n\n$$\\pi_{A,1}=mU_1+qb x^1,\\qquad \\frac{d\\pi_{A,1}}{d\\tau}=qb U^1.$$\n\nThe raised and lowered spatial components agree in this chart. This canonical component can vary when $qbU^1\\ne0$, while the Lorentz force and kinetic-momentum derivative vanish. If any factor vanishes, the canonical component is constant too. The shift is a gauge-dependent covector calculation, not a force or an energy measurement.",
          "dependency_level": 4,
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "David Tong, General Relativity, author-hosted Chapter 1 lecture-note excerpt",
                "url": "https://www.davidtong.org/pdfs/teaching/general-relativity/gr1.pdf",
                "locator": "The exact local action and gauge dictionary is supplied by the final batch-24 items; this item is the reserved D7 polynomial specialization and proves its calculation locally."
              },
              {
                "title": "Eric Poisson, Adam Pound and Ian Vega, The Motion of Point Particles in Curved Spacetime, author manuscript arXiv:1102.0529v3 (2011)",
