                "locator": "Complete 85-page monograph; full relevant sections inspected. Source uses natural units and signature (+---), translated explicitly in local statements."
              }
            ]
          },
          "strategy": "direct",
          "physical_scope": "Adopt specified KKS phase orbit, primitive m,s, chosen H=cP0; no quantum spectrum/unitary Wigner/spin-supplementary or force law inferred.",
          "library": "physics"
        },
        {
          "id": "thm-rpm-h-spinless-kks-identification",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Massive spinless shell reduction is a single KKS orbit",
          "statement": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$. Fix mass $m>0$ in kg and $c>0$ in m/s. For a charge point $(P^a,J^{ab})$, lower indices by $P_b:=\\eta_{ba}P^a$ and $J_{cd}:=\\eta_{ce}\\eta_{df}J^{ef}$, and define $P^2:=\\eta_{ab}P^aP^b$. Let $\\varepsilon_{abcd}$ be the totally antisymmetric Minkowski volume tensor with $\\varepsilon_{0123}=+1$; raising all indices with $\\eta=\\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,1,1)$ gives $\\varepsilon^{0123}=-1$. Let $\\Sigma_m^+$ be the future mass shell in flat Minkowski cotangent space and quotient its complete characteristic lines as in the current draft H8 supplier. The resulting global phase space has coordinates $(a^i,p_i)\\in\\mathbb R^6$ and form $da^i\\wedge dp_i$. Under the charge map of [[thm-rpm-h-poincare-moment-map-and-algebra]], it is globally symplectomorphic to the single coadjoint orbit through $(P=(mc,0),J=0)$. Its image is exactly the future massive charge pairs with $P^2=-m^2c^2$ and $W=0$, where $W^a=\\tfrac12\\varepsilon^{abcd}P_bJ_{cd}$. This statement identifies one smooth orbit; it makes no regularity claim about a union of Casimir level sets.",
          "deps": [
            "thm-rpm-h-poincare-moment-map-and-algebra",
            "thm-rpm-h-flat-shell-global-reduction",
            "thm-coadjoint-orbits-are-symplectic-manifolds",
            "def-countable-choice",
            "def-rpm-h-poincare-charge-space"
          ],
