            ]
          },
          "strategy": "direct",
          "proof_strategy": "direct"
        },
        {
          "id": "pthm-rpm-schwarzschild-null-scattering",
          "kind": "physics-theorem",
          "domain": "physics",
          "library": "physics",
          "title": "Null scattering, the critical impact parameter, and capture in the Schwarzschild exterior model",
          "statement": "Adopt the Schwarzschild exterior vacuum model with $s>0$ and the ideal-light rule that rays are future null geodesics. For an equatorial incoming ray with constants $E>0$, $L\\ge0$, impact parameter $b=L/E$, and\n\n$$H(r)=\\frac{1-s/r}{r^2},\\qquad b_{\\rm c}=\\frac{3\\sqrt3}{2}s,\\qquad r_{\\rm ph}=\\frac32s,$$\n\nthe radial first integral is $\\dot r^2=E^2[1-b^2H(r)]$ as in [[lem-rpm-schwarzschild-null-geodesic-reduction]], where dot denotes affine-parameter derivative. Then:\n\n1. If $b>b_{\\rm c}$, there is a unique outer turning point $r_*(b)>r_{\\rm ph}$, which is reached in finite affine parameter; the ray from infinity turns and returns to infinity. Its total azimuthal advance is\n\n   $$\\Delta\\varphi=2\\int_{r_*}^{\\infty}\\frac{b\\,dr}{r^2\\sqrt{1-b^2H(r)}}.$$\n\n   This integral converges at both endpoints.\n2. If $b=b_{\\rm c}$, the incoming branch from infinity approaches $r_{\\rm ph}$ only as affine parameter tends to $+\\infty$; its azimuthal advance diverges logarithmically.\n3. If $0\\le b<b_{\\rm c}$, the inward branch has no exterior turning point and reaches the boundary $r=s$ of the Schwarzschild exterior in finite affine parameter. Only if the ray is continued in the specified Kruskal model, once it lies in the region $U\\ge0$, does the causal escape result imply that it cannot return to the right exterior.\n\nThese are geodesic-model deductions. The impact threshold is not by itself an observable shadow radius.",
          "deps": [
            "pthm-gr-schwarzschild-vacuum-model",
            "post-gr-ideal-clocks-and-free-fall",
            "lem-rpm-schwarzschild-null-geodesic-reduction",
            "thm-gr-local-geodesics-and-exponential-map",
            "thm-cm-compact-continuation-for-locally-lipschitz-odes",
            "def-gr-kruskal-model-data",
            "lem-gr-kruskal-causal-escape-and-trapping"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "pthm-gr-schwarzschild-vacuum-model": "physical-result",
            "post-gr-ideal-clocks-and-free-fall": "physical-assumption",
            "lem-rpm-schwarzschild-null-geodesic-reduction": "mathematical-premise",
