              }
            ]
          },
          "strategy": "direct",
          "physical_scope": "Conditional geodesic predictions for ideal rays in the adopted Schwarzschild exterior model. Capture beyond r=s is asserted only conditionally in the named Kruskal extension. The statement excludes finite wavelength, wave optics, source/apparatus modelling, plasma, rotation, self-gravity, and empirical shadow or lensing claims.",
          "proof_strategy": "direct"
        },
        {
          "id": "pthm-rpm-static-clock-redshift",
          "kind": "physics-theorem",
          "domain": "physics",
          "library": "physics",
          "title": "Static-clock redshift, proper acceleration, and a controlled weak-field expansion in Schwarzschild",
          "statement": "Adopt the Schwarzschild exterior vacuum model datum $(M,g,N)$ of [[pthm-gr-schwarzschild-vacuum-model]] with $m_*>0$, $s=2G_Nm_*/c^2>0$ and $f(r)=1-s/r$. Let $r_E,r_R>s$ be the emitter and receiver radii of static observers in this model. Let $\\Delta t\\ne0$ be a common Schwarzschild coordinate-time duration over which ideal clocks on these static worldlines accrue proper-time increments $\\Delta\\tau_E$ and $\\Delta\\tau_R$. For the frequency ratio, let $\\eta:J\\to M$ be a specified smooth, affinely parametrized future-directed null geodesic in the exterior and choose $\\lambda_E<\\lambda_R$ in $J$ so that $\\eta(\\lambda_E)$ and $\\eta(\\lambda_R)$ lie on the static worldlines at radii $r_E$ and $r_R$, respectively. Let $\\omega_E$ and $\\omega_R$ be the ideal geometric-optics frequencies assigned by the corresponding static observers at these endpoint events, using the model's geometric-optics identification with observer energy. With $n=f^{-1/2}\\partial_0$ the unit static congruence and $U=cn$ the corresponding four-velocity, the ideal-clock and geometric-optics predictions are\n\n$$\\frac{\\Delta\\tau_R}{\\Delta\\tau_E}=\\frac{\\omega_E}{\\omega_R}=\\sqrt{\\frac{f(r_R)}{f(r_E)}},\\qquad \\frac{\\omega_R}{\\omega_E}=\\sqrt{\\frac{f(r_E)}{f(r_R)}}.$$\n\nThe proper four-acceleration magnitude required to remain static at radius $r>s$ is\n\n$$a(r)=\\sqrt{g(\\nabla_UU,\\nabla_UU)}=\\frac{c^2s}{2r^2\\sqrt{f(r)}}=\\frac{G_Nm_*}{r^2\\sqrt{1-s/r}}.$$\n\nFor any $0\\le\\rho<1$ and radii satisfying $0<s/r_E,s/r_R\\le\\rho$, define $x_i=s/r_i$ and write $\\log:=L$ for the natural integral logarithm of [[def-integral-logarithm]]. The exact logarithmic ratio has the uniform expansion\n\n$$\\log\\frac{\\omega_R}{\\omega_E}=\\frac{s}{2}\\left(\\frac1{r_R}-\\frac1{r_E}\\right)+R,\\qquad |R|\\le\\frac{x_E^2+x_R^2}{4(1-\\rho)}.$$\n\nThese are conditional deductions of the idealized model; no measured redshift or acceleration is asserted.",
          "deps": [
            "pthm-gr-schwarzschild-vacuum-model",
            "post-gr-ideal-clocks-and-free-fall",
            "def-gr-schwarzschild-exterior-model",
            "lem-gr-schwarzschild-static-congruence-and-clock-rates",
            "pthm-gr-schwarzschild-stationary-redshift",
            "def-derivative",
