    {
      "id": "qft-mc03",
      "title": "Finite bounded instruments normalize measurement probabilities",
      "category": "quantum-field-theory-mathematics",
      "library": "mathematics",
      "companion": "qft-mc03-examples",
      "kind": "A",
      "requires": [
        "qm-math-composites"
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "def-qft-finite-bounded-kraus-instrument",
          "kind": "definition",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Finite bounded Kraus instrument",
          "reference": "Local A-page prerequisite added for lem-qft-finite-instrument-normalization; design source research/plan-quantum-field-theory-track.md L84 and QFT C5.",
          "design_state": "local-definition-prerequisite; complete explicit definition",
          "dependency_level": 0,
          "deps": [
            "def-bounded-linear-operator",
            "def-countable-choice",
            "def-hilbert-space",
            "def-hilbert-space-adjoint",
            "def-operator-norm",
            "def-real-and-complex-inner-product-space",
            "def-space-of-bounded-linear-operators",
            "thm-hilbert-adjoint-properties"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-bounded-linear-operator": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-hilbert-space": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-hilbert-space-adjoint": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-operator-norm": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-real-and-complex-inner-product-space": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-space-of-bounded-linear-operators": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-hilbert-adjoint-properties": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice, written $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $H$ be a nonzero complex Hilbert space with inner product linear in its first argument ([[def-hilbert-space]], [[def-real-and-complex-inner-product-space]]). Write $\\mathcal B(H)$ for the bounded linear operators on $H$ ([[def-space-of-bounded-linear-operators]]); for $M\\in\\mathcal B(H)$, $M^*$ is its Hilbert adjoint, characterized by $\\langle Mx,y\\rangle=\\langle x,M^*y\\rangle$ ([[def-hilbert-space-adjoint]]).\n\nUnder this same $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ hypothesis, [[thm-hilbert-adjoint-properties]] gives $M^*\\in\\mathcal B(H)$ and $\\|M^*\\|=\\|M\\|$.\n\nA **finite bounded Kraus instrument datum** on $H$ consists of an integer $m\\ge1$, integers $q_a\\ge0$ for $a=1,\\ldots,m$, and bounded operators $M_{a,r}\\in\\mathcal B(H)$ for $r=1,\\ldots,q_a$. It is **normalized** when\n\n$$\\sum_{a=1}^{m}\\sum_{r=1}^{q_a}M_{a,r}^*M_{a,r}=I_H.$$\n\nEmpty inner sums are zero. For each outcome $a$, define its outcome operator and operation by\n\n$$E_a:=\\sum_{r=1}^{q_a}M_{a,r}^*M_{a,r},\\qquad \\mathcal J_a(X):=\\sum_{r=1}^{q_a}M_{a,r}XM_{a,r}^*\\quad(X\\in\\mathcal B(H)).$$\n\nThese formulas take values in $\\mathcal B(H)$: the adjoint theorem above makes each $M_{a,r}^*$ bounded, and $\\|M_{a,r}XM_{a,r}^*x\\|\\le\\|M_{a,r}\\|\\,\\|X\\|\\,\\|M_{a,r}^*\\|\\,\\|x\\|=\\|M_{a,r}\\|^2\\,\\|X\\|\\,\\|x\\|$; the sums are finite. This definition specifies only the displayed finite Kraus form; it is not a representation theorem for arbitrary instruments and does not assert that an apparatus realizes these data.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "not-applicable"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "J. Watrous, The Theory of Quantum Information (Cambridge University Press, 2018; author-hosted pre-publication manuscript), §2.3.1 pp. 100–102 and §2.3.2 pp. 111–113",
                "url": "https://cs.uwaterloo.ca/~watrous/TQI/TQI.2.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "R. B. Griffiths, Notes on Quantum Information Theory, version 30 Jan. 2004, §7 pp. 1–3, equations (7.2)–(7.9)",
                "url": "https://www.andrew.cmu.edu/course/33-658/qit7.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "library": "mathematics"
        },
        {
          "id": "lem-qft-finite-instrument-normalization",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Finite bounded instruments normalize measurement probabilities",
          "reference": "research/extended-frameworks-2026-10-03/quantum-field-theory/proposed-inventory.json#lem-qft-finite-instrument-normalization; proof module research/extended-frameworks-2026-10-03/quantum-field-theory/complete-local-arguments.md#C5",
          "design_state": "reserved-QFT-MC03; complete conditional argument",
          "dependency_level": 1,
          "deps": [
            "def-countable-choice",
            "def-qft-finite-bounded-kraus-instrument",
            "def-self-adjoint-positive-unitary-and-normal-operator",
            "def-trace-class-operator",
            "def-trace-of-a-trace-class-operator",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-density-and-scalar-spectral-probability",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-nuclear-bounded-cyclicity",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-rank-one-operator-calculus",
            "thm-hilbert-adjoint-properties",
            "thm-trace-class-is-a-two-sided-banach-operator-ideal",
            "thm-trace-is-absolutely-convergent-and-basis-independent"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-qft-finite-bounded-kraus-instrument": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-self-adjoint-positive-unitary-and-normal-operator": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-trace-class-operator": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-trace-of-a-trace-class-operator": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-density-and-scalar-spectral-probability": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-nuclear-bounded-cyclicity": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-rank-one-operator-calculus": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-hilbert-adjoint-properties": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-trace-class-is-a-two-sided-banach-operator-ideal": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-trace-is-absolutely-convergent-and-basis-independent": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $H$ carry a normalized finite bounded Kraus instrument datum as defined in [[def-qft-finite-bounded-kraus-instrument]], and let $\\rho$ be a density operator on $H$: a self-adjoint positive trace-class operator with $\\operatorname{tr}\\rho=1$ ([[lem-nrqm-composites-density-and-scalar-spectral-probability]], [[def-trace-class-operator]], [[def-trace-of-a-trace-class-operator]], [[def-self-adjoint-positive-unitary-and-normal-operator]]). For each outcome $a$, put $p_a:=\\operatorname{tr}(\\mathcal J_a(\\rho))$. Then each $E_a$ is an effect ($E_a\\ge0$ and $I_H-E_a\\ge0$), each $\\mathcal J_a(\\rho)$ is positive trace class, and\n\n$$p_a=\\operatorname{tr}(\\mathcal J_a(\\rho))=\\operatorname{tr}(\\rho E_a)\\in[0,1],\\qquad \\sum_{a=1}^{m}p_a=1.$$\n\nThe nonselective output $\\sum_a\\mathcal J_a(\\rho)$ is a density operator. If $p_a>0$, the normalized conditional state $\\rho_a:=\\mathcal J_a(\\rho)/p_a$ is a density operator; when $p_a=0$, this normalized update is undefined. For a unit vector $\\psi\\in H$, the rank-one density operator $\\rho=T_{\\psi,\\psi}$ has outcome probability $p_a=\\sum_{r=1}^{q_a}\\|M_{a,r}\\psi\\|^2$. These are conditional mathematical identities; they do not assert that an apparatus realizes the instrument or supply a physical measurement postulate.",
          "strategy": "Define the finite bounded Kraus data explicitly, use the trace-norm density expansion and bounded trace cyclicity to prove outcome positivity and normalization, then normalize each positive-trace conditional update.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "J. Watrous, The Theory of Quantum Information (Cambridge University Press, 2018; author-hosted pre-publication manuscript), §2.3.1 pp. 100–102 and §2.3.2 pp. 111–113",
                "url": "https://cs.uwaterloo.ca/~watrous/TQI/TQI.2.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "R. B. Griffiths, Notes on Quantum Information Theory, version 30 Jan. 2004, §7 pp. 1–3, equations (7.2)–(7.9)",
                "url": "https://www.andrew.cmu.edu/course/33-658/qit7.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "library": "mathematics",
          "proof_strategy": "direct"
        }
      ],
      "scaffold": "research/plan-quantum-field-theory-track.md",
      "order": 511
    },
