            "lem-euclidean-gaussian-fourier-transform-with-two-pi-normalization": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-l-two-with-the-integral-pairing-is-a-hilbert-space": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-dominated-convergence": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-double-orthogonal-complement-is-closure": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-nrqm-oscillator-hermite-recurrence": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-complex-exponential-series-converges-everywhere": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "dependency_level": 0,
          "proof_strategy": "direct",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice [[def-countable-choice]]. Let\n$H=L^2(\\mathbb R,dx;\\mathbb C)$ with its first-variable-linear integral pairing,\nand let $Qf(x)=xf(x)$ on\n$D(Q)=\\{f\\in H:xf\\in H\\}$. Let $(g_n)_{n\\ge0}$ be the Hermite functions of\n[[thm-nrqm-oscillator-hermite-recurrence]]. Then $Q$ is self-adjoint on $D(Q)$,\nand the finite linear span of the $g_n$ is a core for $Q$: it is dense in\n$D(Q)$ for the graph norm\n$\\|f\\|_Q=(\\|f\\|_2^2+\\|Qf\\|_2^2)^{1/2}$.",
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Gerald Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics, §8.3 (the harmonic oscillator)",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-schroe/schroe.pdf",
