      "items": [
        {
          "id": "ex-qftmath-spacelike-vacuum-correlation",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "library": "mathematics",
          "physical_scope": null,
          "title": "Positive vacuum correlation for spacelike-separated massless tests",
          "deps": [
            "def-countable-choice",
            "def-qft-scalar-mass-shell",
            "lem-qft-smeared-free-scalar",
            "lem-qft-scalar-causal-commutator",
            "lem-qft-scalar-local-weyl-algebra",
            "lem-smooth-bump-between-concentric-euclidean-balls",
            "thm-dominated-convergence",
            "thm-fubini-theorem-for-l-one-on-sigma-finite-product-spaces",
            "thm-cauchy-schwarz-in-an-inner-product-space"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-qft-scalar-mass-shell": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-qft-smeared-free-scalar": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-qft-scalar-causal-commutator": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-qft-scalar-local-weyl-algebra": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-smooth-bump-between-concentric-euclidean-balls": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-dominated-convergence": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-fubini-theorem-for-l-one-on-sigma-finite-product-spaces": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-cauchy-schwarz-in-an-inner-product-space": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "dependency_level": 6,
          "proof_strategy": "direct",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. In the massless model $\\mu=0$, there are nonnegative\nreal test functions\n$f,g\\in C_c^\\infty(\\mathbb R^4)$ with spacelike-separated supports for which\n$$\\langle\\Omega,\\Phi_0(f)\\Omega\\rangle_2 =\\langle\\Omega,\\Phi_0(g)\\Omega\\rangle_2=0,\\qquad \\langle\\Omega,\\Phi_0(f)\\Phi_0(g)\\Omega\\rangle_2>0.$$\nThe corresponding local Weyl operators commute by\n[[lem-qft-scalar-local-weyl-algebra]]. The nonzero correlation is a\nmathematical vacuum expectation in the specified representation; it is not a\nmeasurement or a signaling effect.",
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Mark Srednicki, Quantum Field Theory, author draft, chapter 4",
                "url": "https://www.physics.ucsb.edu/~mark/ms-qft-DRAFT.pdf",
                "locator": "Complete 616-page author-hosted draft; chapter 4 equations 4.11–4.15, massless two-point function."
              },
              {
                "title": "David Tong, Quantum Field Theory, section 2.7",
                "url": "https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/qft/qfthtml/S2.html",
                "locator": "Author-hosted HTML text of chapter 2, section 2.7, vacuum two-point function and its spacelike value; the complete lecture-note set is also listed as a 155-page PDF."
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "scaffold": "research/plan-quantum-field-theory-track.md",
      "order": 516
    },
    {
      "id": "qft-mc04",
      "title": "Exact massless scalar on a conformally flat external metric",
      "category": "quantum-field-theory-mathematics",
      "library": "mathematics",
      "companion": "qft-mc04-examples",
      "kind": "A",
      "requires": [
        "emg-c01",
        "qft-mf02"
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "thm-qft-conformal-external-scalar",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "library": "mathematics",
          "title": "Exact massless scalar on a conformally flat external metric",
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ of [[def-countable-choice]]. On $M=\\mathbb R^4$ with global coordinates $x=(x^0,x^1,x^2,x^3)$, set $\\eta_{ab}=\\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,1,1)$, orient $M$ by $o=dx^0\\wedge dx^1\\wedge dx^2\\wedge dx^3$, and use $\\partial_0$ to select the standard future cone. Coordinates have length units, derivatives have inverse-length units, and the Fourier phase and conformal factor are dimensionless, consistent with [[def-qft-scalar-mass-shell]]. Thus $\\Box_\\eta$, $\\Box_g$, $R_g$, and $P_g$ have inverse-length-squared units. Let $\\Omega\\in C^\\infty(\\mathbb R^4;(0,\\infty))$ be real and dimensionless, and define the prescribed external Lorentzian metric $g_{ab}=\\Omega^2\\eta_{ab}$. No field equation for $g$ is assumed. Write $d\\mathrm{vol}_g=\\Omega^4d^4x$ for its positive integration density and $\\Box_\\eta=\\eta^{ab}\\partial_a\\partial_b$. Let $R_g$ be the scalar curvature with the convention of [[def-gr-curvature-tensor-and-derived-tensors]], which is also used by [[thm-emg-conformal-einstein-transformation]], and define\n$$\\Box_g h:=\\Omega^{-4}\\partial_a\\!\\left(\\Omega^2\\eta^{ab}\\partial_bh\\right),\\qquad P_g:=\\Box_g-\\frac16R_g.$$\nThe test space is $\\mathcal D=C_c^\\infty(\\mathbb R^4;\\mathbb C)$ with the LF test-function topology of [[def-test-function-topology]]. Let $\\Phi_0$ be the massless Minkowski Fock field and let $\\varpi_0\\in\\mathcal D_{\\rm fin}$ be its normalized vacuum vector, written $|0\\rangle$ in Dirac notation. The common dense invariant domain and field convention are those of [[lem-qft-smeared-free-scalar]] and [[lem-qft-scalar-causal-commutator]]. For $f\\in\\mathcal D$, define the curved-background smeared field by\n$$\\Phi_g(f):=\\Phi_0(\\Omega^3f).$$\n\nThen, with all equalities understood on $\\mathcal D_{\\rm fin}$ or as distributional equalities as appropriate:\n\n1. The exact curvature and scalar wave identities are\n$$R_g=-6\\Omega^{-3}\\Box_\\eta\\Omega,\\qquad P_g(\\Omega^{-1}u)=\\Omega^{-3}\\Box_\\eta u\\quad(u\\in C^\\infty(\\mathbb R^4;\\mathbb C)).$$\n\n2. The map $f\\mapsto\\Phi_g(f)$ is a weak operator-valued distribution on $\\mathcal D_{\\rm fin}$, meaning that for every $\\chi,\\psi\\in\\mathcal D_{\\rm fin}$ the map $f\\mapsto\\langle\\chi,\\Phi_g(f)\\psi\\rangle_2$ is a continuous complex-linear functional on $\\mathcal D$ with its test-function topology. It satisfies $\\Phi_g(P_gf)=0$ for every $f\\in\\mathcal D$. The normalized Minkowski vacuum defines a positive state on the finite polynomial $*$-algebra generated by the real-test fields.\n\n3. If $\\operatorname{supp}f$ and $\\operatorname{supp}h$ are spacelike separated (every pair of points in the two supports has positive $\\eta$-squared separation), then $[\\Phi_g(f),\\Phi_g(h)]=0$ on $\\mathcal D_{\\rm fin}$.\n\n4. The two-point distribution relative to $d\\mathrm{vol}_g(x)d\\mathrm{vol}_g(y)$ is\n$$W_g(x,y)=\\Omega(x)^{-1}\\Omega(y)^{-1}W_0(x,y),$$\nwhere $W_0$ is the massless Minkowski Fock-vacuum two-point distribution from [[lem-qft-smeared-free-scalar]], relative to $d^4x\\,d^4y$ and paired bilinearly as $W_0(f,h)=\\langle\\varpi_0,\\Phi_0(f)\\Phi_0(h)\\varpi_0\\rangle_2$. On compact tests, $P_g$ is formally symmetric for $d\\mathrm{vol}_g$.\n\nThis is a selected free-field representation obtained from one Minkowski Fock vacuum. It asserts no uniqueness of a curved-spacetime state, generic Hadamard-state existence, thermal-state result, renormalized stress-tensor transformation, massive or minimally coupled result, Einstein equation, or backreaction claim. The metric is prescribed background data, not a dynamical solution.",
          "deps": [
            "def-countable-choice",
            "def-fixed-support-test-function-frechet-space",
            "def-gr-curvature-tensor-and-derived-tensors",
            "def-qft-fock-and-test-spaces",
            "def-qft-scalar-mass-shell",
            "def-schwartz-space-and-its-seminorms",
            "def-test-function-topology",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-bounded-tensor-maps",
            "lem-nrqm-composites-permutation-sector-projections",
            "lem-test-function-lf-topology-universal-property",
            "lem-qft-smeared-free-scalar",
            "lem-qft-scalar-causal-commutator",
            "thm-emg-conformal-einstein-transformation",
            "thm-gr-nondegenerate-levi-civita-and-tensor-derivative",
            "thm-fourier-transform-maps-schwartz-space-continuously-to-itself"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-fixed-support-test-function-frechet-space": "mathematical-premise",
