                "url": "https://www.bipm.org/documents/20126/41483022/SI-Brochure-9.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "library": "physics",
          "proof_strategy": "direct"
        },
        {
          "id": "post-qft-constructed-model-and-measurement",
          "kind": "postulate",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "Physical interpretation of a supplied constructed quantum model",
          "reference": "research/extended-frameworks-2026-10-03/quantum-field-theory/quantities-and-postulates.md#constructed-measurement",
          "design_state": "planned adopted model-conditional Born interpretation; exact finite-instrument hypotheses and absence of continuum/empirical claims stated",
          "dependency_level": 2,
          "deps": [
            "def-qft-framework-units",
            "def-qft-finite-bounded-kraus-instrument",
            "def-countable-choice",
            "lem-qft-finite-instrument-normalization",
            "def-projection-valued-measure",
            "def-symmetric-self-adjoint-and-essentially-self-adjoint"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-qft-framework-units": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-qft-finite-bounded-kraus-instrument": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-qft-finite-instrument-normalization": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-projection-valued-measure": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-symmetric-self-adjoint-and-essentially-self-adjoint": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "physical_scope": "Adopts state, finite instrument and actual constructed unitary dynamics only; supplies no missing continuum representation or convergence.",
          "statement": "Adopt the following physical reading only for an explicitly selected model\nwhose mathematical data have actually been constructed. Let $\\mathscr H$ be a\nnonzero complex Hilbert space, let $\\rho_t$ be the model's density operator at\na time $t$ at which a measurement is made, and let\n$\\{M_{a,r}:r=1,\\ldots,q_a\\}_{a=1}^m$ be a supplied normalized finite bounded\nKraus instrument on $\\mathscr H$ in the exact sense of\n[[def-qft-finite-bounded-kraus-instrument]]. Assume the Axiom of Countable\nChoice $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ when using the normalization result of\n[[lem-qft-finite-instrument-normalization]]. Its hypotheses include that\n$\\rho_t$ is a density operator and that the instrument really satisfies\n$\\sum_{a,r}M_{a,r}^*M_{a,r}=I_{\\mathscr H}$; the supplier's result is a draft\nwith a complete conditional proof, not an independent approval or an\napparatus-realization theorem.\n\nPut\n\n$$E_a:=\\sum_rM_{a,r}^*M_{a,r},\\qquad \\mathcal J_a(X):=\\sum_rM_{a,r}XM_{a,r}^*.$$\n\nAs the **Born interpretation postulate** for this selected model, read\n\n$$p_a(t):=\\operatorname{tr}(\\mathcal J_a(\\rho_t)) =\\operatorname{tr}(\\rho_tE_a)$$\n\nas the model probability for outcome $a$. The mathematical supplier proves\n$p_a(t)\\in[0,1]$ and $\\sum_{a=1}^mp_a(t)=1$ under the hypotheses just\nlisted. When $p_a(t)>0$, adopt\n$\\mathcal J_a(\\rho_t)/p_a(t)$ as the model's conditional state after outcome\n$a$; at zero probability no normalized update is assigned. These are\nmodel-level probability assignments, not observations.\n\nIf the selected construction supplies a self-adjoint observable in the sense\nof [[def-symmetric-self-adjoint-and-essentially-self-adjoint]] and its\nspectral projection-valued measure as in\n[[def-projection-valued-measure]], a declared finite Borel partition may be\nused only after its projections have been constructed and verified as a\nfinite projective instrument. In that case the projections are the single\nKraus operators for their outcomes. A supplied bounded effect is read as an\noutcome effect only as part of a supplied normalized instrument; this item\ndoes not construct square roots, a spectral measure, or an instrument from an\narbitrary formal observable.\n\nIf a model has actually constructed a self-adjoint Hamiltonian $\\widehat H$\nand its unitary evolution, adopt the Schrödinger convention\n$U(t)=\\exp(-it\\widehat H/\\hbar)$ and\n$\\rho_t=U(t)\\rho_0U(t)^*$ when that construction establishes that $\\rho_t$\nis a density operator. In the Heisenberg representation use\n$O_H(t)=U(t)^*O\\,U(t)$. This postulate neither constructs the Hamiltonian,\nunitary group, state, field representation, nor their domains.\n\nThe model declaration identifies the selected species, field normalization,\nregulator, preparation and measurement data using\n[[def-qft-framework-units]]. It does not assert that every classical action\nhas a quantization, that every formal state is positive, or that any cutoff\ncan be removed. In particular it supplies no interacting continuum\nfour-dimensional QED Hilbert space, scattering operator, asymptotic\ncompleteness, LSZ limit, or nonperturbative convergence. A formal coefficient\nis not an exact probability without an additional controlled approximation\nmap and a constructed model. Agreement with reported data would test the\nselected approximation and empirical inputs; it would not prove this\npostulate or the model. No reported data are asserted here.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "not-applicable"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "J. Watrous, The Theory of Quantum Information (Cambridge University Press, 2018; author-hosted prepublication manuscript), §2.3.1 pp. 100–102 and §2.3.2 pp. 111–113",
                "url": "https://cs.uwaterloo.ca/~watrous/TQI/TQI.2.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "R. B. Griffiths, Notes on Quantum Information Theory, version 30 Jan. 2004, complete §7, printed pp. 1–3, equations (7.2)–(7.9)",
                "url": "https://www.andrew.cmu.edu/course/33-658/qit7.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "library": "physics"
        }
      ],
      "scaffold": "research/plan-quantum-field-theory-track.md",
      "order": 519
    },
    {
      "id": "qft-c01-examples",
      "title": "Quantum field quantities and compatible SI normalizations — Examples",
      "kind": "B",
      "category": "quantum-field-theory",
      "library": "physics",
      "companion": "qft-c01",
      "requires": [
        "qft-c01",
