        {
          "id": "lem-qft-dirac-covariance-spectrum",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "library": "mathematics",
          "physical_scope": null,
          "title": "Dirac Fock covariance, vacuum cyclicity and spectrum",
          "deps": [
            "def-qft-dirac-projections",
            "lem-qft-dirac-projection-matrices",
            "lem-qft-free-dirac-car-locality",
            "lem-qft-lorentz-boost-rotation-factorization",
            "lem-lorentz-map-preserves-metric-and-causal-structure",
            "lem-qft-dirac-fermionic-translation-spectrum",
            "def-qft-scalar-mass-shell",
            "lem-qft-mass-shell-measure-invariant",
            "def-qft-fock-and-test-spaces",
            "lem-qft-fock-ccr-car",
            "def-countable-choice",
            "def-sr-affine-minkowski-model",
            "def-inertial-frame-and-inertial-chart",
            "def-lorentz-map-and-lorentz-group",
            "lem-smooth-compactly-supported-functions-are-dense-in-ltwo-of-an-open-set",
            "thm-quarter-turn-values-and-shift-formulas"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-qft-dirac-projections": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-qft-dirac-projection-matrices": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-qft-free-dirac-car-locality": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-qft-lorentz-boost-rotation-factorization": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-lorentz-map-preserves-metric-and-causal-structure": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-qft-dirac-fermionic-translation-spectrum": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-qft-scalar-mass-shell": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-qft-mass-shell-measure-invariant": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-qft-fock-and-test-spaces": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-qft-fock-ccr-car": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-sr-affine-minkowski-model": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-inertial-frame-and-inertial-chart": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-lorentz-map-and-lorentz-group": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-smooth-compactly-supported-functions-are-dense-in-ltwo-of-an-open-set": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-quarter-turn-values-and-shift-formulas": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "dependency_level": 6,
          "proof_strategy": "direct",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice [[def-countable-choice]] and the mathematical free Dirac data of [[def-qft-dirac-projections]], [[lem-qft-dirac-projection-matrices]], and [[lem-qft-free-dirac-car-locality]]. Let $G=\\mathbb R^4\\rtimes SO^+(1,3)$ act by $x\\mapsto a+\\Lambda x$, with product $(a_2,\\Lambda_2)(a_1,\\Lambda_1)=(a_2+\\Lambda_2a_1,\\Lambda_2\\Lambda_1)$. Let $\\widetilde G$ be the subgroup of triples $(a,\\Lambda,S)$ generated by translations $(a,I,I)$ and the explicit rotation/boost triples $(0,R_{\\mathbf n}(\\theta),S_R(\\theta))$ and $(0,B_{\\mathbf n}(\\chi),S_B(\\chi))$ of [[lem-qft-dirac-projection-matrices]], with product $(a_2,\\Lambda_2,S_2)(a_1,\\Lambda_1,S_1)=(a_2+\\Lambda_2a_1,\\Lambda_2\\Lambda_1,S_2S_1)$ and the subspace topology from $\\mathbb R^4\\times M_4(\\mathbb R)\\times GL(4,\\mathbb C)$. Its projection onto $G$ is surjective by [[lem-qft-lorentz-boost-rotation-factorization]]. For $\\tilde g=(a,\\Lambda,S)$ define the spinor test pullback\n$$\\tau_{\\tilde g}F(x)=(S^{-1})^\\dagger F(\\Lambda^{-1}(x-a)).$$\nThe fermionic Fock space of [[def-qft-fock-and-test-spaces]] carries a strongly continuous unitary representation $U$ of $\\widetilde G$ such that\n$$U(\\tilde g)\\Psi(F)U(\\tilde g)^{-1}=\\Psi(\\tau_{\\tilde g}F).$$\nLet $\\mathcal A_D^{\\mathrm{gr}}$ be the algebra generated by all bounded $\\Psi(F)$ and $\\Psi(F)^\\dagger$ for Schwartz spinor tests $F$. The vacuum $\\Omega$ is invariant and cyclic for $\\mathcal A_D^{\\mathrm{gr}}$. A $2\\pi$ spatial spin rotation acts as $(-1)^N$ on the $n$-particle sector with value $(-1)^n$; a $4\\pi$ rotation acts as the identity. The translation generators and joint spectral measure are those of [[lem-qft-dirac-fermionic-translation-spectrum]], so the joint spectrum is contained in the closed future cone, $\\Omega$ is the unique zero-energy vector, and for $\\mu>0$ the nonvacuum energy has gap at least $\\mu$. The first-quantized $h_D$ has both signs of energy; this Fock-space generator is a different operator on a different Hilbert space. No general spin-statistics theorem or local cyclicity claim is asserted.",
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "David Tong, Quantum Field Theory, Chapters 4–5",
                "url": "https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/qft/qft.pdf",
                "locator": "Complete 155-page author-hosted notes; Chapter 4 spinor Lorentz representation and Chapter 5 §§5.2–5.4, free Dirac modes, antiparticles, and positive-energy Fock interpretation."
              },
