                "locator": "Full-text HTML lecture notes; printed pp. 3–6, compact U(1) link rotor, integer electric basis, fermionic matter and physical Gauss sector. Their worked model is not identified with this finite-graph model."
              }
            ]
          },
          "physical_scope": "Adopted fixed finite-graph U(1) rotor and finite-CAR regulator with a fixed background and bounded interaction data. Hamiltonian coefficients are assigned energy units; no spatial embedding, continuum approximation or limit, continuum QED identification, empirical realization, or measured prediction is asserted.",
          "reference": "research/extended-frameworks-2026-10-03/quantum-field-theory/workers/qed/proofs.md#Q5",
          "design_state": "Authored from Q5 as a fixed finite graph model; units, operator domains, and no-continuum scope are explicit."
        },
        {
          "id": "pthm-qft-lattice-gauge-existence",
          "kind": "physics-theorem",
          "domain": "physics",
          "library": "physics",
          "title": "Actual interacting physical Gauss-sector dynamics",
          "statement": "Assume the fixed finite-graph model adopted by\n[[post-qft-compact-lattice-gauge-model]]: a finite nonempty oriented graph,\n$s\\ge1$ finite CAR modes per vertex, fixed backgrounds\n$b_x\\in\\{0,\\ldots,s\\}$, link electric operators $E_e$, the joint Gauss\noperators $G_x$, and $H=H_0+V_B+V_F$ on the exact maximal domain\n$D(H_0)$ of [[def-qft-compact-lattice-gauge-data]]. Assume the Axiom of Choice\nand a constant $\\hbar>0$ in joule-seconds. Then the physical sector\n$$\\mathcal H_{\\rm phys}=\\bigcap_{x\\in V}\\ker G_x$$\nis nonzero. The restriction $H_{\\rm phys}:=H|_{D(H)\\cap\\mathcal H_{\\rm phys}}$\nis self-adjoint, and\n$$\\mathcal U_{\\rm phys}(t)=e^{-itH_{\\rm phys}/\\hbar},\\qquad t\\in\\mathbb R,$$\nis a strongly continuous unitary group on $\\mathcal H_{\\rm phys}$ with the\nexact derivative domain $D(H)\\cap\\mathcal H_{\\rm phys}$. This is an exact\nfixed-regulator result conditional on the stated mathematical suppliers; it\nasserts no continuum dynamics or continuum QED construction.",
          "strategy": "direct",
          "deps": [
            "post-qft-compact-lattice-gauge-model",
            "def-qft-compact-lattice-gauge-data",
            "lem-qft-lattice-physical-evolution",
            "lem-qft-lattice-gauss-projection",
            "def-axiom-of-choice",
            "def-countable-choice"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
