    {
      "id": "qft-x03",
      "title": "Regulated soft coherent photon-count prediction",
      "category": "quantum-field-theory",
      "library": "physics",
      "companion": "qft-x03-examples",
      "kind": "A",
      "requires": [
        "qft-g01",
        "qft-mx03",
        "qft-mx04",
        "qft-x01",
        "em-primitives-and-postulates"
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "def-qft-x03-photon-count-pvm",
          "kind": "definition",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "library": "physics",
          "title": "Bosonic Fock number operator and counting PVM",
          "statement": "Let $H$ be a complex Hilbert space and let\n$$\\mathcal F_s(H)=\\bigoplus_{n=0}^{\\infty}H_s^{(n)}$$\nbe its bosonic Fock Hilbert space under\n[[def-qft-fock-and-test-spaces]]. A vector is a square-summable sequence\n$\\Psi=(\\Psi_n)_{n\\ge0}$ with $\\Psi_n\\in H_s^{(n)}$.\n\nDefine the number operator $N$ by\n$$D(N)=\\left\\{\\Psi\\in\\mathcal F_s(H): \\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty}n^2\\|\\Psi_n\\|^2<\\infty\\right\\},\\qquad (N\\Psi)_n=n\\Psi_n.$$\n\nFor every Borel set $B\\subseteq\\mathbb R$, define the sector projection\n$$E_N(B)\\Psi=\\bigl(\\mathbf1_B(n)\\Psi_n\\bigr)_{n\\ge0},\\qquad P_n:=E_N(\\{n\\}).$$\nThe definitions specify a candidate number observable and its candidate\nspectral projections. They assign no physical probability; well-definedness,\nself-adjointness, and the projection-valued-measure property are established\nby [[thm-qft-x03-photon-count-pvm]].",
          "deps": [
            "def-qft-fock-and-test-spaces",
            "def-projection-valued-measure",
            "def-unbounded-linear-operator-domain-and-graph"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-qft-fock-and-test-spaces": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-projection-valued-measure": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-unbounded-linear-operator-domain-and-graph": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "not-applicable"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Mark Srednicki, Quantum Field Theory, author-hosted 2006 prepublication book draft, §55 “Electrodynamics in Coulomb Gauge,” printed pp. 335–338",
                "url": "https://www.physics.ucsb.edu/~mark/ms-qft-DRAFT.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "dependency_level": 1,
          "physical_scope": null,
          "justified_by": [
            "thm-qft-x03-photon-count-pvm"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "thm-qft-x03-photon-count-pvm",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "library": "physics",
          "title": "The Fock number operator has its sector counting PVM",
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice [[def-countable-choice]]. Let $H$ be a complex Hilbert\nspace, and let $N$, $E_N(B)$, and $P_n$ be as in\n[[def-qft-x03-photon-count-pvm]]. Then $N$ is self-adjoint on its stated\ndomain and $E_N$ is a projection-valued measure on the Borel subsets of\n$\\mathbb R$. It is the sector counting resolution: $E_N(B)$ keeps exactly the\nsectors whose integer label lies in $B$, and $N$ multiplies sector $n$ by $n$.\nFor any finite Borel partition $(B_a)_{a=1}^m$ of $\\mathbb R$, the projections\n$E_N(B_a)$ are mutually orthogonal and sum to the identity.",
          "deps": [
            "def-countable-choice",
            "def-qft-fock-and-test-spaces",
            "def-qft-x03-photon-count-pvm",
            "def-projection-valued-measure",
            "def-unbounded-linear-operator-domain-and-graph",
            "def-adjoint-of-a-densely-defined-unbounded-operator",
            "def-symmetric-self-adjoint-and-essentially-self-adjoint"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-qft-fock-and-test-spaces": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-qft-x03-photon-count-pvm": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-projection-valued-measure": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-unbounded-linear-operator-domain-and-graph": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-adjoint-of-a-densely-defined-unbounded-operator": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-symmetric-self-adjoint-and-essentially-self-adjoint": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Mark Srednicki, Quantum Field Theory, author-hosted 2006 prepublication book draft, §55 “Electrodynamics in Coulomb Gauge,” printed pp. 335–338",
                "url": "https://www.physics.ucsb.edu/~mark/ms-qft-DRAFT.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "dependency_level": 2,
          "physical_scope": null,
          "proof_strategy": "direct"
        },
        {
          "id": "pthm-qft-example-soft-coherent-counts",
          "kind": "physics-theorem",
          "domain": "physics",
          "library": "physics",
          "title": "Regulated soft coherent photon-count prediction",
          "statement": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ [[def-countable-choice]]. Use the SI/natural\nnormalizations of [[def-qft-framework-units]] and\n[[def-qft-example-data]], in particular the spacetime metric\n$\\eta=\\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,1,1)$, the algebraic energy-momentum metric\n$h=-\\eta=\\operatorname{diag}(1,-1,-1,-1)$, and the dimensionless coupling\n$g_{\\mathrm{em}}$ with $g_{\\mathrm{em}}^2=4\\pi\\alpha$. For a finite nonempty\nindex set $i=1,\\ldots,m$, take future massive energy-momentum vectors\n$p_i=(E_i,\\mathbf p_i)$ with components in joules and\n$E_i^2-|\\mathbf p_i|^2=M_i^2>0$. Put $\\mathbf v_i=\\mathbf p_i/E_i$, so\n$|\\mathbf v_i|<1$. Choose signs $s_i\\in\\{-1,+1\\}$ and real dimensionless charges\n$Q_i$ satisfying $\\sum_i s_iQ_i=0$. These are prescribed current data, not\ndynamical charged-particle trajectories.\n\nFor $\\mathbf n\\in S^2$, let $q=(\\omega,\\omega\\mathbf n)$ with photon energy\n$\\omega>0$ in joules and define\n$$p_i\\cdot q:=E_i\\omega-\\mathbf p_i\\cdot(\\omega\\mathbf n),\\qquad J^\\mu(q):=\\sum_{i=1}^m s_iQ_i\\frac{p_i^\\mu}{p_i\\cdot q},\\qquad K^\\mu(\\mathbf n):=\\omega J^\\mu(\\omega,\\omega\\mathbf n).$$\nThe dot in this current formula is $h$-contraction; in particular\n$p_i\\cdot q=\\omega E_i(1-\\mathbf v_i\\cdot\\mathbf n)>0$. Choose measurable\nreal orthonormal spatial polarizations $\\epsilon_1(\\mathbf n),\\epsilon_2(\\mathbf n)$\nwith $\\mathbf n\\cdot\\epsilon_r(\\mathbf n)=0$ almost everywhere. Put\n$\\epsilon_r^\\mu=(0,\\epsilon_r)$ and\n$K\\cdot\\epsilon_r:=-\\mathbf K\\cdot\\epsilon_r$. Define the finite nonnegative\nangular coefficient\n$$C:=\\frac{g_{\\mathrm{em}}^2}{2(2\\pi)^3} \\int_{S^2}\\sum_{r=1}^{2}|K(\\mathbf n)\\cdot\\epsilon_r(\\mathbf n)|^2\\,d\\Omega.$$\n\nFor fixed energy cutoffs $0<\\lambda<\\Lambda<\\infty$ in joules, define\n$\\mathfrak h_E=L^2(\\mathbb R^3,d^3\\mathbf q/[(2\\pi)^3 2\\omega];\\mathbb C^2)$,\nwhere $\\omega=|\\mathbf q|$, and\n$$h_{\\lambda,\\Lambda,r}(\\mathbf q) =g_{\\mathrm{em}}J(q)\\cdot\\epsilon_r(\\mathbf q/|\\mathbf q|) \\,\\mathbf1_{\\{\\lambda<|\\mathbf q|<\\Lambda\\}}.$$\nThe current draft mathematical supplier\n[[thm-qft-example-soft-current-angular-coherent]] supplies the $\\mathbb C^3$\ntransverse energy-space norm and unitary conversion. The measurable\northonormal polarization frame gives the pointwise unitary identification\n$h\\mapsto\\sum_{r=1}^2h_r\\epsilon_r$ proved in step 3.1; composing it with\nthat conversion identifies $\\mathfrak h_E$ with the positive transverse\none-particle space $\\mathfrak h_T$ of [[def-qft-photon-transverse-space]]\nby the unitary map below, where for $\\mathbf k\\ne0$ the notation\n$\\epsilon_r(\\mathbf k)$ denotes the homogeneous extension\n$\\epsilon_r(\\mathbf k/|\\mathbf k|)$ of the supplied sphere frame:\n$$(U_Eh)(\\mathbf k)= \\sqrt{\\frac{(\\hbar c)^2}{(2\\pi)^3\\,2|\\mathbf k|}} \\sum_{r=1}^{2}h_r(\\hbar c\\,\\mathbf k)\\epsilon_r(\\mathbf k), \\qquad \\mathbf k\\in\\mathbb R^3\\setminus\\{0\\}.$$\nHere $\\mathbf k$ is a wave vector in $\\mathrm m^{-1}$ and\n$\\hbar c\\,\\mathbf k$ is the corresponding energy-momentum vector in joules.\nSet $N_\\gamma:=C\\log(\\Lambda/\\lambda)$ and prepare the normalized coherent\nvector in the free photon Fock space\n$$\\Psi_{\\lambda,\\Lambda} =e^{-N_\\gamma/2}\\bigoplus_{n=0}^{\\infty} \\frac{(U_Eh_{\\lambda,\\Lambda})^{\\otimes_s n}}{\\sqrt{n!}} \\in\\mathcal F_s(\\mathfrak h_T),$$\nwhere the $n=0$ term is the vacuum sector. Let $P_n$ be the number-sector\nprojection from [[def-qft-x03-photon-count-pvm]] and define\n$p_n$ as the model probability assigned to outcome $n$ by the finite\ntwo-outcome projective partition $\\{\\{n\\},\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{n\\}\\}$.\nThen\n$$p_n=e^{-N_\\gamma}\\frac{N_\\gamma^n}{n!},\\qquad n\\in\\mathbb N_0,$$\nwith $0^0:=1$; these probabilities sum to one, the mean photon count is\n$N_\\gamma$, and the vacuum probability is $e^{-N_\\gamma}$. The expected\nphoton energy is\n$$\\langle\\Psi_{\\lambda,\\Lambda},H_\\gamma\\Psi_{\\lambda,\\Lambda}\\rangle =C(\\Lambda-\\lambda)\\ \\mathrm J,$$\nfor $H_\\gamma=\\hbar c\\,d\\Gamma(|\\mathbf k|)$ of\n[[post-qft-free-photon-model]]. If $C>0$, the family has no Fock-norm or\nprojective-ray limit as $\\lambda\\downarrow0$ (projective-ray convergence means\nnorm convergence after allowing a unit-modulus phase for each cutoff), although\nits mean energy tends to the finite value $C\\Lambda$.\n\nFor the prescribed one-charge rest-to-velocity current with final velocity\n$v\\hat{\\mathbf z}$, $0<v<1$, take\n$s_{\\rm in}=-1$, $Q_{\\rm in}=1$, $p_{\\rm in}=(M,\\mathbf0)$ and\n$s_{\\rm out}=+1$, $Q_{\\rm out}=1$,\n$p_{\\rm out}=(M\\gamma_v,M\\gamma_v v\\hat{\\mathbf z})$, where $M>0$ is the\nrest energy and $\\gamma_v=(1-v^2)^{-1/2}$. The same coefficient is\n$$C(v)=\\frac{\\alpha}{\\pi} \\left(\\frac1v\\log\\frac{1+v}{1-v}-2\\right)>0.$$\nIf $C>0$, the cutoff family has no Fock-norm or projective-ray limit as\n$\\lambda\\downarrow0$; the proof below derives this from adjacent-shell\noverlaps and does not use the supplier's separate conditional infrared-limit\nclause. Its required norm and coherent-state inputs remain conditional on\nthe inspected draft supplier until its upstream inputs are current. This\nprediction concerns only the constructed positive free coherent state and\nits count PVM under the adopted physical assumptions. It does not infer that\na full interacting-QED scattering event emits that state or that a detector\nrealizes this PVM.",
          "deps": [
            "def-countable-choice",
            "def-qft-example-data",
            "def-qft-framework-units",
            "def-qft-fock-and-test-spaces",
            "def-qft-photon-transverse-space",
            "def-qft-x03-photon-count-pvm",
            "lem-qft-segal-weyl-domain",
            "post-qft-constructed-model-and-measurement",
            "post-qft-free-photon-model",
            "thm-qft-example-soft-current-angular-coherent",
            "thm-qft-x03-photon-count-pvm",
            "thm-logarithm-derivative-and-integral"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-qft-example-data": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-qft-framework-units": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-qft-fock-and-test-spaces": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-qft-photon-transverse-space": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-qft-x03-photon-count-pvm": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-qft-segal-weyl-domain": "mathematical-premise",
