      "items": [
        {
          "id": "def-qft-free-scalar-model",
          "kind": "definition",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "Exact real scalar free model",
          "reference": "research/extended-frameworks-2026-10-03/quantum-field-theory/workers/free-fields/proof-modules.md#FF3",
          "design_state": "Exact real scalar specialization with explicit shell, Fock domain and vacuum-subtracted Hamiltonian; conditional on the QFT-F01 physical adoption.",
          "dependency_level": 7,
          "deps": [
            "post-qft-free-field-model",
            "def-qft-framework-units",
            "def-qft-scalar-mass-shell",
            "def-countable-choice",
            "def-qft-fock-and-test-spaces",
            "lem-qft-second-quantized-spectrum",
            "lem-qft-smeared-free-scalar"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "post-qft-free-field-model": "physical-assumption",
            "def-qft-framework-units": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-qft-scalar-mass-shell": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-qft-fock-and-test-spaces": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-qft-second-quantized-spectrum": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-qft-smeared-free-scalar": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "physical_scope": "One real scalar species in four-dimensional flat Minkowski spacetime, with the adopted bosonic Fock representation, inverse-length parameter μ≥0, and exact vacuum-subtracted Hamiltonian ℏc dΓs(ωμ). This definition supplies no interacting term, regulator, point-field product, or empirical universality claim.",
          "empirical_premises": [],
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice [[def-countable-choice]], as in the inspected Fock\nconstruction.\n\nSelect the real-scalar branch of the QFT-F01 physical adoption\n[[post-qft-free-field-model]]: one real spin-zero species with bosonic\nstatistics and the zero-particle vacuum. For a smooth real classical field\n$\\phi_{\\mathrm n}:\\mathbb R^4\\to\\mathbb R$ of canonical length degree $-1$,\nthat postulate adopts\n$$\\frac{S_\\phi}{\\hbar}=-\\frac12\\int_{\\mathbb R^4} \\left(\\eta^{ab}\\partial_a\\phi_{\\mathrm n}\\partial_b\\phi_{\\mathrm n} +\\mu^2\\phi_{\\mathrm n}^2\\right)\\,d^4x.$$\nThe species, statistics, state, and action are physical model inputs. The\npresent item fixes the exact flat-spacetime free Fock model to which the\nlater deductions apply.\n\nUse the oriented and time-oriented Minkowski spacetime, signature\n$\\eta=\\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,1,1)$, and length coordinates $x^0=ct$ and\n$\\mathbf x\\in\\mathbb R^3$ from [[def-qft-framework-units]]. Write\n$\\Box=-\\partial_0^2+\\sum_{j=1}^3\\partial_j^2$. Choose an inverse-length\nparameter $\\mu\\ge0$. When $\\mu>0$, the corresponding SI rest mass is\n$m_{\\mathrm{rest,SI}}=\\hbar\\mu/c>0$; $\\mu=0$ denotes the massless branch and\nassigns no positive rest mass. For $\\mathbf k\\in\\mathbb R^3$, put\n$\\omega_\\mu(\\mathbf k)=\\sqrt{|\\mathbf k|^2+\\mu^2}$, with units\n$\\mathrm m^{-1}$.\n\nLet $H_\\mu^+$, $d\\nu_\\mu$, $H_\\mu=L^2(H_\\mu^+,d\\nu_\\mu;\\mathbb C)$, and\n$K_\\mu:\\mathcal S(\\mathbb R^4)\\to H_\\mu$ be the future mass shell, measure,\none-particle Hilbert space, and Fourier restriction of\n[[def-qft-scalar-mass-shell]]. In the massless case the null apex is omitted;\nit has measure zero. The shell measure is\n$d\\nu_\\mu=d^3\\mathbf k/((2\\pi)^3\\,2\\omega_\\mu(\\mathbf k))$.\n\nUse the symmetric bosonic Fock space $\\mathcal F_s(H_\\mu)$, vacuum\n$\\Omega=(1,0,0,\\ldots)$, and dense finite-particle domain\n$\\mathcal D_{\\mathrm{fin}}$ from\n[[def-qft-fock-and-test-spaces]]. The Fock pairing is linear in its second\nvariable. Creation $a^\\dagger(h)$ is linear in $h$, while annihilation $a(h)$\nis conjugate-linear in $h$. For $f\\in\\mathcal S(\\mathbb R^4)$ define the\ncomplex-linear smeared scalar field on $\\mathcal D_{\\mathrm{fin}}$ by\n\n$$\\Phi_\\mu(f)=a(K_\\mu\\overline f)+a^\\dagger(K_\\mu f).$$\n\nFor real $f$, this is the symmetric scalar field whose self-adjoint closure\nand bounded Weyl functions are constructed in\n[[lem-qft-smeared-free-scalar]]. A smeared field is a domain-qualified\noperator-valued distribution; the item introduces no pointwise operator\n$\\Phi_\\mu(x)$.\n\nDefine $d\\Gamma_s(\\omega_\\mu)$ on the $n$-particle sector as multiplication\nby $\\sum_{r=1}^n\\omega_\\mu(\\mathbf k_r)$, with value zero on the vacuum\nsector. The exact maximal domain is\n\n$$D(d\\Gamma_s(\\omega_\\mu))= \\left\\{\\Psi:\\sum_{n\\ge1}\\int_{(H_\\mu^+)^n} \\left|\\sum_{r=1}^n\\omega_\\mu(\\mathbf k_r)\\right|^2 |\\Psi_n(\\mathbf k_1,\\ldots,\\mathbf k_n)|^2\\,d\\nu_\\mu^n<\\infty\\right\\}.$$\n\nThe physical Hamiltonian of this selected model is the vacuum-subtracted\nself-adjoint operator\n$H_\\mu^{\\mathrm{phys}}=\\hbar c\\,d\\Gamma_s(\\omega_\\mu)$ on that domain, as\ndefined by the multiplier construction of\n[[lem-qft-second-quantized-spectrum]]. It has units of joules and\n$H_\\mu^{\\mathrm{phys}}\\Omega=0$. No infinite zero-point-energy sum is part of\nthis definition. The canonical scalar engineering dimension is\n$\\mathrm m^{-1}$; a spacetime test function of unit $\\mathrm m^{-3}$ makes the\nsmeared field dimensionless, consistently with\n[[def-qft-framework-units]].",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "not-applicable"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "David Tong, Quantum Field Theory, author-hosted full-text Chapter 2",
                "url": "https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/qft/qfthtml/S2.html",
                "locator": "Complete Chapter 2 HTML; §§2.2–2.4 on free scalar modes, vacuum and Fock states; §2.6.1 on spacelike commutativity; §2.7 on the free scalar vacuum two-point function, including printed pp. 23–32, 35–40, and 56–58."
              },
              {
                "title": "Mark Srednicki, Quantum Field Theory, author-hosted 2006 prepublication book draft, §3 Canonical Quantization of Scalar Fields",
                "url": "https://www.physics.ucsb.edu/~mark/ms-qft-DRAFT.pdf",
                "locator": "Complete 616-page book draft; printed pp. 36–42, scalar action, mass-shell measure, mode normalization, canonical commutators and Hamiltonian."
              }
            ]
          },
          "library": "physics"
        },
        {
          "id": "pthm-qft-scalar-free-properties",
          "kind": "physics-theorem",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "Scalar distribution, covariance, locality and spectrum",
          "reference": "research/extended-frameworks-2026-10-03/quantum-field-theory/workers/free-fields/proof-modules.md#FF3-FF4",
          "design_state": "Complete conditional deductions for the real scalar model: Klein-Gordon equation, covariance, forward spectrum, exact mass gap, and local Weyl commutativity.",
          "dependency_level": 8,
          "deps": [
            "post-qft-free-field-model",
