          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "physical_scope": "Conditional properties of the selected four-dimensional real scalar free Fock model: the smeared Klein–Gordon field, proper orthochronous Poincare covariance, vacuum and forward-cone spectrum, exact mass gap, and isotony and spacelike commutativity of bounded local Weyl algebras.",
          "empirical_premises": [],
          "statement": "Assume the scalar model adoption planned in\n[[post-qft-free-field-model]] and Countable Choice\n[[def-countable-choice]]. Let $\\mu\\ge0$ and use the model, shell, field,\nvacuum, and units of [[def-qft-free-scalar-model]] and\n[[def-qft-scalar-mass-shell]]. These are conditional model deductions, with no\nempirical premise.\n\nFor every Schwartz test $f$, $\\Phi_\\mu(f)$ is defined on\n$\\mathcal D_{\\mathrm{fin}}$; for real $f$ it is symmetric and essentially\nself-adjoint there. Distributionally,\n$\\Phi_\\mu((\\Box-\\mu^2)f)=0$. The Fock lift of the proper orthochronous\nPoincare action is unitary, leaves $\\Omega$ invariant, and implements\ncovariance of the smeared field. For real Schwartz tests the vacuum\ntwo-point form is $\\langle\\Omega,\\Phi_\\mu(f)\\Phi_\\mu(g)\\Omega\\rangle=\\langle K_\\mu f,K_\\mu g\\rangle_2$, and it is nonnegative when $g=f$. The\njoint spectrum of spacetime translations is contained in the closed forward\ncone.\n\nFor real compactly supported smooth tests with pairwise spacelike-separated\nsupports, the smeared fields commute on $\\mathcal D_{\\mathrm{fin}}$. The\nbounded local Weyl algebras are isotonic and algebras for spacelike-separated\nregions commute. The physical Hamiltonian is self-adjoint on the exact\nmultiplier domain in [[def-qft-free-scalar-model]], is nonnegative, and has\n$\\Omega$ as its unique zero-energy vector. If $\\mu>0$, the infimum of its\npositive spectrum is $\\hbar c\\mu=m_{\\mathrm{rest,SI}}c^2$. If $\\mu=0$, its\npositive spectrum has no gap above zero.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "David Tong, Quantum Field Theory, author-hosted full-text Chapter 2",
                "url": "https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/qft/qfthtml/S2.html",
                "locator": "Complete Chapter 2 HTML; §§2.2–2.4 on free scalar modes, vacuum and Fock states; §2.6.1 on spacelike commutativity; §2.7 on the free scalar vacuum two-point function, including printed pp. 23–32, 35–40, and 56–58."
              },
              {
                "title": "Mark Srednicki, Quantum Field Theory, author-hosted 2006 prepublication book draft, §3 Canonical Quantization of Scalar Fields",
                "url": "https://www.physics.ucsb.edu/~mark/ms-qft-DRAFT.pdf",
                "locator": "Complete 616-page book draft; printed pp. 36–42, scalar action, mass-shell measure, mode normalization, canonical commutators and Hamiltonian."
              }
            ]
          },
          "library": "physics",
          "proof_strategy": "direct"
        },
        {
          "id": "pthm-qft-scalar-vacuum-moments",
          "kind": "physics-theorem",
          "domain": "physics",
          "title": "Gaussian free vacuum and time-ordered carrier",
          "reference": "research/extended-frameworks-2026-10-03/quantum-field-theory/workers/free-fields/proof-modules.md#FF2-FF3-FF9",
          "design_state": "Complete conditional vacuum Wick recursion, Gaussian Weyl expectation and exact distributional time-ordered two-point carrier; no interacting convergence or local-product claim.",
          "dependency_level": 8,
          "deps": [
            "post-qft-free-field-model",
            "def-qft-free-scalar-model",
            "def-countable-choice",
            "lem-qft-smeared-free-scalar",
            "lem-qft-segal-weyl-domain",
            "lem-qft-free-time-ordered-kernel"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "post-qft-free-field-model": "physical-assumption",
            "def-qft-free-scalar-model": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-qft-smeared-free-scalar": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-qft-segal-weyl-domain": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-qft-free-time-ordered-kernel": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "physical_scope": "Conditional vacuum, smeared-field moments, bounded Weyl expectations and the exact distributional time-ordered two-point carrier for the selected real scalar free Fock model. No interacting convergence or renormalized local product is claimed.",
          "empirical_premises": [],
          "statement": "Assume the scalar model adoption planned in\n[[post-qft-free-field-model]], Countable Choice\n[[def-countable-choice]], and the exact model of\n[[def-qft-free-scalar-model]]. For real Schwartz tests $f_1,\\ldots,f_n$,\nthe vacuum expectation of the ordered product of smeared fields is zero\nwhen $n$ is odd. When $n$ is even, it is the sum over pairings of products\nof the corresponding two-point functions\n$\\langle K_\\mu f_r,K_\\mu f_s\\rangle_2$ for $r<s$ in each pair. For a real\nSchwartz test $f$, the bounded Weyl operator has vacuum expectation\n$\\langle\\Omega,W_\\mu(f)\\Omega\\rangle\n=\\exp(-\\|K_\\mu f\\|_2^2/2)$.\n\nThe time-ordered two-point carrier is the tempered distribution $H_\\mu$\ndefined by the partial spatial Fourier formula of\n[[lem-qft-free-time-ordered-kernel]]. It agrees with the ordered Wightman\ndistributions away from equal-time coincidence and satisfies\n$(\\Box-\\mu^2)H_\\mu=i\\delta_0$. The formula fixes its extension at coincidence\nand includes no additional prefactor $i$. These are conditional deductions\nfor the selected free model.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "David Tong, Quantum Field Theory, author-hosted full-text Chapter 2",
                "url": "https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/qft/qfthtml/S2.html",
                "locator": "Complete Chapter 2 HTML; §§2.2–2.4 on free scalar modes, vacuum and Fock states; §2.6.1 on spacelike commutativity; §2.7 on the free scalar vacuum two-point function, including printed pp. 23–32, 35–40, and 56–58."
              },
              {
                "title": "David Tong, Quantum Field Theory, author-hosted full-text Chapter 3",
                "url": "https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/qft/qfthtml/S3.html",
                "locator": "Complete Chapter 3 HTML; §3.3.1, Wick expansion and contractions, including the displayed vacuum-pairing derivation (printed pp. 56–58)."
              },
              {
                "title": "Mark Srednicki, Quantum Field Theory, author-hosted 2006 prepublication book draft, §3 Canonical Quantization of Scalar Fields",
                "url": "https://www.physics.ucsb.edu/~mark/ms-qft-DRAFT.pdf",
                "locator": "Complete 616-page book draft; printed pp. 36–42 and 67–69, scalar action and normalization, canonical commutators, time-ordered propagator and vacuum pairings."
              }
            ]
          },
          "library": "physics",
          "proof_strategy": "direct"
        }
      ],
      "scaffold": "research/plan-quantum-field-theory-track.md",
      "order": 551
