    {
      "id": "qft-f03",
      "title": "Exact Dirac particle/antiparticle free model",
      "category": "quantum-field-theory",
      "library": "physics",
      "companion": "qft-f03-examples",
      "kind": "A",
      "requires": [
        "qft-f01"
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "def-qft-free-dirac-model",
          "kind": "definition",
          "domain": "physics",
          "library": "physics",
          "title": "Exact Dirac particle/antiparticle free model",
          "statement": "Fix the oriented, time-oriented affine Minkowski spacetime and inertial length coordinates of [[def-qft-framework-units]], with $\\eta=\\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,1,1)$ and $x^0=ct$. The parameter $\\mu\\ge0$ and wave vector $\\mathbf k$ have unit $\\mathrm m^{-1}$; $\\omega(\\mathbf k)=\\sqrt{|\\mathbf k|^2+\\mu^2}$ also has unit $\\mathrm m^{-1}$. For $\\mu>0$, $\\mu=m_{\\mathrm{rest,SI}}c/\\hbar$; $\\mu=0$ is the admitted massless branch. The corresponding SI energy and momentum are $\\hbar c\\omega$ joules and $\\hbar\\mathbf k$ in $\\mathrm{kg\\,m\\,s^{-1}}$. The canonically normalized Dirac field has engineering length degree $-3/2$; a spacetime spinor test has degree $-5/2$, making its spacetime-smearing pairing dimensionless. These are the unit conventions of [[def-qft-framework-units]], not claims about interacting-field scaling.\n\nAdopt the Dirac branch of [[post-qft-free-field-model]]: one free Dirac species, the selected CAR representation and zero-particle vacuum are physical model assumptions. Countable Choice is the mathematical choice strength used by the Fock construction [[def-countable-choice]].\n\nUse $\\mathbb C^4$ spinors and the matrices, mass-shell parameter, one-particle Hilbert space $\\mathcal H_D$, multiplier $h_D(\\mathbf k)=\\boldsymbol\\alpha\\cdot\\mathbf k+\\beta\\mu$, projections $P_\\pm(\\mathbf k)$ and propagator $W_D$ defined in [[def-qft-dirac-projections]]. The mathematical supplier [[lem-qft-dirac-projection-matrices]] establishes that $P_\\pm$ are complementary orthogonal projections of rank two, that $\\mathcal H_\\pm=\\operatorname{ran}P_\\pm$ are closed, and that $h_D$ is self-adjoint on its maximal multiplication domain. The one-particle space of the adopted field is\n$$\\mathcal K_D=\\mathcal H_+\\oplus\\overline{\\mathcal H_-},$$\nwhere the bar denotes the conjugate Hilbert space. Its fermionic Fock space, vacuum and creation/annihilation maps use [[def-qft-fock-and-test-spaces]] and [[lem-qft-fock-ccr-car]].\n\nFor a Schwartz spinor test $F\\in\\mathscr S(\\mathbb R^4;\\mathbb C^4)$, set\n$$\\widehat F(t,\\mathbf k)=\\int_{\\mathbb R^3}e^{-i\\mathbf k\\cdot\\mathbf x}F(t,\\mathbf x)\\,d^3\\mathbf x,\\qquad u_F(\\mathbf k)=\\int_{\\mathbb R}W_D(t,\\mathbf k)\\widehat F(t,\\mathbf k)\\,dt.$$\nThe physical field is the bounded smeared map\n$$\\Psi(F)=c(P_+u_F)+c^\\dagger(\\overline{P_-u_F}),$$\nwith the exact test-map and CAR construction of [[lem-qft-free-dirac-car-locality]]. It is antilinear in $F$. Its positive-energy branch is the particle annihilation term; the conjugate negative-energy branch occurs as antiparticle creation. This is a model assignment: it does not identify negative-energy Fock excitations with physical states, invoke a filled Dirac sea, or prove the general spin-statistics theorem. No pointwise field operator is defined here.",
          "dependency_level": 7,
          "deps": [
            "post-qft-free-field-model",
            "def-qft-framework-units",
            "def-qft-dirac-projections",
            "lem-qft-dirac-projection-matrices",
            "def-qft-fock-and-test-spaces",
            "lem-qft-fock-ccr-car",
            "lem-qft-free-dirac-car-locality",
            "def-countable-choice"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "post-qft-free-field-model": "physical-assumption",
            "def-qft-framework-units": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-qft-dirac-projections": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-qft-dirac-projection-matrices": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-qft-fock-and-test-spaces": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-qft-fock-ccr-car": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-qft-free-dirac-car-locality": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "not-applicable"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "David Tong, Quantum Field Theory, author-hosted full-text Chapter 4",
                "url": "https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/qft/qfthtml/S4.html",
                "locator": "Complete HTML chapter on the Dirac equation, Clifford algebra, spinor representation and plane-wave solutions."
              },
              {
                "title": "David Tong, Quantum Field Theory, author-hosted full-text Chapter 5",
                "url": "https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/qft/qfthtml/S5.html",
                "locator": "Complete HTML chapter; §§5.1.1–5.3, Hamiltonian, fermionic quantization, vacuum, particles and antiparticles."
              },
              {
                "title": "Niklas Beisert, Quantum Field Theory I, ETH Zürich 2025 HS complete lecture notes",
                "url": "https://people.phys.ethz.ch/~nbeisert/lectures/QFT1-25HS-Notes.pdf",
                "locator": "Complete 194-page notes; Chapter 5 §§5.1–5.6, Clifford projectors, spinor covariance, Hamiltonian form and fermionic quantization; pp. 82–83, Dirac-sea comparison."
              }
            ]
          },
          "physical_scope": "One selected noninteracting Dirac species on four-dimensional affine Minkowski spacetime with signature (-+++), length coordinates x^0=ct, and mass parameter μ≥0. The CAR representation, species assignment and vacuum are adopted model data; fields are used only after spacetime smearing. No interaction, empirical claim or general spin-statistics theorem is included.",
          "proof_strategy": "direct"
        },
        {
          "id": "pthm-qft-dirac-free-properties",
          "kind": "physics-theorem",
          "domain": "physics",
          "library": "physics",
          "title": "Dirac CAR, covariance, graded locality and positive Fock energy",
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice and the adopted Dirac branch of [[post-qft-free-field-model]] as specified by [[def-qft-free-dirac-model]]. For all Schwartz spinor tests $F,G$, the bounded smeared field $\\Psi$ is antilinear in its test, satisfies\n$$\\{\\Psi(F),\\Psi(G)\\}=0,\\qquad \\{\\Psi(F),\\Psi(G)^\\dagger\\}=\\langle u_F,u_G\\rangle I,$$\nand solves the tested free Dirac equation. If $F$ and $G$ have compact spacelike-separated supports, the field-field and field-adjoint anticommutators vanish; consequently, finite even polynomials in the bounded smeared fields commute across spacelike-separated regions.\n\nLet $\\widetilde G_D$ be the translation and explicit spin-lift group defined in [[lem-qft-dirac-covariance-spectrum]]. Its strongly continuous unitary Fock representation $U$ satisfies\n$$U(\\widetilde g)\\Psi(F)U(\\widetilde g)^{-1}=\\Psi(\\tau_{\\widetilde g}F),\\qquad \\tau_{\\widetilde g}F(x)=(S^{-1})^\\dagger F(\\Lambda^{-1}(x-a)),$$\nfor $\\widetilde g=(a,\\Lambda,S)$. For the explicit spatial rotation lift, $S_R(2\\pi)=-I_4$ and $S_R(4\\pi)=I_4$; hence the $2\\pi$ test pullback is $F\\mapsto-F$ and $U_{2\\pi}\\Psi(F)U_{2\\pi}^{-1}=-\\Psi(F)$, while the $4\\pi$ test pullback and field action are identities. The vacuum is invariant and cyclic for the global graded field algebra. On the $n$-particle sector, $U_{2\\pi}=(-1)^n I$ and $U_{4\\pi}=I$.\n\nThe joint spectrum of translations lies in the closed future cone and the vacuum is the unique zero-energy vector. For $\\mu>0$, the nonvacuum spectrum has gap at least $\\mu$ in inverse-length units, hence $m_{\\mathrm{rest,SI}}c^2$ in SI energy units. If $K_D$ denotes the length-coordinate time-translation generator of [[lem-qft-dirac-covariance-spectrum]], the physical energy is $H_D^{\\mathrm{SI}}=\\hbar cK_D\\ge0$ on the same domain. This Fock generator acts on a different Hilbert space from the first-quantized multiplier $h_D$, which has both signs of energy. These are conditional deductions in the adopted model, not empirical claims.",
          "dependency_level": 8,
          "deps": [
            "def-qft-free-dirac-model",
            "def-qft-framework-units",
            "post-qft-free-field-model",
            "lem-qft-free-dirac-car-locality",
            "lem-qft-dirac-covariance-spectrum",
            "lem-qft-dirac-projection-matrices",
            "thm-quarter-turn-values-and-shift-formulas",
            "def-countable-choice"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-qft-free-dirac-model": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "def-qft-framework-units": "formulation-prerequisite",
            "post-qft-free-field-model": "physical-assumption",
            "lem-qft-free-dirac-car-locality": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-qft-dirac-covariance-spectrum": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-qft-dirac-projection-matrices": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-quarter-turn-values-and-shift-formulas": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "strategy": "direct",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "David Tong, Quantum Field Theory, author-hosted full-text Chapter 4",
                "url": "https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/qft/qfthtml/S4.html",
                "locator": "Complete HTML chapter on the Dirac equation, Clifford algebra, spinor representation and plane-wave solutions."
              },
              {
                "title": "David Tong, Quantum Field Theory, author-hosted full-text Chapter 5",
                "url": "https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/qft/qfthtml/S5.html",
                "locator": "Complete HTML chapter; §§5.1.1–5.3, Hamiltonian, fermionic quantization, vacuum, particles and antiparticles."
              },
              {
                "title": "Niklas Beisert, Quantum Field Theory I, ETH Zürich 2025 HS complete lecture notes",
                "url": "https://people.phys.ethz.ch/~nbeisert/lectures/QFT1-25HS-Notes.pdf",
                "locator": "Complete 194-page notes; Chapter 5 §§5.1–5.6, Clifford projectors, spinor covariance, Hamiltonian form and fermionic quantization; pp. 82–83, Dirac-sea comparison."
              }
            ]
          },
          "physical_scope": "Conditional conclusions for the selected noninteracting Dirac CAR model on flat affine Minkowski spacetime, with fixed (-+++) signature, length coordinates and μ≥0. No empirical premise, interaction, point-field observable or general spin-statistics claim is used.",
          "proof_strategy": "direct"
        }
      ],
      "scaffold": "research/plan-quantum-field-theory-track.md",
      "order": 553
    },
    {
      "id": "qft-f03-examples",
      "title": "Exact Dirac particle/antiparticle free model — Examples",
      "kind": "B",
