          },
          "physical_scope": "The normalized Gaussian spacetime-smearing family for the real scalar field in the selected four-dimensional free Fock vacuum. It refutes only convergence in this representation's vacuum-vector norm; distributional or renormalized point-field constructions in other senses are outside scope. No empirical observation is asserted.",
          "empirical_premises": [],
          "statement": "Assume all hypotheses of\n[[pthm-qft-free-observable-domain-limits]], including Countable Choice and the\nselected four-dimensional free real scalar Fock model with $\\mu\\ge0$. Fix a\npoint $x_0\\in\\mathbb R^4$ and a nonnegative normalized\nSchwartz Gaussian $\\rho\\in\\mathscr S(\\mathbb R^4)$, and put\n$\\rho_{\\epsilon,x_0}(x)=\\epsilon^{-4}\\rho((x-x_0)/\\epsilon)$. The claim\nthat $\\Phi_\\mu(\\rho_{\\epsilon,x_0})\\Omega$ converges in Fock norm to a finite\nvector as $\\epsilon\\downarrow0$, thereby defining a sharp point field on the\nvacuum by this norm limit, is false.",
          "proof_strategy": "direct",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
