        {
          "id": "thm-qft-bounded-regulator-dyson-factorization",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "library": "mathematics",
          "physical_scope": null,
          "title": "Bounded regulated Dyson convergence and temporal factorization",
          "reference": "research/plan-quantum-field-theory-track.md#regular-polynomial-field-functional-algebra",
          "design_state": "Proves norm convergence, uniqueness, unitarity, composition, and separated-time factorization for bounded strongly continuous self-adjoint operators.",
          "dependency_level": 0,
          "deps": [
            "def-countable-choice",
            "def-hilbert-space",
            "def-space-of-bounded-linear-operators",
            "def-operator-norm",
            "def-hilbert-space-adjoint",
            "thm-extreme-value-metric",
            "def-complex-exponential",
            "lem-complex-exponential-series-converges-everywhere",
            "thm-continuous-on-a-rectangle-is-riemann-integrable",
            "thm-ftc-second-part",
            "thm-algebra-of-derivatives",
            "thm-heine-cantor-metric"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-hilbert-space": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-space-of-bounded-linear-operators": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-operator-norm": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-hilbert-space-adjoint": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-extreme-value-metric": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-complex-exponential": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-complex-exponential-series-converges-everywhere": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-continuous-on-a-rectangle-is-riemann-integrable": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-ftc-second-part": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-algebra-of-derivatives": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-heine-cantor-metric": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "proof_strategy": "direct",
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $\\mathcal H$ be a complex Hilbert space\n([[def-hilbert-space]]), $I=[a,b]$ with $a\\le b$,\nand $V:I\\to\\mathcal B(\\mathcal H)$ a strongly continuous family of\nself-adjoint bounded operators (self-adjoint means $V(t)=V(t)^*$, using the\nHilbert adjoint of [[def-hilbert-space-adjoint]]) with\n$M:=\\sup_{t\\in I}\\|V(t)\\|<\\infty$. Strong continuity means that\n$t\\mapsto V(t)\\psi$ is norm-continuous for every $\\psi\\in\\mathcal H$.\nHere a strongly continuous solution $U:I^2\\to\\mathcal B(\\mathcal H)$ means\nthat, for each fixed $s\\in I$ and $\\psi\\in\\mathcal H$,\n$t\\mapsto U(t,s)\\psi$ is norm-continuous.\nDefine $U_0(t,s)=I_{\\mathcal H}$ and recursively\n$$ U_{n+1}(t,s)\\psi=-i\\int_s^t V(r)U_n(r,s)\\psi\\,dr,\\qquad a\\le s,t\\le b, $$\nwhere the integral is the vector-valued Riemann integral and is oriented when\n$t<s$. Then\n$$ \\|U_0(t,s)\\|\\le1,\\qquad \\|U_n(t,s)\\|\\le \\frac{M^n|t-s|^n}{n!}\\quad(n\\ge1). $$\nFor every complex $z$, $U_z(t,s)=\\sum_{n\\ge0}z^nU_n(t,s)$ converges in\noperator norm, uniformly on $I^2$, and is the unique strongly continuous\nsolution of\n$$ U_z(t,s)=I_{\\mathcal H}-iz\\int_s^t V(r)U_z(r,s)\\,dr . $$\nFor real $z$, $U_z(t,s)$ is unitary (that is, a surjective linear isometry\nof $\\mathcal H$) and obeys\n$U_z(t,r)U_z(r,s)=U_z(t,s)$. If $V_2$ vanishes outside $[a,c]$ and\n$V_1$ vanishes outside $[d,b]$, where $c<d$, then\n$$ U_z^{V_1+V_2}(b,a)=U_z^{V_1}(b,a)U_z^{V_2}(b,a), $$\nwith the later-time factor on the left, provided $a\\le c<d\\le b$. This\nidentity also holds\ncoefficientwise as a formal power series in $z$.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "David Tong, Quantum Field Theory, complete author-hosted Cambridge lecture notes, chapter 3",
                "url": "https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/qft/qfthtml/S3.html",
                "locator": "Complete HTML chapter 3, section 3.1.1, equations (3.221)–(3.225), the time-ordered Dyson series. Its displayed argument is formal; the norm bounds and strong-continuity proof here are supplied locally."
              }
            ]
          }
