    {
      "id": "qft-pir01-examples",
      "title": "Adopted finite-regulator bosonic polynomial model — Examples",
      "kind": "B",
      "category": "quantum-field-theory",
      "library": "physics",
      "companion": "qft-pir01",
      "requires": [
        "qft-pir01"
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "ex-qft-one-mode-interacting-model",
          "kind": "example",
          "domain": "physics",
          "library": "physics",
          "title": "One-mode quartic model is a genuine constructed interacting example",
          "reference": "items/ex-qft-one-mode-interacting-model.md#Example",
          "design_state": "Complete one-mode verification using the actual full L² model and the quartic energy bound. Its local theorem suppliers are escalated because upstream C01 postulates lack current Step 1 readiness; this item is escalated.",
          "dependency_level": 7,
          "deps": [
            "pthm-qft-regulated-interacting-model-evolution",
            "pthm-qft-quartic-model-energy-bound",
            "def-qft-regulated-polynomial-hamiltonian",
            "def-countable-choice"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-qft-regulated-polynomial-hamiltonian": "mathematical-premise",
            "pthm-qft-quartic-model-energy-bound": "physical-result",
            "pthm-qft-regulated-interacting-model-evolution": "physical-result"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Choose $N=1$, $a=1$, $r=1$, and $\\lambda=1$, all dimensionless. The\npotential is $V(q)=q^2/2+q^4$, and the physical Hamiltonian is $H_{\\rm phys}\n=E_*h$ with $E_*>0$ joules. The one-mode space is the full\n$H_1=L^2(\\mathbb R,dq;\\mathbb C)$ of\n[[def-qft-regulated-polynomial-hamiltonian]], not a finite matrix truncation.\nThe positive $q^4$ term is an actual polynomial interaction in this selected\nfinite regulator.",
          "strategy": "1.1 The parameters satisfy $a>0$, $r>0$, and $\\lambda>0$, and\n$V(q)=q^2/2+q^4\\ge q^2/2$, so the coercivity hypotheses hold with\n$c=1/2$ and $C_0=0$. The coordinate remains any real $q$ in\n$L^2(\\mathbb R)$; the characteristic functions\n$\\mathbf 1_{[3n,3n+1)}$, $n\\in\\mathbb N$, are nonzero pairwise\northogonal vectors, so this Hilbert space is infinite-dimensional.\n[F3, algebra]\n\n2.1 Substituting $a=r=\\lambda=1$ into [F2] gives\n$0\\le E_g^{\\rm phys}(1)-E_g^{\\rm phys}(0)\\le3E_*/2$.\nThis is an exact bound for the selected model, not an exact value of either\nground energy. [F2, step 1.1, algebra]\n\n3.1 Applying [F1] to the same selected model gives a global unitary group\n$U_{\\rm phys}(\\tau)$ for every $\\tau\\in\\mathbb R$, norm preservation for\nall states, and differentiability precisely on the stated Hamiltonian\ndomain. The quartic coefficient is positive, and the Hilbert space is\ninfinite-dimensional by step 1.1; thus this is an interacting operator model,\nnot a finite matrix replacement. No observation or continuum extrapolation\nis asserted. [F1, step 1.1, algebra] ∎",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "David Tong, Quantum Field Theory, author-hosted lecture notes, Chapter 3, Interacting Fields",
                "url": "https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/qft/qfthtml/S3.html",
                "locator": "Complete Chapter 3 HTML, real-scalar phi-four interaction discussion."
              },
              {
                "title": "Gerald Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics, 2nd ed., §§4.4 and 8.3",
                "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-schroe/schroe2.pdf",
                "locator": "Printed pp.139–141 and 212–214, Rayleigh–Ritz and oscillator ground state."
              }
            ]
          },
          "physical_scope": "One fixed continuous mode with a positive quartic interaction, actual form-selected operator, global unitary evolution, and the proved energy-increment bound. No data or continuum limit.",
          "empirical_premises": [],
          "proof_strategy": "direct"
        },
        {
          "id": "rem-qft-formal-renormalization-physical-status",
          "kind": "remark",
          "domain": "physics",
          "library": "physics",
          "title": "Formal coefficient renormalization retains its exact status",
          "reference": "items/rem-qft-formal-renormalization-physical-status.md#Physical status",
          "design_state": "Complete scope remark based on the current-ready QFT-IR04 proposition and imported choice definition; the claim is ready at this item, without independent approval.",
          "dependency_level": 5,
          "deps": [
            "prop-qft-four-dimensional-log-scale-anomaly",
            "def-axiom-of-choice"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-axiom-of-choice": "mathematical-premise",
            "prop-qft-four-dimensional-log-scale-anomaly": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice ([[def-axiom-of-choice]]) as in\n[[prop-qft-four-dimensional-log-scale-anomaly]]. That proposition gives an\nexact Euclidean distribution-extension identity for the specified punctured\nkernel $u(x)=1/(16\\pi^4|x|^4)$: changing its cutoff scale changes the\nextension by $(8\\pi^2)^{-1}\\log(\\mu/\\nu)\\delta_0$. Its statement\nexplicitly says this is not a measured running coupling or physical beta\nfunction. The identity does not select a physical renormalization\nprescription, define an experimental observable, or construct a\nLorentzian interacting field. This remark asserts neither existence nor\nnonexistence of a continuum interacting model and supplies no empirical\nclaim.",
          "strategy": "Scope remark; no deductive proof claimed.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "not-applicable"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "David Tong, Quantum Field Theory, author-hosted lecture notes, Chapter 3, Interacting Fields",
                "url": "https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/qft/qfthtml/S3.html",
                "locator": "Complete Chapter 3 HTML, perturbative interaction discussion."
              }
            ]
          },
          "physical_scope": "A scope clarification for one four-dimensional Euclidean distribution-extension identity; it asserts no measured running parameter, Lorentzian observable, or continuum interacting model.",
          "empirical_premises": []
        }
      ],
